(2926,1,'product',2257,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.012nF (12k)\",\"description\":\"The 0.012nF (12K) capacitor is a small-value ceramic capacitor commonly used in electronic circuits for high-frequency filtering, signal coupling, and noise suppression applications. The value 0.012nF is equal to 12 picofarads (12pF), which makes it suitable for RF circuits, oscillator circuits, tuning networks, and high-frequency signal processing. The marking “12K” typically indicates the capacitance value (12pF) and tolerance, where K represents a tolerance of ±10%\",\"info\":\"This type of capacitor is usually non-polarized, meaning it can be connected in any direction within a circuit. It is often available in ceramic disc or small SMD package form. Due to its very low capacitance value, it is mainly used in high-frequency and precision electronic applications rather than power filtering. The capacitor offers stable performance, low loss, and good reliability over a wide temperature range.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"It is widely used in RF transmitters and receivers, crystal oscillator circuits, communication devices, timing circuits, antenna matching networks, and general signal processing circuits. Because of its compact size and stable characteristics, the 12pF capacitor is a common component in communication and microcontroller-based systems.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":316,\"secondary_id\":442,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 03:43:49'),
(2927,1,'product',2258,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.022nF (22)\",\"description\":\"A 0.022 nF ceramic capacitor is equivalent to 22 pF and is usually marked as “22” on the capacitor body. It is a non-polarized capacitor made using a ceramic dielectric and is mainly used in high-frequency and RF applications.\",\"info\":\"The 0.022nF (22) capacitor is a small-value ceramic capacitor commonly used in electronic circuits for high-frequency filtering, signal coupling, and noise suppression applications. The capacitance value 0.022nF is equal to 22 picofarads (22pF), making it suitable for RF circuits, oscillator circuits, timing networks, and signal tuning applications. The marking “22” on the capacitor typically represents the capacitance value of 22pF according to standard capacitor coding.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"This capacitor is non-polarized, allowing it to be connected in any direction within a circuit. It is usually available in ceramic disc or surface-mount (SMD) form and provides stable electrical performance with low loss at high frequencies. Due to its very small capacitance value, it is mainly used in precision electronic circuits rather than power supply filtering.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":316,\"secondary_id\":442,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 03:44:53'),
(2928,1,'product',2256,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.039nF (39)\",\"description\":\"A 0.039 nF ceramic capacitor is equivalent to 39 pF and is typically marked “39” on the capacitor body. It is a non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric and is designed for high-frequency signal applications.\",\"info\":\"Typical voltage ratings include 50 V, 100 V, 250 V, and higher, making them suitable for low-current signal paths. Since it is non-polarized, it can be connected in either direction.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":316,\"secondary_id\":442,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 03:46:12'),
(2929,1,'product',2250,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.1nF (104)\",\"description\":\"A 0.1 µF (104) ceramic capacitor is one of the most widely used non-polarized capacitors in electronics. It uses a ceramic dielectric and is designed to store and release small amounts of electrical energy quickly, making it ideal for noise suppression and decoupling.\",\"info\":\"The code 104 means 10 × 10? pF = 100,000 pF, which equals 100 nF or 0.1 µF. These capacitors are available in ceramic disc (through-hole) and MLCC / SMD packages and offer excellent high-frequency performance, low ESR, and high reliability.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":316,\"secondary_id\":442,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 03:46:21'),
(2930,1,'product',2255,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.56nF (561)\",\"description\":\"A 0.56 nF (561) ceramic capacitor is a small-value, non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric to store electrical charge. The marking 561 represents 560 pF, calculated as 56 × 10¹ pF, which is equal to 0.56 nF.\",\"info\":\"This capacitor value is commonly available in ceramic disc (through-hole) and MLCC / SMD packages. It offers low loss, good frequency stability, and reliable performance at high frequencies, making it suitable for signal-level and RF applications. Typical voltage ratings range from 50 V to 500 V or higher for disc types, while MLCC versions usually range from 16 V to 100 V, depending on size and dielectric.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":316,\"secondary_id\":442,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 03:46:32'),
