(3129,1,'product',2622,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"Dome camera 2MP IPC3612LB AF28 A2\",\"description\":\"The IPC3612LB-AF28-A2 is a 2MP Full HD IP Dome Camera from Uniview (UNV), designed for reliable indoor and outdoor surveillance applications such as offices, shops, homes, warehouses, and commercial buildings.\",\"info\":\"It delivers clear 1080P high-definition video, intelligent human detection, and stable night monitoring performance.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\" IPC3612LB-AF28-A2\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\" 2MP Full HD Dome Camera \",\"mrp\":\"1.00\",\"note\":\"Use correct voltage to avoid camera damage.\\r\\nSecure camera properly to reduce vibration.\\r\\nAvoid direct water exposure.\\r\\nUse compatible video transmitter (VTX).\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":282,\"secondary_id\":283,\"brand_id\":128}]}','2026-02-26 10:34:35'),
(3130,1,'product',2623,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"Bullet Camera 2MP IPC2122LB AF40 A2\",\"description\":\"The Uniview IPC2122LB-AF40-A2 is a 2MP Full HD IP Bullet Camera designed for reliable outdoor and indoor CCTV surveillance.\",\"info\":\"It delivers clear 1080P high-definition video, strong night-vision performance, and intelligent monitoring features suitable for homes, offices, shops, warehouses, and commercial security systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[347],\"model\":\"IPC2122LB AF40 A2\",\"alternative_name\":\"2MP Full HD Bullet Camera\",\"mrp\":\"1\",\"note\":\"Ensure all cables are properly insulated and protected from water exposure or physical damage.\",\"base_image\":\"products/1772103053199-119494804.png\"}','2026-02-26 10:50:53'),
(3131,1,'product',555,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"1 Cell Lithium Charger\",\"description\":\"1 Cell Lithium Charger is an electronic charging module designed to safely charge a single lithium-ion (Li-ion) or lithium-polymer (Li-Po) battery cell, which typically has a nominal voltage of 3.7 V and a full charge voltage of 4.2 V. It operates using a controlled charging method known as Constant Current/Constant Voltage (CC/CV), where the charger first supplies a steady current to the battery and then maintains a fixed voltage of 4.2 V while gradually reducing the current as the battery reaches full capacity.\",\"info\":\"This method ensures safe and efficient charging while preventing overcharging, overheating, and battery damage. Most 1-cell lithium chargers accept a 5 V input supply through USB or DC input and are commonly used in power banks, small electronic projects, robotics kits, portable devices, and 18650 battery applications. Many modules include built-in protection features such as over-current protection, short-circuit protection, thermal regulation, and charge status indicators (LED lights showing charging and full charge status).\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"It is important to use the correct charging current, usually around 0.5C to 1C of the battery capacity, to maintain battery health and extend lifespan. Proper polarity connection (positive to B+ and negative to B–) must be ensured during installation. In system operation, the charger may include a pre-charge phase for deeply discharged batteries, followed by constant current charging, constant voltage topping, and automatic charge termination when the current drops to a small threshold value.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":82,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 11:04:27'),
(3132,1,'product',2257,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.012nF (12k)\",\"description\":\"The 0.012nF (12K) capacitor is a small-value ceramic capacitor commonly used in electronic circuits for high-frequency filtering, signal coupling, and noise suppression applications. The value 0.012nF is equal to 12 picofarads (12pF), which makes it suitable for RF circuits, oscillator circuits, tuning networks, and high-frequency signal processing. The marking “12K” typically indicates the capacitance value (12pF) and tolerance, where K represents a tolerance of ±10%\",\"info\":\"This type of capacitor is usually non-polarized, meaning it can be connected in any direction within a circuit. It is often available in ceramic disc or small SMD package form. Due to its very low capacitance value, it is mainly used in high-frequency and precision electronic applications rather than power filtering. The capacitor offers stable performance, low loss, and good reliability over a wide temperature range.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"Model demo11\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"It is widely used in RF transmitters and receivers, crystal oscillator circuits, communication devices, timing circuits, antenna matching networks, and general signal processing circuits. Because of its compact size and stable characteristics, the 12pF capacitor is a common component in communication and microcontroller-based systems.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":316,\"secondary_id\":442,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 11:06:51'),
(3133,1,'product',2258,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.022nF (22)\",\"description\":\"A 0.022 nF ceramic capacitor is equivalent to 22 pF and is usually marked as “22” on the capacitor body. It is a non-polarized capacitor made using a ceramic dielectric and is mainly used in high-frequency and RF applications.\",\"info\":\"The 0.022nF (22) capacitor is a small-value ceramic capacitor commonly used in electronic circuits for high-frequency filtering, signal coupling, and noise suppression applications. The capacitance value 0.022nF is equal to 22 picofarads (22pF), making it suitable for RF circuits, oscillator circuits, timing networks, and signal tuning applications. The marking “22” on the capacitor typically represents the capacitance value of 22pF according to standard capacitor coding.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"This capacitor is non-polarized, allowing it to be connected in any direction within a circuit. It is usually available in ceramic disc or surface-mount (SMD) form and provides stable electrical performance with low loss at high frequencies. Due to its very small capacitance value, it is mainly used in precision electronic circuits rather than power supply filtering.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":316,\"secondary_id\":442,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 11:07:07'),
(3134,1,'product',2256,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.039nF (39)\",\"description\":\"A 0.039 nF ceramic capacitor is equivalent to 39 pF and is typically marked “39” on the capacitor body. It is a non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric and is designed for high-frequency signal applications.\",\"info\":\"Typical voltage ratings include 50 V, 100 V, 250 V, and higher, making them suitable for low-current signal paths. Since it is non-polarized, it can be connected in either direction.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":316,\"secondary_id\":442,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 11:07:25'),
(3135,1,'product',2254,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.047nF (47)\",\"description\":\"A 0.047 nF ceramic capacitor is equivalent to 47 pF and is identified by the marking 47 on the capacitor body. It is a small-value, non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric, designed mainly for high-frequency applications.\",\"info\":\"Because of its very low capacitance, this value is commonly used in RF circuits, oscillators, tuning networks, and signal shaping applications. Ceramic capacitors of this value offer low loss, good stability, and fast response at high frequencies. They are most often found in ceramic disc (through-hole) form, though SMD versions are also available.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":316,\"secondary_id\":442,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 11:07:40'),
(3136,1,'product',2250,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.1nF (104)\",\"description\":\"A 0.1 µF (104) ceramic capacitor is one of the most widely used non-polarized capacitors in electronics. It uses a ceramic dielectric and is designed to store and release small amounts of electrical energy quickly, making it ideal for noise suppression and decoupling.\",\"info\":\"The code 104 means 10 × 10? pF = 100,000 pF, which equals 100 nF or 0.1 µF. These capacitors are available in ceramic disc (through-hole) and MLCC / SMD packages and offer excellent high-frequency performance, low ESR, and high reliability.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":316,\"secondary_id\":442,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 11:08:06'),
(3137,1,'product',2255,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.56nF (561)\",\"description\":\"A 0.56 nF (561) ceramic capacitor is a small-value, non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric to store electrical charge. The marking 561 represents 560 pF, calculated as 56 × 10¹ pF, which is equal to 0.56 nF.\",\"info\":\"This capacitor value is commonly available in ceramic disc (through-hole) and MLCC / SMD packages. It offers low loss, good frequency stability, and reliable performance at high frequencies, making it suitable for signal-level and RF applications. Typical voltage ratings range from 50 V to 500 V or higher for disc types, while MLCC versions usually range from 16 V to 100 V, depending on size and dielectric.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"A 0.56 nF (561) capacitor is a small-value ceramic capacitor commonly used in electronic circuits for filtering, timing, coupling, and noise suppression applications. The marking “561” follows the standard three-digit capacitor code system, where the first two digits represent the significant figures (56) and the third digit represents the number of zeros in picofarads (pF).\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":316,\"secondary_id\":442,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 11:09:12'),
(3138,1,'product',555,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"1 Cell Lithium Charger\",\"description\":\"1 Cell Lithium Charger is an electronic charging module designed to safely charge a single lithium-ion (Li-ion) or lithium-polymer (Li-Po) battery cell, which typically has a nominal voltage of 3.7 V and a full charge voltage of 4.2 V. It operates using a controlled charging method known as Constant Current/Constant Voltage (CC/CV), where the charger first supplies a steady current to the battery and then maintains a fixed voltage of 4.2 V while gradually reducing the current as the battery reaches full capacity.\",\"info\":\"This method ensures safe and efficient charging while preventing overcharging, overheating, and battery damage. Most 1-cell lithium chargers accept a 5 V input supply through USB or DC input and are commonly used in power banks, small electronic projects, robotics kits, portable devices, and 18650 battery applications. Many modules include built-in protection features such as over-current protection, short-circuit protection, thermal regulation, and charge status indicators (LED lights showing charging and full charge status).\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Lithium Charger\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"It is important to use the correct charging current, usually around 0.5C to 1C of the battery capacity, to maintain battery health and extend lifespan. Proper polarity connection (positive to B+ and negative to B–) must be ensured during installation. In system operation, the charger may include a pre-charge phase for deeply discharged batteries, followed by constant current charging, constant voltage topping, and automatic charge termination when the current drops to a small threshold value.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":82,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 11:09:40'),
(3139,1,'product',608,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"1 ohm Resistor\",\"description\":\"A 1 ohm resistor is a passive electronic component that provides a resistance value of exactly 1 Ω to control the flow of electric current in a circuit. It is designed to create a small voltage drop while allowing relatively high current to pass through, making it useful in current sensing and power regulation applications.\",\"info\":\"A 1 ohm resistor is a low-value fixed resistor with a resistance of 1 ohm, commonly used for current sensing, current limiting, and load balancing in electronic circuits. It is widely used in power circuits and DIY electronics projects.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"Resistor\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"49.00\",\"note\":\"A 1 ohm resistor is a very low-resistance electronic component used to limit current, measure current flow, or control power within a circuit. It provides a resistance value of 1 Ω, meaning it allows relatively high current to pass while creating a small voltage drop according to Ohm’s Law (V = I × R). Because the resistance value is low, 1 ohm resistors are commonly used as current-sensing (shunt) resistors in power supplies, battery management systems, motor drivers, LED circuits, and amplifier circuits.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":413,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 11:12:29'),
(3140,1,'product',2257,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.012nF (12k)\",\"description\":\"The 0.012nF (12K) capacitor is a small-value ceramic capacitor commonly used in electronic circuits for high-frequency filtering, signal coupling, and noise suppression applications. The value 0.012nF is equal to 12 picofarads (12pF), which makes it suitable for RF circuits, oscillator circuits, tuning networks, and high-frequency signal processing. The marking “12K” typically indicates the capacitance value (12pF) and tolerance, where K represents a tolerance of ±10%\",\"info\":\"This type of capacitor is usually non-polarized, meaning it can be connected in any direction within a circuit. It is often available in ceramic disc or small SMD package form. Due to its very low capacitance value, it is mainly used in high-frequency and precision electronic applications rather than power filtering. The capacitor offers stable performance, low loss, and good reliability over a wide temperature range.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"Model demo11\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"It is widely used in RF transmitters and receivers, crystal oscillator circuits, communication devices, timing circuits, antenna matching networks, and general signal processing circuits. Because of its compact size and stable characteristics, the 12pF capacitor is a common component in communication and microcontroller-based systems.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":316,\"secondary_id\":442,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 11:13:09'),
(3141,1,'product',2257,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.012nF (12k)\",\"description\":\"The 0.012nF (12K) capacitor is a small-value ceramic capacitor commonly used in electronic circuits for high-frequency filtering, signal coupling, and noise suppression applications. The value 0.012nF is equal to 12 picofarads (12pF), which makes it suitable for RF circuits, oscillator circuits, tuning networks, and high-frequency signal processing. The marking “12K” typically indicates the capacitance value (12pF) and tolerance, where K represents a tolerance of ±10%\",\"info\":\"This type of capacitor is usually non-polarized, meaning it can be connected in any direction within a circuit. It is often available in ceramic disc or small SMD package form. Due to its very low capacitance value, it is mainly used in high-frequency and precision electronic applications rather than power filtering. The capacitor offers stable performance, low loss, and good reliability over a wide temperature range.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"Model demo11\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"It is widely used in RF transmitters and receivers, crystal oscillator circuits, communication devices, timing circuits, antenna matching networks, and general signal processing circuits. Because of its compact size and stable characteristics, the 12pF capacitor is a common component in communication and microcontroller-based systems.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":316,\"secondary_id\":442,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 11:14:12'),
(3142,1,'product',2158,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"1.7m ohm Resistor\",\"description\":\"A 1.7M? (1.7 mega-ohm) resistor is a high-value fixed resistor used in electronic circuits where very low current flow or high impedance is required.\",\"info\":\"It provides a resistance of 1,700,000 ohms and is commonly used in signal sensing, biasing, timing, and protection circuits.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Resistor\",\"mrp\":\"49.00\",\"note\":\"A 1.7 MΩ (megaohm) resistor is a high-resistance electronic component that provides a resistance value of 1.7 million ohms (1,700,000 Ω). It is used to limit current flow to a very small amount and to create high-voltage drops with minimal current consumption in electronic circuits.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":316,\"secondary_id\":442,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 11:15:37'),
(3143,1,'product',1344,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"10 RELAY GSM with DTMF-TIMER- 7 INPUT Trigger\",\"description\":\"10 RELAY GSM board is designed on Renesas Microcontroller and SIM 800C SIMCOM GSM.\",\"info\":\"It supports all models SIM except JIO 4G LTE.\\r\\n\\r\\nIndividual relays can be controlled ON, OFF by sending SMS.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Relay Module\",\"mrp\":\"1000\",\"note\":\"A 10 Relay GSM with DTMF Timer – 7 Input Trigger is an advanced remote control switching system used to control multiple electrical devices through a mobile network. This device contains 10 independent relay outputs, allowing users to turn ON or OFF up to ten electrical loads such as lights, motors, pumps, generators, or industrial equipment.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":316,\"secondary_id\":442,\"brand_id\":230}]}','2026-02-26 11:26:21'),
(3144,1,'product',2454,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"100 RPM Motors\",\"description\":\"100 RPM motors are low-speed, high-torque geared motors widely used in robotics, automation, and DIY electronics projects.\",\"info\":\"Due to their stable speed, durability, and affordability, 100 RPM motors are a popular choice for both beginners and professional prototyping setups.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"100 RPM Motors\",\"mrp\":\"1.00\",\"note\":\"100 RPM Motors\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":316,\"secondary_id\":442,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 11:31:32'),
