(3150,1,'product',2256,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.039nF (39)\",\"description\":\"A 0.039 nF ceramic capacitor is equivalent to 39 pF and is typically marked “39” on the capacitor body. It is a non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric and is designed for high-frequency signal applications.\",\"info\":\"Typical voltage ratings include 50 V, 100 V, 250 V, and higher, making them suitable for low-current signal paths. Since it is non-polarized, it can be connected in either direction.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"A 0.039 nF (39) capacitor is a small-value capacitor commonly used in high-frequency and signal-processing circuits. The marking “39” follows the standard capacitor coding system, where the value is expressed directly in picofarads (pF) when only two digits are printed. Therefore, “39” represents 39 pF, which is equal to 0.039 nF (since 1000 pF = 1 nF).\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":415,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 11:55:10'),
(3151,1,'product',2254,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.047nF (47)\",\"description\":\"A 0.047 nF ceramic capacitor is equivalent to 47 pF and is identified by the marking 47 on the capacitor body. It is a small-value, non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric, designed mainly for high-frequency applications.\",\"info\":\"Because of its very low capacitance, this value is commonly used in RF circuits, oscillators, tuning networks, and signal shaping applications. Ceramic capacitors of this value offer low loss, good stability, and fast response at high frequencies. They are most often found in ceramic disc (through-hole) form, though SMD versions are also available.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"A 0.047 nF (47) capacitor is a very small-value capacitor commonly used in high-frequency electronic circuits. The marking “47” follows the standard capacitor code system where two digits indicate the value directly in picofarads (pF). Therefore, “47” means 47 pF, which is equal to 0.047 nF (since 1000 pF = 1 nF). This type of capacitor is typically non-polarized, so it can be connected in any direction in a circuit.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":415,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 11:56:09'),
(3152,1,'product',2250,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.1nF (104)\",\"description\":\"A 0.1 µF (104) ceramic capacitor is one of the most widely used non-polarized capacitors in electronics. It uses a ceramic dielectric and is designed to store and release small amounts of electrical energy quickly, making it ideal for noise suppression and decoupling.\",\"info\":\"The code 104 means 10 × 10? pF = 100,000 pF, which equals 100 nF or 0.1 µF. These capacitors are available in ceramic disc (through-hole) and MLCC / SMD packages and offer excellent high-frequency performance, low ESR, and high reliability.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"A 0.1 nF (104) capacitor description requires a small clarification: the marking “104” does not represent 0.1 nF. In the standard three-digit capacitor code system, 104 means 10 followed by 4 zeros in picofarads (pF), which equals 100,000 pF = 100 nF = 0.1 µF. Therefore, a capacitor marked 104 is actually 100 nF (0.1 microfarad), not 0.1 nF.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":416,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 12:03:12'),
(3153,1,'product',2255,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.56nF (561)\",\"description\":\"A 0.56 nF (561) ceramic capacitor is a small-value, non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric to store electrical charge. The marking 561 represents 560 pF, calculated as 56 × 10¹ pF, which is equal to 0.56 nF.\",\"info\":\"This capacitor value is commonly available in ceramic disc (through-hole) and MLCC / SMD packages. It offers low loss, good frequency stability, and reliable performance at high frequencies, making it suitable for signal-level and RF applications. Typical voltage ratings range from 50 V to 500 V or higher for disc types, while MLCC versions usually range from 16 V to 100 V, depending on size and dielectric.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"A 0.56 nF (561) capacitor is a small-value ceramic capacitor commonly used in electronic circuits for filtering, timing, coupling, and noise suppression applications. The marking “561” follows the standard three-digit capacitor code system, where the first two digits represent the significant figures (56) and the third digit represents the number of zeros in picofarads (pF).\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":416,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 12:15:08'),
(3154,1,'product',2256,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.039nF (39)\",\"description\":\"A 0.039 nF ceramic capacitor is equivalent to 39 pF and is typically marked “39” on the capacitor body. It is a non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric and is designed for high-frequency signal applications.\",\"info\":\"Typical voltage ratings include 50 V, 100 V, 250 V, and higher, making them suitable for low-current signal paths. Since it is non-polarized, it can be connected in either direction.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"A 0.039 nF (39) capacitor is a small-value capacitor commonly used in high-frequency and signal-processing circuits. The marking “39” follows the standard capacitor coding system, where the value is expressed directly in picofarads (pF) when only two digits are printed. Therefore, “39” represents 39 pF, which is equal to 0.039 nF (since 1000 pF = 1 nF).\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":416,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 12:15:37'),
(3155,1,'product',2258,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.022nF (22)\",\"description\":\"A 0.022 nF ceramic capacitor is equivalent to 22 pF and is usually marked as “22” on the capacitor body. It is a non-polarized capacitor made using a ceramic dielectric and is mainly used in high-frequency and RF applications.\",\"info\":\"The 0.022nF (22) capacitor is a small-value ceramic capacitor commonly used in electronic circuits for high-frequency filtering, signal coupling, and noise suppression applications. The capacitance value 0.022nF is equal to 22 picofarads (22pF), making it suitable for RF circuits, oscillator circuits, timing networks, and signal tuning applications. The marking “22” on the capacitor typically represents the capacitance value of 22pF according to standard capacitor coding.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"This capacitor is non-polarized, allowing it to be connected in any direction within a circuit. It is usually available in ceramic disc or surface-mount (SMD) form and provides stable electrical performance with low loss at high frequencies. Due to its very small capacitance value, it is mainly used in precision electronic circuits rather than power supply filtering.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":416,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 12:15:51'),
(3156,1,'product',2254,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.047nF (47)\",\"description\":\"A 0.047 nF ceramic capacitor is equivalent to 47 pF and is identified by the marking 47 on the capacitor body. It is a small-value, non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric, designed mainly for high-frequency applications.\",\"info\":\"Because of its very low capacitance, this value is commonly used in RF circuits, oscillators, tuning networks, and signal shaping applications. Ceramic capacitors of this value offer low loss, good stability, and fast response at high frequencies. They are most often found in ceramic disc (through-hole) form, though SMD versions are also available.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"A 0.047 nF (47) capacitor is a very small-value capacitor commonly used in high-frequency electronic circuits. The marking “47” follows the standard capacitor code system where two digits indicate the value directly in picofarads (pF). Therefore, “47” means 47 pF, which is equal to 0.047 nF (since 1000 pF = 1 nF). This type of capacitor is typically non-polarized, so it can be connected in any direction in a circuit.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":416,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 12:16:06'),
(3157,1,'product',2248,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"1.0nF (102)\",\"description\":\"A 1.0 nF (102) ceramic capacitor is a small-value, non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric to store electrical charge. The marking 102 represents 1000 pF, calculated as 10 × 10² pF. This value is widely used in electronic circuits where stable, low-loss capacitance is required.\",\"info\":\"A 1.0 nF ceramic capacitor is typically used for noise suppression, signal coupling, RF filtering, timing networks, and EMI/RFI reduction in analog, digital, and RF circuits. Because it is non-polarized, it can be connected in either direction and works well in AC signal paths.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Ceramic Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"A 1.0 nF (102) capacitor is a small-value capacitor commonly used in electronic circuits for signal filtering, timing, and frequency control applications. The marking “102” follows the standard three-digit capacitor code system, where the first two digits (10) represent the significant figures and the third digit (2) represents the number of zeros in picofarads (pF).\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":416,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 12:18:00'),
