(3180,1,'product',665,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"Tip127\",\"description\":\"The TIP127 is a PNP Darlington power transistor designed for high-current switching and amplification applications. It is commonly used in motor control, relay drivers, power switching, and load control circuits.\",\"info\":\"With its high current gain, it allows low-current signals to control high-power devices, making it ideal for power electronics projects.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"PNP Darlington transistor\",\"mrp\":\"199.00\",\"note\":\"Use heat sink for high current loads.\\r\\nBase resistor is required to limit input current.\\r\\nBeing PNP, polarity is opposite to NPN transistors.\\r\\nAvoid exceeding voltage and current ratings.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":414,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 12:54:33'),
(3181,1,'product',2171,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"102 NTC\",\"description\":\"The 102 NTC thermistor is a temperature-sensitive resistor whose resistance decreases as temperature increases. The “102” marking indicates a 10KΩ resistance at 25°C, making it widely used for temperature sensing and control applications\",\"info\":\"It provides accurate thermal response and stable performance in electronic circuits. This component is commonly used in battery chargers, power supplies, and temperature monitoring systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"102 NTC Thermistor\",\"mrp\":\"149.00\",\"note\":\"102 NTC thermistor is a Negative Temperature Coefficient (NTC) temperature-sensitive resistor with a nominal resistance of 1kΩ (1000 ohms) at 25°C. The marking “102” follows the standard three-digit code system, where the first two digits (10) are the significant figures and the third digit (2) represents the number of zeros. Therefore, 10 × 10² = 1000Ω = 1kΩ. Since it is an NTC type, its resistance decreases as temperature increases and increases as temperature decreases.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":546,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 12:54:47'),
(3182,1,'product',2173,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"103 NTC\",\"description\":\"The 103 NTC thermistor is a temperature-dependent resistor where resistance decreases as temperature increases. The “103” code represents 10KΩ resistance at 25°C, making it suitable for accurate temperature sensing and compensation circuits.\",\"info\":\"It offers fast thermal response, stable characteristics, and reliable performance in electronic devices. This thermistor is widely used in power supplies, battery chargers, and temperature control applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"198\",\"note\":\"103 NTC thermistor is a Negative Temperature Coefficient (NTC) temperature-sensitive resistor with a nominal resistance of 10kΩ (10,000 ohms) at 25°C. The marking “103” follows the standard three-digit code system, where the first two digits (10) represent the significant figures and the third digit (3) represents the number of zeros. Therefore, 10 × 10³ = 10,000Ω = 10kΩ. Since it is an NTC type thermistor, its resistance decreases as temperature increases and increases as temperature decreases.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":546,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 12:56:01'),
(3183,1,'product',2172,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"104 NTC\",\"description\":\"The 104 NTC thermistor is a temperature-sensitive resistor in which resistance decreases as temperature increases. The “104” marking indicates 100KΩ resistance at 25°C, making it suitable for precise temperature sensing and compensation circuits\",\"info\":\"It provides stable performance, high sensitivity, and fast thermal response. This thermistor is commonly used in battery chargers, power supplies, and temperature monitoring systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"NTC Thermistor\",\"mrp\":\"149.00\",\"note\":\"104 NTC thermistor is a Negative Temperature Coefficient (NTC) temperature-sensitive resistor with a nominal resistance of 100kΩ (100,000 ohms) at 25°C. The marking “104” follows the standard three-digit code system, where the first two digits (10) represent the significant figures and the third digit (4) indicates the number of zeros. Therefore, 10 × 10⁴ = 100,000Ω = 100kΩ. As an NTC thermistor, its resistance decreases when temperature increases and increases when temperature decreases.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":546,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 12:57:06'),
(3184,1,'product',2159,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"10m ohm Resistor\",\"description\":\"10 MΩ (megaohm) resistor is a very high-value resistor that provides a resistance of 10,000,000 ohms. Because of its large resistance, it allows only a very small amount of current to flow, making it suitable for low-current and high-impedance applications. It operates according to Ohm’s Law (V = I × R), where a high resistance results in minimal current even when voltage is applied. These resistors are typically available in carbon film, metal film, or surface-mount types, with tolerance ratings such as ±1%, ±5%, or ±10%.\",\"info\":\"It provides a resistance of 10,000,000 ohms, making it ideal for sensitive measurement and control applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Resistor\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"10 MΩ resistor is commonly used in voltage divider circuits, biasing networks for transistors and operational amplifiers, pull-up or pull-down configurations, sensor circuits, timing circuits (RC networks), and input protection circuits. It is especially useful in high-impedance signal applications, such as measuring small signals or preventing floating inputs in microcontroller systems. Since the current flowing through a 10 MΩ resistor is extremely small, power dissipation is usually very low, and it is commonly rated at ¼ watt or ½ watt.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":413,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 12:58:08'),
(3185,1,'product',2249,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"10nF (103)\",\"description\":\"A 10 nF (103) ceramic capacitor is a non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric to store electrical energy. The marking 103 corresponds to 10,000 pF, calculated as 10 × 10³ pF, which is equal to 10 nF or 0.01 µF. This value is very commonly used in general electronic circuits.\",\"info\":\"A 10 nF ceramic capacitor is widely used for noise filtering, signal coupling, decoupling, and EMI/RFI suppression. It is often placed near IC power pins, across signal lines, or in RC timing and filtering networks. Being non-polarized, it can be connected in either direction, making it suitable for both AC and DC applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"10nF (103) capacitor is a small-value non-polarized capacitor commonly used in filtering, coupling, timing, and noise suppression applications. The marking “103” follows the standard three-digit capacitor code system, where the first two digits (10) are the significant figures and the third digit (3) represents the number of zeros in picofarads (pF). Therefore, 10 × 10³ = 10,000 pF, which equals 10nF (0.01µF). This type of capacitor is typically available as a ceramic disc or multilayer ceramic capacitor (MLCC) and can be connected in any direction since it is non-polarized.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":415,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 12:59:11'),
(3186,1,'product',2178,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"10uF 160V Capacitor\",\"description\":\"10µF 160V capacitor is a high-voltage polarized electrolytic capacitor used for energy storage, filtering, and voltage stabilization in high-voltage DC circuits. The capacitance value of 10 microfarads (µF) indicates its ability to store electrical charge, while the 160V rating means it can safely operate at voltages up to 160 volts. Since it is an electrolytic capacitor, it has clearly marked positive (+) and negative (–) terminals, and correct polarity must always be maintained during installation to prevent leakage, overheating, or failure.\",\"info\":\"It is also recommended to discharge the capacitor safely before handling. From a system perspective, the 10µF 160V capacitor improves voltage stability, reduces ripple noise, supports load regulation, and enhances reliability in high-voltage electronic systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"199.00\",\"note\":\"This capacitor is commonly used in SMPS power supplies, inverter circuits, LED driver circuits, high-voltage amplifier sections, industrial equipment, and rectified AC mains filtering applications. It is often placed after a rectifier to smooth high-voltage DC output by reducing ripple and maintaining a stable voltage. It stores energy during voltage peaks and releases it when the voltage drops, helping ensure consistent system operation.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":415,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 13:00:14'),
(3187,1,'product',2189,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"10uF 250V Capacitor\",\"description\":\"10µF 250V capacitor is a high-voltage polarized electrolytic capacitor used for energy storage, filtering, and voltage stabilization in high-voltage DC circuits. The capacitance value of 10 microfarads (µF) indicates its charge storage capability, while the 250V rating means it can safely operate at voltages up to 250 volts. Because it is an electrolytic capacitor, it has clearly marked positive (+) and negative (–) terminals, and correct polarity must be maintained during installation to prevent leakage, overheating, or explosion.\",\"info\":\"This value is commonly available as an aluminum electrolytic capacitor (polarized) and, in some cases, as a film capacitor (non-polarized).\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Capacitor\",\"mrp\":\"199.00\",\"note\":\"This capacitor is commonly used in SMPS power supplies, inverter circuits, industrial power equipment, LED drivers, audio amplifier power sections, and rectified AC mains filtering applications. It is often placed after a bridge rectifier to smooth high-voltage DC output by reducing ripple voltage and stabilizing the supply. It stores energy during voltage peaks and releases it when voltage drops, helping maintain steady system performance.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":415,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 13:02:02'),
(3188,1,'product',2553,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"1100mah battery\",\"description\":\"1100mAh battery is a rechargeable or non-rechargeable power source with a capacity of 1100 milliampere-hours, meaning it can theoretically supply 1100 milliamps (1.1A) for one hour, 550mA for two hours, or lower current for a longer duration depending on load conditions. These batteries are commonly available in chemistries such as Lithium-ion (Li-ion), Lithium-polymer (Li-Po), Nickel-Metal Hydride (NiMH), and sometimes Nickel-Cadmium (NiCd). In most electronics and robotics applications, 1100mAh Li-ion or Li-Po batteries are popular due to their high energy density, lightweight design, and stable output voltage (typically 3.7V nominal for single-cell lithium types).\",\"info\":\"It is widely used in portable electronics, IoT devices, DIY projects, robotics, and backup power applications where moderate runtime is required while keeping size and weight low.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Lithium Battery\",\"mrp\":\"10.00\",\"note\":\"When integrating a 1100mAh battery into a circuit, always use a protection circuit module (PCM/BMS) for lithium types to safeguard against over-voltage, under-voltage, and over-current conditions. Ensure proper voltage regulation using buck or boost converters if the system requires stable 5V or 12V output. Consider the device’s total current consumption to estimate backup time using the formula: Backup Time (hours) ≈ Battery Capacity (mAh) ÷ Load Current (mA).\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":408,\"secondary_id\":\"62\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 13:21:57'),
(3189,1,'category',18,'update',NULL,NULL,'2026-02-26 13:23:41'),
(3190,1,'product',2513,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"110mah Battery\",\"description\":\"A 110mAh battery is a small-capacity rechargeable battery commonly used in compact electronic devices. The term 110mAh (milliampere-hour) indicates that the battery can supply 110 milliamps for 1 hour, or lower current for a longer duration (for example, 55mA for 2 hours). These batteries are most commonly available in Lithium-ion (Li-ion) or Lithium-Polymer (Li-Po) chemistry with a nominal voltage of 3.7V and a fully charged voltage of 4.2V.\",\"info\":\"While not suitable for high-current applications, a 110 mAh battery provides efficient backup and short-duration power for low-energy electronics.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Lithium Battery\",\"mrp\":\"399.00\",\"note\":\"This type of battery is mainly used in Bluetooth headsets, small IoT modules, wearable devices, mini drones, MP3 players, smart bands, and microcontroller-based compact projects. Due to its small size and lightweight design, it is ideal for portable and space-constrained applications.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":408,\"secondary_id\":\"62\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 13:27:43'),
(3191,1,'product',297,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"DWIN Display 12.1inch DMG 12800 Y121 01 NC\",\"description\":\"The DMG12800Y121_01NC is a 12.1-inch industrial-grade TFT LCD module featuring a 1280×800 high-resolution display.\\r\\nDesigned for industrial control systems, embedded devices, and automation panels, this non-touch display provides sharp visuals, wide viewing angles, and long-life reliability in demanding environments.\",\"info\":\"The 12.1inch DMG12800Y121_01NC is a 12.1-inch 1280 × 800 pixel TN-TFT LCD display with a capacitive touch panel, designed for HMI (Human-Machine Interface) and commercial display applications\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"DWIN Display\",\"mrp\":\"11500.00\",\"note\":\"Designed for industrial control systems, embedded devices, and automation panels, this non-touch display provides sharp visuals, wide viewing angles, and long-life reliability in demanding environments.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":436,\"secondary_id\":\"40\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 13:29:02'),
