(3230,1,'product',440,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"12mm LDR Sensor\",\"description\":\"12mm LDR (Light Dependent Resistor) Sensor is a light-sensitive device whose resistance changes based on the amount of light falling on its surface. The 12mm size refers to the diameter of the sensing surface, which provides better light detection and higher sensitivity compared to smaller LDRs.\",\"info\":\"12 mm LDR Sensor (Light Dependent Resistor) is a photosensitive component whose resistance decreases as light intensity increases\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":78,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 14:48:53'),
(3231,1,'product',2540,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"1264TEP1 thermoelectric cooling module\",\"description\":\"The 1264TEP1 is a thermoelectric cooling module (commonly similar to TEC1-12604 type) based on the Peltier effect. It is designed to create a temperature difference when DC power is applied. When current flows through the module, one side becomes cold while the opposite side becomes hot. This module is widely used in small cooling systems, mini refrigerators, water coolers, CPU cooling experiments, medical storage boxes, and scientific projects.\",\"info\":\"It’s part of a family of Bismuth-Telluride (Bi-Te) thermoelectric modules designed to convert heat directly into electrical power using the Seebeck effect when a temperature difference is applied across the device\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Thermoelectric cooling module\",\"mrp\":\"399\",\"note\":\"The device operates based on the Peltier Effect, where heat is transferred between two different materials when electric current passes through them. Reversing the polarity will swap the hot and cold sides.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":165,\"secondary_id\":\"550\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 14:50:05'),
(3232,1,'product',2543,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"12704 Peltier\",\"description\":\"The 12704 Peltier module (commonly labeled TEC1-12704) is a thermoelectric cooling device that works based on the Peltier effect. When DC voltage is applied, one side of the module becomes cold while the opposite side becomes hot. It is widely used in small cooling systems, portable refrigerators, electronic cooling applications, and DIY thermal projects.\",\"info\":\"These modules are common in DIY refrigeration, electronics temperature control, and small cooling projects\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Thermoelectric cooling\",\"mrp\":\"396\",\"note\":\"The module contains multiple P-type and N-type semiconductor junctions sandwiched between ceramic plates. When current flows through the junctions, heat is absorbed on one side and released on the other. Reversing the polarity swaps the hot and cold sides.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":165,\"secondary_id\":\"550\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 14:52:20'),
(3233,1,'product',2542,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"12706 Peltier\",\"description\":\"The 12706 Peltier module (commonly marked as TEC1-12706) is a thermoelectric cooling device that operates using the Peltier effect. When DC power is applied, one side of the module becomes cold while the opposite side becomes hot. It is widely used in mini refrigerators, water coolers, CPU cooling systems, laboratory devices, and portable cooling applications.\",\"info\":\"One side becomes cold while the other becomes hot, allowing you to cool or heat small spaces or components.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Thermoelectric cooling module\",\"mrp\":\"399\",\"note\":\"The module consists of multiple P-type and N-type semiconductor elements placed between two ceramic plates. When current flows, heat is absorbed from one surface (cold side) and transferred to the other surface (hot side). Reversing the power polarity swaps the heating and cooling sides.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":165,\"secondary_id\":\"550\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 14:53:51'),
(3234,1,'product',440,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"12mm LDR Sensor\",\"description\":\"12mm LDR (Light Dependent Resistor) Sensor is a light-sensitive device whose resistance changes based on the amount of light falling on its surface. The 12mm size refers to the diameter of the sensing surface, which provides better light detection and higher sensitivity compared to smaller LDRs.\",\"info\":\"12 mm LDR Sensor (Light Dependent Resistor) is a photosensitive component whose resistance decreases as light intensity increases\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":78,\"secondary_id\":\"549\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-26 14:54:01'),
