(3381,1,'product',240,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"VOICE 8  Record/Playback  Module\",\"description\":\"The VOICE 8 Record/Playback Module is an electronic audio module designed for recording and playing back voice messages or sound clips in embedded and automation projects. It allows users to record audio directly through an onboard microphone and replay the stored voice using push buttons or external trigger signals. The module typically supports multiple recording channels (up to 8 separate voice messages), making it suitable for applications that require different audio prompts or alerts.\",\"info\":\"The module includes a built-in microphone for recording, onboard memory for storing audio data, and an audio output stage capable of driving a small speaker directly. Recording and playback operations are controlled through dedicated buttons or digital input pins, allowing easy interfacing with microcontrollers such as Arduino, ESP8266, ESP32, or other control systems. It operates on a low DC voltage supply (usually 3V–5V) and consumes minimal power, making it suitable for portable and battery-powered devices.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"950.00\",\"note\":\"VOICE 8 record/playback modules are widely used in voice announcement systems, talking toys, security alarms, automation alerts, educational devices, interactive projects, and embedded audio notification systems. Due to simple operation, compact size, and easy integration, the module provides a convenient solution for adding voice feedback to electronic projects.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":165,\"secondary_id\":\"63\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-02-28 07:27:53'),
(3382,1,'brand',288,'create',NULL,'{\"user_id\":\"1\",\"brand_name\":\"Videocon\",\"description\":\"Videocon is a well-known Indian consumer electronics and home appliances brand that was founded in 1979 by Venugopal Dhoot. The company became one of India’s leading manufacturers of televisions, refrigerators, washing machines, air conditioners, and other household appliances. For many years, Videocon was recognized for providing affordable and reliable products across urban and rural markets in India.\",\"info\":\"During its peak period, Videocon expanded into multiple sectors including consumer electronics, oil & gas exploration, telecom services, and DTH (Direct-to-Home) broadcasting. Its DTH service operated under the brand Videocon d2h, offering digital TV services with HD channels and interactive features. Later, Videocon d2h merged with Dish TV to strengthen its position in the DTH market.\",\"note\":\"\",\"system_note\":\"\",\"icon_text\":\"\",\"link\":\"\",\"status\":\"active\",\"image\":\"brands/1772264387427-873868986.png\"}','2026-02-28 07:39:47'),
