(3595,1,'product',2544,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"320Mah battery\",\"description\":\"A 320mAh battery is a small-capacity rechargeable battery commonly used in compact electronic devices such as Bluetooth headsets, smart bands, mini speakers, toys, and IoT modules. The term mAh (milliampere-hour) represents the battery capacity, meaning a 320mAh battery can theoretically supply 320 milliamps of current for one hour, or 160 milliamps for about two hours, depending on the device load. The actual backup time varies based on power consumption and operating conditions.\",\"info\":\"Most 320mAh batteries are Lithium-ion (Li-ion) or Lithium-polymer (Li-Po) types because they are lightweight, rechargeable, and offer good energy density. These batteries usually have a nominal voltage of 3.7V and a full charge voltage of 4.2V. They are designed for low-power applications and typically support several hundred charge cycles if properly maintained.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Lithium Battery\",\"mrp\":\"499\",\"note\":\"320mAh battery include its key technical specifications and operating conditions. It is typically a Lithium-ion (Li-ion) or Lithium-polymer (Li-Po) rechargeable battery with a nominal voltage of 3.7V and a full charge voltage of 4.2V.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":408,\"secondary_id\":\"62\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-02 11:30:52'),
