(3878,1,'product',319,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"ESP8266-01 Base Board\",\"description\":\"Ready to use ESP-01 WIFI Board.\\r\\nOn board 3.3v regulator & power indicator LED.\\r\\nRx level converted to 3.3v , can be used directly with Arduino\\r\\nAll GPIO pins extended using berg pins .\",\"info\":\"The ESP8266-01 itself is a tiny Wi-Fi module with an integrated TCP/IP stack and 3.3 V Wi-Fi SoC that supports 802.11 b/g/n wireless networking and can be commanded via UART/serial or even programmed directly for standalone Wi-Fi tasks.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"499.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":86,\"secondary_id\":\"443\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:21:20'),
(3879,1,'product',2150,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"ESP8266 wifi Module\",\"description\":\"The ESP8266 WiFi Module is a compact and cost-effective wireless microcontroller module developed by Espressif Systems, widely used in Internet of Things (IoT) and embedded electronics projects. It features a built-in TCP/IP protocol stack and integrated Wi-Fi capability based on the IEEE 802.11 b/g/n standard, allowing devices to connect directly to wireless networks and communicate with servers, mobile applications, or cloud platforms without requiring additional networking hardware.\",\"info\":\"The ESP8266 offers multiple GPIO pins along with communication interfaces such as UART, SPI, and I2C, enabling easy integration with sensors, relays, displays, and other peripherals. It operates at 3.3V and includes several power-saving modes, making it suitable for low-power and battery-operated applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"999.00\",\"note\":\"The module can function in Station mode, Access Point mode, or both simultaneously, providing flexibility for wireless networking solutions. Programmable using Arduino IDE, NodeMCU firmware, MicroPython, or AT commands, the ESP8266 WiFi Module is commonly used in smart home automation, wireless monitoring systems, IoT devices, and remote control applications due to its small size, affordability, and dependable wireless performance.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":165,\"secondary_id\":\"145\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:21:55'),
(3880,1,'product',314,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"ESP32-S3 zero Mini Development Board\",\"description\":\"ESP32-S3 Zero Mini Development Board is a compact, low-cost microcontroller board powered by the ESP32-S3 dual-core processor, featuring 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi and Bluetooth LE connectivity\",\"info\":\"Designed for space-constrained IoT and embedded applications, it includes onboard USB-C for programming and power, ample GPIO pins for sensors and peripherals, and typically Flash memory + PSRAM for efficient code execution and data handling. It’s ideal for wireless IoT nodes, wearable devices, sensor hubs, and smart home projects, and can be programmed using Arduino IDE, ESP-IDF, or MicroPython.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"600.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":86,\"secondary_id\":\"177\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:22:25'),
(3881,1,'product',2575,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"6x4 PCB Board\",\"description\":\"A 6x4 PCB board refers to a printed circuit board with dimensions of 6 cm × 4 cm or sometimes 6 inch × 4 inch, depending on the specification. It is commonly used as a base platform for assembling and soldering electronic components in DIY and prototype circuits. The board is typically made of FR4 (fiber-reinforced epoxy laminate) or phenolic material and coated with a thin copper layer for creating circuit connections.\",\"info\":\"6x4 PCB boards are available in single-sided, double-sided, and general-purpose perforated (zero PCB) types. Single-sided boards have copper on one side only, while double-sided boards have copper layers on both sides for more complex circuit layouts. Zero PCBs feature evenly spaced holes (usually 2.54mm pitch) that allow components like resistors, capacitors, ICs, transistors, and connectors to be manually soldered.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"PCB Board\",\"mrp\":\"399\",\"note\":\"This size is suitable for medium-sized electronic projects, power supply circuits, Arduino and microcontroller-based projects, robotics modules, amplifier circuits, and educational lab experiments. The 6x4 size provides more working area compared to smaller boards, allowing better component spacing and organized layout inside enclosures.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":465,\"secondary_id\":\"564\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:22:30'),
(3882,1,'product',805,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"ESP32-CAM-MB Micro USB Download Module\",\"description\":\"The ESP32-CAM-MB is a convenient USB-to-ESP32-CAM programming and power interface module designed to make uploading code to the ESP32-CAM quick and hassle-free. It includes an onboard CH340/CH9102 USB-to-Serial converter and a Micro USB port, eliminating the need for external FTDI programmers or jumper wires.\",\"info\":\"This module allows you to easily program and power the ESP32-CAM using a Micro-USB cable, eliminating the need for external USB-to-TTL converters or manual wiring. It features an onboard USB-to-serial interface and auto-boot circuitry, making firmware uploading simple and reliable through the Arduino IDE or other ESP32 tools.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"999.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":86,\"secondary_id\":\"443\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:23:01'),
(3883,1,'product',2264,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"6V DC Lithium battery\",\"description\":\"A 6V DC lithium battery is a compact, high-efficiency power source designed to deliver a stable 6-volt direct current (DC) output. It is typically made by combining two 3.0V or 3.6/3.7V lithium cells in series and may include a built-in Battery Management System (BMS) for protection.\",\"info\":\"Compared to traditional lead-acid or NiMH batteries, lithium batteries offer higher energy density, lighter weight, and longer life, making them ideal for modern electronic and portable applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Lithium Battery\",\"mrp\":\"399\",\"note\":\"It is typically made by combining two 3.0V or 3.6/3.7V lithium cells in series and may include a built-in Battery Management System (BMS) for protection.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":408,\"secondary_id\":\"62\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:23:18'),
(3884,1,'product',315,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"ESP32-C3 Super Mini USB C - Development Board\",\"description\":\"Compact & Lightweight – Fits into tight spaces without compromising performance\\r\\nWi-Fi 4 & Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) – Reliable wireless communication for IoT applications\",\"info\":\"The ESP32-C3 Super Mini USB-C Development Board is a compact and feature-rich microcontroller board based on the ESP32-C3 RISC-V core, offering 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi and Bluetooth LE 5.0 connectivity.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"499.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":86,\"secondary_id\":\"177\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:23:40'),
(3885,1,'product',2149,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"ESP32 Wifi Module\",\"description\":\"The ESP32 WiFi Module is a powerful and low-cost microcontroller module developed by Espressif Systems, designed for advanced Internet of Things (IoT) and embedded applications. It integrates both Wi-Fi and Bluetooth (Classic and BLE) connectivity in a single chip, enabling wireless communication between devices, cloud servers, and mobile applications.\",\"info\":\"The ESP32 includes multiple GPIO pins and supports various communication interfaces such as UART, SPI, I2C, PWM, ADC, and DAC, allowing easy connection with sensors, displays, relays, and other electronic components. It operates at 3.3V and features low power consumption modes, making it ideal for battery-powered and energy-efficient projects\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"1999.00\",\"note\":\"Widely used in smart home automation, industrial monitoring, wearable devices, robotics, wireless data logging, and remote control systems, the ESP32 WiFi Module can be programmed using Arduino IDE, MicroPython, or ESP-IDF development framework. Its combination of high processing power, wireless connectivity, flexible interfaces, and affordability makes it one of the most popular microcontroller modules for modern IoT development.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":165,\"secondary_id\":\"145\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:24:12'),
