(3906,1,'product',1094,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"7406\",\"description\":\"The 7406 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit that contains six independent inverters (NOT gates) with open-collector outputs.Each inverter outputs the logical opposite of its input, but unlike standard inverter ICs, the open-collector design allows the outputs to sink higher current and interface with higher-voltage loads using an external pull-up resistor.\",\"info\":\"The 7406 contains six independent inverters with open-collector outputs, allowing it to drive higher-voltage loads, relays, or LEDs using external pull-up resistors. It is especially useful for level interfacing and bus driving where wired-OR logic is needed.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"7406\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"7406 IC\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"Each inverter outputs the logical opposite of its input, but unlike standard inverter ICs, the open-collector design allows the outputs to sink higher current and interface with higher-voltage loads using an external pull-up resistor.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:47:01'),
(3907,1,'product',1095,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"7407\",\"description\":\"7407 IC is a TTL hex non-inverting buffer/driver with open-collector outputs, designed for interfacing logic circuits with higher-voltage or higher-current loads. It contains six independent buffer stages that reproduce the input logic level at the output without inversion. \",\"info\":\"The 7407 contains six independent non-inverting buffers with open-collector outputs, allowing it to drive higher-voltage loads, LEDs, or relays using external pull-up resistors. It is commonly used for level interfacing, signal buffering, and wired-OR applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"7407\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"7407\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"Because of its open-collector configuration, the outputs require external pull-up resistors and can be connected to voltages higher than the IC’s supply, making the 7407 ideal for driving relays, lamps, LEDs, and other external devices.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:49:34'),
(3908,1,'product',1102,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74123\",\"description\":\"74123 IC is a dual retriggerable monostable multivibrator from the TTL 74-series, designed to generate precise timing pulses. It contains two independent one-shot circuits, each capable of producing a stable output pulse whose width is determined by external resistor (R) and capacitor (C) values.\",\"info\":\"The 74123 contains two independent retriggerable one-shot timers. Each section can generate a precise output pulse whose width is set by an external resistor and capacitor (RC). Because it is retriggerable, a new trigger arriving before the timing cycle ends will extend the output pulse, making it useful for pulse shaping and timing control.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74123\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74123\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"The 74123 can be retriggered during the output pulse, which extends the pulse duration as long as trigger inputs continue making it ideal for pulse stretching and noise filtering.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:51:04'),
(3909,1,'product',1103,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74174\",\"description\":\"74174 IC is a hex D-type flip-flop from the TTL 74-series, designed for parallel data storage and transfer. It contains six independent D flip-flops that share a common clock (CLK) and an asynchronous clear (CLR) input. On the rising edge of the clock, data present at each D input is simultaneously latched and transferred to the corresponding Q output. \",\"info\":\"The 74123 contains two independent retriggerable one-shot timers. Each section can generate a precise output pulse whose width is set by an external resistor and capacitor (RC). Because it is retriggerable, a new trigger arriving before the timing cycle ends will extend the output pulse, making it useful for pulse shaping and timing control.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74174\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74174\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"The asynchronous clear resets all outputs to logic LOW regardless of the clock state, which is useful for system initialization.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:51:53'),
(3910,1,'product',1098,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74ALS175\",\"description\":\"The 74ALS175 IC is a quad D-type flip-flop with a common clock and asynchronous clear, belonging to the Advanced Low-Power Schottky (ALS) TTL family. It contains four independent D flip-flops, each storing one bit of data. On the rising edge of the clock, the data present at each D input is transferred to its corresponding Q output simultaneously.\",\"info\":\"The 74ALS175 contains four edge-triggered D flip-flops that store data on the rising edge of the clock. An active-LOW asynchronous clear resets all outputs simultaneously. Built using ALS (Advanced Low-power Schottky) TTL technology, it offers faster switching and lower power consumption than standard LS devices.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74ALS175\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74ALS175\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"The asynchronous clear (CLR) input resets all outputs to logic LOW regardless of the clock state, making it useful for system initialization.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:52:38'),
(3911,1,'product',1638,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74CH595\",\"description\":\"The 74HC595 is an 8-bit serial-in, parallel-out shift register IC widely used to expand digital output pins in microcontroller and digital logic applications. It allows multiple outputs to be controlled using only a few input pins by shifting data serially and then outputting it in parallel.\",\"info\":\"The IC includes an internal storage register and output latches, enabling stable and synchronized output control. Operating at high speed with low power consumption, the 74HC595 is commonly used for driving LEDs, seven-segment displays, relays, and other digital loads in Arduino, robotics, and embedded systems projects.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74CH595 IC\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"74HC595 is commonly used for driving LEDs, seven-segment displays, relays, and other digital loads in Arduino, robotics, and embedded systems projects.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":73,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:53:47'),
(3912,1,'product',1099,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74F10\",\"description\":\"74F10 IC is a triple 3-input NAND gate from the Fast TTL (74F) logic family, designed for high-speed digital applications. It contains three independent NAND gates, each accepting three inputs and producing a LOW output only when all three inputs are HIGH. Compared to standard 74LS devices, the 74F10 offers significantly faster propagation delays, making it suitable for high-frequency logic circuits.\",\"info\":\"The 74F10 contains three independent NAND gates, each with three inputs, providing very high-speed switching performance compared to LS devices. It is used in digital logic circuits where fast propagation delay is critical.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74F10\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74F10\",\"mrp\":\"10.00\",\"note\":\"Compared to standard 74LS devices, the 74F10 offers significantly faster propagation delays, making it suitable for high-frequency logic circuits.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:55:36'),
(3913,1,'product',1101,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74F521\",\"description\":\"74F521 IC is an 8-bit identity comparator from the Fast TTL (74F) logic family, designed for high-speed digital comparison applications. It compares two 8-bit binary words (A0–A7 and B0–B7) and produces an equality output (A = B) when all corresponding bits are identical.\",\"info\":\"The 74F521 compares two 8-bit binary words and provides an output indicating whether the two values are exactly equal. Designed with Fast TTL technology, it offers very low propagation delay, making it suitable for high-speed comparison tasks in digital systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74F521\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74F521\",\"mrp\":\"10.00\",\"note\":\"The device also includes cascade inputs and outputs, allowing multiple 74F521 ICs to be connected together for comparing larger word lengths such as 16-bit or 32-bit data.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:56:11'),
(3914,1,'product',1002,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HC02\",\"description\":\"The 74HC02 is a high-speed CMOS quad 2-input NOR gate integrated circuit. It contains four independent NOR gates, each with two inputs and one output, fabricated using HC (High-speed CMOS) technology.\",\"info\":\"The 74HC02 is a high-speed CMOS logic IC that contains four independent 2-input NOR gates in a single package. Each gate performs the NOR logic function, producing a HIGH output only when all inputs are LOW.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HC02\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HC02 IC\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"Designed using high-speed CMOS technology, the IC provides low power consumption along with fast switching performance, making it suitable for digital logic circuits and embedded systems.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:57:24'),
(3915,1,'product',1003,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HC04\",\"description\":\"74HC04IN is a high-speed CMOS hex inverter (NOT gate) IC from the 74HC logic family. It contains six independent inverters that convert a logic HIGH input into a logic LOW output and vice versa.\",\"info\":\"The 74HC04 is a high-speed CMOS logic IC that contains six independent inverter (NOT) gates in a single package. Each inverter outputs the logical opposite of its input signal, converting HIGH to LOW and LOW to HIGH.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HC04\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HC04\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"Designed with low power consumption and fast switching characteristics, the 74HC04 is widely used in digital logic circuits, signal conditioning, waveform generation, and oscillator applications\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:58:09'),
(3916,1,'product',1006,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HC08\",\"description\":\"The 74HC08 is a high-speed CMOS IC that contains four independent 2-input AND logic gates in a single 14-pin package. Each gate performs the logical AND operation, meaning the output becomes HIGH only when both inputs are HIGH.\",\"info\":\"The 74HC08 is a high-speed CMOS logic IC that contains four independent 2-input AND gates in a single package. Each gate performs the AND logic function, producing a HIGH output only when both inputs are HIGH.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HC08\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HC08\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"Built using CMOS technology, the IC offers low power consumption, fast switching speed, and high noise immunity, making it suitable for modern digital circuits.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:59:21'),
(3917,1,'product',1011,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HC10\",\"description\":\"The 74HC10 is a high-speed CMOS logic integrated circuit that contains three independent 3-input NAND gates in a single package.\",\"info\":\"74HC10 is a high-speed CMOS logic IC that contains three independent 3-input NAND gates in a single package\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HC10\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HC10\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates over a wide supply voltage range (typically 2 V to 6 V) and offers low power consumption with fast switching speed.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 07:59:59'),
(3918,1,'product',1024,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HC126\",\"description\":\"The 74HC126 is a high-speed CMOS quad non-inverting buffer with three-state outputs, designed for digital signal buffering and bus interfacing applications\",\"info\":\"74HC126 is a high-speed CMOS logic IC that contains four independent non-inverting buffer gates with 3-state (tri-state) outputs.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HC126\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HC126\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates over a wide supply voltage range (2 V to 6 V) and offers low power consumption with fast switching.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:00:36'),
(3919,1,'product',1031,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HC133\",\"description\":\"The 74HC133 is a High-Speed CMOS 13-input NAND gate IC from the 74HC logic family, designed to perform a NAND operation on thirteen digital input signals\",\"info\":\"74HC133 is a high-speed CMOS logic IC that contains a single 13-input NAND gate\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HC133\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HC133\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates over a wide supply voltage range (2 V to 6 V) and offers low power consumption with fast switching performance.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:01:16'),
(3920,1,'product',1033,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HC138\",\"description\":\"The 74HC138 is a high-speed CMOS 3-to-8 line decoder/demultiplexer widely used in digital electronics for address decoding and device selection.\",\"info\":\"74HC138 is a high-speed CMOS 3-to-8 line decoder/demultiplexer IC. It takes 3 binary input lines and decodes them into one of eight active-LOW outputs, with three enable pins for flexible control\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HC138\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HC138\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates over a wide supply voltage range (2 V to 6 V) and has low power consumption.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:01:49'),
(3921,1,'product',1017,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HC14\",\"description\":\"The 74HC14 is a hex Schmitt trigger inverter IC from the high-speed CMOS (HC) logic family, containing six independent inverters with built-in Schmitt trigger inputs.\",\"info\":\"74HC14 is a high-speed CMOS logic IC that contains six inverters with Schmitt trigger inputs\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HC14\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HC14\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates over a wide supply voltage range (2 V to 6 V) and provides noise immunity and clean signal switching, even with slow or noisy input signals.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:02:23'),
(3922,1,'product',1079,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HC148\",\"description\":\"The 74HC148 is an 8-to-3 priority encoder from the high-speed CMOS (HC) logic family, designed to encode up to eight active-LOW input signals into a 3-bit binary output.\",\"info\":\"The 74HC148 encodes eight active-LOW input signals into a 3-bit binary output, giving priority to the highest-order input when multiple inputs are active at the same time.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HC148\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HC148\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"Built using High-Speed CMOS (HC) technology, it offers low power consumption and high noise immunity compared to TTL devices.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}],\"base_image\":\"products/1772525087510-478343866.jpeg\"}','2026-03-03 08:04:47'),
(3923,1,'product',317,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"ESP32 CAMERA MODULE\",\"description\":\"?Useful?The HK-ESP32-CAM-MB module is a small camera module with a size of 39.8MM*27MM,our esp32 cam can work independently as smallest system and also Support secondary development.\",\"info\":\"Versatile ESP32-CAM board with onboard micro USB (CH-340) for easy programming, Wi-Fi + Bluetooth, and 2 MP OV2640 camera — great for DIY IP camera, streaming, image capture, and IoT projects.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"1999.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":86,\"secondary_id\":\"570\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:10:20'),
(3924,1,'product',316,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"ESP 8266-01 Module\",\"description\":\"NodeMCU is built based on the mature ESP8266 technology to take advantage the abundant resources available on the web.\\r\\n11 digital input/output pins, all pins have interrupt/pwm/12C/one-wire supported(except DO)\",\"info\":\"The ESP8266-01 is a small, low-cost Wi-Fi module based on the ESP8266 SoC that adds 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi connectivity to microcontroller projects\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"1499.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":86,\"secondary_id\":\"570\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:12:42'),
(3925,1,'product',2148,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"ESP 8266- mini wifi module\",\"description\":\"The ESP8266 Mini WiFi Module is a compact and low-cost wireless microcontroller module widely used for Internet of Things (IoT) and embedded system applications. It is based on the ESP8266 chipset developed by Espressif Systems and provides built-in Wi-Fi networking capability, allowing devices to connect directly to wireless networks without requiring an external microcontroller\",\"info\":\"The module operates on the IEEE 802.11 b/g/n standard and supports TCP/IP protocol stack, enabling communication with web servers, mobile applications, and cloud platforms. It features a 32-bit microprocessor running at up to 80/160 MHz, digital GPIO pins, UART, SPI, and I2C interfaces for connecting sensors and peripherals.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"999.00\",\"note\":\"The ESP8266 Mini supports multiple operating modes such as Station mode, Access Point mode, and both combined, making it flexible for smart home automation, wireless monitoring, remote control systems, and DIY electronics projects. It is programmable using Arduino IDE, MicroPython, or AT commands, and operates with low power consumption, making it ideal for battery-powered devices.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":165,\"secondary_id\":\"145\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:13:31'),
(3926,1,'product',1019,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HC32\",\"description\":\"The 74HC32 is a high-speed CMOS logic integrated circuit that contains four independent 2-input OR gates in a single package.\",\"info\":\"74HC32 is a high-speed CMOS logic IC that contains four independent 2-input OR gates in a single package\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HC32\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HC32\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates over a wide supply voltage range (2 V to 6 V) and offers low power consumption with fast switching performance.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:14:57'),
(3927,1,'product',458,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HC595\",\"description\":\"74HC595 is an 8-bit serial-in, parallel-out shift register IC with an output latch. It allows multiple digital outputs to be controlled using just three microcontroller pins (data, clock, latch).\",\"info\":\"Operating at 5 V (and compatible with 3.3 V logic), the 74HC595 is widely used for LED control, display driving, I/O expansion, and digital control applications due to its simplicity, speed, and expandability.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HC595\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HC595\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"Operating at 5 V (and compatible with 3.3 V logic), the 74HC595 is widely used for LED control, display driving, I/O expansion, and digital control applications due to its simplicity, speed, and expandability.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:21:23'),
(3928,1,'product',1118,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HCT02\",\"description\":\"The 74HCT02 is a high-speed CMOS Quad 2-Input NOR gate IC that contains four independent NOR logic gates within a single package\",\"info\":\"The 74HCT02 contains four independent NOR gates, each with two inputs. It operates on CMOS technology for low power consumption while maintaining TTL-compatible input levels, making it ideal for interfacing CMOS circuits with TTL logic.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HCT02\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HCT02\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates on CMOS technology for low power consumption while maintaining TTL-compatible input levels, making it ideal for interfacing CMOS circuits with TTL logic.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:25:00'),
(3929,1,'product',1120,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HCT138\",\"description\":\"The 74HCT138 is a high-speed CMOS 3-to-8 line decoder / demultiplexer designed to be fully compatible with TTL logic levels\",\"info\":\"The 74HCT138 takes 3 binary address inputs and decodes them into one of 8 active-LOW outputs. It includes three enable pins (two active-LOW, one active-HIGH) for flexible control and cascading. With TTL-compatible inputs and low CMOS power consumption, it’s ideal for address decoding in mixed TTL/CMOS systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HCT138\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HCT138\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It includes three enable pins (two active-LOW, one active-HIGH) for flexible control and cascading. With TTL-compatible inputs and low CMOS power consumption, it’s ideal for address decoding in mixed TTL/CMOS systems.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:26:14'),
(3930,1,'product',1119,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HCT14\",\"description\":\"The 74HCT14 is a Hex Schmitt Trigger Inverter IC from the High-Speed CMOS (HCT) logic family, designed to operate at 5V TTL-compatible input levels.\",\"info\":\"The 74HCT14 contains six inverters, each with Schmitt-trigger inputs, which provide hysteresis for clean and stable switching. This makes it excellent for noisy signals, slow-changing inputs, and switch debouncing, while still accepting TTL-level inputs at a 5V supply.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HCT14\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HCT14\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"This makes it excellent for noisy signals, slow-changing inputs, and switch debouncing, while still accepting TTL-level inputs at a 5V supply.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:27:06'),
(3931,1,'product',2403,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"ESC 30A\",\"description\":\"ESC 30A (Electronic Speed Controller) is a widely used component in RC models, drones, quadcopters, airplanes, and robotics projects where precise motor speed control is required.\",\"info\":\"It acts as the bridge between the battery and motor, interpreting throttle signals from the flight controller or receiver and converting them into smooth, controlled motor rotation.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"1.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":165,\"secondary_id\":\"80\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:28:15'),
(3932,1,'product',1121,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HCT244\",\"description\":\"The 74HCT244 is a high-speed octal buffer and line driver designed for digital signal buffering and bus interfacing applications.\",\"info\":\"The 74HCT244 contains eight non-inverting buffers arranged in two groups of four, each controlled by its own active-LOW output enable (OE). \",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HCT244\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HCT244\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"With TTL-level input compatibility and low CMOS power consumption, it is ideal for bus driving and signal buffering in mixed TTL/CMOS systems.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:28:40'),
(3933,1,'product',1122,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HCT245\",\"description\":\"The 74HCT245 is an octal bidirectional bus transceiver designed for reliable data transfer between two 8-bit data buses. It operates on a 5V power supply and is TTL-compatible, making it ideal for interfacing between standard TTL logic and CMOS systems.\",\"info\":\"The 74HCT245 allows 8-bit data to flow in either direction between two buses using a DIR (direction control) pin. Its active-LOW Output Enable (OE) places the outputs in high-impedance when disabled. \",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HCT245\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HCT245\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"With TTL-compatible inputs and low CMOS power consumption, it’s ideal for interfacing TTL logic with CMOS buses.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:31:00'),
(3934,1,'product',1123,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HCT273\",\"description\":\"The 74HCT273 is an octal D-type flip-flop integrated circuit designed for use in digital storage and data-latching applications.\",\"info\":\"The 74HCT273 stores 8 bits of data on the rising edge of the clock and holds the data until the next clock event. An active-LOW asynchronous clear resets all outputs to zero instantly. \",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HCT273\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HCT273\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"With TTL-level input compatibility and low CMOS power consumption, it’s ideal for mixed TTL/CMOS digital systems.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:31:52'),
(3935,1,'product',1124,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HCT374\",\"description\":\"74HCT374 is an octal D-type edge-triggered flip-flop with 3-state outputs, designed for use in digital systems where temporary data storage and bus interfacing are required.\",\"info\":\"The 74HCT374 captures 8 bits of data on the rising edge of the clock and holds them until the next clock pulse. Its tri-state outputs, controlled by an active-LOW Output Enable (OE), allow multiple devices to share a common data bus. \",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HCT374\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HCT374\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"With TTL-compatible inputs and low CMOS power consumption, it’s ideal for mixed TTL/CMOS systems.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:33:12'),
(3936,1,'product',1125,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HCT573\",\"description\":\"The 74HCT573 is an octal transparent latch designed for high-speed data storage and buffering applications.\",\"info\":\"The 74HCT573 allows 8-bit data to pass directly to the outputs when the Latch Enable (LE) is HIGH. When LE goes LOW, the data is latched and held. \",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HCT573\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HCT573\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"Its tri-state outputs, controlled by an active-LOW Output Enable (OE), make it ideal for shared data buses.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:35:19'),
(3937,1,'product',1126,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74HCT574\",\"description\":\"The 74HCT574 is an octal D-type flip-flop integrated circuit with edge-triggered operation and tri-state outputs, designed for high-speed digital data storage and transfer\",\"info\":\"The 74HCT574 captures 8-bit data on the rising edge of the clock and stores it until the next clock event. Its tri-state outputs, controlled by an active-LOW Output Enable (OE), allow multiple devices to share a common data bus.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74HCT574\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74HCT574\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"Its tri-state outputs, controlled by an active-LOW Output Enable (OE), allow multiple devices to share a common data bus.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:36:22'),
(3938,1,'product',1015,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS00\",\"description\":\"The LS00 IC, commonly known as 74LS00, is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) digital logic IC that contains four independent 2-input NAND gates in a single package. Each NAND gate performs a basic logical operation where the output is LOW only when both inputs are HIGH; otherwise, the output remains HIGH.\",\"info\":\"74LS00 is a TTL logic IC that contains four independent 2-input NAND gates in a single package.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS00\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS00\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, offering faster switching speed and lower power consumption compared to standard TTL devices.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:36:57'),
(3939,1,'product',1020,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS01\",\"description\":\"The 74LS01 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) logic IC from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains four independent 2-input NAND gates with open-collector outputs.\",\"info\":\"74LS01 is a TTL logic IC that contains four independent 2-input NAND gates with open-collector outputs.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS01\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS01\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates on a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, offering good speed with reduced power consumption.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:37:19'),
(3940,1,'product',1022,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS02\",\"description\":\"The 74LS02 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains four independent 2-input NOR gates in a single package. A NOR gate produces a HIGH output only when all inputs are LOW; if any input is HIGH, the output becomes LOW.\",\"info\":\"74LS02 is a TTL logic IC that contains four independent 2-input NOR gates in a single package\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS02\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS02\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, offering faster switching and lower power consumption than standard TTL devices.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:38:02'),
(3941,1,'product',1026,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS04\",\"description\":\"The 74LS04 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains six independent NOT gates (inverters) in a single package. Each inverter outputs the logical opposite of its input—when the input is HIGH, the output is LOW, and vice versa.\",\"info\":\"74LS04 is a TTL logic IC that contains six independent NOT gates (hex inverter) in a single package.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS04\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS04\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, providing faster switching speed and lower power consumption than standard TTL devices.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:38:25'),
(3942,1,'product',1028,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS06\",\"description\":\"The 74LS06 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains six independent inverters (NOT gates) with open-collector outputs. Unlike standard inverters, the open-collector design allows the outputs to be connected to higher-voltage loads or wired-AND configurations using an external pull-up resistor.\",\"info\":\"74LS06 is a TTL logic IC that contains six independent inverters (NOT gates) with open-collector outputs. It operates from a 5 V supply and is part of the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, offering reliable switching with reduced power consumption.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS06\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS06\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"The open-collector outputs allow it to drive higher-voltage loads, relays, LEDs, or be used for wired-AND logic with external pull-up resistors.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:40:17'),
(3943,1,'product',2266,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"ER3V / 3.6V Lithium battery\",\"description\":\"The ER3V (3.6V) lithium battery is a primary (non-rechargeable) Lithium Thionyl Chloride (Li-SOCl?) battery designed for long-life, low-current applications.\",\"info\":\"It is widely used in industrial, utility, and embedded electronics where reliability and extended shelf life are critical.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"10.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":408,\"secondary_id\":\"62\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:40:26'),
(3944,1,'product',1029,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS07\",\"description\":\"The 74LS07 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains six independent non-inverting buffers with open-collector outputs. Unlike standard buffer ICs, the open-collector design allows the outputs to be connected to higher-voltage loads or combined in wired-AND configurations using an external pull-up resistor.\",\"info\":\"74LS07 is a TTL logic IC that contains six independent non-inverting buffers with open-collector outputs. It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, providing good speed with lower power consumption.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS07\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS07\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"The open-collector outputs allow it to drive higher-voltage loads, LEDs, relays, or perform wired-AND logic using external pull-up resistors.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:40:44'),
(3945,1,'product',2272,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"ER17500V/3.6V Lithium battery\",\"description\":\"The ER17500V / 3.6V lithium battery is a primary (non-rechargeable) lithium-thionyl chloride (Li-SOCl?) cell designed for long-term, low-to-medium current applications where reliability and long life are essential.\",\"info\":\"High energy density: Lithium thionyl chloride cells store significant energy per unit volume.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"10.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":408,\"secondary_id\":\"62\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:40:51'),
(3946,1,'product',2322,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"ER17330 3.6V Mitsubishi battery\",\"description\":\"The ER17330 3.6V battery is a primary (non-rechargeable) lithium battery commonly used in Mitsubishi Electric PLCs, CNC systems, and industrial controllers\",\"info\":\"It uses Lithium Thionyl Chloride (Li-SOCl?) chemistry, which is ideal for long-term memory backup and low-current applications where reliability is critical.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"10.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":408,\"secondary_id\":\"62\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:41:20'),
(3947,1,'product',1034,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS08 ( CERAMIC )\",\"description\":\"The 74LS08 (Ceramic) is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family, packaged in a ceramic DIP (CDIP) for enhanced reliability and thermal stability. It contains four independent 2-input AND gates, where each gate produces a HIGH output only when both inputs are HIGH.\",\"info\":\"74LS08 (Ceramic) is a TTL logic IC that contains four independent 2-input AND gates in a ceramic DIP package. It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, offering faster switching speed and lower power consumption compared to standard TTL devices.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS08 ( CERAMIC )\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS08 ( CERAMIC )\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, offering faster switching speed and lower power consumption compared to standard TTL devices.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:42:14'),
(3948,1,'product',2143,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"Emergency LED Light Circuit PCB Board\",\"description\":\"An Emergency LED Light Circuit PCB Board is a compact electronic board designed to automatically turn on LED lights during a power failure.\",\"info\":\"It typically integrates a battery charging section, power management, and LED driver circuit on a single PCB, ensuring reliable illumination when mains power is unavailable.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"0.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":465,\"secondary_id\":\"564\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:42:21'),
(3949,1,'product',1037,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS11\",\"description\":\"The 74LS11 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains three independent 3-input AND gates in a single package. Each AND gate produces a HIGH output only when all three inputs are HIGH, making the IC suitable for complex logic conditions where multiple signals must be true simultaneously.\",\"info\":\"74LS11 is a TTL logic IC that contains three independent 3-input AND gates in a single package\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS11\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS11\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, offering faster switching speed and reduced power consumption compared to standard TTL logic.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:43:13'),
(3950,1,'product',2288,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"Electric Soldering Iron\",\"description\":\"An electric soldering iron is a handheld tool used to heat solder (metal alloy) and join metal parts together especially in electronics and electrical work. It converts electrical power into heat through a heating element, allowing the tip to melt solder and create strong, conductive connections between wires, components, and circuit boards.\",\"info\":\"An electric soldering iron is a hand-held tool that uses electricity to generate heat for melting solder, the metal alloy used to join metal parts together. It’s one of the most common tools in electronics, electrical work, and DIY projects because it makes permanent, conductive joints between wires and components.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"10.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":423,\"secondary_id\":\"424\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:43:25'),
(3951,1,'product',1056,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS123\",\"description\":\"The 74LS123 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family designed as a dual retriggerable monostable multivibrator (one-shot timer). It generates a single output pulse of controlled width when triggered by an input signal.\",\"info\":\"74LS123 is a TTL dual retriggerable monostable multivibrator IC. It generates a precise output pulse whose width is set using external resistors and capacitors, and the pulse can be retriggered if a new trigger arrives before the timing period ends.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS123\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS123\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It generates a single output pulse of controlled width when triggered by an input signal.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:44:34'),
(3952,1,'product',1057,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS138\",\"description\":\"The 74LS138 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family used as a 3-to-8 line decoder or demultiplexer. It takes three binary input signals and decodes them into one of eight mutually exclusive active-LOW outputs, depending on the input combination.\",\"info\":\"74LS138 is a TTL 3-to-8 line decoder/demultiplexer IC that converts 3 binary input lines into one of eight active-LOW outputs. It operates from a 5 V supply and includes three enable inputs for flexible control and cascading.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS138\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS138\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It takes three binary input signals and decodes them into one of eight mutually exclusive active-LOW outputs, depending on the input combination.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:45:56'),
(3953,1,'product',1039,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS14\",\"description\":\"The 74LS14 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains six independent inverting gates (NOT gates) with Schmitt trigger inputs.\",\"info\":\"74LS14 is a TTL logic IC that contains six inverters with Schmitt trigger inputs in a single package\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS14\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS14\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, providing improved noise immunity and clean switching for slow or noisy input signals.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:46:52'),
(3954,1,'product',1058,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS145\",\"description\":\"The 74LS145 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family designed as a BCD (Binary Coded Decimal) to decimal decoder/driver. It converts a 4-bit BCD input into one of ten mutually exclusive active-LOW outputs (0–9). Only one output is active at a time, corresponding to the BCD input value.\",\"info\":\"74LS145 is a TTL BCD-to-Decimal decoder/driver IC that converts a 4-bit BCD input into one of ten active-LOW outputs (0–9). It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS145\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS145\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It converts a 4-bit BCD input into one of ten mutually exclusive active-LOW outputs (0–9). Only one output is active at a time, corresponding to the BCD input value.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:47:26'),
(3955,1,'product',1059,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS156\",\"description\":\"The 74LS156 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains two independent 1-of-4 decoders (or demultiplexers) in a single package. Each decoder takes two binary select inputs and activates one of four outputs.\",\"info\":\"The 74LS156 is a TTL logic IC that contains dual 1-of-4 decoder/demultiplexer circuits with open-collector outputs. It converts binary input signals into one of four active LOW outputs, allowing selection or routing of digital signals in logic systems\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS156\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS156\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"Designed using Low-Power Schottky (LS) technology, the IC provides fast switching speed and reliable performance in digital control applications. The open-collector outputs allow wired-OR connections and easy interfacing with different voltage levels using external pull-up resistors.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:47:49'),
(3956,1,'product',1062,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS161\",\"description\":\"The 74LS161 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family, designed as a 4-bit synchronous binary counter. It counts in binary sequence from 0 to 15 (0000 to 1111) with all flip-flops triggered simultaneously by a common clock, ensuring accurate and glitch-free counting.\",\"info\":\"74LS161 is a TTL synchronous 4-bit binary counter IC with asynchronous clear (CLR) and synchronous parallel load features. It counts in binary from 0 to 15 on each rising edge of the clock when enabled.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS161\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS161\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It counts in binary sequence from 0 to 15 (0000 to 1111) with all flip-flops triggered simultaneously by a common clock, ensuring accurate and glitch-free counting.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:48:28'),
(3957,1,'product',1066,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS164\",\"description\":\"The 74LS164 is an 8-bit serial-in, parallel-out shift register belonging to the TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) 74LS family. It is designed to accept serial data and convert it into parallel outputs, making it ideal for expanding output lines in digital systems. \",\"info\":\"74LS164 is a TTL 8-bit serial-in, parallel-out (SIPO) shift register IC. It accepts serial data input and shifts it into eight parallel outputs on each clock pulse. It operates from a 5 V supply and includes an asynchronous clear to reset all outputs.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS164\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS164\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"The IC features two serial data inputs (A and B) which are internally AND-gated, allowing flexible data control.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:51:27'),
(3958,1,'product',1042,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS20\",\"description\":\"The 74LS20 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains two independent 4-input NAND gates in a single package. Each gate produces a LOW output only when all four inputs are HIGH; otherwise, the output remains HIGH.\",\"info\":\"74LS20 is a TTL logic IC that contains two independent 4-input NAND gates in a single package.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS20\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS20\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, offering faster switching speed and lower power consumption than standard TTL devices.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:51:56'),
(3959,1,'product',1068,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS240\",\"description\":\"The 74LS240 is an octal buffer and line driver with tri-state outputs, belonging to the TTL 74LS (Low-Power Schottky) logic family. It is designed to buffer and drive data buses while providing controlled output enable functionality. \",\"info\":\"74LS240 is a TTL octal buffer/line driver IC with inverting outputs and tri-state control. It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, offering good speed with reduced power consumption.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS240\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS240\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"The IC contains eight independent non-inverting buffers, divided into two groups of four, each group controlled by its own active-LOW enable pin.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:54:40'),
(3960,1,'product',1074,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS244\",\"description\":\"The 74LS244 is an octal buffer and line driver with tri-state outputs, belonging to the 74LS (Low-Power Schottky) TTL logic family. It is designed to buffer, isolate, and drive data lines in digital systems while allowing multiple devices to share a common bus. The IC consists of eight non-inverting buffers, arranged in two groups of four, with each group controlled by its own active-LOW output enable pin. \",\"info\":\"The 74LS244 contains eight non-inverting buffers with two independent enable (OE) controls, allowing it to drive data buses efficiently. I\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS244\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS244\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"When the enable input is inactive, the corresponding outputs enter a high-impedance (Hi-Z) state, preventing bus contention.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:55:04'),
(3961,1,'product',1085,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS273\",\"description\":\"The 74LS273 is an octal D-type flip-flop with a common clock and asynchronous clear, belonging to the 74LS (Low-Power Schottky) TTL logic family. It contains eight edge-triggered D flip-flops that store 8 bits of data simultaneously. Data present at the D inputs is latched to the Q outputs on the rising edge of the clock. An active-LOW asynchronous clear input resets all outputs to LOW instantly, independent of the clock.\",\"info\":\"The 74LS273 stores 8 bits of data on the rising edge of the clock and holds the data until the next clock pulse. It features an active-LOW asynchronous clear that resets all outputs to zero. Built using LS (Low-power Schottky) TTL technology, it offers fast and reliable data storage for digital systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS273\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS273\",\"mrp\":\"9\",\"note\":\"Data present at the D inputs is latched to the Q outputs on the rising edge of the clock. An active-LOW asynchronous clear input resets all outputs to LOW instantly, independent of the clock.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:55:32'),
(3962,1,'product',1085,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS273\",\"description\":\"The 74LS273 is an octal D-type flip-flop with a common clock and asynchronous clear, belonging to the 74LS (Low-Power Schottky) TTL logic family. It contains eight edge-triggered D flip-flops that store 8 bits of data simultaneously. Data present at the D inputs is latched to the Q outputs on the rising edge of the clock. An active-LOW asynchronous clear input resets all outputs to LOW instantly, independent of the clock.\",\"info\":\"The 74LS273 stores 8 bits of data on the rising edge of the clock and holds the data until the next clock pulse. It features an active-LOW asynchronous clear that resets all outputs to zero. Built using LS (Low-power Schottky) TTL technology, it offers fast and reliable data storage for digital systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS273\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS273\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"Data present at the D inputs is latched to the Q outputs on the rising edge of the clock. An active-LOW asynchronous clear input resets all outputs to LOW instantly, independent of the clock.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":73,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:55:40'),
(3963,1,'product',1089,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS280\",\"description\":\"The 74LS280 is a 9-bit parity generator and parity checker IC from the 74LS (Low-Power Schottky) TTL logic family. It is designed to generate or verify parity bits for digital data, helping detect data transmission and storage errors. The device accepts eight or nine parallel data inputs and produces both even and odd parity outputs.\",\"info\":\"The 74LS280 generates or checks even and odd parity for 9 input bits, helping detect data transmission or storage errors. It is built using LS (Low-power Schottky) TTL technology, offering fast operation and reliable logic performance in bus and communication circuits.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS280\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS280\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"The device accepts eight or nine parallel data inputs and produces both even and odd parity outputs.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:56:05'),
(3964,1,'product',1044,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS30\",\"description\":\"The 74LS30 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains one 8-input NAND gate in a single package. The output of the gate goes LOW only when all eight inputs are HIGH; if any input is LOW, the output remains HIGH.\",\"info\":\"74LS30 is a TTL logic IC that contains a single 8-input NAND gate in a single package\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS30\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS30\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, providing faster switching speed and lower power consumption than standard TTL devices.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:56:24'),
(3965,1,'product',1045,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS32\",\"description\":\"The 74LS32 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains four independent 2-input OR gates in a single package. Each OR gate outputs a logic HIGH when any one or both of its inputs are HIGH, and outputs LOW only when both inputs are LOW.\",\"info\":\"74LS32 is a TTL logic IC that contains four independent 2-input OR gates in a single package\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS32\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS32\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates on a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, offering faster switching speed and reduced power consumption compared to standard TTL devices.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:57:06'),
(3966,1,'product',1090,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS373\",\"description\":\"The 74LS373 is an octal transparent D-type latch with tri-state outputs, part of the 74LS (Low-Power Schottky) TTL logic family. It is designed to temporarily store and hold 8 bits of data in digital systems. When the Latch Enable (LE) input is HIGH, the outputs follow the inputs (transparent mode). When LE goes LOW, the data present at the inputs is latched and held at the outputs.\",\"info\":\"The 74LS373 allows 8-bit data to pass directly to the outputs when the Latch Enable (LE) is HIGH. When LE goes LOW, the data is latched and held. \",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS373\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS373\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"Its tri-state outputs enable easy connection to shared data buses. Built with LS (Low-power Schottky) TTL technology, it provides fast and reliable operation.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:57:47'),
(3967,1,'product',1092,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS374\",\"description\":\"The 74LS374 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains eight D-type flip-flops that are positive-edge-triggered, meaning data present at the inputs is stored on the rising edge of the clock.\",\"info\":\"The 74LS374 stores 8 bits of data on the rising edge of the clock. Its tri-state outputs allow multiple devices to share a common data bus, while the Output Enable (OE) pin controls when the stored data appears on the outputs.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS374\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS374\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\" Built using LS (Low-power Schottky) TTL technology, it provides fast and reliable data latching.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:58:15'),
(3968,1,'product',1047,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS47\",\"description\":\"The 74LS47 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family, designed to convert Binary Coded Decimal (BCD) inputs into the corresponding signals required to drive a 7-segment LED display.\",\"info\":\"74LS47 is a TTL BCD-to-7-segment decoder/driver IC designed to drive common-anode 7-segment displays\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS47\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS47\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It converts a 4-bit BCD input into the corresponding 7-segment output to display decimal digits 0–9.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:58:41'),
(3969,1,'product',1049,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS51\",\"description\":\"The 74LS51 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family that implements AND-OR-Invert (AOI) logic. It contains two independent AOI logic circuits, each combining multiple AND gates whose outputs are ORed together and then inverted.\",\"info\":\"74LS51 is a TTL logic IC that contains two AND-OR-INVERT (AOI) logic gates in a single package\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS51\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS51\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, offering faster switching and lower power consumption than standard TTL devices.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:59:28'),
(3970,1,'product',1093,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS595\",\"description\":\"The 74LS595 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It functions as an 8-bit serial-in, parallel-out (SIPO) shift register with a separate storage register (latch) and 3-state outputs.\",\"info\":\"The 74LS595 accepts serial data input and shifts it on each clock pulse, then transfers the data to 8 parallel outputs using a latch clock. Its tri-state outputs allow easy connection to shared data buses. Built with LS (Low-power Schottky) TTL technology, it is commonly used to expand output pins in digital systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS595\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS595\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"Its tri-state outputs allow easy connection to shared data buses. Built with LS (Low-power Schottky) TTL technology, it is commonly used to expand output pins in digital systems.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 08:59:59'),
(3971,1,'product',1050,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS74\",\"description\":\"The 74LS74 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains two independent D-type flip-flops, each triggered on the positive (rising) edge of the clock signal. Each flip-flop includes asynchronous preset (SET) and clear (RESET) inputs, allowing the output to be forced to a known state regardless of the clock.\",\"info\":\"74LS74 is a TTL dual D-type flip-flop IC with preset (PRE) and clear (CLR) inputs. It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, providing reliable and fast digital storage.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS74\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS74\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"Each flip-flop includes asynchronous preset (SET) and clear (RESET) inputs, allowing the output to be forced to a known state regardless of the clock.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 09:00:41'),
(3972,1,'product',1053,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS86\",\"description\":\"The 74LS86 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains four independent 2-input Exclusive-OR (XOR) gates in a single package. Each XOR gate produces a HIGH output when the inputs are different (one HIGH and one LOW) and a LOW output when the inputs are the same.\",\"info\":\"74LS86 is a TTL logic IC that contains four independent 2-input XOR (exclusive-OR) gates in a single package.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS86\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS86\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, offering fast switching speed with reduced power consumption.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 09:01:04'),
(3973,1,'product',1055,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"74LS90\",\"description\":\"The 74LS90 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family designed as a decade (divide-by-10) counter. It counts from 0 to 9 in Binary Coded Decimal (BCD) form and then resets to zero, making it ideal for decimal counting applications.\",\"info\":\"74LS90 is a TTL decade counter IC that functions as a divide-by-10 (BCD) counter. It consists of four flip-flops arranged to count from 0 to 9, producing a 4-bit BCD output. It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"74LS90\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"74LS90\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It consists of four flip-flops arranged to count from 0 to 9, producing a 4-bit BCD output. It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 09:01:29'),
(3974,1,'product',253,'delete',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-03 09:02:16'),
(3975,1,'product',1110,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"75110\",\"description\":\"75110 IC is a dual line driver and receiver designed for balanced differential data transmission, commonly used in RS-422 and early serial communication systems. It integrates two differential drivers and two differential receivers in a single package, allowing reliable data transfer over long distances with high noise immunity. Operating from a single 5V supply, the 75110 supports high-speed data communication while maintaining stable performance in electrically noisy environments.\",\"info\":\"The 75110 is designed to drive balanced (differential) transmission lines, improving noise immunity and signal integrity over longer cable distances. It is commonly paired with compatible line receivers in industrial and communication interfaces, especially where reliable data transfer is required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"75110\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"75110\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It is commonly paired with compatible line receivers in industrial and communication interfaces, especially where reliable data transfer is required.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 09:04:53'),
(3976,1,'product',1104,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"75176\",\"description\":\"75176 IC is a differential bus transceiver designed for RS-485 and RS-422 communication systems. It integrates both a line driver and a line receiver in a single package, allowing half-duplex serial communication over long distances using balanced differential signaling. The driver and receiver can be independently enabled or disabled, which helps reduce power consumption and allows multiple devices to share the same bus.\",\"info\":\"The 75176 supports half-duplex differential data transmission, allowing reliable communication over long distances and in noisy environments. It features tri-state outputs so multiple devices can share the same bus, and it is commonly used in industrial and embedded serial communication systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"75176\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"75176\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"The driver and receiver can be independently enabled or disabled, which helps reduce power consumption and allows multiple devices to share the same bus.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 09:05:31'),
(3977,1,'product',1108,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"75477\",\"description\":\"75477 IC is a dual retriggerable monostable multivibrator designed primarily for timing, pulse generation, and audio signal applications. Each section of the IC functions as a one-shot circuit whose output pulse width is controlled by external resistor and capacitor (RC) components. \",\"info\":\"The 75477 contains two independent timing sections that can be configured to generate tones, alarms, sirens, pulse sounds, or timing delays using external resistors and capacitors. It supports astable and monostable operation, making it very flexible for audio and control circuits.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"75477\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"75477\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"The 75477 supports retriggering, meaning the output pulse can be extended if a new trigger occurs before the previous timing cycle ends.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":275,\"secondary_id\":\"73\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 09:06:27'),
(3978,1,'product',2509,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"75mah  Battery\",\"description\":\"The 75mAh battery is a small-capacity rechargeable battery commonly available in lithium-polymer (Li-Po) or lithium-ion type, designed for compact electronic devices requiring lightweight and portable power. It typically provides a nominal voltage of 3.7V, making it suitable for low-power applications such as wearable electronics, Bluetooth devices, miniature IoT modules, and DIY electronics projects.\",\"info\":\"The battery offers stable discharge performance, rechargeable capability, and compact size for space-constrained designs. With proper charging using a compatible lithium battery charger module (such as TP4056), the 75mAh battery delivers reliable operation and long cycle life for small electronic systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Lithium Battery\",\"mrp\":\"499\",\"note\":\"It typically provides a nominal voltage of 3.7V, making it suitable for low-power applications such as wearable electronics, Bluetooth devices, miniature IoT modules, and DIY electronics projects.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":408,\"secondary_id\":\"62\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 09:07:04'),
(3979,1,'product',2160,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"8.1m ohm resistor\",\"description\":\"An 8.1MΩ (8.1 Mega Ohm) resistor is a high-resistance electronic component used to limit current, divide voltage, or provide biasing in electronic circuits. The value 8.1MΩ means 8,100,000 ohms, which makes it suitable for very low-current applications such as signal processing, sensing circuits, timing networks, and high-impedance input stages. Because of its high resistance, it allows only a very small amount of current to pass through.\",\"info\":\"It provides a resistance of 8,100,000 ohms, making it suitable for sensitive signal and measurement applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Resistor\",\"mrp\":\"49\",\"note\":\"8.1MΩ resistors are widely used in voltage divider circuits, feedback networks in amplifiers, leakage current control, sensor circuits, and high-voltage measurement applications.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":413,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 09:09:49'),
(3980,1,'product',1316,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"8051 NUVOTON LEARNER KIT\",\"description\":\"The 8051 Nuvoton Learner Kit is an educational microcontroller development board built around a Nuvoton 8051-series MCU. It’s designed for beginners to learn 8051 architecture, programming, and embedded system interfacing.\",\"info\":\"The kit typically includes onboard peripherals, input/output interfaces, expansion ports, and example projects, making it ideal for hands-on learning in microcontroller fundamentals, digital I/O, timers, serial communication, and real-world interfacing.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"8051 NUVOTON LEARNER KIT\",\"mrp\":\"2900.00\",\"note\":\"It ideal for hands-on learning in microcontroller fundamentals, digital I/O, timers, serial communication, and real-world interfacing.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":86,\"secondary_id\":\"177\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 09:11:49'),
(3981,1,'product',2511,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"90mah  Battery\",\"description\":\"A 90mAh battery is a very small-capacity rechargeable battery commonly used in compact electronic devices such as Bluetooth headsets, smart wearables, mini MP3 players, small IoT modules, toys, and lightweight embedded systems.\",\"info\":\"can be safely charged using a proper protection circuit to prevent overcharging or deep discharge.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Lithium Battery\",\"mrp\":\"499\",\"note\":\"These batteries require a proper CC-CV (constant current–constant voltage) charging method and are typically charged up to 4.2V maximum using a suitable lithium battery charging module.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":408,\"secondary_id\":\"62\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 09:13:10'),
(3982,1,'product',2567,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"9V Cap\",\"description\":\"A 9V battery cap, also known as a 9V battery snap connector, is a small accessory used to easily connect a 9-volt battery to electronic circuits.\",\"info\":\"It securely clips onto the battery terminals and provides pre-attached wires for quick and reliable power connections.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"HW Battery Cap\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"note\":\"It securely clips onto the battery terminals and provides pre-attached wires for quick and reliable power connections.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":82,\"secondary_id\":\"494\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 09:14:05'),
(3983,1,'product',2307,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"9V Lithium Battery\",\"description\":\"A 9V Lithium Battery is a high-performance power source designed for devices that require stable voltage, long life, and reliable operation. Compared to traditional alkaline 9V batteries, lithium versions offer lighter weight, higher energy density, and superior durability, making them ideal for both professional and everyday applications.\",\"info\":\"9V lithium batteries are available in single packs and bulk packaging, with both non-rechargeable and rechargeable (Li-ion with USB charging) options depending on the brand.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Lithium Battery\",\"mrp\":\"499\",\"note\":\"Compared to traditional alkaline 9V batteries, lithium versions offer lighter weight, higher energy density, and superior durability, making them ideal for both professional and everyday applications.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":408,\"secondary_id\":\"62\",\"brand_id\":232}]}','2026-03-03 09:14:48'),
