(4688,1,'product',2873,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"ROCKER SWITCH\",\"description\":\"A Rocker Switch is a common electrical switch used to turn a device ON or OFF by rocking one side of the switch up or down. When one side is pressed, the opposite side rises, creating a simple and reliable switching action. Rocker switches are widely used in home appliances, power supplies, extension boards, electronic projects, and industrial equipment.\",\"info\":\"Rocker switches are designed for panel mounting and are available in various types such as 2-pin, 3-pin, and illuminated switches. Some models include a built-in LED or neon light that glows when the switch is turned ON. They are typically used with AC 110V–250V or DC circuits, depending on the model and rating.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1429],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"base_image\":\"products/1773029353740-399346323.jpg\"}','2026-03-09 04:09:13'),
(4689,1,'product',2874,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"Hikvision 32-Channel NVR\",\"description\":\"The DS-7732NXI-K4 belongs to Hikvision’s K-Series AcuSense NVR line, which uses deep-learning AI technology to detect humans and vehicles.\",\"info\":\"This recorder supports cameras with resolutions up to 12 MP, enabling high-detail surveillance recording.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[359],\"model\":\"DS-7732NXI-K4\",\"alternative_name\":\" NVR 4K 32-Channel \",\"mrp\":\"1\",\"note\":\"Install the NVR in a cool and well-ventilated location to avoid overheating.\",\"base_image\":\"products/1773029413942-20487346.jpg\"}','2026-03-09 04:10:13'),
(4690,1,'product',2875,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"TOGGLE SWITCH 3 PIN\",\"description\":\"A 3-Pin Toggle Switch is a small mechanical switch used to control the flow of electricity in a circuit. It has a lever (toggle) that can be moved up or down to change the switching position. This type of switch usually works as an SPDT (Single Pole Double Throw) switch, allowing one input to connect to one of two outputs.\",\"info\":\"The switch contains three terminals (pins): one common pin and two output pins. When the lever is moved, the common pin connects to either of the other two pins. These switches are widely used in electronic projects, control panels, robotics, power circuits, DIY equipment, and hobby electronics because they are durable and easy to operate.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1427],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"base_image\":\"products/1773029579023-816840100.jpg\"}','2026-03-09 04:12:59'),
(4691,1,'product',2876,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"Hikvision 8-Channel Network Video Recorder \",\"description\":\"The DS-7608NXI-K2 is part of Hikvision’s K-Series AcuSense NVR lineup, which uses deep-learning algorithms to detect humans and vehicles.\",\"info\":\"The recorder supports IP cameras with resolutions up to 12 MP, allowing high-quality and detailed surveillance recording.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[359],\"model\":\"DS-7608NXI-K2  \",\"alternative_name\":\" Network Video Recorder \",\"mrp\":\"1\",\"note\":\"The NVR provides 80 Mbps incoming bandwidth and up to 160 Mbps outgoing bandwidth, ensuring smooth recording and live streaming from multiple cameras.\",\"base_image\":\"products/1773029739309-916721147.jpg\"}','2026-03-09 04:15:39'),
(4692,1,'product',2877,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"6 PIN SELF LOCKING SWITCH\",\"description\":\"A 6 Pin Self Locking Switch is a push-button switch that stays in its position after being pressed. When the button is pressed once, the switch locks in the ON position, and pressing it again releases it back to OFF. This type of switch is commonly used for power control, machine control panels, electronic projects, and industrial equipment.\",\"info\":\"The switch usually works as a DPDT (Double Pole Double Throw) switch with six terminals (pins). These terminals allow the switch to control two separate circuits at the same time. Because of its locking mechanism, the switch maintains its state without needing continuous pressure, making it useful in many electronic and electrical applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1427],\"mrp\":\"47\",\"base_image\":\"products/1773029837979-76523645.jpg\"}','2026-03-09 04:17:17'),
(4693,1,'product',2878,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"ON OFF SWITCH 2A\",\"description\":\"A 2A ON/OFF Switch is a small electrical switch used to control the power supply of electronic devices. It allows the user to easily turn a circuit ON or OFF by pressing or toggling the switch. The 2A rating means the switch can safely handle a current of up to 2 amperes, making it suitable for low-power electronic circuits and small electrical devices.\",\"info\":\"This type of switch usually works as an SPST (Single Pole Single Throw) switch, which simply connects or disconnects the circuit. It is commonly used in DIY electronics, small appliances, battery-powered devices, power adapters, toys, and project boards. The switch is compact, easy to install, and reliable for basic power control.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1423],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"base_image\":\"products/1773029968585-319057710.jpg\"}','2026-03-09 04:19:28'),
(4694,1,'product',2879,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"SLIDE SWITCH\",\"description\":\"A Slide Switch is a small electrical switch used to open or close a circuit by sliding a small lever from one position to another. It is commonly used in electronic devices, DIY projects, toys, and battery-operated equipment because of its compact size and simple operation.\",\"info\":\"Slide switches are available in different types such as 2-pin (ON/OFF), 3-pin (SPDT), and multi-position switches. When the slider is moved, it changes the electrical connection between the terminals. These switches are widely used in PCB circuits, small gadgets, remote controls, and portable electronics due to their reliability and easy installation.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1427],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"base_image\":\"products/1773030084854-390767608.jpg\"}','2026-03-09 04:21:24'),
(4695,1,'product',2880,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"ROUND SWITCH\",\"description\":\"A Round Switch is a circular-shaped electrical switch commonly used to control the power supply of electronic and electrical devices. It usually works as an ON/OFF switch, allowing the user to easily turn equipment on or off. The round shape makes it suitable for panel mounting in appliances, control boxes, and electronic devices.\",\"info\":\"Round switches are widely used in home appliances, power supplies, extension boards, automotive devices, and DIY electronic projects. Some models include a built-in LED or neon indicator that lights up when the switch is in the ON position. They are available in different current and voltage ratings depending on the application.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1427],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"base_image\":\"products/1773030156491-871758489.jpg\"}','2026-03-09 04:22:36'),
(4696,1,'product',2881,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"TOGGLE SWITCH 6 PIN\",\"description\":\"A 6 Pin Toggle Switch is a mechanical switch used to control electrical circuits by moving a metal lever up or down. It contains six terminals (pins) and usually works as a DPDT (Double Pole Double Throw) switch. This allows the switch to control two separate circuits or change the direction of current flow.\",\"info\":\"The switch has two sets of three terminals, where each set controls one circuit. By toggling the lever, the internal contacts change the connection between the terminals. Because of this feature, 6-pin toggle switches are commonly used in motor control circuits, robotics, electronic projects, audio equipment, and control panels.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1427],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"base_image\":\"products/1773030228293-27525231.jpg\"}','2026-03-09 04:23:48'),
(4697,1,'product',2882,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"3 PIN DIP SWITCH\",\"description\":\"A 3 Pin DIP Switch is a small electronic switch designed for PCB (Printed Circuit Board) mounting. It is commonly used to select or configure different settings in electronic circuits. The switch is operated by sliding or toggling a tiny lever, which changes the electrical connection between its pins.\",\"info\":\"The 3-pin DIP switch usually functions as an SPDT (Single Pole Double Throw) switch. It has one common pin and two selectable pins, allowing the circuit to connect to one of two paths. DIP switches are widely used in microcontroller circuits, configuration settings, embedded systems, and electronic modules because they are compact and easy to integrate into PCBs.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1427],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"base_image\":\"products/1773030328952-122166927.jpg\"}','2026-03-09 04:25:28'),
(4698,1,'product',2883,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"4 PIN DIP SWITCH\",\"description\":\"A 4 Pin DIP Switch is a small PCB-mounted configuration switch used in electronic circuits to manually set different operating modes or settings. It is part of the DIP (Dual In-line Package) switch family, designed to be soldered directly onto a printed circuit board.\",\"info\":\"The 4-pin DIP switch usually contains two independent ON/OFF switches, each controlling a separate circuit path. Each switch connects or disconnects two pins when toggled. These switches are commonly used in microcontroller boards, communication devices, embedded systems, and electronic modules for configuration and addressing purposes.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1427],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"base_image\":\"products/1773030588227-518578548.jpg\"}','2026-03-09 04:29:48'),
(4699,1,'product',2884,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"2 PIN DIP SWITCH\",\"description\":\"A 2 Pin DIP Switch is a small PCB-mounted ON/OFF switch used in electronic circuits to manually control or configure a connection. It is part of the DIP (Dual In-line Package) switch family and is designed to be soldered directly onto a printed circuit board.\",\"info\":\"This switch usually works as an SPST (Single Pole Single Throw) switch, meaning it simply connects or disconnects the circuit when the switch is toggled. Due to its compact size, it is widely used in embedded systems, microcontroller circuits, communication devices, and electronic modules for enabling or disabling specific circuit functions.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1427],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"base_image\":\"products/1773030670774-442607592.jpg\"}','2026-03-09 04:31:10'),
(4700,1,'product',2885,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"8 PIN DIP SWITCH\",\"description\":\"An 8 Pin DIP Switch is a compact PCB-mounted configuration switch used in electronic circuits to manually set different operating modes. It belongs to the DIP (Dual In-line Package) switch family and is designed to be soldered directly onto a printed circuit board. The switch contains multiple small ON/OFF levers that allow users to control circuit connections easily.\",\"info\":\"An 8-pin DIP switch typically contains four individual ON/OFF switches, with each switch controlling a pair of pins. By toggling the small switches, users can enable or disable certain functions within a circuit. These switches are widely used in microcontroller boards, communication devices, embedded systems, industrial electronics, and configuration settings.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1427],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"base_image\":\"products/1773030780093-313249665.jpg\"}','2026-03-09 04:33:00'),
(4701,1,'product',2886,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"Hikvision 16-Channel NVR \",\"description\":\"This recorder supports IP cameras with resolutions up to 12 MP, allowing high-detail surveillance recording. \",\"info\":\"The NVR provides up to 160 Mbps incoming bandwidth, enabling stable recording and live streaming from multiple cameras simultaneously.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[359],\"model\":\"DS-7616NXI-K2\",\"mrp\":\"1\",\"note\":\"Install the NVR in a cool and well-ventilated place to avoid overheating.\",\"base_image\":\"products/1773031218671-253789541.jpg\"}','2026-03-09 04:40:18'),
