(4837,1,'product',2949,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BNC Male Connector\",\"description\":\"BNC Male Connector is a type of coaxial RF connector commonly used for connecting coaxial cables in electronic and communication systems. It features a bayonet locking mechanism that allows quick and secure connection to a matching BNC female connector. The connector is widely used in video transmission systems, CCTV cameras, oscilloscopes, radio frequency equipment, and networking devices. Its durable metal construction and secure locking design ensure stable signal transmission with minimal signal loss.\",\"info\":\"BNC stands for Bayonet Neill–Concelman, the name derived from its inventors. The BNC male connector is designed to terminate coaxial cables such as RG59 or RG6 and provides reliable connectivity for both analog and digital signals. It supports frequencies up to several GHz depending on the cable and connector quality. The bayonet coupling mechanism requires a simple push and twist motion to lock the connector securely into place, making installation quick and convenient.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"BNC Connector\",\"mrp\":\"399.00\",\"note\":\"BNC Male Connector is an RF interface component used in coaxial cable systems for transmitting radio frequency signals, video signals, and test signals. It is widely used in CCTV surveillance systems, broadcast equipment, laboratory instruments, and telecommunications devices. The connector provides a stable impedance connection (usually 50Ω or 75Ω) to ensure efficient signal transfer and reduced interference.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":304,\"secondary_id\":\"308\",\"brand_id\":232}],\"alternative_names\":[]}','2026-03-11 14:27:02'),
