(4876,1,'product',2971,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"ATMEGA328P NANO\",\"description\":\"The ATmega328P Nano is a compact microcontroller development board based on the ATmega328P AVR microcontroller, widely used in electronics learning, prototyping, and embedded system projects. It is similar in functionality to the Arduino Uno but comes in a small breadboard-friendly form factor, making it ideal for space-constrained applications. The board typically operates at a 5 V logic level with a 16 MHz clock speed and provides 32 KB Flash memory, 2 KB SRAM, and 1 KB EEPROM for program storage and data handling.\",\"info\":\"The Nano includes 14 digital input/output pins (6 PWM outputs), 8 analog input pins, UART serial communication, SPI and I²C interfaces, allowing easy connection to sensors, displays, relays, and communication modules. It can be powered through a Mini-USB port, VIN pin (about 7–12 V), or regulated 5 V supply, and supports simple programming using the Arduino IDE via USB bootloader.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[584],\"mrp\":\"499\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773305771406-548861433.jpeg\"}','2026-03-12 08:56:11'),
