(5009,1,'product',3053,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"REG 7906\",\"description\":\"7906 is a fixed negative voltage regulator integrated circuit used to provide a stable –6V DC output in electronic power supply circuits. It is part of the 79xx series of negative voltage regulators, where the last two digits represent the regulated output voltage level. The IC accepts a more negative unregulated DC input voltage (typically about –8V to –25V) and regulates it to a constant –6V output.\",\"info\":\"The 7906 regulator includes internal protection features such as thermal shutdown, current limiting, and short-circuit protection to ensure safe and reliable operation. It is commonly used in dual power supply systems, analog circuits, operational amplifier applications, communication equipment, and laboratory power supplies that require a stable negative voltage\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[657],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773467641260-880634877.jpg\"}','2026-03-14 05:54:01'),
(5010,1,'product',3054,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"Optical Cables\",\"description\":\"Optical cables, also called fiber optic cables, are communication cables that transmit data using light signals instead of electrical signals. They are widely used for high-speed internet, telecom networks, data centers, CCTV networking, and long-distance communication systems.\",\"info\":\"Optical cables are made of very thin glass or plastic fibers protected by multiple outer layers.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[94],\"mrp\":\"1\",\"note\":\"Avoid sharp bending or twisting of the fiber cable\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773468168277-100335019.jfif\"}','2026-03-14 06:02:48'),
(5011,1,'product',3055,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"REG 7908\",\"description\":\"7908 is a fixed negative voltage regulator integrated circuit designed to provide a stable –8V DC output in electronic power supply circuits. It belongs to the 79xx series of negative voltage regulators, where the number indicates the regulated output voltage value. The IC accepts a more negative unregulated input voltage (typically around –10V to –25V) and regulates it to a constant –8V output suitable for various analog and digital applications.\",\"info\":\"The 7908 regulator includes built-in protection features such as thermal shutdown, internal current limiting, and short-circuit protection to ensure safe and reliable operation. It is commonly used in dual power supply units, operational amplifier circuits, audio systems, communication equipment, and industrial control electronics that require a stable negative voltage. For proper operation and improved stability, input and output filter capacitors are usually connected near the regulator terminals. Due to its simple usage, stable performance, and rugged design, the 7908 is widely used in electronic power supply designs.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[657],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773468747819-760639033.jpg\"}','2026-03-14 06:12:27'),
(5012,1,'product',3056,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"REG 7909\",\"description\":\"7909 is a fixed negative voltage regulator integrated circuit used to provide a stable –9V DC output in electronic power supply circuits. It is part of the 79xx series of negative voltage regulators, where the last two digits indicate the regulated output voltage. The IC accepts a more negative unregulated input voltage (typically around –11V to –25V) and regulates it to a constant –9V output suitable for various electronic devices.\",\"info\":\"The 7909 regulator includes built-in protection features such as thermal shutdown, current limiting, and short-circuit protection to ensure safe and reliable operation. It is commonly used in dual power supply systems, operational amplifier circuits, audio equipment, communication devices, laboratory power supplies, and industrial control circuits that require a stable negative voltage.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[657],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773468830182-586169558.jpg\"}','2026-03-14 06:13:50'),
