(5021,1,'product',3061,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"REG 78L08\",\"description\":\"78L08 is a fixed positive voltage regulator integrated circuit designed to provide a stable +8V DC output in low-current electronic applications. It belongs to the 78xx regulator series, and the letter “L” indicates a low current version, typically capable of supplying up to about 100 mA. The IC accepts a higher unregulated DC input voltage (generally around 10V to 20V) and regulates it to a constant 8V output.\",\"info\":\"The 78L08 includes built-in protection features such as thermal shutdown and internal current limiting, which help ensure safe and reliable operation. It is commonly used in small power supply circuits, audio pre-amplifiers, sensor modules, communication devices, and educational electronics projects that require a stable +8V supply.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[657],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773469590782-309354578.jpg\"}','2026-03-14 06:26:30'),
(5022,1,'product',3062,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"REG 78L12\",\"description\":\"78L12 is a fixed positive voltage regulator integrated circuit designed to provide a stable +12V DC output in low-current electronic applications. It belongs to the popular 78xx voltage regulator series, where the number indicates the regulated output voltage level and the letter “L” denotes the low-current version. This IC is typically capable of supplying output current up to about 100 mA, making it suitable for small power requirements.\",\"info\":\"The 78L12 accepts a higher unregulated DC input voltage (usually around 14V to 25V) and converts it into a constant 12V output. It features built-in protection mechanisms such as thermal shutdown and internal current limiting, which help prevent damage due to overheating or short circuits. The IC offers good line and load regulation, ensuring a stable output voltage even with input or load variations\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[657],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773470252351-125423327.jpg\"}','2026-03-14 06:37:32'),
(5023,1,'product',3063,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"REG 78L15\",\"description\":\"78L15 is a fixed positive voltage regulator integrated circuit designed to provide a stable +15V DC output in low-current electronic applications. It belongs to the 78xx regulator series, and the letter “L” indicates the low-current version, typically capable of supplying up to about 100 mA. The IC accepts a higher unregulated DC input voltage (generally around 17V to 30V) and regulates it to a constant 15V output suitable for various circuits.\",\"info\":\"The 78L15 includes internal protection features such as thermal shutdown and current limiting to ensure safe and reliable operation. It offers good line and load regulation, helping maintain a steady output voltage even when input voltage or load conditions change. This regulator is commonly used in small power supply units, analog circuits, audio pre-amplifiers, communication equipment, sensor modules, and educational electronics projects that require a stable +15V supply.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[657],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773470586799-486601378.jpg\"}','2026-03-14 06:43:06'),
(5024,1,'product',3064,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"REG 78L18\",\"description\":\"78L18 is a fixed positive voltage regulator integrated circuit designed to provide a stable +18V DC output in low-current electronic applications. It belongs to the 78xx regulator family, and the letter “L” indicates the low-current version, typically capable of supplying up to about 100 mA of output current. The IC accepts a higher unregulated DC input voltage (usually around 21V to 30V) and regulates it to a constant 18V output suitable for various analog and digital circuits.\",\"info\":\"The 78L18 includes built-in protection features such as thermal shutdown and internal current limiting, which help ensure safe and reliable operation. It offers good line and load regulation, maintaining a stable output even when input voltage or load conditions vary. This regulator is commonly used in audio circuits, communication equipment, sensor supply sections, small power supply units, laboratory projects, and educational electronics experiments that require a steady +18V source.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[657],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773471683052-445042220.jpg\"}','2026-03-14 07:01:23'),
(5025,1,'product',3065,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"REG 79L05\",\"description\":\"79L05 is a fixed negative voltage regulator integrated circuit designed to provide a stable –5V DC output in low-current electronic applications. It belongs to the 79xx series of negative regulators, and the letter “L” indicates the low-current version, typically capable of supplying up to about 100 mA. The IC accepts a more negative unregulated DC input voltage (generally around –7V to –20V) and regulates it to a constant –5V output.\",\"info\":\"The 79L05 includes built-in protection features such as thermal shutdown and internal current limiting, which help ensure safe and reliable operation. It provides good line and load regulation, maintaining a steady output voltage even with variations in input supply or load conditions. This regulator is commonly used in dual power supply circuits, operational amplifier systems, signal processing circuits, communication devices, and educational electronics projects that require a stable negative voltage.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[657],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773472325161-280674794.jpg\"}','2026-03-14 07:12:05'),
