(5081,1,'product',3121,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IRF730\",\"description\":\"IRF730 is a power N-channel MOSFET transistor designed for high-voltage switching applications in electronic and power control circuits. It operates in enhancement mode, meaning the device turns ON when a suitable positive voltage is applied to the gate terminal. The MOSFET is capable of handling high drain-source voltage with moderate current capacity, making it suitable for various switching tasks.\",\"info\":\"IRF730 offers low ON-state resistance, fast switching characteristics, and good thermal stability, which help improve efficiency in power conversion circuits. It is commonly used in switch-mode power supplies (SMPS), inverter circuits, DC-DC converters, motor control systems, lighting control units, and general power switching applications\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773639390439-183325046.jpg\"}','2026-03-16 05:36:30'),
(5082,1,'product',3122,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IRF830\",\"description\":\"IRF830 is a high-voltage power N-channel MOSFET transistor used for switching and power control applications in electronic circuits. It operates in enhancement mode, meaning the device turns ON when a suitable positive voltage is applied to the gate terminal. The MOSFET is capable of handling high drain-source voltage with moderate current capability, making it suitable for various high-voltage switching tasks.\",\"info\":\"IRF830 offers fast switching speed, low gate drive power requirement, and good thermal stability, which help improve efficiency in power conversion circuits. It is commonly used in switch-mode power supplies (SMPS), inverter circuits, lighting control systems, DC-DC converters, motor control units, and industrial power control applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773639484833-942817268.jpg\"}','2026-03-16 05:38:04'),
(5083,1,'product',3123,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IRF840\",\"description\":\"IRF840 is a high-voltage power N-channel MOSFET transistor used for switching and power control applications in electronic circuits. It operates in enhancement mode, meaning the device turns ON when a suitable positive voltage is applied to the gate terminal. The MOSFET can withstand high drain-source voltage and moderate current levels, making it suitable for high-voltage switching operations.\",\"info\":\"IRF840 provides fast switching performance, relatively low ON-state resistance, and good thermal stability, which help improve efficiency in power conversion circuits. It is commonly used in switch-mode power supplies (SMPS), inverter circuits, lighting control systems, DC-DC converters, motor drive circuits, and industrial power control equipment. The device is usually available in a TO-220 package and typically requires a proper heat sink for reliable high-power operation. Due to its rugged construction and dependable performance, IRF840 is widely used in embedded electronics, hobby projects, and industrial switching applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773640324095-438594188.jpg\"}','2026-03-16 05:52:04'),
(5084,1,'product',3124,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IRF2807\",\"description\":\"IRF2807 is a power N-channel MOSFET transistor designed for high-current, low-voltage switching applications in power electronic circuits. It operates in enhancement mode, meaning the device turns ON when a suitable positive voltage is applied to the gate terminal. The MOSFET is capable of handling very high drain current with low drain-source resistance, making it suitable for efficient power switching tasks.\",\"info\":\"IRF2807 offers very low ON-state resistance, fast switching speed, and good thermal performance, which help reduce conduction losses and improve overall circuit efficiency. It is commonly used in DC motor control, battery management systems, DC-DC converters, inverter circuits, SMPS designs, and automotive power electronics. The device is typically available in a TO-220 power package and generally requires a proper heat sink for reliable operation at high current levels.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773640436013-341414774.jpg\"}','2026-03-16 05:53:56'),
(5085,1,'product',3125,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"Optical 4 Meter cable\",\"description\":\"A 4-meter optical cable is a short-to-medium length fiber optic patch cord used for connecting devices such as fiber modem (ONU), Wi-Fi router, network switch, patch panel, or fiber distribution box.\",\"info\":\"It is suitable for indoor broadband and networking setups where equipment is placed a few meters apart.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1538],\"model\":\"Optical  cable\",\"mrp\":\"1\",\"note\":\"Keep connectors clean and covered with dust caps\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773640758261-934175899.jfif\"}','2026-03-16 05:59:18'),
(5086,1,'product',3126,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IRF3205\",\"description\":\"IRF3205 is a high-performance N-channel power MOSFET widely used for switching and power control applications in electronic circuits. It is designed to handle high current (up to about 110A) and moderate voltage levels (55V drain-source voltage) with very low ON-state resistance, which helps reduce power loss and improve efficiency\",\"info\":\"Due to its fast switching capability and rugged construction, the IRF3205 is commonly used in inverters, DC motor drivers, SMPS power supplies, battery chargers, DC-DC converters, and high-power LED drivers. The device is available in a TO-220 package, making it easy to mount on a heat sink for thermal management during high-load operation. Proper gate drive voltage, heat dissipation, and protection components such as gate resistors and flyback diodes are recommended to ensure reliable and long-term performance.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773640762426-280492277.jpg\"}','2026-03-16 05:59:22'),
(5087,1,'product',3127,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IRF3710\",\"description\":\"IRF3710 is a powerful N-channel enhancement mode MOSFET designed for high-speed switching and high-current applications. It can handle drain-source voltage up to about 100V and continuous drain current around 57A, making it suitable for medium-to-high power electronic circuits. The device features low ON-state resistance, which helps to reduce heat generation and improve overall efficiency in switching operations.\",\"info\":\"Because of its fast switching characteristics and rugged design, the IRF3710 is widely used in inverters, motor control circuits, DC-DC converters, switching power supplies (SMPS), battery chargers, and power amplifier stages. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, allowing easy mounting with a heat sink for better thermal performance. For reliable operation, proper gate drive voltage, heat dissipation, and protection components such as gate resistors and flyback diodes should be used, especially when driving inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773640958879-43482476.png\"}','2026-03-16 06:02:38');
INSERT INTO `audit_logs` VALUES
(5088,1,'product',3128,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IRFP3710\",\"description\":\"IRFP3710 is a high-power N-channel MOSFET designed for efficient switching and power control in heavy-duty electronic applications. It is capable of handling high drain-source voltage (about 100V) and very high continuous drain current (around 57A or more depending on cooling conditions). The device features low ON-state resistance, which reduces conduction losses and improves overall circuit efficiency. Due to its fast switching performance and rugged construction, IRFP3710 is commonly used in inverters, high-power SMPS circuits, motor drivers, DC-DC converters, battery charging systems, and audio power amplifier stages.\",\"info\":\"It is typically available in a TO-247 package, which provides better heat dissipation compared to smaller packages and allows reliable operation in high-current environments when used with an appropriate heat sink. For stable performance, designers usually provide a suitable gate drive voltage (around 10–12V), gate resistor, and protection components such as flyback diodes when controlling inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773641788159-311017388.jpg\"}','2026-03-16 06:16:28'),
(5089,1,'product',3129,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IRF3415\",\"description\":\"IRF3415 is a reliable N-channel power MOSFET designed for efficient high-speed switching and power management applications. It supports a drain-source voltage of about 150V and can handle high current levels (around 40A depending on operating conditions and cooling). The device features low ON-state resistance, which helps reduce power dissipation and improves efficiency in switching circuits.\",\"info\":\"Because of its strong switching capability and rugged construction, the IRF3415 is widely used in SMPS power supplies, DC-DC converters, inverter circuits, motor control systems, battery charging units, and high-power electronic switching applications. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, allowing easy mounting on a heat sink for better thermal performance during continuous high-load operation. For reliable performance, designers typically use an adequate gate drive voltage, proper heat dissipation, and protection components such as gate resistors and flyback diodes, especially when driving inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773642549681-95134486.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 06:29:09'),
(5090,1,'product',3130,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IRF4905\",\"description\":\"IRF4905 is a high-power P-channel MOSFET mainly used for high-current switching and power control applications. It is designed to operate with a drain-source voltage of about −55V and can handle continuous drain current up to around −70A under proper cooling conditions. The device offers low ON-state resistance, which helps minimize conduction losses and improves overall efficiency in power circuits. Due to its fast switching characteristics and rugged construction, IRF4905 is widely used in battery protection circuits, DC motor control, inverter stages, power supply switching, load switching, and automotive electronics.\",\"info\":\"It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, making it easy to mount on a heat sink for better thermal management during high-load operation. For stable and reliable performance, designers typically provide an appropriate negative gate drive voltage, gate resistor, and protective components such as flyback diodes when switching inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773642607263-463935343.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 06:30:07'),
(5091,1,'product',3131,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IRF9520\",\"description\":\"IRF9520 is a widely used P-channel power MOSFET designed for medium-power switching and control applications. It can withstand a drain-source voltage of about −100V and supports continuous drain current around −6A to −10A depending on cooling and operating conditions. The device offers reasonably low ON-state resistance, which helps reduce power loss and improves efficiency in switching circuits.\",\"info\":\"Because of its reliable switching performance and simple gate drive requirements, the IRF9520 is commonly used in power supply circuits, load switching, motor control stages, battery-operated systems, audio amplifier sections, and DC-DC converter designs. It is generally available in a TO-220 package, allowing easy installation with a heat sink for better thermal dissipation during continuous operation. For safe and stable performance, designers typically use proper gate drive voltage, a gate resistor for switching stability, and protection components such as flyback diodes when driving inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773642677003-183951196.jpg\"}','2026-03-16 06:31:17'),
(5092,1,'product',3132,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IRF9530\",\"description\":\"IRF9530 is a P-channel enhancement mode power MOSFET commonly used for switching and power management in electronic circuits. It is designed to handle a drain-source voltage of about −100V and can carry continuous drain current up to around −12A under proper cooling conditions. The device provides moderate ON-state resistance, enabling efficient operation in medium-power switching applications.\",\"info\":\"Due to its dependable switching characteristics and rugged construction, the IRF9530 is widely used in power supply circuits, DC motor control, inverter sections, battery-powered equipment, load switching stages, and audio amplifier circuits. It is typically available in a TO-220 package, which allows convenient mounting on a heat sink for improved heat dissipation during prolonged high-load operation. For stable and reliable performance, designers usually ensure an appropriate negative gate drive voltage, use of a gate resistor, and protective components such as flyback diodes when switching inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773642730171-693332063.jpg\"}','2026-03-16 06:32:10'),
(5093,1,'product',3133,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IRF9540\",\"description\":\"IRF9540 is a commonly used P-channel power MOSFET designed for high-voltage and medium-current switching applications. It can handle a drain-source voltage of about −100V and supports continuous drain current up to around −19A depending on operating conditions and heat dissipation. The device offers relatively low ON-state resistance, which helps reduce power loss and improves efficiency in switching circuits.\",\"info\":\"Because of its reliable switching performance and rugged structure, the IRF9540 is widely used in SMPS power supplies, inverter circuits, motor control stages, battery-operated systems, DC-DC converters, and load switching applications. It is generally available in a TO-220 package, allowing easy mounting with a heat sink for better thermal management during high-load operation. For safe and stable performance, designers typically provide an appropriate negative gate drive voltage, gate resistor for switching stability, and protective components such as flyback diodes when controlling inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773642814344-784208969.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 06:33:34'),
(5094,1,'product',3134,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IRF9630\",\"description\":\"IRF9630 is a P-channel enhancement mode power MOSFET designed for high-voltage switching and power control applications. It is capable of handling a drain-source voltage of about −200V and supports continuous drain current around −6A to −8A depending on operating conditions and heat dissipation. The device features moderate ON-state resistance, allowing efficient performance in medium-power switching circuits.\",\"info\":\"Due to its rugged construction and reliable switching characteristics, the IRF9630 is commonly used in SMPS power supplies, inverter stages, motor control circuits, load switching applications, battery-powered equipment, and DC-DC converter designs. It is typically available in a TO-220 package, making it easy to mount on a heat sink for improved thermal management during continuous operation. For stable and safe performance, designers usually apply a suitable negative gate drive voltage, gate resistor for controlled switching, and protective components such as flyback diodes when driving inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773642894263-818835414.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 06:34:54'),
(5095,1,'product',3135,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IRF9640\",\"description\":\"IRF9640 is a high-voltage P-channel power MOSFET designed for switching and power control in medium-power electronic applications. It can withstand a drain-source voltage of about −200V and handle continuous drain current around −10A to −11A depending on cooling and operating conditions. The device offers moderate ON-state resistance, which helps maintain reasonable efficiency in switching circuits while operating at higher voltages.\",\"info\":\"Because of its reliable switching characteristics and rugged design, the IRF9640 is widely used in SMPS power supplies, inverter circuits, motor control stages, DC-DC converters, load switching, and battery-operated equipment. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, allowing easy mounting with a heat sink for improved heat dissipation during continuous high-load operation. For stable and safe performance, designers typically provide an appropriate negative gate drive voltage, a gate resistor for controlled switching, and protection components such as flyback diodes when driving inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773642956587-581157659.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 06:35:56'),
(5096,1,'product',3136,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IRFZ44\",\"description\":\"IRFZ44 is a popular N-channel power MOSFET used for high-speed switching and power control in various electronic circuits. It is designed to handle a drain-source voltage of about 55V and supports continuous drain current up to around 49A under proper cooling conditions. The device features low ON-state resistance, which helps reduce conduction losses and improves overall efficiency in switching applications.\",\"info\":\"Due to its fast switching characteristics and rugged construction, the IRFZ44 is widely used in inverter circuits, DC motor speed control, SMPS power supplies, DC-DC converters, battery chargers, and high-power LED drivers. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, allowing easy mounting on a heat sink for better thermal management during continuous high-load operation. For reliable performance, designers typically use a suitable gate drive voltage (around 10V), a gate resistor for stable switching, and protection components such as flyback diodes when controlling inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773643017111-417806655.jpg\"}','2026-03-16 06:36:57'),
(5097,1,'product',3137,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IRFZ48\",\"description\":\"IRFZ48 is a high-current N-channel power MOSFET designed for efficient switching and power control applications in electronic circuits. It can withstand a drain-source voltage of about 55V and handle continuous drain current up to around 60A depending on operating conditions and proper heat dissipation. The device features low ON-state resistance, which helps reduce conduction losses and improves overall efficiency in switching circuits.\",\"info\":\"Because of its fast switching capability and rugged construction, the IRFZ48 is widely used in inverter systems, DC motor speed control circuits, switching power supplies (SMPS), DC-DC converters, battery chargers, automotive electronics, and high-power LED drivers. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, allowing convenient mounting on a heat sink for better thermal performance during high-load operation. For stable and reliable performance, designers typically provide an appropriate gate drive voltage (around 10V), a gate resistor for controlled switching, and protective components such as flyback diodes when switching inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773643083490-536139193.jpg\"}','2026-03-16 06:38:03'),
(5098,1,'product',3138,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"4N60\",\"description\":\"4N60 is a high-voltage N-channel power MOSFET widely used in switching power supply and power control applications. It is designed to withstand a drain-source voltage of about 600V and can handle continuous drain current around 4A depending on cooling and operating conditions. The device provides good switching performance and moderate ON-state resistance, making it suitable for high-voltage, low-to-medium current circuits.\",\"info\":\"Because of its reliable operation and rugged structure, the 4N60 MOSFET is commonly used in SMPS power supplies, LED driver circuits, inverter stages, battery chargers, AC-DC converters, and other high-voltage switching applications. It is generally available in a TO-220 package, allowing easy mounting on a heat sink for better thermal dissipation during continuous operation. For safe and stable performance, designers usually provide an appropriate gate drive voltage, a gate resistor for controlled switching, and protection components such as snubber circuits or flyback diodes when used with inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773643197383-462042133.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 06:39:57'),
(5099,1,'product',3139,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"Optical  5 Meter Cables\",\"description\":\"A 5-meter optical cable is a fiber optic patch cord used to connect devices such as fiber modem (ONU), Wi-Fi router, network switch, patch panel, or fiber distribution box.\\r\\nIt is suitable for indoor broadband installations and networking setups where equipment is placed a few meters apart.\",\"info\":\"Constructed with thin glass or plastic fiber core that transmits data as light signals.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1538],\"alternative_name\":\"Optical Cables \",\"mrp\":\"1\",\"note\":\"Keep connectors clean and protected with dust caps\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773643766533-373986000.jfif\"}','2026-03-16 06:49:26'),
(5100,1,'product',3140,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"2SK962\",\"description\":\"2SK962 is an N-channel power MOSFET designed for high-voltage switching and power control applications. It is typically rated for a drain-source voltage of around 900V and supports continuous drain current of about 6A under suitable operating and cooling conditions. The device offers stable switching characteristics and is suitable for circuits where high voltage handling capability is required with moderate current load.\",\"info\":\"Due to its rugged construction and reliable performance, the 2SK962 is widely used in switching mode power supplies (SMPS), inverter circuits, CRT and monitor power sections, high-voltage regulators, and industrial power control systems. It is commonly available in a TO-220 style package, allowing convenient mounting on a heat sink to improve thermal management during continuous operation. For safe and efficient performance, designers usually ensure proper gate drive voltage, controlled switching with a gate resistor, and protection components such as snubber networks or flyback diodes when operating with inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773644551743-76544654.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 07:02:31'),
(5101,1,'product',3141,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IRFBG30\",\"description\":\"IRFBG30 is a high-voltage N-channel power MOSFET designed for efficient switching and power control in electronic circuits. It can withstand a drain-source voltage of about 1000V and is capable of handling continuous drain current around 3A–4A, depending on operating conditions and heat dissipation. The device features stable switching characteristics and moderate ON-state resistance, making it suitable for high-voltage, low-to-medium current applications.\",\"info\":\"Because of its rugged construction and reliable performance, IRFBG30 is commonly used in switch-mode power supplies (SMPS), inverter circuits, high-voltage regulators, industrial power control systems, CRT monitor power stages, and AC-DC converter applications. It is generally available in a TO-220 package, allowing easy mounting on a heat sink for improved thermal management during continuous operation. For safe and stable performance, designers typically use an appropriate gate drive voltage, gate resistor for controlled switching, and protection components such as snubber networks or flyback diodes when switching inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773644606191-389836039.jpg\"}','2026-03-16 07:03:26'),
(5102,1,'product',3142,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16TTS12\",\"description\":\"16TTS12 is a high-power SCR (Silicon Controlled Rectifier / Thyristor) designed for controlled rectification and switching in high-voltage power circuits. It is typically rated for a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 1200V and can handle average forward current around 16A, making it suitable for medium-to-high power industrial applications. The device operates by applying a trigger pulse at the gate terminal, which allows current to flow between the anode and cathode until the current drops below the holding level.\",\"info\":\"Because of its rugged construction and reliable switching characteristics, the 16TTS12 is widely used in controlled rectifiers, AC voltage regulators, motor speed control systems, battery chargers, inverter circuits, welding equipment, and industrial power control applications. It is commonly available in a stud-type power package, which enables efficient heat dissipation when mounted on an appropriate heat sink. For safe and stable operation, proper gate triggering circuitry, snubber networks, and adequate thermal management are recommended during high-load usage.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773644670545-521731461.jpg\"}','2026-03-16 07:04:30'),
(5103,1,'product',3143,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"25TTS12\",\"description\":\"25TTS12 is a high-power SCR (Silicon Controlled Rectifier / Thyristor) used for controlled switching and rectification in industrial and power electronic circuits. It is typically rated for a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 1200V and can handle average forward current around 25A, depending on cooling and operating conditions. The device is triggered by applying a gate pulse, which allows current to flow between the anode and cathode until the current falls below the holding level.\",\"info\":\"Because of its rugged construction and dependable performance, the 25TTS12 is widely used in controlled rectifier circuits, AC voltage regulators, motor speed controllers, battery charging systems, inverter stages, welding machines, and industrial power control equipment. It usually comes in a stud-type power package, allowing strong mechanical mounting and efficient heat dissipation when fixed to a suitable heat sink. For safe and reliable operation, designers typically use proper gate triggering circuits, snubber networks, and adequate thermal management during high-power applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773644728061-35217877.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 07:05:28'),
(5104,1,'product',3144,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"20ETS12\",\"description\":\"20ETS12 is a high-power SCR (Silicon Controlled Rectifier / Thyristor) designed for controlled rectification and switching in high-voltage power electronic circuits. It is typically rated for a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 1200 V and can handle an average forward current around 20 A, depending on operating conditions and heat dissipation. The device is turned ON by applying a trigger pulse to the gate terminal, allowing current to flow from anode to cathode until the current falls below the holding level.\",\"info\":\"Due to its rugged construction and reliable switching characteristics, the 20ETS12 is widely used in AC power control systems, controlled rectifiers, motor speed controllers, battery chargers, inverter circuits, welding equipment, and industrial power regulation applications. It is commonly available in a stud-type power package, which enables secure mounting on a heat sink for efficient thermal management during continuous high-load operation. For safe and stable performance, proper gate triggering circuitry, snubber networks, and adequate cooling arrangements are recommended.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773644797715-37489208.jpg\"}','2026-03-16 07:06:37'),
(5105,1,'product',3145,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"40TPS12\",\"description\":\"40TPS12 is a high-power SCR (Silicon Controlled Rectifier / Thyristor) used for controlled switching and rectification in heavy-duty power electronic applications. It is generally rated for a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 1200 V and can handle an average forward current around 40 A, depending on operating temperature and cooling conditions. The device is switched ON by applying a gate trigger pulse, allowing current to flow between the anode and cathode until the current drops below the holding level.\",\"info\":\"Because of its rugged design and high current capability, the 40TPS12 is widely used in industrial rectifier units, AC voltage regulators, motor speed control systems, battery charging equipment, inverter stages, welding machines, and other industrial power control circuits. It is commonly available in a stud-type power package, enabling strong mechanical mounting and efficient heat dissipation when installed on a suitable heat sink. For reliable operation, proper gate drive circuitry, snubber protection networks, and effective thermal management are recommended in high-power applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773644856162-208893052.jpg\"}','2026-03-16 07:07:36'),
(5106,1,'product',3146,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"40TTS12\",\"description\":\"40TTS12 is a high-power SCR (Silicon Controlled Rectifier / Thyristor) designed for controlled rectification and switching in industrial power electronic circuits. It is typically rated for a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 1200 V and can handle an average forward current of around 40 A, depending on operating conditions and cooling arrangements. The device is triggered into conduction by applying a gate pulse, allowing current to flow from the anode to the cathode until the current falls below the holding level.\",\"info\":\"Due to its rugged construction and reliable performance, the 40TTS12 is widely used in controlled rectifiers, AC voltage regulators, motor speed control systems, battery chargers, inverter circuits, welding machines, and industrial power control equipment. It generally comes in a stud-type power package, enabling strong mechanical mounting and effective heat dissipation when fitted with a suitable heat sink. For safe and stable operation, designers typically use proper gate triggering circuits, snubber networks, and adequate thermal management in high-power applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773644926777-579631849.jpg\"}','2026-03-16 07:08:46'),
(5107,1,'product',3147,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"CT60AM\",\"description\":\"CT60AM is a high-power SCR (Silicon Controlled Rectifier) / Thyristor module designed for heavy-duty power control and rectification applications. It is typically capable of handling high blocking voltage (around 600V to 1200V depending on variant) and high forward current capacity of about 60A, making it suitable for industrial and high-power electronic circuits. The device operates by applying a trigger signal at the gate terminal, which allows current conduction between the anode and cathode until the current drops below the holding level.\",\"info\":\"Because of its robust construction and high reliability, CT60AM is widely used in controlled rectifier units, motor speed control systems, AC voltage regulators, battery charging equipment, inverter stages, welding machines, and industrial automation power circuits. It is usually available in a power module or stud-type package, allowing secure mounting on a heat sink or metal chassis for efficient heat dissipation during continuous high-load operation. For safe and stable performance, proper gate triggering circuits, snubber protection networks, and adequate cooling arrangements are recommended in practical applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773644994267-835960888.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 07:09:54'),
(5108,1,'product',3148,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"55NF06\",\"description\":\"55NF06 (commonly known as STP55NF06) is a widely used N-channel power MOSFET designed for low-voltage, high-current switching applications. It can withstand a drain-source voltage of about 60 V and is capable of handling continuous drain current up to around 50–55 A, depending on cooling conditions. The device features very low ON-state resistance, which helps reduce power loss and improves efficiency in switching circuits.\",\"info\":\"Because of its fast switching performance and rugged structure, the 55NF06 MOSFET is commonly used in DC motor drivers, inverter circuits, SMPS power supplies, DC-DC converters, battery charging systems, automotive electronics, and high-power LED control applications. It is typically available in a TO-220 package, allowing easy mounting on a heat sink for better thermal management during high-load operation. For reliable performance, designers usually provide a suitable gate drive voltage (around 10 V), a gate resistor for stable switching, and protection components such as flyback diodes when switching inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773645062034-878240388.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 07:11:02'),
(5109,1,'product',3149,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"80NF10\",\"description\":\"80NF10 (commonly referred to as STP80NF10) is a high-current N-channel power MOSFET designed for efficient low-to-medium voltage switching applications. It can typically withstand a drain-source voltage of about 100 V and handle continuous drain current up to around 70–80 A, depending on operating temperature and cooling conditions. The device offers low ON-state resistance, which helps minimize conduction losses and improve efficiency in power switching circuits.\",\"info\":\"Due to its fast switching capability and rugged construction, the 80NF10 MOSFET is widely used in inverter systems, DC motor control circuits, switching mode power supplies (SMPS), DC-DC converters, battery charging equipment, automotive electronics, and high-power LED drivers. It is generally available in a TO-220 package, allowing convenient mounting on a heat sink for effective thermal dissipation during continuous high-load operation. For reliable and stable performance, designers typically use an appropriate gate drive voltage (around 10 V), a gate resistor for controlled switching, and protective components such as flyback diodes when driving inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773645156480-399323562.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 07:12:36'),
(5110,1,'product',3150,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"80NF55\",\"description\":\"80NF55 (commonly known as STP80NF55) is a high-voltage N-channel power MOSFET designed for efficient switching and power control in medium-to-high power electronic circuits. It can typically withstand a drain-source voltage of about 55 V and is capable of handling continuous drain current up to around 70–80 A, depending on operating temperature and proper heat dissipation. The device features low ON-state resistance, which helps reduce conduction losses and improves efficiency in switching applications.\",\"info\":\"Because of its fast switching performance and rugged design, the 80NF55 MOSFET is widely used in inverter circuits, DC motor speed control, switching mode power supplies (SMPS), DC-DC converters, battery charging systems, automotive electronics, and high-power LED driver circuits. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, allowing easy mounting on a heat sink for better thermal management during high-load operation. For reliable performance, designers usually provide an appropriate gate drive voltage (around 10 V), a gate resistor for switching stability, and protection components such as flyback diodes when controlling inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773645216654-371439313.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 07:13:36'),
(5111,1,'product',3151,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"90NF03\",\"description\":\"90NF03 (commonly referred to as STP90NF03) is a low-voltage, high-current N-channel power MOSFET designed for efficient switching and power control in DC electronic circuits. It typically supports a drain-source voltage of about 30 V and can handle continuous drain current up to around 80–90 A, depending on operating temperature and proper heat dissipation. The device features very low ON-state resistance, which helps minimize power loss and improves overall efficiency in high-current switching applications.\",\"info\":\"Because of its fast switching capability and rugged construction, the 90NF03 MOSFET is widely used in DC motor control systems, inverter circuits, SMPS power supplies, battery-powered equipment, DC-DC converters, automotive electronics, and high-power LED driver circuits. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, allowing convenient mounting on a heat sink for improved thermal performance during continuous high-load operation. For stable and reliable performance, designers typically use a suitable gate drive voltage (around 10 V), a gate resistor for controlled switching, and protection components such as flyback diodes when driving inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773645284548-763498640.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 07:14:44'),
(5112,1,'product',3152,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"15N120\",\"description\":\"15N120 (commonly known as STP15N120) is a high-voltage N-channel power MOSFET designed for switching and power control in high-voltage electronic circuits. It is typically rated for a drain-source voltage of about 1200 V and can handle continuous drain current around 12 A to 15 A, depending on operating conditions and proper heat dissipation. The device offers stable switching performance and moderate ON-state resistance, making it suitable for applications where high voltage handling capability is required.\",\"info\":\"Because of its rugged construction and reliable operation, the 15N120 MOSFET is widely used in switch-mode power supplies (SMPS), inverter circuits, industrial power control systems, LED driver circuits, AC-DC converters, and high-voltage DC-DC converter designs. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, allowing easy mounting on a heat sink for improved thermal management during continuous high-load operation. For safe and stable performance, designers usually provide an appropriate gate drive voltage, gate resistor for controlled switching, and protection components such as snubber networks or flyback diodes when switching inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773645349756-350158405.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 07:15:49'),
(5113,1,'product',3153,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"5LO380\",\"description\":\"5LO380 is a high-voltage power switching device (commonly used as a MOSFET or power transistor depending on manufacturer series) designed for use in switch-mode power supplies and high-voltage electronic circuits. It is typically capable of handling high collector/drain voltage in the range of about 700 V–900 V and supports moderate current levels, making it suitable for off-line power supply and inverter applications. The device is built for reliable switching performance, good thermal stability, and rugged operation in demanding power control environments.\",\"info\":\"Because of its high-voltage capability, the 5LO380 is commonly used in SMPS circuits, LED driver power stages, inverter sections, industrial power control systems, CRT/monitor power units, and AC-DC conversion circuits. It is generally available in a TO-220 or similar power package, allowing convenient mounting on a heat sink for efficient heat dissipation during continuous operation. For safe and stable use, designers typically include proper gate/base drive circuitry, snubber or protection networks, and adequate cooling arrangements in practical power designs.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773645414433-553032774.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 07:16:54'),
(5114,1,'product',3154,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"FAN7392\",\"description\":\"FAN7392 is a high-speed high-side and low-side gate driver IC designed to drive MOSFETs or IGBTs in half-bridge and full-bridge power switching circuits. It is capable of operating with high floating supply voltage (up to around 600 V) and provides strong output drive capability for efficient switching performance. The IC includes features such as under-voltage lockout (UVLO), matched propagation delay, and high noise immunity, making it suitable for reliable operation in high-power electronic systems.\",\"info\":\"Because of its fast switching characteristics and robust design, the FAN7392 is widely used in inverter circuits, motor drive systems, induction heating equipment, switching mode power supplies (SMPS), UPS systems, and DC-AC converter applications. It is commonly available in a SOP / DIP power package, allowing compact PCB mounting in modern power electronics designs. For proper operation, designers typically use suitable bootstrap components, gate resistors, proper PCB layout, and adequate isolation techniques to ensure stable and efficient switching performance.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773646177194-922611147.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 07:29:37'),
(5115,1,'product',3155,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"FQA38N30\",\"description\":\"FQA38N30 is a high-power N-channel MOSFET designed for efficient switching and power control in medium-to-high voltage electronic circuits. It is typically rated for a drain-source voltage of about 300 V and can handle continuous drain current around 30 A to 38 A, depending on operating temperature and heat-sink conditions. The device features low ON-state resistance and fast switching capability, which helps reduce power loss and improve efficiency in high-power switching applications.\",\"info\":\"Because of its rugged construction and reliable performance, the FQA38N30 MOSFET is widely used in inverter systems, switching mode power supplies (SMPS), motor control circuits, DC-DC converters, induction heating equipment, UPS systems, and power amplifier stages. It is generally available in a TO-3P / TO-247 style power package, allowing secure mounting on a heat sink for effective thermal dissipation during continuous high-load operation. For stable performance, designers typically use a suitable gate drive voltage (around 10–15 V), gate resistor for controlled switching, and protective components such as snubber or flyback networks when driving inductive loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773646263802-929197365.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 07:31:03'),
(5116,1,'product',3156,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IR2110\",\"description\":\"IR2110 is a widely used high-side and low-side gate driver IC designed to drive MOSFETs and IGBTs in half-bridge and full-bridge power switching circuits. It can operate with a high-side floating voltage up to about 500–600 V, making it suitable for high-voltage inverter and motor control applications. The IC provides high peak output current, fast switching speed, under-voltage lockout protection, and strong noise immunity, which helps ensure efficient and reliable switching performance.\",\"info\":\"Because of its versatility and rugged design, the IR2110 is commonly used in DC-AC inverters, UPS systems, SMPS power supplies, induction heating equipment, solar inverter circuits, and motor driver applications. It is available in DIP and SOIC packages, allowing easy integration into both prototype and compact PCB designs. For proper operation, designers typically use suitable bootstrap components, gate resistors, proper PCB grounding/layout, and isolation techniques to achieve stable and efficient switching in practical power electronics circuits.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773646343690-995315759.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 07:32:23'),
(5117,1,'product',3157,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IR2121\",\"description\":\"IR2121 is a high-performance high-side gate driver IC designed to drive N-channel MOSFETs or IGBTs in high-voltage power switching applications. It can operate with a floating high-side voltage up to about 600 V, making it suitable for off-line and industrial power control circuits. The device provides fast switching capability, high peak gate drive current, under-voltage lockout protection, and built-in over-current detection, which helps improve system reliability and protection.\",\"info\":\"Because of its robust design and protective features, the IR2121 is widely used in inverter circuits, motor drive systems, switching mode power supplies (SMPS), UPS equipment, induction heating units, and DC-AC converter applications. It is commonly available in DIP or SOIC packages, allowing convenient PCB mounting in both prototype and compact power electronics designs. For stable operation, designers typically use proper bootstrap supply components, gate resistors, current-sense networks, and careful PCB layout to ensure efficient and reliable switching performance.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773646409908-643721585.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 07:33:29'),
(5118,1,'product',3158,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"IR2152\",\"description\":\"IR2152 is a self-oscillating half-bridge gate driver IC designed to drive MOSFETs or IGBTs in high-voltage power conversion circuits. It combines a high-side and low-side driver with an internal oscillator, allowing simple implementation of half-bridge inverter and SMPS designs without requiring an external PWM controller. The IC can typically operate with floating high-side voltage up to about 600 V, making it suitable for offline AC-DC and DC-AC power applications.\",\"info\":\"Because of its built-in oscillator, reliable switching performance, and simple circuit design, the IR2152 is widely used in electronic ballasts, SMPS power supplies, inverter circuits, LED drivers, induction heating units, and low-cost DC-AC converter applications. It is commonly available in DIP and SOIC packages, enabling easy PCB mounting for both prototype and compact power electronics systems. For stable and efficient operation, designers generally use suitable bootstrap components, timing resistor-capacitor network, gate resistors, and proper PCB grounding/layout techniques.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773646573038-974491053.jpg\"}','2026-03-16 07:36:13'),
(5119,1,'product',3159,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"AD421 BN\",\"description\":\"AD421BN is a precision 4–20 mA current loop transmitter IC developed for industrial process control and instrumentation applications. It is designed to convert digital or analog input signals into a standard 4–20 mA current output, which is widely used in industrial automation systems for reliable long-distance signal transmission with high noise immunity. The device integrates key functions such as voltage regulation, current control circuitry, reference source, and protection features, enabling simple and accurate implementation of transmitter modules.\",\"info\":\"Because of its high accuracy and stable performance, the AD421BN is commonly used in PLC systems, industrial sensors, pressure and temperature transmitters, data acquisition systems, and process control equipment. It is generally available in a DIP package, allowing easy PCB mounting and integration into industrial electronic designs. For proper operation, designers typically use suitable external sensing components, calibration networks, and filtering arrangements to achieve precise and reliable current loop transmission.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773647309818-373600016.jpg\"}','2026-03-16 07:48:29'),
(5120,1,'product',3160,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"AD536 AJH\",\"description\":\"AD536AJH is a precision true RMS-to-DC converter integrated circuit manufactured for accurate measurement of AC signals. It converts an AC input waveform into a proportional DC output voltage representing the true RMS value, independent of waveform shape. The device offers high accuracy, wide dynamic range, and good temperature stability, making it suitable for precision instrumentation and signal processing applications.\",\"info\":\"Because of its reliable performance and ability to measure complex waveforms, the AD536AJH is widely used in digital multimeters, power measurement equipment, audio level monitoring systems, industrial instrumentation, data acquisition systems, and laboratory test equipment. It is typically available in a metal can (TO-100 / TO-99 style) or DIP package, allowing secure mounting and shielding for sensitive measurement circuits. For proper operation, designers usually provide external averaging components, calibration adjustments, and proper shielding/grounding techniques to achieve stable and accurate RMS measurements.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773647411949-440556752.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 07:50:11'),
(5121,1,'product',3161,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"AD581 JH\",\"description\":\"AD581JH is a high-stability precision voltage reference IC designed to provide an accurate and temperature-compensated reference voltage for analog and digital measurement systems. It typically offers a stable reference output (commonly around 10 V) with low drift, low noise, and excellent long-term stability, making it suitable for precision instrumentation and calibration circuits. The device integrates internal temperature compensation and trimming, ensuring consistent performance over a wide operating temperature range.\",\"info\":\"Due to its reliable accuracy and robust construction, the AD581JH is widely used in digital multimeters, data acquisition systems, ADC/DAC reference circuits, laboratory test equipment, industrial process control instruments, and calibration standards. It is commonly available in a metal can (TO-99 / TO-100 style) package, which provides good shielding and thermal stability for sensitive analog applications. For best performance, designers typically use proper decoupling capacitors, stable power supply filtering, and careful PCB layout to maintain precision and reduce noise effects.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773647471043-107385278.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 07:51:11'),
(5122,1,'product',3162,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"AD590\",\"description\":\"AD590 is a precision two-terminal temperature sensor IC that outputs a current proportional to absolute temperature. It typically produces 1 µA per Kelvin (µA/K), which means the output current changes linearly with temperature, making it easy to measure temperature using simple resistor or amplifier circuits. The device offers high accuracy, good linearity, low self-heating, and excellent long-term stability, making it suitable for precision temperature sensing applications.\",\"info\":\"Because of its reliable performance and simple interface, the AD590 is widely used in industrial temperature monitoring, HVAC systems, data acquisition equipment, instrumentation, thermal protection circuits, and scientific measurement systems. It is commonly available in metal can (TO-52 / TO-99) and TO-92 packages, allowing flexible mounting for both laboratory and industrial environments. For best accuracy, designers typically use stable biasing, proper calibration, and shielding or filtering techniques to reduce noise and improve measurement stability.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773647545421-188371190.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 07:52:25'),
(5123,1,'product',3163,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"AD620\",\"description\":\"AD620 is a low-cost, high-accuracy instrumentation amplifier IC widely used for amplifying very small differential signals in noisy environments. It offers high input impedance, low offset voltage, low noise, and excellent common-mode rejection ratio (CMRR), making it ideal for precision signal conditioning applications. The amplifier gain can be easily set from 1 to 1000 using a single external resistor, which simplifies circuit design and calibration.\",\"info\":\"Because of its stable performance and easy gain control, the AD620 is commonly used in medical instrumentation (such as ECG/EEG amplifiers), load cell and strain gauge signal conditioning, temperature measurement systems, data acquisition equipment, industrial process control, and sensor interface circuits. It is typically available in DIP and SOIC packages, allowing convenient use in both prototype and compact PCB designs. For best performance, designers usually apply proper power supply decoupling, shielding, and careful PCB layout to reduce noise and ensure accurate signal amplification.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773647616582-871087495.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 07:53:36'),
(5124,1,'product',3164,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"AD633JH\",\"description\":\"AD633JH is a precision four-quadrant analog multiplier IC used for mathematical signal processing in analog circuits. It can perform operations such as multiplication, division, modulation, demodulation, squaring, and frequency mixing of analog signals. The device features laser-trimmed accuracy, wide bandwidth, low offset, and good temperature stability, making it suitable for reliable signal processing applications.\",\"info\":\"Because of its versatility and stable performance, the AD633JH is widely used in communication systems (AM modulation and demodulation), signal conditioning circuits, automatic gain control systems, instrumentation, function generators, and analog computation circuits. It is commonly available in a metal can (TO-99 / TO-100 style) or DIP package, allowing good shielding and easy integration into precision analog designs. For best results, designers typically use proper power supply decoupling, signal filtering, and careful PCB grounding/layout techniques to maintain accuracy and reduce noise effects.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773647682635-291253996.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 07:54:42'),
(5125,1,'product',3165,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"AD7538\",\"description\":\"AD7538 is an 8-bit digital-to-analog converter (DAC) IC designed to convert digital input data into a proportional analog output signal. It features a current output architecture, good linearity, fast settling time, and low power consumption, making it suitable for precision signal generation and control applications. The device is compatible with standard microprocessor and microcontroller systems, allowing easy interfacing for digital control of analog circuits.\",\"info\":\"Because of its reliable performance and simple interface, the AD7538 is widely used in data acquisition systems, waveform generation circuits, industrial control equipment, instrumentation, programmable gain control systems, and communication electronics. It is commonly available in a DIP package, enabling convenient PCB mounting in both prototype and production designs. For accurate operation, designers typically use a stable reference source, output amplifier stage, proper decoupling capacitors, and careful PCB layout to ensure clean and precise analog output signals.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773651500431-90519442.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 08:58:20'),
(5126,1,'product',3166,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"AD7541\",\"description\":\"AD7541 is a precision 12-bit digital-to-analog converter (DAC) IC designed to convert digital input data into a proportional analog output signal. It uses a current-output R-2R ladder architecture, providing good linearity, fast settling time, and low power consumption, which makes it suitable for high-accuracy signal generation and control applications. The device can be easily interfaced with microprocessors and microcontrollers, allowing digital systems to control analog circuits with high resolution.\",\"info\":\"Because of its stable performance and precision characteristics, the AD7541 is widely used in data acquisition systems, programmable power supplies, waveform generation circuits, instrumentation equipment, industrial process control, and communication electronics. It is typically available in a DIP package, enabling convenient PCB mounting for both laboratory and production designs. For reliable and accurate operation, designers usually provide a stable reference voltage source, output amplifier stage, proper power-supply decoupling, and careful PCB grounding/layout to minimize noise and maintain output accuracy.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773651577878-798365895.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 08:59:37'),
(5127,1,'product',3167,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"AD7703\",\"description\":\"AD7703 is a precision sigma-delta analog-to-digital converter (ADC) designed for measuring low-level analog signals with high resolution and accuracy. It typically provides 16-bit resolution, low noise performance, and built-in digital filtering, making it suitable for direct interface with sensors such as load cells, pressure sensors, and temperature transducers. The device includes an on-chip programmable gain amplifier (PGA) and reference circuitry, which simplifies signal conditioning and reduces the need for external components.\",\"info\":\"Because of its high accuracy and stable operation, the AD7703 is widely used in industrial process control, weighing scales, instrumentation systems, data acquisition equipment, and microcontroller-based measurement applications. It is commonly available in DIP and surface-mount packages, allowing flexible integration into both prototype and compact PCB designs. For reliable performance, designers typically use proper reference voltage sources, input filtering networks, decoupling capacitors, and careful PCB layout to minimize noise and achieve precise digital conversion results.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773651780773-241488310.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 09:03:00'),
(5128,1,'product',3168,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"AD7705\",\"description\":\"AD7705 is a precision 16-bit sigma-delta analog-to-digital converter (ADC) designed for accurate measurement of low-level analog signals. It features an on-chip programmable gain amplifier (PGA), digital filtering, and serial interface, allowing direct connection to sensors and microcontrollers with minimal external components. The device provides high resolution, low noise performance, and excellent accuracy, making it suitable for applications requiring precise data acquisition and signal conditioning.\",\"info\":\"Because of its reliable performance and simple interfacing capability, the AD7705 is widely used in weighing scales and load cell systems, industrial process control, temperature and pressure measurement, instrumentation equipment, data acquisition systems, and microcontroller-based monitoring circuits. It is commonly available in DIP and surface-mount packages, enabling flexible PCB integration for both prototype and production designs. For best results, designers typically use stable reference voltage sources, proper input filtering, decoupling capacitors, and careful PCB layout to reduce noise and ensure accurate digital conversion.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773652212767-231657942.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 09:10:12'),
(5129,1,'product',3169,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"AD7751\",\"description\":\"AD7751 is a dedicated single-phase energy metering IC designed for accurate measurement of electrical power consumption in AC systems. It integrates precision analog-to-digital conversion, digital signal processing, and pulse output circuitry, enabling direct calculation of real power and energy usage. The device accepts voltage and current inputs from sensors such as current transformers or shunt resistors and provides a frequency or pulse output proportional to consumed energy, which can be easily interfaced with microcontrollers or counters.\",\"info\":\"Because of its high accuracy, low drift, and stable performance, the AD7751 is widely used in electronic energy meters, smart power monitoring systems, industrial power measurement equipment, billing meters, and load monitoring applications. It is commonly available in DIP and surface-mount packages, allowing convenient PCB mounting in both prototype and commercial metering designs. For reliable operation, designers typically use proper signal conditioning networks, stable reference components, input filtering, and careful PCB layout to achieve precise energy measurement and long-term stability.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773652306863-505493960.jpg\"}','2026-03-16 09:11:46'),
(5130,1,'product',3170,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"OP177\",\"description\":\"OP177 is a high-precision operational amplifier (op-amp) designed for applications requiring very low offset voltage, low drift, and excellent long-term stability. It offers low noise performance and high open-loop gain, making it ideal for accurate signal amplification and conditioning in precision analog circuits. The device operates over a wide supply voltage range and maintains stable performance across varying temperatures.\",\"info\":\"Because of its reliable accuracy and stability, the OP177 is widely used in instrumentation systems, data acquisition equipment, sensor signal conditioning circuits, precision voltage references, active filters, and industrial measurement applications. It is typically available in DIP and metal can packages, allowing flexible integration into both laboratory prototypes and compact PCB designs. For best performance, designers generally use proper power supply decoupling, shielding, and careful PCB grounding/layout techniques to minimize noise and maintain high measurement accuracy.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773653189026-346820422.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 09:26:29'),
(5131,1,'product',3171,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"TOP223Y\",\"description\":\"TOP223Y is an integrated offline switch-mode power supply (SMPS) controller IC from Power Integrations, designed for efficient AC-DC power conversion in low-power electronic equipment. It combines a high-voltage power MOSFET, PWM controller, oscillator, protection circuitry, and thermal shutdown within a single device, which simplifies SMPS design and reduces the need for external components. The IC typically operates directly from mains input after rectification, making it suitable for compact and cost-effective power supply solutions.\",\"info\":\"Because of its high efficiency, built-in protection features, and simple circuit implementation, the TOP223Y is widely used in mobile chargers, standby power supplies, TV and set-top box power units, adapters, LED driver circuits, and various consumer electronic SMPS applications. It is commonly available in a TO-220 style package, allowing easy mounting with proper heat dissipation arrangements. For reliable operation, designers usually include snubber networks, feedback circuitry, input filtering, and careful PCB layout to ensure stable and safe power conversion.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773653335003-488477826.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 09:28:55'),
(5132,1,'product',3172,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"TOP224Y\",\"description\":\"TOP224Y is an integrated offline switch-mode power supply (SMPS) controller IC developed by Power Integrations for compact and efficient AC-DC power conversion. It combines a high-voltage power MOSFET, PWM control circuitry, oscillator, current limiting, thermal shutdown, and protection features in a single device, which significantly reduces external component count and simplifies SMPS design. The IC is designed to operate directly from rectified mains input, making it suitable for low-power power supplies used in consumer and industrial electronics.\",\"info\":\"Due to its high efficiency, built-in safety protections, and simple implementation, the TOP224Y is widely used in mobile phone chargers, standby power supplies, television and set-top box SMPS units, adapters, LED drivers, battery chargers, and other compact offline power supply applications. It is typically available in a TO-220 style package, allowing easy heat dissipation when mounted on a suitable heat sink or PCB copper area. For reliable operation, designers generally include proper input filtering, snubber networks, feedback control circuits, and careful PCB layout to ensure stable and safe power conversion.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773653429249-608695311.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 09:30:29'),
(5133,1,'product',3173,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"TOP225Y\",\"description\":\"TOP225Y is an integrated offline switch-mode power supply (SMPS) controller IC from Power Integrations, designed for efficient AC-DC conversion in compact power supply designs. It incorporates a high-voltage power MOSFET, PWM controller, oscillator, current limiting, thermal shutdown, and other protection features within a single device, reducing the number of external components and simplifying circuit design. The IC is intended to operate directly from rectified AC mains, making it suitable for low-to-medium power offline SMPS applications.\",\"info\":\"Because of its high efficiency, built-in safety protections, and ease of implementation, the TOP225Y is widely used in mobile chargers, standby power supplies, TV and set-top box SMPS circuits, LED driver units, battery chargers, adapters, and various consumer electronic power supplies. It is typically available in a TO-220 style package, allowing effective heat dissipation when mounted on a heat sink or PCB copper area. For stable and reliable operation, designers usually include proper input EMI filtering, snubber networks, feedback regulation components, and careful PCB layout to ensure safe and efficient power conversion.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773653512409-100649257.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 09:31:52'),
(5134,1,'product',3174,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"TOP226Y\",\"description\":\"TOP226Y is an integrated offline switch-mode power supply (SMPS) controller IC designed for efficient AC-DC power conversion in low-to-medium power electronic equipment. It combines a high-voltage power MOSFET, PWM controller, oscillator, current limiting, thermal shutdown, and fault protection circuitry in a single device, which reduces external component count and simplifies SMPS circuit design. The IC is intended to operate directly from rectified AC mains input, making it suitable for compact and cost-effective power supply solutions.\",\"info\":\"Because of its high efficiency, reliable protection features, and simple implementation, the TOP226Y is widely used in mobile and laptop adapters, standby power supplies, television and set-top box SMPS units, LED driver circuits, battery chargers, and other consumer or industrial offline power supply applications. It is typically available in a TO-220 style package, allowing effective heat dissipation when mounted on a suitable heat sink or PCB copper area. For stable operation, designers generally include proper input EMI filtering, snubber networks, feedback regulation components, and careful PCB layout techniques to ensure safe and efficient power conversion\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773653628826-566182275.jpeg\"}','2026-03-16 09:33:48'),
