(5178,1,'product',3212,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"LNK409EG\",\"description\":\"LNK409EG is an integrated offline switch-mode power supply (SMPS) controller IC from the LinkSwitch-PH series by Power Integrations, mainly designed for isolated LED driver and power conversion applications. The device combines a high-voltage power MOSFET, PWM control circuitry, oscillator, current limiting, thermal shutdown, and auto-restart protection in a single package. This high level of integration simplifies circuit design, reduces the number of external components, and improves overall system reliability. It is intended to operate directly from rectified AC mains input, making it suitable for compact and efficient LED lighting power supplies.\",\"info\":\"Because of its high efficiency, accurate current control capability, and built-in protection features, the LNK409EG is widely used in LED bulbs, LED panel drivers, street lighting power supplies, industrial lighting systems, adapters, and other offline AC-DC converter applications. It is typically available in an eSIP package, allowing effective heat dissipation when mounted on a suitable heat sink or PCB copper area. For stable and safe operation, designers generally include proper input EMI filtering, snubber networks, feedback regulation circuitry, and careful PCB layout to ensure efficient and long-term power conversion performance.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773729875384-454770876.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 06:44:35'),
(5179,1,'product',3213,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"LNK419EG\",\"description\":\"LNK419EG is an integrated offline switch-mode power supply (SMPS) controller IC from the LinkSwitch-PH series by Power Integrations, specially designed for isolated LED driver and AC-DC power conversion applications. The device integrates a high-voltage power MOSFET, PWM control circuit, oscillator, precise current-control circuitry, current limiting, thermal shutdown, and auto-restart protection within a single package. This high level of integration simplifies circuit design, reduces external component count, and improves system reliability. It is intended to operate directly from rectified AC mains input, making it suitable for compact and energy-efficient lighting power supplies.\",\"info\":\"Because of its high efficiency, good power factor capability, and accurate constant-current output performance, the LNK419EG is widely used in LED bulb drivers, LED panel light power supplies, street lighting systems, industrial lighting units, adapters, and other offline AC-DC converter applications. It is commonly available in an eSIP package, which allows effective heat dissipation when mounted on a suitable heat sink or PCB copper area. For stable and reliable operation, designers typically include proper input EMI filtering, snubber networks, feedback regulation components, and careful PCB layout techniques to ensure efficient and long-term power conversion.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773730385342-741360381.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 06:53:05'),
(5180,1,'product',3214,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"LNK460VG\",\"description\":\"LNK460VG is an integrated offline switch-mode power supply (SMPS) controller IC from the LinkSwitch-PL series by Power Integrations. It is mainly designed for isolated constant-current LED driver and AC-DC power conversion applications. The device combines a high-voltage power MOSFET, PWM controller, oscillator, accurate current regulation circuitry, current limiting, thermal shutdown, and auto-restart protection within a single compact package. This high level of integration reduces external component count, simplifies design, and improves overall system reliability. It is intended to operate directly from rectified AC mains input, making it suitable for compact and efficient lighting power supplies.\",\"info\":\"Because of its high efficiency, good power factor capability, and precise constant-current output, the LNK460VG is widely used in LED bulb drivers, LED panel lights, street lighting systems, industrial lighting power supplies, adapters, and other offline AC-DC converter circuits. It is typically available in an eSIP-7C / eSIP-style power package, allowing effective heat dissipation when mounted on a suitable heat sink or PCB copper area. For stable and safe operation, designers usually include proper input EMI filtering, snubber or surge protection components, feedback regulation networks, and careful PCB layout techniques to ensure efficient and long-term power conversion performance.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773730516824-644751061.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 06:55:16'),
(5181,1,'product',3215,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"LNK460KG\",\"description\":\"LNK460KG is an integrated offline switch-mode power supply (SMPS) controller IC from the LinkSwitch-PL family by Power Integrations. It is mainly designed for isolated constant-current LED driver and AC-DC power conversion applications. The device integrates a high-voltage power MOSFET, PWM control circuitry, oscillator, accurate current-regulation circuit, current-limit protection, thermal shutdown, and auto-restart fault protection in a single compact package. This high level of integration reduces external component count and simplifies the design of efficient offline power supplies.\",\"info\":\"Because of its high efficiency, low standby consumption, good power-factor capability, and precise constant-current output, the LNK460KG is widely used in LED bulb drivers, LED panel and street lighting power supplies, industrial lighting systems, adapters, and various consumer or industrial AC-DC converter circuits. It is typically available in an eSIP-7C / eSIP-style power package, allowing effective heat dissipation when mounted on a suitable heat sink or PCB copper area. For stable and reliable operation, designers generally include proper input EMI filtering, surge/snubber protection networks, feedback regulation components, and careful PCB layout techniques to ensure safe and long-term power conversion performance.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773730674325-2782927.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 06:57:54'),
(5182,1,'product',3216,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"LNK501PN\",\"description\":\"LNK501PN is an integrated offline switch-mode power supply (SMPS) switching IC from the LinkSwitch family by Power Integrations. It combines a high-voltage power MOSFET, oscillator, ON/OFF control scheme, current-limit protection, thermal shutdown, and auto-restart fault protection within a single compact device. This high level of integration reduces external component count and simplifies the design of low-power AC-DC flyback converter circuits. The IC is designed to operate directly from rectified AC mains input, making it suitable for compact and economical power supply solutions.\",\"info\":\"Because of its high efficiency, low standby power consumption, and built-in safety protections, the LNK501PN is widely used in mobile phone chargers, standby power supplies, small power adapters, LED driver circuits, appliance control modules, and various consumer electronic auxiliary power supplies. It is typically available in a DIP-8 package, allowing convenient PCB mounting and reliable operation in production designs. For stable and safe performance, designers usually include proper input EMI filtering, snubber or surge protection components, feedback regulation circuitry, and careful PCB layout techniques to ensure efficient and long-term power conversion.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773730813190-138121017.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 07:00:13'),
(5183,1,'product',3217,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"LNK604PG\",\"description\":\"LNK604PG is an integrated offline switch-mode power supply (SMPS) controller IC from the LinkSwitch-II / LinkSwitch family by Power Integrations. It combines a high-voltage power MOSFET, internal oscillator, ON-OFF control method, current-limit protection, thermal shutdown, and auto-restart fault protection within a single compact device. This high level of integration significantly reduces the number of external components and simplifies the design of low-power isolated AC-DC flyback converters. The IC is designed to operate directly from rectified AC mains input, making it suitable for compact and cost-effective power supply designs.\",\"info\":\"Because of its high efficiency, low standby power consumption, and reliable built-in protection features, the LNK604PG is widely used in mobile phone chargers, standby auxiliary power supplies, small AC-DC adapters, LED driver circuits, appliance control power modules, and various consumer electronic SMPS applications. It is typically available in a DIP-8C package, allowing convenient PCB mounting and dependable performance in practical circuits. For stable and safe operation, designers generally include proper input EMI filtering, snubber or surge protection networks, feedback regulation components, and careful PCB layout techniques to ensure efficient and long-term power conversion.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773733512788-174905903.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 07:45:12'),
(5184,1,'product',3218,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"LNK605DG\",\"description\":\"LNK605DG is an integrated offline switch-mode power supply (SMPS) controller IC from the LinkSwitch-II family by Power Integrations. It incorporates a high-voltage power MOSFET, internal oscillator, ON/OFF control scheme, current-limit protection, thermal shutdown, and auto-restart fault protection within a single compact device. This high level of integration reduces the need for many external components and simplifies the design of low-power isolated AC-DC flyback converters. The IC is intended to operate directly from rectified AC mains input, making it suitable for compact and cost-effective power supply designs.\",\"info\":\"Because of its high efficiency, low standby power consumption, and built-in protection features, the LNK605DG is widely used in mobile chargers, standby auxiliary power supplies, small AC-DC adapters, LED driver circuits, appliance control modules, and various consumer electronic SMPS applications. It is typically available in a SO-8 (surface-mount) package, allowing compact PCB layout and reliable operation in modern power supply designs. For stable and safe performance, designers generally include proper input EMI filtering, snubber or surge protection components, feedback regulation circuitry, and careful PCB layout techniques to ensure efficient and long-term power conversion.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[651],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773734088649-31471898.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 07:54:48'),
