(5193,1,'product',3225,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"93LC66\",\"description\":\"93LC66 is a serial EEPROM (Electrically Erasable Programmable Read-Only Memory) IC used for reliable non-volatile data storage in electronic circuits. It typically provides 4 Kbit (512 × 8 or 256 × 16) memory capacity and uses a Microwire serial interface, allowing easy communication with microcontrollers and digital systems using only a few control pins. The device supports low power consumption, high data retention, and multiple write/erase cycles, making it suitable for long-term storage of configuration or calibration data.\",\"info\":\"Because of its compact design and dependable performance, the 93LC66 is widely used in embedded systems, industrial control equipment, instrumentation, communication devices, automotive electronics, and consumer products. It is commonly available in DIP and surface-mount packages, enabling flexible PCB integration. For proper operation, designers typically use pull-up resistors, proper clock timing, and stable power supply decoupling to ensure accurate data communication and reliable memory performance.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773736446445-656205603.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 08:34:06'),
(5194,1,'product',3226,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"24LC256\",\"description\":\"24LC256 is a widely used serial EEPROM (Electrically Erasable Programmable Read-Only Memory) IC designed for non-volatile data storage in embedded electronic systems. It provides 256 Kbit (32K × 8) memory capacity and communicates through a standard I²C (two-wire) interface, which allows easy connection to microcontrollers using only SDA (data) and SCL (clock) lines. The device supports low power operation, high write endurance, and long data retention, making it suitable for storing configuration settings, calibration values, logs, and other important data.\",\"info\":\"Because of its compact size and reliable performance, the 24LC256 is commonly used in microcontroller-based projects, industrial automation systems, instrumentation, communication devices, automotive electronics, and consumer products. It is available in DIP and surface-mount packages, enabling flexible PCB design. For stable operation, designers typically include pull-up resistors on the I²C lines, proper supply decoupling, and correct device addressing to ensure accurate data transfer and dependable memory performance.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773736621788-55071950.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 08:37:01'),
(5195,1,'product',3227,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"24LC512\",\"description\":\"24LC512 is a 512-Kbit (64 KB) serial EEPROM memory integrated circuit widely used for non-volatile data storage in electronic and embedded systems. It communicates through the I²C two-wire interface, allowing easy connection with microcontrollers such as Arduino, PIC, AVR, and ARM controllers. The device operates over a wide supply voltage range of 2.5 V to 5.5 V, making it suitable for both low-power and standard logic applications.\",\"info\":\"The IC includes three hardware address pins (A0–A2) that enable multiple devices to be connected on the same I²C bus, and a write-protect (WP) pin to prevent accidental data modification. The 24LC512 is commonly used in data logging, configuration storage, calibration data saving, consumer electronics, industrial control systems, smart meters, and IoT devices, where secure and permanent storage of small to medium amounts of data is required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773736820425-578589897.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 08:40:20'),
(5196,1,'product',3228,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"12F675\",\"description\":\"PIC12F675 is a compact 8-bit microcontroller from Microchip, designed for low-cost and space-constrained embedded applications. It belongs to the PIC12 family and comes in a small 8-pin package, making it suitable for simple control circuits and compact electronic projects. The controller features 1K words of Flash program memory, 64 bytes of EEPROM data memory, and 64 bytes of RAM, allowing it to store program instructions as well as non-volatile user data.\",\"info\":\"It operates with a supply voltage typically between 2.0 V and 5.5 V and includes an internal 4 MHz oscillator, which eliminates the need for an external crystal in many designs. The PIC12F675 provides six general-purpose I/O pins, an integrated 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels, timers, comparator modules, and power-saving features such as sleep mode and watchdog timer. Due to its simplicity, low power consumption, and built-in peripherals, it is commonly used in sensor interfacing, small automation systems, battery-powered devices, LED control circuits, security products, and basic embedded control applications where reliable and efficient microcontroller operation is required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773736914876-635780415.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 08:41:54'),
(5197,1,'product',3229,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"12F508\",\"description\":\"IC12F508 is a small and cost-effective 8-bit microcontroller from Microchip, designed for simple embedded control applications where minimal size and low power consumption are important. It is available in an 8-pin package and provides 512 words of program memory, 25 bytes of RAM, and a limited number of general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with external components. The device operates over a wide supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator (typically 4 MHz), which removes the need for an external clock in most designs.\",\"info\":\"The PIC12F508 features basic peripherals such as Timer0, watchdog timer, internal reset circuitry, and power-saving sleep mode, enabling reliable operation in low-power electronic systems. Unlike some higher models, it does not include built-in ADC or EEPROM data memory, making it suitable mainly for simple switching, timing, LED control, small automation circuits, alarms, toys, and basic consumer electronic products where straightforward programmable control is required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773737023893-841721425.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 08:43:43'),
(5198,1,'product',3230,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"12F509\",\"description\":\"PIC12F509 is a compact and low-cost 8-bit microcontroller from Microchip, designed for simple embedded control applications where small size and low power consumption are essential. It comes in an 8-pin package and provides 1K words of program memory and about 41 bytes of RAM, allowing it to handle basic control logic and timing tasks. The device operates within a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes a built-in internal RC oscillator (typically 4 MHz), which eliminates the need for an external crystal in many circuits.\",\"info\":\"The PIC12F509 offers general-purpose I/O pins, Timer0, a watchdog timer, power-on reset, and sleep mode for energy-efficient operation in battery-powered systems. It does not include advanced peripherals such as ADC or hardware serial communication, making it suitable for simple switching circuits, LED flashers, alarms, toys, remote controls, small automation devices, and basic consumer electronic products where reliable and economical programmable control is required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773737095089-750720604.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 08:44:55'),
(5199,1,'product',3231,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"12F510\",\"description\":\"PIC12F510 is a small and economical 8-bit microcontroller from Microchip, designed for simple embedded control applications that require low power consumption and minimal external components. It is available in an 8-pin package and features about 1K words of program memory and 64 bytes of RAM, providing sufficient space for basic control programs and temporary data storage. The microcontroller operates over a wide supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes a built-in internal oscillator (typically around 4 MHz), eliminating the need for an external clock source in most designs\",\"info\":\"It provides several general-purpose input/output pins, along with essential peripherals such as Timer0, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for efficient and reliable operation. The PIC12F510 does not include advanced modules like ADC or hardware serial communication, so it is mainly used in simple automation circuits, LED control units, small household electronics, security alarms, timers, toys, and battery-operated devices, where low cost, compact size, and dependable programmable control are important.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773737172300-212895346.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 08:46:12'),
(5200,1,'product',3232,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"12F615\",\"description\":\"PIC12F615 is a compact 8-bit microcontroller from Microchip, designed for low-cost and space-limited embedded control applications. It is available in an 8-pin package and provides around 1K words of Flash program memory, 64 bytes of EEPROM data memory, and 64 bytes of RAM, enabling both program storage and non-volatile data retention. The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes a built-in internal oscillator (up to 8 MHz), which reduces the need for external timing components.\",\"info\":\"The PIC12F615 offers up to six general-purpose I/O pins, an integrated 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) for reading analog signals, PWM capability for motor or LED brightness control, Timer0, comparator functions, watchdog timer, brown-out reset, and low-power sleep mode for energy-efficient operation. Because of its small size, built-in peripherals, and reliable performance, it is commonly used in sensor interfacing circuits, LED dimmers, small motor control systems, battery-powered devices, home appliances, security systems, and basic industrial or consumer electronic applications where simple programmable control and analog signal handling are required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773737258072-81747398.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 08:47:38'),
(5201,1,'product',3233,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"12F629\",\"description\":\"PIC12F629 is a compact and low-power 8-bit microcontroller from Microchip, widely used in small embedded control and automation applications. It is available in an 8-pin package and provides about 1K words of Flash program memory, 64 bytes of EEPROM data memory, and 64 bytes of RAM, allowing both program storage and non-volatile data retention. The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator (typically 4 MHz), which reduces the need for external clock components.\",\"info\":\"The PIC12F629 offers up to six general-purpose I/O pins, an internal comparator module, Timer0, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for efficient battery-operated designs. Although it does not include a built-in ADC module, it is suitable for digital control tasks such as LED control circuits, alarms, timers, small automation systems, remote control devices, security products, and simple consumer electronic equipment, where compact size, reliability, and economical programmable control are important.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773737369098-930364893.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 08:49:29'),
(5202,1,'product',3234,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"12F683\",\"description\":\"PIC12F683 is a small and efficient 8-bit microcontroller from Microchip, designed for compact embedded control applications that require low power consumption and built-in analog features. It is available in an 8-pin package and provides about 2K words of Flash program memory, 128 bytes of EEPROM data memory, and 128 bytes of RAM, offering adequate space for program execution and non-volatile data storage. The device operates over a wide supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator that can run up to 8 MHz, reducing the need for external timing components.\",\"info\":\"The PIC12F683 features up to six general-purpose I/O pins, a 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple channels for reading analog signals, PWM (CCP module) for motor speed or LED brightness control, Timer0 and Timer1, comparator module, watchdog timer, brown-out reset, and sleep mode for power-saving operation. Because of its compact size and integrated peripherals, it is commonly used in sensor interfacing, LED dimmers, battery-powered devices, small motor control systems, security circuits, home appliances, and general consumer or industrial electronic control applications where reliable and economical programmable control is required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773737468087-304490815.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 08:51:08'),
(5203,1,'product',3235,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16C54\",\"description\":\"PIC16C54 is an early-generation 8-bit microcontroller from Microchip, designed for simple embedded control applications requiring low cost and reliable operation. It belongs to the PIC16C5X family and is typically available in 18-pin and 28-pin packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output ports for interfacing with external devices. The controller uses OTP (One-Time Programmable) ROM program memory of about 512 words, along with a small amount of internal RAM for temporary data storage.\",\"info\":\"It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 3.0 V to 5.5 V and can work with either an external crystal/RC oscillator or clock source, depending on the configuration. The PIC16C54 includes basic built-in features such as Timer0, watchdog timer, power-on reset, and sleep mode for low-power operation. Although it does not provide advanced peripherals like ADC, EEPROM, or hardware serial communication, it is suitable for simple control tasks such as LED sequencing, alarm circuits, small automation systems, toys, timers, and basic consumer electronic products, where straightforward programmable logic and dependable performance are required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773737542780-470702383.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 08:52:22'),
(5204,1,'product',3236,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16C716\",\"description\":\"PIC16C716 is an 8-bit microcontroller from Microchip belonging to the PIC16C7X family, designed for embedded control applications that require both digital and analog interfacing. It is typically available in an 18-pin DIP or SOIC package and provides about 2K words of OTP (One-Time Programmable) program memory, along with RAM for data processing. The device operates with a supply voltage of approximately 4.0 V to 5.5 V and supports different clock sources such as external crystal, RC oscillator, or clock input, depending on system requirements.\",\"info\":\"One of the key features of the PIC16C716 is its built-in 8-channel 8-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC), which allows the microcontroller to directly read analog sensor signals. It also includes Timer0, watchdog timer, power-on reset, sleep mode for low-power operation, and multiple general-purpose I/O pins for controlling external circuits. Although it does not provide advanced communication peripherals like hardware UART or I²C modules, it is suitable for sensor monitoring systems, industrial control units, measurement instruments, small automation devices, motor control circuits, and consumer electronic products, where basic analog signal processing and dependable programmable control are required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773737644374-614552659.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 08:54:04'),
(5205,1,'product',3237,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F72\",\"description\":\"PIC16F72 is an 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for reliable embedded control and automation applications that require both digital and analog interfacing. It belongs to the PIC16F7X family and is commonly available in a 28-pin DIP or SOIC package, providing multiple input/output ports for connecting external components. The controller features about 2K words of Flash program memory, 128 bytes of RAM, and non-volatile data storage capability, allowing easy reprogramming during development and field updates.\",\"info\":\"The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and supports various clock options such as external crystal, RC oscillator, or clock input. A key feature of the PIC16F72 is its built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels, enabling direct interfacing with analog sensors and measurement circuits. It also includes Timer0, Timer1 and Timer2, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, PWM capability (CCP module), and low-power sleep mode for efficient system operation.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773737720736-7858366.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 08:55:20'),
(5206,1,'product',3238,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F73\",\"description\":\"PIC16F73 is a versatile 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require multiple peripherals and analog signal processing capability. It belongs to the PIC16F7X family and is typically available in a 28-pin DIP or SOIC package, offering several general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with external circuits. The microcontroller provides about 4K words of Flash program memory, 192 bytes of RAM, and 128 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing both program storage and non-volatile data retention.\",\"info\":\"It operates within a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and supports different clock options such as external crystal, RC oscillator, or external clock input. The PIC16F73 includes a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels, making it suitable for reading analog sensor signals. It also features Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, PWM capability through the CCP module, SPI/I²C (MSSP) serial communication interface, watchdog timer, brown-out reset, power-on reset, and low-power sleep mode for energy-efficient operation.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773737802129-568798089.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 08:56:42'),
(5207,1,'product',3239,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F74\",\"description\":\"PIC16F74 is a powerful and widely used 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require multiple input/output lines and integrated analog features. It belongs to the PIC16F7X family and is commonly available in a 40-pin DIP or 44-pin SMD package, providing several digital I/O ports for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, and other external devices. The microcontroller offers about 4K words of Flash program memory, 192 bytes of RAM, and 128 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing easy program updates and reliable storage of user data or configuration parameters.\",\"info\":\"The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and supports different clock sources such as external crystal, RC oscillator, or external clock input. A major feature of the PIC16F74 is its built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple channels for accurate reading of analog signals. It also includes Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, PWM output through the CCP module for motor speed or LED brightness control, and a hardware SPI/I²C serial communication interface (MSSP) for connecting memory devices, sensors, or other controllers. Additional features such as watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode improve system reliability and energy efficiency.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773737873355-110653546.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 08:57:53'),
(5208,1,'product',3240,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F76\",\"description\":\"PIC16F76 is an advanced 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require multiple input/output ports and analog signal processing capability. It belongs to the PIC16F7X family and is typically available in a 28-pin DIP or SOIC package, providing several general-purpose I/O pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, and other external circuits. The microcontroller features about 8K words of Flash program memory, 368 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing efficient program execution and reliable non-volatile storage of configuration or user data.\",\"info\":\"The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and supports different clock options such as external crystal, RC oscillator, or external clock input. It includes a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for measuring analog signals, along with Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and PWM output through the CCP module for motor speed or LED brightness control. The PIC16F76 also provides a hardware SPI/I²C serial communication interface (MSSP) for easy connection to external memory devices, sensors, or other controllers. Additional features such as watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode enhance system reliability and energy efficiency.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773737950695-123460355.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 08:59:10'),
(5209,1,'product',3241,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F88\",\"description\":\"PIC16F88 is a compact and versatile 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, widely used in embedded control applications that require both digital and analog interfacing. It is commonly available in an 18-pin DIP or SOIC package and provides about 4K words of Flash program memory, 368 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable storage of program code as well as non-volatile user data. The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator that can run up to 8 MHz, reducing the need for external clock components in many designs.\",\"info\":\"The PIC16F88 features up to 16 general-purpose I/O pins, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for sensor interfacing, PWM output through the CCP module for motor speed or LED brightness control, and essential timing resources such as Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2. It also provides USART serial communication, comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for energy-efficient operation in battery-powered systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773738090962-765193872.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 09:01:30'),
(5210,1,'product',3242,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F505\",\"description\":\"PIC16F505 is a small and low-cost 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for simple embedded control and automation applications where compact size and low power consumption are important. It is typically available in 14-pin and 20-pin packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with switches, LEDs, relays, and other external components. The microcontroller features about 1K words of Flash program memory and 72 bytes of RAM, allowing basic program execution and temporary data storage.\",\"info\":\"The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator (typically around 4 MHz), which helps reduce the need for external clock circuitry. It provides essential built-in functions such as Timer0, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for reliable and energy-efficient operation. The PIC16F505 does not include advanced peripherals like ADC or hardware serial communication modules, making it most suitable for simple control systems such as LED flashing circuits, small automation devices, alarm systems, toys, timers, and basic consumer electronic products, where economical programmable control and dependable performance are required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773738167803-82856298.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 09:02:47'),
(5211,1,'product',3243,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F506\",\"description\":\"PIC16F506 is a compact and economical 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, intended for simple embedded control applications where low power consumption and small size are important. It is commonly available in 14-pin and 20-pin packages, providing several general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with switches, LEDs, relays, and other external components. The device offers about 1K words of Flash program memory and around 67 bytes of RAM, allowing basic program execution and temporary data storage for control tasks.\",\"info\":\"The microcontroller operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal RC oscillator (typically around 4 MHz), which reduces the need for external timing components in many designs. It incorporates essential built-in features such as Timer0, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode to improve reliability and energy efficiency, especially in battery-operated devices. Although it does not include advanced peripherals such as ADC modules or hardware communication interfaces, the PIC16F506 is widely used in simple automation systems, LED control circuits, timers, alarm units, small household electronics, toys, and other cost-sensitive consumer electronic applications where straightforward programmable control is required\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773738247794-248539764.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 09:04:07'),
(5212,1,'product',3244,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F616\",\"description\":\"PIC16F616 is a compact and low-power 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require reliable digital operation along with some integrated analog and timing features. It is commonly available in 14-pin and 20-pin packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with switches, LEDs, relays, sensors, and other external circuits. The microcontroller includes about 2K words of Flash program memory, 128 bytes of RAM, and 128 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing easy program updates and non-volatile storage of configuration or user data.\",\"info\":\"The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and features an internal oscillator that can run up to around 8 MHz, reducing the need for external clock components in many designs. It offers built-in peripherals such as Timer0, Timer1, Timer2, PWM capability (ECCP module) for motor speed or LED brightness control, comparator module, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for energy-efficient operation. Because of its small size, integrated features, and dependable performance, the PIC16F616 is widely used in LED lighting control, battery-powered devices, small motor control circuits, security systems, sensor-based automation, home appliances, and general consumer electronic products, where compact programmable control is required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773738322429-913101964.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 09:05:22'),
(5213,1,'product',3245,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F628\",\"description\":\"PIC16F628 is a popular and versatile 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, widely used in embedded systems and automation projects due to its low cost, compact size, and built-in communication features. It is typically available in an 18-pin DIP or SOIC package and provides about 2K words of Flash program memory, 224 bytes of RAM, and 128 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable program storage and non-volatile data retention. The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator (up to around 4 MHz), which reduces the need for external clock components in many designs.\",\"info\":\"The PIC16F628 offers up to 16 general-purpose I/O pins, built-in USART serial communication for interfacing with computers or other controllers, Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, PWM capability through the CCP module, and comparator modules for simple analog signal detection. It also includes essential reliability features such as watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for energy-efficient operation. Because of its flexible peripherals and dependable performance, the PIC16F628 is commonly used in serial communication projects, display control systems, alarm and security circuits, motor control units, automation devices, measurement instruments, and various consumer or industrial electronic applications, where compact programmable control and communication capability are required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773738399401-576992742.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 09:06:39'),
(5214,1,'product',3246,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F676\",\"description\":\"PIC16F676 is a compact and low-power 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require both digital processing and analog signal measurement. It is commonly available in a 14-pin DIP or SOIC package, making it suitable for space-constrained circuit designs. The microcontroller provides about 1K words of Flash program memory, 64 bytes of RAM, and 128 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable storage of program code as well as non-volatile user data. It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator (typically up to 4 MHz), which helps reduce the need for external clock components.\",\"info\":\"The PIC16F676 features up to 12 general-purpose I/O pins, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for sensor interfacing, Timer0 and Timer1, comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for efficient operation in battery-powered systems. Because of its small size, integrated analog capability, and dependable performance, it is widely used in sensor monitoring circuits, temperature or voltage measurement systems, LED control units, small automation devices, security products, home appliances, and other consumer or industrial electronic applications where simple programmable control and analog signal handling are required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773738468284-36351514.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 09:07:48'),
