(5216,1,'product',3247,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F677\",\"description\":\"PIC16F677 is a compact and low-power 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require multiple input/output lines and analog signal processing capability. It is commonly available in a 20-pin DIP or SOIC package, making it suitable for small electronic circuit designs. The microcontroller provides about 2K words of Flash program memory, 128 bytes of RAM, and 128 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable storage of program instructions and non-volatile user data. It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator (typically up to 4 MHz), which helps reduce the need for external timing components.\",\"info\":\"The PIC16F677 features multiple general-purpose I/O pins, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with several input channels for direct sensor interfacing, Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, PWM capability through the CCP module for motor speed or LED brightness control, comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for energy-efficient operation. Because of its integrated analog functions and compact size, it is widely used in sensor monitoring systems, LED lighting control circuits, small motor control units, automation devices, battery-powered equipment, home appliances, and general consumer or industrial electronic applications, where simple programmable control and analog measurement are required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773739551439-772678669.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 09:25:51'),
(5217,1,'product',3248,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F684\",\"description\":\"PIC16F684 is a compact and feature-rich 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require reliable digital processing along with analog and PWM capabilities. It is typically available in 14-pin DIP and SOIC packages, making it suitable for space-limited electronic designs. The microcontroller provides about 2K words of Flash program memory, 128 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing easy reprogramming and secure non-volatile storage of user or configuration data.\",\"info\":\"The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator that can run up to around 8 MHz, reducing the need for external timing components in many circuits. The PIC16F684 features multiple general-purpose I/O pins, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with several channels for sensor interfacing, Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and PWM output through the CCP module for applications such as motor speed control or LED dimming. It also includes comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for efficient operation in battery-powered systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773739637799-602045758.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 09:27:17'),
(5218,1,'product',3249,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F688\",\"description\":\"PIC16F688 is a compact and versatile 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require both digital processing and analog interfacing features. It is commonly available in 14-pin DIP and SOIC packages, making it suitable for space-constrained electronic designs. The microcontroller provides about 4K words of Flash program memory, 256 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable storage of program code as well as non-volatile user or configuration data. It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator that can run up to around 8 MHz, reducing the need for external clock components.\",\"info\":\"The PIC16F688 features several general-purpose I/O pins, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for sensor interfacing, Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and PWM capability through the CCP module for motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment. It also includes comparator modules, USART serial communication, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for efficient operation in battery-powered devices. Because of its small size, integrated peripherals, and dependable performance, it is widely used in sensor monitoring systems, LED lighting control, small motor drives, automation equipment, home appliances, security devices, and general consumer or industrial electronic applications, where flexible programmable control and mixed-signal capability are required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773739715751-430329825.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 09:28:35'),
(5219,1,'product',3250,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F689\",\"description\":\"PIC16F689 is a compact and low-power 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require multiple input/output pins and integrated analog features. It is commonly available in a 20-pin DIP or SOIC package, making it suitable for space-constrained electronic circuit designs. The microcontroller provides about 4K words of Flash program memory, 256 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable program execution and secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data. It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator that can run up to around 8 MHz, reducing the need for external clock components in many applications.\",\"info\":\"The PIC16F689 features several general-purpose I/O pins, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for sensor interfacing, Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and PWM capability through the CCP module for applications such as motor speed control or LED dimming. It also includes comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode, ensuring reliable and energy-efficient system operation. Because of its compact size, flexible peripherals, and dependable performance, the PIC16F689 is widely used in sensor monitoring systems, LED lighting controllers, small automation equipment, home appliances, battery-powered devices, security products, and various consumer or industrial electronic applications, where economical programmable control and mixed-signal capability are required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773739804149-286662930.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 09:30:04'),
(5220,1,'product',3251,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F690\",\"description\":\"PIC16F690 is a versatile and low-power 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, widely used in embedded control and automation applications that require multiple input/output lines and analog signal processing capability. It is typically available in a 20-pin DIP or SOIC package, making it suitable for compact electronic designs. The microcontroller provides about 4K words of Flash program memory, 256 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable program storage along with non-volatile user data retention. It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator that can run up to around 8 MHz, reducing the need for external timing components in many circuits.\",\"info\":\"The PIC16F690 features multiple general-purpose I/O pins, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with several input channels for sensor interfacing, Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and PWM output through the CCP module for applications such as motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment. It also provides comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode to improve system reliability and energy efficiency. Because of its compact size, flexible peripheral set, and dependable performance, the PIC16F690 is widely used in sensor monitoring systems, LED lighting control circuits, small motor drives, automation devices, home appliances, battery-powered equipment, security products, and general consumer or industrial electronic applications, where economical programmable control and mixed-signal capability are required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773739989741-252175310.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 09:33:09'),
(5221,1,'product',3252,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F870\",\"description\":\"PIC16F870 is a reliable and widely used 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control and automation applications that require multiple digital I/O lines and analog signal processing capability. It belongs to the PIC16F87X family and is commonly available in a 28-pin DIP or SOIC package, providing several input/output ports for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, and other external devices. The microcontroller offers about 2K words of Flash program memory, 128 bytes of RAM, and 64 bytes of EEPROM data memory, enabling easy program updates and secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data. It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and supports various clock options such as external crystal, RC oscillator, or external clock input.\",\"info\":\"The PIC16F870 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for accurate measurement of analog signals, along with Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and PWM capability through the CCP module for motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment. It also includes SPI/I²C serial communication (MSSP module) for connecting external memory devices or sensors, as well as watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for efficient operation in battery-powered systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773740106233-886459533.png\"}','2026-03-17 09:35:06'),
(5222,1,'product',3253,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F873\",\"description\":\"PIC16F870 is a reliable and widely used 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control and automation applications that require multiple digital I/O lines and analog signal processing capability. It belongs to the PIC16F87X family and is commonly available in a 28-pin DIP or SOIC package, providing several input/output ports for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, and other external devices. The microcontroller offers about 2K words of Flash program memory, 128 bytes of RAM, and 64 bytes of EEPROM data memory, enabling easy program updates and secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data.\",\"info\":\"The PIC16F870 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for accurate measurement of analog signals, along with Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and PWM capability through the CCP module for motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment. It also includes SPI/I²C serial communication (MSSP module) for connecting external memory devices or sensors, as well as watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for efficient operation in battery-powered systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773740558456-824659619.jpg\"}','2026-03-17 09:42:38'),
(5223,1,'product',3254,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F876\",\"description\":\"PIC16F876 is a powerful and widely used 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control and automation applications that require multiple digital input/output lines and advanced analog processing capability. It belongs to the PIC16F87X family and is commonly available in a 28-pin DIP or SOIC package, making it suitable for compact yet feature-rich circuit designs. The microcontroller provides about 8K words of Flash program memory, 368 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable program execution and secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data\",\"info\":\"The PIC16F876 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for accurate measurement of analog signals from sensors and control circuits. It also includes Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, PWM output through the CCP module for applications such as motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment, and a hardware SPI/I²C serial communication interface (MSSP) for easy connection to memory devices, displays, and other controllers\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773804641123-282799322.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 03:30:41'),
(5224,1,'product',3255,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F877A\",\"description\":\"PIC16F877A is a highly popular and versatile 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, widely used in embedded systems, automation projects, and educational applications due to its rich peripheral set and reliable performance. It belongs to the PIC16F87X family and is commonly available in a 40-pin DIP or 44-pin SMD package, providing a large number of general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, motors, and communication devices. The microcontroller offers about 8K words of Flash program memory, 368 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing easy program development along with secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data. It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 4.0 V to 5.5 V and supports different clock options such as external crystal, RC oscillator, or external clock input.\",\"info\":\"The PIC16F877A includes a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple channels for accurate analog signal measurement, along with Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and two CCP modules that support PWM generation for motor control and LED dimming applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773804769811-157274055.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 03:32:49'),
(5225,1,'product',3256,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F882\",\"description\":\"PIC16F882 is a feature-rich 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require reliable digital processing together with analog measurement and communication capability. It is commonly available in 28-pin DIP and SMD packages, offering multiple general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, and other external circuits. The microcontroller provides about 4K words of Flash program memory, 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, and 368 bytes of RAM, allowing easy reprogramming and secure storage of user or configuration data\",\"info\":\"The PIC16F882 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for direct sensor interfacing, along with Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and PWM capability through the CCP module for applications such as motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment. It also includes hardware serial communication interfaces such as USART and SPI/I²C (MSSP module) for easy connectivity with computers, memory devices, and other controllers. Additional functions like comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode improve system reliability and energy efficiency.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773804891145-832618452.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 03:34:51'),
(5226,1,'product',3257,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F883\",\"description\":\"PIC16F883 is a versatile and low-power 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require digital processing along with analog signal measurement and communication capability. It is commonly available in 28-pin DIP or SMD packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, and other external devices. The microcontroller offers about 4K words of Flash program memory, 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, and 368 bytes of RAM, allowing reliable program execution and secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data.\",\"info\":\"The PIC16F883 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with several input channels for accurate sensor interfacing, along with Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and PWM capability through the CCP module for motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment. It also includes hardware serial communication interfaces such as USART and SPI/I²C (MSSP module) for easy connection to computers, memory devices, and other controllers. Additional functions such as comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode enhance system reliability and energy efficiency\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773805246744-731440437.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 03:40:46'),
(5227,1,'product',3258,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F886\",\"description\":\"PIC16F886 is a versatile and low-power 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require multiple input/output pins, analog signal processing, and communication capability. It is commonly available in 28-pin DIP and SMD packages, making it suitable for compact yet feature-rich electronic circuit designs. The microcontroller provides about 8K words of Flash program memory, 368 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable program execution along with secure non-volatile storage of user or configuration data.\",\"info\":\"The PIC16F886 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for direct interfacing with sensors and measurement circuits. It also includes Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, PWM output through the CCP module for motor speed control or LED dimming, and hardware serial communication interfaces such as USART and SPI/I²C (MSSP module) for easy connectivity with computers, memory devices, and other controllers. Additional integrated functions such as comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode enhance system reliability and energy efficiency\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773805357493-52762410.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 03:42:37'),
(5228,1,'product',3259,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F887\",\"description\":\"PIC16F887 is a widely used and versatile 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require a large number of input/output pins along with analog and communication features. It belongs to the PIC16F88X family and is commonly available in 40-pin DIP and 44-pin SMD packages, making it suitable for both development boards and industrial circuit designs. The microcontroller provides about 8K words of Flash program memory, 368 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable program execution and non-volatile storage of user settings or configuration data. It operates over a wide supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator that can run up to around 8 MHz, reducing the need for external clock components in many applications.\",\"info\":\"The PIC16F887 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple channels for accurate measurement of analog signals from sensors. It also includes Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, PWM output through CCP modules for motor control or LED brightness adjustment, and hardware serial communication interfaces such as USART and SPI/I²C (MSSP module) for easy connectivity with computers, displays, memory devices, and other controllers. Additional integrated features like comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode enhance reliability and energy efficiency.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773805694548-234938579.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 03:48:14'),
(5229,1,'product',3260,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F913\",\"description\":\"PIC16F913 is a compact and feature-rich 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require analog signal processing and direct LCD display interfacing. It is commonly available in 28-pin DIP and SMD packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output pins for connecting sensors, switches, relays, and display modules. The microcontroller offers about 4K words of Flash program memory, 128 bytes of EEPROM data memory, and 256 bytes of RAM, allowing reliable program storage along with non-volatile data retention. It operates over a wide supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator (typically up to 8 MHz), reducing the need for external clock components in many designs.\",\"info\":\"A key feature of the PIC16F913 is its integrated LCD driver module, which allows direct control of segmented LCD displays without additional external driver ICs. It also includes a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for sensor interfacing, along with Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for energy-efficient operation. Because of its LCD driving capability, compact size, and dependable performance, the PIC16F913 is widely used in digital meters, home appliance control panels, battery-powered instruments, small automation devices, medical equipment, and other consumer or industrial electronic applications where direct display control and mixed-signal processing are required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773805783795-767137274.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 03:49:43'),
(5230,1,'product',3261,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F917\",\"description\":\"PIC16F917 is a feature-rich 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require analog signal processing and direct control of LCD displays. It belongs to the PIC16F91X family and is commonly available in 40-pin DIP and SMD packages, providing a large number of general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, switches, relays, and communication circuits. The microcontroller includes about 8K words of Flash program memory, 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, and 368 bytes of RAM, enabling reliable program execution along with secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data.\",\"info\":\"A major feature of the PIC16F917 is its built-in LCD driver module, which allows direct interfacing with segmented LCD panels without additional external driver ICs, making it ideal for display-oriented control systems. The device also includes a 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for sensor measurement, along with Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, PWM capability through the CCP module, comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for energy-efficient operation\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773805876888-73467984.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 03:51:16'),
(5231,1,'product',3262,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F1501\",\"description\":\"PIC16F1501 is a modern and low-power 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for compact embedded control applications that require flexible peripherals and efficient operation. It is typically available in 8-pin and 14-pin packages, making it suitable for space-constrained electronic designs. The microcontroller provides about 3.5 KB of Flash program memory, 256 bytes of RAM, and 128 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable program storage along with non-volatile data retention. It operates over a wide supply voltage range of approximately 1.8 V to 5.5 V, which makes it suitable for both battery-powered and standard logic systems.\",\"info\":\"The PIC16F1501 includes an internal oscillator (up to 16 MHz) that reduces the need for external clock components. It features several general-purpose I/O pins, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) for sensor interfacing, PWM capability through CCP/PWM modules for applications such as motor speed control or LED dimming, and Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2 for timing and counting functions. Additional integrated features such as comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out reset, configurable logic cells (CLC), and low-power sleep mode enhance system flexibility, reliability, and energy efficiency\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773806027237-853868604.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 03:53:47'),
(5232,1,'product',3263,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16F1508\",\"description\":\"PIC16F1508 is a modern and feature-rich 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require flexible peripherals, analog capability, and low-power operation. It is commonly available in 20-pin DIP and SMD packages, making it suitable for compact electronic circuit designs. The microcontroller provides about 7 KB of Flash program memory, 512 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable program execution along with secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data. It operates over a wide supply voltage range of approximately 1.8 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal high-speed oscillator (up to 16 MHz), reducing the need for external clock components in many applications.\",\"info\":\"The PIC16F1508 features multiple general-purpose I/O pins, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with several input channels for sensor interfacing, and enhanced PWM modules suitable for LED brightness control or small motor driving applications. It also includes Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for efficient operation in battery-powered systems. In addition, modern internal features such as Configurable Logic Cells (CLC) and peripheral pin select improve design flexibility\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773806140755-366137104.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 03:55:40'),
(5233,1,'product',3264,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"18F252\",\"description\":\"PIC18F252 is a high-performance 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require faster processing speed, advanced communication features, and reliable analog interfacing. It belongs to the PIC18F family and is commonly available in 28-pin DIP and SMD packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output pins for connecting sensors, displays, relays, and communication devices. The microcontroller offers about 32 KB of Flash program memory, 1.5 KB of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing efficient program execution and secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data. It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and supports various clock options such as external crystal, RC oscillator, or internal clock source.\",\"info\":\"The PIC18F252 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for accurate analog signal measurement, along with several timers and PWM capability through CCP modules for motor control or LED dimming applications. It also provides hardware communication interfaces including USART, SPI, and I²C, enabling easy connectivity with computers, memory devices, displays, and other controllers. Additional integrated functions such as watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode enhance system reliability and energy efficiency.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773806260270-387056230.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 03:57:40'),
(5234,1,'product',3265,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"18F452\",\"description\":\"PIC18F452 is a powerful and widely used 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for advanced embedded control and automation applications that require higher program memory, multiple I/O lines, and reliable communication features. It belongs to the PIC18F family and is commonly available in 40-pin DIP and 44-pin SMD packages, providing a large number of general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, motors, and communication devices. The microcontroller includes about 32 KB of Flash program memory, 1.5 KB of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing efficient program execution along with secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data.\",\"info\":\"The PIC18F452 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for accurate measurement of analog signals. It also includes several timers, PWM capability through CCP modules for motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment, and hardware communication interfaces such as USART, SPI, and I²C, enabling easy connectivity with computers, sensors, memory devices, and other controllers\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773806375863-84916640.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 03:59:35'),
(5235,1,'product',3266,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"18F458\",\"description\":\"PIC18F458 is a high-performance 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require fast processing, advanced communication features, and reliable analog interfacing. It belongs to the PIC18F family and is commonly available in 40-pin DIP and 44-pin SMD packages, providing a large number of general-purpose input/output pins for connecting sensors, displays, relays, motors, and communication devices. The microcontroller offers about 32 KB of Flash program memory, 1.5 KB of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing efficient program execution along with secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data.\",\"info\":\"A key feature of the PIC18F458 is its integrated CAN (Controller Area Network) communication module, which makes it especially suitable for automotive and industrial networking applications. It also includes a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for accurate measurement of analog signals, along with multiple timers and PWM capability through CCP modules for motor speed control or power regulation tasks. Standard communication interfaces such as USART, SPI, and I²C are also provided for easy connectivity with computers, memory devices, sensors, and display modules\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773806525565-577760743.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 04:02:05'),
(5236,1,'product',3267,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"18F2520\",\"description\":\"PIC18F2520 is a high-performance and feature-rich 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require fast processing speed, advanced peripherals, and reliable communication capability. It belongs to the PIC18F family and is commonly available in 28-pin DIP and SMD packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, motors, and other external devices. The microcontroller offers about 32 KB of Flash program memory, 1.5 KB of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing efficient program execution along with secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data\",\"info\":\"The PIC18F2520 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for accurate analog signal measurement. It also includes multiple timers, PWM capability through CCP/ECCP modules for applications such as motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment, and hardware communication interfaces including USART, SPI, and I²C, enabling easy connectivity with computers, sensors, memory devices, and display modules. Additional integrated features such as watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, fail-safe clock monitor, and low-power sleep mode improve system reliability and energy efficiency.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773806615441-393635943.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 04:03:35'),
(5237,1,'product',3268,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"18F2550\",\"description\":\"PIC18F2550 is a powerful and widely used 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control and communication applications that require USB connectivity and reliable analog interfacing. It belongs to the PIC18F family and is commonly available in 28-pin DIP and SMD packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, motors, and communication devices\",\"info\":\"The microcontroller includes about 32 KB of Flash program memory, 2 KB of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing efficient program execution along with secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data. It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and supports various clock options such as external crystal, PLL-based high-speed clock, or internal oscillator, enabling flexible system design.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773806740663-725726642.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 04:05:40'),
(5238,1,'product',3269,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"18F4520\",\"description\":\"PIC18F4520 is a high-performance and feature-rich 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, widely used in advanced embedded control and automation applications that require fast processing, large program memory, and multiple communication interfaces. It belongs to the PIC18F family and is commonly available in 40-pin DIP and 44-pin SMD packages, providing a large number of general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, motors, and communication devices.\",\"info\":\"The PIC18F4520 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for accurate measurement of analog signals. It also includes multiple timer modules, enhanced PWM capability through CCP/ECCP modules for motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment, and hardware communication interfaces such as USART, SPI, and I²C, enabling easy connectivity with computers, sensors, displays, and external memory devices. Additional integrated features such as watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, fail-safe clock monitor, and low-power sleep mode enhance system reliability and energy efficiency.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773807393812-613577739.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 04:16:33'),
(5239,1,'product',3270,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"18F4550\",\"description\":\"PIC18F4550 is a powerful and widely used 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require high processing speed, USB communication capability, and flexible peripheral integration. It belongs to the PIC18F family and is commonly available in 40-pin DIP and 44-pin SMD packages, providing a large number of general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, motors, and communication devices\",\"info\":\"A major feature of the PIC18F4550 is its integrated Full-Speed USB 2.0 interface, enabling direct connection to computers for data communication, firmware updates, and USB device control without requiring additional USB controller ICs. The device also includes a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for sensor measurement, along with several timers and enhanced PWM capability through CCP/ECCP modules for motor control or LED dimming applications. It provides hardware communication interfaces such as USART, SPI, and I²C for easy connectivity with memory devices, displays, sensors, and other controllers\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773807509773-830239971.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 04:18:29'),
(5240,1,'product',3271,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"18F4620\",\"description\":\"PIC18F4620 is a high-performance 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for advanced embedded control and automation applications that require large program memory, multiple communication interfaces, and reliable analog processing capability. It belongs to the PIC18F family and is commonly available in 40-pin DIP and 44-pin SMD packages, providing a large number of general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, motors, and communication modules. The microcontroller offers about 64 KB of Flash program memory, 3.9 KB of RAM, and 1 KB of EEPROM data memory, allowing efficient execution of complex programs along with secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data\",\"info\":\"The PIC18F4620 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for accurate sensor signal measurement. It also includes multiple timer modules, enhanced PWM capability through CCP/ECCP modules for motor control or LED brightness adjustment, and hardware serial communication interfaces such as USART and SPI/I²C (MSSP module) for easy connectivity with computers, memory devices, displays, and other controllers. Additional integrated functions such as watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, fail-safe clock monitoring, and low-power sleep mode improve system reliability and energy efficiency.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773807614533-710830488.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 04:20:14'),
(5241,1,'product',3272,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"30F2010\",\"description\":\"dsPIC30F2010 is a high-performance 16-bit Digital Signal Controller (DSC) from Microchip, designed for embedded applications that require fast processing speed, precise motor control capability, and advanced signal processing features. It combines the functionality of a microcontroller with digital signal processing performance, making it suitable for real-time control systems. The device is commonly available in 28-pin DIP and SMD packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, power circuits, and communication modules. It offers about 12 KB of Flash program memory and 1 KB of RAM, enabling efficient execution of control algorithms and signal-processing tasks.\",\"info\":\"The dsPIC30F2010 operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 4.5 V to 5.5 V and supports various clock sources such as external crystal or oscillator modules, allowing high-speed operation up to several tens of MIPS. It features advanced peripherals including high-resolution PWM modules specifically designed for motor control and power conversion applications, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels, Timer modules, quadrature encoder interface (QEI) for position sensing, and hardware serial communication interfaces such as UART, SPI, and I²C for system connectivity.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773807828005-674038469.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 04:23:48'),
(5242,1,'product',3273,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"30F3010\",\"description\":\"dsPIC30F3010 is a high-performance 16-bit Digital Signal Controller (DSC) from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require fast computation, precise motor control, and real-time signal processing capability. It combines the features of a traditional microcontroller with digital signal processing performance, making it suitable for advanced automation and power electronics systems. The device is commonly available in 28-pin DIP and SMD packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, drivers, and communication modules. It offers about 24 KB of Flash program memory and 2 KB of RAM, allowing efficient execution of control algorithms and signal-processing routines.\",\"info\":\"The dsPIC30F3010 typically operates with a supply voltage around 4.5 V to 5.5 V and supports external crystal or oscillator clock sources, enabling high-speed operation up to several tens of MIPS. It features advanced peripherals such as motor-control PWM modules, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple channels, Timer modules, and interfaces for UART, SPI, and I²C communication, allowing easy connectivity with other controllers, sensors, and display units.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773808031167-154266200.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 04:27:11'),
(5243,1,'product',3274,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"30F3010\",\"description\":\"dsPIC30F3010 is a 16-bit Digital Signal Controller (DSC) developed by Microchip Technology, designed to combine the processing capability of a digital signal processor with the flexibility of a microcontroller. It operates at speeds up to 30 MIPS and features around 24 KB of Flash program memory and 2 KB of RAM, making it suitable for real-time embedded control applications.\",\"info\":\"The device includes integrated peripherals such as a 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC), multiple 16-bit timers, motor-control PWM modules, and communication interfaces like UART, SPI, and I²C. It typically operates within a voltage range of 4.5 V to 5.5 V and supports in-circuit serial programming (ICSP) for easy firmware updates. Due to its DSP engine and high-speed performance, the dsPIC30F3010 is widely used in motor control systems, power converters and inverters, robotics, automation equipment, and industrial control applications where precise timing and signal processing are required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773808709784-133388426.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 04:38:29'),
(5244,1,'product',3274,'delete',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-18 04:38:50'),
(5245,1,'product',3275,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"30F3011\",\"description\":\"dsPIC30F3011 is a 16-bit Digital Signal Controller (DSC) from Microchip Technology that combines the features of a high-performance microcontroller with digital signal processing capability. It can operate at speeds up to about 30 MIPS and is designed for real-time control applications that require fast mathematical processing and precise timing. The device typically includes around 24 KB of Flash program memory and about 2 KB of RAM for data storage\",\"info\":\"It integrates several useful peripherals such as a 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC), multiple 16-bit timers, motor-control PWM modules, and serial communication interfaces like UART, SPI, and I²C. The controller generally operates in the 4.5 V to 5.5 V supply voltage range and supports in-circuit serial programming (ICSP) for convenient firmware development and updates. Because of its DSP engine and built-in control peripherals, the dsPIC30F3011 is commonly used in motor drive systems, switched-mode power supplies, inverters, robotics, industrial automation equipment, and other embedded systems that require efficient signal processing and control performance.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773808838203-204670711.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 04:40:38'),
(5246,1,'product',3276,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"30F3012\",\"description\":\"dsPIC30F3012 is a 16-bit Digital Signal Controller (DSC) developed by Microchip Technology, designed to provide the combined advantages of a microcontroller and a digital signal processor for high-speed embedded control applications. It operates at performance levels of up to about 30 MIPS and typically features around 24 KB of Flash program memory along with approximately 2 KB of data RAM. The device includes several integrated peripherals such as a 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC), multiple 16-bit timers, enhanced motor-control PWM modules, and standard communication interfaces like UART, SPI, and I²C, enabling flexible system connectivity\",\"info\":\"It generally works with a supply voltage range of about 4.5 V to 5.5 V and supports In-Circuit Serial Programming (ICSP) for easy firmware loading and updates. Owing to its DSP processing capability and precise real-time control features, the dsPIC30F3012 is widely used in applications such as AC/DC motor drives, switched-mode power supplies, inverters, robotics systems, industrial automation controllers, and embedded signal-processing equipment.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773808920303-432196790.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 04:42:00'),
(5247,1,'product',3277,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"30F4011\",\"description\":\"dsPIC30F4011 is a high-performance 16-bit Digital Signal Controller (DSC) from Microchip Technology, designed to combine microcontroller functionality with digital signal processing capability for advanced real-time control applications. It can operate at speeds of up to about 30 MIPS and typically provides around 48 KB of Flash program memory and approximately 2 KB of data RAM, allowing it to handle complex control algorithms and signal-processing tasks. The controller includes a range of integrated peripherals such as a multi-channel 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC), multiple 16-bit timers, enhanced motor-control PWM modules, input capture and output compare features, and communication interfaces including UART, SPI, and I²C for system connectivity\",\"info\":\"It generally operates within a supply voltage range of about 4.5 V to 5.5 V and supports In-Circuit Serial Programming (ICSP) for convenient firmware development and updates. Because of its powerful DSP engine and dedicated control peripherals, the dsPIC30F4011 is widely used in applications such as AC and DC motor drives, power inverters, switched-mode power supplies, robotics, industrial automation systems, and other embedded control solutions that require accurate timing and fast signal processing.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773809009266-990785679.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 04:43:29'),
(5248,1,'product',3278,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"MCP602\",\"description\":\"MCP602 is a low-power, dual operational amplifier (op-amp) integrated circuit manufactured by Microchip Technology, designed for general-purpose analog signal conditioning and amplification applications. It operates with a single supply voltage ranging approximately from 2.7 V to 6.0 V, making it suitable for battery-powered and low-voltage electronic circuits. The device offers rail-to-rail input and output capability, allowing it to handle signals close to the supply voltage limits and improving dynamic range in low-voltage systems\",\"info\":\"MCP602 features low input bias current, low offset voltage, and good bandwidth performance, which help provide accurate amplification and stable operation in sensor interfaces, active filters, signal buffering, data acquisition systems, and audio processing circuits. It is commonly available in small packages such as DIP, SOIC, and MSOP, enabling easy integration into compact embedded designs and analog control applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773809087514-250544185.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 04:44:47'),
(5249,1,'product',3279,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"MCP604\",\"description\":\"MCP604 is a low-power, quad operational amplifier (op-amp) integrated circuit from Microchip Technology, designed for general-purpose analog signal amplification and conditioning in low-voltage electronic systems. It operates with a single supply voltage typically ranging from about 2.5 V to 6.0 V and provides rail-to-rail input and output capability, allowing it to process signals close to the supply limits and making it suitable for battery-operated devices\",\"info\":\"The device features low input bias current, low quiescent current consumption, and stable performance, which helps improve accuracy and efficiency in applications such as sensor signal conditioning, active filters, voltage followers, integrators, data acquisition circuits, and portable instrumentation. MCP604 is commonly available in compact packages like DIP, SOIC, and TSSOP, enabling easy use in space-constrained embedded systems and analog control designs.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773809172816-774032557.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 04:46:12'),
(5250,1,'product',3280,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"MCP3201\",\"description\":\"MCP3201 is a 12-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) integrated circuit developed by Microchip Technology, designed for accurate and low-power data acquisition in embedded systems. It uses a successive approximation (SAR) conversion technique and communicates with microcontrollers through a high-speed SPI serial interface, allowing easy integration into digital control and measurement applications\",\"info\":\"The device typically operates with a single supply voltage in the range of about 2.7 V to 5.5 V and can achieve sampling rates up to around 100 ksps, depending on the clock frequency. MCP3201 provides good resolution and conversion accuracy, making it suitable for sensor interfacing, industrial monitoring, battery-powered instruments, medical devices, and data logging systems. Its compact package options and low power consumption help designers implement reliable analog signal measurement solutions in portable and space-constrained electronic designs.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773809297877-798058543.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 04:48:17'),
(5251,1,'product',3281,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"MCP3202\",\"description\":\"MCP3202 is a 12-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) IC from Microchip Technology designed for precise analog signal measurement in embedded and data-acquisition systems. It uses a successive approximation (SAR) conversion method and communicates with microcontrollers through a high-speed SPI serial interface, enabling simple and efficient digital integration. The device provides two analog input channels that can be configured for single-ended or pseudo-differential operation, offering flexibility in sensor interfacing and signal monitoring applications\",\"info\":\"It typically operates with a single supply voltage in the range of about 2.7 V to 5.5 V and can achieve sampling speeds of up to approximately 100 ksps depending on the clock input. With low power consumption, good conversion accuracy, and compact package options such as DIP and SOIC, the MCP3202 is widely used in instrumentation, industrial control, portable measurement equipment, battery-powered devices, and general embedded analog data acquisition systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773809923574-912378044.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 04:58:43'),
(5252,1,'product',3282,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"MCP3204\",\"description\":\"MCP3204 is a 12-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) integrated circuit from Microchip Technology, designed for accurate multi-channel analog signal measurement in embedded and data-acquisition applications. It uses a successive approximation (SAR) conversion technique and communicates with microcontrollers through a high-speed SPI serial interface, allowing simple integration into digital systems. The device provides four analog input channels that can be configured as single-ended or pseudo-differential inputs, offering flexibility for sensor interfacing and signal monitoring\",\"info\":\"It typically operates with a single supply voltage in the range of about 2.7 V to 5.5 V and supports sampling rates up to around 100 ksps, depending on the clock frequency. With low power consumption, good linearity, and compact package options such as DIP and SOIC, the MCP3204 is commonly used in industrial control, instrumentation, portable measurement equipment, data logging systems, and general embedded analog signal processing applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773810170600-641635661.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 05:02:50'),
(5253,1,'product',3283,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"MCP3208\",\"description\":\"MCP3208 is a 12-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) integrated circuit manufactured by Microchip Technology, designed for high-accuracy multi-channel analog data acquisition in embedded electronic systems. It uses a successive approximation (SAR) conversion method and communicates with microcontrollers through a high-speed SPI serial interface, enabling simple and reliable digital communication. The device provides eight analog input channels, which can be configured for single-ended or pseudo-differential operation, allowing flexible connection of multiple sensors and analog signals.\",\"info\":\"MCP3208 typically operates from a single supply voltage in the range of approximately 2.7 V to 5.5 V and supports sampling rates up to about 100 ksps, depending on the system clock. It features low power consumption, good conversion accuracy, and stable performance, making it suitable for applications such as industrial monitoring, instrumentation systems, robotics, portable measurement devices, medical equipment, and general embedded data-logging and control solutions.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773810835623-2838960.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 05:13:55'),
(5254,1,'product',3284,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"MCP4728\",\"description\":\"MCP4728 is a quad 12-bit Digital-to-Analog Converter (DAC) integrated circuit from Microchip Technology, designed for precise generation of analog voltage signals in embedded and control systems. It communicates with microcontrollers through an I²C serial interface, allowing multiple DAC outputs to be controlled using only a few communication lines. The device provides four independent DAC output channels, each capable of producing rail-to-rail analog output voltages referenced to the supply or an internal reference, enabling flexible signal generation and calibration functions.\",\"info\":\"MCP4728 typically operates from a single supply voltage in the range of about 2.7 V to 5.5 V and includes non-volatile EEPROM memory to store DAC settings, allowing the outputs to retain their programmed values even after power cycling. With low power consumption, good linearity, and compact package options, it is widely used in applications such as waveform generation, programmable voltage sources, motor control feedback systems, instrumentation, industrial automation, and embedded signal-processing circuits.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773811184250-435544767.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 05:19:44'),
(5255,1,'product',3285,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"MCP2551\",\"description\":\"MCP2551 is a high-speed CAN (Controller Area Network) transceiver integrated circuit developed by Microchip Technology, used to interface a CAN protocol controller with the physical two-wire CAN bus. It is designed to support communication speeds of up to 1 Mb/s, making it suitable for real-time networking applications in automotive and industrial systems. The device operates typically with a 5 V supply voltage and provides differential transmit and receive capability through the CANH and CANL bus lines, helping to improve noise immunity and reliable data transmission over long distances.\",\"info\":\"MCP2551 includes features such as short-circuit protection, thermal shutdown, and slope control for reducing electromagnetic interference (EMI). It also supports standby mode for lower power consumption in energy-efficient designs. Due to its robust performance and compliance with CAN standards, the MCP2551 is widely used in automotive electronics, industrial automation networks, robotics, building control systems, and distributed embedded communication applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773811489257-973912892.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 05:24:49'),
(5256,1,'product',3286,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"MCP4921\",\"description\":\"MCP4921 is a 12-bit Digital-to-Analog Converter (DAC) integrated circuit from Microchip Technology, designed to provide accurate and stable analog voltage output in embedded electronic systems. It uses a high-speed SPI serial interface, allowing microcontrollers and digital processors to control the analog output easily with minimal wiring. The device features a single DAC channel with buffered voltage output and typically operates with a supply voltage range of about 2.7 V to 5.5 V, making it suitable for both low-power and standard logic applications.\",\"info\":\"MCP4921 offers good linearity, fast settling time, and selectable gain configuration, enabling flexible output voltage scaling for signal generation and control functions. With its low power consumption and compact package options such as DIP and SOIC, it is commonly used in applications like waveform generation, programmable voltage sources, motor control reference circuits, instrumentation systems, audio signal adjustment, and general embedded analog output applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773811605436-146946538.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 05:26:45'),
(5257,1,'product',3287,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"MCP4922\",\"description\":\"MCP4922 is a dual 12-bit Digital-to-Analog Converter (DAC) integrated circuit manufactured by Microchip Technology, designed for generating precise analog voltage outputs in embedded control and signal-processing applications. It communicates with microcontrollers and digital systems through a high-speed SPI serial interface, enabling fast and simple control of its two independent DAC output channels. The device typically operates with a single supply voltage in the range of about 2.7 V to 5.5 V and provides buffered, rail-to-rail voltage outputs with selectable gain settings for flexible output scaling\",\"info\":\"MCP4922 offers good linearity, low power consumption, and fast settling time, making it suitable for waveform generation, programmable reference voltage creation, audio level control, motor drive feedback systems, instrumentation equipment, and general embedded analog output applications. It is commonly available in compact packages such as DIP and SOIC, allowing easy integration into both prototype and production electronic designs.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773811894516-773690987.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 05:31:34'),
(5258,1,'product',3288,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"MCP9701\",\"description\":\"MCP9701 is a low-power analog temperature sensor integrated circuit from Microchip Technology, designed to provide a voltage output that is directly proportional to ambient temperature. It operates with a wide supply voltage range, typically from about 2.3 V to 5.5 V, making it suitable for battery-powered and low-voltage embedded systems. The device produces a linear analog output with a temperature coefficient of approximately 19.5 mV/°C, allowing simple interfacing with microcontroller ADC inputs for temperature monitoring and control.\",\"info\":\"MCP9701 features low quiescent current consumption, fast thermal response, and good accuracy without requiring complex calibration circuitry. It is commonly available in small packages such as TO-92, SOT-23, and SC-70, enabling use in compact electronic designs. Due to its simplicity and efficiency, the MCP9701 is widely used in applications such as environmental monitoring, power supply temperature protection, consumer electronics, industrial control equipment, and portable measurement systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1539],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773812891643-92965961.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 05:48:11'),
