(5266,1,'product',3289,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"YY Universal A/C Remote Control\",\"description\":\"The YY-1311 remote is a replacement / universal air-conditioner remote control mainly used to operate split or window AC units.\",\"info\":\"Works using infrared (IR) signal to control the air conditioner.Usually comes with a small LCD display to show temperature and operating mode.Designed with plastic body and rubber keypad buttons for easy handling.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1544],\"model\":\"YY-1311\",\"alternative_name\":\"A/C Remote\",\"mrp\":\"1\",\"note\":\"Keep the remote away from water and wet hands.\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773818259592-752528225.jfif\"}','2026-03-18 07:17:39'),
(5267,1,'product',3290,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"87C52X2BN\",\"description\":\"87C52X2BN is an 8-bit microcontroller based on the popular 8051 architecture, originally manufactured by Philips (now NXP Semiconductors). It belongs to the high-speed 80C51 family and is designed for embedded control applications requiring reliable digital processing and peripheral interfacing. The device typically features 8 KB of EPROM program memory, 256 bytes of internal RAM, and operates at higher clock speeds compared to standard 8051 controllers due to its X2 mode, which allows faster instruction execution\",\"info\":\"It includes built-in peripherals such as three 16-bit timers/counters, a full-duplex UART serial port, multiple interrupt sources, and 32 programmable I/O lines for connecting external devices like displays, relays, sensors, and communication modules. The microcontroller generally operates with a 5 V supply and supports external crystal oscillators for system clock generation. Because of its stable performance and familiar instruction set, the 87C52X2BN is widely used in industrial control systems, instrumentation equipment, consumer electronics, automation projects, and educational embedded system designs.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1541],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773819053089-906014684.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 07:30:53'),
(5268,1,'product',3291,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"89C61EQ (W78E365)\",\"description\":\"89C61EQ (W78E365) is a high-performance 8-bit microcontroller based on the standard 8051 architecture, manufactured by Winbond (and also referenced with compatible versions from other vendors). It is designed for embedded control applications that require faster processing and flexible memory options. The controller typically provides Flash program memory (around 64 KB) and internal RAM, allowing storage of application code and data within the chip.\",\"info\":\"It supports higher operating speeds compared to traditional 8051 devices and includes built-in peripherals such as multiple 16-bit timers/counters, a full-duplex UART serial communication interface, watchdog timer, and up to 32 programmable I/O pins for interfacing with external components. The device usually operates with a 5 V power supply and requires an external crystal oscillator for clock generation. Due to its reliable performance and compatibility with the widely used 8051 instruction set, the 89C61EQ (W78E365) is commonly used in industrial automation, instrumentation systems, communication equipment, consumer electronics, and general embedded system designs.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1541],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773819656718-921767574.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 07:40:56'),
(5269,1,'product',3292,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"89V51RD2BN\",\"description\":\"89V51RD2BN (P89V51RD2BN) is a high-performance 8-bit microcontroller based on the standard 8051 architecture, manufactured by NXP (formerly Philips). It is designed for embedded control applications that require fast execution speed, large on-chip program memory, and flexible peripheral interfacing. The device typically features 64 KB of Flash program memory and 1 KB of internal RAM, allowing application code storage and efficient data handling within the chip. It supports In-System Programming (ISP) and In-Application Programming (IAP), enabling firmware updates without removing the microcontroller from the circuit.\",\"info\":\"The controller includes built-in peripherals such as three 16-bit timers/counters, a full-duplex UART serial communication interface, watchdog timer, power-saving modes, and up to 32 programmable I/O pins for connecting sensors, displays, relays, and communication modules. It usually operates with a 5 V supply voltage and uses an external crystal oscillator for clock generation. Due to its high speed and compatibility with the widely used 8051 instruction set, the 89V51RD2BN is commonly used in industrial automation systems, instrumentation equipment, consumer electronics, motor control circuits, communication devices, and general embedded system applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1541],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773819761542-80466464.png\"}','2026-03-18 07:42:41'),
(5270,1,'product',3293,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"PCF8563\",\"description\":\"PCF8563 is a low-power Real-Time Clock (RTC) and calendar IC developed by NXP Semiconductors, designed to keep accurate time and date information in embedded electronic systems. It communicates with microcontrollers through a two-wire I²C serial interface, allowing simple connection using minimal pins. The device maintains data such as seconds, minutes, hours, day, date, month, and year, and includes features like programmable alarms, timer functions, and interrupt output for event-based control.\",\"info\":\"PCF8563 operates with a wide supply voltage range of approximately 1.0 V to 5.5 V, making it suitable for battery-backed and low-power portable devices. It requires an external 32.768 kHz crystal oscillator for accurate timekeeping and consumes very low current, enabling long battery life in standby operation. The IC is commonly available in compact packages such as SOIC and TSSOP, allowing easy integration into space-constrained designs. Due to its reliable timekeeping performance and simple interfacing, PCF8563 is widely used in digital clocks, energy meters, data loggers, industrial controllers, communication equipment, and consumer electronic products.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1541],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773820356258-887410686.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 07:52:36'),
(5271,1,'product',3294,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"PCF8574P\",\"description\":\"PCF8574P is an 8-bit remote input/output (I/O) expander integrated circuit developed by NXP Semiconductors, designed to increase the number of digital input and output pins available to a microcontroller. It communicates through a two-wire I²C serial interface, allowing multiple devices to be connected on the same bus using configurable hardware addresses. The IC provides eight quasi-bidirectional I/O ports, which can be used as either inputs or outputs without needing separate direction control registers, simplifying circuit design.\",\"info\":\"The device typically operates with a supply voltage range of about 2.5 V to 6 V and features low power consumption, making it suitable for battery-powered and embedded applications. It also includes an interrupt output pin, which can notify the microcontroller when an input state changes, improving system efficiency. The PCF8574P is commonly available in DIP-16 and SOIC packages and is widely used for applications such as LCD interfacing, keypad scanning, LED control, relay driving, industrial automation systems, and general embedded I/O expansion tasks where additional digital ports are required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1541],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773820625510-702828368.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 07:57:05'),
(5272,1,'product',3295,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"PCF8583\",\"description\":\"PCF8583 is a low-power real-time clock and calendar IC developed by NXP Semiconductors, designed to provide accurate timekeeping and event timing functions in embedded electronic systems. It communicates with microcontrollers through a two-wire I²C serial interface, allowing simple data transfer using minimal connection lines. The device can store and track time and date information such as seconds, minutes, hours, day, month, and year (with limited year counting) and also includes alarm, timer, and event counter functions for scheduling and monitoring operations.\",\"info\":\"PCF8583 typically operates with a supply voltage range of about 2.5 V to 6 V and requires an external 32.768 kHz crystal oscillator to maintain accurate clock timing. It features low power consumption, making it suitable for battery-backup applications where continuous timekeeping is required even when the main system power is off. The IC is commonly available in DIP and SOIC packages, enabling easy integration into both prototype and production designs. Because of its reliable operation and simple interfacing, the PCF8583 is widely used in digital clocks, energy meters, data logging systems, industrial automation equipment, communication devices, and various consumer electronic products that require real-time scheduling and time tracking.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1541],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773820722004-279927667.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 07:58:42'),
(5273,1,'product',3296,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"PCF8591\",\"description\":\"PCF8591 is an 8-bit analog-to-digital and digital-to-analog converter IC developed by NXP Semiconductors, designed for simple analog data acquisition and signal generation in embedded systems. It communicates with microcontrollers through a two-wire I²C serial interface, allowing multiple devices to share the same communication bus. The device provides four analog input channels that can be configured as single-ended or differential inputs, along with one analog voltage output (DAC) for generating reference or control signals.\",\"info\":\"PCF8591 typically operates with a supply voltage range of about 2.5 V to 6 V and features low power consumption, making it suitable for portable and battery-powered applications. It includes an internal sample-and-hold circuit and on-chip oscillator, simplifying external component requirements. The IC is commonly available in DIP and SOIC packages, enabling easy use in both development and production circuits. Due to its simple interfacing and versatile analog functions, PCF8591 is widely used in sensor interfacing, data logging, industrial control systems, robotics projects, educational experiments, and general embedded analog signal processing applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1541],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773820878788-24044194.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 08:01:18'),
(5274,1,'product',3297,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"87C52X2FN\",\"description\":\"87C52X2FN is a high-speed 8-bit microcontroller based on the widely used 8051 architecture, originally manufactured by Philips (now NXP Semiconductors). It belongs to the enhanced 80C51 family and is designed for embedded control applications requiring reliable operation and faster instruction execution. The controller typically provides about 8 KB of EPROM program memory and 256 bytes of internal RAM, allowing storage of application programs and data within the chip.\",\"info\":\"The device supports X2 mode operation, which enables higher processing speed by reducing the number of clock cycles required per instruction compared to standard 8051 controllers. It includes built-in peripherals such as three 16-bit timers/counters, a full-duplex UART serial communication interface, multiple interrupt sources, and up to 32 programmable I/O pins for interfacing with external components like sensors, displays, relays, and communication modules. The microcontroller generally operates with a 5 V supply voltage and requires an external crystal oscillator for clock generation.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1541],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773821176011-913845610.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 08:06:16'),
(5275,1,'category',633,'create',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-18 08:10:01'),
(5276,1,'category_brand_mapping',633,'update',NULL,'\"{\\\"assigned_brands\\\":[232,230]}\"','2026-03-18 08:10:54'),
(5277,1,'product',3298,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"80C85\",\"description\":\"80C85 is a CMOS version of the classic 8-bit 8085 microprocessor, designed for general-purpose computing and embedded control applications. It is capable of addressing up to 64 KB of memory and features a multiplexed address and data bus, allowing efficient communication with external memory and peripheral devices. The processor operates with a single +5 V power supply and includes an on-chip clock generator, reducing the need for additional external timing circuitry.\",\"info\":\"The 80C85 supports multiple interrupt inputs, serial input/output lines, and status/control signals, enabling flexible interfacing with external hardware such as RAM, ROM, input/output ports, and communication modules. Due to its stable architecture, simple instruction set, and ease of system design, the 80C85 has been widely used in educational training kits, industrial controllers, instrumentation systems, early computer systems, and embedded development projects where basic processing and control functions are required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1546],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773821675755-570043824.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 08:14:35'),
(5278,1,'product',3299,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"80C88\",\"description\":\"80C88 is a CMOS version of the classic Intel 8088 8-bit microprocessor, designed for general-purpose computing and embedded control applications. Internally it uses a 16-bit architecture, but it communicates with external memory and peripherals through an 8-bit data bus, which helps reduce system cost and simplifies hardware design. The processor can address up to 1 MB of memory using its segmented memory architecture and typically operates with a single +5 V power supply.\",\"info\":\"The 80C88 includes a six-byte instruction prefetch queue, arithmetic logic unit (ALU), general-purpose registers, and various control and status signals for interfacing with external RAM, ROM, and input/output devices. It supports hardware interrupts, serial data communication lines, and clock synchronization features, enabling flexible system implementation. Due to its compatibility with the widely used x86 instruction set and reliable performance, the 80C88 has been used in early personal computers, industrial controllers, instrumentation equipment, communication systems, and educational microprocessor training kits where structured data processing and control operations are required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1546],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773822125767-84157606.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 08:22:05'),
(5279,1,'product',3300,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"82C51\",\"description\":\"82C51 is a CMOS version of the classic 8251 Universal Synchronous/Asynchronous Receiver Transmitter (USART) integrated circuit, designed to provide serial communication capability to microprocessor-based systems. It allows data transmission and reception in both synchronous and asynchronous modes, making it suitable for a wide range of communication applications. The device interfaces easily with microprocessors such as the 8085, 8086, and other bus-based systems, enabling conversion between parallel data from the CPU and serial data for communication lines.\",\"info\":\"The IC typically operates with a single +5 V supply and supports programmable features such as baud rate selection, character length, parity control, and stop bits, allowing flexible configuration of serial communication protocols. It includes transmit and receive buffers, status signals, and interrupt capability to improve communication efficiency and reduce processor workload. Due to its reliable operation and standard interface design, the 82C51 is widely used in industrial communication systems, data terminals, instrumentation equipment, embedded controllers, and educational microprocessor development kits where serial data transfer is required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1546],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773822738756-863480605.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 08:32:18'),
(5280,1,'product',3301,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"82C54\",\"description\":\"82C54 is a CMOS version of the 8254 Programmable Interval Timer (PIT) integrated circuit, used to generate accurate timing delays, frequency signals, and event counting functions in microprocessor-based systems. The device contains three independent 16-bit counters, each of which can be programmed to operate in various timing modes such as rate generator, square-wave generator, software-triggered strobe, and hardware-triggered strobe.\",\"info\":\"It typically operates from a single +5 V supply and interfaces easily with common microprocessors like the 8085, 8086, and similar bus-oriented systems. Each counter has separate clock, gate, and output pins, allowing flexible use for tasks such as time delay generation, frequency division, pulse counting, waveform generation, and real-time system control. Because of its reliable performance and programmable operation, the 82C54 is widely used in industrial automation equipment, communication systems, embedded controllers, instrumentation, and educational microprocessor training kits where precise timing control is required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1546],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773822850470-730719935.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 08:34:10'),
(5281,1,'product',3302,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"82C55\",\"description\":\"82C55 is a CMOS version of the classic 8255 Programmable Peripheral Interface (PPI) integrated circuit, designed to provide flexible digital input/output expansion for microprocessor-based systems. It offers 24 programmable I/O lines, organized into three 8-bit ports (Port A, Port B, and Port C), which can be configured for input or output operation in different modes. The device interfaces easily with common microprocessors such as the 8085, 8086, and similar bus-based controllers, enabling efficient connection of external devices like keyboards, displays, relays, printers, and sensors.\",\"info\":\"The IC typically operates with a single +5 V power supply and supports multiple operating modes including simple I/O mode, strobed I/O mode, and bidirectional bus mode, allowing reliable data transfer between the CPU and peripheral devices. It also provides handshaking and interrupt capability to improve system performance in real-time applications. Due to its simple programmability, stable operation, and wide compatibility, the 82C55 is widely used in industrial automation systems, instrumentation equipment, embedded controllers, communication devices, and educational microprocessor development kits where additional digital interfacing is required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1546],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773822976346-621869658.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 08:36:16'),
(5282,1,'product',3303,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"82C59\",\"description\":\"82C59 is a CMOS version of the 8259 Programmable Interrupt Controller (PIC) integrated circuit, designed to manage multiple interrupt requests in microprocessor-based systems. It helps prioritize and control hardware interrupts, allowing the CPU to respond efficiently to external events. The device can handle up to 8 interrupt input lines, and multiple 82C59 ICs can be cascaded to support up to 64 interrupt sources, making it suitable for complex control applications.\",\"info\":\"The IC typically operates with a single +5 V supply and interfaces easily with common microprocessors such as the 8085, 8086, and similar bus-oriented systems. It provides features like interrupt masking, priority resolution, interrupt vector generation, and programmable operating modes, which improve system performance and simplify interrupt management. Because of its reliable operation and flexible configuration, the 82C59 is widely used in industrial control systems, communication equipment, instrumentation, embedded controllers, and educational microprocessor training kits where efficient handling of multiple hardware interrupts is required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1546],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773823115826-548569639.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 08:38:35'),
(5283,1,'product',3304,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"YY Universal A/C Remote Control\",\"description\":\"Works using infrared (IR) signal technology to send commands to the AC indoor unit.Usually has an LCD display to show temperature, fan mode, timer, and other settings.\",\"info\":\"Operates using AAA batteries.Often requires manual code setting or auto-search setup for brand matching.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1544],\"model\":\"YY-264\",\"alternative_name\":\"Universal A/C Remote \",\"mrp\":\"1\",\"note\":\"Supports essential cooling and comfort settings\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773823701571-885444588.jfif\"}','2026-03-18 08:48:21'),
(5284,1,'product',3305,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"C106M\",\"description\":\"C106M is a Silicon Controlled Rectifier (SCR), a type of thyristor used for switching and controlling AC or DC power in electronic circuits. It is designed to handle moderate current and voltage levels, making it suitable for various power control applications. The device has three terminals — anode, cathode, and gate — and once triggered by a small gate current, it allows current to flow between anode and cathode until the current drops below its holding level.\",\"info\":\"C106M typically supports blocking voltages in the range of about 400 V (depending on variant) and can conduct several amperes of load current, making it useful in practical power control designs. It is commonly available in TO-225 / TO-126 type packages, allowing easy mounting and heat dissipation. Because of its reliable switching characteristics and simple gate triggering, the C106M SCR is widely used in light dimmers, heater control circuits, motor speed control systems, battery chargers, power regulators, and industrial switching applications where controlled rectification and load management are required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773823755611-82268383.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 08:49:15'),
(5285,1,'product',3306,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BT139-800\",\"description\":\"BT139-800 is a bidirectional TRIAC (Triode for Alternating Current) used for switching and phase-control of AC loads in power electronics circuits. It is designed to control relatively high voltage and current loads, making it suitable for domestic and industrial AC power control applications. The device has three terminals — MT1 (Main Terminal 1), MT2 (Main Terminal 2), and Gate, and it can conduct current in both directions once triggered by a gate pulse.\",\"info\":\"This TRIAC typically supports a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 800 V and can handle load currents up to 16 A (depending on cooling and circuit conditions). It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, allowing easy mounting on heat sinks for better thermal performance. Because of its reliable switching characteristics and high voltage capability, the BT139-800 is widely used in light dimmers, fan speed regulators, heater control circuits, AC motor control systems, solid-state relays, and general AC power switching applications where efficient control of alternating current loads is required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773823868574-292742070.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 08:51:08'),
(5286,1,'product',2257,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"0.012nF (12k)\",\"description\":\"\",\"info\":\"\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":416,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}],\"alternative_names\":[]}','2026-03-18 08:55:15'),
(5287,1,'product',3307,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BTA12-600\",\"description\":\"BTA12-600 is a bidirectional TRIAC used for controlling AC power in switching and phase-control applications. It is designed to handle medium to high current loads, making it suitable for domestic appliances and industrial power control circuits. The device has three terminals — MT1 (Main Terminal 1), MT2 (Main Terminal 2), and Gate, and once triggered by a gate signal, it can conduct current in both directions through the AC cycle.\",\"info\":\"This TRIAC typically supports a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 600 V and a current rating around 12 A, depending on heat-sink conditions and operating environment. It is commonly available in an insulated TO-220 package, which simplifies mounting on heat sinks and improves electrical isolation. Because of its reliable performance and easy gate triggering, the BTA12-600 is widely used in light dimmers, fan regulators, heater control systems, AC motor speed controllers, solid-state relays, and general AC load switching applications where efficient control of mains power is required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773824171808-787588457.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 08:56:11'),
(5288,1,'product',3308,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BTA16-600\",\"description\":\"BTA16-600 is a bidirectional TRIAC (AC power switching device) used for controlling alternating-current loads in domestic and industrial electronic circuits. It is designed to handle relatively high load currents and can conduct current in both directions once a triggering signal is applied to its gate terminal. The device has three terminals — MT1 (Main Terminal 1), MT2 (Main Terminal 2), and Gate, and is commonly used in phase-control circuits for regulating AC power.\",\"info\":\"This TRIAC typically supports a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 600 V and a current rating up to around 16 A, depending on proper heat-sink usage and operating conditions. It is generally available in an insulated TO-220 package, which helps simplify mounting and provides electrical isolation from the heat sink. Due to its robust switching capability and reliable performance, the BTA16-600 is widely used in light dimmers, fan speed regulators, heater controllers, AC motor speed control circuits, solid-state relays, and general mains power switching applications where efficient control of AC loads is required.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773824270426-731530663.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 08:57:50'),
(5289,1,'product',3309,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"Huayu Universal AC Remote \",\"description\":\"Works using infrared (IR) signal to control the AC indoor unit.Usually plug-and-play or simple code setup depending on AC model.\",\"info\":\"Comes with a digital LCD display showing temperature and mode settings.Designed with lightweight plastic body and rubber keypad buttons.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1543],\"model\":\"K-6600\",\"alternative_name\":\"Universal AC Remote \",\"mrp\":\"1\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773824931796-819992904.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 09:08:51'),
(5290,1,'product',3310,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BTA40-600\",\"description\":\"BTA40-600 is a high-power bidirectional TRIAC used for switching and phase control of large AC loads in industrial and domestic power electronics circuits. It allows current to flow in both directions between the main terminals when a triggering pulse is applied to the gate, making it suitable for efficient control of alternating-current power. The device has three terminals — MT1, MT2, and Gate, and is designed to operate reliably in high-current applications.\",\"info\":\"This TRIAC typically features a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 600 V and can handle load currents up to approximately 40 A, depending on proper heat-sink usage and operating conditions. It is generally supplied in a TO-3P or high-power insulated package, which provides improved thermal dissipation and electrical isolation from the heat sink.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773825078329-301728067.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 09:11:18'),
(5291,1,'product',3311,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BTA41-600\",\"description\":\"BTA41-600 is a high-current bidirectional TRIAC used for switching and phase-angle control of AC loads in power electronics applications. It allows current to flow in both directions between the main terminals once a gate trigger pulse is applied, making it suitable for controlling mains-operated equipment. The device has three terminals — MT1 (Main Terminal 1), MT2 (Main Terminal 2), and Gate, and is designed for reliable operation in heavy-duty circuits.\",\"info\":\"This TRIAC typically supports a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 600 V and can handle load currents up to around 40 A or more, depending on proper heat-sink design and operating conditions. It is usually available in a TO-3P / high-power insulated package, which improves thermal performance and simplifies mounting with electrical isolation.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773825196438-795324149.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 09:13:16'),
(5292,1,'product',3312,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"TYN612\",\"description\":\"TYN612 is a silicon controlled rectifier (SCR) designed for switching and controlled rectification of AC or DC power in electronic circuits. It has three terminals — anode, cathode, and gate — and once triggered by a small gate current, it conducts current from anode to cathode until the current falls below the holding level. This makes it suitable for controlled power delivery applications.\",\"info\":\"The device typically supports a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 600 V and can handle load currents around 12 A (depending on proper heat-sink conditions and circuit design). It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, which allows easy mounting and effective heat dissipation in power control circuits.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773825310541-567090754.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 09:15:10'),
(5293,1,'product',3313,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"TYN616\",\"description\":\"TYN616 is a high-voltage silicon controlled rectifier (SCR) designed for switching and controlled rectification of AC or DC power in industrial and domestic electronic circuits. It has three terminals — anode, cathode, and gate, and once a small triggering current is applied to the gate, the device allows current to flow between anode and cathode until the load current drops below the holding value.\",\"info\":\"This SCR typically supports a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 800 V and can handle load currents up to around 16 A, depending on proper heat-sink usage and operating conditions. It is usually available in a TO-220 power package, which helps in efficient heat dissipation and easy mounting on heat sinks.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773825396069-449505582.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 09:16:36'),
(5294,1,'product',3314,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"YY Universal A/C Remote Control\",\"description\":\"Works using infrared (IR) signal technology to communicate with the AC indoor unit.Comes with a digital LCD display showing temperature, fan speed, and operating mode.\",\"info\":\"Supports multiple AC brand codes and may require manual code setup or auto search.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1544],\"model\":\"YY-200\",\"alternative_name\":\" Universal A/C Remote\",\"mrp\":\"1\",\"note\":\"Keep away from water, moisture, and high heat\",\"alternative_names\":[]}','2026-03-18 09:17:51'),
(5295,1,'product',3315,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BC337-40\",\"description\":\"BC337-40 is a general-purpose NPN bipolar junction transistor (BJT) widely used for switching and amplification in low-power electronic circuits. It is designed to handle moderate current levels and provides high current gain, making it suitable for interfacing digital logic with loads such as relays, LEDs, buzzers, and small motors. The device is typically available in a compact TO-92 package and has three terminals — collector, base, and emitter.\",\"info\":\"This transistor generally supports a collector-emitter voltage of up to about 45 V and can handle collector currents up to around 800 mA, depending on operating conditions and heat dissipation. The “-40” suffix indicates a higher DC current gain group (hFE) compared to other BC337 variants, which helps improve switching sensitivity and amplification performance.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773825524766-143016694.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 09:18:44'),
(5296,1,'product',3316,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BC558\",\"description\":\"BC558 is a general-purpose PNP bipolar junction transistor (BJT) widely used for low-power switching and signal amplification in electronic circuits. It is typically available in a compact TO-92 package and has three terminals — emitter, base, and collector. This transistor is designed for small-signal applications and works as a complementary device to popular NPN transistors such as BC547 or BC337.\",\"info\":\"The BC558 generally supports a collector-emitter voltage of up to about 30 V and can handle collector currents up to around 100 mA, depending on operating conditions. It provides good current gain and low noise characteristics, making it suitable for audio and signal processing circuits.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773825628205-730544759.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 09:20:28'),
(5297,1,'product',3317,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BC550\",\"description\":\"BC550 is a low-noise NPN bipolar junction transistor (BJT) designed for signal amplification and low-current switching applications in electronic circuits. It is commonly available in a compact TO-92 package and has three terminals — collector, base, and emitter. This transistor is specially optimized for low-noise performance, making it suitable for sensitive audio and signal-processing stages.\",\"info\":\"The BC550 typically supports a collector-emitter voltage of up to about 45 V and can handle collector currents up to around 100 mA, depending on operating conditions. It offers good current gain and stable electrical characteristics, which help improve signal quality in amplification circuits.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773825716700-622021682.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 09:21:56'),
(5298,1,'product',3318,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BC618\",\"description\":\"BC618 is a general-purpose NPN bipolar junction transistor (BJT) used for low-power switching and signal amplification in electronic circuits. It is typically available in a compact TO-92 package and has three terminals — collector, base, and emitter — enabling it to function as an electronic switch or amplifier.\",\"info\":\"The transistor is designed to operate with moderate collector-emitter voltage levels (around 30–45 V depending on variant) and can handle collector currents up to roughly 100 mA, making it suitable for small-signal and driver applications. It provides good current gain and stable performance, allowing efficient interfacing between low-power control circuits and external loads.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773825999429-596927296.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 09:26:39'),
(5299,1,'product',3319,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BC635\",\"description\":\"BC635 is a general-purpose NPN bipolar junction transistor (BJT) designed for switching and amplification in medium-power electronic circuits. It is usually supplied in a compact TO-92 package and has three terminals — collector, base, and emitter — allowing it to function as an electronic switch or signal amplifier.\",\"info\":\"The device typically supports a collector-emitter voltage up to about 45 V and can handle collector currents up to around 1 A, depending on operating conditions and proper heat dissipation. It provides good current gain and fast switching characteristics, which make it suitable for driving loads that require more current than standard small-signal transistors.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773826395452-237476546.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 09:33:15'),
(5300,1,'product',3320,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BC807\",\"description\":\"BC807 is a general-purpose PNP bipolar junction transistor (BJT) designed mainly for surface-mount electronic circuits. It is commonly available in a compact SOT-23 package, making it suitable for high-density PCB designs and portable devices. The transistor has three terminals — emitter, base, and collector — and is used for signal amplification as well as low-to-medium current switching applications.\",\"info\":\"The device typically supports a collector-emitter voltage of up to about 45 V and can handle collector currents up to around 500 mA, depending on operating conditions and heat dissipation. It offers good current gain and fast switching characteristics, enabling efficient interfacing between logic circuits and loads such as LEDs, relays (with driver stages), and small motors.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773826784433-658728718.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 09:39:44'),
(5301,1,'product',3321,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BD241\",\"description\":\"BD241 is a medium-power NPN bipolar junction transistor (BJT) designed for switching and amplification in power electronic circuits. It is typically available in a TO-220 package, which allows efficient heat dissipation and easy mounting on a heat sink for higher current operation. The device has three terminals — collector, base, and emitter, enabling it to function as a power switch or amplifier stage.\",\"info\":\"The transistor generally supports a collector-emitter voltage of around 45 V to 80 V (depending on variant) and can handle collector currents up to about 3 A, making it suitable for driving moderate power loads. It provides good current gain and reliable thermal performance, which helps ensure stable operation in demanding applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773826937424-26327004.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 09:42:17'),
(5302,1,'product',3322,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"YY Universal A/C Remote Control\",\"description\":\"Works using infrared (IR) signal technology to communicate with the AC indoor unit.Usually comes with a digital LCD screen showing temperature, fan speed, and mode settings.\",\"info\":\"Enables convenient control of cooling functions from a distance.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1544],\"model\":\"K-LG1358 \",\"mrp\":\"1\",\"note\":\"Avoid dropping or strong impact\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773827555938-925522753.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 09:52:35'),
(5303,1,'category_brand_mapping',632,'update',NULL,'\"{\\\"assigned_brands\\\":[300,301,232]}\"','2026-03-18 09:55:02'),
(5304,1,'product',3323,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BD679\",\"description\":\"BD679 is a medium-power NPN Darlington transistor designed for high-gain switching and amplification applications in electronic circuits. A Darlington configuration internally connects two transistors to provide very high current gain, allowing small base currents to control relatively large load currents. The device is commonly available in a TO-126 / TO-225 style package and has three terminals — collector, base, and emitter.\",\"info\":\"The transistor typically supports a collector-emitter voltage of about 80 V and can handle collector currents up to around 4 A, depending on proper heat dissipation and operating conditions. It also includes an internal base-emitter resistor and protection diode, which helps improve switching reliability and simplifies circuit design.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773827981719-283153196.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 09:59:41'),
(5305,1,'product',3324,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BD682\",\"description\":\"BD682 is a medium-power PNP Darlington transistor designed for high-gain switching and amplification in power electronic circuits. Internally it consists of two transistors connected in Darlington configuration, providing very high current gain, which allows a small base current to control relatively large collector currents. The device is commonly available in a TO-126 / TO-225 package and has three terminals — emitter, base, and collector.\",\"info\":\"It typically supports a collector-emitter voltage of about 80 V and can handle collector currents up to around 4 A, depending on heat-sink conditions and operating environment. The transistor usually includes an internal base-emitter resistor and protection diode, which helps improve switching reliability and simplifies circuit design.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773828531067-137820093.jpg\"}','2026-03-18 10:08:51'),
(5306,1,'product',3325,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"Azone Universal Remote \",\"description\":\"Works using infrared (IR) signal technology to control the device.Many models support multiple brand codes and can be set using manual code entry or auto-search function.\",\"info\":\"Usually features a lightweight plastic body, rubber keypad, and LCD display (for AC remotes).Powered by AAA batteries and suitable for home and office use.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1548],\"mrp\":\"1\",\"note\":\"Easy plug-and-play operation in many models\",\"alternative_names\":[]}','2026-03-18 11:33:13'),
(5307,1,'product',3326,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"AC Remote \",\"description\":\"Works using infrared (IR) signal technology to communicate with the AC indoor unit.Usually features a digital LCD display to show temperature, mode, timer, and fan speed.\",\"info\":\"Many versions support direct use or simple code-setting (manual / auto search).Powered by AAA batteries for convenient daily use.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1548],\"model\":\"JE-JJ2\",\"mrp\":\"1\",\"note\":\"Do not expose the remote to water, moisture, or high heat\",\"alternative_names\":[]}','2026-03-18 11:50:32'),
