(5319,1,'product',3327,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BS170\",\"description\":\"BS170 is an N-channel enhancement mode MOSFET widely used in low-power electronic switching and amplification applications. It is designed in a compact TO-92 through-hole package, which makes it convenient for PCB mounting and breadboard prototyping. This MOSFET can handle a maximum drain-to-source voltage of around 60 volts and a continuous drain current of approximately 500 mA under suitable operating conditions.\",\"info\":\"In amplifier circuits, the BS170 can be used for signal processing and low-noise applications. Its simple three-pin configuration — gate, drain, and source — makes circuit design easy for beginners and professionals. Proper gate protection is important because the MOSFET gate is sensitive to static electricity. Heat dissipation should be considered when operating near maximum current ratings. The BS170 is also valued for its low cost, easy availability, and reliable performance in hobby, educational, and commercial electronics projects. Overall, it is a versatile and efficient component for small signal and switching applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773891334762-517048232.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 03:35:34'),
(5320,1,'product',3328,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BUZ71\",\"description\":\"UZ71 is an N-channel enhancement mode power MOSFET designed for high-current and high-voltage switching applications. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, which allows efficient heat dissipation and easy mounting on heat sinks. This MOSFET can withstand a drain-to-source voltage of around 50V and can handle high drain current, making it suitable for power control circuits. The BUZ71 offers relatively low ON resistance, which helps reduce power loss during switching operations\",\"info\":\"The device supports fast switching speed, which improves efficiency in high-frequency applications. Its rugged construction ensures reliable performance in industrial and consumer electronic systems. Proper heat sink usage is recommended when operating at high load conditions to prevent thermal damage. Gate protection using resistors or zener diodes helps improve device life and stability. The simple three-terminal configuration — Gate, Drain, and Source — makes circuit design straightforward. Overall, BUZ71 is a dependable and cost-effective MOSFET for medium-power switching and control applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773891419327-847238372.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 03:36:59'),
(5321,1,'product',3329,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BYQ28-200\",\"description\":\"BYQ28-200 is a high-efficiency ultrafast recovery rectifier diode designed for high-frequency power rectification and switching applications. It is typically available in a TO-220 package, which allows good heat dissipation and easy mounting on heat sinks in power circuits. The diode has a maximum repetitive peak reverse voltage of about 200 volts, making it suitable for medium-voltage power supply designs.\",\"info\":\"The device is commonly used in output rectification stages of switched-mode power supplies and high-frequency rectifier circuits. Its rugged construction ensures reliable operation under high-temperature and high-current conditions. Proper heat sinking is recommended during high load operation to avoid thermal stress and extend component life. Correct polarity must always be maintained during installation since it is a rectifier device. The BYQ28-200 also helps reduce switching losses and electromagnetic interference in power electronics systems. Due to its stable performance, easy availability, and efficient operation, it is widely used in industrial, commercial, and hobby power supply projects.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[551],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773891670452-343716347.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 03:41:10'),
(5322,1,'product',3330,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BYV32-200\",\"description\":\"BYV32-200 is a high-performance ultrafast recovery rectifier diode designed for use in high-frequency power supply and switching circuits. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, which allows efficient heat dissipation and easy installation on heat sinks for improved thermal performance. The diode typically supports a maximum repetitive reverse voltage of about 200 volts and can handle relatively high forward current, making it suitable for medium-power rectification applications.\",\"info\":\"The device is known for stable operation under high-temperature conditions and reliable performance in industrial as well as consumer electronic equipment. Proper heat sink usage is recommended when operating at higher current levels to prevent overheating. Care must be taken to maintain correct polarity during installation since it is a rectifier diode. Due to its rugged construction, fast switching capability, and good efficiency, the BYV32-200 is a popular choice in modern power electronics designs.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[551],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773891784981-542455652.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 03:43:04'),
(5323,1,'product',3331,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"BYV96E\",\"description\":\"BYV96E is a fast recovery rectifier diode mainly used in high-frequency rectification and switching power applications. It is generally available in an axial lead DO-15 package, making it suitable for through-hole mounting in power supply and converter circuits. The diode is designed to handle a high repetitive reverse voltage (around 1000V) and moderate forward current, which makes it useful in medium-power electronic designs. Its fast reverse recovery time helps to reduce switching losses and improve efficiency in circuits operating at high frequencies.\",\"info\":\"The BYV96E is commonly used in SMPS, inverter circuits, freewheeling protection, snubber networks, and DC-DC converters. It also provides low forward voltage drop, which contributes to lower heat generation and better overall performance. Due to its rugged construction, the device can operate reliably in demanding electrical environments. Proper lead spacing and adequate ventilation or heat dissipation should be ensured when used near maximum ratings. Correct polarity must always be maintained during installation since it functions as a rectifier. The diode is valued for its stable performance, durability, and wide availability, making it suitable for industrial equipment, consumer electronics, and hobby power projects.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[551],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773891863319-217354965.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 03:44:23'),
(5324,1,'product',3332,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"MJE3055\",\"description\":\"MJE3055 is a widely used NPN silicon power transistor designed for medium-power amplification and switching applications. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, which allows effective heat dissipation and convenient mounting on heat sinks in power circuits. This transistor can handle relatively high collector current and voltage, making it suitable for power control stages in electronic equipment. The MJE3055 provides good gain characteristics and reliable switching performance, which helps improve efficiency in amplifier and regulator circuits.\",\"info\":\"The transistor features a simple three-terminal configuration — Base, Collector, and Emitter, which makes circuit design straightforward for both beginners and professionals. Proper biasing and base current limiting resistors are recommended to ensure stable operation and long device life. When used near maximum ratings, adequate cooling arrangements should be provided to avoid thermal damage. The MJE3055 is valued for its low cost, easy availability, and dependable performance in industrial, educational, and hobby electronics projects.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773891938820-509777127.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 03:45:38'),
(5325,1,'product',3333,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"MJE13005\",\"description\":\"MJE13005 is a high-voltage NPN power switching transistor commonly used in switched-mode power supplies and high-frequency switching circuits. It is typically available in a TO-220 package, which allows efficient heat dissipation and easy mounting on heat sinks for improved thermal management. This transistor is designed to withstand high collector-emitter voltage (around 400V) and moderate collector current, making it suitable for offline power supply designs. The MJE13005 offers fast switching characteristics and good current gain, which helps improve efficiency and performance in switching regulator circuits\",\"info\":\"It is widely used in SMPS, inverter circuits, CFL and LED drivers, battery chargers, and power converters. Due to its rugged internal structure, the device provides reliable operation under high-voltage stress when proper biasing and cooling are maintained. The transistor has a simple three-pin configuration — Base, Collector, and Emitter, which simplifies circuit design and servicing. Proper base resistor selection and snubber or protection networks are recommended to enhance switching stability and device life. Adequate heat sinking is essential when operating near maximum load conditions to prevent overheating. Because of its low cost, durability, and wide availability, the MJE13005 is a popular choice in consumer and industrial power electronics applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773892007336-810784189.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 03:46:47'),
(5326,1,'product',3334,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"MBR2045\",\"description\":\"MBR2045 is a high-current Schottky barrier rectifier diode designed for low-voltage, high-efficiency power supply applications. It is generally available in a TO-220 package, which provides good heat dissipation and allows easy mounting on a heat sink for improved thermal performance. The diode typically supports a maximum reverse voltage of about 45 volts and can handle high forward current up to around 20 amperes, making it suitable for output rectification in switched-mode power supplies.\",\"info\":\"The MBR2045 also features fast switching characteristics, enabling reliable performance in high-frequency applications such as DC-DC converters, inverters, battery chargers, and power regulators. It is often used as a dual rectifier diode, commonly configured in center-tap rectification circuits. The device provides stable operation under high current conditions when proper heat sinking and PCB layout are maintained. Correct polarity and proper mounting insulation should be ensured during installation. Because of its high efficiency, rugged design, and wide availability, the MBR2045 is widely used in industrial equipment, computer power supplies, and various consumer electronic power systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[551],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773892268496-867031233.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 03:51:08'),
(5327,1,'product',3335,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"MBR3045\",\"description\":\"MBR3045 is a high-current Schottky barrier rectifier diode mainly used in low-voltage, high-efficiency power supply circuits. It is usually available in a TO-220 package, which allows effective heat dissipation and easy mounting on heat sinks for reliable operation under heavy load conditions. This diode typically supports a maximum reverse voltage of about 45 volts and can handle high forward current up to around 30 amperes, making it suitable for medium to high-power rectification stages.\",\"info\":\"The MBR3045 provides a very low forward voltage drop, which helps reduce power loss and heat generation, thereby improving overall system efficiency. Due to its fast switching characteristics, it is widely used in SMPS output rectification, DC-DC converters, inverters, battery chargers, and power regulation circuits. The device is commonly designed as a dual common-cathode rectifier, allowing flexible configuration in center-tap transformer applications. Its rugged construction ensures stable performance in industrial and consumer electronic equipment. Proper heat sink usage and correct polarity connection are important to prevent thermal damage and ensure long service life. Because of its high efficiency, durability, and wide availability, the MBR3045 is a popular choice in computer power supplies, solar power systems, and other high-current DC power applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[551],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773892368236-846413605.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 03:52:48'),
(5328,1,'product',3336,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"MBR3060\",\"description\":\"MBR3060 is a high-current Schottky barrier rectifier diode designed for efficient rectification in low-voltage and high-frequency power supply circuits. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, which enables effective heat dissipation and easy mounting on heat sinks for improved thermal performance. This diode typically supports a maximum reverse voltage of about 60 volts and can handle forward current up to around 30 amperes, making it suitable for medium to high-power applications.\",\"info\":\"It also features fast switching characteristics, allowing reliable operation in high-frequency circuits such as switched-mode power supplies, DC-DC converters, battery chargers, solar inverters, and power regulators. The device is usually configured as a dual rectifier (common cathode), enabling flexible design in center-tap rectification stages. Its rugged construction ensures stable performance under heavy load and varying temperature conditions. Proper heat sink installation and correct polarity connection are important to prevent overheating and extend the component’s service life. Due to its high efficiency, durability, and wide availability, the MBR3060 is widely used in computer SMPS units, industrial power modules, and other high-current DC power systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[551],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773892458847-51742062.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 03:54:18'),
(5329,1,'product',3337,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"MBR20100\",\"description\":\"MBR20100 is a high-performance Schottky barrier rectifier diode designed for efficient power rectification in low-to-medium voltage power supply applications. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, which allows easy mounting on a heat sink and provides good thermal dissipation during high current operation. This diode typically supports a maximum reverse voltage of around 100 volts and a forward current rating of about 20 amperes, making it suitable for SMPS output stages and DC power distribution circuits.\",\"info\":\"The MBR20100 offers a very low forward voltage drop, which helps minimize power loss and improves overall system efficiency. Due to its fast switching capability, it performs well in high-frequency applications such as DC-DC converters, battery chargers, solar power systems, and inverters. The device is generally configured as a dual common-cathode rectifier, allowing flexible use in center-tap rectification circuits. Its rugged design ensures reliable performance under varying load and temperature conditions. Proper heat sink usage and correct polarity connection are essential for safe and long-term operation. Because of its high efficiency, stable characteristics, and wide availability, the MBR20100 is widely used in industrial equipment, computer power supplies, and various consumer electronic power systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[551],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773892539663-550486891.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 03:55:39'),
(5330,1,'product',3338,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"MBR20200\",\"description\":\"MBR20200 is a high-voltage Schottky barrier rectifier diode designed for efficient power rectification in switched-mode power supplies and high-frequency converter circuits. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, which allows effective heat dissipation and easy mounting on heat sinks for reliable operation at high current levels. This diode typically supports a maximum reverse voltage of about 200 volts and can handle forward current up to around 20 amperes, making it suitable for medium-power rectification stages. One of its key advantages is the low forward voltage drop, which helps reduce power loss and improves overall system efficiency.\",\"info\":\"The MBR20200 also features fast switching characteristics, enabling stable performance in high-frequency applications such as DC-DC converters, inverters, battery chargers, solar power systems, and SMPS output rectification. It is usually configured as a dual common-cathode rectifier, allowing flexible use in center-tap transformer designs. The device provides reliable operation under varying load and temperature conditions when proper heat sinking is used. Correct polarity connection and adequate PCB layout spacing are important for safe installation. Because of its rugged construction, efficiency, and wide availability, the MBR20200 is widely used in industrial power modules, computer SMPS units, and other high-current DC power circuits.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[551],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773892644468-655024265.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 03:57:24'),
(5331,1,'product',3339,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"2N2646\",\"description\":\"2N2646 is a well-known Unijunction Transistor (UJT) used mainly for timing, triggering, and pulse generation applications in electronic circuits. It is typically available in a compact TO-92 package, which makes it convenient for PCB mounting and breadboard prototyping. The device operates on the principle of negative resistance characteristics, allowing it to generate stable pulses and oscillations in relaxation oscillator circuits. The 2N2646 is widely used in SCR and TRIAC triggering circuits, phase control systems, and timing control units\",\"info\":\"It features three terminals known as Emitter (E), Base-1 (B1), and Base-2 (B2), which are used for controlling conduction and pulse generation. Due to its simple construction and reliable operation, it is suitable for educational, industrial, and hobby electronics projects. The transistor requires only a few external components to build oscillator or triggering circuits, making circuit design easy and economical. It provides stable switching performance over a wide range of supply voltages and temperatures. Proper resistor and capacitor selection is important for accurate timing operation. Care should be taken to avoid exceeding maximum emitter voltage and power dissipation limits. Because of its low cost, durability, and ease of use, the 2N2646 remains popular in waveform generation and controlled switching applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773892720952-37836445.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 03:58:40'),
(5332,1,'product',3340,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"2N2907\",\"description\":\"2N2907 is a widely used PNP bipolar junction transistor (BJT) designed for general-purpose switching and amplification applications. It is commonly available in a compact TO-92 package, which makes it suitable for PCB mounting as well as breadboard prototyping. This transistor can handle moderate collector current and voltage, making it useful in low-power control and signal processing circuits. The 2N2907 provides good current gain and reliable switching characteristics, allowing efficient operation in digital and analog electronic designs\",\"info\":\"It is frequently used in audio amplifier stages, relay and LED driver circuits, small motor control, and signal amplification applications. The device has three terminals — Emitter, Base, and Collector — which makes circuit connections simple and easy to understand. Because it is a PNP transistor, it conducts when the base is driven to a lower potential than the emitter. Proper base resistor selection is important to control base current and ensure stable performance. When used near maximum ratings, suitable heat dissipation and correct biasing should be provided. The 2N2907 is valued for its low cost, easy availability, and dependable performance, making it a popular choice in educational projects, consumer electronics, and industrial control circuits.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773892796787-728199860.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 03:59:56'),
(5333,1,'product',3341,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"A1015\",\"description\":\"A1015, also known as 2SA1015, is a low-noise PNP bipolar junction transistor widely used in small signal amplification and switching circuits. It is commonly available in a compact TO-92 package, which makes it suitable for PCB mounting and breadboard prototyping. This transistor is designed to handle moderate collector-emitter voltage (around 50V) and low to medium collector current, making it ideal for signal processing applications. The A1015 provides good current gain and low noise characteristics, which help improve audio quality in pre-amplifier and tone control circuits\",\"info\":\"It is frequently used in audio amplifier stages, oscillator circuits, signal amplification, and general-purpose switching applications. The device has three terminals — Emitter, Base, and Collector — allowing simple circuit design and easy replacement. Because it is a PNP transistor, conduction occurs when the base voltage is lower than the emitter voltage. Proper base biasing and current limiting resistors should be used to ensure stable operation and long device life. Adequate heat dissipation may be required when operating near maximum ratings. Due to its reliable performance, low cost, and wide availability, the A1015 is commonly used in consumer electronics, educational kits, and hobby electronic projects.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773892964228-92438565.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 04:02:44'),
(5334,1,'product',3342,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"2SC945\",\"description\":\"C945, also known as 2SC945, is a general-purpose NPN bipolar junction transistor widely used in small signal amplification and switching applications. It is commonly available in a compact TO-92 package, making it suitable for PCB mounting as well as breadboard prototyping. This transistor is designed to handle moderate collector-emitter voltage (around 50V) and low to medium collector current, which makes it ideal for signal processing and control circuits. The C945 offers good current gain and low noise performance, allowing it to be effectively used in audio pre-amplifier stages, tone control circuits, and oscillator designs.\",\"info\":\"It is also frequently used in relay drivers, LED switching circuits, small motor control, and digital logic interfacing. The device has three terminals — Collector, Base, and Emitter — which makes circuit design simple and easy for beginners and professionals. Proper base resistor selection is important to control base current and maintain stable operation. When used near maximum ratings, suitable heat dissipation and correct biasing should be ensured. Due to its low cost, easy availability, and dependable performance, the C945 transistor is commonly found in consumer electronics, DIY electronics kits, and educational projects.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773893088588-927491929.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 04:04:48'),
(5335,1,'product',3343,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"2N6107\",\"description\":\"2N6107 is a PNP silicon power transistor designed for medium-to-high power amplification and switching applications in electronic circuits. It is typically available in a TO-220 package, which allows efficient heat dissipation and convenient mounting on heat sinks for reliable operation at higher load conditions. This transistor can withstand relatively high collector-emitter voltage (around 70–80V) and supports higher collector current, making it suitable for power control stages\",\"info\":\"The 2N6107 provides good current gain and stable switching performance, which helps improve efficiency in regulator and driver circuits. It is widely used in audio power amplifiers, voltage regulator circuits, motor control systems, inverter stages, and general power switching applications. The device features a simple three-terminal configuration — Base, Collector, and Emitter, enabling straightforward circuit design and servicing. Proper base biasing and current-limiting resistors should be used to ensure safe and stable operation. Adequate heat sinking is recommended when the transistor is operated near its maximum ratings to prevent thermal damage. Due to its rugged construction, dependable performance, and wide availability, the 2N6107 is commonly used in industrial equipment, consumer electronics, and hobby power projects.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[533],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773893410936-776926019.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 04:10:10'),
