(5338,1,'product',3344,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"28C64\",\"description\":\"28C64 is a non-volatile parallel EEPROM memory IC that provides 64 kilobits (8K × 8 bytes) of data storage capacity. It is widely used in microprocessor and microcontroller-based systems to store program data, configuration settings, lookup tables, and calibration values. The device retains stored information even when the power supply is turned off, making it suitable for permanent or semi-permanent data storage applications. The 28C64 usually operates with a standard 5-volt power supply and supports fast read and write operations through its parallel interface. It features multiple address lines for memory location selection and bidirectional data lines for reading and writing data\",\"info\":\"Control signals such as Chip Enable (CE), Output Enable (OE), and Write Enable (WE) are used to manage memory access. Unlike older EPROM devices, this EEPROM allows electrical byte-level erase and programming, eliminating the need for ultraviolet light erasing. The IC offers high endurance and long data retention, ensuring reliable performance over thousands of write cycles. Proper timing control and stable voltage supply are important for correct operation. The 28C64 is commonly available in DIP packages, making it easy to use in educational kits, industrial control systems, embedded projects, and digital storage circuits.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1551],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773893860871-601437631.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 04:17:40'),
(5339,1,'product',3345,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"AT89C55\",\"description\":\"89C55 (commonly AT89C55) is an 8-bit 8051-based microcontroller widely used in embedded control and digital electronics applications. It features Flash programmable memory, allowing users to easily write, erase, and reprogram application code. The device typically provides 20KB of Flash program memory, along with RAM, timers, serial communication interface, and multiple I/O ports. It operates with a standard 5V power supply and supports clock frequencies suitable for general-purpose control tasks.\",\"info\":\"The 89C55 includes four 8-bit parallel I/O ports, enabling easy interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, motors, and other digital components. Built-in peripherals such as timers/counters, UART serial port, and interrupt system help simplify embedded system design. It is commonly used in industrial automation systems, home appliance control, robotics, instrumentation, and educational development kits. The IC is generally available in DIP and SMD packages, making it suitable for both prototyping and mass production. Proper crystal oscillator connection and reset circuitry are required for reliable operation. Due to its stable performance, easy programming features, and wide availability, the 89C55 remains popular among students, hobbyists, and engineers working with classic 8051 architecture projects.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1551],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773894052215-466544936.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 04:20:52'),
(5340,1,'product',3346,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"AT89C2051\",\"description\":\"89C2051 (commonly AT89C2051) is a compact 8-bit 8051-based microcontroller designed for small embedded control applications. It contains 2KB of Flash programmable program memory, allowing easy development, modification, and reprogramming of embedded software. The device operates with a 5-volt power supply and supports standard crystal oscillator clock circuits for stable timing performance. It provides 15 programmable I/O lines, enabling direct interfacing with switches, LEDs, sensors, displays, relays, and other digital components.\",\"info\":\"The microcontroller includes important built-in peripherals such as timers/counters, interrupt system, and full-duplex serial communication (UART), which simplify embedded system design. Due to its small 20-pin package, the 89C2051 is ideal for compact circuit layouts and low-cost control systems. It is widely used in home appliance controllers, automation circuits, security systems, instrumentation, robotics projects, and educational development kits. Proper reset circuitry and oscillator connections are required for reliable operation. The IC offers low power consumption and stable performance, making it suitable for battery-operated and portable electronic devices. Because of its easy programming features, dependable operation, and wide availability, the 89C2051 remains popular in both hobby and industrial embedded applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1551],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773894191847-182372660.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 04:23:11'),
(5341,1,'product',3347,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"AT89C4051\",\"description\":\"89C4051 (commonly AT89C4051) is a compact 8-bit microcontroller based on the 8051 architecture, designed for small and medium embedded control applications. It features 4KB of Flash programmable program memory, allowing easy development, modification, and reprogramming of application code. The device typically operates with a 5-volt power supply and uses an external crystal oscillator to generate the system clock for reliable timing operation. It provides around 15 programmable input/output pins, enabling direct interfacing with switches, LEDs, relays, sensors, displays, and other digital components.\",\"info\":\"The microcontroller includes useful built-in peripherals such as timers/counters, interrupt system, and full-duplex serial communication (UART), which help simplify embedded system design. Because of its small 20-pin package, the 89C4051 is suitable for compact PCB layouts and low-cost control systems. It is widely used in home appliance controllers, industrial automation circuits, security devices, robotics projects, instrumentation, and educational development kits. Proper reset circuitry and stable clock connections are necessary to ensure dependable performance. The IC offers low power consumption, stable operation, and easy programming capability, making it a popular choice for students, hobbyists, and engineers working with classic 8051-based designs.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1551],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773894274235-81316693.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 04:24:34'),
(5342,1,'product',3348,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"AT89S8253\",\"description\":\"89S8253 (commonly AT89S8253) is an advanced 8-bit microcontroller based on the 8051 architecture, designed for embedded control and automation applications. It features 12KB of in-system programmable Flash memory, allowing program code to be written, erased, and updated without removing the IC from the circuit. The device also includes internal EEPROM data memory, which is useful for storing configuration data and system parameters even when power is removed. It operates with a 5-volt supply and supports standard crystal oscillator clock circuits for stable timing performance\",\"info\":\"The microcontroller provides 32 programmable I/O lines through four parallel ports, enabling easy interfacing with displays, sensors, relays, motors, and communication modules. Built-in peripherals such as timers/counters, interrupt controller, watchdog timer, and full-duplex serial UART help simplify system design. It also supports SPI programming interface, making firmware updates convenient in development and production environments. The 89S8253 is widely used in industrial automation systems, instrumentation, robotics, consumer electronic products, and educational development kits. Proper reset circuitry, clock connections, and power supply decoupling are important for reliable operation. Because of its stable performance, flexible memory features, and easy programming capability, the 89S8253 remains a practical choice for many classic 8051-based embedded applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1551],\"mrp\":\"49\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773894356587-649892750.jpg\"}','2026-03-19 04:25:56'),
(5343,2,'sector_title_multitab_heading',11,'create',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-19 05:26:44'),
(5344,1,'product',2249,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"10nF (103)\",\"description\":\"A 10 nF (103) ceramic capacitor is a non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric to store electrical energy. The marking 103 corresponds to 10,000 pF, calculated as 10 × 10³ pF, which is equal to 10 nF or 0.01 µF. This value is very commonly used in general electronic circuits.\",\"info\":\"A 10 nF ceramic capacitor is widely used for noise filtering, signal coupling, decoupling, and EMI/RFI suppression. It is often placed near IC power pins, across signal lines, or in RC timing and filtering networks. Being non-polarized, it can be connected in either direction, making it suitable for both AC and DC applications.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"10nF (103) capacitor is a small-value non-polarized capacitor commonly used in filtering, coupling, timing, and noise suppression applications. The marking “103” follows the standard three-digit capacitor code system, where the first two digits (10) are the significant figures and the third digit (3) represents the number of zeros in picofarads (pF). Therefore, 10 × 10³ = 10,000 pF, which equals 10nF (0.01µF). This type of capacitor is typically available as a ceramic disc or multilayer ceramic capacitor (MLCC) and can be connected in any direction since it is non-polarized.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":416,\"secondary_id\":0,\"brand_id\":232}],\"alternative_names\":[]}','2026-03-19 09:37:15'),
(5345,1,'product',3349,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"Coaxial Cable with BNC Connector\",\"description\":\"Coaxial cables with BNC connectors are available in different types such as RG59 and RG6, with RG59 being most common for CCTV installations due to its flexibility and adequate performance over shorter distances, while RG6 is used for longer runs with better shielding. These cables are known for their durability, resistance to electromagnetic interference (EMI), and ease of installation.\",\"info\":\"BNC connectors are typically made of metal with nickel or gold plating to enhance conductivity and corrosion resistance. They are compatible with a wide range of devices including cameras, video recorders, oscilloscopes, and test equipment.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1480],\"alternative_name\":\"Camera Conector\",\"mrp\":\"399\",\"note\":\"Always ensure proper cable length and quality to avoid signal degradation, especially in long-distance installations. Secure connections are essential—loose BNC connectors can cause signal loss or distortion. It is recommended to use high-quality shielded cables in environments with high electrical noise. Regular inspection of connectors and cable insulation helps maintain performance and longevity.\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773919748530-102380074.jpeg\"}','2026-03-19 11:29:08'),
(5346,1,'product',3350,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"Female VGA Connector\",\"description\":\"Female VGA Connector is a 15-pin analog interface port used to receive video signals from devices such as computers, laptops, and media players. It is commonly known as a HD-15 (High Density D-subminiature) connector and features three rows of five holes (pins) arranged in a trapezoidal shape. The female VGA connector is typically found on monitors, projectors, and extension cables, allowing a male VGA plug to connect securely.\",\"info\":\"Female VGA connectors are widely used in legacy systems and are usually color-coded blue for easy identification. They support various resolutions depending on the cable quality and hardware, commonly up to 1080p, though signal quality may degrade over longer distances. The connector includes screw holes on both sides to secure the connection firmly, preventing accidental disconnection.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[94],\"alternative_name\":\"VGA Connector\",\"mrp\":\"399\",\"note\":\"VGA does not carry audio signals, so separate audio cables are required when sound transmission is needed. Despite being largely replaced by HDMI and DisplayPort, VGA is still used in many industrial, educational, and older office setups.\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773921889857-735842220.jpeg\"}','2026-03-19 12:04:49'),
(5347,1,'product',3351,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"Male VGA Connector\",\"description\":\"Male VGA Connector is a 15-pin analog plug used to transmit video signals from a source device such as a computer, CPU, or laptop to a display device like a monitor or projector. It is also known as an HD-15 (High Density D-sub) connector and features three rows of exposed pins arranged in a trapezoidal shape. The male VGA connector is typically attached to the end of a VGA cable and is designed to fit securely into a female VGA port, ensuring proper alignment and stable signal transmission.\",\"info\":\"Male VGA connectors are commonly found on VGA cables and older graphics cards. They are usually blue in color for easy identification and include two side screws that allow the connector to be tightened into the female port, preventing accidental disconnection. These connectors carry analog video signals only and support various display resolutions, though performance depends on cable quality and length. VGA connections are widely used in older desktop systems, projectors, and industrial display setups.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[94],\"alternative_name\":\"VGA Connector\",\"mrp\":\"399\",\"note\":\"Always handle the connector carefully to avoid bending or breaking the pins, as damaged pins can cause display issues such as missing colors or no signal. Ensure the connector is properly aligned before inserting it into the port. Avoid excessive force while connecting or disconnecting.\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773922434812-139771412.jpeg\"}','2026-03-19 12:13:54'),
(5348,1,'product',3352,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"RS232 Male Connector\",\"description\":\"RS232 Male Connector is a standard serial communication interface plug used to transmit data between devices such as computers, modems, industrial machines, and networking equipment. It is commonly available in a DB9 (9-pin) or sometimes DB25 (25-pin) configuration, with the DB9 being the most widely used. The male connector features exposed metal pins arranged in a D-shaped (D-subminiature) housing, which ensures correct orientation and secure connection when plugged into a corresponding female port.\",\"info\":\"RS232 male connectors operate using voltage signals (typically between +3V to +15V and -3V to -15V) to represent binary data. They are widely used in legacy systems, industrial automation, POS machines, CNC equipment, and embedded systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[94],\"alternative_name\":\"RS232 Connector\",\"mrp\":\"399\",\"note\":\"The connector includes screw locks on either side to secure the connection and prevent accidental disconnection. RS232 communication is relatively slow compared to modern interfaces, typically supporting data rates up to 115.2 kbps, but it is highly reliable for short-distance communication (usually up to 15 meters).\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773922688074-559425907.jpeg\"}','2026-03-19 12:18:08'),
(5349,1,'product',3353,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"RS232 Female Connector\",\"description\":\"RS232 Female Connector is a standard serial communication port designed to receive data connections from an RS232 male connector. It is most commonly found in a DB9 (9-pin) configuration, though older systems may use a DB25 (25-pin) version. The female connector features 9 holes (sockets) arranged in a D-shaped (D-subminiature) layout, ensuring proper alignment and secure mating with the corresponding male plug.\",\"info\":\"RS232 female connectors are typically mounted on devices such as PCs, PLCs, modems, POS systems, and embedded hardware. They use voltage-based signaling (positive and negative voltage levels) to transmit binary data asynchronously. The connector includes threaded screw locks on both sides, allowing the attached male connector to be tightened securely for stable communication.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[94],\"alternative_name\":\"RS232 Connector\",\"mrp\":\"399\",\"note\":\"Always match the correct pin configuration (straight-through or null modem) depending on the communication requirement. Ensure the connector is clean and free from dust or corrosion to maintain proper contact. Tighten the screws firmly to avoid loose connections that can cause data errors. Avoid applying excessive force while connecting or disconnecting.\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1773922836417-236353770.jpeg\"}','2026-03-19 12:20:36'),
