(5385,1,'product',179,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"SG 90 Servo Motor\",\"description\":\"you’re referring to the 9G Micro Servo Motor, often labeled as SG90, TG9e, or TowerPro 9G — the most popular and economical servo for small robotics, model planes, and educational Arduino projects.\",\"info\":\"The 9g micro servo (often called SG90) is a very compact, lightweight PWM-controlled servo widely used in hobby and educational projects.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"400.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":196,\"secondary_id\":422,\"brand_id\":232}],\"alternative_names\":[]}','2026-03-25 11:16:19'),
(5386,1,'product',492,'delete',NULL,NULL,'2026-03-25 11:17:18'),
(5387,1,'product',3366,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"L-Type Bo Motor\",\"description\":\"An L-Type BO Motor (Battery Operated Motor) is a right-angle geared DC motor commonly used in robotics and DIY vehicle projects. Unlike standard BO motors, this motor has an L-shaped (90°) gearbox design, where the motor shaft and output shaft are positioned at a right angle. This unique structure allows better space management and flexible mounting in compact robotic designs.\",\"info\":\"The motor operates on low voltage (typically 3V to 12V DC) and includes an internal gear mechanism that reduces speed while increasing torque. This makes it ideal for driving wheels and carrying loads in small robots and automated systems.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1287],\"mrp\":\"399\",\"alternative_names\":[]}','2026-03-25 11:57:21'),
(5388,1,'product',298,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"1CH 5V Relay Module\",\"description\":\"1CH 5V Relay Module is a small control board with a single 5 V-powered electromechanical relay that lets a low-voltage logic signal from a microcontroller (like Arduino, ESP32, PIC, AVR, or Raspberry Pi with level shifting) switch a higher-power AC or DC load such as lights, motors, fans, or appliances\",\"info\":\"COM (Common), NO (Normally Open), and NC (Normally Closed) terminals for flexible switching.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"Relay Module\",\"mrp\":\"399\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":165,\"secondary_id\":\"58\",\"brand_id\":232}],\"alternative_names\":[]}','2026-03-25 12:38:52'),
(5389,1,'product',286,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"4CH 12v Relay Module\",\"description\":\"4CH 12V Relay Module is a board with four independent 12 V-powered electromechanical relays that let you control four separate high-power loads (like lights, fans, motors, appliances, etc.) using low-voltage control signals from microcontrollers (Arduino, Raspberry Pi with level shifting, PIC, etc.)\",\"info\":\"Each relay typically provides Common (COM), Normally Open (NO), and Normally Closed (NC) contacts and has LED indicators for status. These modules are commonly used in home automation, industrial control, robotics, and IoT projects to safely switch AC/DC loads with electrical isolation between the control and power sides.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"499\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":165,\"secondary_id\":\"58\",\"brand_id\":232}],\"alternative_names\":[]}','2026-03-25 12:52:20'),
(5390,1,'product',293,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"4CH 5v RELAY Module\",\"description\":\"4CH 5V Relay Module is a control board that contains four independent 5 V-powered electromechanical relays, allowing a low-voltage control signal (from microcontrollers like Arduino, ESP32, PIC, AVR, Raspberry Pi with level shifting, etc.) to safely switch higher-power AC/DC loads such as lights, motors, fans, and appliances.\",\"info\":\"Each relay provides Common (COM), Normally Open (NO), and Normally Closed (NC) contacts and usually has LED indicators showing relay status. These modules are commonly used in home automation, robotics, IoT systems, and embedded control projects to interface logic-level electronics with real-world power circuits.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"399\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":165,\"secondary_id\":\"58\",\"brand_id\":232}],\"alternative_names\":[]}','2026-03-25 12:52:44'),
(5391,1,'product',292,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"16CHANNEL 5V Relay Module\",\"description\":\"A 16-Channel 5 V Relay Module lets you control sixteen separate high-power circuits using a single board and simple digital signals from microcontroller GPIOs\",\"info\":\"These modules are widely used in home automation, robotics, industrial control panels, IoT systems, and smart projects where multiple devices need switching from low-voltage logic.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"1499\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":165,\"secondary_id\":\"58\",\"brand_id\":232}],\"alternative_names\":[]}','2026-03-25 12:53:08'),
(5392,1,'product',3367,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"8Ch 5V Relay Module\",\"description\":\"An 8 Channel 5V Relay Module is an electronic switching board that allows a microcontroller such as Arduino, Raspberry Pi, or other logic systems to control up to 8 high-power electrical devices simultaneously. Each channel consists of a relay that acts as an electrically operated switch, enabling safe control of AC or DC loads using low-voltage signals (5V).\",\"info\":\"This module is widely used in home automation, industrial control systems, IoT projects, and robotics, where multiple devices like lights, fans, motors, or appliances need to be controlled programmatically.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[17],\"alternative_name\":\"Relay Module\",\"mrp\":\"799\",\"alternative_names\":[]}','2026-03-25 13:04:17'),
(5393,1,'product',3368,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"12V Sugar Cube Relay\",\"description\":\"A 12V Sugar Cube Relay is a compact electromechanical switching device widely used in electronic circuits to control high-power loads using a low-voltage control signal. It gets the name “sugar cube” due to its small cube-shaped plastic casing, making it ideal for PCB mounting in compact designs. These relays are commonly found in automation systems, power control circuits, and embedded electronics.\",\"info\":\"The relay operates using a 12V DC coil. When voltage is applied to the coil, it creates a magnetic field that pulls an internal switch, changing the connection between its terminals. This allows a low-power circuit (like a microcontroller) to safely control high-voltage or high-current devices.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[17],\"alternative_name\":\"Relay\",\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[]}','2026-03-25 13:18:22'),
(5394,1,'product',3368,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"12V Sugar Cube Relay\",\"description\":\"A 12V Sugar Cube Relay is a compact electromechanical switching device widely used in electronic circuits to control high-power loads using a low-voltage control signal. It gets the name “sugar cube” due to its small cube-shaped plastic casing, making it ideal for PCB mounting in compact designs. These relays are commonly found in automation systems, power control circuits, and embedded electronics.\",\"info\":\"The relay operates using a 12V DC coil. When voltage is applied to the coil, it creates a magnetic field that pulls an internal switch, changing the connection between its terminals. This allows a low-power circuit (like a microcontroller) to safely control high-voltage or high-current devices.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"99.00\",\"note\":\"\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":165,\"secondary_id\":58,\"brand_id\":232}],\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1774444731136-933817029.jpeg\"}','2026-03-25 13:18:51'),
(5395,1,'product',3369,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"12v Power Relay\",\"description\":\"A 12V Power Relay is an electromechanical switching device designed to control high-current or high-voltage loads using a 12V DC control signal. It is commonly used in automotive systems, industrial control panels, home automation, and power switching applications. Compared to small relays (like sugar cube relays), power relays are built to handle higher current loads (10A to 40A or more).\",\"info\":\"When 12V is applied to the relay coil, it creates a magnetic field that moves an internal armature, switching the contacts from one position to another. This allows a low-power circuit (like a switch, microcontroller, or sensor) to safely control heavy electrical devices.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[17],\"alternative_name\":\"Industrial Relay\",\"mrp\":\"199\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1774444959697-918704280.jpeg\"}','2026-03-25 13:22:39'),
