(5594,1,'product',2132,'update',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"UltraSonic sensor Module\",\"description\":\"The Ultrasonic Sensor Module is an electronic distance measuring device used to detect objects and measure distance using ultrasonic sound waves. It works by transmitting high-frequency sound pulses (usually around 40 kHz) through a transmitter and then receiving the reflected echo from nearby objects using a receiver. The module calculates the distance based on the time taken for the sound wave to travel to the object and return, making it a reliable non-contact measurement sensor.\",\"info\":\"One of the most commonly used ultrasonic modules is the HC-SR04, which provides accurate distance measurement and easy interfacing with microcontrollers such as Arduino, ESP8266, ESP32, Raspberry Pi, and STM32 boards. The sensor typically includes four pins: VCC, GND, Trigger, and Echo. A short trigger pulse initiates measurement, and the echo pin outputs a signal whose duration corresponds to the detected distance. The module operates on 5V DC power and offers stable performance in various lighting conditions since it relies on sound instead of light.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"model\":\"\",\"series\":\"\",\"alternative_name\":\"\",\"mrp\":\"499.00\",\"note\":\"Ultrasonic sensor modules are widely used in obstacle avoidance robots, distance measurement systems, water level monitoring, parking assistance systems, automation projects, and smart IoT applications. Due to their accuracy, low cost, and simple operation, they are highly popular in educational and industrial electronics projects.\",\"mappings\":[{\"primary_id\":165,\"secondary_id\":\"638\",\"brand_id\":232}],\"alternative_names\":[]}','2026-03-27 10:42:39'),
