(5670,1,'product',3402,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"14D141 MOV Thermister\",\"description\":\"The 14D141 MOV (Metal Oxide Varistor) is a voltage-dependent resistor used primarily for protecting electronic circuits from voltage spikes and surges. Although sometimes mistakenly called a thermistor, it is actually a varistor, meaning its resistance changes with applied voltage rather than temperature. The “14D141” designation indicates a 14 mm disc diameter and a varistor voltage of approximately 140V.\",\"info\":\"Under normal voltage conditions, the MOV has very high resistance and allows minimal current flow. However, when a voltage surge occurs (such as lightning or switching spikes), its resistance drops rapidly, diverting excess current away from sensitive components and preventing damage.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1603],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1775019963631-803783399.jpg\"}','2026-04-01 05:06:03'),
(5671,1,'product',3403,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"14D681 MOV Thermistor\",\"description\":\"The 14D681 MOV is a Metal Oxide Varistor used for protecting electronic circuits against high-voltage surges and transient spikes. Although sometimes incorrectly referred to as a thermistor, it is actually a voltage-dependent resistor.The code “14D681” indicates a 14 mm disc size and a varistor voltage of approximately 680V. Under normal operating conditions, the MOV exhibits very high resistance and allows negligible current flow.\",\"info\":\"The code “14D681” indicates a 14 mm disc size and a varistor voltage of approximately 680V. Under normal operating conditions, the MOV exhibits very high resistance and allows negligible current flow. When a voltage surge occurs, its resistance drops rapidly, allowing it to absorb and divert excess voltage, thereby safeguarding sensitive components.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1603],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1775020451972-145113317.jpg\"}','2026-04-01 05:14:11'),
