(5676,1,'product',3406,'create',NULL,'{\"product_name\":\"14D271 MOV Thermistor\",\"description\":\"The 14D271 MOV is a Metal Oxide Varistor used for protecting electronic circuits from voltage surges and transient spikes. It is often mistakenly called a thermistor, but it actually works based on voltage changes rather than temperature. The code “14D271” indicates a 14 mm disc diameter and a varistor voltage of approximately 270V. Under normal voltage conditions, the MOV has very high resistance and allows very little current to pass.\",\"info\":\"The code “14D271” indicates a 14 mm disc diameter and a varistor voltage of approximately 270V. Under normal voltage conditions, the MOV has very high resistance and allows very little current to pass. When a voltage spike occurs, its resistance drops instantly, enabling it to absorb and clamp the excess voltage, thereby protecting sensitive components from damage.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"mappings\":[1603],\"mrp\":\"99\",\"alternative_names\":[],\"base_image\":\"products/1775021502660-921916991.jpg\"}','2026-04-01 05:31:42'),
