(278,'FPV','An FPV Camera (First-Person View Camera) is a small, lightweight camera used mainly in drones, RC cars, and robotics to transmit live video in real time to a screen, goggles, or receiver.','FPV cameras are designed for low latency, wide viewing angles, and good performance in varying light conditions, making them ideal for racing drones, aerial photography setups, surveillance projects, and DIY electronics applications.','FPV systems transmit live video signals to goggles, monitors, or mobile devices, giving the operator an immersive viewing experience as if they are inside the vehicle or aircraft. FPV technology is widely used in drone racing, aerial videography, surveillance, inspection work, and recreational flying due to its precise control and enhanced navigation capabilities.','Modern FPV setups include cameras, video transmitters, receivers, antennas, and specialized goggles designed for low latency and high-quality video transmission, making FPV an important technology in advanced remote-control and unmanned aerial systems.','brands/1771498494737-191148320.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:07:04','2026-02-26 07:52:38'),
