(58,1,19,15,'secondary',165,'Relay Modules','Solid State Relay (SSR) Boards are advanced switching modules designed for fast, reliable, and noise-free control of electrical loads.','With features like optical isolation, low control voltage, and stable performance under high loads, SSR relay boards ensure safe and efficient switching in demanding environments.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772014492909-97588657.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-26 13:46:44'),
(59,1,19,15,'secondary',165,'Charging Module and Buck boost converter','A charging module is an electronic board used to safely charge rechargeable batteries such as Li-ion and Li-Po cells, A buck-boost converter is a DC-DC power converter that can step up (boost) or step down (buck) voltage to maintain a stable output.','It features overcharge, over-discharge, and short-circuit protection, ensuring stable and efficient battery charging for DIY electronics and power supply projects.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1771670236787-662521479.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-26 13:43:45'),
(61,1,19,17,'secondary',281,'Laptop  Adaptor','A laptop adapter, also known as a laptop charger or power adapter, is an essential accessory used to supply the correct voltage and current to a laptop','It converts the AC power from a wall outlet into DC power that the laptop can use safely.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1771681498773-242890276.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 13:44:58'),
(62,1,19,20,'secondary',408,'Li-ion Batteries','Li-ion (Lithium-ion) batteries are high-performance rechargeable power sources widely used in electronics, robotics, power banks, LED projects, and industrial applications.','Available in cylindrical cells (like 18650), flat Li-Po packs, and custom battery modules, they deliver stable and reliable power for both low-current and high-load devices.','Lithium-ion (Li-ion) batteries are rechargeable energy storage devices widely used in modern electronics and electric systems. They store and release electrical energy through the movement of lithium ions between the positive electrode (cathode) and negative electrode (anode). Li-ion batteries are known for their high energy density, lightweight design, long cycle life, and low self-discharge rate.','A single Li-ion cell typically has a nominal voltage of 3.6V to 3.7V, which is much higher than traditional AA or AAA batteries. These batteries are commonly used in smartphones, laptops, power banks, electric vehicles (EVs), solar storage systems, drones, and portable electronics.','categories/1771681964547-517827228.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-26 09:43:36'),
(63,1,19,15,'secondary',165,'Voice and Touch Sensor module','A Voice Sensor Module detects sound levels in the environment and converts them into electrical signals. It is commonly used in projects that require sound-based triggering such as claps, voice commands, or noise detection.','This module typically includes a microphone, an adjustable sensitivity potentiometer, and a comparator IC that produces digital output when sound crosses a set threshold.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772018566169-88607559.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-25 11:22:46'),
(64,1,19,20,'secondary',408,'CMOS Cell Coin Cell','A CMOS cell, commonly known as a coin cell battery, is a small, round lithium battery used to power the BIOS/CMOS memory in computers, clocks, and small electronic devices','It provides long-lasting, stable voltage and ensures system settings and time are retained even when the main power is off.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1771670452248-868635308.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 10:40:52'),
