(67,1,19,15,'secondary',165,'Vibration Sensor Module','A Vibration Sensor Module is an electronic device designed to detect vibration, movement, or sudden shocks. It is widely used in DIY electronics, security systems, robotics, alarms, and automation projects.','This module typically uses a spring-type vibration switch or piezoelectric sensor that triggers an output when movement or vibration is detected. The onboard circuitry includes a digital output, sensitivity adjustment (in some models), and a stable compar',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772018442536-797474608.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-25 11:20:42'),
(68,1,19,15,'secondary',78,'Photodiode','A photodiode is a semiconductor device that converts light into an electrical current.','When light photons strike the photodiode, they create electron-hole pairs, resulting in a small current flow',NULL,NULL,'categories/1771684781922-418420608.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 14:39:41'),
(70,1,19,14,'secondary',332,'Bluetooth Speakers','Bluetooth speakers are wireless audio devices that use Bluetooth technology to stream music, calls, or sound from smartphones, laptops, tablets, and other compatible gadgets','Their portability makes them ideal for home use, travel, outdoor activities, parties, and hands-free calling.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1771666338344-364001203.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 09:52:49'),
(71,1,19,15,'secondary',165,'Color Sensor Module','A colour sensor module is an electronic device used to detect and measure the colour of an object by analyzing its red, green, and blue (RGB) light components','These modules use photodiodes or filters to convert light into signals, enabling accurate colour recognition in robotics, automation, sorting machines, and DIY electronics projects.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1771670664115-758852769.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 10:44:24'),
(73,1,19,20,'secondary',275,'Product IC','Product IC refers to a wide range of integrated circuits used in electronic devices for various functions such as processing, power management, signal conversion, and control operations','From microcontrollers and amplifiers to logic gates and memory chips, Product ICs play a vital role in ensuring that devices operate efficiently and meet industry standards.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772013774921-822318189.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-25 10:02:54'),
(76,1,19,15,'secondary',165,'Temperature Humidity','A Temperature & Humidity Sensor is an electronic device designed to accurately measure the surrounding air temperature and moisture levels.','Many modules come with easy-to-use digital interfaces, making them ideal for both beginners and advanced IoT projects.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772017364832-848199632.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-25 11:02:44'),
(77,1,19,15,'secondary',165,'Water Soil Sensor Module','A Water Soil Sensor Module is an easy-to-use electronic sensor designed to measure the moisture level in soil','It helps determine whether the soil is dry, moist, or fully wet, making it ideal for automatic plant watering systems, smart irrigation, and gardening projects.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772018750768-560097262.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-25 11:25:50'),
(78,1,19,15,'primary',NULL,'Sensor Only (Without Module)','A sensor without a module refers to the raw sensing element that directly detects physical changes such as temperature, light, motion, pressure, or sound.','They are typically used by engineers and hobbyists who need precise control over how the sensor is integrated into their system.','c','d','categories/1772116375127-537294745.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-26 14:32:55'),
(79,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Converter','A Converter is an essential electronic device used to change electrical parameters such as voltage, current, or signal type to match the requirements of different equipment.','It ensures smooth and safe operation by converting power from one form to another—for example, AC to DC, DC to DC, or voltage step-up/step-down.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1771671772908-530201544.jpeg',0,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-05 13:39:40'),
