(84,1,19,20,'secondary',275,'Product Ic base','Using an IC base improves durability, simplifies troubleshooting, and enhances the overall lifespan of electronic components.','An IC Base, also known as an IC Socket, is a holder used to mount integrated circuits securely onto a PCB without soldering the IC directly.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772013823937-165663361.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-25 10:03:43'),
(86,1,19,15,'primary',NULL,'Microcontroller Boards','A PCB (Printed Circuit Board) is a flat board used to mechanically support and electrically connect electronic components.','Electronic boards come in various forms—single-layer, double-layer, and multi-layer PCBs—depending on complexity and application.','Microcontroller boards are compact development platforms that contain a programmable microcontroller chip along with supporting components such as voltage regulators, clock circuits, USB interface, and input/output pins. These boards are widely used in electronics projects, embedded systems, robotics, automation, IoT applications, and educational learning.','Microcontroller boards allow users to write, upload, and execute programs to control sensors, motors, displays, relays, and communication modules. They support digital and analog input/output operations and various communication protocols such as UART, I2C, and SPI. Popular boards are designed for easy programming through USB connection and are compatible with dedicated development software (IDE).','categories/1771596549191-930683120.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-20 14:09:09'),
(87,1,19,15,'secondary',165,'RTC Module','RTC (Real-Time Clock) Module is an electronic device used to keep accurate track of current time and date, even when the main system power is turned off. It contains a dedicated RTC IC (such as DS3231 or DS1307), a crystal oscillator for precise timing, and a small backup coin cell battery to maintain time during power failures. The module communicates with microcontrollers like Arduino, Raspberry Pi, and other embedded systems using the I2C protocol, allowing easy integration into digital clocks, data loggers, alarm systems, attendance systems, and automation projects.','RTC modules are widely used in applications where accurate timekeeping is essential. For example, in data logging systems, they record timestamps for temperature or sensor readings. In IoT and automation systems, they help schedule tasks at specific times. Advanced RTC modules like the DS3231 provide high accuracy with built-in temperature compensation, making them suitable for industrial and long-term timing applications. Due to their low power consumption, reliability, and easy interfacing, RTC modules are essential components in embedded and robotics projects.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772015541871-960684828.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-26 13:48:30'),
(88,1,19,15,'secondary',548,'FT232RL USB to TTL Converter','A USB to TTL Converter is a small interface module used to connect a computer’s USB port to devices that communicate using TTL serial (UART) signals','It is ideal for programming, debugging, and communicating with microcontrollers, development boards (Arduino, ESP8266/ESP32, STM32, AVR, PIC), routers, GSM modules, GPS modules, and other embedded systems.','FT232RL USB to TTL Converter','FT232RL USB to TTL Converter','categories/1772018119314-244545256.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-26 14:21:18'),
