(96,1,19,16,'secondary',212,'Headphones','Headphones are personal audio devices designed to deliver high-quality sound directly to your ears','They come in various styles—including wired, wireless, over-ear, on-ear, and in-ear—making them suitable for music, gaming, calls, entertainment, and professional audio work. Modern headphones offer enhanced bass, noise cancellation, comfortable design, a',NULL,NULL,'categories/1771679658269-238971134.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 13:14:18'),
(97,1,19,16,'secondary',212,'Ear Buds','Ear Buds are compact audio devices designed to fit inside the ear canal and deliver personal sound output from electronic devices such as smartphones, laptops, tablets, and music players. They convert electrical audio signals into sound waves using small internal speaker drivers. Ear buds are available in wired and wireless (Bluetooth) versions.','Modern earbuds are designed for comfort, portability, and clear sound quality. Many models use silicone ear tips to provide a secure fit and passive noise isolation, while premium versions may include active noise cancellation (ANC) technology to reduce background noise.','They are widely used for music listening, phone calls, online classes, gaming, and workouts. Important specifications to consider when selecting earbuds include sound quality, driver size, battery life (for wireless models), connectivity range, impedance, sensitivity, and durability.','Most earbuds include features such as built-in microphones for calls, volume control buttons, noise isolation, and touch controls in advanced models.','categories/1771678626746-656774774.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 12:57:06'),
