(105,1,19,14,'primary',NULL,'FM Radio','An FM Radio is a compact and user-friendly audio device designed to receive Frequency Modulation (FM) broadcast signals, delivering clear and high-quality sound.','FM Radios come in various designs—portable, pocket-sized, desktop, or integrated into other systems—making them ideal for home, office, and outdoor use.','FM Radio (Frequency Modulation Radio) is an electronic device used to receive and play audio broadcasts transmitted over FM frequency bands. It operates typically in the frequency range of 88 MHz to 108 MHz, delivering clear sound quality with reduced noise compared to AM radio. FM radios are widely used for entertainment, news, music, and emergency broadcast information.','FM radio systems consist of a tuner circuit, antenna, amplifier section, and speaker output. A proper antenna connection improves signal strength and reception clarity. FM radios are commonly used in homes, vehicles, workshops, rural areas, and educational electronics projects.','categories/1771594733619-158393237.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-20 13:38:53'),
(106,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Glue Gun and Stick','A Glue Gun is a versatile handheld tool used for bonding materials quickly and efficiently.','lue guns are available in high-temperature, low-temperature, and dual-temperature models to suit different crafting, repair, and industrial applications.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1771679014509-840620223.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 13:03:34'),
