(256,1,20,23,'primary',NULL,'Electricals Wires','Wires are electrical conductors used to carry electric current from one point to another in residential, commercial, and industrial electrical systems.','Electrical wires are typically made of copper or aluminum and are insulated with materials like PVC to prevent electric shocks and short circuits.','Electrical wires are conductive cables used to transmit electrical power from one point to another within residential, commercial, and industrial installations. They are commonly made of high-quality copper or aluminum conductors and are insulated with PVC or other protective materials to ensure safety and durability.','Electrical wires are available in different sizes (measured in sq.mm or gauge), depending on the current-carrying capacity required for the application. Proper wire selection is important to prevent overheating, voltage drop, and power loss.','categories/1771594631961-915515711.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-20 13:37:11'),
(257,1,20,23,'primary',NULL,'Electrical Switches','Switches are electrical devices used to control the flow of electricity by turning electrical circuits ON or OFF.','They play a vital role in operating lights, fans, and electrical appliances safely and conveniently in residential, commercial, and industrial installations.','Electrical switches are devices used to control the flow of electricity in a circuit by turning power ON or OFF. They are essential components in residential, commercial, and industrial electrical systems. Switches allow safe and convenient operation of electrical appliances such as lights, fans, sockets, and other equipment.','Electrical switches are available in various types including one-way switches, two-way switches, modular switches, rocker switches, and industrial toggle switches. They are designed for different voltage and current ratings depending on the application.','categories/1771594464861-315936112.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-09 13:53:09'),
