(391,1,19,14,'secondary',9,'Audio Cables and Connectors','Audio Cables and Connectors are hardware components used to transmit audio signals between audio devices such as speakers, headphones, microphones, amplifiers, mixers, TVs, computers, and home theater systems. They ensure clear and reliable sound transfer','Audio Cables and Connectors are used to connect audio devices and transmit sound signals between source and output equipment in home, professional, and commercial audio systems.','Audio Cables and Connectors are used to connect audio devices and transmit sound signals. They support analog and digital audio transmission. Commonly used in home audio systems, computers, studios, and vehicles.','Supports analog signals (voltage-based) and digital signals (binary data). Cable quality (shielding, conductor material) affects signal clarity and noise reduction. Connector type determines compatibility and audio format support. Balanced connectors (e.g','categories/1771664637256-417352000.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-27 09:30:00'),
(392,1,19,14,'secondary',9,'Audio PIN and Jack','Audio PIN and Jack are physical connectors used to connect audio cables to audio devices for transmitting sound signals. They serve as the interface point where audio input or output occurs between devices such as mobiles, computers, speakers, microphones','Audio PIN and Jack are connectors used to interface audio cables with devices, enabling the transfer of sound signals between sources (phones, computers, instruments) and outputs (speakers, headphones, amplifiers).','Audio PIN and Jack are connectors used to connect audio cables to devices. The PIN (plug) is the male connector on the cable. The JACK (socket) is the female port on the device.','Used for audio input and output connections. Supports mono and stereo audio signals. Commonly found in mobiles, laptops, speakers, headphones, amplifiers, and mixers. Proper matching of pin and jack ensures clear sound and stable connection. Available in ','categories/1771664828997-169090565.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 09:07:09'),
(393,1,19,18,'secondary',223,'LED TV','An LED TV (Light Emitting Diode Television) is a modern flat-panel television that uses LED backlighting to illuminate an LCD screen. Compared to older LCD TVs that used CCFL (fluorescent) backlights, LED TVs are thinner, brighter, more energy-efficient, ','An LED TV offers a balanced combination of performance, design, and efficiency, making it the most popular choice for modern television viewing in homes and businesses.','LED TV uses LED backlighting, not self-emitting pixels. Thinner and lighter than older LCD and plasma TVs. Available in HD, Full HD, 4K, and 8K resolutions. Edge-lit models are slimmer; full-array models give better contrast. Smart LED TVs support apps, W','LED Backlight Technology: Uses LEDs for improved brightness and contrast. Slim & Lightweight Design: Easy to wall-mount or place on stands. High Resolution Support: Available in HD, Full HD, 4K Ultra HD, and 8K. Enhanced Picture Quality: Better color accu','categories/1771682461062-907632804.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 14:01:01'),
(394,1,19,18,'secondary',223,'Smart TV','A Smart TV is an advanced television that combines traditional TV display technology with internet connectivity and built-in software platforms, allowing users to stream content, browse the web, install apps, and access online services directly without ex','A Smart TV transforms a standard television into an all-in-one entertainment hub, offering convenience, connectivity, and access to digital content, making it ideal for modern homes and commercial environments.','Smart TV requires internet connection for full functionality. Built-in OS allows apps, streaming, and updates without external devices. Supports OTT platforms, YouTube, and music apps. Voice control available on supported models. Screen mirroring and cast','A Smart TV functions as a complete digital entertainment and connectivity hub, reducing the need for additional set-top boxes or streaming devices.','categories/1772016288736-269491527.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-25 10:44:48'),
(395,1,19,18,'primary',NULL,'Android TV','Android TV is a smart television platform developed by Google that brings the Android operating system to TVs. It allows users to stream content, install apps, play games, and use voice commands directly on the television through an intuitive, content-foc','Android TV turns a television into a powerful smart entertainment system, combining the flexibility of Android apps with a smooth, user-friendly TV experience suitable for homes, offices, and commercial environments.','Android TV is optimized for large-screen television use. Requires internet connectivity for apps, updates, and streaming services. Supports a wide range of apps and games via Google Play Store. Built-in Chromecast enables easy screen casting from mobile a','Android TV offers a flexible, customizable, and future-ready smart TV experience, combining Google services with a user-friendly interface.','categories/1771663739151-761118703.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 08:48:59'),
(396,1,19,18,'secondary',223,'Curved TV','A Curved TV is a television with a slightly curved screen design that wraps around the viewer’s field of vision. The curve is designed to create a more immersive and panoramic viewing experience, making the screen feel wider and deeper compared to flat TV','A Curved TV offers a visually immersive and premium viewing experience, best suited for single-viewer or centered seating arrangements rather than wide-angle group viewing.','Designed to deliver a more immersive viewing experience than flat TVs. Best suited for centered seating positions; side-angle viewing is less effective. More noticeable benefits on large screen sizes. Reduces edge distortion and can improve depth percepti','Curved TVs are best for users who prioritize immersive, single-viewer or centered viewing experiences over flexibility in seating and placement.','categories/1771672140928-345974959.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 11:09:00'),
(397,1,19,18,'secondary',223,'Google TV','Google TV is a smart TV platform developed by Google that organizes movies, TV shows, live TV, and apps from multiple streaming services into one unified, easy-to-use interface. It focuses on content discovery, personalization, and seamless integration wi','Google TV is a smart TV operating system by Google that brings together content from multiple streaming apps into one unified, content-first interface. It focuses on easy discovery, personalization, and voice control.','Google TV is a smart TV platform developed by Google. It is built on Android TV, with a more content-focused interface. Shows movies and TV shows from multiple streaming apps in one place. Provides personalized recommendations based on user preferences. S','Ideal for users who prefer OTT streaming, voice control, and personalized content discovery on smart televisions.','categories/1771679058520-653304736.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 13:04:18'),
(399,1,19,16,'secondary',3,'Smartphones','A smartphone is a portable, handheld electronic device that combines the functions of a mobile phone with advanced computing capabilities. It features a touchscreen interface, powerful processors, internet connectivity, and supports a wide range of applic','Smartphones are powerful personal computing devices that integrate communication, multimedia, and smart services into a compact, always-connected form factor.','Smartphones combine communication, computing, and multimedia in one device. Touchscreen is the primary input method; physical buttons are minimal. Requires regular charging; battery life depends on usage and capacity. Performance varies based on processor','Built-in cameras have largely replaced compact digital cameras. Data security depends on biometric locks and user practices. Accessories like cases, screen protectors, and chargers enhance usability.','categories/1772016466171-609446368.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-25 10:47:46'),
(400,1,19,16,'secondary',3,'Android Mobiles','Android mobiles are smartphones that run on the Android operating system, developed by Google. They are known for their flexibility, wide device variety, and strong app ecosystem, making them one of the most popular smartphone choices worldwide.','Android mobiles are flexible, feature-rich smartphones offering a wide range of hardware options, deep customization, and access to a vast app ecosystem for everyday and professional use.','Android mobiles run on Google’s Android operating system. Offer high customization through themes, widgets, and launchers. Available in wide price ranges from entry-level to premium. App support depends on Google Play Services availability. Performance va','Android mobiles provide a flexible and customizable smartphone experience, making them one of the most widely used mobile platforms worldwide.','categories/1771663691653-432102568.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 08:48:11'),
(401,1,19,16,'secondary',3,'Apple iPhone','The Apple iPhone is a premium smartphone developed by Apple, known for its high-quality design, powerful performance, and seamless software–hardware integration. It runs on Apple’s proprietary iOS operating system, offering a smooth, secure, and user-frie','The Apple iPhone is a high-performance, secure, and premium smartphone, designed for users who value reliability, long-term software support, and a tightly integrated digital ecosystem.','Designed and developed by Apple. Runs on iOS, known for smooth performance and long-term software updates. Strong focus on security and privacy (Face ID, encryption, app permissions). Premium build quality with durable materials. Performance optimized thr','The iPhone is ideal for users who prefer a secure, reliable, and tightly integrated smartphone experience with consistent performance and long-term support.','categories/1771663951421-990029111.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 08:52:31'),
(404,1,18,13,'secondary',480,'Modem','A modem (Modulator–Demodulator) is a networking device that enables computers, routers, and other digital devices to connect to the internet by converting data between digital signals and the signals used by internet service providers (ISPs).','A modem is the critical gateway device that connects local networks to the internet by translating ISP signals into usable digital data.','Modem is mandatory for accessing internet services from an ISP. Must be compatible with the ISP’s technology (DSL, Cable, Fiber, or Wireless). A modem alone provides internet access but does not create Wi-Fi unless it includes a router. Modem–router combo','Modems serve as the core connection point between users and their internet service provider, making them essential for reliable broadband connectivity.','categories/1771682848784-158554870.jpeg',0,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-09 12:28:34'),
(405,35,18,25,'secondary',480,'Network Hubs','A network hub is a basic networking device used to connect multiple computers or network devices within a local area network (LAN). It operates at the physical layer (Layer 1) of the OSI model and simply broadcasts incoming data to all connected ports, wi','Network hubs are simple and low-cost networking devices, suitable for basic connectivity needs. However, due to inefficiency and lack of traffic control, they are largely replaced today by switches and routers in modern networks.','Operate at OSI Layer 1 (Physical Layer). Broadcast data to all connected devices. Do not filter, route, or manage traffic. All devices share the same bandwidth. High chance of network collisions. No MAC address learning or security features. Simple plug-a','Network hubs are mainly of historical and educational importance, as modern networks require efficient traffic handling and security provided by switches and routers.','categories/1771683589917-318244065.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-09 12:27:00'),
(406,1,18,13,'secondary',115,'LAN or Ethernet Cable','A LAN cable, commonly known as an Ethernet cable, is a wired networking cable used to connect devices such as computers, routers, switches, modems, and network printers within a Local Area Network (LAN). It enables high-speed, stable, and secure data tran','LAN / Ethernet cables provide reliable, high-speed wired connectivity, forming the backbone of modern networking infrastructure in homes, offices, and enterprises.','Provides stable and reliable wired network connectivity. Preferred over Wi-Fi for low latency and high-speed connections. Maximum standard cable length is 100 meters. Performance depends on category (Cat5e, Cat6, Cat6a, etc.). Proper crimping and pin orde','LAN / Ethernet cables are the foundation of wired networking, ensuring consistent speed, security, and reliability across network environments.','categories/1771681447070-248102909.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 13:44:07'),
(407,1,21,24,'secondary',298,'Firewall and Security Appliances','Firewall and Security Appliances are dedicated hardware devices designed to protect networks, systems, and data from unauthorized access, cyber threats, and malicious traffic. They act as a security barrier between trusted internal networks and untrusted ','Firewall and Security Appliances are critical infrastructure components that provide centralized, high-performance network protection, ensuring secure communication, threat prevention, and compliance in modern IT environments.','Act as the first line of defense against cyber threats. Installed at the network perimeter for maximum protection. Protect multiple devices with centralized security policies. Require regular firmware and threat signature updates. Performance must match n','Firewall and Security Appliances are mission-critical security components, ensuring safe, controlled, and reliable network operations in today’s threat-prone digital landscape.','categories/1771676188339-525106790.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 12:16:28'),
(408,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Batteries','A battery is a device that stores chemical energy and converts it to electrical energy to power electrical/electronic devices.','It consists of one or more electrochemical cells with terminals that supply this power when connected to a circuit.','Batteries','Batteries','categories/1771665169578-984178664.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 09:12:49'),
(409,1,19,15,'secondary',196,'Bo Motor one Shift','A BO Motor (Battery Operated Motor) – One Shaft is a small DC geared motor widely used in robotics, DIY electronics, and educational projects.','It features a single output shaft designed to easily mount wheels, pulleys, or gears, making it ideal for simple motion and drive applications.','Bo Motor L1 Shift','Bo Motor L1 Shift','categories/1771667896403-291024452.jpeg',0,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-05 06:27:09'),
(410,1,19,15,'secondary',196,'Bo Motor L Two Shaft','A BO Motor L Two Shaft is a DC geared motor with an L-shaped (right-angle) gearbox and two output shafts.','This design allows power to be taken from both sides of the gearbox, making it highly useful in robotics and DIY mechanical projects where synchronized movement or encoder mounting is required.','Bo Motor L Two Shaft','Bo Motor L Two Shaft','categories/1771667838430-374022682.jpeg',0,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-05 06:27:13'),
(411,1,19,15,'secondary',196,'Bo Motor Type','BO Motors L-type are DC geared motors with an L-shaped (right-angle) gearbox, where the motor shaft and output shaft are at 90 degrees to each other.','This compact design provides better torque and easier mounting in tight spaces, making them very popular in robotics, DIY electronics, and educational projects.','Bo Motors Ltype 150RPM','Bo Motors Ltype 150RPM','categories/1771667978645-932599520.jpeg',0,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-05 06:27:02'),
(412,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Basic Electronics Components','Basic electronic components are the fundamental building blocks used to design and assemble electronic circuits.','They control the flow of electricity, store energy, amplify signals, and perform switching operations. These components are essential for DIY electronics, robotics, embedded systems, and repair work.','Basic Components','Basic Components','categories/1771665087178-342379580.jpeg',0,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 10:05:43'),
(413,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Resistors','A resistor is a basic electronic component used to limit, control, or regulate the flow of electric current in a circuit.','It works by providing a specific amount of resistance, measured in ohms (Ω), which helps protect components and ensure proper voltage and current levels.','Resistors','Resistors','categories/1771598653283-180338128.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-20 14:44:13'),
(414,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Transistor','A transistor is a fundamental active electronic component used to amplify signals or act as an electronic switch.','It is one of the most important building blocks in modern electronics, found in everything from simple DIY circuits to computers, TVs, and industrial equipment.','Transistor','Transistor','categories/1771599153617-730983791.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-20 14:52:33'),
(415,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Capacitors','A capacitor is a basic electronic component used to store and release electrical energy in the form of an electric charge','Capacitors are widely used in electronic circuits for filtering, smoothing, coupling, timing, and energy storage.','Capacitors','Capacitors','categories/1771669241826-106157747.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 10:20:41'),
(416,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Ceramic Capacitor','A ceramic capacitor is a non-polarized electronic component used to store small amounts of electrical charge','It is made using ceramic material as the dielectric and is widely used in electronic circuits for noise filtering, decoupling, coupling, and signal stabilization.','A Ceramic Capacitor is a non-polarized electronic component used to store and release electrical energy in a circuit. It is made using ceramic material as the dielectric (insulating material) between two conductive plates.','Ceramic capacitors are widely used in electronic circuits for filtering, noise reduction, coupling, decoupling, and voltage smoothing. They are small in size, lightweight, low-cost, and highly reliable, making them one of the most commonly used capacitors in electronic devices.','categories/1771589119307-79600345.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-20 12:05:19'),
(417,1,19,15,'secondary',196,'Small Toy Motor Yellow','The small yellow toy motor, commonly known as a BO motor (Battery Operated motor), is a compact DC geared motor widely used in toy cars, DIY electronics, and beginner robotics projects','Its lightweight plastic (usually yellow) gearbox provides a good balance of speed and torque while operating safely on low voltages.','Small Toy Motor Yellow','Small Toy Motor Yellow','categories/1772016252394-956535121.jpeg',0,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-05 06:29:26'),
(418,1,19,15,'secondary',196,'Big Toy DC Motor Yellow','Big yellow toy DC motors are high-torque DC geared motors commonly used in larger toy vehicles, robotics, and DIY automation projects','Compared to small yellow BO motors, these have a bigger gearbox and motor, delivering more torque and better load handling while still operating on safe, low voltages.','Big Toy DC Motors Yellow','Big Toy DC Motors Yellow','categories/1771665384881-414426625.jpeg',0,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-05 06:27:55'),
(419,1,2,1,'secondary',203,'Jumper Wires','Jumper wires are short electrical connecting wires used to make quick and temporary connections between electronic components, modules, and breadboards.','They are essential for prototyping, testing, and learning electronics without soldering.','Jumper Wires','Jumper Wires','assets/uploads/category/Jumper_Wires/Jumper_Wires_image.jpg',0,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-09 11:21:31'),
(420,1,19,20,'secondary',614,'LED Lights','LED Lights (Light Emitting Diodes) are energy-efficient electronic light sources that emit light when electric current flows through them','LEDs are widely used in electronics, lighting, indicators, displays, and decorative applications due to their low power consumption, long life, and compact size.','LED Lights','LED Lights','categories/1771682395219-473016832.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-09 14:13:11'),
(421,1,19,15,'secondary',196,'Gear Motors','Gear Motors are electric motors combined with a gearbox to reduce speed and increase torque. The gearbox contains a set of gears that convert the high-speed, low-torque output of the motor into a lower-speed, high-torque output suitable for driving mechanical loads.','Gear motors are commonly available in DC, AC, and stepper motor types, and they come in different voltage ratings such as 6V, 12V, and 24V.','gear motors are widely used in robotics, automation systems, conveyor belts, vending machines, power windows, electric locks, and industrial machinery. For example, small DC gear motors are popular in robotic car chassis kits because they provide enough torque to move the vehicle while maintaining controlled speed.','When selecting a gear motor, important factors include voltage rating, RPM (speed), torque output, gear ratio, current consumption, and load requirements.','categories/1771677170708-418232712.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 12:32:50'),
(422,1,19,15,'secondary',196,'Servo Motors','Servo Motor is a small, high-precision motor used to control angular position, speed, and acceleration in electronic and robotics applications. Unlike normal DC motors that rotate continuously, servo motors are designed to rotate to a specific angle (usually between 0° and 180°) and hold that position accurately. They consist of a DC motor, internal gear system, position sensor (potentiometer), and a control circuit built into a compact housing. Servo motors are controlled using PWM (Pulse Width Modulation) signals from microcontrollers like Arduino, Raspberry Pi, and other development boards.','Servo motors are widely used in robotics, automation systems, robotic arms, RC cars, drones, camera gimbals, and industrial machines where precise movement is required. Common types include micro servo motors (like SG90) for lightweight projects and high-torque metal gear servos (like MG995) for heavy-duty applications.','They operate typically at 5V–7.4V and provide accurate positioning with low power consumption. Because of their precision, reliability, and ease of control, servo motors are essential components in modern robotics and embedded system projects.',NULL,'categories/1772016025866-221723700.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-25 10:40:25'),
(423,1,19,33,'secondary',628,'Soldering Iron','Soldering is the process of joining electronic components by melting a filler metal called solder to create a strong, conductive, and permanent electrical connection','It is one of the most essential skills in electronics assembly, repair, and DIY projects.','Soldering','Soldering','categories/1771598917888-248785934.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-12 09:29:17'),
(424,1,19,21,'secondary',628,'NOEL Soldering Iron','NOEL soldering irons are electric hand tools designed to heat solder so it melts and bonds electronic components together on a PCB (printed circuit board) or wiring joints','They are widely used in electronics assembly, repair, DIY projects, and basic electrical tasks','NOEL 8W Soldering Iron','NOEL 8W Soldering Iron','categories/1771683998603-57812983.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-12 09:25:47'),
(425,1,19,33,'secondary',628,'Soldering Flux Paste','Soldering flux paste is a chemical substance used in soldering to improve the flow and bonding of solder. It helps clean metal surfaces, remove oxides, and enable better wetting so that solder forms strong, reliable electrical and mechanical joints.','Flux is especially useful when soldering circuit boards, wires, connectors, and components in electronics work.','Soldering Flux Paste','Soldering Flux Paste','categories/1772016704748-167725869.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-12 09:33:37'),
(426,1,19,33,'secondary',628,'Soldering Wire and Lead','Soldering wire is a thin metal wire used to join two or more electronic components by melting and forming a strong electrical and mechanical connection. It is commonly used in electronics assembly, PCB (Printed Circuit Board) work, electrical repairs, and circuit building. When heated using a soldering iron, the wire melts and flows into the joint, creating a secure bond after cooling.','Soldering wire is usually made of a mixture of tin (Sn) and lead (Pb) or a lead-free alloy. It often contains a flux core inside the wire, which helps clean the metal surfaces and improves the bonding process. Soldering wires are available in different thicknesses depending on the application, such as fine work in electronics or heavy electrical connections.','Lead solder traditionally consists of a tin-lead alloy, commonly in ratios such as 60% tin and 40% lead (60/40) or 63/37. This type of solder melts at a lower temperature and flows smoothly, making it easy to use for beginners and professionals. It provides strong joints and good electrical conductivity.','However, due to health and environmental concerns, lead-free solder is now widely used. Lead-free solder is typically made from tin mixed with silver and copper (Sn-Ag-Cu alloy). It melts at a slightly higher temperature but is safer and complies with modern environmental standards.','categories/1772015011805-43844034.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-12 09:35:26'),
(427,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Multimeter','A multimeter is an essential electrical testing and measuring instrument used to measure voltage, current, resistance, and other electrical parameters in circuits and devices','It is widely used by electricians, electronics technicians, engineers, students, and DIY users for troubleshooting, installation, maintenance, and testing of electrical and electronic equipment.','A multimeter is an essential electrical measuring instrument used to test and measure various electrical parameters such as voltage (AC/DC), current (AC/DC), and resistance. It is widely used by electricians, technicians, engineers, students, and hobbyists for troubleshooting and maintaining electrical and electronic circuits.','Multimeters are available in two main types: digital multimeter (DMM) and analog multimeter. Digital multimeters provide accurate readings on an LCD display, while analog multimeters use a needle indicator. Modern digital multimeters often include additional features such as continuity testing, diode testing, transistor testing, capacitance measurement, frequency measurement, and temperature testing depending on the model.','categories/1771597423131-945670244.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-27 10:09:58'),
(429,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Diode','A diode is a two-terminal semiconductor electronic component that allows electric current to flow in only one direction and blocks current in the opposite direction. It is one of the most basic and essential components used in electronic circuits.','A diode is a basic electronic component that allows current to flow in one direction only and blocks it in the reverse direction. It is made using a PN junction semiconductor and is widely used in almost all electronic circuits.','Diodes are mainly used for rectification, circuit protection, voltage regulation, and signal control. They play a key role in converting AC to DC power.','Correct polarity connection is mandatory Use current-limiting resistor where required. Heat dissipation may be required for high-current diodes. Select diode based on voltage and current rating. Protect from over-voltage and over-current','categories/1771592669974-596705456.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-20 13:04:29'),
(430,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Zener Diode','A Zener diode is a special type of semiconductor diode designed to operate reliably in the reverse breakdown region. Unlike a normal diode, which is damaged by reverse breakdown, a Zener diode is specifically made to allow current to flow in reverse direc','A Zener diode is made using a heavily doped PN junction, which allows it to have a precise and low breakdown voltage, known as the Zener voltage (Vᶻ).','A Zener diode is a special-purpose semiconductor diode designed to operate in the reverse bias breakdown region. Unlike a normal diode, which blocks reverse current, a Zener diode allows current to flow in reverse once a specific voltage—called the Zener ','The main function of a Zener diode is voltage regulation. When connected in reverse bias, it maintains a constant output voltage even if the input voltage or load current changes, provided it operates within its rated limits.','categories/1771599480674-265809268.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-20 14:58:00'),
(431,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Switches','A switch is an electromechanical or electronic component used to open or close an electrical circuit, thereby controlling the flow of current. Switches allow users or systems to turn devices ON or OFF or to change the path of current in a circuit.','A switch is a basic electronic and electrical component used to control the flow of electric current in a circuit. It works by opening (OFF) or closing (ON) the circuit, allowing or stopping the flow of electricity.','Switches can be manually operated, mechanically triggered, or electronically controlled. They are essential for power control, user input, and circuit selection in almost all electronic devices.','Switches are available in different forms such as toggle, push button, rocker, slide, and rotary switches, each designed for specific applications. They are widely used in home appliances, industrial machines, electronic projects, and control systems.','categories/1772017305471-252027717.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-07 09:59:28'),
(432,1,19,15,'secondary',78,'Relays','A relay is an electrically operated switch used to control a high-voltage or high-current circuit using a low-voltage signal. It allows safe isolation between the control circuit and the load circuit, making it an essential component in control and automa','A relay is an electrically operated switching device used to control high-voltage or high-current circuits with a low-voltage control signal. It works on the principle of electromagnetism and provides electrical isolation between the control circuit and t','When voltage is applied to the relay coil, it generates a magnetic field that moves an internal armature. This movement opens or closes the contacts, allowing or interrupting the flow of current in the load circuit. When the coil is turned off, the contac','Relays are widely used in industrial automation, power systems, home appliances, protection circuits, and microcontroller-based projects. They enable safe and reliable switching of electrical loads such as motors, lamps, heaters, and high-power devices.','categories/1772014561816-402551485.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-26 13:47:32'),
(433,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Inductors','An inductor is a passive electronic component that stores energy in the form of a magnetic field when electric current flows through it. Inductors resist changes in current and are commonly used in power supplies, filters, and signal conditioning circuits','An inductor is a passive electronic component that stores electrical energy in the form of a magnetic field when current flows through it. It resists changes in current, making it an important component in power control and signal filtering circuits.','Inductors are typically made by winding a coil of insulated copper wire around a core made of air, iron, or ferrite. The ability of an inductor to store energy is called inductance, and it is measured in Henries (H).','Inductors are widely used in power supplies, SMPS circuits, filters, RF circuits, and energy storage applications. They allow DC current to pass easily while opposing AC or rapidly changing currents.','categories/1771680296749-48427760.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 13:24:56'),
(434,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Buzzer','A buzzer is an electronic audio signaling device used to produce sound, typically for alerts, warnings, or notifications in electronic circuits. It converts electrical energy into audible sound and is commonly used in alarms, indicators, and electronic pr','A buzzer is an electronic sound-producing component used to generate audible alerts or indications in electronic circuits. It converts electrical energy into sound and is commonly used for warnings, alarms, and status notifications.','Buzzers operate using either a piezoelectric element or an electromagnetic mechanism. When voltage is applied, the internal element vibrates, producing sound. Some buzzers generate sound automatically, while others require an external signal.','Buzzers are widely used in alarm systems, home appliances, security devices, electronic instruments, and microcontroller-based projects. They are preferred because of their small size, low power consumption, low cost, and reliability.','categories/1771668323123-450135645.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 10:05:23'),
(435,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Crystal Resistor','A crystal (crystal oscillator) is an electronic component used to generate a precise and stable clock frequency in electronic circuits. It is most commonly made from quartz crystal, which has the property of piezoelectricity.','A crystal (quartz crystal) is an electronic frequency-control component used to generate a stable and precise clock signal in electronic circuits. It operates based on the piezoelectric property of quartz, where the crystal vibrates at a fixed frequency w','Crystals are mainly used to provide accurate timing and synchronization in electronic systems. The oscillation frequency is determined by the physical dimensions and cut of the quartz crystal, making it highly stable and reliable.','Crystals are widely used in microcontrollers, microprocessors, real-time clocks, communication devices, computers, and digital electronics. Common frequencies include 32.768 kHz for clock circuits and 8 MHz to 16 MHz for microcontroller applications.','categories/1771671926212-69116368.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 11:05:26'),
(436,1,19,15,'primary',NULL,'Display','A display is an electronic output device used to visually present information such as text, numbers, symbols, or graphics generated by an electronic system. Displays allow users to see system status, data, and results clearly.','A display is an electronic output device used to visually present information such as numbers, text, symbols, or graphics from an electronic system. It enables users to easily monitor system status, data readings, and operational messages.','Displays work by converting electrical signals into visible light or patterns. Depending on the technology used, displays may emit light (LED, OLED) or control light passing through them (LCD).','Displays are widely used in mobile phones, televisions, computers, measuring instruments, industrial panels, and embedded electronics projects. Common types include LCD, LED, OLED, seven-segment, and TFT displays.','categories/1771593716031-756747873.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-20 13:21:56'),
(437,1,19,17,'secondary',436,'LED and LCD Display','An LED Display (Light Emitting Diode Display) is an electronic display device that uses LEDs as light sources to show information such as numbers, text, symbols, or graphics. Each LED emits light when current flows through it, making the display bright an','An LCD Display (Liquid Crystal Display) is an electronic display device that uses liquid crystal material to control light and display information. LCDs do not produce light by themselves; instead, they use a backlight to make characters or images visible','An LCD Display (Liquid Crystal Display) is an electronic display device that uses liquid crystal material to control light and display information. LCDs do not produce light by themselves; instead, they use a backlight to make characters or images visible','An LCD display (Liquid Crystal Display) is an electronic display that uses liquid crystals to control light and form visible characters or images. LCDs do not emit light on their own; instead, they use a backlight to illuminate the display. They are commo','categories/1772020276456-339564694.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-25 11:51:16'),
(438,1,19,15,'secondary',436,'OLED Display','An OLED Display (Organic Light Emitting Diode Display) is an advanced electronic display technology in which organic compounds emit light when an electric current passes through them. Unlike LCDs, OLED displays are self-emissive, meaning no backlight is r','Each pixel in an OLED display produces its own light, allowing for deep blacks, high contrast, wide viewing angles, and fast response times. OLED displays are thin, lightweight, and flexible compared to traditional display technologies.','OLED displays are widely used in smartphones, smartwatches, televisions, industrial displays, and embedded electronics projects due to their high image quality and low power consumption, especially when displaying dark content.','OLED displays are commonly used in smartphones, televisions, wearable devices, industrial panels, and embedded system projects. Their superior visual quality and compact design make them an important component in modern electronic systems.','categories/1771684102704-313780421.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 14:28:22'),
(439,1,19,15,'secondary',436,'Seven Segment Display','A Seven Segment Display is an electronic display device used to show numerical digits (0–9) and a limited set of characters. It is called “seven segment” because it consists of seven individual LED segments arranged in the shape of the number “8”.','A seven segment display is a simple electronic numeric display device used to show digits from 0 to 9 and a few basic characters. It consists of seven individual LED segments arranged in a rectangular pattern, along with an optional decimal point.','Each digit is formed by lighting specific combinations of these segments. Seven segment displays are available in common anode and common cathode configurations, depending on how the LEDs are electrically connected.','Seven segment displays are widely used in digital clocks, calculators, counters, timers, measuring instruments, and electronic panels. They are popular because of their simplicity, low cost, low power consumption, and easy interfacing with microcontroller','categories/1772016122348-608952851.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-25 10:42:02'),
(440,1,19,15,'primary',NULL,'Dot Matrix Display','A Dot Matrix Display is an electronic display device made up of a matrix of small dots (usually LEDs) arranged in rows and columns. Each dot acts as an individual light element, and by controlling these dots, the display can show letters, numbers, symbols','A dot matrix display is an electronic display device composed of a grid (matrix) of small dots, usually LEDs, arranged in rows and columns. By selectively turning these dots ON and OFF, the display can show alphabets, numbers, symbols, and simple graphics','Dot matrix displays are more flexible than seven-segment displays because they can represent multiple characters and scrolling messages. Common configurations include 5×7, 8×8, and larger matrices.','They are widely used in electronic notice boards, scrolling message displays, advertising panels, industrial information systems, and embedded electronics projects. Dot matrix displays are valued for their versatility, durability, and good visibility.','categories/1771674110810-73328093.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-04-10 05:26:40'),
(441,1,19,15,'secondary',316,'Arduino Nano Board','The Arduino Nano is a compact, complete, and breadboard-friendly microcontroller development board based on the ATmega328P microcontroller. It offers the same functionality as the Arduino Uno but in a much smaller form factor, making it ideal for embedded','The Arduino Nano is a compact, complete, and breadboard-friendly microcontroller development board based on the ATmega328P microcontroller. It offers the same functionality as the Arduino Uno but in a much smaller form factor, making it ideal for embedded','The board can be powered and programmed through a USB connection or an external power source via the VIN pin. It supports digital and analog input/output, along with standard communication interfaces such as UART, I²C, and SPI.','The Arduino Nano is widely used in embedded systems, IoT devices, robotics, automation projects, and educational electronics. Its small size, low cost, ease of programming, and strong community support make it a popular choice for both beginners and profe','categories/1771664125417-793426518.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 08:55:25'),
(442,1,19,15,'secondary',316,'Arduino AtMega','The ATmega is a family of 8-bit AVR microcontrollers developed by Atmel (now Microchip Technology) and widely used as the core controller in Arduino boards. Popular Arduino boards like Arduino Uno, Nano, and Mega are built around ATmega microcontrollers s','The ATmega is a family of 8-bit AVR microcontrollers developed by Atmel (now Microchip Technology) and widely used as the core controller in Arduino boards. Popular Arduino boards like Arduino Uno, Nano, and Mega are built around ATmega microcontrollers s','The ATmega is a family of 8-bit AVR microcontrollers developed by Atmel (now part of Microchip Technology) and is widely used as the main controller in Arduino boards. Popular Arduino boards such as the Arduino Uno and Arduino Nano are based on the ATmega','The ATmega is a family of 8-bit AVR microcontrollers developed by Atmel (now part of Microchip Technology) and is widely used as the main controller in Arduino boards. Popular Arduino boards such as the Arduino Uno and Arduino Nano are based on the ATmega','categories/1771664010307-218213420.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 08:53:30'),
(443,1,19,15,'secondary',86,'ESP Boards','ESP Boards are Wi-Fi and Bluetooth-enabled microcontroller development boards based on the ESP8266 and ESP32 chips developed by Espressif Systems. These boards are widely used in IoT (Internet of Things), automation, and wireless embedded projects.','ESP boards are microcontroller development boards with built-in Wi-Fi and (in some models) Bluetooth connectivity, developed by Espressif Systems. They are mainly based on the ESP8266 and ESP32 chips and are widely used in IoT and wireless embedded applic','ESP boards are microcontroller development boards with built-in Wi-Fi and (in some models) Bluetooth connectivity, developed by Espressif Systems. They are mainly based on the ESP8266 and ESP32 chips and are widely used in IoT and wireless embedded applic','ESP boards integrate a microcontroller, wireless communication, GPIO pins, ADC, timers, and communication interfaces on a single board. This allows devices to connect directly to the internet or local networks without the need for external communication m','categories/1771677238806-497879644.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 12:33:58'),
(444,1,19,15,'secondary',86,'Nodemcu Board','The NodeMCU is an open-source IoT development board based on the ESP8266 Wi-Fi microcontroller, designed to make internet-connected and wireless projects simple and cost-effective. It combines a powerful microcontroller with built-in Wi-Fi, USB interface,','The NodeMCU is an open-source IoT development board based on the ESP8266 Wi-Fi microcontroller, designed to make internet-connected and wireless projects simple and cost-effective. It combines a powerful microcontroller with built-in Wi-Fi, USB interface,','NodeMCU can be programmed using the Arduino IDE or other supported environments. It allows the board to connect directly to Wi-Fi networks, send and receive data from web servers, cloud platforms, and mobile applications, and control connected devices.','The NodeMCU board is widely used in IoT applications, smart home automation, remote monitoring systems, and educational projects. Its popularity comes from its low cost, ease of use, built-in Wi-Fi, and strong community support, making it ideal for both b','categories/1771683950979-453696052.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 14:25:50'),
(445,1,19,15,'primary',NULL,'Project Antenna','An antenna is an electronic component used to transmit and receive electromagnetic waves, enabling wireless communication between electronic devices. It converts electrical signals into radio waves during transmission and radio waves back into electrical ','An antenna is an electronic component used to transmit and receive wireless signals in the form of electromagnetic waves. It acts as an interface between electronic circuits and free space, enabling communication without physical connections.','Antennas work by converting electrical signals into radio waves during transmission and converting received radio waves back into electrical signals. The design, size, and shape of an antenna depend on the operating frequency and application.','Antennas are widely used in Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, mobile phones, radio and TV broadcasting, GPS systems, satellite communication, and IoT devices. Proper antenna selection and placement are essential for achieving good signal strength, range, and reliable com','categories/1772114542911-821962062.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-26 14:02:22'),
(446,1,19,15,'secondary',86,'LED and LCD Board','LED and LCD boards are display boards used in electronic systems to show visual output such as numbers, text, symbols, or system status. They act as an interface between the electronic circuit and the user, making it easier to understand system operation.','An LED board uses multiple light-emitting diodes arranged on a board to provide bright visual indication. LED boards are commonly used for status indicators, counters, timers, and signal displays because of their high brightness, fast response, and long l','An LCD board (Liquid Crystal Display board) uses liquid crystal technology with a built-in controller to display characters or simple graphics. LCD boards are widely used in embedded systems, measuring instruments, automation panels, and IoT projects due ','Both LED and LCD boards are popular in electronics projects because they are easy to interface with microcontrollers, reliable, and cost-effective.','categories/1771682342129-524206991.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 13:59:02'),
(447,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'TV Power Adapter','A TV Power Adapter is an electronic power device used to convert high-voltage AC power from a wall outlet into a regulated DC voltage required to operate televisions or related TV devices. It is commonly used with LED TVs, LCD TVs, smart TV boxes, set-top boxes, and portable televisions that require external power adapters. The adapter typically supports an input range of 100–240V AC and converts it into a specific DC output such as 12V, 19V, or 24V, depending on the television model and power requirement.','TV power adapters are usually built using Switch Mode Power Supply (SMPS) technology, which allows efficient power conversion, compact size, and reduced heat generation. They include essential internal components such as transformers, rectifiers, filters, and voltage regulation circuits that provide stable and reliable output power.','Most adapters also include protection features like overvoltage protection, short-circuit protection, and overcurrent protection to ensure safe operation. Using the correct voltage rating, connector type, and polarity is important to maintain proper functioning and prevent damage to the television or connected device.',NULL,'categories/1771644763853-442932545.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-04-10 05:27:50'),
(448,1,19,14,'primary',NULL,'Audio Boards','Audio boards are electronic circuit boards designed to process, amplify, record, or output sound signals. They are used to handle audio input from sources like microphones, Bluetooth, or line-in, and provide audio output to speakers or headphones.','Audio boards are electronic circuit boards designed to process, amplify, record, or output sound signals. They are used to handle audio input from sources like microphones, Bluetooth, or line-in, and provide audio output to speakers or headphones.','Audio boards are electronic modules designed to process, amplify, and output audio signals in electronic systems. They integrate audio-related components such as amplifier ICs, decoders, and control circuits on a single board, making them easy to use in p','Audio boards can accept sound input from sources like microphones, AUX ports, USB, SD cards, or Bluetooth, and provide audio output to speakers or headphones. Some boards also support volume control and audio effects.','categories/1771664477283-565995735.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 09:01:17'),
(449,1,20,23,'secondary',427,'Digital Multimeter','A Digital Multimeter (DMM) is an electronic measuring instrument used to measure electrical quantities such as voltage, current, and resistance. It displays measurement values in digital form on an LCD or LED screen, providing accurate and easy-to-read re','A digital multimeter (DMM) is an electronic measuring instrument used to measure electrical parameters such as voltage, current, and resistance. It displays the measured values in numerical (digital) form, making readings clear and accurate.','Digital multimeters work by converting the electrical quantity being measured into a digital signal using an internal analog-to-digital converter (ADC). The result is then shown on an LCD display. Many modern digital multimeters also provide additional fu','Digital multimeters work by converting the electrical quantity being measured into a digital signal using an internal analog-to-digital converter (ADC). The result is then shown on an LCD display. Many modern digital multimeters also provide additional fu','categories/1771673806807-772476357.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 11:36:46'),
(450,1,2,1,'secondary',230,'MotherBoard','A motherboard is the main circuit board of a computer or electronic system that connects and allows communication between all the essential components. It acts as the central backbone that holds and links the processor, memory, storage, and peripheral dev','A motherboard is the primary circuit board of a computer system that connects and coordinates all major hardware components. It provides the electrical connections and communication pathways that allow components such as the CPU, memory, storage devices, ','The motherboard contains key elements including the CPU socket, RAM slots, chipset, power connectors, expansion slots, and input/output ports. It distributes power to components, manages data transfer, and supports system expansion through add-on cards an','Motherboards are used in desktop computers, laptops, servers, industrial computers, and embedded systems. They are essential for system functionality and are designed to be compatible with specific processors, memory types, and form factors.','assets/uploads/category/MotherBoard/1768977013_image.jpeg',0,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-09 11:21:31'),
(451,1,19,15,'secondary',320,'four Wheel Chassis Kit','A Four Wheels Chassis Kit is a foundational mechanical platform used in robotics and mobile electronics projects, providing a sturdy base for building a small vehicle or robot. Typically constructed from durable materials like acrylic, aluminum, or plastic, the kit includes a frame with four wheel mounts, four wheels with rubber tires for traction, and often two or more DC motors or geared motors to drive the wheels.','Some kits also come with motor mounts, brackets, spacers, and screws for easy assembly. The design of a four-wheel chassis offers stability and balance compared to two- or three-wheel platforms, making it suitable for carrying additional components such as microcontrollers (Arduino, Raspberry Pi, ESP32), sensors (ultrasonic, infrared, LIDAR), battery packs, and motor drivers.','Four-wheel chassis kits vary in size and configuration but generally support differential or all-wheel drive systems, allowing smooth movement, turning, and navigation in flat indoor or outdoor environments.','Using a four-wheel chassis simplifies the mechanical aspect of a build, letting hobbyists and engineers focus on electronics, programming, and control algorithms. Overall, this kit provides a versatile, easy-to-assemble base that helps creators bring mobile robotic designs to life with strength, expandability, and reliable performance.','categories/1771676669140-809261911.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 12:24:29'),
(452,1,2,1,'secondary',320,'All Types of Wheels','All Types of Wheels','All Types of Wheels','All Types of Wheels','All Types of Wheels','assets/uploads/category/All_Types_of_Wheels/1768989914_image.jpeg',0,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-09 11:21:31'),
(453,1,19,15,'primary',NULL,'Motor Drives','Motor drivers are interface boards that let your microcontroller (Arduino/ESP32/STM32/Raspberry Pi) control motors safely by handling higher voltages and currents than the MCU pins can provide.','Motor drivers are interface boards that let your microcontroller (Arduino/ESP32/STM32/Raspberry Pi) control motors safely by handling higher voltages and currents than the MCU pins can provide.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1771683476054-766962251.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-03 09:16:04'),
(454,1,19,17,'secondary',215,'Wired Keyboard and Mouse Combo','A wired keyboard and mouse combo is a reliable USB input solution designed for everyday computer and laptop use.','It includes a full-size keyboard for comfortable typing and a wired optical mouse for smooth and accurate cursor control.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772019011607-413992244.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-25 11:30:11'),
(455,1,19,17,'secondary',215,'Wireless Keyboard and Mouse Combo','A wireless keyboard and mouse combo is a convenient input solution that uses wireless connectivity (typically 2.4 GHz RF with a USB receiver or Bluetooth) to connect both the keyboard and mouse to your computer or laptop without cables','A wireless keyboard and mouse combo is a convenient input solution that uses wireless connectivity (typically 2.4 GHz RF with a USB receiver or Bluetooth) to connect both the keyboard and mouse to your computer or laptop without cables',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772019343593-655609099.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-25 11:35:43'),
(457,1,19,15,'secondary',165,'PIR Sensor','A PIR Sensor is an electronic sensor used to detect motion by sensing changes in infrared radiation emitted by humans or animals','It is called passive because it does not emit energy; instead, it detects IR heat naturally radiated from objects. PIR sensors are widely used in motion detectors, security systems, automatic lighting, and smart home applications.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1771684890884-905692155.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 14:41:30'),
(458,1,19,15,'secondary',165,'Reed Switch Module','A Reed Switch Module is a magnetic sensing device used to detect the presence or absence of a magnetic field. It consists of a small glass-encapsulated reed switch and a supporting circuit board with output pins for easy connection to microcontrollers like Arduino, Raspberry Pi, and other development boards.','Inside the glass tube, two thin metal reeds remain separated under normal conditions, but when a magnet comes near, the reeds attract each other and close the circuit, generating a digital signal. This simple working principle makes the module highly reliable, low power consuming, and fast in response.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772014439731-607740810.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-26 13:45:50'),
(459,1,19,15,'secondary',196,'DC Motor','A Direct Current (DC) motor is an electrical machine that converts direct current electrical energy into mechanical energy, primarily through rotating motion. It operates on the principle that a current-carrying conductor placed in a magnetic field experiences torque, causing it to spin. These motors are valued for high starting torque and precise speed control. ','A DC motor is an electric motor that converts direct current (DC) electrical energy into mechanical energy, typically for rotational motion','DC Motor','DC Motor','categories/1771672567652-24296365.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 11:16:07'),
(460,1,19,15,'secondary',196,'Vibration Motor','A Vibration Motor is a small DC motor designed to generate vibration instead of continuous rotational motion. It works using an eccentric rotating mass (ERM) attached to the motor shaft, which creates vibration when it spins. These motors are compact, lightweight, and operate at low voltages (typically 3V–5V), making them suitable for portable electronic devices and embedded systems. Vibration motors are commonly used in mobile phones, wearable devices, game controllers, medical alert systems, robotics projects, and tactile feedback applications.','They provide haptic feedback by converting electrical signals into physical vibration, alerting users through touch rather than sound. Due to their simple structure, low power consumption, and easy interfacing with microcontrollers like Arduino and Raspberry Pi, vibration motors are widely used in electronic and IoT-based projects.','Vibration Motor','Vibration Motor','categories/1772018398198-455696920.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-25 11:19:58'),
(461,1,19,15,'secondary',196,'Air Pump Motor','An Air Pump Motor is an electrical device used to convert electrical energy into mechanical energy to compress or move air. It creates airflow or air pressure for various applications such as inflating objects, aeration, air circulation, and pneumatic systems.','An Air Pump Motor is an electrical device that converts electrical energy into mechanical energy to move or compress air. It works by using a motor-driven mechanism such as a diaphragm or piston to create airflow or generate air pressure.','When powered by AC or DC supply, the motor rotates and drives the internal pumping system, drawing air in through an inlet valve and pushing it out through an outlet valve. Air pump motors are available in different voltage ratings like 3V, 6V, 12V, 24V DC and 110V/220V AC, depending on the application.','These motors are widely used in aquarium aeration systems, tyre inflators, medical equipment like nebulizers and BP monitors, air beds, balloons, oxygen systems, and small pneumatic projects.','categories/1771662077821-96091067.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-21 08:21:17'),
(462,1,19,15,'secondary',196,'Water Pump Motor','Water Pump Motor is an electromechanical device used to move water from one place to another by converting electrical energy into mechanical energy. In electronics and robotics projects, small DC water pump motors are commonly used, which operate on low voltages such as 3V, 6V, or 12V.','These pumps can be submersible (placed inside water) or non-submersible (external type). When power is supplied, the internal motor rotates an impeller that creates pressure, allowing water to flow through the outlet pipe.','Water pump motors are widely used in irrigation systems, aquarium circulation, water fountains, cooling systems, automatic plant watering projects, and smart agriculture systems. In embedded and IoT applications, they are controlled using relay modules or motor driver circuits connected to microcontrollers like Arduino or Raspberry Pi.','Many models are compact, lightweight, energy-efficient, and designed for continuous operation. Because of their reliable performance and easy integration, water pump motors are essential components in automation, robotics, and water management projects.','categories/1772018709407-94465411.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-25 11:25:09'),
(464,1,19,16,'secondary',3,'Keypad phones','Keypad phones are telephone devices that use a numeric keypad  for dialing numbers. They are commonly used in landline telephone systems for homes, offices, hotels, and call centers. Keypad phones offer quick and accurate dialing compared to rotary phones','They support basic features like redial, mute, flash, and volume control. These phones are reliable, easy to use, and suitable for daily voice communication.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1771681092414-372418592.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-05 14:17:12'),
(465,1,19,15,'primary',NULL,'Project Boards','Boards are flat platforms used in electronics to mount, connect, and support components. They help organize circuits, provide electrical connections, and make building, testing, or finalizing electronic projects easier.','Commonly used boards include breadboards for testing, PCBs for permanent circuits, and prototyping boards for semi-permanent designs.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1773062204145-375381354.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-09 13:16:44'),
(466,1,2,1,'secondary',10,'SMPS Power Supply','SMPS Power Supply','SMPS Power Supply','SMPS Power Supply','SMPS Power Supply','assets/uploads/category/SMPS_Power_Supply/1769502230_image.jpeg',0,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-03-09 11:21:31'),
(467,1,19,15,'secondary',323,'Raspberry Pi Camera Module','The Raspberry Pi Camera Module is a compact and high-quality camera designed specifically to work with Raspberry Pi boards through the dedicated CSI (Camera Serial Interface) port. It enables users to capture high-resolution images and record full HD videos, making it ideal for projects such as surveillance systems, robotics vision, face recognition, smart doorbells, wildlife monitoring, and time-lapse photography. Popular versions include the 8MP Camera Module V2 and the 12.3MP HQ Camera, which supports interchangeable lenses for professional imaging applications.','The module connects via a flat ribbon cable, ensuring fast data transfer and low CPU usage compared to USB cameras. It supports still image capture, 1080p video recording, and various image formats through the Raspberry Pi OS using Python libraries like Picamera. Due to its small size, lightweight design, and easy integration, the Raspberry Pi Camera Module is widely used in IoT, embedded systems, AI-based projects, and educational electronics applications.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772014322912-781871152.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-25 10:12:02'),
(468,1,19,15,'secondary',30,'RFID Cards','RFID Cards (Radio-Frequency Identification Cards) are contactless cards that use radio waves to transmit data wirelessly. They contain a small embedded chip and antenna that communicate with an RFID reader when the card is brought close—no swiping or phys','RFID (Radio-Frequency Identification) cards are smart cards that use radio waves to exchange data with a reader wirelessly. Each card contains a tiny microchip (to store data) and an antenna (to transmit data).','The reader emits a radio signal. The card’s antenna picks up the signal. The chip sends stored information back to the reader. The system verifies the data and grants or denies access','Door and gate access systems. Employee and student ID cards. Public transportation. Hotel key cards. Cashless payment systems. Attendance and time tracking','categories/1772014674752-866694733.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-25 10:17:54'),
(469,1,19,15,'secondary',30,'RFID Tags','RFID Tags (Radio-Frequency Identification Tags) are small electronic devices used to identify, track, and manage objects wirelessly using radio waves. They store data on a microchip and transmit it to an RFID reader through an antenna—no physical contact ','When an RFID reader sends out a radio signal, the tag’s antenna receives it. The tag then responds by transmitting its stored data (such as a unique ID number) back to the reader for identification or tracking.','LF (125–134 kHz): Short range, animal tracking, access control. HF (13.56 MHz / NFC): Smart labels, library systems, ticketing. UHF (860–960 MHz): Long range, supply chain, inventory, logistics','RFID (Radio-Frequency Identification) tags are small electronic devices used to identify and track objects wirelessly using radio waves. Each tag contains a microchip to store data and an antenna to transmit that data to an RFID reader.','categories/1772014846434-344201250.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-10 06:21:24','2026-02-25 10:20:46'),
