(534,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Battery Charger','A battery charger is a device that restores energy to rechargeable batteries by forcing electric current into them. Chargers are designed for specific battery types (Ni-MH, Li-ion, lead-acid, etc.) and must match the battery’s voltage and chemistry to work safely.','Always use a charger that matches the battery’s voltage and chemistry.\r\nOvercharging can reduce battery life or cause overheating.\r\nSmart chargers automatically stop or reduce charging when full.\r\nCharging should be done in a dry, well-ventilated area.\r\nCheck polarity (+ and − terminals) before connecting.','Input Source: Connects to AC mains (household electricity) or sometimes DC (like a car cigarette lighter).\r\nOutput: Provides controlled electrical current/voltage to a battery.\r\nCharging Mode: Can be simple (constant current) or smart (adjusts current based on battery condition).\r\nIndicators: LEDs or screens show charge level, errors, or status (charging/ready).','AC to DC Conversion: Charger converts alternating current (AC) to direct current (DC).\r\nCurrent Control: Supplies constant current during initial charging stage.\r\nVoltage Regulation: Maintains constant voltage as battery nears full charge.\r\nCut-off / Float Mode: Reduces or stops charging once battery is full to prevent damage.\r\nProtection Features: Many chargers include short-circuit, reverse polarity, and temperature protection systems.','categories/1772095738216-105952961.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-26 08:48:58','2026-02-26 09:25:49'),
(535,1,19,20,'secondary',408,'AA Battery','An AA Battery is a standard-sized cylindrical dry cell battery widely used to power portable electronic devices. It typically provides a nominal voltage of 1.5V in alkaline and zinc-carbon types, while rechargeable versions such as NiMH (Nickel-Metal Hydride) provide about 1.2V. AA batteries are commonly used in remote controls, wall clocks, toys, flashlights, wireless keyboards, cameras, and various electronic and robotics projects.','They are available in disposable (alkaline, zinc-carbon, lithium) and rechargeable types, offering flexibility depending on power requirements and usage frequency.','AA batteries are popular because of their compact size, easy availability, stable output voltage, and moderate energy capacity.','In embedded systems and DIY electronics, multiple AA batteries are often connected in series to achieve higher voltages like 3V, 6V, or 9V for powering motors, microcontrollers, and other components.','categories/1772098332912-963608854.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-26 09:32:12','2026-02-26 09:32:12'),
(536,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'AA Battery Charger','The AA battery charger supplies controlled electrical current to safely recharge AA batteries. Modern chargers include automatic charging control, LED indicators, and overcharge protection to improve battery life and safety.\r\nMost chargers support multiple battery slots, allowing 2 or 4 batteries to be charged simultaneously.','An AA Battery Charger is an electronic device used to recharge AA-size rechargeable batteries such as Ni-MH (Nickel Metal Hydride) and Ni-Cd (Nickel Cadmium) batteries. It is commonly used for household electronics, toys, remotes, wireless devices, and cameras.','Use only rechargeable AA batteries (not normal alkaline cells).\r\nInsert batteries with correct polarity (+/–).\r\nDo not mix old and new batteries.\r\nRemove batteries after full charge if charger has no auto cut feature.','Connect charger to power supply first.\r\nInsert AA batteries properly into slots.\r\nCharging LED turns ON during charging.\r\nIndicator changes color or turns OFF when charging completes.\r\nRecommended charging time: 4–8 hours depending on capacity.','categories/1772098563886-564764466.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-26 09:36:03','2026-04-10 05:08:51'),
(537,1,19,20,'secondary',408,'AAA Battery','An AAA battery (also known as a triple-A battery) is a small, cylindrical dry cell battery commonly used in low to medium power electronic devices. It is smaller than an AA battery and typically measures about 44.5 mm in length and 10.5 mm in diameter. AAA batteries are widely used in remote controls, wireless keyboards and mice, wall clocks, toys, LED flashlights, TV remotes, and small portable electronics.','They are available in different chemical types such as alkaline, lithium, and rechargeable nickel-metal hydride (NiMH). The standard nominal voltage of a AAA battery is 1.5V for alkaline and lithium types, while rechargeable NiMH versions usually provide 1.2V. Because of their compact size, AAA batteries are lightweight and convenient for small devices requiring moderate power consumption.','AAA batteries operate by converting stored chemical energy into electrical energy through an electrochemical reaction between the anode and cathode. Alkaline AAA batteries offer good shelf life (up to 5–10 years) and are suitable for everyday household devices.','Lithium AAA batteries provide longer life and better performance in extreme temperatures, making them suitable for high-drain devices. Rechargeable NiMH AAA batteries can be recharged hundreds of times, making them cost-effective and environmentally friendly over long-term use. However, rechargeable batteries require compatible chargers and proper handling to maintain efficiency and lifespan.','categories/1772098687638-581290683.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-26 09:38:07','2026-02-26 09:38:07'),
(538,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'abc','abc','abc','abc','abc',NULL,0,1,'active','2026-02-26 10:06:21','2026-02-26 10:10:38'),
(539,1,19,20,'secondary',538,'def','def','def','def','def',NULL,0,1,'active','2026-02-26 10:06:43','2026-02-26 10:10:45'),
(540,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'AAA Battery Charger','AAA battery chargers provide controlled charging current to safely recharge batteries and extend their lifespan. Most modern chargers support AA & AAA batteries together, with automatic charging control and LED indicators showing charging status.\r\nThey are commonly available in 2-slot or 4-slot charging designs and may operate using AC power or USB input.','An AAA Battery Charger is a device used to recharge AAA-size rechargeable batteries, mainly Ni-MH (Nickel Metal Hydride) and Ni-Cd (Nickel Cadmium) batteries. It is widely used for small electronic devices requiring compact power sources.','Use only rechargeable AAA batteries.\r\nDo not charge alkaline batteries.\r\nInsert batteries with correct polarity (+/–).\r\nAvoid mixing different battery capacities.','Connect charger to power supply.\r\n\r\nInsert AAA batteries properly into slots.\r\nLED indicator shows charging process.\r\nIndicator changes when charging completes.\r\nTypical charging time: 3–6 hours depending on battery capacity.','categories/1772100412310-683819123.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-26 10:06:52','2026-04-13 05:30:38'),
(541,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'AA/AAA Combo Charger','An AA/AAA Combo Charger is a versatile charging device designed to recharge both AA and AAA size rechargeable batteries in a single unit. It is commonly used for Nickel-Metal Hydride (Ni-MH) and Nickel-Cadmium (Ni-Cd) batteries and is widely applied in homes, laboratories, schools, and electronic workshops.','AA batteries generally have a nominal voltage of 1.2V (rechargeable) with capacities ranging from 1200mAh to 3000mAh, while AAA batteries also have a nominal voltage of 1.2V with capacities typically between 600mAh and 1200mAh.','Always use rechargeable AA/AAA batteries (Ni-MH or Ni-Cd) with the charger; never attempt to charge non-rechargeable alkaline batteries. Insert batteries with correct polarity as indicated in the slots. Avoid mixing old and new batteries during charging. Use batteries of the same type and capacity together for best performance. Ensure proper ventilation during charging and unplug the charger when not in use. Regularly inspect charging contacts for dust or corrosion.','The AA/AAA combo charger system consists of an AC-to-DC power conversion unit (transformer or SMPS), rectifier circuit, voltage regulator, constant current charging circuit, and protection circuitry. In smart chargers, a microcontroller or dedicated charging IC monitors battery voltage, temperature, and charge termination using methods such as negative delta V (-ΔV) detection or temperature sensing. LED indicators or display panels provide charging status feedback. Proper insulation, grounding, and thermal management are essential for safe system operation and long battery life.','categories/1772101814984-211923997.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-26 10:07:47','2026-04-13 05:30:38'),
(542,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'9V Battery Charger','A 9V Battery Charger is an electronic device used to recharge 9-volt rechargeable batteries safely and efficiently. It is commonly designed for rechargeable battery types such as Nickel-Cadmium (Ni-Cd), Nickel-Metal Hydride (Ni-MH), and Lithium-ion (Li-ion) 9V batteries.','9V rechargeable battery typically has a nominal voltage of 8.4V or 9.6V depending on its chemistry. The charger’s output voltage and current rating must match the battery specifications. Charging time varies based on battery capacity (measured in mAh) and charger current output. Slow chargers provide low current for safe overnight charging, while fast chargers deliver higher current with built-in control circuits.','Always check battery chemistry before charging, as Li-ion batteries require dedicated chargers with precise voltage regulation and protection circuits. Avoid mixing different battery types in multi-slot chargers. Do not overcharge or leave batteries unattended for long periods unless the charger has automatic cut-off. Store batteries in a cool, dry place when not in use. Regularly inspect the charger cable and terminals for damage.','The 9V battery charger system generally consists of an AC input section, step-down transformer or switching power supply, rectifier circuit, voltage regulator, current limiting circuit, charging control IC, LED indicator circuit, and output terminals.','categories/1772101604727-323599339.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-26 10:08:18','2026-04-13 05:30:15'),
