(545,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Ni-Cd Battery Charger',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,'active','2026-02-26 10:28:28','2026-04-13 05:30:45'),
(546,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'NTC Thermistor','NTC Thermistor (Negative Temperature Coefficient Thermistor) is a temperature-sensitive resistor whose resistance decreases as temperature increases. It is made from semiconductor materials such as metal oxides, and it is widely used for temperature sensing, temperature control, and inrush current limiting applications. At low temperatures, the resistance of an NTC thermistor is high, and as the temperature rises, its resistance drops significantly.','NTC thermistors are available in different resistance values such as 5kΩ, 10kΩ, 47kΩ, and 100kΩ at 25°C (commonly referred to as R25 value). They come in bead type, disc type, and surface-mount (SMD) packages. In temperature sensing applications, they are often used in voltage divider circuits with microcontrollers, thermostats, battery management systems, air conditioners, refrigerators, medical devices, and automotive temperature monitoring systems.','In power supply circuits, NTC thermistors are also used as inrush current limiters, where they reduce the high initial surge current when equipment is powered ON.','NTC thermistors are sensitive to temperature changes, proper placement is important for accurate measurement. In inrush current limiting applications, they must be rated for appropriate current and power handling capacity.','categories/1772110366500-351655821.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-26 12:52:46','2026-02-26 12:52:46'),
(547,1,19,15,'primary',NULL,'Motor Driver','An electronics motor driver is an electronic circuit or module used to control the speed, direction, and operation of a motor using low-power control signals from a microcontroller such as Arduino, Raspberry Pi, or other embedded systems. Since microcontrollers cannot supply enough current to drive motors directly, a motor driver acts as an interface between the control circuit and the motor by amplifying current and handling higher voltages safely.','Motor drivers are commonly used to control DC motors, stepper motors, and servo motors in robotics, automation systems, conveyor systems, electric vehicles, and industrial machines. Popular motor driver ICs include L298N and L293D, which use an H-Bridge circuit configuration to control motor direction (forward and reverse). By applying Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) signals from a microcontroller, the motor speed can be adjusted efficiently.','Technically, motor drivers support different voltage and current ratings depending on the model. For example, L298N can typically handle motor voltages up to 35V and current around 2A per channel (with proper cooling). Protection features such as flyback diodes, overcurrent protection, and thermal shutdown are often included to protect the circuit from back EMF generated by motors.','Always match motor voltage and current with driver specifications. Use external power supply for motors instead of powering from microcontroller directly. Connect ground (GND) of driver and controller together for proper signal reference.Use heat sinks for high-current applications. For precise control, use PWM signals from the controller.','categories/1772112816519-598669971.jpeg',0,1,'active','2026-02-26 13:33:36','2026-02-26 13:34:16'),
(548,1,19,15,'primary',NULL,'USB to TTL','USB to TTL modules act as a bridge between USB and serial devices. Inside the module, a USB-UART IC (such as CP2102, CH340G, FT232RL, PL2303) converts USB data into TX/RX serial signals.','A USB to TTL Converter is an electronic interface device used to convert USB signals from a computer into TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) serial communication signals.\r\nIt allows communication between a PC/Laptop and microcontrollers or embedded devices through UART serial communication.','Match voltage level (3.3V or 5V) before connection.\r\nAlways match voltage level (3.3V or 5V) before connecting.\r\nTX pin connects to RX and RX connects to TX.\r\nInstall correct USB driver before use.\r\nTTL is NOT RS232 voltage — do not connect directly to RS232 ports.\r\nAvoid powering high-current devices from VCC pin.','Connect GND first for stable communication.\r\nSelect correct COM port in software (Arduino IDE / Flash tool).\r\nSet correct baud rate in program.\r\nDisconnect external power while uploading firmware (if required).\r\nUse short USB cable to avoid communication errors.\r\nCheck device manager to confirm driver installation.','categories/1772115565298-41021538.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-26 14:19:25','2026-02-26 14:19:25'),
(549,1,19,15,'secondary',78,'LDR Sensor','The LDR is made from semiconductor material (usually cadmium sulfide). It detects surrounding light and converts light energy into electrical resistance variation.','An LDR (Light Dependent Resistor), also called a photoresistor, is an electronic component whose resistance changes according to light intensity.\r\nWhen light increases, resistance decreases; when light decreases, resistance increases.','LDR gives analog output, not digital directly.\r\nAvoid exposure to excessive heat or moisture.\r\nResponse is slower compared to photodiodes.\r\nUse proper resistor value for accurate readings.','Connect LDR in voltage divider configuration.\r\n\r\nOne side to VCC, other through resistor to GND.\r\n\r\nRead output from middle junction to analog pin.\r\n\r\nCalibrate threshold value in software.\r\n\r\nKeep sensor facing light source for accurate detection.','categories/1772117054076-584478308.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-26 14:44:14','2026-02-26 14:44:14'),
(550,1,19,15,'secondary',165,'Thermoelectric Cooling Module','A Thermoelectric Cooling Module, commonly known as a Peltier module, is a solid-state electronic device that produces a temperature difference when DC electrical power is applied. It works based on the Peltier Effect, where heat is transferred from one side of the module to the other when current flows through it. As a result, one surface becomes cold while the opposite surface becomes hot.','The module is made of multiple P-type and N-type semiconductor elements sandwiched between two ceramic plates. These semiconductor junctions are electrically connected in series and thermally connected in parallel. When powered, electrons move across the junctions, absorbing heat on one side (cooling surface) and releasing it on the other side (heating surface).','Mini refrigerators and portable coolers. CPU and electronic component cooling. Medical storage boxes. Car seat cooling systems. Scientific and laboratory experiments.','Always attach a heat sink and cooling fan to the hot side to prevent overheating. Use thermal paste for efficient heat transfer. Requires high current power supply (commonly 4–6A for 12V models).','categories/1772117254980-996669298.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-26 14:47:34','2026-02-26 14:47:34'),
(551,1,19,20,'secondary',427,'Analog Multimeter','An Analog Multimeter is a basic electrical measuring instrument used to measure voltage (AC/DC), current (DC), and resistance. It displays the measured value using a moving needle that points to numbers printed on a calibrated scale. The deflection of the needle indicates the magnitude of the electrical quantity being measured. It is commonly used in electrical laboratories, repair work, and educational institutions for testing and troubleshooting circuits.','The working principle of an analog multimeter is based on the Permanent Magnet Moving Coil (PMMC) mechanism. When current flows through the coil placed inside a magnetic field, a force is produced that causes the needle to move.','The amount of needle deflection is directly proportional to the current flowing through the coil. With the help of internal resistors and shunt arrangements, the same meter can measure different ranges of voltage, current, and resistance.','It is important to start with the highest range to prevent damage to the meter. Although analog multimeters are less accurate compared to digital meters, they are useful for observing gradual changes and fluctuations in electrical signals.','categories/1772187671521-307209022.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-27 10:21:11','2026-02-27 10:21:11'),
(552,1,19,20,'secondary',427,'Clamp Multimeter','A Clamp Multimeter, also known as a clamp meter, is a special type of digital multimeter designed mainly to measure AC or DC current without directly touching or disconnecting the circuit. It has a hinged jaw (clamp) at the top that can open and close around a conductor to measure the magnetic field produced by the flowing current.','In addition to current measurement, most clamp meters can also measure voltage (AC/DC), resistance, continuity, frequency, and sometimes temperature. It is widely used in electrical maintenance, industrial systems, and power distribution testing because it allows safe and quick current measurement.','The working principle of a clamp multimeter is based on electromagnetic induction. When AC current flows through a conductor, it generates a magnetic field around it. The clamp jaw contains a current transformer (CT) sensor that detects this magnetic field and converts it into a proportional electrical signal, which is then processed and displayed digitally.','In DC clamp meters, a Hall Effect sensor is used to detect the magnetic field produced by DC current. The internal circuit then converts the measured signal into a digital value using an analog-to-digital converter.','categories/1772188007986-348991805.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-27 10:26:47','2026-02-27 10:26:47'),
(553,1,19,20,'secondary',427,'Auto-Ranging Multimeter','An Auto-Ranging Multimeter is a type of digital multimeter that automatically selects the correct measurement range for voltage, current, or resistance. Unlike manual multimeters, where the user must choose the appropriate range before measuring, an auto-ranging multimeter detects the input signal level and adjusts itself to display the most accurate reading.','It is widely used in electronics labs, electrical maintenance, industrial servicing, and troubleshooting because it simplifies operation and reduces the chance of selecting the wrong range.','The instrument can measure AC/DC voltage, AC/DC current, resistance, continuity, diode, and in advanced models, capacitance, frequency, and temperature. It has an LCD display, function selector switch, input terminals (COM, VΩ, mA, 10A), internal battery, and built-in protection circuits. Since it automatically adjusts the range, it is very user-friendly and suitable for beginners as well as professionals.','The working principle of an auto-ranging multimeter is based on Analog-to-Digital Conversion (ADC) and internal microcontroller control. When an input signal is applied, the ADC converts the analog signal into digital data.','categories/1772188157065-580797845.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-27 10:29:17','2026-02-27 10:29:17'),
(554,1,19,21,'secondary',628,'RMA Soldering Wire','RMA Soldering Wire stands for Rosin Mildly Activated solder wire. It is a type of flux-cored solder wire that contains a mildly activated rosin flux inside the core. This flux helps remove light oxidation from metal surfaces and improves solder flow during the soldering process. RMA solder is commonly used in electronics assembly, PCB soldering, repair work, and electrical component connections where clean and reliable joints are required.','RMA soldering wire is typically made from tin-lead (Sn-Pb) alloy such as 60/40 or 63/37 ratio, or it may also be available in lead-free compositions like tin-silver-copper (SAC). The rosin-based flux inside the wire activates when heated and cleans the metal surfaces, allowing the molten solder to bond properly.','Compared to RA (Rosin Activated) flux, RMA flux is less aggressive and leaves minimal residue. The residue is generally non-corrosive and may not require cleaning in many electronic applications. RMA solder wires are available in different diameters for fine PCB work and general electrical soldering.','RMA soldering wire works by combining metal alloy and flux in a single wire. When heated with a soldering iron, the flux core melts first and cleans the metal surfaces by removing oxidation. Immediately after, the solder alloy melts and flows into the joint, creating a strong mechanical and electrical connection. Once cooled, the solder solidifies and forms a stable bond between the connected components.','categories/1772188801171-8092748.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-27 10:40:01','2026-03-12 09:25:47'),
(555,1,19,20,'secondary',408,'9V Battery','A 9V Battery is a small rectangular power source commonly used in electronic devices and small electrical circuits. It provides a nominal output of 9 volts and is widely used in smoke detectors, multimeters, toys, radios, and small electronic projects. The battery has two snap connectors on the top: a smaller circular positive terminal and a larger hexagonal negative terminal.','9V batteries are compact, lightweight, and easy to connect, making them popular for portable and low-power applications.','A 9V battery works based on electrochemical reactions inside its cells. Chemical energy stored in the battery is converted into electrical energy through reactions between the anode (negative terminal), cathode (positive terminal), and electrolyte.','When connected to a circuit, electrons flow from the negative terminal through the external circuit to the positive terminal, providing power to the connected device. The series arrangement of internal cells ensures the combined voltage output reaches 9 volts. Once the chemical reactants are depleted, the battery can no longer supply power and must be replaced or recharged (if rechargeable type).','categories/1772188990733-958758593.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-27 10:43:10','2026-02-27 10:43:10'),
(556,1,19,14,'primary',NULL,'Tweeters','A Tweeter is a small loudspeaker designed specifically to reproduce high-frequency (treble) sounds, typically from about 2 kHz to 20 kHz. It handles sharp and clear audio elements such as vocals, cymbals, and high musical notes. Tweeters are commonly used in home audio systems, car audio systems, PA systems, and professional sound setups. Because high-frequency sounds require fast vibration, tweeters use lightweight diaphragms to produce clear and detailed sound.','Tweeters are usually smaller in size compared to woofers and mid-range speakers. They are often made with materials like silk, metal (aluminum or titanium), or ceramic diaphragms.','Tweeters work on the principle of electromagnetic induction, similar to other dynamic speakers. When an audio signal flows through the voice coil placed in a magnetic field, it creates motion. This motion moves the lightweight diaphragm back and forth rapidly, producing high-frequency sound waves.','Because high-frequency sounds require very fast vibration, the diaphragm is made thin and light to respond quickly to electrical signals. The crossover system filters the audio signal so that only high-frequency signals reach the tweeter, ensuring clear sound output and long life of the speaker.','categories/1772189192508-154630860.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-27 10:46:32','2026-03-05 13:31:41'),
(557,1,19,15,'secondary',436,'LCD Display','An LCD (Liquid Crystal Display) is an electronic display device used to show text, numbers, images, and graphics. It works by using liquid crystals that control light passing through them to create visible characters or images. LCDs are widely used in electronic devices such as calculators, digital clocks, televisions, computers, industrial equipment, and embedded systems like Arduino projects.','LCD displays are popular because they consume low power, are lightweight, and produce clear output. Common types include character LCDs (like 16x2 or 20x4) and graphical LCDs for displaying images and custom graphics.','LCD works on the principle of light modulation using liquid crystals. Liquid crystals do not emit light directly; instead, they control the passage of light from a backlight source. When voltage is applied to specific segments or pixels, the liquid crystals align in a way that either blocks or allows light to pass through, forming characters or images on the screen.','The display controller receives data signals and activates specific pixels in a timed sequence. The backlight provides illumination, making the display visible even in low light conditions.','categories/1772191616517-405251479.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-27 11:26:56','2026-02-27 11:26:56'),
(558,1,19,15,'secondary',320,'Caster Wheels','Caster wheels are small wheels mounted inside a rotating frame (called a fork or housing) that allow objects to move smoothly in different directions. Unlike motor-driven wheels, caster wheels are free-moving support wheels used to balance and guide movement. They are commonly attached to the bottom of robots, furniture, carts, machines, and mobile equipment to provide easy mobility and flexible steering.','A caster wheel usually consists of a wheel, swivel mechanism, mounting plate or stem, and bearing system, allowing the wheel to rotate and change direction freely.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772260219439-947484694.jpg',0,1,'active','2026-02-28 06:30:19','2026-02-28 07:14:13'),
(559,1,19,15,'secondary',320,'Bo Motor Wheels','These wheels usually come with a D-shaft fitting, perfectly matching BO gear motors.\r\nMost commonly available size is 65mm diameter, ideal for beginner robotics projects.\r\nThey are simple, durable, and easy to attach to motor shafts.','BO Motor Wheels are lightweight plastic or rubber wheels specially designed to fit BO (Battery Operated) DC geared motors used in robotics and Arduino car projects.\r\nThey are commonly used in robot cars, line follower robots, and obstacle avoidance robots.','Ensure correct D-shaft alignment before fitting.\r\nDo not force the wheel onto the shaft.\r\nLarger wheels reduce torque but increase speed.\r\nUse rubber grip wheels for better traction.','Tight fit ensures smooth motion.\r\nUse 2 wheels + 1 caster wheel for balance.\r\nMatch motor RPM with wheel size.\r\nCheck wheel alignment to avoid vibration.','categories/1772260641444-70966963.webp',1,1,'active','2026-02-28 06:37:21','2026-02-28 06:37:21'),
(560,1,19,15,'secondary',320,'Castor Wheels','Caster wheels rotate freely in any direction, allowing robots or platforms to move smoothly without needing an additional motor.\r\nThey reduce friction and help maintain stability during movement.\r\nTypes include ball caster, single wheel caster, and swivel caster designs.','A Castor Wheel (Caster Wheel) is a free-rotating support wheel used in robots, carts, and movable equipment to provide balance and smooth movement.\r\nIn robotics, it is commonly used as a support wheel along with two driven motor wheels.','Use caster wheel for balance in 2-wheel robots.\r\nInstall at correct height for smooth movement.\r\nChoose low-friction type for better efficiency.\r\nEnsure mounting screws are tight.','Place caster wheel opposite motor wheels.\r\nMaintain equal ground clearance.\r\nAvoid excessive load on small caster wheels.\r\nTest rotation freely before operation.','categories/1772261234775-816447147.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-28 06:47:14','2026-02-28 06:47:14'),
(561,1,19,14,'secondary',332,'wall speaker','A wall speaker is an audio speaker designed to be mounted directly on a wall to provide clear and evenly distributed sound in indoor or semi-outdoor environments. These speakers are commonly used in public address (PA) systems, homes, offices, schools, temples, shopping malls, and conference halls where floor space needs to be saved while maintaining good sound coverage.','Wall speakers usually come in a compact enclosure with mounting brackets that allow easy installation and adjustable sound direction. They are connected to an audio amplifier or PA system through wired connections and are engineered to deliver speech clarity and background music efficiently across large areas.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772262441552-562173431.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-28 07:07:21','2026-02-28 07:11:49'),
(562,1,19,15,'secondary',320,'Two Wheel Chassis Kit','The 2WD chassis kit acts as the base structure of a robot. Two DC geared motors drive the main wheels, while a caster wheel supports movement and stability.','A Two Wheel Chassis Kit (2WD Robot Chassis) is a basic robotic platform used to build robot cars and automation projects.\r\nIt includes two motor-driven wheels and a support caster wheel for balance.\r\nThis kit is widely used for Arduino, Raspberry Pi, and robotics learning projects.','Use motor driver to control motors safely.\r\nEnsure equal motor wiring polarity.\r\nBalance battery weight properly.\r\nTighten all screws before operation.','Connect motors to motor driver outputs.\r\nUse caster wheel at front or rear for balance.\r\nKeep wiring organized to avoid wheel blockage.\r\nTest motor direction before programming.','categories/1772263393552-999689052.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-28 07:23:13','2026-02-28 07:23:13'),
(563,1,19,15,'secondary',320,'DC Motor Tyres','These tyres are mounted on plastic rims that connect directly to motor shafts (usually D-shaft type). The rubber outer layer increases grip and reduces slipping, making them ideal for robot cars and automation platforms.','DC Motor Tyres are rubber or silicone-covered wheels designed to fit DC gear motors used in robotics and DIY vehicle projects.\r\nThey provide improved traction, stability, and smooth robot movement.','Arduino robot car\r\n\r\nLine follower robot\r\n\r\nObstacle avoidance robot\r\nBluetooth / WiFi robot\r\nSTEM robotics kits\r\nDIY automation vehicles','Larger tyres increase speed but reduce torque.\r\nRubber tyres give better grip than plastic wheels.\r\nEnsure tight shaft fitting.\r\nSelect tyre size based on motor RPM.','categories/1772264875679-967877823.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-28 07:47:55','2026-02-28 07:47:55'),
(564,1,19,15,'secondary',465,'PCB Boards','A PCB (Printed Circuit Board) is a flat insulating board used to mechanically support and electrically connect electronic components through copper conductive pathways. Instead of using many wires, a PCB uses thin copper tracks (called traces) to connect components like resistors, capacitors, diodes, transistors, and ICs. Most PCBs are made from FR-4 (fiberglass reinforced epoxy) material, which provides strength, insulation, and heat resistance. PCBs make electronic circuits compact, neat, reliable, and suitable for mass production.','Electronic components such as resistors, capacitors, diodes, transistors, and integrated circuits are mounted on the board either through through-hole technology (THT) or surface mount technology (SMT), depending on the design requirements. PCBs can be single-layer, double-layer, or multilayer, based on the number of copper layers used to form connections.','PCBs improve performance by reducing electrical noise, enhancing signal flow, and increasing durability. Important technical considerations in PCB design include track width, grounding methods, component spacing, heat dissipation, and proper insulation distance to prevent short circuits','Standard PCB thickness is usually around 1.6 mm, and copper thickness commonly used is 1 oz per square foot. PCBs are designed using specialized software such as Eagle, KiCad, or Altium Designer, and manufactured through processes like etching, drilling, plating, and solder masking. They are widely used in consumer electronics, industrial systems, medical devices, automotive electronics, and communication equipment, forming the backbone of modern electronic systems.','categories/1772449521304-788580546.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-02 11:05:21','2026-03-02 11:05:21'),
(565,1,19,15,'secondary',465,'BreadBoard','A typical breadboard consists of two main sections: the terminal strips in the center area where components are connected, and the power rails on the sides (usually marked with red and blue lines) used for supplying positive and ground connections. In the terminal section, holes are connected in groups (usually five holes per row), while the center gap allows integrated circuits (ICs) to be placed across it without shorting pins.','Breadboards are commonly used in schools, colleges, and electronics labs for Arduino projects, sensor testing, and small prototype circuits. ','Proper wiring and neat jumper connections help avoid short circuits and confusion. Breadboards are not ideal for high-frequency or high-power applications due to loose connections and internal resistance.','Overall, a breadboard is an essential tool for beginners and professionals to quickly design, test, and modify electronic circuits efficiently.','categories/1772449718993-325270584.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-02 11:08:38','2026-03-02 11:08:38'),
(566,1,19,15,'secondary',465,'Solar Board','A solar board, commonly known as a solar panel, is a device that converts sunlight into electrical energy using photovoltaic (PV) cells. These cells are typically made from silicon and generate direct current (DC) electricity when exposed to sunlight. When sunlight hits the solar cells, it excites electrons and creates an electric flow, which can be used to power electronic devices or charge batteries. Solar boards are widely used in homes, street lights, calculators, water pumps, and small electronic projects.','Solar panels are available in different types such as monocrystalline, polycrystalline, and thin-film panels. Monocrystalline panels are more efficient and compact, while polycrystalline panels are cost-effective. The output voltage and current of a solar board depend on its size, number of cells, and sunlight intensity.','Small solar boards may produce 3V, 6V, 9V, or 12V DC, while larger panels used in homes can produce much higher power ratings like 100W, 200W, or more. Since solar panels produce DC output, additional components such as charge controllers, batteries, and inverters are often used in a complete solar system.','Solar boards provide clean, renewable, and eco-friendly energy without producing pollution. Proper angle placement toward sunlight increases efficiency. Dust and shading can reduce power output, so regular cleaning is important. Solar panels work best in direct sunlight but can still produce limited power in cloudy conditions. They are low-maintenance and have a long lifespan, typically 20–25 years.','categories/1772449921663-404777071.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-02 11:12:01','2026-03-09 13:42:17'),
(567,1,19,20,'secondary',10,'Power Supply Board','A Power Supply Board is an electronic circuit board designed to convert electrical power from one form to another and provide a stable output voltage to other components or systems. Its main function is to convert AC (Alternating Current) from mains electricity into regulated DC (Direct Current) suitable for electronic devices. It ensures proper voltage, current control, and protection for connected circuits. Power supply boards are commonly used in TVs, computers, LED drivers, industrial control panels, battery chargers, and embedded systems.','There are different types of power supply boards, such as Linear Power Supplies and SMPS (Switched Mode Power Supplies). Linear supplies use transformers and voltage regulators for smooth output but are larger and less efficient. SMPS boards are more compact, efficient, and widely used in modern electronics.','Power Supply Board is an electronic circuit board designed to convert and regulate electrical power to provide a stable output voltage for electronic devices. It typically converts AC (alternating current) from mains electricity into regulated DC (direct current) required by circuits and components. Power supply boards may be linear or switched-mode (SMPS) types, with SMPS being more compact and efficient.','The board generally includes components such as a transformer for voltage conversion, rectifier diodes to convert AC to DC, filter capacitors to smooth ripple voltage, voltage regulators or PWM controllers for stable output, and protection elements like fuses and overcurrent protection circuits.','categories/1772454793301-191026694.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-02 12:33:13','2026-03-02 12:33:13'),
(568,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Heat Shrink sleeve','A Heat Shrink Sleeve (also called heat shrink tubing) is a protective insulating tube used to cover and protect electrical wires, solder joints, and cable connections. It is made from polymer materials that shrink tightly around wires when heat is applied using a heat gun or hot air source. Once heated, the sleeve contracts and forms a secure, insulated, and protective covering over the connection.','Heat shrink sleeves are commonly made from polyolefin material and are available in different diameters, thicknesses, and colors. They typically have shrink ratios such as 2:1, 3:1, or 4:1, meaning the tube shrinks to half, one-third, or one-fourth of its original diameter. Some heat shrink sleeves include adhesive lining inside (dual-wall type) to provide waterproof sealing and stronger mechanical protection.','They are widely used in electrical wiring, automotive harnesses, battery connections, PCB wiring, cable management, and industrial equipment.',' Heat shrink sleeves improve safety by preventing short circuits, protecting against moisture, dust, vibration, and mechanical damage.','categories/1772458214786-238592377.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-02 13:30:14','2026-03-02 13:30:14'),
(569,1,19,14,'secondary',332,'Multimedia speaker','A Multimedia Speaker is an audio output device designed to reproduce sound from various electronic sources such as computers, laptops, TVs, mobile phones, music players, and gaming consoles. Unlike basic speakers, multimedia speakers often include additional features like built-in amplifiers, enhanced bass speakers (woofers), Bluetooth connectivity, USB/SD playback, and remote controls for easy volume and mode selection.','Multimedia speakers are commonly used in homes, offices, classrooms, and entertainment setups to deliver richer and louder audio compared to built-in device speakers. They come in various configurations such as 2.0 (two speakers), 2.1 (two satellites + subwoofer), 5.1 (surround sound), and more, depending on the desired audio experience.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772512417872-270025073.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-03 04:33:37','2026-03-03 04:33:37'),
(570,1,19,15,'secondary',86,'ESP 32 Module','The ESP32 module is a powerful and low-cost Wi-Fi and Bluetooth-enabled microcontroller developed by Espressif Systems. It is widely used in IoT (Internet of Things), embedded systems, automation, and smart device applications due to its high performance and built-in wireless connectivity.','The ESP32 features a dual-core 32-bit Xtensa LX6 processor with clock speeds up to 240 MHz, integrated Wi-Fi (802.11 b/g/n) and Bluetooth (Classic + BLE), making it suitable for wireless communication projects. It operates at 3.3V logic level and typically includes multiple GPIO pins, ADC (Analog to Digital Converter), DAC (Digital to Analog Converter), PWM channels, SPI, I2C, UART, and touch sensor inputs.','The module supports programming through the Arduino IDE, ESP-IDF (Espressif IoT Development Framework), and MicroPython, making it flexible for beginners and advanced developers. It also includes built-in features like deep sleep mode for low power consumption, hardware encryption, secure boot, and real-time clock (RTC), which are useful for battery-powered and secure IoT applications.','In practical applications, the ESP32 is commonly used in home automation systems, smart agriculture, wireless sensor networks, robotics, weather monitoring systems, industrial automation, and web server-based control systems. Important system notes include ensuring a stable 5V USB input (internally regulated to 3.3V), proper antenna placement for better Wi-Fi signal strength, and avoiding direct 5V signals to GPIO pins, as they are not 5V tolerant.','categories/1772523086246-246207366.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-03 07:31:26','2026-03-03 07:31:26'),
(571,1,19,15,'secondary',165,'GSM Antenna','A GSM antenna is a communication antenna designed to transmit and receive signals over the Global System for Mobile Communications (GSM) network, typically operating in frequency bands such as 850 MHz, 900 MHz, 1800 MHz, and 1900 MHz. It is commonly used with GSM modules like SIM800, SIM900, and other cellular communication devices to enable SMS, voice calls, and mobile data transmission. The antenna improves signal strength, coverage range, and communication reliability in embedded and IoT applications.','GSM antennas are available in various types, including external magnetic-mount antennas, PCB antennas, spring antennas, and stub (rubber duck) antennas. External antennas usually connect via connectors such as SMA, u.FL, or IPEX, providing better reception compared to onboard PCB antennas.','These antennas are widely used in IoT systems, GPS trackers, vehicle tracking devices, smart meters, security systems, remote monitoring systems, industrial automation, and GSM-based alarm systems.','Important specifications to consider include frequency range, gain (dBi), impedance (typically 50 ohms), connector type, cable length, and operating environment to ensure proper compatibility and optimal performance in communication systems.','categories/1772531042883-381220052.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-03 09:44:02','2026-03-03 09:44:02'),
(572,1,19,15,'secondary',316,'Arduino Leonardo board','The Arduino Leonardo is a microcontroller development board based on the ATmega32U4, designed and released by Arduino. Unlike the Arduino Uno, the Leonardo uses the ATmega32U4 which has built-in USB communication, allowing it to appear as a keyboard, mouse, or other USB Human Interface Device (HID) directly when connected to a computer. This makes it especially useful for projects involving USB control, automation, and custom input devices.','The board operates at 5V logic level with a 16 MHz clock speed and includes 20 digital I/O pins (7 can be used as PWM outputs), 12 analog input pins, 32 KB of flash memory (4 KB used by bootloader), 2.5 KB SRAM, and 1 KB EEPROM. It supports communication interfaces such as UART, SPI, and I2C, and can be powered through the micro USB port or external power supply (7–12V recommended).','The Arduino Leonardo is widely used in robotics, automation systems, gaming controllers, USB keyboard/mouse emulation projects, data logging, sensor-based systems, and IoT prototypes. It is fully programmable using the Arduino IDE, making it beginner-friendly while still powerful for advanced embedded applications.','Operates at 5V, but some communication pins use 3.3V internally check sensor compatibility. Avoid supplying more than 12V through the VIN pin to prevent overheating. Because it has native USB support, the board may disconnect and reconnect during sketch uploads. GPIO pins have limited current output (typically 20mA per pin), so external drivers or transistors are required for high-power loads.','categories/1772534806898-439887765.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-03 10:46:46','2026-03-03 10:46:46'),
(573,1,19,14,'secondary',332,'Tower Speakers','Tower Speakers are tall, floor-standing loudspeakers designed to deliver high-quality and powerful audio for home entertainment systems. They usually contain multiple speaker drivers such as woofers for bass, midrange drivers for vocals, and tweeters for high-frequency sounds, all enclosed in a single vertical cabinet. Because of their large size and internal volume, tower speakers can produce deeper bass and clearer sound compared to small bookshelf speakers.','Tower speakers are typically designed as 2-way, 3-way, or 4-way speaker systems, depending on how many drivers and frequency ranges they handle. Most tower speakers operate within a frequency range of about 35 Hz to 20 kHz, covering the full spectrum of human hearing. They are usually connected to an amplifier or AV receiver through speaker wires, and their power handling capacity may range from 50W to 300W or more depending on the model.','Tower speakers are ideal for large rooms and home theatre setups because they can fill a space with rich and immersive sound. Proper placement is important; they should normally be positioned on the floor with some distance from the wall to avoid sound distortion. The cabinet is usually made from wood, MDF, or composite materials to reduce vibrations and improve audio clarity. Some models include built-in subwoofers or powered amplification, while others require an external amplifier.','In an audio system, tower speakers usually function as the main left and right channel speakers in a stereo or surround sound configuration. They connect to the amplifier output terminals using speaker cables and work together with other components such as subwoofers, center speakers, and AV receivers to create a complete audio system.','categories/1772623074794-490897483.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-04 11:17:54','2026-03-04 11:17:54'),
(574,1,19,15,'secondary',165,'Hall Effect Sensor Module','The Hall Effect Sensor Module is a magnetic field detection module used for sensing the presence, strength, and polarity of a magnetic field. ','It uses a high-sensitivity Hall Effect sensor that outputs a digital signal whenever a magnet comes near the sensing area.','Hall Effect Sensor Module','Hall Effect Sensor Module','categories/1772626749121-751184995.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-04 12:19:09','2026-03-04 12:19:09'),
(575,1,19,15,'secondary',165,'Optical dust sensor','An optical dust sensor is an electronic module used to detect and measure particulate matter (dust) in the air.','It works by using a light source and a photodetector—when dust particles pass through the sensor’s light beam, they scatter light, which is then detected and converted into an electrical signal proportional to dust concentration.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772627970025-927662236.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-04 12:39:30','2026-03-04 12:39:30'),
(576,1,19,15,'secondary',196,'Drone Motor with Set','Drone Motor with Set','Drone Motor with Set','Drone Motor with Set','Drone Motor with Set','categories/1772628267488-477238025.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-04 12:44:27','2026-03-04 12:44:27'),
(577,1,19,14,'secondary',9,'Speaker Wires','Speaker Wires','Speaker Wires',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772628592239-439060170.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-04 12:49:52','2026-03-04 12:49:52'),
(578,1,19,15,'secondary',165,'Joystick Module','The KY-023 Dual Axis Joystick module uses a uses a biaxial potentiometer to control the X and Y axis. When pushed down, it activates a switch. Based on the PS2 controller’s joystick, it’s used to control a wide range of projects from RC vehicles to color LEDs.','This module consists of two 10k? potentiometers perpendicularly placed to control the X and Y axes by changing resistance when moving the joystick. A push button is activated when the joystick is pushed down on the Z axis. It has 5 male header pins.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772629077913-527573277.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-04 12:57:57','2026-03-04 12:57:57'),
(579,1,19,15,'secondary',165,'Laser Diode','This low-cost Laser Diode or Laser Light is commonly used in security devices and pointers. This Red Laser diode is rated for 5mW with a nominal voltage between 2.2V and 3V. ','Just like other LED Diodes the Laser Diode should also be used with a driver circuit to limit the current through it. The wave length of Laser light normally range from 635nm to 66nm.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772629224256-850723481.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-04 13:00:24','2026-03-04 13:00:24'),
(580,1,19,15,'primary',NULL,'Project Cable & Connector','Project Cable & Connector','Project Cable & Connector',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772629718692-935158257.jpeg',0,1,'active','2026-03-04 13:08:38','2026-03-05 13:10:24'),
(581,1,19,15,'secondary',203,'Uno Cable','UNO Cable usually refers to the USB cable used with the Arduino UNO development board. This cable connects the Arduino UNO to a computer for programming, power, and serial communication.','The UNO cable isn’t a special board part — it’s simply the USB cable that connects your Arduino UNO to your computer for programming and power. If you need one, get a USB-A to USB-B cable (sometimes called a printer cable) unless your specific board uses a different USB connector.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772629797502-934693303.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-04 13:09:57','2026-03-04 13:09:57'),
(582,1,19,15,'secondary',196,'ynamo motor',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,1,'active','2026-03-05 05:44:42','2026-03-05 06:30:38'),
(583,1,19,15,'secondary',196,'Dynamo motor','A Dynamo Motor is a small electrical generator that converts mechanical energy into electrical energy using electromagnetic induction. When the shaft of the dynamo rotates, it produces electrical power that can be used to operate lights or charge small electronic devices. Dynamos are commonly used in bicycles, small generators, educational projects, and DIY electronics experiments.','In bicycles, a dynamo motor is usually connected to the wheel so that when the wheel rotates, the dynamo generates electricity to power front and rear lights. Small dynamo motors are also used in science projects and energy-generation demonstrations to show how motion can be converted into electricity.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772689635196-86852177.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-05 05:47:15','2026-03-05 05:47:15'),
(584,1,19,15,'secondary',196,'Plastic Gear Set','A Plastic Gear Set is a collection of small gears and mechanical components used to transfer motion and power between rotating parts. These sets usually include different types of gears such as spur gears, crown gears, worm gears, rack gears, pulleys, and axles, allowing users to build various gear mechanisms for mechanical and robotics projects',NULL,NULL,NULL,'categories/1772689975512-845727660.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-05 05:52:55','2026-03-05 05:52:55'),
(585,1,19,15,'secondary',196,'BO Motor','A BO Motor (Battery Operated Motor) is a small DC geared motor commonly used in robotics and DIY electronic projects. It converts electrical energy from a battery into mechanical rotation to drive wheels or mechanical parts. These motors are lightweight, low-cost, and designed to operate at low voltages such as 3V–12V, making them suitable for battery-powered devices',NULL,'BO motors usually include a plastic gearbox attached to a small DC motor. The gearbox reduces speed and increases torque, allowing the motor to move robot wheels or small machines effectively. Because of their simple design and good torque at low voltage, they are widely used in robot cars, educational kits, and science projects',NULL,'categories/1772692348553-662922074.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-05 06:32:28','2026-03-05 06:32:28'),
(586,1,19,15,'secondary',320,'chassis ','A Robot Chassis is the structural base or frame used to build a robot or robotic vehicle. It provides a platform to mount important components such as motors, wheels, batteries, sensors, motor drivers, and microcontrollers (like Arduino). Chassis kits are commonly made from materials such as acrylic, plastic, aluminum, or metal, which provide strength while keeping the robot lightweight.','Most robot chassis kits come with mounting holes and slots to easily attach BO motors, wheels, caster wheels, and electronic modules. They are widely used in robot car projects, line follower robots, obstacle avoiding robots, and educational robotics experiments.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1772693308297-662508367.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-05 06:48:28','2026-03-05 06:48:28'),
(587,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'PCT Connector','PCT Connector is a compact and reliable electrical wire connector used to join two or more electrical wires safely without soldering. It is commonly used in electrical installations, lighting systems, and electronic projects. The connector uses a spring clamp or lever mechanism to firmly hold the wire, ensuring a strong electrical connection while preventing loose contacts. PCT connectors are usually made from flame-retardant plastic housing with copper conductive parts, which helps provide durability and safety during operation.','PCT connectors are available in multiple models such as 2-pin, 3-pin, 4-pin, or 5-pin connectors, allowing multiple wires to be connected in a single compact unit. They are widely used in LED lighting systems, distribution boxes, electrical panels, and automation equipment because they simplify wiring and reduce installation time.','Most PCT connectors support voltage ratings up to 250V–450V and current ratings ranging from 24A to 32A, depending on the model. Their transparent or semi-transparent body design allows users to easily check whether the wire is inserted correctly.','PCT connectors highlight their key advantages such as tool-free installation, reusable design, and strong vibration resistance. They provide a safe connection that reduces the risk of short circuits or overheating compared to twisted wire joints. Proper wire stripping length must be maintained before inserting the wire to ensure a secure connection.','categories/1772705175460-566526648.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-05 10:06:15','2026-03-05 10:06:15'),
(588,1,20,22,'primary',NULL,'XT Connector','XT Connector is a high-current electrical connector widely used in battery-powered electronic systems such as RC vehicles, drones, robotics, and battery packs. The name XT refers to the series of connectors designed to handle high current transmission safely and efficiently. These connectors are typically made with high-temperature nylon plastic housing and gold-plated brass contacts, which provide excellent conductivity and durability.','XT connectors are polarized, meaning they are designed so they can only be connected in one direction, preventing reverse polarity and protecting electronic circuits from damage. They are commonly used to connect Li-Po batteries to electronic speed controllers (ESC), power distribution boards, and other high-power devices.','XT connectors are available in different types such as XT30, XT60, and XT90, where the number usually indicates the approximate maximum current rating. For example, XT30 is suitable for around 30A, XT60 for about 60A, and XT90 can support currents up to around 90A or more. These connectors are widely used in remote control cars, quadcopters, electric bikes, robotics systems, and battery charging setups.','XT connectors highlight their strong mechanical grip, low resistance connection, and high temperature resistance, making them reliable for demanding applications. They require soldering to attach wires, and proper insulation and soldering techniques should be used to ensure a safe connection.','categories/1772709395717-37115592.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-05 11:16:35','2026-03-05 11:16:35'),
(589,1,19,16,'secondary',212,'PVC Socket Wire','PVC Socket Wire is a commonly used electrical wire designed for connecting power sockets, electronic devices, and small electrical appliances. It is insulated with Polyvinyl Chloride (PVC) material, which provides good electrical insulation, flexibility, and protection against moisture, heat, and mechanical damage. PVC socket wires are widely used in household electrical systems, extension cords, adapters, and electronic power connections.','PVC socket wires are available in different connector types and configurations depending on the application. Two common types include V8 Socket Wire Type PVC and Type C Socket Wire Type PVC. The V8 Socket Wire Type PVC is typically used for devices that require a figure-8 style connector, often seen in small electronics such as audio systems, adapters, and LED devices. The Type C Socket Wire Type PVC is commonly used with Type-C style power connectors or small electronic charging systems that require stable and reliable power delivery.','PVC socket wires highlight their flexibility, lightweight design, and strong insulation properties. They are easy to install and handle during wiring or device assembly. Proper insulation thickness and good-quality copper conductors help reduce power loss and improve efficiency.','PVC socket wires play an important role in power distribution and device connectivity systems. They serve as the link between power outlets and electronic equipment, ensuring stable and safe electrical transmission.','categories/1772711149219-351295845.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-05 11:45:49','2026-03-05 11:45:49'),
(590,1,19,17,'secondary',215,'Cooling Fan','Cooling Fan is an electronic device used to reduce heat and maintain proper temperature in electrical and electronic systems. It works by rotating blades that move air across components, helping to dissipate heat generated during operation. Cooling fans are commonly used in computers, power supplies, amplifiers, LED systems, industrial equipment, and electronic circuits to prevent overheating and improve system performance.','Cooling fans come in various sizes, voltage ratings, and airflow capacities depending on the application. Common voltage types include 5V, 12V, and 24V DC fans, and sizes typically range from 30mm to 120mm or larger. They may include two or three wire connections for power and speed monitoring.','Cooling fans are widely used in computer cabinets, inverters, battery systems, control panels, and electronic enclosures where continuous airflow is required to maintain safe operating temperatures. Proper airflow helps protect sensitive components such as processors, power transistors, and voltage regulators.','From a system perspective, cooling fans are a key part of the thermal control system in electronic and electrical equipment. They work together with heat sinks, ventilation openings, and temperature control circuits to regulate internal temperatures. By maintaining proper airflow and heat dissipation, cooling fans improve the reliability, safety, and efficiency of systems such as computers, power electronics, industrial machines, and communication equipment, ensuring stable and continuous operation.','categories/1772713544539-569419559.jpeg',0,1,'active','2026-03-05 12:25:44','2026-03-05 12:41:54'),
(591,1,19,14,'primary',NULL,'Car Set Wire','Car Set Wire is a specially designed wiring harness used for connecting car audio systems such as stereos, speakers, amplifiers, and accessories to a vehicle’s electrical system. It typically consists of color-coded, insulated wires that simplify installation and ensure correct connections for power, ground, speakers, and control signals. The insulation is made to withstand heat, vibration, and electrical load commonly found in automotive environments.','Car set wires are widely used in car stereo installation, speaker upgrades, amplifier connections, and replacement of damaged or factory wiring. Designed for durability and reliable signal transmission, these wires help maintain clear audio output and stable power supply. ','The insulation is made to withstand heat, vibration, and electrical load commonly found in automotive environments.','Overall, car set wire provides a safe, organized, and efficient solution for automotive audio and electrical installations.','categories/1772715193770-416554199.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-05 12:53:13','2026-04-10 05:40:17'),
(592,1,19,15,'secondary',203,'Nano Cable','Nano Cable is a small USB cable commonly used to connect an Arduino Nano development board to a computer or power source. This cable usually has a USB Type-A connector on one end and a Mini-USB connector on the other end, allowing communication between the computer and the Nano board. The Nano cable is used for programming, data transfer, and power supply to the microcontroller.','Nano cable supports both power transmission and serial data communication between the microcontroller and a computer. It typically operates with a 5V power supply from the USB port and also enables communication through USB-to-Serial converters such as the CH340 or FT232 chips present on many Nano boards.','These cables are widely used in robotics, IoT projects, sensor systems, automation systems, and educational electronics projects. The cable length usually ranges from 30 cm to 1 meter, providing enough flexibility for development setups.','Nano cables highlight that they are essential for programming and debugging Arduino Nano boards. A good quality cable ensures stable data transfer and reliable power delivery. Some USB cables only provide power but not data transfer, so it is important to use a data-capable USB cable when uploading programs. The cable should also be handled carefully to avoid damage to the connectors or internal wires.','categories/1772716356644-963674721.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-05 13:12:36','2026-03-05 13:12:36'),
(593,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'DC Power Supply Adapter','A Power Supply Adapter is an electronic device used to convert electrical power from one form to another so that electronic devices can operate safely and efficiently. It typically converts high-voltage AC power from a wall outlet into low-voltage DC power required by devices such as routers, LED lights, audio equipment, microcontrollers, and other electronic circuits. Power supply adapters are available in various voltage and current ratings such as 5V, 9V, 12V, or 24V, depending on the device requirements. They usually come with a plug connector that fits the power input socket of the device.','Power supply adapters are commonly used in home electronics, computer peripherals, CCTV systems, and DIY electronics projects. They consist of internal components like a transformer, rectifier, filter capacitors, and voltage regulation circuits that stabilize the output voltage. Modern adapters are usually switching power supplies (SMPS), which are compact, lightweight, and energy efficient compared to older linear adapters. The adapter label generally displays important specifications such as input voltage, output voltage, current rating, polarity, and power rating to ensure compatibility with the connected device.','When using a power supply adapter, it is important to match the correct voltage and polarity required by the device to avoid damage. The current rating of the adapter should be equal to or higher than the device’s required current.','Power supply adapter is categorized as a power management component used to provide external power to electronic modules or devices. It is commonly listed with specifications such as input range, output voltage, current capacity, connector type, and efficiency rating. For system integration, selecting a stable and reliable adapter ensures consistent power delivery, protects circuits from voltage fluctuations, and improves the overall reliability and lifespan of the connected electronic equipment.','categories/1772803979023-602844931.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-06 10:37:11','2026-04-10 05:27:50'),
(594,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'2 Yard Power Cable','A 2 Yard Power Cable is an electrical cable designed to supply power from a wall outlet to electronic devices and equipment. The cable has a length of 2 yards (approximately 1.8 meters), providing convenient reach between the power source and the device. It is commonly used for connecting devices such as televisions, computers, monitors, printers, audio systems, power adapters, and other household or electronic equipment.','A 2 yard power cable usually includes standard AC power connectors, such as a two-pin or three-pin plug on one end and a compatible connector on the other end depending on the device type. The copper conductors inside the cable provide efficient electrical conductivity, while the insulation protects against electrical leakage and external damage.','These cables are designed to handle standard household voltages such as 110V–240V AC, making them suitable for many electronic appliances and devices.','When using a 2 yard power cable, ensure that the cable is compatible with the device and rated for the required voltage and current. Avoid bending the cable sharply or placing heavy objects on it, as this can damage the internal wires.','categories/1772804504095-256724299.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-06 13:41:44','2026-04-10 04:32:09'),
(595,35,18,25,'primary',NULL,'Network Device','A router is a networking device that connects multiple networks together and directs data packets between them. It commonly connects a local network (LAN) to the internet.','Routers assign IP addresses, manage traffic, and allow multiple devices to share one internet connection.','Used in homes, offices, and enterprises\r\nSupports wired and wireless connections\r\nOften includes firewall and DHCP features\r\n\r\n','Default IP usually: 192.168.0.1 or 192.168.1.1\r\nConfigure through web interface\r\nSecure with strong admin password','categories/1772811381749-766079832.png',0,1,'active','2026-03-06 15:36:21','2026-04-03 07:44:59'),
(596,35,18,25,'primary',NULL,'Modems','A modem (Modulator–Demodulator) is a networking device that enables computers, routers, and other digital devices to connect to the internet by converting data between digital signals and the signals used by internet service providers (ISPs).','A modem is the critical gateway device that connects local networks to the internet by translating ISP signals into usable digital data.','Modem is mandatory for accessing internet services from an ISP. Must be compatible with the ISP’s technology (DSL, Cable, Fiber, or Wireless). A modem alone provides internet access but does not create Wi-Fi unless it includes a router. Modem–router combo devices save space and reduce cabling. Speed performance depends on modem standard and ISP plan. Should be powered continuously for stable connectivity. Proper ventilation helps prevent overheating. Indicator LEDs show power, internet status, and data activity. Firmware updates improve stability and security. Commonly used in homes, offices, and commercial networks.','Modems serve as the core connection point between users and their internet service provider, making them essential for reliable broadband connectivity.','categories/1772814604176-496824849.png',1,1,'active','2026-03-06 16:28:35','2026-04-10 05:28:32'),
(597,1,19,20,'secondary',10,'Extension Plug','An extension plug is an electrical accessory used to extend the reach of a power source by connecting electrical devices to a power outlet through an extension cable. It is designed with insulated pins and a durable outer body, usually made of high-quality plastic or fire-resistant material, to ensure safety and reliability. Extension plugs are commonly used in homes, offices, workshops, and electronic service centers to power multiple appliances or devices when the original socket is not easily accessible.','Extension plugs are widely used for connecting electrical equipment like televisions, computers, chargers, power adapters, soldering irons, and other household or electronic devices. They are typically compatible with standard AC power supplies such as 220–240V used in many countries including India. The internal wiring of the plug is designed to securely hold the cable and maintain proper electrical contact with the socket pins.','When using an extension plug, it is important to ensure that the current rating of the plug matches the connected device to prevent overheating or electrical damage. Always use good quality cables and properly tighten the internal connections during installation. Avoid using extension plugs in wet environments or with damaged wires. Regular inspection of the plug and cable can help maintain safety and prevent electrical hazards.','Extension plugs are essential components in electrical and electronic systems where temporary or flexible power connections are required. They are widely used in power distribution setups, repair stations, laboratories, and household electrical arrangements. Proper installation and safe handling of extension plugs ensure efficient power delivery, device protection, and reduced risk of short circuits or electrical failures.','categories/1772877283937-545314854.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 09:54:43','2026-03-07 09:54:43'),
(598,1,19,20,'secondary',10,'International Adapter','An international adapter is a travel-friendly electrical accessory designed to allow electronic devices to be connected to power outlets in different countries with varying plug types and socket standards. It converts the physical shape of a plug so that it can fit into foreign power outlets without changing the voltage of the electricity. International adapters are commonly used by travelers to power devices such as mobile phone chargers, laptops, cameras, and other electronic gadgets when visiting countries with different plug configurations.','International adapters typically support multiple plug standards such as US, UK, EU, and AU types, making them compatible with power sockets in many regions around the world. They are usually made from high-quality heat-resistant plastic with metal contact pins to ensure durability and safe electrical conduction. Some models include built-in USB ports, surge protection, safety shutters, and fuse protection to enhance functionality and device safety.','It is important to note that an international adapter does not convert voltage; it only changes the plug shape. Therefore, users must ensure that their electronic device supports the local voltage before plugging it in. Always check the power rating of the adapter and avoid connecting high-power appliances like heaters or hair dryers unless the adapter is specifically designed for such loads. Use the adapter in dry environments and handle it carefully to prevent damage to the internal contacts.','International adapters play a crucial role in global connectivity by enabling electronic devices to operate across different electrical systems. They are widely used by travelers, business professionals, and technicians who frequently work with international equipment. A well-designed adapter ensures secure connections, stable power delivery, and compatibility with multiple socket standards, making it an essential accessory for international travel and global electronic device usage.','categories/1772877518264-936636147.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 09:58:38','2026-03-07 09:58:38'),
(599,1,19,20,'secondary',431,'Socket Type Switch','A Project Socket Type Switch is an electrical component commonly used in electronic projects, DIY circuits, and prototype boards to control the flow of electrical power to connected devices. It combines a socket connection with a switch mechanism, allowing users to easily turn power on or off without disconnecting the power source. These switches are widely used in electronic labs, hobby projects, robotics, and embedded systems where controlled power distribution is required.','Project socket type switches are typically designed to work with AC or DC power sources depending on the model. They are made with durable plastic housings and metal internal contacts to ensure proper conductivity and safety. Many of these switches are compatible with standard project boards, power modules, and adapters, making them suitable for testing and development environments. They may come in different designs such as rocker switches, toggle switches, or push switches integrated with a power socket for easy connection.','When using a project socket type switch, ensure that the voltage and current ratings match the requirements of the connected device or circuit. Proper wiring and insulation are important to avoid short circuits or electrical damage. It is recommended to mount the switch securely on the project enclosure or board to maintain stability and prevent loose connections. Always test the switch functionality before connecting sensitive electronic components.','In electronic systems and development environments, project socket type switches help provide convenient and safe power control. They are commonly used in prototype setups, educational projects, automation systems, and experimental circuits. By allowing quick power switching and secure socket connections, these components improve system usability, safety, and flexibility during testing and development stages.','categories/1772877833020-768979670.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 10:03:53','2026-03-07 10:03:53'),
(600,1,19,20,'secondary',431,'On/Off Switch','An On/Off switch is a basic electrical control device used to start or stop the flow of electricity in an electrical or electronic circuit. It functions by either completing the circuit (ON position) to allow current to flow or breaking the circuit (OFF position) to stop the current. On/Off switches are widely used in household appliances, electronic devices, power supplies, lighting systems, and industrial equipment to provide simple and reliable control of electrical power.','On/Off switches are available in different types such as rocker switches, toggle switches, push-button switches, and slide switches depending on the application. They are typically made with durable plastic or metal housings and conductive internal contacts that ensure efficient electrical connectivity. These switches support various voltage and current ratings and can be used in both AC and DC circuits. Many On/Off switches also include features like indicator lights, waterproof designs, and panel mounting options for easy installation.','When selecting an On/Off switch, it is important to consider the voltage and current rating to match the device or circuit requirements. Using a switch with a lower rating than required may cause overheating or failure. Ensure proper wiring and insulation during installation to prevent short circuits or electrical hazards. Regular inspection and maintenance can help ensure long-term reliability and safe operation.','In electrical and electronic systems, On/Off switches play a critical role in power management and device control. They allow users to safely operate equipment, conserve energy, and protect circuits from unnecessary power usage. Because of their simple design and reliable performance, On/Off switches are essential components in consumer electronics, electrical installations, and various engineering applications.','categories/1772878025515-444675504.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 10:07:05','2026-03-07 10:07:05'),
(601,1,19,20,'secondary',431,'Push Button','A push button is a simple electrical switch that is activated by pressing a button to control the flow of electricity in a circuit. When the button is pressed, it either completes or interrupts the circuit depending on the switch type, and when released it usually returns to its original position using a spring mechanism. Push buttons are widely used in electronic devices, control panels, doorbells, calculators, industrial machines, and automation systems to provide quick and easy user input or control.','Push buttons are available in different types such as momentary push buttons (which work only while pressed) and latching push buttons (which remain in the pressed state until pressed again). They are typically made with durable plastic or metal housings and metal contact terminals for reliable electrical connection. Push buttons can be used in both low-voltage electronic circuits and higher voltage electrical systems depending on their rating. Some push buttons also include LED indicators, waterproof designs, or panel-mount structures for different applications.','When using a push button switch, it is important to select one with the correct voltage and current rating suitable for the circuit. Proper wiring and secure mounting should be ensured to avoid loose connections or electrical faults. In electronic projects, push buttons are often connected with resistors or microcontrollers for input control. Regular inspection can help maintain proper operation and prevent wear or damage.','Push buttons are essential control components in many electrical and electronic systems. They provide simple manual control for starting, stopping, or triggering operations in devices and machinery. Due to their compact size, reliability, and ease of use, push buttons are commonly used in automation systems, consumer electronics, industrial equipment, and DIY electronic projects.','categories/1772878182565-510754762.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 10:09:42','2026-03-07 10:09:42'),
(602,1,20,23,'primary',NULL,'Tester','A tester is a basic electrical tool used to check the presence of voltage or electrical current in a wire, socket, or electrical device. It is commonly used by electricians, technicians, and hobbyists to identify live wires and ensure safe electrical connections. A typical tester consists of a metal probe tip, an insulated handle, and an internal indicator such as a small neon lamp or LED that lights up when voltage is detected. Testers are widely used for troubleshooting electrical circuits and verifying power supply in household and industrial electrical systems.','Electrical testers are designed to detect AC voltage in electrical outlets, switches, extension boards, and wiring systems. The probe tip is placed on the conductor or socket terminal while the user touches the metal contact at the end of the tester to complete a small circuit through the body. When voltage is present, the indicator inside the tester glows, confirming that the line is live. Testers are usually compatible with standard voltage ranges such as 100V–250V AC, which makes them suitable for most residential electrical systems.','While using a tester, always ensure that the handle insulation is intact and dry to prevent electric shock. The tester should be used carefully and only for checking voltage presence, not for measuring exact electrical values like current or resistance. Avoid using damaged testers or those with loose components. Proper handling and storage of the tester help maintain safety and reliability during electrical testing.','In electrical maintenance and installation systems, testers are essential diagnostic tools used to identify live circuits and verify electrical connections before performing repair or installation work. They help improve safety by preventing accidental contact with live wires and assist technicians in troubleshooting electrical faults quickly and efficiently. Testers are widely used in electrical workshops, construction sites, repair centers, and household electrical maintenance.','categories/1772878368476-416132877.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 10:12:48','2026-03-07 10:12:48'),
(603,1,20,23,'primary',NULL,'Insulation Tape','Insulation tape, also known as electrical tape, is a type of pressure-sensitive adhesive tape used to insulate electrical wires and other conductive materials. It is commonly made from flexible materials such as PVC (polyvinyl chloride) that provide good electrical insulation and durability. Insulation tape is widely used in electrical installations, wiring repairs, and electronic projects to protect wires from short circuits, moisture, and environmental damage while ensuring safe electrical connections.','Insulation tape is designed to withstand electrical voltage and provide strong insulation for exposed wires and cable joints. It is flexible, stretchable, and easy to wrap around irregular shapes, making it suitable for various electrical applications. The tape is available in multiple colors such as black, red, blue, yellow, and green, which are often used for wire identification and phase marking in electrical systems. High-quality insulation tapes also offer resistance to heat, abrasion, and chemicals, ensuring long-lasting protection.','When using insulation tape, ensure the wire connection is properly twisted or secured before wrapping the tape. Wrap the tape tightly and evenly around the exposed area to provide complete insulation and protection. Avoid using damaged or low-quality tape, as it may lose adhesion or insulation properties over time. Store insulation tape in a cool and dry place to maintain its adhesive strength and flexibility.','Insulation tape plays an important role in electrical safety and maintenance by preventing electrical leakage, short circuits, and accidental contact with live wires. It is widely used in residential wiring, industrial electrical systems, electronic repair work, and DIY electrical projects. Proper use of insulation tape helps maintain reliable electrical connections and improves the overall safety of electrical installations.','categories/1772878616762-242450307.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 10:16:56','2026-03-07 10:16:56'),
(604,1,20,23,'primary',NULL,'Screwdriver','A screwdriver is a hand tool used to tighten or loosen screws in various mechanical, electrical, and electronic applications. It consists of a handle and a metal shaft with a specially shaped tip designed to fit into the head of a screw. Screwdrivers are essential tools in repair work, assembly tasks, and maintenance activities. They are widely used in households, workshops, electronic repair centers, and industrial environments for installing or removing screws from different types of equipment and devices.','Screwdrivers are available in many types depending on the screw head design, such as flat-head (slotted), Phillips, Torx, and hex screwdrivers. The handle is usually made from plastic, rubber, or insulated material to provide a comfortable grip and safety during use. Some screwdrivers are specially designed with insulated handles to protect users when working with electrical components. Screwdrivers also come in various sizes to match different screw dimensions and applications, including precision screwdrivers used for small electronic devices.','When using a screwdriver, always choose the correct type and size that matches the screw head to avoid damaging the screw or the tool. Apply steady pressure while turning the screwdriver to ensure proper grip and prevent slipping. For electrical work, insulated screwdrivers should be used to reduce the risk of electric shock. Keeping screwdrivers clean and storing them properly helps maintain their performance and durability.','In electrical and mechanical systems, screwdrivers are essential tools for assembling, repairing, and maintaining equipment. They are commonly used in electronic device servicing, electrical installations, automotive repair, and general hardware work. Because of their simplicity and effectiveness, screwdrivers remain one of the most important and frequently used tools in technical and maintenance operations.','categories/1772879079194-108226298.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 10:24:39','2026-03-07 10:24:39'),
(605,1,20,23,'primary',NULL,'Wire Cutter','A wire cutter is a hand tool designed specifically for cutting electrical wires, cables, and small metal wires with precision and ease. It typically consists of two sharp cutting edges joined by a pivot, along with insulated handles that provide a firm grip and safety during operation. Wire cutters are widely used by electricians, technicians, and electronic hobbyists for cutting and trimming wires during electrical installations, repairs, and electronic assembly work.','Wire cutters are usually made from hardened steel to ensure durability and sharp cutting performance. The handles are commonly coated with plastic or rubber insulation to provide comfort and protection while working with electrical components. Some wire cutters are designed with additional features such as wire stripping sections or crimping areas, allowing users to perform multiple tasks with a single tool. They are suitable for cutting copper, aluminum, and other soft metal wires used in electrical and electronic applications.','When using a wire cutter, ensure the tool is suitable for the thickness and type of wire being cut to avoid damaging the blades. Do not use wire cutters on hardened steel or materials beyond their rated capacity, as this can damage the cutting edges. Always handle the tool carefully and store it in a dry place to prevent rust and maintain sharpness. Regular cleaning and occasional lubrication of the pivot joint help extend the tool’s lifespan.','Wire cutters are essential tools in electrical and electronic systems for preparing wires during installation, repair, and maintenance tasks. They help ensure clean and accurate cuts, which are important for proper electrical connections and circuit reliability. Due to their efficiency and versatility, wire cutters are commonly used in electrical workshops, industrial maintenance, telecommunications, and DIY electronics projects.','categories/1772879335395-585872733.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 10:28:55','2026-03-07 10:28:55'),
(606,1,20,23,'primary',NULL,'Knife','A knife is a versatile hand tool used for cutting, trimming, and shaping various materials such as wires, cables, insulation, plastic, and packaging. In electrical and electronic work, knives are commonly used to strip wire insulation, cut cable jackets, and prepare materials during installation or repair tasks. A typical knife consists of a sharp metal blade and a handle designed to provide a firm and comfortable grip for precise cutting.','Knives used in electrical and technical work are often designed with strong stainless steel or carbon steel blades to ensure durability and sharpness. The handle is usually made from plastic, rubber, or other non-slip materials to provide safety and better control while cutting. Some knives also feature retractable blades or replaceable blade systems, allowing users to maintain sharp cutting performance over time. They are widely used by electricians, technicians, craftsmen, and DIY enthusiasts in various maintenance and assembly applications.','When using a knife, it is important to handle it carefully to prevent accidental cuts or injuries. Always cut away from the body and ensure a stable grip on the material being cut. Use a sharp blade for clean and efficient cutting, as dull blades require more force and may cause slipping. Store the knife safely when not in use and replace damaged or worn blades to maintain proper performance and safety.','In electrical and mechanical systems, knives are essential tools for preparing materials and assisting in installation or repair tasks. They are frequently used in wiring work, cable preparation, packaging removal, and general workshop activities. A well-maintained knife improves efficiency, accuracy, and safety during technical and maintenance operations.','categories/1774949286296-78015898.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 10:34:25','2026-03-31 09:28:06'),
(607,1,19,16,'secondary',212,'NeckBand','A neckband is a type of wireless audio device designed to be worn comfortably around the neck while providing high-quality sound through connected earbuds. It is commonly used for listening to music, making phone calls, and attending online meetings without the need for wired connections. Neckbands use Bluetooth technology to connect with smartphones, tablets, laptops, and other compatible devices, offering convenience and mobility for everyday use.','Neckband earphones typically consist of a flexible band that rests around the neck, with earbuds connected by short wires. The neckband houses important components such as the battery, Bluetooth module, control buttons, and sometimes a microphone for hands-free calling. Most neckbands support features like noise reduction, magnetic earbuds, voice assistant compatibility, and long battery life that can last several hours on a single charge. They usually charge through USB ports such as Micro-USB or USB Type-C.','When using a neckband, it is important to charge the battery regularly and avoid exposing the device to water, excessive heat, or physical damage. Keeping the earbuds clean helps maintain sound quality and hygiene. Users should also ensure the device is paired properly with their smartphone or audio device to avoid connectivity issues. Proper storage and careful handling can extend the life of the neckband.','Neckbands are widely used in modern wireless audio systems due to their comfort, portability, and reliable Bluetooth connectivity. They are suitable for activities such as commuting, exercising, working, and entertainment. Because of their lightweight design and convenient controls, neckband earphones have become a popular alternative to traditional wired headphones and fully wireless earbuds.','categories/1772879801289-61721662.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 10:36:41','2026-03-07 10:36:41'),
(608,1,19,16,'secondary',212,'Earphones','Earphones are compact audio devices designed to deliver sound directly into the ears for personal listening. They are commonly used with smartphones, tablets, computers, music players, and other audio devices to listen to music, watch videos, play games, or make voice calls. Earphones are small, lightweight, and portable, making them convenient for everyday use at home, work, or while traveling.','Earphones are available in both wired and wireless types. Wired earphones usually connect through a 3.5mm audio jack or USB port, while wireless earphones use Bluetooth technology to connect with devices. They typically include small speakers called drivers that produce sound, along with cables or wireless modules and sometimes an in-line microphone and control buttons for managing calls and music playback. Many modern earphones also include features such as noise isolation, high-definition audio output, and comfortable silicone ear tips for better fit and sound quality.','When using earphones, it is recommended to keep the volume at a safe level to protect hearing health. Regularly cleaning the ear tips helps maintain hygiene and sound clarity. Avoid pulling the cable forcefully in wired earphones to prevent damage. Proper storage in a case or pouch can help protect the earphones from dust, moisture, and tangling.','Earphones play an important role in personal audio systems by providing a private listening experience without disturbing others. They are widely used for communication, entertainment, online learning, and professional tasks such as voice recording or video conferencing. Due to their compact design and easy connectivity, earphones remain one of the most popular accessories in modern electronic devices.','categories/1772879989276-895157490.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 10:39:49','2026-03-07 10:39:49'),
(609,1,19,16,'secondary',212,'Mobile Stand','A mobile stand is a small support accessory designed to hold a smartphone in a stable and upright position. It allows users to place their mobile device on a desk, table, or other flat surface for convenient viewing and hands-free operation. Mobile stands are commonly used for watching videos, attending online meetings, video calls, reading, gaming, or charging the phone while keeping it easily accessible.','Mobile stands are typically made from materials such as plastic, metal, silicone, or acrylic to provide durability and stability. They are available in various designs, including adjustable stands, foldable stands, and desktop holders that support both vertical and horizontal phone positions. Some models include features like anti-slip pads, charging cable slots, adjustable viewing angles, and compact foldable structures for easy portability. Mobile stands are compatible with most smartphone sizes and are widely used in homes, offices, and workstations.','When using a mobile stand, ensure that the device is placed securely to avoid slipping or falling. Choose a stand that supports the size and weight of your smartphone for better stability. Avoid placing the stand on uneven or slippery surfaces. Regular cleaning of the stand helps maintain its grip and appearance.','Mobile stands are practical accessories that improve convenience and ergonomics when using smartphones. They help users maintain better viewing angles, reduce the need to hold the phone for long periods, and support multitasking during work or entertainment. Because of their simple design and functionality, mobile stands are widely used in personal, educational, and professional environments.','categories/1772880505925-507920889.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 10:48:25','2026-03-07 10:48:25'),
(610,1,19,16,'secondary',212,'Silicone Earbuds','Silicone earbuds are soft ear tips made from flexible silicone material that are designed to fit over the speaker end of earphones or in-ear headphones. They help provide a comfortable fit inside the ear while improving sound quality and noise isolation. Silicone earbuds create a gentle seal in the ear canal, which helps deliver clearer audio and better bass performance during music listening, calls, or other audio activities.','Silicone earbuds are widely used in in-ear earphones and wireless earbuds. They are typically made from high-quality, skin-friendly silicone that is soft, durable, and reusable. These earbuds come in different sizes such as small, medium, and large to fit different ear shapes and provide a secure fit. Many modern earphones include multiple silicone earbud sizes so users can choose the most comfortable option. Silicone earbuds also help reduce external noise by providing passive noise isolation, improving the overall listening experience.','To maintain hygiene and sound quality, silicone earbuds should be cleaned regularly using a soft cloth or mild cleaning solution. Avoid using sharp objects that may damage the silicone material. If the earbuds become worn, loose, or damaged, they should be replaced to maintain comfort and audio performance. Proper storage of earphones with silicone earbuds can help prevent dust and dirt buildup.','Silicone earbuds are essential accessories in personal audio systems as they enhance comfort, fit, and sound performance of in-ear earphones. They are widely used in consumer electronics, mobile accessories, and professional audio equipment. By providing better sealing and noise isolation, silicone earbuds improve audio clarity and ensure a more enjoyable listening experience.','categories/1772880646784-236291980.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 10:50:46','2026-03-07 10:50:46'),
(611,1,19,16,'secondary',212,'Smart Watch & Charger','A smart watch is a wearable electronic device designed to be worn on the wrist that provides various digital features such as time display, fitness tracking, notifications, and connectivity with smartphones. It combines the functionality of a traditional wristwatch with advanced smart technology, allowing users to monitor health data, receive calls or messages, and control certain smartphone functions directly from the watch. A smart watch charger is an accessory used to recharge the battery of the smartwatch, ensuring continuous operation and reliable performance.','Smart watches are equipped with features such as heart rate monitoring, step counting, sleep tracking, GPS tracking, and smartphone notifications. Many models also support Bluetooth connectivity, touchscreen displays, and compatibility with mobile operating systems such as Android or iOS. The charger used for smart watches is usually a magnetic or dock-style charger that connects easily to the watch for safe and efficient charging. Most smart watches are powered by rechargeable lithium-ion batteries and are charged through USB cables connected to adapters, laptops, or power banks.','When using a smart watch and its charger, it is important to use the compatible charging cable or dock provided for the specific model. Avoid exposing the device to water or extreme heat while charging. Keep the charging contacts clean and ensure proper alignment with the charger to maintain efficient power transfer. Regular charging and proper handling help extend the battery life and maintain the overall performance of the smart watch.','Smart watches and their chargers are important components of modern wearable technology systems. They provide users with convenient access to health monitoring, communication, and smart device integration. The charger ensures that the device remains powered for daily activities, fitness tracking, and digital connectivity, making the smart watch a valuable accessory in personal technology and mobile ecosystems.','categories/1772880800810-349345215.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 10:53:20','2026-03-07 10:53:20'),
(612,1,19,16,'secondary',212,'USB Wireless Dongle','A USB wireless dongle is a small device that connects to a computer or other compatible device through a USB port to provide wireless communication capabilities. It is commonly used to enable Wi-Fi or Bluetooth connectivity in devices that do not have built-in wireless support. USB wireless dongles are compact, portable, and easy to use, making them a convenient solution for connecting laptops, desktops, and other electronic devices to wireless networks or peripherals.','USB wireless dongles typically support technologies such as Wi-Fi or Bluetooth depending on the type of dongle. A Wi-Fi dongle allows a computer to connect to wireless internet networks, while a Bluetooth dongle enables wireless communication with devices such as keyboards, mice, speakers, headphones, and smartphones. These dongles usually operate through plug-and-play functionality, meaning they can be connected directly to the USB port and automatically recognized by the operating system. They are compatible with many systems including Windows, Linux, and sometimes macOS.','When using a USB wireless dongle, ensure that the device drivers are properly installed if required by the operating system. For better signal performance, the dongle should be connected to a USB port that is not obstructed by metal surfaces or other electronic interference. It is also recommended to safely remove the dongle when not in use to prevent physical damage to the USB connector.','USB wireless dongles are widely used in computer networking and peripheral connectivity systems. They provide a simple and cost-effective way to add wireless functionality to devices without internal wireless hardware. Because of their portability and easy installation, USB wireless dongles are commonly used in homes, offices, and technical environments for wireless internet access and device connectivity.','categories/1772881086207-622606186.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 10:58:06','2026-03-07 10:58:06'),
(613,1,19,16,'secondary',212,'Selfie Stick','A selfie stick is a portable handheld accessory designed to hold a smartphone or small camera at an extended distance to capture wider selfies, group photos, and videos. It usually consists of a telescopic rod, an adjustable phone holder clamp, and a handle with a shutter control button. Many modern selfie sticks connect to smartphones through Bluetooth, allowing users to take photos remotely without touching the phone screen.','Some basic models use a wired connection through the 3.5 mm audio jack, while advanced models may include a built-in tripod stand, 360° rotating head, and adjustable angles for better framing. Selfie sticks are widely used for travel photography, vlogging, social media content creation, and video recording, making it easier to capture stable and wider shots.','Selfie sticks are typically made from lightweight aluminum or stainless steel with a plastic or rubber grip for comfortable handling. They are compatible with most Android and iOS smartphones and can extend from about 20 cm to over 100 cm depending on the model. The phone holder usually has rubber pads to prevent slipping or scratches. Some models include a detachable Bluetooth remote, allowing the user to place the stick on a tripod and capture photos from a distance.','The selfie stick operates as a simple mechanical extension device with optional electronic control. In Bluetooth models, the internal remote pairs with the smartphone and sends a camera shutter command when the button is pressed. Power is usually supplied by a small rechargeable lithium battery or coin cell battery inside the handle. For wired versions, the shutter button sends a signal through the audio jack interface to trigger the camera application.','categories/1772881433514-189235025.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 11:03:53','2026-03-07 11:03:53'),
(614,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Lights','Lights are devices used to produce illumination so that objects and surroundings can be clearly seen in dark or low-light conditions. They convert electrical energy into visible light using different technologies such as incandescent bulbs, fluorescent lamps, LED lights, halogen lamps, and CFL lamps. Lights are widely used in homes, offices, streets, vehicles, industries, and electronic devices for visibility, safety, decoration, and signaling.','Modern lighting systems mainly use LED technology because it consumes less power, produces less heat, and has a longer lifespan compared to traditional bulbs. Lights may be installed in ceiling fixtures, lamps, panels, floodlights, tube lights, and portable lighting devices depending on the application.','Lighting devices come in different brightness levels (lumens), power ratings (watts), and color temperatures such as warm white, cool white, and daylight. LED lights are preferred for energy efficiency and durability, while decorative lights are used for events, festivals, and interior design. Proper wiring, correct voltage supply, and the use of suitable holders or fixtures are important for safe operation.','A lighting system typically includes a power source, switch or control circuit, wiring, and the light unit itself. When electricity flows through the light component (such as a filament or LED semiconductor), energy is converted into light. In LED lights, a driver circuit regulates the current and voltage to protect the LEDs and ensure stable brightness. Some advanced lighting systems include dimmers, motion sensors, timers, or smart controllers that allow automatic or remote operation.','categories/1773065246931-439236550.png',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 11:08:50','2026-03-09 14:15:07'),
(615,1,19,20,'secondary',614,'Torch Light','A torch light (flashlight) is a portable handheld lighting device used to provide illumination in dark areas. It typically consists of a light source (usually LED), batteries, a switch, and a protective outer casing. Torch lights are widely used for emergency lighting, outdoor activities, repair work, security, and household use. Earlier torch lights used incandescent bulbs, but modern models mainly use LED lights because they consume less power, produce brighter light, and last much longer.','Modern torch lights are often powered by AA, AAA, lithium-ion rechargeable batteries, or built-in rechargeable battery packs. Many models include additional features like multiple brightness modes, zoom focus, waterproof design, and USB charging. High-power LED torches can produce very bright light and are commonly used in camping, security patrol, emergency rescue, and technical work. The outer body is usually made of plastic, aluminum, or metal alloy to protect the internal components and improve durability.','Always ensure the correct battery type and polarity when inserting batteries into the torch light. Avoid leaving batteries inside the torch for a long time if it is not in use, as leakage can damage the device. Recharge rechargeable models properly using the recommended charger. Keep the lens clean for better brightness and avoid dropping the torch from height to prevent internal damage.','The torch light works through a simple electrical circuit consisting of a battery (power source), switch, LED or bulb (light source), and connecting wires or contacts. When the switch is turned on, the circuit closes and electrical energy flows from the battery to the LED, producing light. In LED torches, a small driver circuit may regulate the current to protect the LED and maintain stable brightness.','categories/1772882252837-371857302.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 11:17:32','2026-03-07 11:17:32'),
(616,1,19,20,'secondary',614,'USB Light','A USB light is a small portable lighting device that operates using power supplied through a USB port. It is commonly used with laptops, desktop computers, power banks, USB adapters, and mobile chargers to provide convenient lighting in dark environments. USB lights usually use energy-efficient LED technology, which produces bright illumination while consuming very little power. Many models are designed with a flexible neck or adjustable head, allowing the user to direct the light to a specific area such as a keyboard, desk, or workspace.','USB lights are lightweight and compact, making them easy to carry in bags or pockets. They typically operate on a 5V DC power supply, which is the standard voltage provided by USB ports. Some models include features like touch switches, brightness control, color lighting modes, or foldable designs. Because of their low power consumption, they are ideal for use with power banks and portable devices for extended periods without draining much energy.','Always ensure the USB port provides the correct 5V output to avoid damage to the light. Do not bend the flexible neck excessively, as repeated stress may damage internal wires. Keep the USB connector clean and free from dust or moisture for proper electrical contact. USB lights are mainly designed for close-range illumination, so they may not provide sufficient brightness for large areas.','A USB light works using a simple electronic circuit powered directly by the 5V supply from the USB port. When the USB connector is plugged into a device, electrical power flows to the LED light module. In many designs, a small resistor or driver circuit regulates the current to protect the LED from overcurrent. When the switch is activated, the circuit completes and the LED emits light. The flexible or adjustable structure helps position the light effectively, while the low power requirement ensures efficient operation with most USB-powered devices.','categories/1772882880707-529126419.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 11:28:00','2026-03-07 11:28:00'),
(617,1,19,20,'secondary',614,'Ring Light','A Ring Light is a circular lighting device designed to provide uniform and shadow-free illumination for photography, videography, live streaming, makeup application, and content creation. It typically consists of LED lights arranged in a circular frame with a mounting space in the center for a camera or smartphone. The ring design helps distribute light evenly on the subject, reducing harsh shadows and improving brightness and clarity.','Ring lights are available in different sizes and power ratings, usually ranging from small portable USB-powered models to larger studio-grade lights with adjustable brightness and color temperature. Many ring lights include features such as dimming control, warm and cool light modes, phone holders, tripod stands, and remote controls.','Ring lights should be positioned directly in front of the subject to achieve the best lighting effect. Adjust the brightness level according to the environment to avoid overexposure. Ensure the tripod or stand is stable before use. Avoid touching the LED surface while the device is powered on, and always use the recommended power adapter or USB source to prevent damage.','Ring lights are commonly used by photographers, vloggers, beauty professionals, and online educators to achieve professional-quality lighting.','categories/1772883950591-743999634.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 11:45:50','2026-03-07 11:45:50'),
(618,1,19,20,'secondary',614,'LED Spotlight','An LED Spotlight is a focused lighting device that uses Light Emitting Diodes (LEDs) to produce a concentrated beam of light for highlighting specific areas or objects. It is commonly used for indoor and outdoor lighting applications such as stage lighting, display lighting, architectural lighting, and security illumination. LED spotlights are designed to provide bright and efficient lighting while consuming less power compared to traditional halogen or incandescent spotlights. They are compact, durable, and provide instant illumination with minimal heat generation.','LED spotlights are available in various wattages, beam angles, and color temperatures to suit different lighting needs. They can be used in homes, commercial spaces, gardens, and shops to highlight decorations, signboards, artwork, or landscape features. Many models are equipped with adjustable heads that allow users to direct light precisely where it is needed. LED technology ensures longer lifespan, energy efficiency, and consistent brightness over time.','Ensure the spotlight is installed securely in the correct position for effective lighting. Use the recommended voltage and power supply to prevent damage to the LED components.','Avoid direct contact with water unless the spotlight is rated for outdoor or waterproof use. Proper ventilation should be maintained to allow heat dissipation and ensure long-lasting performance.','categories/1772884183853-644615323.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 11:49:43','2026-03-07 11:49:43'),
(619,1,19,20,'secondary',614,'Strip Light','A Strip Light is a flexible lighting solution made with a series of small LED lights mounted on a narrow circuit board strip. It is commonly used for decorative and ambient lighting in homes, offices, shops, and display areas. The strip design allows it to be easily installed in tight or curved spaces such as under cabinets, along ceilings, behind televisions, or inside showcases. Strip lights provide bright and uniform illumination while consuming very low power, making them an energy-efficient lighting option.','Strip lights are available in various lengths, colors, and brightness levels to suit different lighting needs. They may come in single-color or RGB versions that allow users to change colors using a remote controller or mobile app. Most strip lights have an adhesive backing for easy installation and can be cut at marked intervals to fit specific spaces. They usually operate using low voltage power adapters such as 5V, 12V, or 24V depending on the model.','Ensure the surface is clean and dry before sticking the strip light for better adhesion. Use the correct power adapter specified for the strip light to avoid damage. Avoid bending the strip sharply as it may damage the circuit. For outdoor or humid environments, use waterproof strip lights to ensure safety and durability.','The strip design allows it to be easily installed in tight or curved spaces such as under cabinets, along ceilings, behind televisions, or inside showcases. Strip lights provide bright and uniform illumination while consuming very low power, making them an energy-efficient lighting option.','categories/1772884418959-839255560.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 11:53:38','2026-03-09 14:13:53'),
(620,1,19,17,'secondary',215,'Sata Cable','A SATA Cable (Serial Advanced Technology Attachment Cable) is a data transfer cable used to connect storage devices such as hard disk drives (HDDs), solid-state drives (SSDs), and optical drives to a computer’s motherboard. It is designed to provide fast and reliable data communication between the storage device and the system.','SATA cables support high-speed data transfer depending on the SATA version, such as SATA I (1.5 Gb/s), SATA II (3 Gb/s), and SATA III (6 Gb/s). They usually have a 7-pin connector on both ends and may include locking clips to ensure a secure connection. SATA cables are used along with a separate SATA power cable that supplies power from the power supply unit to the storage device.','Ensure the SATA cable is properly connected to both the motherboard and the storage device for reliable data transfer. Avoid bending the cable sharply as it may damage the internal wiring. Always turn off the computer before installing or removing the cable. Use high-quality SATA cables to maintain stable and high-speed data performance.','SATA cables are commonly used in desktop computers, servers, and other electronic systems that require internal storage connectivity. The cable is thin and flexible, making it easier to manage inside computer cabinets compared to older IDE cables.','categories/1772884538155-47664163.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 11:55:38','2026-03-07 11:55:38'),
(621,1,19,17,'primary',NULL,'Hubs and Ports','Hubs and Ports are essential connectivity components used in computers and electronic devices to connect multiple peripherals and expand the number of available input and output interfaces. A hub is a device that allows several devices such as keyboards, mice, printers, storage drives, and other USB devices to connect to a single port on a computer. Ports, on the other hand, are the physical interfaces on a device where cables or connectors are plugged in to enable communication, power transfer, or data exchange.','Hubs and ports are commonly found in computers, laptops, networking equipment, and electronic devices. USB hubs are widely used to increase the number of USB ports available on a device. Ports can include various types such as USB ports, HDMI ports, Ethernet ports, audio ports, and charging ports. These interfaces allow devices to transfer data, connect to displays, access networks, and power external devices. Modern hubs may also support high-speed data transfer, fast charging, and compatibility with different devices.','When using hubs, ensure that the connected devices do not exceed the hub’s power capacity, especially for devices that require higher power. Use compatible cables and connectors to avoid connection issues. Avoid forcing connectors into ports to prevent physical damage. Always keep ports clean and free from dust to maintain reliable connectivity.','Together, hubs and ports help improve device connectivity and make it easier to manage multiple hardware connections.','categories/1772884692749-826936021.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-07 11:58:12','2026-03-07 11:58:12'),
(622,1,19,20,'secondary',431,'Rocker switch','A Rocker Switch is a common electrical switch used to turn a device ON or OFF by rocking one side of the switch up or down. When one side is pressed, the opposite side rises, creating a simple and reliable switching action. Rocker switches are widely used in home appliances, power supplies, extension boards, electronic projects, and industrial equipment.','Rocker switches are designed for panel mounting and are available in various types such as 2-pin, 3-pin, and illuminated switches. Some models include a built-in LED or neon light that glows when the switch is turned ON. They are typically used with AC 110V–250V or DC circuits, depending on the model and rating.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,'active','2026-03-09 04:07:28','2026-03-09 04:07:28'),
(623,1,19,15,'secondary',203,'DC PUMP TUBE ','A DC Pump Tube is a flexible plastic or silicone pipe used with DC water pumps to carry water from the pump outlet to another location. It is commonly used in DIY electronics projects, aquarium systems, water circulation setups, cooling systems, and small fountain projects. The tube is lightweight, flexible, and easy to connect to mini DC pumps.','The tube is connected to the inlet or outlet nozzle of a DC water pump to allow smooth flow of water or other liquids. It is available in different diameters and lengths depending on the pump size. Because of its flexibility, it can easily be routed through small spaces in robotics projects, cooling systems, and laboratory setups.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1773032212442-125239736.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-09 04:56:52','2026-03-09 04:56:52'),
(624,1,21,24,'secondary',293,'CCTV Storage Combo','A CCTV Storage Combo usually refers to a package that includes a DVR/NVR recorder and a surveillance hard disk (HDD) designed specifically for 24/7 video recording.','The storage device saves the video footage captured by CCTV cameras so it can be viewed later for security or investigation purposes.','Always use surveillance-grade HDDs instead of normal computer hard disks.',NULL,'categories/1773035320182-467029502.jpg',0,1,'active','2026-03-09 05:44:24','2026-03-09 08:58:42'),
(625,1,21,24,'secondary',282,'Solar CCTV Camera','A solar CCTV camera works by using photovoltaic solar panels to convert sunlight into electricity, which charges an internal battery.','Most solar CCTV cameras include wireless connectivity (Wi-Fi or 4G SIM) so users can watch live video and receive alerts through a mobile app from anywhere.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1773115481963-17276658.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-10 04:04:41','2026-03-10 04:04:41'),
(626,1,21,24,'secondary',298,'Power Connectors','Power Connectors are electrical connectors used to safely connect a power source to electronic devices or circuits. They allow electricity to flow from batteries, adapters, or power supplies to equipment such as electronic modules, appliances, and DIY projects. Power connectors are designed to provide secure and reliable power connections.','There are many types of power connectors depending on the application. Common types include DC barrel connectors, battery connectors, screw terminal connectors, USB power connectors, and plug-and-socket connectors. These connectors are widely used in CCTV systems, LED lighting, routers, power supplies, robotics, and electronics projects.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1773118416522-648289805.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-10 04:53:36','2026-03-10 04:53:36'),
(627,1,19,16,'secondary',212,'Mobile Holder','A Mobile Holder is a useful accessory designed to hold and support a mobile phone securely in a fixed position. It allows users to place their smartphones on a table, desk, car dashboard, or other surfaces without holding the device by hand. Mobile holders are commonly made from plastic, metal, or silicone materials and are designed to provide stability and convenience while watching videos, attending video calls, browsing, or charging the phone.','Mobile holders come in different types such as desk mobile holders, car mobile holders, adjustable stands, magnetic holders, and foldable holders. Some models allow adjustable viewing angles so users can set the phone in a comfortable position for viewing or typing. Many mobile holders are designed to be lightweight, portable, and compatible with different smartphone sizes. They also help reduce hand fatigue and prevent accidental drops by keeping the device firmly supported.','Mobile holders improve convenience and ergonomics while using smartphones for long periods. They are commonly used for watching movies, online meetings, video recording, navigation in cars, and charging. Some holders include anti-slip pads, adjustable arms, or rotating joints for better stability and flexibility. Proper placement and compatibility with the phone size should be considered for effective use.','They are widely used in homes, offices, vehicles, and workplaces to keep mobile phones safe and easily accessible','categories/1773143453687-885070212.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-10 11:50:53','2026-03-10 11:50:53'),
(628,1,19,33,'primary',NULL,'Soldering Tools',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,'active','2026-03-12 09:23:44','2026-03-12 09:23:44'),
(629,35,18,13,'secondary',115,'Optical cable','Optical cables contain very thin glass or plastic fibers protected by multiple insulation layers. Data travels as light pulses through the fiber core, enabling very fast and reliable data transmission over long distances.','An optical cable, also called a fiber optic cable, is a communication cable that transmits data using light signals instead of electrical signals. It is widely used for high-speed internet, telecom networks, data centers, CCTV networking, and long-distance communication systems.',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,1,'active','2026-03-14 06:20:40','2026-04-09 08:06:31'),
(630,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Microcontroller IC (MCU)','Microcontroller IC (MCU) From Microchip Technology is a leading semiconductor manufacturer known for designing and producing a wide range of microcontrollers, analog ICs, memory devices, power-management chips, communication interfaces, and embedded system solutions. The company is especially popular for its PIC microcontrollers, AVR microcontrollers, and development tools, which are widely used by engineers, students, and industries for embedded electronics design.','Microcontroller IC (MCU) From Microchip products are commonly found in consumer electronics, industrial automation systems, automotive electronics, IoT devices, communication equipment, medical instruments, and power supply circuits. The company also provides extensive software support, development environments (such as MPLAB), and reference designs, making it easier for designers to develop reliable electronic products. Due to its strong focus on innovation, quality, and long-term product availability, Microchip Technology is considered one of the key suppliers in the global embedded electronics and semiconductor industry.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1773735914633-285004652.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 08:25:14','2026-04-06 15:40:44'),
(631,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Semiconductors','Semiconductors are materials whose electrical conductivity lies between that of conductors (like copper) and insulators (like glass). Their conductivity can be controlled by adding impurities (a process called doping), applying electric fields, light, or temperature changes, which makes them highly useful in electronic devices. Common semiconductor materials include silicon, germanium, and gallium arsenide. Semiconductor technology is the foundation of modern electronics, enabling the creation of components such as diodes, transistors, integrated circuits (ICs), sensors, and microprocessors','These devices are widely used in computers, mobile phones, communication systems, power control circuits, automotive electronics, and industrial automation. Due to their ability to efficiently control current and voltage, semiconductors play a critical role in signal processing, switching, amplification, and energy conversion in both low-power and high-power electronic applications.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1773814307778-9787161.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 06:11:47','2026-03-18 06:11:47'),
(632,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'AC Remote ','AC remotes usually work using infrared (IR) signals to communicate with the air conditioner.They are powered by AAA or AA batteries and have a small LCD display screen that shows temperature and operating mode.','Some models are brand-specific remotes, while others are universal AC remotes that can work with many AC brands.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1773815658708-484324649.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 06:34:18','2026-03-18 06:34:18'),
(633,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Microprocessor','A microprocessor is a programmable electronic device that functions as the central processing unit (CPU) of a computer or embedded system. It is fabricated using semiconductor technology and is designed to perform arithmetic calculations, logical operations, data processing, and control tasks based on instructions stored in memory. A microprocessor typically includes key internal units such as the Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU), control unit, registers, and data/address buses, which work together to execute programs step by step.','Microprocessors operate by fetching instructions from external memory, decoding them, and then executing the required operations while interacting with input/output devices. Unlike microcontrollers, they usually require external RAM, ROM, and peripheral interface circuits to build a complete working system. Microprocessors are widely used in applications such as computers, laptops, industrial automation systems, communication equipment, robotics, instrumentation, and embedded control systems, where complex data processing and decision-making tasks are required. Their performance is generally determined by factors such as clock speed, data bus width, instruction set architecture, and power efficiency.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1773821401486-869679399.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 08:10:01','2026-03-18 08:10:01'),
(634,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Atmel','Atmel was a well-known semiconductor company that specialized in the design and manufacture of microcontrollers, memory devices, and application-specific integrated circuits. The company was founded in 1984 in the United States and became highly popular in the embedded electronics industry due to its reliable and cost-effective products. Atmel gained worldwide recognition for its AVR series microcontrollers, which are widely used in educational kits, industrial automation systems, consumer electronics, and hobby projects.','Many popular development platforms, including Arduino boards, were originally based on Atmel microcontroller technology. The company also produced EEPROM, Flash memory, touch controller ICs, RF devices, and power management solutions. Atmel components were known for their low power consumption, easy programming features, and stable performance, making them suitable for battery-operated and embedded applications. In 2016, Atmel was officially acquired by Microchip Technology, and its product lines continued under the Microchip brand. Engineers and students still commonly refer to AVR controllers as Atmel devices due to their long-standing popularity. The company played a significant role in advancing embedded system design and digital control technology. Even today, Atmel-based designs remain widely used in industrial equipment, robotics, smart devices, and DIY electronics projects.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1773893759967-244581541.jpg',0,1,'active','2026-03-19 04:15:59','2026-04-09 06:17:43'),
(635,1,19,15,'secondary',203,'Multi Strand Wire','A multi strand wire is an electrical conductor made up of multiple thin strands of metal, usually copper or aluminum, twisted together to form a single flexible wire. This construction improves flexibility compared to single solid wires, making it ideal for applications where frequent bending or movement is required, such as in household wiring, automotive systems, electronic devices, and control panels.','Multi strand wires also offer better conductivity and reduced chances of breakage under mechanical stress. They are commonly insulated with materials like PVC or rubber to ensure safety and durability, and are available in various sizes and current ratings depending on the application.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1774338056237-80434668.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-24 07:40:56','2026-03-24 07:40:56'),
(636,33,12,34,'primary',NULL,'dsss','qqq','q','s','s',NULL,0,1,'active','2026-03-26 08:27:03','2026-04-09 06:24:55'),
(637,1,1,1,'primary',NULL,'fde','ew','ew','we',NULL,NULL,0,1,'active','2026-03-26 08:36:07','2026-04-09 07:59:03'),
(638,1,19,15,'secondary',165,'Ultrasonic Sensor','An Ultrasonic Sensor is an electronic device used to measure distance by using high-frequency sound waves that are inaudible to humans. It works by emitting ultrasonic pulses from a transmitter and then measuring the time it takes for the echo to return after reflecting off an object. Based on this time delay, the sensor calculates the distance using the speed of sound.','One of the most commonly used modules is the HC-SR04, which operates at around 5V DC and provides accurate distance measurements typically ranging from 2 cm to 400 cm. The sensor has four main pins—VCC, GND, TRIG, and ECHO—and is widely compatible with microcontrollers like Arduino and Raspberry Pi.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1774608038129-787760551.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-27 10:40:38','2026-03-27 10:40:38'),
(639,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Lithium Battery Holder','A lithium battery holder is a specially designed component used to securely hold and connect lithium-based batteries, such as 18650 or 14500 lithium-ion cells, in electronic circuits and devices. It provides a safe and convenient way to insert and remove batteries without the need for soldering, making it ideal for prototyping, DIY projects, and battery-powered applications. These holders are typically made from durable plastic with metal spring contacts that ensure proper electrical conductivity and stable positioning of the battery.','Available in various configurations such as single-cell, dual-cell, or multiple-cell arrangements, lithium battery holders support both series and parallel connections depending on the design. Many models come with pre-attached wires or PCB mounting options for easy integration. By ensuring secure contact and proper alignment, lithium battery holders help improve safety, prevent short circuits, and enhance the overall reliability of battery-operated systems.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1774959979339-617482395.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-31 12:26:19','2026-04-10 05:25:34'),
(640,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Mov Thermistor','An MOV thermistor, more accurately known as a Metal Oxide Varistor (MOV), is a voltage-dependent resistor used to protect electronic circuits from voltage spikes and surges. It is commonly made from zinc oxide grains and appears as a small disc-shaped component, typically blue or orange in color. The resistance of an MOV changes with the applied voltage under normal conditions, it has very high resistance, but when a high voltage surge occurs, its resistance drops sharply, allowing excess voltage to be diverted and protecting sensitive components.','MOVs are widely used in power supplies, surge protectors, home appliances, and industrial equipment. They respond quickly to transient voltages such as lightning or switching surges, helping to prevent damage and extend the lifespan of electronic devices. Their compact size, fast response time, and cost-effectiveness make them an essential safety component in modern electronic circuits.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1774968116033-807458580.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-31 14:41:56','2026-03-31 14:41:56'),
(641,1,19,20,'secondary',272,'14D Mov Thermistor','A 14D MOV thermistor, commonly referred to as a 14D Metal Oxide Varistor (MOV), is a voltage-dependent protection component designed to safeguard electronic circuits from high voltage spikes and transient surges. The “14D” designation indicates a disc diameter of approximately 14mm, which allows it to handle higher energy absorption compared to smaller varistors. These components are typically made from zinc oxide material and are easily recognized by their round, disc-like shape, usually in blue color.','14D MOV thermistors are widely used in power supplies, inverters, home appliances, industrial control systems, and surge protection devices. They offer fast response time, high surge handling capability, and reliable performance, making them an essential component for enhancing the safety and durability of electronic equipment.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1774968233788-753661750.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-31 14:43:53','2026-04-16 06:33:30'),
(642,1,19,20,'secondary',640,'7D Mov Thermistor','A 7D MOV thermistor, commonly known as a 7D Metal Oxide Varistor (MOV), is a compact voltage-dependent resistor used to protect electronic circuits from voltage spikes and transient surges. The “7D” designation refers to the disc size of approximately 7mm in diameter, making it suitable for low to moderate power applications where space is limited. These components are typically made from zinc oxide and are recognized by their small, disc-shaped design.','7D MOV thermistors are widely used in small power supplies, adapters, LED drivers, consumer electronics, and control circuits. Due to their fast response time, compact size, and cost-effectiveness, they are an essential protective component for improving the reliability and safety of electronic devices.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1774968327116-121844420.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-31 14:45:27','2026-03-31 14:45:27'),
(643,1,19,20,'secondary',272,'10D Mov Thermistor','A 10D MOV thermistor, commonly referred to as a 10D Metal Oxide Varistor (MOV), is a voltage-dependent resistor designed to protect electronic circuits from voltage spikes and transient surges. The “10D” indicates a disc diameter of approximately 10mm, offering a balance between compact size and moderate energy absorption capability. These components are typically made from zinc oxide material and have a round, disc-shaped structure, usually coated in blue or similar colors.','10D MOV thermistors are widely used in power supplies, adapters, LED drivers, home appliances, and industrial control circuits. They provide fast response, reliable surge protection, and cost-effective performance, making them an essential component for enhancing the safety and longevity of electronic systems.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1774968460878-93681206.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-31 14:47:40','2026-04-16 06:33:30'),
(644,1,19,20,'secondary',408,'SLA VRLA Battery','An SLA (Sealed Lead Acid) battery, also known as a VRLA (Valve Regulated Lead Acid) battery, is a rechargeable battery designed to be maintenance-free and spill-proof. Unlike traditional flooded batteries, it does not require water topping and can operate in various orientations.','Voltage: 6V, 12V (most common)\r\nCapacity: 1Ah to 200Ah+\r\nCharging Voltage: ~13.5V – 14.5V (for 12V battery)\r\nCycle Life: 200–1000 cycles (depends on usage)\r\nOperating Temperature: -15°C to 50°C',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775020950277-327271864.avif',1,1,'active','2026-04-01 05:22:30','2026-04-01 05:22:30'),
(645,1,19,18,'primary',NULL,'Converter','HDMI to VGA, VGA to HDMI converters, and DisplayPort interfaces are essential connectivity solutions used to bridge compatibility between different display technologies. An HDMI to VGA converter allows modern digital devices to connect with older analog displays by converting digital signals into analog format, often including audio output support. In contrast, a VGA to HDMI converter enables legacy devices with analog output to connect to modern digital screens, requiring active signal conversion and usually external power along with audio integration.','Meanwhile, DisplayPort is a high-performance digital interface designed for modern systems, capable of transmitting high-resolution video and audio with superior quality, supporting advanced features like high refresh rates and multiple display connections. Together, these technologies ensure seamless integration between old and new hardware, making them highly useful in offices, educational setups, home entertainment, and professional environments where mixed display standards are commonly used.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775136700252-936518748.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 13:31:40','2026-04-02 13:31:40'),
(646,35,18,25,'primary',NULL,'palm meter','palm meter','palm meter','palm meter','palm meter','categories/1775219201278-155085852.png',1,1,'active','2026-04-03 12:26:41','2026-04-03 12:26:41'),
(647,35,18,25,'secondary',646,'meter meter','meter meter','meter meter','meter meter','meter meter','categories/1775219302285-39868905.png',1,1,'active','2026-04-03 12:28:22','2026-04-03 12:28:22'),
(648,35,18,13,'primary',NULL,'WIFI USB DONGLES','A WiFi USB Dongle (also called a wireless USB adapter) is a compact device that allows desktops, laptops, and other USB-enabled devices to connect to a wireless network. It is an ideal solution for systems without built-in WiFi or for upgrading older devices to access modern wireless networks.','These dongles support wireless standards like IEEE 802.11 b/g/n/ac, offering speeds ranging from 150 Mbps to 300 Mbps and higher, depending on the model. They typically operate on the 2.4GHz band, while advanced versions support dual-band (2.4GHz + 5GHz) for faster and more stable connections.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775311453265-216931131.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-04 14:04:13','2026-04-10 05:28:32'),
(649,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'X',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,'active','2026-04-06 09:47:36','2026-04-06 09:47:36'),
(650,35,18,13,'primary',NULL,'Projector X','A projector is an electronic device that displays images, videos, or presentations onto a large screen or wall by projecting light through a lens. It is commonly used for home entertainment, classrooms, offices, and cinema setups.','Large Screen Display: Much bigger than TVs (100–300 inches possible)\r\n Brightness (Lumens): Determines visibility in light or dark rooms\r\n Resolution:\r\n720p (basic)\r\n1080p (Full HD)\r\n4K (high quality)\r\nConnectivity: HDMI, USB, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth\r\nBuilt-in Speakers: Some models include audio output',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775476134640-854957750.png',1,1,'active','2026-04-06 11:48:54','2026-04-06 11:48:54'),
(651,1,19,14,'primary',NULL,'Music receiver','A Wireless Music Receiver is a compact device that allows you to stream audio wirelessly from your smartphone, tablet, or laptop to wired speakers, home theater systems, or car stereos. It uses Bluetooth technology to receive audio signals and outputs them through a 3.5mm AUX jack or RCA connection.','Most wireless music receivers offer stable connectivity, clear sound quality, and low power consumption. Many models are powered via USB and support quick pairing with a wide range of Bluetooth-enabled devices.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775483860737-198680639.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-06 13:57:40','2026-04-10 05:40:21'),
(652,1,19,16,'secondary',3,'Desktop Phone','A desktop phone is a fixed communication device designed for office desks, reception areas, and business environments. Unlike mobile phones, it remains stationary and is typically connected through a landline (PSTN) or internet-based systems such as VoIP (Voice over Internet Protocol). Desktop phones are widely used in corporate offices, call centers, and institutions because they offer reliable voice quality, stable connectivity, and professional call handling features.','Most modern desktop phones come with LCD displays, programmable keys, speakerphone, call transfer, conferencing, call hold, and speed dial functions. Advanced models support HD voice, multiple line management, PoE (Power over Ethernet), and integration with office communication systems. Known for durability and ease of use, desktop phones are ideal for continuous communication needs in professional settings.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775544425014-868686516.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-07 06:47:05','2026-04-07 06:47:05'),
(653,1,19,17,'secondary',215,'Wireless Bluetooth & Mouse Combo','A Wireless Bluetooth Keyboard & Mouse Combo is a convenient computer accessory set that includes a keyboard and mouse designed to work without cables, providing a clean and clutter-free workspace. These combos use Bluetooth or 2.4GHz wireless technology to connect seamlessly to devices such as desktops, laptops, tablets, and even smart TVs.',' Wireless connectivity (Bluetooth / 2.4GHz USB receiver)\r\n Single receiver for both keyboard & mouse\r\n Plug & play – no software required\r\n Comfortable typing with multimedia keys\r\n High-precision optical mouse (800–1600 DPI)\r\n Long battery life with power-saving mod',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775555235509-509334037.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-04-07 09:37:58','2026-04-07 09:47:15'),
(654,1,19,20,'secondary',275,'Memory ICs','A Memory Integrated Circuit (IC) is a semiconductor device designed to store digital data (binary 0s and 1s) within an electronic system. These chips, featuring densely packed memory cells and support circuitry (address decoders, amplifiers), are categorized into volatile (RAM) for temporary workspace and non-volatile (ROM/Flash) for permanent data storage.',' A memory IC is a small chip that stores data for electronic devices. It\'s like a mini-library, holding all the information a device needs to function. the Memory IC serves as the dynamic workspace of the processor.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775571610508-560822198.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-07 14:20:10','2026-04-07 14:20:10'),
(655,1,19,20,'secondary',275,'OPTO Coupler','An optocoupler (or opto-isolator) is a semiconductor component that transfers electrical signals between isolated circuits using light, providing electrical isolation and protecting low-voltage components (like microcontrollers) from high-voltage transients. It consists of an infrared LED and a photosensitive detector (transistor, TRIAC, or SCR) within a single package.','An optocoupler (also called optoisolator) is a semiconductor device that allows an electrical signal to be transmitted between two isolated circuits',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775571923826-698987100.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-07 14:25:23','2026-04-07 14:25:23'),
(656,1,19,14,'primary',NULL,'Amplifier','An electrical or electronic amplifier is a circuit that uses an external power supply to generate an output signal that is a larger replica of its input. An audio amplifier (an easily recognizable application) is used to increase the volume of a speaker\'s voice so they can be heard more easily in large areas.','An amplifier is an electrical two-port network that produces a signal at the output port that is a replica of the signal applied to the input port, but increased in magnitude.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775625515234-97600236.jfif',0,1,'active','2026-04-08 05:18:35','2026-04-08 05:28:06'),
(657,1,19,20,'secondary',414,'power transistor','A power transistor is a type of transistor designed to handle high current and high voltage, making it suitable for power amplification and switching applications. Unlike small signal transistors, power transistors are built with a larger structure to dissipate heat and manage higher electrical loads.','A power transistor is an essential electronic component used to control and amplify high power signals, widely used in power electronics, industrial systems, and consumer devices.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775653882110-364946423.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-08 13:11:22','2026-04-08 13:11:22'),
(658,1,20,23,'primary',NULL,'AMPLIFIER',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,1,'active','2026-04-09 04:08:20','2026-04-09 04:09:18'),
(659,1,19,14,'secondary',332,'FM Player','An FM Player is an electronic device designed to receive FM radio signals and play audio through speakers or headphones. In modern devices, it is often combined with MP3 playback features, allowing users to enjoy both live radio broadcasts and stored music.','FM Radio Reception – Tune into local radio stations\r\nAuto Scan & Save – Automatically searches and stores channels\r\nDigital Display – Shows frequency, track, and mode\r\nUSB / SD Card Support (in combo models) – Play MP3 songs directly\r\nBluetooth Connectivity (in advanced models) – Wireless audio streaming\r\nRemote Control – Easy operation from a distance\r\nCompact Design – Suitable for home, car, or portable use',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775711216231-718359380.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-04-09 05:06:56','2026-04-09 05:06:56'),
(660,1,20,23,'primary',NULL,'jd','jd','dj','dj',NULL,NULL,0,1,'active','2026-04-09 05:25:29','2026-04-09 08:01:18'),
(661,1,20,22,'primary',NULL,'ew','ew','we','we','we',NULL,0,1,'active','2026-04-09 05:26:40','2026-04-09 07:58:28'),
(662,1,20,22,'secondary',207,'trh','tr',NULL,'rt','rt','categories/1775716083260-58449482.png',1,1,'active','2026-04-09 06:28:03','2026-04-09 06:28:03'),
(663,1,20,23,'primary',NULL,'h','hh','hh','hh',NULL,NULL,0,1,'active','2026-04-09 06:36:06','2026-04-09 08:00:10'),
(664,1,20,23,'primary',NULL,'huuu','h','h','h',NULL,'categories/1775716918911-860906170.jpg',0,1,'active','2026-04-09 06:41:58','2026-04-09 08:00:55'),
(665,1,19,20,'secondary',414,'Regulator','A voltage regulator is an electronic component or circuit that maintains a constant output voltage regardless of changes in input voltage or load conditions. It is essential in electronic systems to ensure that devices receive a stable and safe voltage supply.','Voltage regulators are widely used in power supplies, electronic devices, battery-operated systems, and embedded circuits to protect components from voltage fluctuations.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775733291938-60520101.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-09 11:14:51','2026-04-09 11:14:51'),
(666,1,19,14,'secondary',9,'woofers & speakers','A speaker (loudspeaker) is an electronic device that converts electrical audio signals into sound waves. It works by using a voice coil and magnet to vibrate a cone, producing audible sound.','Speakers are used in many devices such as TVs, mobile phones, computers, home theater systems, and audio amplifiers. They can reproduce a wide range of frequencies depending on their design.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775743482493-934757483.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-09 14:04:42','2026-04-09 14:04:42'),
(667,1,19,20,'primary',NULL,'Scanner','A scanner is an electronic device used to convert physical documents, photos, or images into digital format. It captures the content and saves it on a computer or storage device as files like PDF, JPEG, or PNG.','High resolution (DPI) for clear images\r\nColor and black & white scanning\r\nUSB / Wi-Fi connectivity\r\nOCR (Optical Character Recognition) for text editing',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775795185051-586665300.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-04-10 04:26:25','2026-04-10 04:40:47'),
(668,1,19,20,'secondary',667,'Fingerprint scanner','A fingerprint scanner is a biometric security device that captures and analyzes the unique ridges and valleys of a fingertip to identify or verify a user. By converting these physical patterns into a digital template, they provide secure access control for devices, facilities, and data.','Sensor Type: Optical, Capacitive (most common), Ultrasonic (high-end)\r\nResolution: 500 dots per inch (DPI) standard, some 569+ DPI\r\nImage Gray Scale: 8 Bits/Pixel (256 Gray Levels)\r\nScanning Speed: < 0.5 - 1.0 second per authentication\r\nFalse Acceptance Rate (FAR): \r\n 0.001% (high security)\r\nFalse Rejection Rate (FRR): \r\n 1.0%\r\nInterface: USB 2.0, UART/TTL, Bluetooth',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775795424106-862034024.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-04-10 04:30:24','2026-04-10 04:30:24'),
(669,1,19,15,'secondary',165,'Fingerprint optical sensor','An Optical Fingerprint Sensor Module is a compact electronic module that captures fingerprint images using optical (light-based) technology and processes them for biometric authentication. It is widely used in embedded systems and IoT projects.','Built-in optical sensor + processor\r\n500 DPI resolution for clear fingerprint capture\r\nUART / Serial interface for easy communication\r\nInternal memory to store multiple fingerprints\r\nFast matching & enrollment process\r\nCompact and easy to integrate',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775800263237-625471288.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-04-10 05:51:03','2026-04-10 05:51:03'),
(670,1,19,15,'secondary',78,'Opticat Dust Sensor','An Optical Dust Sensor is an electronic device used to detect and measure dust particles in the air. It works using light (usually infrared) to sense the presence of fine particles such as smoke, pollen, and pollution.','Real-time dust detection\r\nHigh sensitivity to fine particles (PM2.5/PM10)\r\nLow power consumption\r\nAnalog or digital output\r\nCompact and easy to integrate',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775802242819-322454988.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-04-10 06:24:02','2026-04-10 06:24:02'),
(671,1,19,14,'secondary',9,'plastic grill','An SRC plastic speaker grill is a protective cover used in front of speakers and woofers to protect the cone from dust, damage, and physical contact. It also gives a stylish look to speaker boxes and car audio systems.','An SRC plastic speaker grill is a low-cost protective cover used for woofers and speakers, offering safety, durability, and better appearance for audio systems.',NULL,NULL,'categories/1775829183262-769941113.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-10 13:53:03','2026-04-10 13:53:03'),
