(147,'NUCLEO F303RE',NULL,NULL,NULL,2100.00,'The NUCLEO-F303RE is a powerful development board from STMicroelectronics designed for prototyping and developing embedded applications using the STM32F303RE microcontroller, which is based on the ARM Cortex-M4 core. It operates at a clock speed of up to 72 MHz and includes a built-in floating-point unit (FPU) and digital signal processing (DSP) instructions, making it suitable for real-time control, motor control, signal processing, and industrial applications.','The board features an onboard ST-LINK/V2-1 debugger and programmer, allowing direct programming and debugging through a USB connection without requiring external hardware. It supports multiple development environments including STM32CubeIDE, Keil MDK, IAR Embedded Workbench, and Arduino IDE','The STM32F303RE microcontroller includes rich peripherals such as ADCs, DACs, timers, UART, SPI, I2C, CAN interface, and PWM outputs, making the board ideal for advanced embedded system design. It is widely used in motor control systems, robotics, industrial automation, sensor interfacing, data acquisition, and educational embedded development due to its high processing performance and extensive peripheral support.',NULL,'products/1771993821852-96946252.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 04:30:21'),
