(608,'1 ohm Resistor','Resistor',NULL,NULL,49.00,'A 1 ohm resistor is a passive electronic component that provides a resistance value of exactly 1 Ω to control the flow of electric current in a circuit. It is designed to create a small voltage drop while allowing relatively high current to pass through, making it useful in current sensing and power regulation applications.','A 1 ohm resistor is a low-value fixed resistor with a resistance of 1 ohm, commonly used for current sensing, current limiting, and load balancing in electronic circuits. It is widely used in power circuits and DIY electronics projects.','A 1 ohm resistor is a very low-resistance electronic component used to limit current, measure current flow, or control power within a circuit. It provides a resistance value of 1 Ω, meaning it allows relatively high current to pass while creating a small voltage drop according to Ohm’s Law (V = I × R). Because the resistance value is low, 1 ohm resistors are commonly used as current-sensing (shunt) resistors in power supplies, battery management systems, motor drivers, LED circuits, and amplifier circuits.',NULL,'products/1771646005703-540901343.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 11:12:29'),
