(697,'NTC Thermistor',NULL,NULL,'NTC Module',399.00,'The NTC Thermistor (Negative Temperature Coefficient Thermistor) is a temperature-sensitive resistor whose resistance decreases as temperature increases. It is made from semiconductor materials such as metal oxides, which provide high sensitivity to temperature changes. When the surrounding temperature rises, the electrical resistance of the thermistor drops significantly, allowing it to accurately measure temperature variations. Due to this characteristic, NTC thermistors are widely used for temperature sensing, monitoring, and compensation applications in electronic circuits.','NTC thermistors are commonly available in various resistance values such as 10KΩ, 47KΩ, or 100KΩ at 25°C, and they operate with low power consumption. They can be easily interfaced with microcontrollers like Arduino, ESP8266, and ESP32 using a voltage divider circuit to convert resistance changes into measurable voltage signals.','NTC thermistors are widely used in battery temperature monitoring, power supplies, HVAC systems, medical devices, automotive electronics, home appliances, and IoT temperature control systems. They are also used for inrush current limiting and thermal protection in electronic equipment.',NULL,'products/1771993690483-722960043.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-06 06:52:54'),
