(759,'Y8429',NULL,NULL,NULL,160.00,'The Y8429 Transistor is a general-purpose NPN bipolar junction transistor (BJT) commonly used in electronic circuits for switching and signal amplification applications. It is designed to control current flow by using a small input signal at the base terminal to regulate a larger current between the collector and emitter terminals. Due to its reliable performance and fast switching characteristics, the Y8429 transistor is suitable for low to medium power electronic designs.','This transistor is typically used in amplifier circuits, driver stages, oscillator circuits, and electronic switching applications. It can be used to drive relays, LEDs, small motors, and other loads when connected with appropriate biasing components. The device is generally available in a compact TO-92 or similar package, making it easy to mount on PCB boards and prototype circuits. Like other NPN transistors, it operates by allowing current flow when the base receives a positive signal relative to the emitter.','The Y8429 transistor is widely applied in consumer electronics, audio circuits, automation systems, educational electronics projects, and embedded control circuits because of its small size, low cost, and dependable operation.',NULL,'products/1772015409267-242613950.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 10:30:09'),
