(778,'Capacitive Proximity Sensor',NULL,NULL,NULL,1499.00,'Capacitive Proximity Sensor is a non-contact detection device used to sense metallic and non-metallic objects, including plastic, glass, wood, liquids, paper, grain, powders, and more. It works by creating an electrostatic field around its sensing face; when an object enters this field, the sensor detects the change in capacitance and outputs a signal.','A capacitive proximity sensor is a non-contact sensor used to detect the presence of both metallic and non-metallic objects. It works by sensing changes in capacitance caused when an object enters the sensor’s electric field.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771844382490-119373951.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 10:59:42'),
