(978,'VGA (Video Graphics Array) Cable',NULL,NULL,NULL,999.00,'1 meter,1.5 meters,3 meters,5 meters,10 meters,15 meters,20 meters,30 meters. A VGA cable is an analog video transmission cable used to connect computers, laptops, and other video sources to displays such as monitors, projectors, and TVs. It uses a 15-pin D-sub connector and is commonly found on older or legacy devices.','VGA (Video Graphics Array) Cable is an analog video cable used to connect a computer or laptop to a monitor, projector, or display. It features a 15-pin D-sub connector and supports video resolutions commonly up to 1080p (depending on cable quality and length).',NULL,NULL,'products/1772006929554-747514062.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 08:08:49'),
