(980,'Tata Steel TMT bars in Fe 415 grade',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'Tata Steel TMT Bars in Fe 415 Grade are high-quality thermo-mechanically treated reinforcement bars manufactured by Tata Steel for use in residential, commercial, and infrastructure construction. The Fe 415 grade indicates a minimum yield strength of 415 N/mm², making these bars suitable for structures that require good strength along with excellent ductility and flexibility.','These TMT bars offer superior bonding strength with concrete, ensuring better structural stability and durability over long periods. They are manufactured with controlled chemical composition to provide high corrosion resistance, weldability, and uniform mechanical properties.','The ribs on the bar surface enhance grip with concrete, reducing slippage and improving overall reinforcement performance. Tata Steel TMT bars are widely used in houses, buildings, bridges, columns, beams, slabs, and RCC structures, especially where reliable and long-lasting reinforcement is required.',NULL,'products/1772003893808-305678333.jpg',0,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-04 12:32:00'),
(981,'Tata Steel TMT bars in Fe 500 grade',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'Tata Steel TMT bars in Fe 500 grade are widely available in various millimeter (mm) diameters, commonly including 8mm, 10mm, 12mm, 16mm, 20mm, 25mm, and 32mm, used for different structural needs in residential and commercial projects, offering good strength and ductility for general construction.','Tata Steel TMT Bars in Fe 500 Grade are high-strength thermo-mechanically treated reinforcement bars manufactured by Tata Steel for modern construction applications requiring superior load-bearing capacity and durability. The Fe 500 grade denotes a minimum yield strength of 500 N/mm², making these bars stronger than Fe 415 grade and suitable for heavy structural and high-rise construction','These TMT bars provide excellent bonding with concrete due to their specially designed rib pattern, improving structural stability and reducing the chances of slippage. Tata Steel ensures controlled chemical composition and precise manufacturing processes, resulting in improved corrosion resistance, weldability, and uniform mechanical properties. The bars also offer good earthquake resistance because of their high elongation and bendability, making them suitable for seismic-prone areas.',NULL,'products/1772004077952-777490955.jpg',0,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-04 12:32:09'),
