(1000,'IC 1','1','1','IC 1',10.00,'The IC 1 (Integrated Circuit 1) generally refers to an electronic integrated circuit used as a primary component in an electronic system or circuit diagram, where components are numbered for identification. An integrated circuit (IC) is a miniature electronic device fabricated on a semiconductor chip that contains multiple electronic components such as transistors, resistors, and capacitors interconnected to perform a specific function','Depending on the circuit design, IC 1 may represent different types of ICs such as logic gates, timers, counters, microcontrollers, amplifiers, or voltage regulators. These devices operate with low power consumption, high reliability, and compact size compared to discrete components.','ICs are commonly found in consumer electronics, communication systems, computers, industrial automation equipment, and embedded systems. Their small form factor and high functionality make them essential building blocks in modern electronic devices and circuit designs.',NULL,'products/1771911985362-636762559.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 05:46:25'),
