(1043,'LM393',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM393 is a dual voltage comparator integrated circuit that contains two independent, high-gain comparators in a single package','LM393 is a dual voltage comparator IC that contains two independent comparators in a single package.','It operates from a single power supply or dual supplies and features open-collector outputs, allowing easy interfacing with logic circuits using pull-up resistors.',NULL,'products/1771918044928-384457470.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:27:24'),
(1044,'74LS30','74LS30',NULL,'74LS30',99.00,'The 74LS30 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains one 8-input NAND gate in a single package. The output of the gate goes LOW only when all eight inputs are HIGH; if any input is LOW, the output remains HIGH.','74LS30 is a TTL logic IC that contains a single 8-input NAND gate in a single package','It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, providing faster switching speed and lower power consumption than standard TTL devices.',NULL,'products/1771828250551-524324547.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:56:24'),
(1045,'74LS32','74LS32',NULL,'74LS32',99.00,'The 74LS32 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains four independent 2-input OR gates in a single package. Each OR gate outputs a logic HIGH when any one or both of its inputs are HIGH, and outputs LOW only when both inputs are LOW.','74LS32 is a TTL logic IC that contains four independent 2-input OR gates in a single package','It operates on a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, offering faster switching speed and reduced power consumption compared to standard TTL devices.',NULL,'products/1771828280466-393056609.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:57:06'),
(1046,'LM442',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'“LM442” is not a commonly recognized standard IC number like LM358, LM393, LM386, etc., and it can refer to different parts depending on the manufacturer or may be a partial/short code.','LM442 is an operational amplifier (op-amp) IC used for general-purpose analog signal amplification and conditioning.','It is designed to operate with single or dual power supplies and is suitable for audio, sensor interfacing, active filters, and control circuits.',NULL,'products/1771917910752-30661425.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:25:10'),
(1047,'74LS47','74LS47',NULL,'74LS47',99.00,'The 74LS47 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family, designed to convert Binary Coded Decimal (BCD) inputs into the corresponding signals required to drive a 7-segment LED display.','74LS47 is a TTL BCD-to-7-segment decoder/driver IC designed to drive common-anode 7-segment displays','It converts a 4-bit BCD input into the corresponding 7-segment output to display decimal digits 0–9.',NULL,'products/1771828402007-324481048.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:58:41'),
(1048,'LM555',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM555 (commonly known as the 555 Timer IC) is a versatile and widely used timing and oscillator integrated circuit','LM555 is a widely used timer and oscillator IC capable of operating in monostable, astable, and bistable modes.','It works over a wide supply voltage range (typically 4.5 V to 15 V) and can generate accurate time delays, pulses, and square-wave signals using external resistors and capacitors.',NULL,'products/1771917935087-312682332.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:25:35'),
(1049,'74LS51','74LS51',NULL,'74LS51',99.00,'The 74LS51 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family that implements AND-OR-Invert (AOI) logic. It contains two independent AOI logic circuits, each combining multiple AND gates whose outputs are ORed together and then inverted.','74LS51 is a TTL logic IC that contains two AND-OR-INVERT (AOI) logic gates in a single package','It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, offering faster switching and lower power consumption than standard TTL devices.',NULL,'products/1771828423572-386993386.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:59:28'),
(1050,'74LS74','74LS74',NULL,'74LS74',99.00,'The 74LS74 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains two independent D-type flip-flops, each triggered on the positive (rising) edge of the clock signal. Each flip-flop includes asynchronous preset (SET) and clear (RESET) inputs, allowing the output to be forced to a known state regardless of the clock.','74LS74 is a TTL dual D-type flip-flop IC with preset (PRE) and clear (CLR) inputs. It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, providing reliable and fast digital storage.','Each flip-flop includes asynchronous preset (SET) and clear (RESET) inputs, allowing the output to be forced to a known state regardless of the clock.',NULL,'products/1771828542464-754335394.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 09:00:41'),
(1051,'LM556',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM556 is a dual version of the popular 555 timer IC, containing two independent 555 timers in a single package','LM556 is a dual version of the 555 timer IC, containing two independent timers in a single package. Each timer can operate in monostable, astable, or bistable modes, just like the LM555.','It operates over a wide supply voltage range (typically 4.5 V to 15 V) and is commonly used in timing circuits, pulse generators, oscillators, PWM control, and sequential timing applications, helping reduce component count compared to using two separate 555 ICs.',NULL,'products/1771918070467-767164118.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:27:50'),
(1052,'LM564',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM564 is a precision voltage reference and regulator integrated circuit designed to provide a stable and accurate reference voltage for analog and digital circuits.','LM564 is a special-purpose analog IC used mainly in signal generation and control applications. It is commonly associated with voltage-controlled oscillator (VCO)–based circuits, where the output frequency varies with an input control voltage.','The LM564 is used in function generators, tone generators, modulation circuits, and timing/control systems',NULL,'products/1771918368347-698625617.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:32:48'),
(1053,'74LS86','74LS86',NULL,'74LS86',99.00,'The 74LS86 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains four independent 2-input Exclusive-OR (XOR) gates in a single package. Each XOR gate produces a HIGH output when the inputs are different (one HIGH and one LOW) and a LOW output when the inputs are the same.','74LS86 is a TTL logic IC that contains four independent 2-input XOR (exclusive-OR) gates in a single package.','It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, offering fast switching speed with reduced power consumption.',NULL,'products/1771828569804-543009238.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 09:01:04'),
(1054,'LM567',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM567 is a tone decoder IC based on a Phase-Locked Loop (PLL). It is designed to detect a specific frequency (tone) from an input signal and provide a digital output when that exact frequency is present.','LM567 is a tone decoder / phase-locked loop (PLL) IC designed to detect a specific frequency set by external resistors and capacitors.','When the input signal matches the preset frequency, the output is activated, making it useful for frequency detection and control applications.',NULL,'products/1771918143755-799892654.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:29:03'),
(1055,'74LS90','74LS90',NULL,'74LS90',99.00,'The 74LS90 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family designed as a decade (divide-by-10) counter. It counts from 0 to 9 in Binary Coded Decimal (BCD) form and then resets to zero, making it ideal for decimal counting applications.','74LS90 is a TTL decade counter IC that functions as a divide-by-10 (BCD) counter. It consists of four flip-flops arranged to count from 0 to 9, producing a 4-bit BCD output. It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series.','It consists of four flip-flops arranged to count from 0 to 9, producing a 4-bit BCD output. It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series.',NULL,'products/1771828594168-856075319.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 09:01:29'),
(1056,'74LS123','74LS123',NULL,'74LS123',99.00,'The 74LS123 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family designed as a dual retriggerable monostable multivibrator (one-shot timer). It generates a single output pulse of controlled width when triggered by an input signal.','74LS123 is a TTL dual retriggerable monostable multivibrator IC. It generates a precise output pulse whose width is set using external resistors and capacitors, and the pulse can be retriggered if a new trigger arrives before the timing period ends.','It generates a single output pulse of controlled width when triggered by an input signal.',NULL,'products/1771827003439-322976192.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:44:34'),
(1057,'74LS138','74LS138',NULL,'74LS138',99.00,'The 74LS138 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family used as a 3-to-8 line decoder or demultiplexer. It takes three binary input signals and decodes them into one of eight mutually exclusive active-LOW outputs, depending on the input combination.','74LS138 is a TTL 3-to-8 line decoder/demultiplexer IC that converts 3 binary input lines into one of eight active-LOW outputs. It operates from a 5 V supply and includes three enable inputs for flexible control and cascading.','It takes three binary input signals and decodes them into one of eight mutually exclusive active-LOW outputs, depending on the input combination.',NULL,'products/1771827033761-697889243.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:45:56'),
(1058,'74LS145','74LS145',NULL,'74LS145',99.00,'The 74LS145 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family designed as a BCD (Binary Coded Decimal) to decimal decoder/driver. It converts a 4-bit BCD input into one of ten mutually exclusive active-LOW outputs (0–9). Only one output is active at a time, corresponding to the BCD input value.','74LS145 is a TTL BCD-to-Decimal decoder/driver IC that converts a 4-bit BCD input into one of ten active-LOW outputs (0–9). It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series.','It converts a 4-bit BCD input into one of ten mutually exclusive active-LOW outputs (0–9). Only one output is active at a time, corresponding to the BCD input value.',NULL,'products/1771827089096-215885361.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:47:26'),
(1059,'74LS156','74LS156',NULL,'74LS156',99.00,'The 74LS156 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains two independent 1-of-4 decoders (or demultiplexers) in a single package. Each decoder takes two binary select inputs and activates one of four outputs.','The 74LS156 is a TTL logic IC that contains dual 1-of-4 decoder/demultiplexer circuits with open-collector outputs. It converts binary input signals into one of four active LOW outputs, allowing selection or routing of digital signals in logic systems','Designed using Low-Power Schottky (LS) technology, the IC provides fast switching speed and reliable performance in digital control applications. The open-collector outputs allow wired-OR connections and easy interfacing with different voltage levels using external pull-up resistors.',NULL,'products/1771827368797-701391096.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:47:49'),
(1060,'LM570 IC',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM570 is a Phase-Locked Loop (PLL) based FM demodulator IC used to demodulate frequency-modulated (FM) signals into audio or baseband output.','LM570 IC is a low-distortion compandor (compressor/expander) IC used in audio signal processing. It compresses the dynamic range of audio signals during transmission and expands it back during reception, helping to reduce noise and improve signal quality.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771918164837-645504557.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:29:24'),
(1061,'LM594',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM594 is a quad operational amplifier (op-amp) IC that contains four independent, low-power op-amps in a single package','LM594 is a monolithic current regulator IC designed to provide a constant current output over a wide range of supply voltages. It is commonly used in applications where stable current control is required rather than voltage regulation.','The LM594 is widely used for LED driving, sensor excitation, biasing circuits, and current source applications, offering simple design, good stability, and reliable performance.',NULL,'products/1771918200079-312012256.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:30:00'),
(1062,'74LS161','74LS161',NULL,'74LS161',99.00,'The 74LS161 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family, designed as a 4-bit synchronous binary counter. It counts in binary sequence from 0 to 15 (0000 to 1111) with all flip-flops triggered simultaneously by a common clock, ensuring accurate and glitch-free counting.','74LS161 is a TTL synchronous 4-bit binary counter IC with asynchronous clear (CLR) and synchronous parallel load features. It counts in binary from 0 to 15 on each rising edge of the clock when enabled.','It counts in binary sequence from 0 to 15 (0000 to 1111) with all flip-flops triggered simultaneously by a common clock, ensuring accurate and glitch-free counting.',NULL,'products/1771828019344-938338244.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:48:28'),
(1063,'LM741',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM741 is a classic single operational amplifier (op-amp) IC widely used for analog signal amplification and processing.','LM741 is a general-purpose operational amplifier (op-amp) IC widely used in analog signal amplification and processing. It typically operates with dual power supplies (for example ±12 V or ±15 V) and offers high gain, internal frequency compensation, and stable operation.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771918234696-675644434.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:30:34'),
(1064,'LM723',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM723 is a precision voltage regulator IC designed to build highly stable and adjustable power supplies.','LM723 is a precision voltage regulator IC used to design adjustable and fixed DC power supplies. It includes an internal voltage reference, error amplifier, pass transistor driver, and current limiting, allowing flexible regulation over a wide voltage range.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771918213011-816139047.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:30:13'),
(1065,'LM747',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM747 is a dual operational amplifier (op-amp) integrated circuit that contains two independent general-purpose op-amps in a single package','LM747 is a dual operational amplifier (op-amp) IC, essentially two LM741-type op-amps in a single package. It is designed for general-purpose analog applications and typically operates with dual power supplies',NULL,NULL,'products/1771918258491-281165469.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:30:58'),
(1066,'74LS164','74LS164',NULL,'74LS164',99.00,'The 74LS164 is an 8-bit serial-in, parallel-out shift register belonging to the TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) 74LS family. It is designed to accept serial data and convert it into parallel outputs, making it ideal for expanding output lines in digital systems. ','74LS164 is a TTL 8-bit serial-in, parallel-out (SIPO) shift register IC. It accepts serial data input and shifts it into eight parallel outputs on each clock pulse. It operates from a 5 V supply and includes an asynchronous clear to reset all outputs.','The IC features two serial data inputs (A and B) which are internally AND-gated, allowing flexible data control.',NULL,'products/1771828043946-577591579.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:51:27'),
(1067,'LM2903',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM2903 is a dual voltage comparator integrated circuit that contains two independent, high-gain comparators in a single package','LM2903 is a dual voltage comparator IC, functionally similar to the LM393, designed for automotive and industrial applications. It operates from a single power supply over a wide voltage range and features open-collector outputs for flexible interfacing.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771916832827-448113852.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:07:12'),
(1068,'74LS240','74LS240',NULL,'74LS240',99.00,'The 74LS240 is an octal buffer and line driver with tri-state outputs, belonging to the TTL 74LS (Low-Power Schottky) logic family. It is designed to buffer and drive data buses while providing controlled output enable functionality. ','74LS240 is a TTL octal buffer/line driver IC with inverting outputs and tri-state control. It operates from a 5 V supply and belongs to the Low-Power Schottky (LS) series, offering good speed with reduced power consumption.','The IC contains eight independent non-inverting buffers, divided into two groups of four, each group controlled by its own active-LOW enable pin.',NULL,'products/1771828133527-499181330.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:54:40'),
(1069,'LM2904',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM2904 is a dual operational amplifier (op-amp) IC, functionally similar to the LM358, designed for single-supply operation over a wide voltage range. It offers low power consumption and can operate from single or dual power supplies, making it suitable for many analog applications.','The LM2904 is commonly used in signal amplification, sensor interfacing, active filters, and control circuits, especially in automotive and industrial environments where reliability and wide temperature operation are required.','LM2904 is a dual low-power operational amplifier (op-amp) IC designed for single-supply operation',NULL,'products/1771916853296-409666147.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:07:33'),
(1070,'LM2907',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM2907 is a frequency-to-voltage (F/V) converter integrated circuit that converts an input frequency signal into a proportional DC voltage output.','LM2907 is a frequency-to-voltage converter IC that converts an input frequency signal into a proportional DC output voltage. It is designed for tachometer and speed-sensing applications and can operate from a wide supply voltage range, making it suitable for automotive and industrial use.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771916879773-55588666.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:07:59'),
(1071,'LM2917',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM2917 is a frequency-to-voltage (F/V) converter IC that converts an input frequency or pulse signal into a proportional DC output voltage','LM2917 is a frequency-to-voltage converter IC with an integrated Zener voltage regulator, making it especially suitable for automotive and industrial applications. It converts an input frequency (such as pulses from a sensor) into a proportional DC output voltage.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771916901448-339490984.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:08:21'),
(1072,'IC AMS1117 3.3V',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'IC AMS1117 3.3V is a fixed 3.3V low-dropout (LDO) linear voltage regulator IC designed to provide a stable and reliable 3.3V output from a higher input voltage.','IC AMS1117 3.3V is a low-dropout (LDO) linear voltage regulator IC that provides a fixed 3.3 V regulated output. It can deliver up to 800 mA output current with a low dropout voltage, making it suitable for converting higher DC voltages to 3.3 V efficiently.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771916459493-614392262.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-04-06 14:18:27'),
(1073,'LM2931  TO 92',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM2931 (TO-92) is a low dropout (LDO) linear voltage regulator IC designed for automotive and industrial applications where a stable regulated voltage is required even when the input voltage is close to the output voltage','The LM2931 in TO-92 package provides a stable regulated output voltage even when the input voltage is only slightly higher than the output (low dropout).','It is known for reverse-battery protection, load dump protection, and low quiescent current, making it ideal for battery-powered and vehicle applications. The TO-92 package is compact and suitable for low-current circuits.',NULL,'products/1771916922786-435420924.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:08:42'),
(1074,'74LS244','74LS244',NULL,'74LS244',99.00,'The 74LS244 is an octal buffer and line driver with tri-state outputs, belonging to the 74LS (Low-Power Schottky) TTL logic family. It is designed to buffer, isolate, and drive data lines in digital systems while allowing multiple devices to share a common bus. The IC consists of eight non-inverting buffers, arranged in two groups of four, with each group controlled by its own active-LOW output enable pin. ','The 74LS244 contains eight non-inverting buffers with two independent enable (OE) controls, allowing it to drive data buses efficiently. I','When the enable input is inactive, the corresponding outputs enter a high-impedance (Hi-Z) state, preventing bus contention.',NULL,'products/1771828168077-803586611.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:55:04'),
(1075,'LM2575t-5',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM2575T-5 is a fixed 5V step-down (buck) switching voltage regulator IC designed to efficiently convert a higher DC input voltage into a stable 5V output','The LM2575T-5 efficiently converts a higher DC input voltage into a regulated 5V output using switching technology, delivering up to 1A output current with high efficiency. It operates at 52 kHz, requires few external components, and includes thermal shutdown and current-limit protection, making it suitable for compact and reliable power supply designs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771916749957-481787825.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:05:49'),
(1076,'LM2575T -ADJ',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM2575T-ADJ is an adjustable step-down (buck) switching voltage regulator IC used to efficiently convert a higher DC input voltage into a lower, adjustable DC output voltage.','The LM2575T-ADJ efficiently converts a higher DC input voltage to a user-set output voltage using external resistors. It can deliver up to 1A output current with good efficiency and operates at a 52 kHz switching frequency.','With built-in current limiting and thermal shutdown, it is reliable and easy to use for custom power supply designs.',NULL,'products/1771916725108-940409050.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:05:25'),
(1077,'LM2576 T-ADJ',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM2576T-ADJ is a high-current adjustable step-down (buck) switching voltage regulator IC designed to efficiently convert a higher DC input voltage into a lower, adjustable DC output voltage.','The LM2576T-ADJ converts a higher DC input voltage into a user-adjustable regulated output using external resistors.','It can supply up to 3A output current with high efficiency and operates at a 52 kHz switching frequency. With built-in thermal shutdown, current limiting, and safe-area protection, it is widely used in robust power supply designs.',NULL,'products/1771916808891-233195122.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:06:48'),
(1078,'LM2576 -5V',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM2576-5.0 is a fixed 5V step-down (buck) switching voltage regulator IC capable of delivering up to 3A output current.','The LM2576-5V efficiently converts a higher DC input voltage into a stable 5V output and can deliver up to 3A output current.','It operates at a 52 kHz switching frequency and needs only a few external components. With built-in thermal shutdown, current limiting, and short-circuit protection, it is ideal for high-current 5V power supplies.',NULL,'products/1771916776547-471138058.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:06:16'),
(1079,'74HC148','74HC148',NULL,'74HC148',99.00,'The 74HC148 is an 8-to-3 priority encoder from the high-speed CMOS (HC) logic family, designed to encode up to eight active-LOW input signals into a 3-bit binary output.','The 74HC148 encodes eight active-LOW input signals into a 3-bit binary output, giving priority to the highest-order input when multiple inputs are active at the same time.','Built using High-Speed CMOS (HC) technology, it offers low power consumption and high noise immunity compared to TTL devices.',NULL,'products/1772525087510-478343866.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:04:47'),
(1080,'LM2936 ( TO92)',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM2936 in the TO-92 package is a low dropout (LDO) linear voltage regulator designed to provide a stable regulated output with very low quiescent current.','The LM2936 in TO-92 package provides a stable regulated output with very low dropout voltage and low quiescent current, making it ideal for long-life battery systems. It includes reverse battery protection, short-circuit protection, and thermal shutdown, ensuring reliable operation in harsh environments.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771916943663-350616855.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:09:03'),
(1081,'LM2950- 3.3V',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM2950-3.3V is a fixed 3.3V low-dropout (LDO) linear voltage regulator designed for automotive, industrial, and battery-powered applications','The LM2950-3.3V provides a stable 3.3V regulated output with very low dropout voltage and low quiescent current, helping extend battery life. It includes reverse battery protection, short-circuit protection, and thermal shutdown, making it reliable for harsh electrical environments.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771917234022-511019505.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:13:54'),
(1082,'LM2950- 5V',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM2950-5V is a fixed 5V low-dropout (LDO) linear voltage regulator designed to deliver a stable 5V output with very low quiescent (standby) current.','The LM2950-5V provides a stable 5V output with low dropout voltage and very low quiescent current, making it ideal for systems that must stay powered during low battery conditions. It features reverse battery protection, short-circuit protection, and thermal shutdown for reliable operation.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771917251389-496878395.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:14:11'),
(1083,'SLIM54HC163',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'SLIM 54HC163 is a high-speed CMOS 4-bit synchronous binary counter designed for reliable counting applications in digital systems.','',NULL,NULL,'products/1772001183201-532930675.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 06:33:03'),
(1084,'LM2940',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM2940 is a high-current low dropout (LDO) linear voltage regulator IC designed mainly for automotive and industrial applications.','The LM2940 provides a stable regulated output even with a small difference between input and output voltage (low dropout). It can supply up to 1A output current and includes reverse battery protection, load dump protection, and thermal shutdown, making it highly reliable in harsh automotive environments.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771917214572-340991763.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:13:34'),
(1085,'74LS273','74LS273',NULL,'74LS273',99.00,'The 74LS273 is an octal D-type flip-flop with a common clock and asynchronous clear, belonging to the 74LS (Low-Power Schottky) TTL logic family. It contains eight edge-triggered D flip-flops that store 8 bits of data simultaneously. Data present at the D inputs is latched to the Q outputs on the rising edge of the clock. An active-LOW asynchronous clear input resets all outputs to LOW instantly, independent of the clock.','The 74LS273 stores 8 bits of data on the rising edge of the clock and holds the data until the next clock pulse. It features an active-LOW asynchronous clear that resets all outputs to zero. Built using LS (Low-power Schottky) TTL technology, it offers fast and reliable data storage for digital systems.','Data present at the D inputs is latched to the Q outputs on the rising edge of the clock. An active-LOW asynchronous clear input resets all outputs to LOW instantly, independent of the clock.',NULL,'products/1771828192985-243041845.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:55:40'),
(1086,'LM3914',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM3914 is an LED display driver IC used to visualize analog voltage levels with a linear scale.','The LM3914 drives up to 10 LEDs to display an analog signal level in either dot mode (single LED on) or bar mode (multiple LEDs on). It has a built-in voltage reference and resistor network, allowing easy adjustment of display range and LED current with minimal external components.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771917797340-722755724.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:23:17'),
(1087,'LM3915',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM3915 is an LED display driver IC used to indicate analog signal levels on a logarithmic (3 dB per step) scale.','The LM3915 drives 10 LEDs to display an analog input level on a logarithmic (3 dB per step) scale, which closely matches the human ear’s response to sound. It supports both dot mode and bar mode operation and includes a built-in voltage reference and adjustable LED current, requiring very few external components.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771918029192-996340503.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:27:09'),
(1088,'SLIMHC164',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The 54HC164 is a high-speed CMOS 8-bit serial-in, parallel-out shift register designed for reliable digital data shifting and storage applications.','',NULL,NULL,'products/1772001202796-96677726.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 06:33:22'),
(1089,'74LS280','74LS280',NULL,'74LS280',99.00,'The 74LS280 is a 9-bit parity generator and parity checker IC from the 74LS (Low-Power Schottky) TTL logic family. It is designed to generate or verify parity bits for digital data, helping detect data transmission and storage errors. The device accepts eight or nine parallel data inputs and produces both even and odd parity outputs.','The 74LS280 generates or checks even and odd parity for 9 input bits, helping detect data transmission or storage errors. It is built using LS (Low-power Schottky) TTL technology, offering fast operation and reliable logic performance in bus and communication circuits.','The device accepts eight or nine parallel data inputs and produces both even and odd parity outputs.',NULL,'products/1771828216443-174644120.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:56:05'),
(1090,'74LS373','74LS373',NULL,'74LS373',99.00,'The 74LS373 is an octal transparent D-type latch with tri-state outputs, part of the 74LS (Low-Power Schottky) TTL logic family. It is designed to temporarily store and hold 8 bits of data in digital systems. When the Latch Enable (LE) input is HIGH, the outputs follow the inputs (transparent mode). When LE goes LOW, the data present at the inputs is latched and held at the outputs.','The 74LS373 allows 8-bit data to pass directly to the outputs when the Latch Enable (LE) is HIGH. When LE goes LOW, the data is latched and held. ','Its tri-state outputs enable easy connection to shared data buses. Built with LS (Low-power Schottky) TTL technology, it provides fast and reliable operation.',NULL,'products/1771828307804-350850531.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:57:47'),
(1091,'54hc193',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The 54HC193 is a high-speed CMOS 4-bit synchronous up/down binary counter that belongs to the 54HC logic family and operates over a wide military-grade temperature range','',NULL,NULL,'products/1771822157045-117282787.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 04:49:17'),
(1092,'74LS374','74LS374',NULL,'74LS374',99.00,'The 74LS374 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It contains eight D-type flip-flops that are positive-edge-triggered, meaning data present at the inputs is stored on the rising edge of the clock.','The 74LS374 stores 8 bits of data on the rising edge of the clock. Its tri-state outputs allow multiple devices to share a common data bus, while the Output Enable (OE) pin controls when the stored data appears on the outputs.',' Built using LS (Low-power Schottky) TTL technology, it provides fast and reliable data latching.',NULL,'products/1771828375845-20641039.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:58:15'),
(1093,'74LS595','74LS595',NULL,'74LS595',99.00,'The 74LS595 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit from the Low-Power Schottky (LS) family. It functions as an 8-bit serial-in, parallel-out (SIPO) shift register with a separate storage register (latch) and 3-state outputs.','The 74LS595 accepts serial data input and shifts it on each clock pulse, then transfers the data to 8 parallel outputs using a latch clock. Its tri-state outputs allow easy connection to shared data buses. Built with LS (Low-power Schottky) TTL technology, it is commonly used to expand output pins in digital systems.','Its tri-state outputs allow easy connection to shared data buses. Built with LS (Low-power Schottky) TTL technology, it is commonly used to expand output pins in digital systems.',NULL,'products/1771828514936-823678280.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:59:59'),
(1094,'7406','7406',NULL,'7406 IC',99.00,'The 7406 is a TTL (Transistor-Transistor Logic) integrated circuit that contains six independent inverters (NOT gates) with open-collector outputs.Each inverter outputs the logical opposite of its input, but unlike standard inverter ICs, the open-collector design allows the outputs to sink higher current and interface with higher-voltage loads using an external pull-up resistor.','The 7406 contains six independent inverters with open-collector outputs, allowing it to drive higher-voltage loads, relays, or LEDs using external pull-up resistors. It is especially useful for level interfacing and bus driving where wired-OR logic is needed.','Each inverter outputs the logical opposite of its input, but unlike standard inverter ICs, the open-collector design allows the outputs to sink higher current and interface with higher-voltage loads using an external pull-up resistor.',NULL,'products/1771825452467-86536781.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 07:47:01'),
(1095,'7407','7407',NULL,'7407',99.00,'7407 IC is a TTL hex non-inverting buffer/driver with open-collector outputs, designed for interfacing logic circuits with higher-voltage or higher-current loads. It contains six independent buffer stages that reproduce the input logic level at the output without inversion. ','The 7407 contains six independent non-inverting buffers with open-collector outputs, allowing it to drive higher-voltage loads, LEDs, or relays using external pull-up resistors. It is commonly used for level interfacing, signal buffering, and wired-OR applications.','Because of its open-collector configuration, the outputs require external pull-up resistors and can be connected to voltages higher than the IC’s supply, making the 7407 ideal for driving relays, lamps, LEDs, and other external devices.',NULL,'products/1771825549679-841391892.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 07:49:34'),
(1096,'54HC244',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The 54HC244 is a high-speed CMOS octal buffer/line driver with tri-state outputs, designed to provide increased driving capability for bus-oriented systems.','The 54HC244 is a high-speed CMOS octal buffer and line driver integrated circuit designed to improve signal strength and isolate digital circuits. It contains eight non-inverting buffers with 3-state outputs, making it ideal for data bus driving and signal buffering applications.','The 54HC244 belongs to the HC (High-Speed CMOS) logic family and is commonly used to increase fan-out, protect logic circuits, and drive long transmission lines. The IC has two independent groups of four buffers, each controlled by an output enable (OE) pin.',NULL,'products/1771822282448-372523296.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 04:51:22'),
(1097,'54HC245',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The 54HC245 (often seen as SN74HC245 / 74HC245) is an octal bidirectional bus transceiver integrated circuit widely used in digital electronics to manage data flow between two data buses.','The 54HC245 is a high-speed CMOS octal bus transceiver designed for bidirectional data communication between two data buses. It allows digital data to move in either direction while providing buffering and electrical isolation between circuits.','The 54HC245 belongs to the HC (High-Speed CMOS) logic family and contains eight bidirectional buffers with 3-state outputs. A Direction (DIR) control pin determines the data flow direction, while an Output Enable (OE) pin controls whether the outputs are active or placed in a high-impedance state.',NULL,'products/1771822332515-577744328.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 04:52:12'),
(1098,'74ALS175','74ALS175',NULL,'74ALS175',99.00,'The 74ALS175 IC is a quad D-type flip-flop with a common clock and asynchronous clear, belonging to the Advanced Low-Power Schottky (ALS) TTL family. It contains four independent D flip-flops, each storing one bit of data. On the rising edge of the clock, the data present at each D input is transferred to its corresponding Q output simultaneously.','The 74ALS175 contains four edge-triggered D flip-flops that store data on the rising edge of the clock. An active-LOW asynchronous clear resets all outputs simultaneously. Built using ALS (Advanced Low-power Schottky) TTL technology, it offers faster switching and lower power consumption than standard LS devices.','The asynchronous clear (CLR) input resets all outputs to logic LOW regardless of the clock state, making it useful for system initialization.',NULL,'products/1771825638280-344189501.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 07:52:38'),
(1099,'74F10','74F10',NULL,'74F10',10.00,'74F10 IC is a triple 3-input NAND gate from the Fast TTL (74F) logic family, designed for high-speed digital applications. It contains three independent NAND gates, each accepting three inputs and producing a LOW output only when all three inputs are HIGH. Compared to standard 74LS devices, the 74F10 offers significantly faster propagation delays, making it suitable for high-frequency logic circuits.','The 74F10 contains three independent NAND gates, each with three inputs, providing very high-speed switching performance compared to LS devices. It is used in digital logic circuits where fast propagation delay is critical.','Compared to standard 74LS devices, the 74F10 offers significantly faster propagation delays, making it suitable for high-frequency logic circuits.',NULL,'products/1771825745824-129709861.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 07:55:36'),
(1100,'54HC259',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The 54HC259 is a high-speed CMOS 8-bit addressable latch from the 54HC logic family, designed for reliable data storage and control applications.','The 54HC259 is a high-speed CMOS 8-bit addressable latch integrated circuit used to store and control individual output lines using binary address inputs. It allows one selected output to be set or reset without affecting the other outputs, making it useful for digital control and memory selection applications.','The 54HC259 belongs to the HC (High-Speed CMOS) logic family and contains eight latch outputs that can be individually controlled through a 3-bit address input. A selected output can be set HIGH or LOW using data and enable control signals.',NULL,'products/1771822383771-977902725.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 04:53:03'),
(1101,'74F521','74F521',NULL,'74F521',10.00,'74F521 IC is an 8-bit identity comparator from the Fast TTL (74F) logic family, designed for high-speed digital comparison applications. It compares two 8-bit binary words (A0–A7 and B0–B7) and produces an equality output (A = B) when all corresponding bits are identical.','The 74F521 compares two 8-bit binary words and provides an output indicating whether the two values are exactly equal. Designed with Fast TTL technology, it offers very low propagation delay, making it suitable for high-speed comparison tasks in digital systems.','The device also includes cascade inputs and outputs, allowing multiple 74F521 ICs to be connected together for comparing larger word lengths such as 16-bit or 32-bit data.',NULL,'products/1771825774553-490646700.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 07:56:11'),
(1102,'74123','74123',NULL,'74123',99.00,'74123 IC is a dual retriggerable monostable multivibrator from the TTL 74-series, designed to generate precise timing pulses. It contains two independent one-shot circuits, each capable of producing a stable output pulse whose width is determined by external resistor (R) and capacitor (C) values.','The 74123 contains two independent retriggerable one-shot timers. Each section can generate a precise output pulse whose width is set by an external resistor and capacitor (RC). Because it is retriggerable, a new trigger arriving before the timing cycle ends will extend the output pulse, making it useful for pulse shaping and timing control.','The 74123 can be retriggered during the output pulse, which extends the pulse duration as long as trigger inputs continue making it ideal for pulse stretching and noise filtering.',NULL,'products/1771825583436-229512116.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 07:51:04'),
(1103,'74174','74174',NULL,'74174',99.00,'74174 IC is a hex D-type flip-flop from the TTL 74-series, designed for parallel data storage and transfer. It contains six independent D flip-flops that share a common clock (CLK) and an asynchronous clear (CLR) input. On the rising edge of the clock, data present at each D input is simultaneously latched and transferred to the corresponding Q output. ','The 74123 contains two independent retriggerable one-shot timers. Each section can generate a precise output pulse whose width is set by an external resistor and capacitor (RC). Because it is retriggerable, a new trigger arriving before the timing cycle ends will extend the output pulse, making it useful for pulse shaping and timing control.','The asynchronous clear resets all outputs to logic LOW regardless of the clock state, which is useful for system initialization.',NULL,'products/1771825613410-512438654.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 07:51:53'),
(1104,'75176','75176',NULL,'75176',99.00,'75176 IC is a differential bus transceiver designed for RS-485 and RS-422 communication systems. It integrates both a line driver and a line receiver in a single package, allowing half-duplex serial communication over long distances using balanced differential signaling. The driver and receiver can be independently enabled or disabled, which helps reduce power consumption and allows multiple devices to share the same bus.','The 75176 supports half-duplex differential data transmission, allowing reliable communication over long distances and in noisy environments. It features tri-state outputs so multiple devices can share the same bus, and it is commonly used in industrial and embedded serial communication systems.','The driver and receiver can be independently enabled or disabled, which helps reduce power consumption and allows multiple devices to share the same bus.',NULL,'products/1771828817909-871234072.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 09:05:31'),
(1105,'54HC273',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The 54HC273 is an 8-bit D-type edge-triggered register built using High-Speed CMOS (HC) technology, designed for reliable data storage in digital systems.','The 54HC273 is a high-speed CMOS octal D-type flip-flop integrated circuit featuring eight edge-triggered storage registers with a common clock and asynchronous clear input. It is widely used for data storage, buffering, and synchronization in digital systems.','The 54HC273 belongs to the HC (High-Speed CMOS) logic family and contains eight D flip-flops sharing a single clock signal. Data present at the input pins is transferred to the outputs simultaneously on the rising edge of the clock.',NULL,'products/1771822443092-143705697.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 04:54:03'),
(1106,'54HC367',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The 54HC367 is a high-speed CMOS hex buffer/line driver IC designed to improve signal integrity and provide increased drive capability in digital circuits.','The 54HC367 is a high-speed CMOS hex buffer/line driver with inverting outputs and 3-state control, designed to strengthen digital signals and isolate circuits in data bus systems. It contains six independent buffer drivers divided into two enable-controlled groups.','The 54HC367 belongs to the HC (High-Speed CMOS) logic family and is used to buffer, invert, and drive digital signals over longer distances or higher loads. Each buffer output is the logical inverse of its input.',NULL,'products/1771822485276-938764514.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 04:54:45'),
(1107,'54HC373',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The 54HC373 is a high-speed CMOS octal transparent latch from the 54HC logic family, designed for applications requiring temporary data storage and bus interfacing','The 54HC373 is a high-speed CMOS octal transparent latch with 3-state outputs, used for temporary data storage and bus interfacing in digital systems. It can store 8-bit data and hold it stable at the output until new data is latched.','The 54HC373 belongs to the HC (High-Speed CMOS) logic family and contains eight D-type latches with a common Latch Enable (LE) and Output Enable (OE) control.',NULL,'products/1771822536311-792640478.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 04:55:36'),
(1108,'75477','75477',NULL,'75477',99.00,'75477 IC is a dual retriggerable monostable multivibrator designed primarily for timing, pulse generation, and audio signal applications. Each section of the IC functions as a one-shot circuit whose output pulse width is controlled by external resistor and capacitor (RC) components. ','The 75477 contains two independent timing sections that can be configured to generate tones, alarms, sirens, pulse sounds, or timing delays using external resistors and capacitors. It supports astable and monostable operation, making it very flexible for audio and control circuits.','The 75477 supports retriggering, meaning the output pulse can be extended if a new trigger occurs before the previous timing cycle ends.',NULL,'products/1771828844335-625646639.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 09:06:27'),
(1109,'54HC374',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The 54HC374 is a high-speed CMOS octal D-type flip-flop with 3-state outputs, designed for buffering and registering 8-bit data in digital systems.','The 54HC374 is a high-speed CMOS octal D-type edge-triggered flip-flop with 3-state outputs, used for synchronized data storage and bus interfacing in digital electronic systems. It stores 8-bit data simultaneously and transfers it to outputs on a clock signal.','The 54HC374 belongs to the HC (High-Speed CMOS) logic family and consists of eight D flip-flops sharing a common clock input. Data applied at the inputs is captured on the rising edge of the clock and held until the next clock pulse.',NULL,'products/1771822585518-111621532.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 04:56:25'),
(1110,'75110','75110',NULL,'75110',99.00,'75110 IC is a dual line driver and receiver designed for balanced differential data transmission, commonly used in RS-422 and early serial communication systems. It integrates two differential drivers and two differential receivers in a single package, allowing reliable data transfer over long distances with high noise immunity. Operating from a single 5V supply, the 75110 supports high-speed data communication while maintaining stable performance in electrically noisy environments.','The 75110 is designed to drive balanced (differential) transmission lines, improving noise immunity and signal integrity over longer cable distances. It is commonly paired with compatible line receivers in industrial and communication interfaces, especially where reliable data transfer is required.','It is commonly paired with compatible line receivers in industrial and communication interfaces, especially where reliable data transfer is required.',NULL,'products/1771828796887-334849202.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 09:04:53'),
(1111,'54HC541',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The 54HC541 is a high-speed CMOS octal buffer/line driver with three-state outputs, designed for reliable data buffering and bus driving applications.','The 54HC541 is a high-speed CMOS octal buffer and line driver with non-inverting 3-state outputs, designed to strengthen digital signals and isolate circuits in data bus systems. It is commonly used for memory addressing, bus buffering, and signal driving applications.','The 54HC541 belongs to the HC (High-Speed CMOS) logic family and contains eight independent non-inverting buffers. The IC includes two output enable pins that control all outputs, allowing the device to disconnect from a shared data bus by entering a high-impedance (Hi-Z) state.',NULL,'products/1771822821627-875667652.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 05:00:21'),
(1112,'54HC573',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The 54HC573 is a high-speed CMOS octal transparent latch with 3-state outputs, designed for buffering and temporary storage of 8-bit data.','The 54HC573 is a high-speed CMOS octal transparent latch with 3-state outputs, used for temporary data storage and bus interfacing in digital electronic systems. It stores 8-bit data and holds it stable until new data is latched.','The 54HC573 belongs to the HC (High-Speed CMOS) logic family and contains eight D-type latches controlled by a common Latch Enable (LE) and Output Enable (OE) signal.',NULL,'products/1771822868749-646763875.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 05:01:08'),
(1113,'54HC574',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The 54HC574 is a high-speed CMOS octal D-type edge-triggered flip-flop with 3-state outputs, designed for reliable data storage and bus-oriented digital systems','The 54HC574 is a high-speed CMOS octal D-type edge-triggered flip-flop with 3-state outputs, designed for synchronized data storage and bus-oriented digital systems. It stores 8-bit data simultaneously and transfers it to outputs on a clock signal.','The 54HC574 belongs to the HC (High-Speed CMOS) logic family and contains eight edge-triggered D flip-flops sharing a common clock input. Data present at the inputs is captured on the rising edge of the clock and held until the next clock pulse.',NULL,'products/1771822917422-329473058.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 05:01:57'),
(1114,'54HC595',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The 54HC595 is an 8-bit serial-in, parallel-out shift register with an integrated output latch, widely used to expand the number of digital outputs from a microcontroller using only a few pins. It operates on high-speed CMOS (HC) technology','The 54HC595 is a high-speed CMOS 8-bit serial-in, parallel-out (SIPO) shift register with an output storage latch and 3-state outputs. It is widely used to expand microcontroller output pins and control LEDs, displays, and digital devices using only a few control lines.','The 54HC595 belongs to the HC (High-Speed CMOS) logic family and combines a shift register and a storage register (latch) in one IC. Data is entered serially (one bit at a time) and then transferred simultaneously to parallel outputs.',NULL,'products/1771822971901-164887523.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 05:02:51'),
(1115,'54HC4052',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The 54HC4052 is a high-speed CMOS dual 4-channel analog multiplexer/demultiplexer IC that allows bidirectional switching of analog or digital signals.','The 54HC4052 is a high-speed CMOS dual 4-channel analog multiplexer/demultiplexer IC used to switch analog or digital signals between multiple inputs and a single output line. It allows one of four channels to be selected electronically using binary control signals.','The 54HC4052 belongs to the HC CMOS logic family and contains two independent 4-channel multiplexers inside one IC. Each multiplexer can route one of four inputs to a common output',NULL,'products/1771822630373-134501283.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 04:57:10'),
(1116,'54HC4075',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The 54HC4075 is a High-Speed CMOS Triple 3-Input OR Gate integrated circuit from the 54HC logic family, designed for reliable digital signal processing in high-performance and industrial applications','The 54HC4075 is a high-speed CMOS Triple 3-Input OR Gate integrated circuit. It contains three independent OR gates, each having three inputs and one output, used in digital logic circuits for combining multiple signals into a single output.','The 54HC4075 belongs to the HC (High-Speed CMOS) logic family and performs the logical OR operation. The output of each gate becomes HIGH when any one or more inputs are HIGH.',NULL,'products/1771822732368-900186824.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 04:58:52'),
(1117,'54HC4538',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The 54HC4538 is a dual precision retriggerable monostable multivibrator IC fabricated using High-Speed CMOS (HC) technology, designed for applications requiring accurate and stable timing pulses.','The 54HC4538 is a high-speed CMOS dual precision monostable multivibrator, commonly called a one-shot timer IC. It generates a single output pulse of controlled duration when triggered by an input signal. The pulse width is determined using an external resistor and capacitor.','The 54HC4538 contains two independent monostable circuits in a single IC. Each section produces a precise output pulse when triggered by a rising or falling edge input. Unlike simple timer circuits, this IC provides stable and accurate timing that is largely independent of supply voltage variations.',NULL,'products/1771822778607-978818681.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 04:59:38'),
(1118,'74HCT02','74HCT02',NULL,'74HCT02',99.00,'The 74HCT02 is a high-speed CMOS Quad 2-Input NOR gate IC that contains four independent NOR logic gates within a single package','The 74HCT02 contains four independent NOR gates, each with two inputs. It operates on CMOS technology for low power consumption while maintaining TTL-compatible input levels, making it ideal for interfacing CMOS circuits with TTL logic.','It operates on CMOS technology for low power consumption while maintaining TTL-compatible input levels, making it ideal for interfacing CMOS circuits with TTL logic.',NULL,'products/1771826181927-275627410.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:25:00'),
(1119,'74HCT14','74HCT14',NULL,'74HCT14',99.00,'The 74HCT14 is a Hex Schmitt Trigger Inverter IC from the High-Speed CMOS (HCT) logic family, designed to operate at 5V TTL-compatible input levels.','The 74HCT14 contains six inverters, each with Schmitt-trigger inputs, which provide hysteresis for clean and stable switching. This makes it excellent for noisy signals, slow-changing inputs, and switch debouncing, while still accepting TTL-level inputs at a 5V supply.','This makes it excellent for noisy signals, slow-changing inputs, and switch debouncing, while still accepting TTL-level inputs at a 5V supply.',NULL,'products/1771826284579-471791335.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:27:06'),
(1120,'74HCT138','74HCT138',NULL,'74HCT138',99.00,'The 74HCT138 is a high-speed CMOS 3-to-8 line decoder / demultiplexer designed to be fully compatible with TTL logic levels','The 74HCT138 takes 3 binary address inputs and decodes them into one of 8 active-LOW outputs. It includes three enable pins (two active-LOW, one active-HIGH) for flexible control and cascading. With TTL-compatible inputs and low CMOS power consumption, it’s ideal for address decoding in mixed TTL/CMOS systems.','It includes three enable pins (two active-LOW, one active-HIGH) for flexible control and cascading. With TTL-compatible inputs and low CMOS power consumption, it’s ideal for address decoding in mixed TTL/CMOS systems.',NULL,'products/1771826203768-125620987.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:26:14'),
(1121,'74HCT244','74HCT244',NULL,'74HCT244',99.00,'The 74HCT244 is a high-speed octal buffer and line driver designed for digital signal buffering and bus interfacing applications.','The 74HCT244 contains eight non-inverting buffers arranged in two groups of four, each controlled by its own active-LOW output enable (OE). ','With TTL-level input compatibility and low CMOS power consumption, it is ideal for bus driving and signal buffering in mixed TTL/CMOS systems.',NULL,'products/1771826308220-441920410.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:28:40'),
(1122,'74HCT245','74HCT245',NULL,'74HCT245',99.00,'The 74HCT245 is an octal bidirectional bus transceiver designed for reliable data transfer between two 8-bit data buses. It operates on a 5V power supply and is TTL-compatible, making it ideal for interfacing between standard TTL logic and CMOS systems.','The 74HCT245 allows 8-bit data to flow in either direction between two buses using a DIR (direction control) pin. Its active-LOW Output Enable (OE) places the outputs in high-impedance when disabled. ','With TTL-compatible inputs and low CMOS power consumption, it’s ideal for interfacing TTL logic with CMOS buses.',NULL,'products/1771826331280-319824204.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:31:00'),
(1123,'74HCT273','74HCT273',NULL,'74HCT273',99.00,'The 74HCT273 is an octal D-type flip-flop integrated circuit designed for use in digital storage and data-latching applications.','The 74HCT273 stores 8 bits of data on the rising edge of the clock and holds the data until the next clock event. An active-LOW asynchronous clear resets all outputs to zero instantly. ','With TTL-level input compatibility and low CMOS power consumption, it’s ideal for mixed TTL/CMOS digital systems.',NULL,'products/1771826369428-12378661.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:31:52'),
(1124,'74HCT374','74HCT374',NULL,'74HCT374',99.00,'74HCT374 is an octal D-type edge-triggered flip-flop with 3-state outputs, designed for use in digital systems where temporary data storage and bus interfacing are required.','The 74HCT374 captures 8 bits of data on the rising edge of the clock and holds them until the next clock pulse. Its tri-state outputs, controlled by an active-LOW Output Enable (OE), allow multiple devices to share a common data bus. ','With TTL-compatible inputs and low CMOS power consumption, it’s ideal for mixed TTL/CMOS systems.',NULL,'products/1771826394189-246411764.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:33:12'),
(1125,'74HCT573','74HCT573',NULL,'74HCT573',99.00,'The 74HCT573 is an octal transparent latch designed for high-speed data storage and buffering applications.','The 74HCT573 allows 8-bit data to pass directly to the outputs when the Latch Enable (LE) is HIGH. When LE goes LOW, the data is latched and held. ','Its tri-state outputs, controlled by an active-LOW Output Enable (OE), make it ideal for shared data buses.',NULL,'products/1771826420840-234526999.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:35:19'),
(1126,'74HCT574','74HCT574',NULL,'74HCT574',99.00,'The 74HCT574 is an octal D-type flip-flop integrated circuit with edge-triggered operation and tri-state outputs, designed for high-speed digital data storage and transfer','The 74HCT574 captures 8-bit data on the rising edge of the clock and stores it until the next clock event. Its tri-state outputs, controlled by an active-LOW Output Enable (OE), allow multiple devices to share a common data bus.','Its tri-state outputs, controlled by an active-LOW Output Enable (OE), allow multiple devices to share a common data bus.',NULL,'products/1771826440543-51507725.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 08:36:22'),
(1127,'HT1380',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The HT1380 is a low-power real-time clock (RTC) integrated circuit designed to provide accurate timekeeping functions such as seconds, minutes, hours, day, date, month, and year tracking','The HT1380 keeps track of seconds, minutes, hours, day, date, month, and year, with automatic leap-year correction.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771910849450-421474903.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 05:27:29'),
(1128,'HT9170',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'HT9170 is a DTMF (Dual Tone Multi-Frequency) decoder integrated circuit commonly used in telecommunication and remote control applications.','The HT9170 decodes DTMF tones (like those generated by telephone keypads) and converts them into a 4-bit digital output. It features high detection accuracy, noise immunity, and provides data valid and steering outputs for easy interfacing with microcontrollers or logic circuits.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771910890757-720445937.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 05:28:10'),
(1129,'HT12E&12D',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'HT12E and HT12D are commonly used encoder–decoder integrated circuits designed for simple remote control and wireless data transmission applications','The HT12E (Encoder) converts parallel address and data inputs into a serial data stream suitable for RF/IR transmission. The HT12D (Decoder) receives the serial data, checks the address, and then reproduces the original data outputs when a valid transmission is detected. This pair is widely used with 315 MHz / 433 MHz RF modules.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771910826766-547808433.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 05:27:06'),
(1130,'HT9020',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'HT9020 is a dedicated tone-signal decoding integrated circuit designed to reliably detect and decode standard dual-tone multi-frequency signals commonly used in telephone and remote control systems.','The HT9020 generates DTMF tone pairs corresponding to keypad inputs (0–9, *, #, A–D). When a key input is applied, it outputs the correct audio-frequency DTMF signal, which can be transmitted over telephone lines, RF links, or audio channels. It is often used together with DTMF decoders like HT9170 or MT8870.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771910869994-648305339.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 05:27:49'),
(1131,'APR6008',NULL,NULL,NULL,299.00,'The APR6008 is a standalone voice recording and playback integrated circuit designed for simple, non-volatile audio storage applications','The APR6008 allows recording and playback of human voice or audio using an external microphone and speaker. It stores audio in non-volatile analog memory, so the recorded sound is retained even when power is removed.','It stores audio in non-volatile analog memory, so the recorded sound is retained even when power is removed.',NULL,'products/1771833084040-376399246.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 10:28:30'),
(1132,'APR33A3C2',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The APR33A3C2 is a standalone voice recording and playback integrated circuit designed for simple, low-cost audio storage applications. I','The APR33A3C2 can record and play back voice or audio using an external microphone and speaker. It offers non-volatile analog storage, so recordings are retained even after power is removed. The IC supports multiple message segments, push-button or microcontroller control, and provides good audio quality for short voice prompts.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771833050368-350565110.jpg',0,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 10:14:01'),
(1133,'APR6016',NULL,NULL,'APR6016 IC',299.00,'APR 6016 is a single-chip analog voice recording and playback integrated circuit designed for simple audio storage applications.','The APR6016 allows recording and playback of voice or audio through an external microphone and speaker. It uses non-volatile analog memory, so recorded messages are retained even when power is removed.','It uses non-volatile analog memory, so recorded messages are retained even when power is removed.',NULL,'products/1771833107325-423330939.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 10:31:55'),
(1134,'APR89042',NULL,NULL,NULL,299.00,'The APR89042 is an integrated voice recording and playback IC designed for simple, reliable audio storage applications','The APR89042 allows recording and playback of voice or audio with even when power is removed. It supports multiple message segments, push-button or microcontroller control, and delivers better audio quality compared to older APR series ICs. Recording time depends on sampling mode and configuration.','Recording time depends on sampling mode and configuration.',NULL,'products/1771833127095-811768332.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 10:32:23'),
(1135,'APR89341',NULL,NULL,'APR89341 IC',299.00,'The APR89341 is a single-chip audio recording and playback IC designed for compact voice and sound applications.','The APR89341 can record and play back voice or audio using non-volatile analog memory, so recordings remain stored even when power is removed. It supports multiple message segments, keypad or microcontroller control, and provides clear audio output, making it suitable for professional voice announcement applications.','It supports multiple message segments, keypad or microcontroller control, and provides clear audio output, making it suitable for professional voice announcement applications.',NULL,'products/1771833146040-219095761.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 10:32:56'),
(1136,'AP89170',NULL,NULL,'AP89170 IC',99.00,'AP89170 is an integrated circuit commonly used in electronic control and signal-processing applications where stable and reliable performance is required.','The AP89170 allows recording and playback of voice or audio using non-volatile memory, so recorded messages are retained even after power is removed. It supports push-button control or microcontroller interfacing and provides clear audio output through an external speaker or amplifier, making it suitable for standalone voice modules.','It supports push-button control or microcontroller interfacing and provides clear audio output through an external speaker or amplifier, making it suitable for standalone voice modules.',NULL,'products/1771832309750-776873396.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 10:01:49'),
(1137,'AP9010',NULL,NULL,'AP9010 IC',99.00,'AP9010 is a compact power-management integrated circuit designed to provide stable and efficient voltage regulation in electronic systems.','The AP9010 allows recording and playback of voice or audio through an external microphone and speaker. It uses non-volatile memory, so recorded messages are retained even when power is turned off. ','With simple key control and low component count, it’s well suited for small, low-cost voice modules.',NULL,'products/1771832310535-691842836.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 10:02:33'),
(1138,'CD4001',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4001 is a CMOS quad 2-input NOR gate integrated circuit that contains four independent NOR logic gates within a single package.','The CD4001 contains four independent NOR gates, each with two inputs. Built with CMOS technology, it offers very low power consumption, wide operating voltage range, and good noise immunity, making it suitable for both digital logic and low-power applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771844632439-763855330.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:03:52'),
(1139,'CD4011',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'CD4011 is a CMOS quad 2-input NAND gate integrated circuit widely used in digital electronics for logic control and signal processing','The CD4011 contains four independent NAND gates, each with two inputs. Built using CMOS technology, it offers very low power consumption, high noise immunity, and a wide operating voltage range, making it suitable for both low-power and general-purpose digital logic applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771844680103-661014887.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:04:40'),
(1140,'CD4007',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4007 is a CMOS transistor array IC that contains three pairs of complementary MOSFETs (N-channel and P-channel) fabricated on a single chip.','The CD4007 contains three pairs of complementary MOS transistors (PMOS & NMOS) that can be configured as logic inverters, buffers, switches, or simple analog circuits. Unlike fixed-function logic gates, it exposes the transistors directly, making it useful for custom CMOS logic, learning CMOS operation, and building experimental circuits.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771844658690-43604806.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:04:18'),
(1141,'CD4015',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4015 is a CMOS dual 4-bit static shift register integrated circuit, designed for serial data storage and transfer in digital electronics','The CD4015 contains two independent 4-bit shift registers that can be clocked separately or cascaded to form an 8-bit shift register. It accepts serial data inputs and provides parallel outputs, making it useful for data storage, delay lines, and simple data manipulation. CMOS technology ensures low power consumption and wide operating voltage range.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771844703187-83986461.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:05:03'),
(1142,'CD4016',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4016 is a CMOS quad bilateral analog switch IC that contains four independent, electronically controlled switches.','The CD4016 contains four independent bilateral analog switches that can pass analog or digital signals in either direction when enabled. Each switch is controlled by a logic input and offers low power consumption and a wide operating voltage range, making it suitable for signal routing and switching applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771844753553-988638955.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:05:53'),
(1143,'IC HEF4017BP',NULL,NULL,NULL,69.00,'The IC HEF4017BP is a CMOS decade counter and divider IC that produces 10 sequential outputs from a single clock input.','The IC HEF4017BP counts incoming clock pulses and sequentially activates one of ten outputs (Q0–Q9) at a time. After the tenth pulse, it resets back to Q0. With low power consumption, wide operating voltage, and decoded outputs, it’s very popular for sequencing and LED chaser circuits.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845085308-328471908.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-04-07 13:20:00'),
(1144,'CD4018',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4018 is a CMOS presettable divide-by-N counter widely used in digital timing and frequency-division applications.','The CD4018 functions as a programmable frequency divider, where the division ratio (N) is set using external preset inputs. It counts clock pulses and provides a divided output frequency, making it useful for timing and clock-scaling applications. CMOS technology gives it low power consumption and a wide operating voltage range.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845103951-379661544.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:11:43'),
(1145,'CD4020',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4020 is a CMOS-based 14-stage binary ripple counter designed for low-power digital counting and frequency division applications.','The CD4020 counts incoming clock pulses and divides the input frequency by powers of two, providing multiple divided outputs (from ÷2 up to ÷16384). Built with CMOS technology, it offers very low power consumption, wide operating voltage range, and good noise immunity, making it ideal for timing and clock division applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845124324-341402459.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:12:04'),
(1146,'CD4021',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'CD4021 is a CMOS 8-stage static shift register with parallel inputs and serial output, commonly used to convert multiple parallel digital signals into a single serial data stream.','The CD4021 loads 8 parallel input bits simultaneously and then shifts them out serially on each clock pulse. It features a parallel load control, clock input, and serial output, making it ideal for reducing the number of input lines required by a microcontroller. CMOS technology ensures low power consumption and a wide operating voltage range.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845145582-798413808.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:12:25'),
(1147,'CD4023',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4023 is a CMOS logic integrated circuit that contains three independent 3-input NAND gates within a single package.','The CD4023 contains three independent NAND gates, each with three inputs. Using CMOS technology, it offers very low power consumption, high noise immunity, and a wide operating voltage range, making it suitable for low-power and general digital logic applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773460616214-979017243.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-14 03:56:56'),
(1148,'CD4027',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4027 is a CMOS dual J-K master–slave flip-flop integrated circuit designed for reliable digital storage and control applications.','The CD4027 contains two independent JK flip-flops, each with asynchronous SET and RESET inputs. It can operate in toggle, set/reset, or data storage modes, making it a versatile building block for counters, dividers, and control logic. CMOS technology ensures low power consumption and a wide operating voltage range.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845189773-898515551.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:13:09'),
(1149,'CD4028',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4028 is a CMOS BCD-to-decimal decoder integrated circuit designed to convert a 4-bit binary-coded decimal input into ten distinct output lines','The CD4028 takes a 4-bit BCD input (0000–1001) and activates one of ten outputs (0–9) corresponding to the decimal value. All outputs are active-HIGH, and only one output is active at a time. CMOS technology gives it low power consumption and a wide operating voltage range.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845212807-217128189.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:13:32'),
(1150,'CD4030',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4030 is a CMOS-based quad exclusive-OR (XOR) logic integrated circuit that contains four independent XOR gates within a single package.','The CD4030 contains four independent XOR gates, each producing a HIGH output when the two inputs are different. With CMOS technology, it offers low power consumption, high noise immunity, and a wide operating voltage range, making it suitable for many digital logic applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845233080-224078620.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:13:53'),
(1151,'CD4035',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4035 is a CMOS-based 4-bit universal shift register designed for flexible digital data handling with very low power consumption.','The CD4035 can load 4 bits in parallel or shift data serially depending on the control input. It supports both left and right shifting (via control logic) and provides parallel outputs, making it flexible for data storage and manipulation. CMOS technology ensures low power consumption and a wide operating voltage range.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845255493-983632152.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:14:15'),
(1152,'CD4040',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4040 is a 12-stage binary ripple counter IC from the CMOS 4000 series, designed for low-power digital counting and frequency division applications','The CD4040 counts incoming clock pulses and provides multiple divided outputs, dividing the input frequency by powers of two from ÷2 up to ÷4096. With CMOS technology, it offers very low power consumption, high noise immunity, and a wide operating voltage range, making it ideal for timing and clock division applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845278475-104209520.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:14:38'),
(1153,'CD4042',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4042 is a CMOS quad transparent latch integrated circuit designed for temporary data storage and signal holding in digital systems.','The CD4042 contains four independent D-type latches. Data present at each D input is transferred to the corresponding output when the clock (enable) input is active, and held when it is inactive. CMOS technology provides low power consumption, high noise immunity, and a wide operating voltage range.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845343883-250897959.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:15:43'),
(1154,'CD4043',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4043 is a CMOS quad R-S (reset–set) latch IC that contains four independent R-S latches with 3-state buffered outputs.','The CD4043 contains four independent R-S latches with buffered outputs. Each latch stores a logic state based on its SET and RESET inputs and holds that state until changed. Using CMOS technology, it offers low power consumption, high noise immunity, and a wide operating voltage range.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845364800-90207101.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:16:04'),
(1155,'CD4046',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4046 is a CMOS Phase-Locked Loop (PLL) integrated circuit widely used in frequency synthesis, clock recovery, FM demodulation, motor speed control, and signal synchronization applications.','The CD4046 contains a voltage-controlled oscillator (VCO) and two different phase comparators, allowing it to lock an output signal to the phase and frequency of an input signal. With CMOS technology, it offers low power consumption, wide operating voltage range, and flexible configuration, making it ideal for frequency control and synchronization applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845385979-373621303.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:16:25'),
(1156,'CD4047',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4047 is a CMOS multivibrator IC that can operate in both astable and monostable modes, making it highly useful for timing and oscillator applications','The CD4047 can operate in monostable (one-shot) or astable (oscillator) mode using external resistor and capacitor components. In astable mode, it provides two complementary outputs',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845407283-54884149.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:16:47'),
(1157,'UC3842',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'UC3842 is a current-mode PWM (Pulse Width Modulation) controller IC widely used in switch-mode power supplies (SMPS)','The UC3842 provides fixed-frequency current-mode control, enabling efficient and stable regulation in flyback, forward, and boost converters. It features a high-current totem-pole gate driver for directly driving power MOSFETs, along with undervoltage lockout (UVLO), current limiting, and thermal protection, making it a popular choice for offline and DC-DC power supply designs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1772006136424-834964573.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 07:55:36'),
(1158,'UC3843',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'UC3843 is a current-mode PWM (Pulse Width Modulation) controller IC used in switch-mode power supplies (SMPS).','The UC3843 provides fixed-frequency current-mode control for efficient and stable SMPS designs such as flyback, forward, and boost converters. Compared to UC3842, it has lower undervoltage lockout (UVLO) thresholds, making it suitable for low-voltage startup applications. It includes a high-current gate driver, current limiting, and thermal protection.',NULL,NULL,'products/1772006157437-303796971.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 07:55:57'),
(1159,'UC3844',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'UC3844 is a current-mode PWM (Pulse Width Modulation) controller IC used in switch-mode power supplies (SMPS) such as flyback and forward converters','The UC3844 provides fixed-frequency current-mode control for efficient and stable SMPS designs such as flyback and forward converters. Compared to UC3842/3843, it has lower maximum duty cycle and different UVLO thresholds, making it suitable for specific power supply topologies where tighter duty-cycle control is required. It includes a high-current gate driver, current limiting, and undervoltage lockout.',NULL,NULL,'products/1772006175824-982716324.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 07:56:15'),
(1160,'UC3845',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'UC3845 is a current-mode PWM (Pulse Width Modulation) controller IC used in switch-mode power supplies (SMPS) such as flyback and forward converters.','The UC3845 provides fixed-frequency current-mode control for efficient SMPS designs such as flyback and forward converters',NULL,NULL,'products/1772006197765-436587849.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 07:56:37'),
(1161,'CD4049',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4049 is a CMOS hex inverter IC that contains six independent NOT gates, commonly used for logic-level inversion, signal conditioning, and buffering applications','The CD4049 contains six inverting buffers that can operate over a wide supply voltage range. It is commonly used for logic inversion, signal buffering, and even level shifting (when powered appropriately). CMOS technology provides low power consumption and good noise immunity.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845431006-705739674.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:17:11'),
(1162,'UC3854AN',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'UC3854AN is a high-performance Power Factor Correction (PFC) controller IC designed to implement active power factor correction in AC-DC switch-mode power supplies.','The UC3854AN is designed to implement average current-mode Power Factor Correction, shaping the input current to follow the AC line voltage and achieve a near-unity power factor. It is commonly used in boost-type PFC front ends for offline power supplies.','The IC integrates voltage regulation, current control, multiplier, and protection features, making it suitable for high-efficiency power designs.',NULL,'products/1772006217873-903103631.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 07:56:57'),
(1163,'LM4250',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM4250 is a programmable, low-power operational amplifier (op-amp) IC designed for applications where very low power consumption and adjustable performance are required.','The LM4250 operates with extremely low supply current (in the microamp range), making it ideal for circuits where power consumption is critical. It allows external programming of bias current, so you can trade off speed and power as needed. Despite its low power usage, it provides stable and reliable amplification for low-frequency signals.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771917894454-63018087.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:24:54'),
(1164,'LM3524',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM3524 is a pulse-width modulation (PWM) controller IC designed for switch-mode power supplies (SMPS), DC-DC converters, and inverter applications.','The LM3524 integrates a precision voltage reference, error amplifier, oscillator, PWM comparator, and dual totem-pole outputs for driving external power transistors','It supports push-pull, half-bridge, and single-ended converter topologies and includes soft-start and current-limit control, making it a classic choice for regulated power supply designs.',NULL,'products/1771917589876-509554324.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:19:49'),
(1165,'LM3525',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'LM3525 is a pulse-width modulation (PWM) controller IC used in switch-mode power supplies (SMPS), DC-DC converters, and inverter circuits.','The LM3525 integrates a 5V precision reference, error amplifier, oscillator, PWM comparator, and dual totem-pole outputs capable of driving external power transistors.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771917609577-849032478.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 07:20:09'),
(1166,'CD4050',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'CD4050 is a CMOS hex non-inverting buffer IC commonly used for logic level shifting and signal buffering.','The CD4050 contains six non-inverting buffers designed to accept higher input voltages while operating at a lower supply voltage, making it ideal for logic level shifting. Built with CMOS technology, it offers low power consumption, high input impedance, and good noise immunity.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845455743-321580047.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:17:35'),
(1167,'IC 78M05',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'The IC 78M05 regulator typically accepts an input voltage between 7V and 35V DC and regulates it down to a steady 5V output with built-in protection features such as thermal shutdown, current limiting, and short-circuit protection. It is usually available in a TO-220 package with three pins: Input, Ground, and Output. Although simple to use, a heat sink may be required when supplying higher current loads because excess voltage is dissipated as heat.','The IC 78M05 (7805 Voltage Regulator) is a widely used linear voltage regulator IC designed to provide a stable +5V DC output from a higher input voltage source. It belongs to the popular 78xx series of fixed positive voltage regulators, where “05” indicates the 5-volt output.','The IC 78M05 is widely used in power supply circuits, Arduino and microcontroller projects, embedded systems, battery-powered devices, chargers, and educational electronics kits. Its ease of use, low cost, and reliable voltage regulation make it one of the most commonly used power management ICs in electronics.',NULL,'products/1771998163409-199133861.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-04-06 15:02:40'),
(1169,'REG 7812',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'The REG 7812 (7812 Voltage Regulator) is a fixed positive linear voltage regulator IC from the widely used 78xx series, designed to provide a stable +12V DC output from a higher DC input voltage. It is commonly used in power supply circuits to deliver a constant and regulated voltage, ensuring reliable performance of electronic devices even when input voltage or load conditions vary. The regulator helps protect sensitive components from voltage fluctuations and electrical noise.','The 7812 typically operates with an input voltage range of about 14V to 35V DC and can supply output current up to 1A, depending on cooling conditions. It includes built-in protection features such as thermal shutdown, internal current limiting, and short-circuit protection, which enhance safety and durability during operation. The IC is usually available in a TO-220 package with three terminals: Input, Ground, and Output. A heat sink is recommended when used in higher current applications because excess voltage is dissipated as heat.','The REG 7812 is widely used in power adapters, audio amplifiers, motor control circuits, communication equipment, industrial electronics, and embedded system power supplies where a stable 12V output is required. Its simple design, low cost, and dependable voltage regulation make it one of the most commonly used voltage regulator ICs in electronics.',NULL,'products/1771998039644-408793475.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 05:40:39'),
(1170,'REG 7806',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'The REG 7806 (7806 Voltage Regulator) is a fixed positive linear voltage regulator IC from the 78xx series, designed to provide a stable +6V DC output from a higher input voltage source. It is commonly used in electronic circuits where a constant 6-volt supply is required to power components and devices safely. The regulator maintains a steady output voltage even when there are variations in input voltage or load conditions, ensuring reliable circuit performance.','The 7806 typically accepts an input voltage range of about 8V to 35V DC and regulates it down to a fixed 6V output. It includes built-in protection features such as thermal shutdown, current limiting, and short-circuit protection, which help prevent damage caused by overheating or excessive current. The IC is usually available in a TO-220 package with three terminals: Input, Ground, and Output. A heat sink may be required when operating at higher current levels because excess voltage is dissipated as heat.','The REG 7806 is widely used in power supply circuits, battery-operated equipment, audio devices, communication systems, embedded electronics, and general electronic projects that require a regulated 6V power source. Its simple design, reliability, and ease of implementation make it a common choice for voltage regulation applications.',NULL,'products/1771997883562-573144718.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 05:38:03'),
(1171,'CD4052',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'CD4051 is an 8-channel analog multiplexer/demultiplexer IC from the CMOS 4000 series, used to route one of eight analog or digital signals to a single common input/output line.','CD4052 is a Dual 4-Channel Analog Multiplexer/Demultiplexer IC from the CMOS 4000 series. It is commonly used to switch multiple analog or digital signals using just a few control lines.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845473953-226884503.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:17:53'),
(1172,'REG 7808',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'The REG 7808 (7808 Voltage Regulator) is a fixed positive linear voltage regulator IC belonging to the 78xx series, designed to deliver a stable +8V DC output from a higher DC input voltage. It is commonly used in electronic circuits that require a regulated 8-volt power supply to ensure stable and reliable operation of components. The regulator maintains constant output voltage even when the input voltage or load current changes, protecting sensitive electronic devices from voltage fluctuations.','The 7808 typically operates with an input voltage range of approximately 10V to 35V DC and can supply output current up to 1A under proper cooling conditions. The IC includes internal protection features such as thermal shutdown, current limiting, and short-circuit protection, which help prevent damage during overload or overheating situations. It is usually available in a TO-220 package with three terminals: Input, Ground, and Output. A heat sink is recommended when operating at higher loads because excess voltage is dissipated as heat.','The REG 7808 is widely used in power supply units, audio equipment, communication devices, industrial electronics, embedded systems, and general electronic projects that require a steady 8V regulated output. Its simple design, durability, and ease of use make it a reliable solution for voltage regulation applications.',NULL,'products/1771997932241-970641113.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 05:38:52'),
(1173,'CD4053',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'CD4053 is a CMOS triple 2-channel analog multiplexer/demultiplexer IC that allows bidirectional switching of analog or digital signals','D4053 is a Triple 2-Channel Analog Multiplexer/Demultiplexer (Analog Switch) IC from the CMOS 4000 series. It lets you switch three independent signals, each between two paths, using digital control inputs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845496245-542330078.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:18:16'),
(1174,'CD4060',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4060 is a CMOS 14-stage binary ripple counter with a built-in oscillator, widely used for timing, frequency division, and clock generation applications.','CD4060 is a CMOS 14-stage binary ripple counter with a built-in oscillator. It’s widely used for timing, frequency division, and clock generation—just add a resistor–capacitor (RC) network or a crystal.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845532080-377352825.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:18:52'),
(1175,'REG 7809',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'The REG 7809 (7809 Voltage Regulator) is a fixed positive linear voltage regulator IC from the popular 78xx series, designed to provide a stable +9V DC output from a higher input voltage source. It is widely used in electronic circuits that require a regulated 9-volt supply for reliable and noise-free operation. The regulator maintains constant output voltage even when there are fluctuations in input voltage or load current, protecting sensitive electronic components.','The 7809 typically accepts an input voltage range of about 11V to 35V DC and can deliver output current up to 1A, depending on heat dissipation conditions. It includes built-in protection features such as thermal shutdown, current limiting, and short-circuit protection, ensuring safe and durable operation. The IC is commonly available in a TO-220 package with three terminals: Input, Ground, and Output. A heat sink is recommended for higher current applications since excess voltage is dissipated as heat during regulation.','The REG 7809 is commonly used in power supply circuits, audio amplifiers, communication equipment, embedded systems, battery chargers, and general electronic projects where a stable 9V supply is required. Its simplicity, reliability, and low cost make it a standard voltage regulation solution in electronics design.',NULL,'products/1771997982482-297298003.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 05:39:42'),
(1176,'CD4063',NULL,NULL,NULL,2.00,'The CD4063 is a CMOS 4-bit magnitude comparator integrated circuit used to compare two 4-bit binary numbers and determine their relative size.','CD4063 is a 4-bit binary magnitude comparator IC from the CMOS 4000 series. It compares two 4-bit binary numbers and tells you whether A is greater than B, A is equal to B, or A is less than B.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771845555773-146728666.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-23 11:19:15'),
(1177,'32 inch LG LED TV','32 inch LG LED TV',NULL,'32 inch LG LED TV',1.00,'The 32-inch LG LED TV is a compact and energy-efficient television designed for home entertainment, bedrooms, offices, and small living spaces. It features an HD-Ready LED display that confirms clear picture quality with vibrant colors and wide viewing angles','LG Smart TVs run on WebOS, providing easy access to OTT apps like Netflix, Prime Video, and YouTube. Built-in Wi-Fi and smart features allow seamless streaming and screen sharing from mobile devices.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771669210936-78035008.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-21 10:20:10'),
