(1321,'STM32F103 C8 BLUEPILL',NULL,NULL,NULL,499.00,'The STM32F103 C8 “Blue Pill” is a low-cost, compact ARM Cortex-M3 development board based on the STM32F103C8T6 microcontroller.','It provides an affordable platform for embedded system prototyping with multiple digital/analog I/O pins, communication interfaces (UART, SPI, I²C, USB), and can be programmed using IDEs like Arduino (with STM32 support), STM32CubeIDE, or PlatformIO. Popular in hobby and professional projects, it’s ideal for motor control, sensor interfacing, robotics, and IoT applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1772003656647-321964427.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 07:14:16'),
(1322,'ST link v2 Programmer Dongle',NULL,NULL,NULL,500.00,'The ST-Link V2 is a USB in-circuit debugger and programmer tool from STMicroelectronics used to program and debug STM8 and STM32 microcontrollers','It connects to a computer via USB and interfaces with target boards through SWD/JTAG or SWIM protocols, allowing you to upload firmware, set breakpoints, and step through code using development environments like STM32CubeIDE. This dongle is essential for embedded development, firmware debugging, and real-time code analysis with STM32/STM8 boards.',NULL,NULL,'products/1772003527303-769897028.jpg',0,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-04 12:31:11'),
(1323,'NUCLEO F446RE',NULL,NULL,NULL,3100.00,'The NUCLEO-F446RE is a compact STM32 Nucleo-64 development board from STMicroelectronics built around the STM32F446RET6 ARM Cortex-M4 microcontroller.','It provides an affordable and flexible platform for embedded system prototyping and learning, with built-in ST-LINK/V2-1 programmer/debugger, Arduino Uno R3 compatibility, and ST Morpho expansion headers to connect shields and modules easily.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771993887194-368111358.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 04:31:27'),
(1324,'NUCLEO F410',NULL,NULL,NULL,2550.00,'The NUCLEO-F410 (officially the NUCLEO-F410RB) is a compact STM32 Nucleo-64 development board from STMicroelectronics featuring the STM32F410RB ARM Cortex-M4 microcontroller','It offers an integrated ST-LINK/V2-1 debugger/programmer, Arduino Uno R3 expansion headers, and ST Morpho expansion pins, making it ideal for embedded system prototyping, sensor interfacing, and learning ARM development.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771993845579-703925564.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 04:30:45'),
