(2119,'Zeb 9PPM2UM 9 port POE Switch','Zeb 9PPM2UM',NULL,NULL,5999.00,'The Zebronics ZEB-9PPM2UM is an unmanaged 9-port PoE (Power over Ethernet) network switch designed mainly for CCTV surveillance systems, IP cameras, wireless access points, and network devices. It allows both power and data transmission through a single Ethernet cable, simplifying installation and reducing wiring cost.','This switch is widely used in security camera installations where multiple PoE cameras need centralized power and networking without separate adapters.','9 Self-adaptive PoE ports\r\n2 × 10/100 Mbps uplink ports\r\nUp to 30W power per port\r\n150W total PoE power budget\r\nSupports IEEE 802.3af / 802.3at PoE standards',NULL,'products/1772015661572-828593927.jpg',0,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-06 16:15:50'),
(2120,'D-Link CAT6 Networking Cable',NULL,NULL,NULL,14999.00,'The D-Link cable you asked about is a Category-6 (CAT6) Ethernet cable. CAT6 cables are a standard for wired networking that support higher performance than older standards (like CAT5 or CAT5e).','Brand	D-Link\r\nConnector Gender	Male-to-Male\r\nItem Weight	10570 Grams\r\nItem Length	30500 Centimetres',NULL,NULL,'products/1771904616007-414778206.jpg',0,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-06 16:15:55'),
(2121,'CAT6 flat cctv cable',NULL,NULL,NULL,9999.00,'Category 6 cable (CAT6) is a widely used standard Ethernet cable type supporting up to ~250 MHz bandwidth; over short to moderate distances it can support high-speed data transfer, often up to 1 Gbps, making it enough for IP-camera video streams, DVR/NVR data transfer, etc.','Introducing Indoplast\'s Cat 6 flat cable, designed specifically for CCTV applications in elevators. Engineered with precision and reliability in mind, this cable ensures seamless transmission of high-definition video signals, providing clear and crisp footage for enhanced security monitoring.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771844581968-227151164.jpg',0,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-06 16:15:39'),
(2122,'Mist Maker',NULL,NULL,NULL,400.00,'A Mist Maker is an ultrasonic mist generator that uses high-frequency vibrations to create a fine, cool mist from water. These devices are commonly used in humidifiers, indoor fountains, hydroponics systems, decorative water features, and aroma diffusers. The mist produced adds moisture to the air or creates a visual fog effect without heating the water, making it energy-efficient and safe for various environments.','Ultrasonic mist makers typically operate at frequencies around 1.7 MHz, generating tiny water droplets for a smooth, fog-like mist. Many units come with LED lights for added visual appeal in fountains or decorative setups. They are compact, easy to install, and can be submerged in shallow water containers or reservoirs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771990423258-448910423.jpg',0,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-04 12:27:14'),
(2123,'Motor Speed Control Module',NULL,NULL,NULL,550.00,'The Motor Speed Control Module is an electronic device used to regulate and adjust the speed of DC motors by controlling the voltage or pulse signal supplied to the motor. Most modern motor speed controller modules use PWM (Pulse Width Modulation) technology, which varies the duty cycle of the electrical signal to efficiently control motor speed without significant power loss','The module typically includes a control potentiometer for manual speed adjustment, power input terminals, motor output terminals, and a driver circuit built using MOSFET or motor driver IC components. It supports a wide range of DC motors and commonly operates within voltage ranges such as 3V–35V DC (depending on the model), making it suitable for robotics, automation systems, DIY electronics, and industrial control applications.','Motor speed control modules are widely used in robot cars, cooling fans, conveyor systems, pumps, electric tools, home automation devices, and educational electronics projects where adjustable motor speed is required.',NULL,'products/1771991015820-724105352.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 03:43:35'),
(2124,'Color Sensor Module TCS3200D/TCS2300',NULL,NULL,'TCS 3200 colour sensor',900.00,'High-resolution conversion of light intensity to frequency.\r\nThe pins have 2.54 mm pitch.\r\nMil-convenient for bitmap board.\r\nProgrammable color and full-scale output frequency.\r\nCommunicate directly with a microcontroller.\r\nLow-profile surface mount package.','Operating Voltage: 3V-5V\r\nHigh-resolution conversion of light intensity to frequency.\r\nChip pins all has drawn for standard 100.\r\nPut the needle (2.54 mm).\r\nMil-convenient for bitmap board.\r\nProgrammable color and full-scale output frequency.\r\nCommunicate directly with a microcontroller.\r\nLow-profile surface mount package.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771903915638-918510083.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-06 06:49:41'),
(2125,'Laser Sensor HW-493',NULL,NULL,NULL,550.00,'The Laser Sensor HW-493 is a compact laser emitter module commonly used in Arduino, ESP8266, ESP32, and other embedded electronics projects for light detection, positioning, and security applications. It contains a semiconductor laser diode that produces a 650 nm red laser beam, along with a built-in driver circuit and current-limiting resistor to ensure stable and safe operation','The module typically operates on 3V–5V DC power and consumes low current (around 30–40 mA), making it suitable for microcontroller-based systems and battery-powered projects. The HW-493 provides a simple 3-pin interface (VCC, GND, Signal/Enable), allowing the laser to be turned ON or OFF using a digital output pin from a controller.','This laser module works by emitting a focused red light beam that can be detected by a photoresistor, photodiode, or laser receiver sensor. When the beam is interrupted, the connected system can trigger an action such as an alarm, counter, or automation response.',NULL,'products/1771914917068-37853877.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 06:35:17'),
(2126,'Laser Receiver Module',NULL,NULL,NULL,600.00,'xcluma Laser Beam Sensor Module Tube Laser Receiver Module Non-Modulator','PCB size:1.52cm x 2.22cm Working Voltage: 5 Volt DC Output: 4-5 Volt DC\r\nOn detecting a laser signal, output goes at high level (5V) until laser signal is there. NOTE: This sensor is non-modulator, to be used indoors away from any bright light or direct sunlight',NULL,NULL,'products/1771914809426-491547594.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 06:33:29'),
(2127,'Laser Diode',NULL,NULL,NULL,100.00,'This low-cost Laser Diode or Laser Light is commonly used in security devices and pointers. This Red Laser diode is rated for 5mW with a nominal voltage between 2.2V and 3V. ','Just like other LED Diodes the Laser Diode should also be used with a driver circuit to limit the current through it. The wave length of Laser light normally range from 635nm to 66nm.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771914737755-992940634.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-04 13:02:14'),
(2128,'PCA9685 16 channel Servo Motor Driver',NULL,NULL,'16 Channel servo bit module',800.00,'The PCA9685 16-Channel Servo Motor Driver is a PWM (Pulse Width Modulation) controller module designed to control multiple servo motors or LEDs using a single microcontroller. It is based on the PCA9685 PWM driver IC, which communicates through the I2C interface, allowing efficient control of up to 16 independent channels while using only two communication pins (SDA and SCL). This greatly reduces the processing load on microcontrollers such as Arduino, ESP8266, ESP32, Raspberry Pi, and STM32 boards.','The module generates precise 12-bit PWM signals, providing 4096 levels of resolution for accurate servo positioning and smooth motor movement. It includes an onboard clock and supports adjustable PWM frequency, typically ranging from 40 Hz to 1000 Hz, making it suitable for both servo motors and LED dimming applications.','The PCA9685 servo driver features dedicated external power input for motors, ensuring stable operation without overloading the microcontroller’s power supply. It is widely used in robotics, robotic arms, humanoid robots, automation systems, RC projects, animatronics, and multi-servo control applications due to its reliability, scalability, and precise PWM control capability.',NULL,'products/1771995509845-736179771.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-06 04:32:17'),
(2129,'BTS7960B  Motor Driver Module',NULL,NULL,'Motor Driver Module BTS7960B',800.00,'The BTS7960B Motor Driver Module is a high-power H-bridge motor driver used to control large DC motors with high current requirements. It is commonly used in robotics, electric vehicles, CNC machines, and automation systems where powerful motors need precise speed and direction control. The module is based on the BTS7960B half-bridge driver IC and is often arranged as a dual H-bridge configuration to drive motors forward and reverse','This driver uses chips BTS7960 composed of high-power drive full H-bridge driver module with thermal over-current protection. Double BTS7960 H-bridge driver circuit, with a strong drive and braking, effectively isolating the microcontroller and motor driver, high-current 43A\r\n5V isolate with MCU, and effectively protect MCU\r\n5V power indicator on board\r\nVoltage indication of motor driver output end',NULL,NULL,'products/1771844090758-804256279.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-06 04:18:06'),
(2130,'PWM DC Motor Speed Controller',NULL,NULL,NULL,600.00,'The PWM DC Motor Speed Controller is an electronic control module used to regulate the speed of DC motors efficiently using Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) technology. Instead of reducing voltage directly, the controller rapidly switches the power supply ON and OFF at high frequency, adjusting the duty cycle to control motor speed while maintaining torque and minimizing power loss.','The module typically includes a rotary potentiometer knob for manual speed adjustment, power input terminals, motor output terminals, and a driver circuit built using MOSFETs or dedicated control ICs. It supports a wide range of DC motors and commonly operates within voltage ranges such as 6V–28V or 3V–35V DC depending on the model, with current handling capacities ranging from 3A to 10A or higher','PWM DC motor speed controllers are widely used in robotics, electric fans, pumps, conveyor systems, DIY motor projects, automation equipment, and battery-powered devices where adjustable motor speed and energy efficiency are required. Their compact size, easy wiring, and reliable performance make them suitable for both hobby electronics and industrial control applications.',NULL,'products/1771996795403-880987207.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 05:19:55'),
(2131,'1203B PWM DC Motor Speed Regulator',NULL,NULL,'1203B PWM DC Motor Speed Regulator(Motor Drivers)',499.00,'The 1203B PWM DC Motor Speed Regulator is a compact controller used to adjust the speed of DC motors using Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) technology. It provides smooth and efficient speed control without significant power loss','The module includes a rotary knob for easy adjustment and a digital display for monitoring speed level. It is widely used in DIY projects, robotics, fans, pumps, and small motor applications.','The 1203B PWM DC Motor Speed Regulator is a compact electronic module designed to control the speed of DC motors using Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) technology. It efficiently adjusts motor speed by changing the duty cycle of the output signal instead of reducing voltage directly, which helps maintain motor torque and reduces power loss. This makes it more efficient and generates less heat compared to traditional variable resistors or linear control methods.',NULL,'products/1771654719269-536527266.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 13:47:58'),
(2132,'UltraSonic sensor Module',NULL,NULL,'HC-SRO4 Ultrasonic module',499.00,'The Ultrasonic Sensor Module is an electronic distance measuring device used to detect objects and measure distance using ultrasonic sound waves. It works by transmitting high-frequency sound pulses (usually around 40 kHz) through a transmitter and then receiving the reflected echo from nearby objects using a receiver. The module calculates the distance based on the time taken for the sound wave to travel to the object and return, making it a reliable non-contact measurement sensor.','One of the most commonly used ultrasonic modules is the HC-SR04, which provides accurate distance measurement and easy interfacing with microcontrollers such as Arduino, ESP8266, ESP32, Raspberry Pi, and STM32 boards. The sensor typically includes four pins: VCC, GND, Trigger, and Echo. A short trigger pulse initiates measurement, and the echo pin outputs a signal whose duration corresponds to the detected distance. The module operates on 5V DC power and offers stable performance in various lighting conditions since it relies on sound instead of light.','Ultrasonic sensor modules are widely used in obstacle avoidance robots, distance measurement systems, water level monitoring, parking assistance systems, automation projects, and smart IoT applications. Due to their accuracy, low cost, and simple operation, they are highly popular in educational and industrial electronics projects.',NULL,'products/1772006335065-449288448.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-06 04:51:52'),
(2133,'OLED Display Module',NULL,NULL,NULL,0.00,'The OLED Display Module (Organic Light Emitting Diode Display) is a compact and energy-efficient display device widely used in embedded systems and IoT projects for showing text, graphics, and sensor data. Unlike traditional LCD displays, OLED technology does not require a backlight because each pixel emits its own light, resulting in high contrast, wide viewing angles, faster response time, and lower power consumption. This makes OLED displays highly suitable for portable and battery-powered electronic devices.','Most OLED modules commonly use display sizes such as 0.96 inch or 1.3 inch with resolutions like 128×64 or 128×32 pixels. They typically communicate using I2C or SPI interfaces, allowing easy connection with microcontrollers such as Arduino, ESP8266, ESP32, Raspberry Pi, and STM32 boards. The module operates at 3.3V or 5V, and includes an onboard controller (commonly SSD1306 or SH1106) that simplifies display control through available software libraries.','OLED display modules are widely used in IoT dashboards, wearable devices, digital meters, sensor monitoring systems, robotics, smart home projects, and portable instruments. Due to their small size, clear visibility, low power usage, and simple interfacing, OLED displays are one of the most popular display solutions for modern electronics and embedded development projects.',NULL,'products/1771994315781-430576416.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 04:38:35'),
(2134,'Buzzer Small',NULL,NULL,'12V Golli buzzer 12mm',99.00,'A Small Buzzer is a compact electronic sound-producing component used to generate beeps, alerts, and warning tones in electronic circuits.','Small buzzers are available as active (built-in oscillator, works directly with DC supply) and passive (requires an external signal or PWM)',NULL,NULL,'products/1771844270005-98291909.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-06 08:19:46'),
(2135,'Buzzer Big',NULL,NULL,'Buzzer',99.00,'A Big Buzzer is a high-sound electronic alert device designed to produce loud and clear audio signals for warnings and notifications.','Compared to small buzzers, big buzzers generate higher decibel output, making them suitable for industrial, commercial, and outdoor applications where sound must be heard over long distances or noisy environments.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771844250986-640162502.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-04 12:06:29'),
(2136,'Mini LCD Digital Thermometer',NULL,NULL,NULL,0.00,'A Mini LCD Digital Thermometer is a compact electronic device used to measure and display temperature digitally on a clear LCD screen.','These thermometers typically use an NTC temperature sensor or probe, offering accurate readings over a wide temperature range',NULL,NULL,'products/1771990382816-759277790.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 03:33:02'),
(2137,'DS18B20 Waterproof Digital Temperature',NULL,NULL,'DS18B20 TEMPERATURE SENSOR WITH WIRE',499.00,'The DS18B20 Waterproof Digital Temperature Sensor is a high-accuracy, digital temperature sensor sealed in a stainless steel probe, making it suitable for wet, humid, and harsh environments.','It uses the 1-Wire communication protocol, allowing multiple sensors to be connected on a single data line, each with a unique ID.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771906164498-659586343.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-06 06:28:47'),
(2139,'12V Voltage Regulator Power Supply Board',NULL,NULL,'Power Supply Board',499.00,'Most 12V regulator boards use linear voltage regulator ICs such as 7812 or switching regulator circuits (buck converters). Linear regulators are simple and low-noise but may generate more heat, while switching regulators are more efficient and suitable for higher current applications. The board typically includes components such as filter capacitors, heat sinks, rectifier diodes (if AC input), and protection circuits to improve performance and safety.','It ensures consistent voltage for sensitive electronics by filtering noise and compensating for input/load variations. These boards are available in linear (clean output, more heat) and switching/buck (high efficiency, low heat) designs.','A 12V Voltage Regulator Power Supply Board is an electronic module designed to provide a stable and regulated 12V DC output from a higher or fluctuating input voltage. It is commonly used in electronic circuits, robotics, Arduino projects, CCTV systems, LED strips, and industrial control systems where a constant 12V supply is required. The board ensures that even if the input voltage changes slightly, the output remains steady at 12V, protecting connected components from voltage variations.',NULL,'products/1771655538868-249336215.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-02 12:36:23'),
(2141,'TP4056 USB to Type-C',NULL,NULL,NULL,0.00,'The TP4056 USB to Type-C module is a compact single-cell Li-ion / Li-Po battery charging board designed for modern Type-C 5V input','It is based on the TP4056 linear charger IC and provides safe, constant-current / constant-voltage (CC/CV) charging for 3.7V rechargeable batteries.',NULL,NULL,'products/1772004779133-182040755.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 07:32:59'),
(2142,'TP4056 USB To V8',NULL,NULL,NULL,0.00,'The TP4056 USB to V8 (Micro-USB) module is a compact single-cell Li-ion / Li-Po battery charger board that accepts 5V input via Micro-USB (V8).','Built around the TP4056 linear charging IC, it uses a CC/CV (constant-current / constant-voltage) charging profile to safely charge 3.7V rechargeable batteries.',NULL,NULL,'products/1772004798870-245588902.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 07:33:18'),
(2143,'Emergency LED Light Circuit PCB Board',NULL,NULL,NULL,0.00,'An Emergency LED Light Circuit PCB Board is a compact electronic board designed to automatically turn on LED lights during a power failure.','It typically integrates a battery charging section, power management, and LED driver circuit on a single PCB, ensuring reliable illumination when mains power is unavailable.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771906800810-283684017.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 04:20:00'),
(2144,'ARDUINO UNO R3 CP2102',NULL,NULL,'ARDUINO UNO R3 CP2102',1499.00,'The Arduino UNO R3 CP2102 is a popular microcontroller development board based on the ATmega328P microcontroller, designed for electronics prototyping, embedded systems, and educational projects. This version uses the CP2102 USB-to-Serial converter instead of the standard ATmega16U2, providing stable USB communication between the computer and the board.','It allows easy programming through the Arduino IDE via USB connection. The board features multiple digital and analog input/output pins, PWM outputs, and serial communication interfaces, making it suitable for robotics, automation, IoT, and sensor-based applications. Its open-source hardware design and wide library support make it ideal for beginners and professionals alike.','This version uses the CP2102 USB-to-Serial converter instead of the standard ATmega16U2, providing stable USB communication between the computer and the board.',NULL,'products/1771834757732-301626634.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 10:59:39'),
(2145,'ESP32 expansion board',NULL,NULL,NULL,499.00,'The ESP32 Expansion Board is a development support board designed to enhance the usability and connectivity of ESP32 development modules by providing easy access to all input and output pins. It acts as an interface platform that simplifies circuit connections, making prototyping and project development faster and more reliable','The board typically includes clearly labeled GPIO pin headers, power input terminals, voltage regulation circuits, and multiple interface options such as UART, I2C, SPI, and PWM connections. Many ESP32 expansion boards also provide additional features like 5V/3.3V power output pins, USB power support, reset and boot buttons, and screw terminals for secure wiring of sensors, relays, and external devices.','This expansion board is commonly used in IoT development, home automation, robotics, industrial monitoring, and embedded system projects where multiple sensors and modules need to be connected easily. It helps reduce wiring errors and eliminates the need for breadboards in permanent setups.',NULL,'products/1771907573911-923343057.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 04:32:53'),
(2146,'Water Pump DC 6-12Volt 385',NULL,NULL,NULL,999.00,'The DC Water Pump 6–12V (Model 385) is a compact and efficient miniature water pump designed for low-voltage DC operation, commonly used in DIY electronics, automation, and small liquid transfer applications. It operates using a brushed DC motor that drives an internal impeller to move water smoothly through the inlet and outlet ports. The pump is designed for continuous water flow and provides reliable performance when powered by batteries, power adapters, or motor driver circuits.','This pump typically works within a voltage range of 6V to 12V DC, with optimal performance around 12V, delivering higher water flow and pressure at increased voltage levels. It features a durable plastic body, low noise operation, and simple two-wire connection for easy installation. The pump is suitable for clean water and light liquid circulation but is not intended for corrosive liquids or dry running operation. Speed and flow rate can also be controlled using a PWM motor speed controller.','The DC 385 water pump is widely used in automatic plant watering systems, aquarium circulation, water fountains, cooling systems, robotics projects, DIY irrigation setups, and IoT-based fluid control applications. Its small size, low power consumption, and easy interfacing make it ideal for educational and prototype projects.',NULL,'products/1772012919033-211751472.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-31 11:13:30'),
(2147,'Air Pump Motor',NULL,NULL,NULL,499.00,'An air pump motor is an electric motor designed to generate airflow by converting electrical energy into mechanical motion, which drives a diaphragm, piston, or rotary vane mechanism to push air. These motors are commonly available in DC (3V, 6V, 9V, 12V) and AC versions, depending on the application. Mini DC air pump motors are widely used in aquariums, medical devices, air purifiers, inflatable products, DIY science projects, pneumatic systems, and small automation setups.','Air pump motors are available in DC and AC versions and come in various sizes depending on airflow and pressure requirements.','Air pump motor include operating voltage, current consumption, airflow rate (L/min), pressure rating (kPa or PSI), noise level, and power consumption. Proper ventilation and correct power supply are essential to ensure safe and long-lasting performance.',NULL,'products/1771831239363-487934809.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 09:23:21'),
(2148,'ESP 8266- mini wifi module',NULL,NULL,NULL,999.00,'The ESP8266 Mini WiFi Module is a compact and low-cost wireless microcontroller module widely used for Internet of Things (IoT) and embedded system applications. It is based on the ESP8266 chipset developed by Espressif Systems and provides built-in Wi-Fi networking capability, allowing devices to connect directly to wireless networks without requiring an external microcontroller','The module operates on the IEEE 802.11 b/g/n standard and supports TCP/IP protocol stack, enabling communication with web servers, mobile applications, and cloud platforms. It features a 32-bit microprocessor running at up to 80/160 MHz, digital GPIO pins, UART, SPI, and I2C interfaces for connecting sensors and peripherals.','The ESP8266 Mini supports multiple operating modes such as Station mode, Access Point mode, and both combined, making it flexible for smart home automation, wireless monitoring, remote control systems, and DIY electronics projects. It is programmable using Arduino IDE, MicroPython, or AT commands, and operates with low power consumption, making it ideal for battery-powered devices.',NULL,'products/1771907312258-327277141.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 04:28:32'),
(2149,'ESP32 Wifi Module',NULL,NULL,NULL,1999.00,'The ESP32 WiFi Module is a powerful and low-cost microcontroller module developed by Espressif Systems, designed for advanced Internet of Things (IoT) and embedded applications. It integrates both Wi-Fi and Bluetooth (Classic and BLE) connectivity in a single chip, enabling wireless communication between devices, cloud servers, and mobile applications.','The ESP32 includes multiple GPIO pins and supports various communication interfaces such as UART, SPI, I2C, PWM, ADC, and DAC, allowing easy connection with sensors, displays, relays, and other electronic components. It operates at 3.3V and features low power consumption modes, making it ideal for battery-powered and energy-efficient projects','Widely used in smart home automation, industrial monitoring, wearable devices, robotics, wireless data logging, and remote control systems, the ESP32 WiFi Module can be programmed using Arduino IDE, MicroPython, or ESP-IDF development framework. Its combination of high processing power, wireless connectivity, flexible interfaces, and affordability makes it one of the most popular microcontroller modules for modern IoT development.',NULL,'products/1771907655673-568249255.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 04:34:15'),
(2150,'ESP8266 wifi Module',NULL,NULL,NULL,999.00,'The ESP8266 WiFi Module is a compact and cost-effective wireless microcontroller module developed by Espressif Systems, widely used in Internet of Things (IoT) and embedded electronics projects. It features a built-in TCP/IP protocol stack and integrated Wi-Fi capability based on the IEEE 802.11 b/g/n standard, allowing devices to connect directly to wireless networks and communicate with servers, mobile applications, or cloud platforms without requiring additional networking hardware.','The ESP8266 offers multiple GPIO pins along with communication interfaces such as UART, SPI, and I2C, enabling easy integration with sensors, relays, displays, and other peripherals. It operates at 3.3V and includes several power-saving modes, making it suitable for low-power and battery-operated applications.','The module can function in Station mode, Access Point mode, or both simultaneously, providing flexibility for wireless networking solutions. Programmable using Arduino IDE, NodeMCU firmware, MicroPython, or AT commands, the ESP8266 WiFi Module is commonly used in smart home automation, wireless monitoring systems, IoT devices, and remote control applications due to its small size, affordability, and dependable wireless performance.',NULL,'products/1771908119648-96052440.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 04:41:59'),
(2151,'FP280-CN/11415 Mini Electric Motor',NULL,NULL,NULL,399.00,'The FP280-CN / 11415 is a miniature DC electric motor from the popular 280 series of small motors commonly used in hobby, robotics, and low-power applications','These motors are known for their compact size, reliable performance, and ease of use, running on low DC voltages such as 3 V to 12 V.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771908698275-143335715.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-25 09:52:34'),
(2152,'DC Double sided Toy Motor',NULL,NULL,NULL,199.00,'The DC Double-Sided Toy Motor is a small DC motor featuring shafts on both sides, allowing mechanical connection from either end for flexible design applications. It is commonly used in toy cars, DIY robotics, educational kits, and small automation projects','Operating on low DC voltage, the motor provides smooth rotation and moderate speed suitable for lightweight mechanical movements. Its compact size, lightweight construction, and easy wiring make it ideal for hobby electronics and prototype development where dual-side shaft output is required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771904737315-553730181.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 03:45:37'),
(2153,'DC Toy Motor (red)',NULL,NULL,NULL,199.00,'The DC Toy Motor (Red) is a small, lightweight electric motor commonly used in toy cars, hobby electronics, and DIY projects. Designed to operate on low DC voltage, it provides high rotational speed with simple two-wire operation.','The motor changes rotation direction by reversing the power polarity, making it easy to control in basic circuits. Its compact size and low power consumption make it ideal for educational kits, robotics experiments, and battery-operated devices.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771904803468-908163082.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 03:46:43'),
(2154,'DC Toy Motor (yellow)',NULL,NULL,NULL,199.00,'The DC Toy Motor (Yellow) is a compact low-voltage electric motor widely used in toy cars, hobby electronics, and educational DIY projects. It operates on DC power and provides high rotational speed suitable for lightweight mechanical applications.','The motor features a simple two-wire connection, and its rotation direction can be changed by reversing the polarity of the power supply. With its lightweight plastic body and easy mounting design, the yellow DC toy motor is ideal for beginner robotics, school projects, and small automation experiments.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771904905713-708264184.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 03:48:25'),
(2155,'Small DC Electric Motor (yellow)',NULL,NULL,NULL,199.00,'The Small DC Electric Motor (Yellow) is a compact and lightweight brushed DC motor commonly used in hobby electronics, robotics, and educational projects. It operates on direct current (DC) power and converts electrical energy into mechanical rotational motion through electromagnetic interaction inside the motor.The motor is typically housed in a yellow plastic gearbox casing, which provides speed reduction and increased torque, making it ideal for small robotic vehicles and moving mechanisms.','This motor usually operates within a voltage range of 3V to 12V DC, with optimal performance around 6V, offering moderate speed and good torque suitable for lightweight applications. It features two terminals for simple power connection, where reversing the polarity changes the rotation direction. The integrated gearbox helps improve control and efficiency, allowing the motor to drive wheels, gears, or mechanical parts smoothly.','The yellow DC geared motor is widely used in robot cars, line follower robots, obstacle avoidance robots, DIY automation projects, educational kits, and small mechanical systems. Due to its low cost, easy operation, and durable design, it is one of the most popular motors for beginner robotics and prototype development.',NULL,'products/1772001403280-229700318.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 06:36:43'),
(2156,'Big DC Electric Motor (yellow)',NULL,NULL,'Big DC Electric Motor (yellow)',299.00,'The Big Yellow DC Electric Motor, commonly known as a yellow gear motor or TT motor, is a high-torque DC motor widely used in robotics and DIY electronic projects. It includes an internal gearbox that reduces speed while increasing torque, making it ideal for robot cars and automation applications.','The motor operates on low DC voltage and provides stable rotation with efficient power consumption. Its lightweight plastic housing and easy mounting design make it suitable for educational kits, prototype development, and hobby electronics projects.','It includes an internal gearbox that reduces speed while increasing torque, making it ideal for robot cars and automation applications.',NULL,'products/1771840318658-292847654.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 11:15:54'),
(2157,'32k ohm Resistor',NULL,NULL,'Resistor',49.00,'A 32kΩ (32,000 ohms) resistor is a passive electronic component used to limit or control the flow of electric current in a circuit. The value 32kΩ means the resistor provides 32,000 ohms of resistance to current flow. Resistors are commonly used in voltage divider circuits, signal conditioning, pull-up or pull-down configurations, timing circuits, and current limiting applications. They are available in both through-hole and surface-mount (SMD) types depending on the circuit design.','This resistor is widely used in signal conditioning, timing circuits, sensor interfacing, pull-up/pull-down networks, audio circuits, and microcontroller applications where precise resistance values are required.','In color-coded through-hole resistors, a 32kΩ resistor typically has the color bands Orange–Red–Orange–Gold (for ±5% tolerance). In SMD form, it may be marked as “3202”, where 320 × 10² equals 32,000 ohms. Resistors are made from materials like carbon film, metal film, or wire-wound elements. Metal film resistors are preferred in precision circuits because of their better accuracy and low noise characteristics.',NULL,'products/1771669495022-133802376.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-02 11:35:33'),
(2158,'1.7m ohm Resistor',NULL,NULL,'Resistor',49.00,'A 1.7 MΩ (megaohm) resistor is a high-value resistor that provides a resistance of 1,700,000 ohms to limit electrical current flow in a circuit. Because of its large resistance value, it allows only a very small amount of current to pass, making it suitable for low-current and high-voltage applications.','It provides a resistance of 1,700,000 ohms and is commonly used in signal sensing, biasing, timing, and protection circuits.','A 1.7 MΩ (megaohm) resistor is a high-resistance electronic component that provides a resistance value of 1.7 million ohms (1,700,000 Ω). It is used to limit current flow to a very small amount and to create high-voltage drops with minimal current consumption in electronic circuits.',NULL,'products/1771649000687-535618991.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 12:35:53'),
(2159,'10m ohm Resistor',NULL,NULL,'Resistor',99.00,'10 MΩ (megaohm) resistor is a very high-value resistor that provides a resistance of 10,000,000 ohms. Because of its large resistance, it allows only a very small amount of current to flow, making it suitable for low-current and high-impedance applications. It operates according to Ohm’s Law (V = I × R), where a high resistance results in minimal current even when voltage is applied. These resistors are typically available in carbon film, metal film, or surface-mount types, with tolerance ratings such as ±1%, ±5%, or ±10%.','It provides a resistance of 10,000,000 ohms, making it ideal for sensitive measurement and control applications.','10 MΩ resistor is commonly used in voltage divider circuits, biasing networks for transistors and operational amplifiers, pull-up or pull-down configurations, sensor circuits, timing circuits (RC networks), and input protection circuits. It is especially useful in high-impedance signal applications, such as measuring small signals or preventing floating inputs in microcontroller systems. Since the current flowing through a 10 MΩ resistor is extremely small, power dissipation is usually very low, and it is commonly rated at ¼ watt or ½ watt.',NULL,'products/1771653078180-227209501.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 12:58:08'),
(2160,'8.1m ohm resistor',NULL,NULL,'Resistor',49.00,'An 8.1MΩ (8.1 Mega Ohm) resistor is a high-resistance electronic component used to limit current, divide voltage, or provide biasing in electronic circuits. The value 8.1MΩ means 8,100,000 ohms, which makes it suitable for very low-current applications such as signal processing, sensing circuits, timing networks, and high-impedance input stages. Because of its high resistance, it allows only a very small amount of current to pass through.','It provides a resistance of 8,100,000 ohms, making it suitable for sensitive signal and measurement applications.','8.1MΩ resistors are widely used in voltage divider circuits, feedback networks in amplifiers, leakage current control, sensor circuits, and high-voltage measurement applications.',NULL,'products/1771829367164-549147500.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 09:09:49'),
(2161,'BF495',NULL,NULL,'Transistor',99.00,'BF495 is an NPN RF (Radio Frequency) transistor designed for high-frequency amplification and switching applications.','It is commonly used in VHF/UHF amplifiers, RF oscillators, IF stages, and communication equipment where stable performance at higher frequencies is required.','It is commonly used in VHF/UHF amplifiers, RF oscillators, IF stages, and communication equipment where stable performance at higher frequencies is required.',NULL,'products/1771840574348-78403769.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 11:12:54'),
(2162,'46 ohm Resistor',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'A 46? (46 ohm) resistor is a low-to-mid value fixed resistor used to limit current, control signal levels, and provide precise impedance matching in electronic circuits.','The 46? value is a precision (E96-series) resistor, most commonly available with ±1% tolerance.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771673545578-543804376.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-11 11:19:01'),
(2163,'BF422',NULL,NULL,'Transistor',199.00,'The BF422 is a high-voltage NPN bipolar junction transistor (BJT) designed for amplification and switching applications in electronic circuits. It is especially suitable for video amplifier stages, television circuits, and high-voltage signal processing, where stable operation and reliable performance are required.','The transistor supports high collector-emitter voltage handling while maintaining low power consumption and good signal gain. Packaged in a compact TO-92 through-hole case, the BF422 is easy to mount on PCBs and is widely used in analog circuits, driver stages, and general-purpose electronic designs requiring moderate current and high voltage capability.','It is especially suitable for video amplifier stages, television circuits, and high-voltage signal processing, where stable operation and reliable performance are required.',NULL,'products/1771840103454-908727794.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 11:12:22'),
(2164,'B764',NULL,NULL,'Transistor',99.00,'The B764 (2SB764) is a PNP power transistor commonly used in audio amplifier and power regulation circuits. It is designed for medium to high-power switching and amplification applications, providing stable performance and good thermal reliability.','The transistor is typically paired with complementary NPN transistors in push-pull amplifier stages to deliver efficient audio output. With its TO-220 package, the B764 allows easy mounting with a heatsink for improved heat dissipation, making it suitable for amplifier boards, power supplies, and electronic control circuits.','With its TO-220 package, the B764 allows easy mounting with a heatsink for improved heat dissipation, making it suitable for amplifier boards, power supplies, and electronic control circuits.',NULL,'products/1771836014164-29998495.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 11:07:12'),
(2165,'3055T',NULL,NULL,'Transistor',101.00,'The 3055T (2N3055T) is a high-power NPN bipolar junction transistor commonly used in power amplifier and voltage regulator circuits.','The transistor offers good thermal stability and reliable performance in audio amplifiers, power supplies, and inverter circuits. Its compact TO-220 package allows easy mounting with a heatsink for better heat dissipation.','It is designed for switching and amplification applications requiring high current handling capability.',NULL,'products/1771668971576-476378543.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-02 12:59:15'),
(2166,'BT134 Transistor',NULL,NULL,'BT134 Transistor',99.00,'The BT134 is a sensitive-gate TRIAC (Triode for Alternating Current) used for controlling AC power in switching and phase-control applications. It allows bidirectional current flow and can control both halves of an AC waveform using a small gate trigger signal.','The BT134 is commonly used in light dimmers, fan speed controllers, heater controls, and motor speed regulation circuits. With its compact TO-220 package.','It provides reliable switching performance and efficient heat dissipation when mounted with a heatsink, making it suitable for household and industrial AC control applications.',NULL,'products/1771844026291-8906843.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 11:59:52'),
(2167,'P321J',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'The P321J is a polyester film capacitor commonly used in electronic circuits for signal coupling, filtering, timing, and noise suppression applications. The marking “321J” typically indicates the capacitor value and tolerance, where 321 represents a capacitance value of 320 pF (0.00032 µF) and J denotes a tolerance of ±5%. Polyester film capacitors are known for their stable electrical characteristics, low loss, and good reliability, making them suitable for both analog and digital electronic circuits.','This capacitor is non-polarized, meaning it can be connected in any direction within a circuit. It provides good insulation resistance and stable performance over a wide temperature range, which makes it useful in audio circuits, oscillators, timing networks, power supply filtering, and general electronic equipment.','Polyester capacitors like the P321J are widely used in consumer electronics, communication devices, industrial control boards, and DIY electronics projects due to their durability and consistent capacitance performance.',NULL,'products/1771995030156-466778425.png',0,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-04-09 14:05:13'),
(2169,'Reed Switch Sensor',NULL,NULL,NULL,199.00,'The Reed Switch Sensor is a magnetic proximity sensor used to detect the presence or absence of a magnetic field. It consists of two thin ferromagnetic metal reeds sealed inside a small glass tube filled with inert gas. When a magnet comes close to the sensor, the reeds attract each other and make electrical contact, closing the circuit. When the magnet moves away, the reeds separate, opening the circuit again','Reed switch sensors are available in Normally Open (NO), Normally Closed (NC), or changeover types, depending on application requirements. They operate without physical contact, resulting in low wear, long life, and high reliability. The sensor can be directly interfaced with microcontrollers such as Arduino, ESP8266, ESP32, or security control systems, as it works like a standard digital switch. It requires very low power and can operate over a wide voltage range depending on the model.','Reed switch sensors are widely used in door and window security systems, alarm systems, position detection, speed counting, water level monitoring, automotive sensing, and industrial automation. Because of their compact size, fast response, and simple installation, they are commonly used in both consumer electronics and industrial sensing applications.',NULL,'products/1771997772516-534274579.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 05:36:12'),
(2170,'LDR Sensor',NULL,NULL,NULL,199.00,'The LDR Sensor (Light Dependent Resistor Sensor) is an electronic light-sensing device used to detect the intensity of light in the surrounding environment. It works based on the principle of photoconductivity, where the resistance of the LDR changes according to the amount of light falling on its surface','An LDR sensor module typically includes a photoresistor, comparator IC, adjustable potentiometer for sensitivity control, and digital/analog output pins for easy interfacing with microcontrollers such as Arduino, ESP8266, and ESP32, LDR Sensor, 5mm, 12mm, 20mm','LDR sensors are widely used in automatic street lighting systems, smart home automation, solar garden lights, light-activated switches, security systems, brightness control circuits, and robotics projects. Due to its simple design, low cost, low power consumption, and reliable performance, the LDR sensor is one of the most commonly used light detection components in electronic and automation applications.',NULL,'products/1771915306992-628712955.jpeg',0,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-04-02 11:02:06'),
(2171,'102 NTC',NULL,NULL,'102 NTC Thermistor',149.00,'The 102 NTC thermistor is a temperature-sensitive resistor whose resistance decreases as temperature increases. The “102” marking indicates a 10KΩ resistance at 25°C, making it widely used for temperature sensing and control applications','It provides accurate thermal response and stable performance in electronic circuits. This component is commonly used in battery chargers, power supplies, and temperature monitoring systems.','102 NTC thermistor is a Negative Temperature Coefficient (NTC) temperature-sensitive resistor with a nominal resistance of 1kΩ (1000 ohms) at 25°C. The marking “102” follows the standard three-digit code system, where the first two digits (10) are the significant figures and the third digit (2) represents the number of zeros. Therefore, 10 × 10² = 1000Ω = 1kΩ. Since it is an NTC type, its resistance decreases as temperature increases and increases as temperature decreases.',NULL,'products/1771652520364-757453913.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 12:54:47'),
(2172,'104 NTC',NULL,NULL,'NTC Thermistor',149.00,'The 104 NTC thermistor is a temperature-sensitive resistor in which resistance decreases as temperature increases. The “104” marking indicates 100KΩ resistance at 25°C, making it suitable for precise temperature sensing and compensation circuits','It provides stable performance, high sensitivity, and fast thermal response. This thermistor is commonly used in battery chargers, power supplies, and temperature monitoring systems.','104 NTC thermistor is a Negative Temperature Coefficient (NTC) temperature-sensitive resistor with a nominal resistance of 100kΩ (100,000 ohms) at 25°C. The marking “104” follows the standard three-digit code system, where the first two digits (10) represent the significant figures and the third digit (4) indicates the number of zeros. Therefore, 10 × 10⁴ = 100,000Ω = 100kΩ. As an NTC thermistor, its resistance decreases when temperature increases and increases when temperature decreases.',NULL,'products/1771652960157-635770093.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 12:57:06'),
(2173,'103 NTC',NULL,NULL,NULL,198.00,'The 103 NTC thermistor is a temperature-dependent resistor where resistance decreases as temperature increases. The “103” code represents 10KΩ resistance at 25°C, making it suitable for accurate temperature sensing and compensation circuits.','It offers fast thermal response, stable characteristics, and reliable performance in electronic devices. This thermistor is widely used in power supplies, battery chargers, and temperature control applications.','103 NTC thermistor is a Negative Temperature Coefficient (NTC) temperature-sensitive resistor with a nominal resistance of 10kΩ (10,000 ohms) at 25°C. The marking “103” follows the standard three-digit code system, where the first two digits (10) represent the significant figures and the third digit (3) represents the number of zeros. Therefore, 10 × 10³ = 10,000Ω = 10kΩ. Since it is an NTC type thermistor, its resistance decreases as temperature increases and increases as temperature decreases.',NULL,'products/1771652619017-401167484.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 12:56:01'),
(2174,'472 NTC','NTC Thermistor',NULL,NULL,199.00,'The 472 NTC thermistor is a temperature-sensitive resistor in which resistance decreases as temperature increases, making it suitable for temperature sensing and compensation applications. The “472” marking indicates a resistance value of 4.7KΩ at 25°C, commonly used in electronic control circuits for accurate thermal monitoring.','It provides fast thermal response, high sensitivity, and stable performance across a wide temperature range. This thermistor is widely used in battery chargers, power supplies, air conditioners, home appliances, and industrial electronic systems for temperature detection and protection.','Typically available in an epoxy-coated bead type with radial leads, the 472 NTC offers reliable operation, compact size, and easy PCB mounting for various electronic designs.',NULL,'products/1771674464431-984205884.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 06:20:59'),
(2175,'22uF 160V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'22µF 160V capacitor is an electronic component used in electrical and electronic circuits to store and release electrical energy when required. The value 22 microfarads (µF) represents the capacitance, which indicates how much electrical charge the capacitor can store, while 160 volts (V) represents the maximum voltage the capacitor can safely handle without failure. This type of capacitor is commonly available as an aluminum electrolytic capacitor, which usually has a cylindrical body with two leads and is marked with its capacitance and voltage rating for identification.','22µF 160V capacitor is widely used for power supply filtering, voltage smoothing, signal coupling, and decoupling applications. It helps stabilize voltage levels by reducing ripple in power supplies and allows AC signals to pass while blocking DC in amplifier circuits. Because of its 160V rating, it can be safely used in circuits that operate at relatively high voltages such as power supply units, LED drivers, audio amplifier circuits, and switching power supplies.','Electrolytic capacitors of this type are polarized components, meaning they have positive and negative terminals that must be connected correctly in the circuit. Incorrect polarity may damage the capacitor or cause it to fail. These capacitors are typically designed to operate within temperature ranges such as –40°C to +105°C, depending on the manufacturer. Proper selection and correct installation ensure reliable operation, longer lifespan, and stable performance in electronic systems.',NULL,'products/1771663821469-708233629.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-04 11:47:45'),
(2176,'1uF 160V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'A 1µF 160V capacitor is a high-voltage capacitor used for signal coupling, decoupling, timing, and filtering in electronic circuits that operate at elevated voltages','Depending on the application, this value is commonly available as an electrolytic (polarized) or a film capacitor (non-polarized).','Depending on the application, this value is commonly available as an electrolytic (polarized) or a film capacitor (non-polarized).',NULL,'products/1771658705774-850100332.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-04 11:09:12'),
(2177,'10uF 450V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'10µF 450V capacitor is a high-voltage electrolytic capacitor designed to store and release electrical energy while maintaining stable voltage in electronic circuits. With a capacitance of 10 microfarads and a maximum rated voltage of 450 volts, it is commonly used in power electronics where high DC voltage handling is required.','This capacitor is typically polarized, meaning it has positive and negative terminals that must be connected correctly to avoid damage. It is widely used for filtering, smoothing, and decoupling in power supply circuits, especially after rectifiers to reduce voltage ripple. Due to its high voltage rating, it is well-suited for SMPS (Switched Mode Power Supplies), inverters, amplifiers, UPS systems, LED drivers, and industrial control circuits.','A 10µF 450V capacitor is a high-voltage electrolytic capacitor designed to store electrical energy and filter high DC voltages in electronic circuits. The value 10 microfarads (µF) represents the capacitance, which indicates the amount of charge it can store, while 450 volts (V) is the maximum voltage it can safely withstand.',NULL,'products/1771653588121-940237291.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-02 12:27:15'),
(2178,'10uF 160V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'10µF 160V capacitor is a high-voltage polarized electrolytic capacitor used for energy storage, filtering, and voltage stabilization in high-voltage DC circuits. The capacitance value of 10 microfarads (µF) indicates its ability to store electrical charge, while the 160V rating means it can safely operate at voltages up to 160 volts. Since it is an electrolytic capacitor, it has clearly marked positive (+) and negative (–) terminals, and correct polarity must always be maintained during installation to prevent leakage, overheating, or failure.','It is also recommended to discharge the capacitor safely before handling. From a system perspective, the 10µF 160V capacitor improves voltage stability, reduces ripple noise, supports load regulation, and enhances reliability in high-voltage electronic systems.','This capacitor is commonly used in SMPS power supplies, inverter circuits, LED driver circuits, high-voltage amplifier sections, industrial equipment, and rectified AC mains filtering applications. It is often placed after a rectifier to smooth high-voltage DC output by reducing ripple and maintaining a stable voltage. It stores energy during voltage peaks and releases it when the voltage drops, helping ensure consistent system operation.',NULL,'products/1771653352991-641655715.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 13:00:14'),
(2179,'33uF 160V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'A 33µF 160V capacitor is a high-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor used to store energy, smooth DC voltage, and reduce ripple in electronic circuits that operate at higher voltages','It is a polarized component, so correct polarity must be observed during installation.','A 33µF 160V capacitor is a medium-capacitance, high-voltage electrolytic capacitor commonly used in power supply and amplifier circuits. The value 33 microfarads (µF) represents the amount of electrical charge it can store, while the 160V rating indicates the maximum voltage the capacitor can safely handle. It is typically used in rectified DC sections, SMPS circuits, audio amplifiers, inverter boards, and industrial electronic systems where moderate capacitance and higher voltage tolerance are required.',NULL,'products/1771669776150-541681867.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-02 13:04:42'),
(2180,'1000uF 16V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'1000µF 16V capacitor is a low-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor commonly used for energy storage, filtering, and smoothing in electronic circuits. With a relatively high capacitance of 1000 microfarads and a maximum rated voltage of 16 volts, it is ideal for circuits operating at low to moderate DC voltages.','Capacitance: 1000µF\r\nVoltage rating: 16V DC\r\nType: Aluminum electrolytic (polarized)\r\nMain uses: Filtering, smoothing, bulk decoupling\r\nCommon applications: Audio circuits, power supplies, Arduino/MCU boards','A 1000µF 16V capacitor is an electrolytic capacitor commonly used in power supply and filtering applications. The value 1000 microfarads (µF) indicates its ability to store a relatively large amount of electrical charge, while the 16V rating means it can safely operate at voltages up to 16 volts. This type of capacitor is usually polarized, meaning it has clearly marked positive (+) and negative (–) terminals that must be connected correctly in a DC circuit. Incorrect polarity can cause leakage, overheating, or failure.',NULL,'products/1771651461049-413593947.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 12:36:48'),
(2181,'47uF 160V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'47µF 160V capacitor is an electronic component used to store electrical energy and release it when required in an electronic circuit. The capacitance value 47 microfarads (µF) indicates the amount of electric charge the capacitor can store, while the 160 volts (V) rating specifies the maximum voltage the capacitor can safely handle without breakdown.','47µF 160V capacitor is an electronic component used to store electrical energy and release it when required in an electronic circuit. The capacitance value 47 microfarads (µF) indicates the amount of electric charge the capacitor can store, while the 160 volts (V) rating specifies the maximum voltage the capacitor can safely handle without breakdown.','47µF 160V capacitor is widely used for power supply filtering, voltage smoothing, signal coupling, and decoupling applications. It helps reduce voltage ripple in power supplies and ensures a stable DC output. In audio and amplifier circuits, it can be used to block DC components while allowing AC signals to pass between stages.',NULL,'products/1771820890554-12339061.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-04 11:53:44'),
(2182,'220uF 160V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'A 220µF 160V capacitor is a high-capacitance, high-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor used to store energy, smooth DC output, and reduce ripple voltage in power and control circuits operating at elevated voltages','It is a polarized component, so correct polarity is essential during installation.','It is a polarized component, so correct polarity is essential during installation.',NULL,'products/1771663126698-731874556.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-04 11:04:34'),
(2183,'2.2uF 160V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'A 2.2µF 160V capacitor is an electronic component used to store and release electrical energy in a circuit. The value 2.2µF (microfarads) represents the capacitance, which indicates the amount of electrical charge the capacitor can store, while 160V represents the maximum voltage that the capacitor can safely handle without damage. These capacitors are commonly available as electrolytic capacitors or sometimes film capacitors, and they are widely used in electronic circuits for filtering, coupling, decoupling, and timing applications.','In electronic circuits, a 2.2µF 160V capacitor is often used in power supply filtering, audio circuits, signal coupling, and voltage smoothing. Because of its relatively high voltage rating, it can be used in circuits where voltage levels are higher, such as in power adapters, amplifier circuits, LED drivers, and switching power supplies.','These capacitors typically come in a cylindrical aluminum body with two radial leads at the bottom. The body is marked with its capacitance value (2.2µF) and voltage rating (160V) for easy identification. They are designed to operate within a specified temperature range, commonly –40°C to +105°C, depending on the manufacturer.',NULL,'products/1771659258436-684684341.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-04 11:22:56'),
(2184,'100uF 25V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'100µF 25V capacitor is a low- to medium-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor widely used for filtering, smoothing, and decoupling in electronic circuits. With a capacitance of 100 microfarads and a maximum rated voltage of 25 volts DC, it is suitable for many general-purpose applications where stable DC voltage is required.','100µF 25V capacitor is frequently used in microcontroller boards, audio circuits, DC adapters, voltage regulator outputs, LED drivers, and consumer electronics. It usually comes in a radial-lead cylindrical package, making it easy to solder onto PCBs.','A 100µF 25V capacitor is a polarized electrolytic capacitor commonly used in low- to medium-voltage DC electronic circuits for filtering, coupling, and voltage stabilization. The capacitance value of 100 microfarads (µF) indicates its ability to store a moderate amount of electrical energy, while the 25V rating means it can safely operate in circuits with voltages up to 25 volts. Since it is an electrolytic capacitor, it has clearly marked positive (+) and negative (–) terminals, and correct polarity must be maintained during installation to avoid leakage, overheating, or damage.',NULL,'products/1771652182018-923377868.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 12:41:56'),
(2185,'4.7uF 160V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'4.7µF 160V capacitor is a medium-capacitance, high-voltage capacitor commonly used in power supply and amplifier circuits. The value 4.7 microfarads (µF) indicates the amount of electrical charge it can store, while the 160V rating represents the maximum voltage it can safely withstand. It is typically used in rectified DC sections, SMPS (Switched Mode Power Supply) circuits, inverter boards, and audio systems where moderate capacitance and higher voltage tolerance are required.','This value is commonly available as an aluminum electrolytic (polarized) or a film capacitor (non-polarized), depending on stability and lifetime requirements.','Most 4.7µF 160V capacitors are electrolytic capacitors, which are polarized components and must be connected with correct positive (+) and negative (–) polarity. They help smooth DC voltage, reduce ripple, filter noise, and stabilize circuit performance. Because of the higher voltage rating, they are physically larger than low-voltage capacitors of similar capacitance.',NULL,'products/1771672061408-931775939.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-02 13:39:40'),
(2186,'100uF 160V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'A 100µF 160V capacitor is a high-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor designed to store electrical energy, smooth DC voltage, and reduce ripple in circuits operating at elevated voltages','This capacitor is commonly used in SMPS power supplies, inverter circuits, LED driver circuits, industrial equipment, audio amplifiers, and high-voltage DC filtering applications. It is often placed after a rectifier circuit to smooth high-voltage DC output by reducing ripple voltage. It stores energy when the voltage increases and releases it when the voltage drops, helping to maintain stable and steady DC output in high-voltage systems.','A 100µF 160V capacitor is a high-voltage polarized electrolytic capacitor used in power supply and high-voltage electronic circuits. The capacitance value of 100 microfarads (µF) indicates its ability to store electrical energy, while the 160V rating means it can safely operate at voltages up to 160 volts. Since it is an electrolytic type capacitor, it has clearly marked positive (+) and negative (–) terminals, and correct polarity must always be maintained during installation to prevent failure or explosion.',NULL,'products/1771652026542-869683601.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 12:40:19'),
(2187,'47uF 100V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'47µF 100V capacitor is a medium-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor used for filtering, smoothing, and energy storage in electronic circuits. It has a capacitance of 47 microfarads and a maximum rated voltage of 100 volts DC, making it suitable for circuits that operate at higher voltages than standard low-voltage electronics.','47µF 100V capacitor is widely used in SMPS circuits, audio amplifiers, power adapters, industrial control boards, inverter circuits, and high-voltage DC sections of electronic devices. It is usually available in a radial-lead cylindrical package, designed for reliable PCB mounting and long service life.','It has a capacitance of 47 microfarads and a maximum rated voltage of 100 volts DC, making it suitable for circuits that operate at higher voltages than standard low-voltage electronics.',NULL,'products/1771674563021-170644771.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-04 11:52:44'),
(2188,'4.7uF 250V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'4.7µF 250V capacitor is a high-voltage capacitor commonly used in power supply circuits, SMPS (Switched Mode Power Supply) units, audio amplifiers, and inverter boards. The value 4.7 microfarads (µF) indicates its charge storage capacity, while the 250V rating specifies the maximum voltage the capacitor can safely handle. It is typically used in rectified DC sections and high-voltage filtering applications where moderate capacitance and reliable voltage stability are required.','This value is commonly available as an aluminum electrolytic (polarized) or a film capacitor (non-polarized), depending on application requirements.','Most 4.7µF 250V capacitors are electrolytic capacitors, which are polarized and must be connected with correct positive (+) and negative (–) terminals. They help smooth DC voltage, reduce ripple, suppress noise, and stabilize circuit performance. Due to the higher voltage rating, these capacitors are larger in size compared to low-voltage types.',NULL,'products/1771672085875-755167252.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-02 13:41:08'),
(2189,'10uF 250V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'10µF 250V capacitor is a high-voltage polarized electrolytic capacitor used for energy storage, filtering, and voltage stabilization in high-voltage DC circuits. The capacitance value of 10 microfarads (µF) indicates its charge storage capability, while the 250V rating means it can safely operate at voltages up to 250 volts. Because it is an electrolytic capacitor, it has clearly marked positive (+) and negative (–) terminals, and correct polarity must be maintained during installation to prevent leakage, overheating, or explosion.','This value is commonly available as an aluminum electrolytic capacitor (polarized) and, in some cases, as a film capacitor (non-polarized).','This capacitor is commonly used in SMPS power supplies, inverter circuits, industrial power equipment, LED drivers, audio amplifier power sections, and rectified AC mains filtering applications. It is often placed after a bridge rectifier to smooth high-voltage DC output by reducing ripple voltage and stabilizing the supply. It stores energy during voltage peaks and releases it when voltage drops, helping maintain steady system performance.',NULL,'products/1771653415806-911168342.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 13:02:02'),
(2190,'4.7uF 400V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'A 4.7µF 400V capacitor is a high-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor used in electronic circuits that require reliable performance at elevated DC voltages.','4.7µF 400V capacitor is widely used in SMPS power supplies, LED drivers, inverters, audio amplifiers, UPS systems, and industrial electronic equipment. It typically comes in a radial-lead cylindrical package with an insulated aluminum body for durability and safe PCB mounting.','With a capacitance of 4.7 microfarads and a maximum rated voltage of 400 volts DC, it is ideal for applications where voltage handling is more critical than large capacitance.',NULL,'products/1771672112109-225033950.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-02 13:41:43'),
(2191,'47uF 250V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'47µF 250V capacitor is an electronic component used in electrical and electronic circuits to store and release electrical energy when needed. The value 47 microfarads (µF) represents the capacitance, which indicates the amount of electrical charge the capacitor can store, while 250 volts (V) represents the maximum voltage the capacitor can safely withstand.','This type of capacitor is commonly available as an aluminum electrolytic capacitor, which usually has a cylindrical body with two leads and is marked with its capacitance value and voltage rating for easy identification.','47µF 250V capacitor is widely used for power supply filtering, voltage smoothing, signal coupling, and decoupling applications. It helps reduce voltage ripple in power supply circuits and stabilizes the output voltage. In amplifier circuits, it allows AC signals to pass while blocking DC components between different stages.',NULL,'products/1771820918505-902925559.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-04 11:55:08'),
(2192,'4.7uF 450V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'4.7µF 450V capacitor is a high-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor designed for use in electronic circuits that operate at very high DC voltages.','4.7µF 450V capacitor is widely used in SMPS power supplies, LED drivers, inverters, audio amplifiers, UPS systems, and industrial electronic equipment. It is typically available in a radial-leaded cylindrical aluminum body, insulated for safety and reliable PCB mounting.','With a capacitance of 4.7 microfarads and a maximum rated voltage of 450 volts DC, it is commonly used where compact size and high voltage tolerance are required.',NULL,'products/1771672136901-782854167.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-02 13:42:43'),
(2193,'33uF 250V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'A 33µF 250V capacitor is a high-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor used to store energy, smooth DC voltage, and reduce ripple in electronic circuits that operate at elevated voltages','It is a polarized component, so correct polarity must be maintained during installation.','A 33µF 250V capacitor is a high-voltage electrolytic capacitor used in power supply, SMPS (Switched Mode Power Supply), amplifier, and inverter circuits. The value 33 microfarads (µF) indicates its charge storage capacity, while the 250V rating specifies the maximum voltage it can safely withstand. This makes it suitable for medium to high-voltage DC sections, especially after rectification in AC-to-DC conversion circuits.',NULL,'products/1771669798156-245760337.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-02 13:05:48'),
(2194,'100uF 63V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'100µF 63V capacitor is a medium-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor commonly used for filtering, smoothing, and decoupling in electronic circuits. With a capacitance of 100 microfarads and a maximum rated voltage of 63 volts DC, it is suitable for applications that operate at higher voltages than standard low-voltage electronics.','100µF 63V capacitor is widely used in power supplies, audio amplifiers, SMPS circuits, industrial control boards, motor driver circuits, and consumer electronics. It typically comes in a radial-lead cylindrical aluminum body, designed for easy PCB mounting and reliable long-term performance.','100µF 63V capacitor is a polarized electrolytic capacitor used for energy storage, filtering, and voltage stabilization in medium-voltage DC circuits. The capacitance value of 100 microfarads (µF) indicates its ability to store electrical charge, while the 63V rating means it can safely operate at voltages up to 63 volts. Because it is an electrolytic capacitor, it has clearly marked positive (+) and negative (–) terminals, and correct polarity must be maintained during installation to avoid leakage, overheating, or failure.',NULL,'products/1771652349252-725076475.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 12:50:42'),
(2195,'22uF 250V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'A 22µF 250V capacitor is a high-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor designed to store energy, smooth DC voltage, and reduce ripple in electronic circuits operating at elevated voltages','It is a polarized component, so correct polarity must be observed during installation.','Electrolytic capacitors of this type are polarized components, meaning they have positive and negative terminals that must be connected correctly in the circuit. Incorrect polarity may damage the capacitor or cause it to fail. These capacitors are typically designed to operate within temperature ranges such as –40°C to +105°C, depending on the manufacturer. ',NULL,'products/1771663862896-227636926.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-04 11:48:16'),
(2196,'3.3uF 250V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'A 3.3µF 250V capacitor is a high-voltage capacitor used in electronic circuits for signal coupling, decoupling, timing, and filtering where higher DC voltage handling is required','This value is commonly available in aluminum electrolytic (polarized) and film (non-polarized) types.','3.3µF 250V capacitor is an electronic component used to store and release electrical energy in medium to high-voltage circuits. The value 3.3 microfarads (µF) indicates the capacitance, which determines how much charge it can store, while the 250V rating represents the maximum voltage the capacitor can safely handle.',NULL,'products/1771667142854-742484082.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-02 12:51:40'),
(2197,'1000uF 35V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'1000µF 35V capacitor is a medium-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor widely used for bulk energy storage, filtering, and smoothing in electronic circuits. With a high capacitance of 1000 microfarads and a maximum rated voltage of 35 volts DC, it is well suited for power lines that require stable voltage and high current handling.','1000µF 35V capacitor is frequently used in power supplies, audio amplifiers, motor driver circuits, SMPS secondary sections, LED power circuits, and industrial control electronics. It usually comes in a radial-lead cylindrical aluminum body, providing easy PCB mounting and reliable long-term performance.','A 1000µF 35V capacitor is a polarized electrolytic capacitor widely used for power supply filtering, energy storage, and voltage stabilization in electronic circuits. The capacitance value of 1000 microfarads (µF) indicates its ability to store a large amount of electrical charge, while the 35V rating means it can safely handle voltages up to 35 volts. Since it is an electrolytic type, it has clearly marked positive (+) and negative (–) terminals, and correct polarity must be maintained during installation to prevent damage or failure.',NULL,'products/1771651822607-75175166.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 12:38:05'),
(2198,'100uF 250V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'A 100µF 250V capacitor is a high-capacitance, high-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor used to store electrical energy, smooth DC voltage, and reduce ripple in power and control circuits that operate at elevated voltages','This capacitor is commonly used in SMPS power supplies, inverter circuits, industrial power systems, audio amplifier power sections, LED drivers, and rectified AC mains filtering applications. After AC voltage is converted to DC using a rectifier, this capacitor helps smooth the DC output by reducing ripple voltage and maintaining stable power. It stores energy during voltage peaks and releases it during voltage drops, ensuring consistent system performance.','A 100µF 250V capacitor is a high-voltage polarized electrolytic capacitor designed for energy storage and DC filtering in high-voltage electronic circuits. The capacitance value of 100 microfarads (µF) indicates its ability to store electrical charge, while the 250V rating means it can safely operate at voltages up to 250 volts. Because it is an electrolytic capacitor, it has clearly marked positive (+) and negative (–) terminals, and correct polarity must be observed during installation to prevent leakage, overheating, or explosion.',NULL,'products/1771652075223-478432415.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 12:41:12'),
(2199,'470uF 35V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'470µF 35V capacitor is a medium-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor commonly used for filtering, smoothing, and energy storage in electronic circuits. With a capacitance of 470 microfarads and a maximum rated voltage of 35 volts DC, it is ideal for power supply and control circuits that operate at moderate voltages.','470µF 35V capacitor is widely used in DC power supplies, audio amplifiers, SMPS secondary circuits, motor driver boards, LED driver circuits, and consumer electronics. It generally comes in a radial-lead cylindrical aluminum package, designed for easy PCB mounting and long service life.','A 470µF 35V capacitor is a medium-to-high value electrolytic capacitor commonly used for power supply filtering, decoupling, and energy storage in low to medium voltage electronic circuits. The 470 microfarads (µF) capacitance allows it to store a moderate amount of electrical charge, making it effective for smoothing DC voltage and reducing ripple after rectification.',NULL,'products/1771674160049-188716420.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 06:17:02'),
(2200,'2.2uF 250V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'A 2.2µF 250V capacitor is an electronic component used to store electrical energy and release it when required in an electronic circuit. The value 2.2 microfarads (µF) indicates the capacitance, which represents the amount of electric charge the capacitor can hold, while 250 volts (V) indicates the maximum voltage the capacitor can safely withstand.','These capacitors are commonly available as electrolytic capacitors or polyester/film capacitors, and they are widely used in power supply circuits, audio equipment, and electronic control systems. Because of the higher voltage rating of 250V, this capacitor can operate safely in circuits that handle relatively high voltage levels such as power converters, amplifier circuits, LED drivers, and switching power supplies.','2.2µF 250V capacitor is often used for filtering, coupling, decoupling, and signal smoothing. In power supply sections, it helps reduce voltage ripple and stabilize the output voltage. In audio circuits, it can be used for signal coupling between amplifier stages to block DC while allowing AC signals to pass.',NULL,'products/1771659292257-655225357.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-04 11:34:42'),
