(2202,'100uF 35V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'A 100µF 35V capacitor is a polarized electrolytic capacitor used for energy storage, filtering, and voltage stabilization in low- to medium-voltage DC circuits. The capacitance value of 100 microfarads (µF) indicates its ability to store electrical charge, while the 35V rating means it can safely operate at voltages up to 35 volts. Since it is an electrolytic capacitor, it has clearly marked positive (+) and negative (–) terminals, and correct polarity must be followed during installation to prevent leakage, overheating, or failure.','A 35V capacitor is suitable for 12V and 24V systems. Proper placement near power supply lines improves filtering efficiency, and adequate ventilation is recommended since electrolytic capacitors can degrade over time due to heat. From a system perspective, the 100µF 35V capacitor enhances voltage stability, reduces electrical noise, supports load variations, and ensures reliable performance in DC electronic systems.','This capacitor is commonly used in 24V DC power supplies, audio amplifier circuits, motor driver boards, SMPS outputs, battery charging circuits, and microcontroller-based systems. Its main function is to smooth DC voltage by reducing ripple and stabilizing output after rectification. It also provides temporary energy storage to handle sudden load changes, improving circuit stability and performance.',NULL,'products/1771652244537-22441357.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 12:43:28'),
(2203,'4700uF 25V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',499.00,'4700µF 25V capacitor is a high-capacitance aluminum electrolytic capacitor designed for bulk energy storage, filtering, and smoothing in low- to medium-voltage electronic circuits. With a very large capacitance of 4700 microfarads and a maximum rated voltage of 25 volts DC, it is ideal for applications that require strong ripple reduction and stable power delivery.','4700µF 25V capacitor is widely used in audio amplifiers, DC power supplies, motor driver circuits, LED power supplies, SMPS secondary sections, and consumer electronics. It typically comes in a radial-lead cylindrical aluminum body, suitable for PCB mounting and long-term reliable operation.','A 4700µF 25V capacitor is a high-capacity electrolytic capacitor commonly used in power supply filtering and energy storage applications in electronic circuits. The value 4700 microfarads (µF) indicates a large capacitance, making it suitable for smoothing ripple voltage in DC power supplies, especially after rectification in AC-to-DC converters.',NULL,'products/1771673629585-281078315.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 06:11:44'),
(2204,'47uF 35V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'A 47µF 35V capacitor is a medium-value electrolytic capacitor commonly used in electronic circuits for filtering, decoupling, coupling, and energy storage applications. The capacitance value of 47 microfarads (µF) allows it to store a moderate amount of electrical charge, making it suitable for smoothing DC voltage and reducing ripple in low to medium voltage power supplies. The 35V rating indicates the maximum DC voltage the capacitor can safely handle; for better durability and longer lifespan, it is recommended to operate it below 25–30V.','This capacitor is polarized, meaning it has clearly marked positive (+) and negative (–) terminals and must be connected correctly. Incorrect polarity can cause overheating, leakage, bulging, or failure. It typically comes in a cylindrical aluminum casing with radial leads for PCB mounting and is usually available with temperature ratings of 85°C or 105°C.','The 47µF 35V capacitor is widely used in 12V–24V DC power supplies, audio amplifier circuits, voltage regulator output filtering, microcontroller boards, LED driver circuits, motor driver boards, and general electronic applications. It helps stabilize voltage, reduce noise, and provide temporary energy during sudden load changes.',NULL,'products/1771821161466-732103037.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 06:31:52'),
