(2241,'10uF 350V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'A 10µF 350V capacitor is a high-voltage capacitor commonly used in power supply circuits, SMPS (Switched Mode Power Supplies), amplifiers, and inverter circuits. The value 10 microfarads (µF) indicates the capacitance, which determines how much electrical charge the capacitor can store, while 350V represents the maximum voltage it can safely handle. This type of capacitor is typically used in circuits where high DC voltage is present, such as rectified mains power sections.','This capacitor helps smooth DC voltage, reduce ripple noise, and stabilize circuit performance. Built for reliable operation, it offers good endurance and stable electrical characteristics.','Most 10µF 350V capacitors are electrolytic capacitors, which are polarized components and must be connected with correct polarity (positive and negative terminals). They are designed to smooth high-voltage DC output, filter ripple voltage, and stabilize power supply lines. Because of the high voltage rating, these capacitors are physically larger compared to low-voltage capacitors of the same capacitance.',NULL,'products/1771653546648-179780471.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-02 12:26:05'),
(2242,'220uF 450V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'The 220µF 450V capacitor is a high-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor designed for power supply filtering and energy storage in electronic circuits','It is commonly used in SMPS power supplies, LED drivers, inverters, and amplifier systems to smooth rectified DC voltage and reduce ripple noise. Built for high reliability, it ensures stable operation in high-voltage applications.','The 220µF 450V capacitor is a high-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor designed for power supply filtering and energy storage in electronic circuits',NULL,'products/1771663620165-623324915.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-04 11:07:49'),
(2243,'470uF 450V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',198.00,'The 470µF 450V capacitor is a high-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor widely used in power supply and energy storage applications. It is designed to smooth and filter rectified DC voltage by reducing ripple and electrical noise in high-power electronic circuits.','This capacitor is commonly found in SMPS power supplies, inverters, LED drivers, industrial equipment, and audio amplifier power sections where stable high-voltage operation is required. Being a polarized component, it must be connected with correct polarity for safe operation','Built with durable aluminum electrolytic construction, it provides high capacitance, reliable performance, and long service life under proper operating conditions. The capacitor is typically available in a radial lead through-hole package and operates efficiently in circuits requiring high voltage handling and stable DC filtering.',NULL,'products/1771674256718-225921570.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 06:17:36'),
(2244,'470uF 250V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'The 470µF 250V capacitor is a high-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor designed for power supply filtering, energy storage, and voltage smoothing applications. It is commonly used in SMPS power supplies, inverter circuits, LED drivers, and industrial electronic equipment to reduce ripple voltage and stabilize DC output after rectification.This polarized capacitor provides high capacitance with reliable performance, making it suitable for high-voltage and high-current circuits.','Built with durable aluminum electrolyte construction, it offers good endurance, stable electrical characteristics, and long operational life when used within rated voltage and temperature limits. Typically available in a radial lead through-hole package, the 470µF 250V capacitor is widely used in power electronics and amplifier power sections for efficient and stable circuit operation.','A 470µF 250V capacitor is a high-voltage electrolytic capacitor designed for applications that require large capacitance with the ability to handle high DC voltage. The capacitance value of 470 microfarads (µF) allows it to store a significant amount of electrical energy, while the 250V rating means it can safely operate in circuits up to 250 volts DC. For reliability and longer life, it is recommended to use the capacitor at least 15–20% below its maximum rated voltage.',NULL,'products/1771674134362-281815958.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 06:15:39'),
(2245,'10000uF 50V Capacitor','Capacitor',NULL,'Capacitor',99.00,'10000µF 50V capacitor is widely used in amplifier circuits, SMPS power supplies, inverter systems, motor driver circuits, and battery charging systems. Its main function is to smooth rectified DC voltage by reducing ripple and stabilizing the output voltage. After AC is converted to DC using a rectifier, this capacitor stores energy during voltage peaks and releases it during drops, resulting in a more stable and clean DC output.','This capacitor is commonly used in amplifiers, power supplies, inverters, and industrial electronic equipment. Designed for stable performance, it provides reliable operation in high-voltage and high-current circuits.','10000µF 50V capacitor is a high-capacitance electrolytic capacitor mainly used for power supply filtering and energy storage in electronic circuits. The value 10000 microfarads (µF) indicates that the capacitor can store a large amount of electrical charge, while the 50V rating means it can safely operate at voltages up to 50 volts.',NULL,'products/1771651407192-735969237.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 12:33:49'),
(2246,'1500uF 6.3V Capacitor',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'The 1500µF 6.3V capacitor is a low-voltage aluminum electrolytic capacitor widely used for power filtering and voltage stabilization in electronic circuits. It helps smooth DC output by reducing ripple and electrical noise.','This capacitor is commonly found in motherboards, SMPS circuits, and low-voltage power supply applications. It offers reliable performance with good capacitance stability and long operating life.','A 1500µF 6.3V capacitor is a high-capacitance, low-voltage electrolytic capacitor commonly used in power supply filtering and voltage stabilization circuits. The value 1500 microfarads (µF) indicates a large charge storage capacity, making it suitable for smoothing ripple voltage and stabilizing DC output in low-voltage electronic systems. The 6.3V rating means the capacitor can safely operate in circuits where the voltage does not exceed 6.3 volts.',NULL,'products/1771656661768-32623766.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-02 12:43:47'),
(2247,'Current Sensor Module',NULL,NULL,NULL,399.00,'A Current Sensor Module is an electronic device used to measure the flow of electrical current in a circuit and convert it into a readable voltage signal. Most commonly based on Hall-effect sensing technology (such as ACS712 or ACS758), the module can measure both AC and DC current safely without direct electrical contact with the measuring circuit.','It provides an analog output proportional to the current, allowing easy interfacing with microcontrollers like Arduino, ESP32, and Raspberry Pi. These modules are widely used in power monitoring, battery management systems, motor control, and energy measurement applications due to their accuracy, electrical isolation, and simple integration.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771904588014-851095348.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-24 03:43:08'),
(2248,'1.0nF (102)',NULL,NULL,'Ceramic Capacitor',99.00,'A 1.0 nF (102) ceramic capacitor is a small-value, non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric to store electrical charge. The marking 102 represents 1000 pF, calculated as 10 × 10² pF. This value is widely used in electronic circuits where stable, low-loss capacitance is required.','A 1.0 nF ceramic capacitor is typically used for noise suppression, signal coupling, RF filtering, timing networks, and EMI/RFI reduction in analog, digital, and RF circuits. Because it is non-polarized, it can be connected in either direction and works well in AC signal paths.','A 1.0 nF (102) capacitor is a small-value capacitor commonly used in electronic circuits for signal filtering, timing, and frequency control applications. The marking “102” follows the standard three-digit capacitor code system, where the first two digits (10) represent the significant figures and the third digit (2) represents the number of zeros in picofarads (pF).',NULL,'products/1771647861049-497645556.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 12:18:00'),
(2249,'10nF (103)',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',99.00,'A 10 nF (103) ceramic capacitor is a non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric to store electrical energy. The marking 103 corresponds to 10,000 pF, calculated as 10 × 10³ pF, which is equal to 10 nF or 0.01 µF. This value is very commonly used in general electronic circuits.','A 10 nF ceramic capacitor is widely used for noise filtering, signal coupling, decoupling, and EMI/RFI suppression. It is often placed near IC power pins, across signal lines, or in RC timing and filtering networks. Being non-polarized, it can be connected in either direction, making it suitable for both AC and DC applications.','10nF (103) capacitor is a small-value non-polarized capacitor commonly used in filtering, coupling, timing, and noise suppression applications. The marking “103” follows the standard three-digit capacitor code system, where the first two digits (10) are the significant figures and the third digit (3) represents the number of zeros in picofarads (pF). Therefore, 10 × 10³ = 10,000 pF, which equals 10nF (0.01µF). This type of capacitor is typically available as a ceramic disc or multilayer ceramic capacitor (MLCC) and can be connected in any direction since it is non-polarized.',NULL,'products/1771653116546-578656485.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 12:59:11'),
(2250,'0.1nF (104)',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',99.00,'A 0.1 µF (104) ceramic capacitor is one of the most widely used non-polarized capacitors in electronics. It uses a ceramic dielectric and is designed to store and release small amounts of electrical energy quickly, making it ideal for noise suppression and decoupling.','The code 104 means 10 × 10? pF = 100,000 pF, which equals 100 nF or 0.1 µF. These capacitors are available in ceramic disc (through-hole) and MLCC / SMD packages and offer excellent high-frequency performance, low ESR, and high reliability.','A 0.1 nF (104) capacitor description requires a small clarification: the marking “104” does not represent 0.1 nF. In the standard three-digit capacitor code system, 104 means 10 followed by 4 zeros in picofarads (pF), which equals 100,000 pF = 100 nF = 0.1 µF. Therefore, a capacitor marked 104 is actually 100 nF (0.1 microfarad), not 0.1 nF.',NULL,'products/1771648640364-37765021.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 12:03:12'),
(2251,'22nF (223)',NULL,NULL,'Ceramic Capacitor',99.00,'This capacitor value is commonly available in ceramic disc (through-hole) and MLCC / SMD packages. It offers good stability, low dielectric loss, and reliable high-frequency performance. Typical voltage ratings range from 50 V to 630 V for disc types, while MLCC versions usually range from 16 V to 100 V, depending on size and dielectric class.','A 22 nF ceramic capacitor is widely used for signal coupling, noise filtering, decoupling, and EMI/RFI suppression in analog, digital, and power-supply circuits. Because it is non-polarized, it can be connected in either direction and works well in both AC and DC applications.','Typical voltage ratings range from 50 V to 630 V for disc types, while MLCC versions usually range from 16 V to 100 V, depending on size and dielectric class.',NULL,'products/1771663780623-172027251.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-04 11:46:23'),
(2252,'2.2nF (222)',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',199.00,'A 2.2 nF (222) ceramic capacitor is a small-value, non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric to store and release electrical charge efficiently. The marking 222 represents 2,200 pF, calculated as 22 × 10² pF, which equals 2.2 nF or 0.0022 µF.','This capacitor is available in ceramic disc (through-hole) and MLCC / SMD forms. It offers good high-frequency characteristics, low dielectric loss, and stable performance across a wide temperature range. ','Typical voltage ratings include 50 V, 100 V, 250 V, 400 V, and 630 V for disc capacitors, while MLCC versions usually range from 16 V to 100 V, depending on size and dielectric type.',NULL,'products/1771659226873-53708591.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-04 11:20:46'),
(2253,'47nF (473)',NULL,NULL,'Ceramic Capacitor',99.00,'A 47 nF (473) ceramic capacitor is a non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric to store and release electrical energy efficiently. The marking 473 represents 47,000 pF, calculated as 47 × 10³ pF, which is equal to 47 nF or 0.047 µF.','This capacitor value is widely available in ceramic disc (through-hole) and MLCC / SMD types. It offers good high-frequency performance, low dielectric loss, and stable operation, making it suitable for general-purpose electronic circuits. Typical voltage ratings range from 50 V to 630 V for disc capacitors, while MLCC versions are commonly rated 16 V to 100 V, depending on package size and dielectric class.','A 47nF (473) ceramic capacitor is a small, non-polarized capacitor widely used in electronic circuits for filtering, noise suppression, coupling, and decoupling applications. The value 47nF (nanofarads) is equal to 0.047µF, and the marking “473” follows the standard capacitor code system, where the first two digits (47) represent the significant figures and the third digit (3) represents the number of zeros in picofarads. So, 47 × 10³ pF = 47,000 pF, which equals 47nF.',NULL,'products/1771674530490-843083823.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 06:23:41'),
(2254,'0.047nF (47)',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',99.00,'A 0.047 nF ceramic capacitor is equivalent to 47 pF and is identified by the marking 47 on the capacitor body. It is a small-value, non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric, designed mainly for high-frequency applications.','Because of its very low capacitance, this value is commonly used in RF circuits, oscillators, tuning networks, and signal shaping applications. Ceramic capacitors of this value offer low loss, good stability, and fast response at high frequencies. They are most often found in ceramic disc (through-hole) form, though SMD versions are also available.','A 0.047 nF (47) capacitor is a very small-value capacitor commonly used in high-frequency electronic circuits. The marking “47” follows the standard capacitor code system where two digits indicate the value directly in picofarads (pF). Therefore, “47” means 47 pF, which is equal to 0.047 nF (since 1000 pF = 1 nF). This type of capacitor is typically non-polarized, so it can be connected in any direction in a circuit.',NULL,'products/1771648683937-237642705.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 11:56:09'),
(2255,'0.56nF (561)',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',99.00,'A 0.56 nF (561) ceramic capacitor is a small-value, non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric to store electrical charge. The marking 561 represents 560 pF, calculated as 56 × 10¹ pF, which is equal to 0.56 nF.','This capacitor value is commonly available in ceramic disc (through-hole) and MLCC / SMD packages. It offers low loss, good frequency stability, and reliable performance at high frequencies, making it suitable for signal-level and RF applications. Typical voltage ratings range from 50 V to 500 V or higher for disc types, while MLCC versions usually range from 16 V to 100 V, depending on size and dielectric.','A 0.56 nF (561) capacitor is a small-value ceramic capacitor commonly used in electronic circuits for filtering, timing, coupling, and noise suppression applications. The marking “561” follows the standard three-digit capacitor code system, where the first two digits represent the significant figures (56) and the third digit represents the number of zeros in picofarads (pF).',NULL,'products/1771648598340-132901053.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 11:09:12'),
(2256,'0.039nF (39)',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',99.00,'A 0.039 nF ceramic capacitor is equivalent to 39 pF and is typically marked “39” on the capacitor body. It is a non-polarized capacitor that uses a ceramic dielectric and is designed for high-frequency signal applications.','Typical voltage ratings include 50 V, 100 V, 250 V, and higher, making them suitable for low-current signal paths. Since it is non-polarized, it can be connected in either direction.','A 0.039 nF (39) capacitor is a small-value capacitor commonly used in high-frequency and signal-processing circuits. The marking “39” follows the standard capacitor coding system, where the value is expressed directly in picofarads (pF) when only two digits are printed. Therefore, “39” represents 39 pF, which is equal to 0.039 nF (since 1000 pF = 1 nF).',NULL,'products/1771648725344-283251256.png',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 11:55:10'),
(2257,'0.012nF (12k)',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'','',NULL,NULL,'products/1771648811184-858193948.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-18 08:55:15'),
(2258,'0.022nF (22)',NULL,NULL,'Capacitor',99.00,'A 0.022 nF ceramic capacitor is equivalent to 22 pF and is usually marked as “22” on the capacitor body. It is a non-polarized capacitor made using a ceramic dielectric and is mainly used in high-frequency and RF applications.','The 0.022nF (22) capacitor is a small-value ceramic capacitor commonly used in electronic circuits for high-frequency filtering, signal coupling, and noise suppression applications. The capacitance value 0.022nF is equal to 22 picofarads (22pF), making it suitable for RF circuits, oscillator circuits, timing networks, and signal tuning applications. The marking “22” on the capacitor typically represents the capacitance value of 22pF according to standard capacitor coding.','This capacitor is non-polarized, allowing it to be connected in any direction within a circuit. It is usually available in ceramic disc or surface-mount (SMD) form and provides stable electrical performance with low loss at high frequencies. Due to its very small capacitance value, it is mainly used in precision electronic circuits rather than power supply filtering.',NULL,'products/1771648762693-190042424.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-26 11:07:07'),
(2259,'boAt Ear-buds',NULL,NULL,NULL,1999.00,'boAt is a popular Indian consumer electronics and audio accessories brand known for stylish, feature-rich, and value-for-money audio products, especially earbuds (wireless & wired).','Bluetooth earbuds connected by a neckband cable — often with longer battery life.','boAt is a popular Indian consumer electronics and audio accessories brand known for stylish, feature-rich, and value-for-money audio products, especially earbuds (wireless & wired).',NULL,'products/1771843220867-210875497.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 11:31:06'),
(2260,'One Bolt ONB-011 Earbuds',NULL,NULL,NULL,1999.00,'One Bolt ONB-011 Earbuds are stylish and compact true wireless Bluetooth earbuds designed for everyday music listening and calling. These earbuds provide clear sound quality with balanced bass, making them suitable for music, online classes, and hands-free calls. The lightweight in-ear design ensures a comfortable fit for long usage, while the portable charging case allows easy carrying and extended battery backup.','The ONB-011 earbuds typically support Bluetooth connectivity for quick pairing with smartphones, tablets, and laptops. They come with built-in microphones for clear voice calls and touch/button controls for managing music and calls. With rechargeable battery support and a sleek modern look, One Bolt ONB-011 earbuds are ideal for daily use at home, office, travel, or workouts.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771994382158-32583980.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 03:30:21'),
(2261,'boAt TWS Wireless Headset',NULL,NULL,'Earbuds',999.00,'boAt TWS Wireless Headsets are popular True Wireless Stereo (TWS) earbuds from boAt, one of India’s top lifestyle and audio accessories brands. These earbuds combine wire-free convenience, bold design, and solid audio performance — especially for music, calls, and everyday use.','True Wireless Stereo (TWS): Left and right earbuds pair with each other without wires, delivering stereo sound.','These earbuds combine wire-free convenience, bold design, and solid audio performance — especially for music, calls, and everyday use.',NULL,'products/1771843278774-893964913.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 11:22:46'),
(2262,'Xtreme Bluetooth Speaker',NULL,NULL,NULL,1999.00,'The Xtreme Bluetooth Speaker is a high-performance wireless speaker designed to deliver powerful sound, deep bass, and clear vocals for both indoor and outdoor use. Built with a rugged yet stylish body, it is ideal for music lovers who want loud output, portability, and long-lasting performance in one device.','The Xtreme Bluetooth Speaker offers an excellent balance of sound quality, portability, and versatile features, making it a dependable choice for everyday music and entertainment needs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1772015093547-740520251.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 10:24:53'),
(2263,'3.6V 2000 mAh battery',NULL,NULL,'Lithium Battery',491.00,'A 3.6V 2000 mAh battery is a rechargeable lithium-based battery commonly used in electronic devices that require stable voltage and long backup time.','This battery is often available in Lithium-ion (Li-ion) or Lithium-thionyl chloride (Li-SOCl?) variants. The rechargeable Li-ion version is widely used due to its high energy density, lightweight design, and long cycle life.','It provides a nominal voltage of 3.6 volts with a capacity of 2000 milliampere-hours, making it suitable for both low-power and medium-power applications.',NULL,'products/1774082596042-592155652.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-21 08:43:16'),
(2264,'6V DC Lithium battery',NULL,NULL,'Lithium Battery',399.00,'A 6V DC lithium battery is a compact, high-efficiency power source designed to deliver a stable 6-volt direct current (DC) output. It is typically made by combining two 3.0V or 3.6/3.7V lithium cells in series and may include a built-in Battery Management System (BMS) for protection.','Compared to traditional lead-acid or NiMH batteries, lithium batteries offer higher energy density, lighter weight, and longer life, making them ideal for modern electronic and portable applications.','It is typically made by combining two 3.0V or 3.6/3.7V lithium cells in series and may include a built-in Battery Management System (BMS) for protection.',NULL,'products/1771824091708-196767722.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-03-03 07:23:18'),
(2265,'Panasonic 6V battery',NULL,NULL,NULL,10.00,'A Panasonic 6V battery is a reliable power source manufactured by Panasonic, known worldwide for high-quality batteries and electronic components.','Panasonic 6V batteries are widely used in electronics, industrial equipment, medical devices, and backup power systems due to their safety, durability, and consistent performance.',NULL,NULL,'products/1771995070536-461790917.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-02-13 10:15:23','2026-02-25 04:51:10'),
