(2753,'Hikvision Turret Camera 5 MP','DS-2CE76H0T-ITPFS',NULL,' Turret Camera 5 MP ',1.00,'The DS-2CE76H0T-ITPFS is a 5-megapixel analog HD turret (dome-style) CCTV camera designed for DVR-based surveillance systems.','The camera operates with HD-TVI technology, allowing high-quality video transmission through a standard coaxial cable (BNC) to a DVR recorder.','It also features a built-in microphone, enabling audio over coaxial cable so both sound and video can be recorded together.',NULL,'products/1772786156084-191864155.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-06 08:35:56','2026-03-06 08:35:56'),
(2754,'Hikvision Bullet Camera 5MP ','DS-2CE11H0T-PIRLO',NULL,NULL,1.00,'The DS-2CE11H0T-PIRLO is a 5-megapixel analog HD mini bullet CCTV camera designed for DVR-based surveillance systems.','It also includes a strobe light alarm that flashes when motion is detected to help deter intruders.','A key feature of this model is the PIR (Passive Infrared) motion detection sensor, which can detect human movement and trigger alarms or alerts in real time.',NULL,'products/1772786559025-406472969.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-03-06 08:42:39','2026-03-06 08:42:39'),
(2755,'Hikvision Turret Camera 5 MP','DS-2CE71H0T-PIRLO',NULL,'5 MP  Turret Camera',1.00,'The DS-2CE71H0T-PIRLO is a 5-megapixel analog HD turret (dome-style) CCTV camera designed for DVR-based surveillance systems.','A special feature of this model is the built-in PIR (Passive Infrared) motion detection sensor, which detects human movement and can trigger alarms when motion is detected.','The camera is available with 2.8 mm or 3.6 mm fixed lens options to provide different viewing angles.',NULL,'products/1772787081007-750556446.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-06 08:51:21','2026-03-06 08:51:21'),
(2756,'Basic Calculator',NULL,NULL,NULL,599.00,'A Basic Calculator is a simple electronic device used to perform fundamental mathematical operations quickly and accurately. It is commonly used by students, office workers, shopkeepers, and engineers for everyday calculations. A basic calculator typically supports essential arithmetic functions such as addition (+), subtraction (−), multiplication (×), and division (÷). Most models also include extra keys for percentage (%), square root (√), memory functions, and clear/reset operations, making calculations easier and more efficient','Basic calculators are designed with a numeric keypad, function buttons, and an LCD or LED display to show numbers and results. They are usually battery-powered or solar-powered, making them portable and convenient to use anywhere. These calculators are widely used in schools, offices, retail shops, laboratories, and homes for tasks such as accounting, budgeting, and simple mathematical problem-solving. Because of their simplicity, reliability, and low cost, basic calculators remain one of the most commonly used electronic calculation tools',NULL,NULL,'products/1772788309988-462141358.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-06 09:11:49','2026-03-06 09:11:49'),
(2757,'Hikvision Bullet Camera 2 MP','DS-2CE10DF0T-PFS',NULL,NULL,1.00,'The DS-2CE10DF0T-PFS is a 2-megapixel analog HD ColorVu mini bullet CCTV camera designed for DVR-based surveillance systems.','It uses a 2 MP CMOS image sensor to capture Full-HD video at 1920 × 1080 resolution, providing clear monitoring for homes, offices, shops, and outdoor areas.','The camera supports white-light night illumination up to about 20 meters, ensuring bright color images at night instead of traditional black-and-white infrared footage.',NULL,'products/1772788342810-951345031.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-03-06 09:12:22','2026-03-06 09:12:22'),
(2758,'GST Calculator',NULL,NULL,NULL,999.00,'A GST Calculator is a tool used to calculate the Goods and Services Tax (GST) amount on products or services. It helps businesses, shopkeepers, accountants, and customers quickly determine the GST amount and the final price including or excluding tax. GST calculators are widely used in countries like India where GST is applied to goods and services at different tax rates such as 5%, 12%, 18%, and 28%.','The calculator works by entering the original price of the product or service and selecting the applicable GST percentage. It then automatically calculates the GST amount and shows the total price including GST. Some GST calculators also allow reverse calculation, where users can find the original price and GST amount from a GST-inclusive price. This tool helps simplify tax calculations, reduce manual errors, and save time in billing, invoicing, and financial management. GST calculators are commonly available as online tools, mobile apps, and built-in features in accounting software and billing systems',NULL,NULL,'products/1772788401125-674235437.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-06 09:13:21','2026-03-06 09:13:21'),
(2759,'Scientific Calculator',NULL,NULL,NULL,1499.00,'A Scientific Calculator is an advanced electronic calculator designed to perform complex mathematical and scientific calculations. Unlike a basic calculator that handles simple arithmetic operations, a scientific calculator can perform functions such as trigonometry (sin, cos, tan), logarithms (log, ln), exponents, powers, roots, fractions, and statistical calculations. These calculators are widely used by students, engineers, scientists, and professionals in fields such as mathematics, physics, chemistry, and engineering.','Scientific calculators usually feature a large keypad with multiple function buttons and a digital display, allowing users to perform advanced calculations quickly and accurately. Many models support bracket operations, memory storage, angle conversions (degrees, radians, grads), and scientific notation, which are essential for solving complex equations and formulas. Some modern scientific calculators also include multi-line displays, equation solving, and programming features. Because of their ability to handle advanced mathematical functions efficiently, scientific calculators are commonly used in schools, colleges, laboratories, and technical work environments',NULL,NULL,'products/1772788501286-17743886.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-06 09:15:01','2026-03-06 09:15:01'),
