(3072,'OP07',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'OP07 is a precision operational amplifier (op-amp) integrated circuit designed for applications that require very low input offset voltage and high accuracy. It is widely used in analog signal processing circuits where stable and precise amplification is important. The IC operates with dual power supplies (such as ±12V or ±15V), although it can also be used in single-supply configurations with proper biasing.','OP07 offers low noise, low drift, high open-loop gain, and excellent temperature stability, making it suitable for sensitive measurement and control systems. It also includes offset null pins, which allow users to adjust and minimize output error caused by input offset voltage. The IC is commonly used in instrumentation amplifiers, sensor signal conditioning circuits, active filters, data acquisition systems, voltage comparators, and laboratory equipment',NULL,NULL,'products/1773475968124-777745680.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 08:12:48','2026-03-14 08:12:48'),
(3073,'MCT2E',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'MCT2E is an opto-isolator (optocoupler) integrated circuit used to provide electrical isolation between input and output circuits while transferring signals using light. It consists of an infrared LED on the input side and a phototransistor on the output side, allowing signals to pass without direct electrical connection. This helps protect sensitive electronic components from high voltage spikes, noise, and ground loop problems.','The MCT2E operates with low input current and supports standard digital switching applications, making it suitable for microcontroller interfacing and power control circuits. It offers high isolation voltage, good reliability, and low power consumption, which are important features in industrial and control systems. The IC is commonly used in SMPS feedback circuits, relay driver isolation, triac triggering, signal isolation, automation systems, and communication interfaces. Due to its simple interfacing, safety isolation capability, and dependable performance, MCT2E is widely used in power electronics and embedded electronic designs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773476067467-87457647.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 08:14:27','2026-03-14 08:14:27'),
(3074,'MCT6',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'MCT6 is an opto-isolator (optocoupler) integrated circuit used to provide electrical isolation between two circuits while allowing signal transfer through light. It contains an infrared LED at the input side and a phototransistor at the output side, which enables safe signal coupling without direct electrical connection. This isolation helps protect low-voltage control circuits from high-voltage spikes, electrical noise, and ground loop issues.','The MCT6 operates with low input current and supports digital switching applications, making it suitable for microcontroller and logic interfacing. It offers good isolation voltage, reliable performance, and low power consumption, which are important for industrial and automation systems. The IC is commonly used in SMPS feedback control, relay and triac driver circuits, signal isolation, industrial control equipment, and communication interfaces',NULL,NULL,'products/1773476230372-569676516.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 08:17:10','2026-03-14 08:17:10'),
(3075,'4N33',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'4N33 is an opto-isolator (optocoupler) integrated circuit used to provide electrical isolation between input and output circuits while transferring signals through light. It consists of an infrared LED on the input side and a phototransistor with base connection on the output side, allowing flexible signal control and amplification. This design helps protect sensitive electronic components from high voltage surges, electrical noise, and ground loop problems.','The 4N33 offers good current transfer ratio, high isolation voltage, and reliable switching performance, making it suitable for both analog and digital interfacing applications. It operates with low input drive current and can be used in microcontroller interfaces, SMPS feedback circuits, relay driver isolation, triac triggering circuits, and industrial control systems. Due to its stable operation, simple interfacing, and effective signal isolation capability, the 4N33 is widely used in power electronics, communication equipment, and embedded electronic project designs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773476335292-776967977.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 08:18:55','2026-03-14 08:18:55'),
(3076,'4N35',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'4N35 is a popular opto-isolator (optocoupler) integrated circuit used to provide electrical isolation between input and output circuits while allowing signal transfer using light. It consists of an infrared LED on the input side and a phototransistor on the output side, enabling safe signal coupling without a direct electrical connection. This helps protect sensitive control circuits from high voltage spikes, electrical noise, and ground loop interference.','The 4N35 offers good current transfer ratio, high isolation voltage, and reliable switching characteristics, making it suitable for both analog and digital signal interfacing. It operates with low input current and can be easily used with microcontrollers, logic circuits, and power control systems. The IC is commonly used in SMPS feedback circuits, relay driver isolation, triac triggering, industrial automation systems, and communication interfaces. Due to its simple application circuit, stable performance, and effective safety isolation, the 4N35 is widely used in power electronics and embedded electronic projects.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773476456418-693334469.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 08:20:56','2026-03-14 08:20:56'),
(3077,'6N136',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'6N136 is a high-speed opto-isolator (optocoupler) integrated circuit designed for fast digital signal isolation between two electrically separate circuits. It contains an infrared LED at the input side and a high-gain photodetector with output amplifier and open-collector output on the output side. This design allows high data transfer rates and reliable switching performance, making it suitable for communication and logic interface applications.','The 6N136 provides high isolation voltage, low propagation delay, and good noise immunity, which help protect sensitive low-voltage control circuits from high-voltage transients and electrical interference. It operates with low input drive current and is commonly used in microcontroller and microprocessor interfacing, SMPS feedback control, digital communication links, gate drive circuits, and industrial automation systems. Due to its fast response, stable operation, and effective electrical isolation, the 6N136 is widely used in high-speed embedded and power electronic designs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773476596423-224375941.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 08:23:16','2026-03-14 08:23:16'),
(3078,'6N137',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'6N137 is a high-speed opto-isolator (optocoupler) integrated circuit used for fast and reliable digital signal isolation between two electrically separate circuits. It consists of an infrared LED at the input side and a high-gain photodiode with integrated output amplifier and open-collector output on the output side. This internal design enables very fast switching speed, low propagation delay, and high data transfer capability, making it suitable for high-frequency logic applications.','The 6N137 provides high isolation voltage, strong noise immunity, and stable performance, which helps protect sensitive control circuits from high-voltage spikes and electrical interference. It operates with low input current and typically requires an external pull-up resistor at the output.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773477392755-555583699.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 08:36:32','2026-03-14 08:36:32'),
(3079,'6N139',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'6N139 is a high-gain opto-isolator (optocoupler) integrated circuit used to provide electrical isolation between input and output circuits while transferring signals through light. It contains an infrared LED on the input side and a phototransistor with amplifier stage on the output side, which helps achieve a high current transfer ratio and reliable signal amplification. This design protects sensitive control circuits from high voltage spikes, electrical noise, and ground loop interference.','The 6N139 offers high isolation voltage, good noise immunity, and stable switching performance, making it suitable for both digital and low-speed communication applications. It operates with low input current and typically uses an open-collector output with an external pull-up resistor.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773479041495-834517106.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 09:04:01','2026-03-14 09:04:01'),
(3080,'H11G1',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'H11G1 is an opto-isolator (optocoupler) integrated circuit designed to provide electrical isolation between input and output circuits while transferring signals through light. It consists of an infrared LED on the input side and a photodarlington transistor on the output side, which offers very high current gain and improved sensitivity. This helps protect low-voltage control circuits from high voltage surges, electrical noise, and ground loop problems.','The H11G1 provides high isolation voltage, good noise immunity, and reliable switching characteristics, making it suitable for low-speed signal isolation applications. It operates with low input drive current and is commonly used in relay driver isolation, SMPS feedback circuits, industrial control systems, alarm circuits, and microcontroller interfacing. Due to its high output gain, simple interfacing, and dependable performance, the H11G1 is widely used in power electronics and embedded electronic designs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773479131002-494256046.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 09:05:31','2026-03-14 09:05:31'),
(3081,'H11L1',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'H11L1 is a Schmitt trigger opto-isolator (optocoupler) integrated circuit used for high-noise-immunity digital signal isolation between input and output circuits. It consists of an infrared LED on the input side and an integrated photodetector with Schmitt trigger logic output on the output side. This design provides clean switching action, fast response, and stable output even with slow or noisy input signals.','The H11L1 offers high isolation voltage, low propagation delay, and excellent noise rejection, making it suitable for reliable digital interfacing. It operates with low input current and typically provides a TTL/CMOS compatible output, allowing easy connection to microcontrollers and logic circuits. The IC is commonly used in pulse shaping circuits, digital communication interfaces, SMPS control systems, motor control circuits, industrial automation equipment, and signal conditioning applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773479874064-95557324.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 09:17:54','2026-03-14 09:17:54'),
(3082,'CNY17-2',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'CNY17-2 is a phototransistor opto-isolator (optocoupler) integrated circuit used to provide electrical isolation between input and output circuits while allowing signal transfer through light. It consists of an infrared LED on the input side and a silicon phototransistor on the output side, enabling safe signal coupling without a direct electrical connection. This helps protect sensitive electronic components from high-voltage transients, electrical noise, and ground loop interference.','The CNY17-2 offers a moderate current transfer ratio (CTR), good isolation voltage, and reliable switching performance, making it suitable for general-purpose signal isolation. It operates with low input drive current and can be easily interfaced with microcontrollers, logic circuits, and power control stages. The IC is commonly used in SMPS feedback circuits, relay driver isolation, triac triggering, industrial automation systems, communication interfaces, and measurement equipment.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773480006000-919266066.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 09:20:06','2026-03-14 09:20:06'),
