(3085,'MOC3011',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'MOC3011 is an opto-isolated triac driver integrated circuit used for safely controlling AC loads while providing electrical isolation between low-voltage control circuits and high-voltage power circuits. It contains an infrared LED on the input side and a light-activated triac driver on the output side, allowing AC devices to be switched without direct electrical connection. This helps protect sensitive electronic components from high voltage surges, electrical noise, and ground loop problems.','The MOC3011 is designed for random phase triggering, which makes it suitable for applications such as light dimmers, motor speed control circuits, heater control systems, and solid-state relay designs. It operates with low input drive current and typically requires an external power triac for controlling high-power loads',NULL,NULL,'products/1773480507813-414177525.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 09:28:27','2026-03-14 09:28:27'),
