(3088,'MOC3022',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'MOC3022 is an opto-isolated triac driver integrated circuit used for controlling AC loads with electrical isolation between the low-voltage control side and the high-voltage power side. It consists of an infrared LED at the input and a light-activated triac driver at the output, allowing safe switching of AC devices without direct electrical connection. This isolation helps protect sensitive electronic circuits from high-voltage spikes, electrical noise, and surge conditions.','The MOC3022 is designed for random phase triggering, which makes it suitable for applications such as lamp dimmer circuits, fan and motor speed control, heater power regulation, and solid-state relay systems. It operates with low input current and usually requires an external power triac to control high-power loads.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773481560471-862966354.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 09:46:00','2026-03-14 09:46:00'),
(3089,'MOC3041',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'MOC3041 is an opto-isolated triac driver integrated circuit with zero-cross detection, used for safely controlling AC loads while providing electrical isolation between low-voltage control circuits and high-voltage power circuits. It contains an infrared LED on the input side and a zero-crossing triac driver on the output side, allowing AC devices to be switched ON when the AC waveform crosses zero voltage. This feature helps reduce electrical noise, surge current, and electromagnetic interference.','The MOC3041 operates with low input drive current and typically requires an external power triac to control high-power AC loads. It is commonly used in heater control systems, lamp switching circuits, solid-state relays, home appliance control units, and industrial automation equipment where simple ON/OFF control with minimal noise is required. Due to its high isolation voltage, reliable performance, and easy interfacing, MOC3041 is widely used in power electronics and embedded control applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773481703542-344574688.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 09:48:23','2026-03-14 09:48:23'),
(3090,'MOC3052',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'MOC3052 is an opto-isolated triac driver integrated circuit with zero-cross switching feature, used for safe control of AC loads while providing electrical isolation between low-voltage control circuits and high-voltage power circuits. It consists of an infrared LED at the input side and a light-activated triac driver with zero-cross detection at the output side, allowing AC devices to turn ON near the zero-voltage point of the AC waveform. This helps reduce electrical noise, inrush current, and electromagnetic interference.','The MOC3052 operates with low input drive current and normally requires an external power triac to handle high-power loads. It offers high isolation voltage, reliable switching performance, and simple interfacing, making it suitable for heater control systems, lamp switching, solid-state relay circuits, motor control units, industrial automation equipment, and home appliance control applications. Due to its stable operation and improved noise performance, the MOC3052 is widely used in embedded and power electronic designs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773482589624-591097956.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 10:03:09','2026-03-14 10:03:09'),
(3091,'MOC3061',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'MOC3061 is an opto-isolated triac driver integrated circuit with zero-cross detection, used for safely controlling AC loads while maintaining electrical isolation between low-voltage control circuits and high-voltage power circuits. It contains an infrared LED at the input and a light-activated triac driver at the output, which switches the load ON when the AC waveform passes through the zero-voltage point. This feature helps reduce switching noise, surge current, and electromagnetic interference.','The MOC3061 operates with low input drive current and typically requires an external power triac to control high-power AC devices. It provides good isolation voltage, reliable switching performance, and simple interfacing, making it suitable for heater control systems, lamp switching circuits, solid-state relays, home appliance control units, and industrial automation equipment. Due to its stable operation and improved noise suppression, the MOC3061 is widely used in power electronics and embedded control applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773482760180-442181999.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 10:06:00','2026-03-14 10:06:00'),
(3092,'MOC3063',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'MOC3063 is an opto-isolated triac driver integrated circuit with zero-cross switching feature, used for safe control of AC loads while providing electrical isolation between low-voltage control circuits and high-voltage power circuits. It consists of an infrared LED on the input side and a light-activated triac driver with built-in zero-cross detection on the output side, which allows the load to switch ON when the AC waveform crosses zero voltage. This helps reduce electrical noise, inrush current, and electromagnetic interference.','The MOC3063 operates with low input trigger current and normally requires an external power triac for controlling high-power AC devices. It offers high isolation voltage, reliable switching performance, and simple interfacing, making it suitable for heater control systems, lamp switching circuits, solid-state relays, motor control units, home appliance controllers, and industrial automation equipment. Due to its stable operation and improved noise suppression capability, the MOC3063 is widely used in power electronics and embedded control designs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773482840158-620354786.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 10:07:20','2026-03-14 10:07:20'),
(3093,'MOC3083',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'MOC3083 is an opto-isolated triac driver integrated circuit with zero-cross switching, used for safely controlling AC loads while providing electrical isolation between low-voltage control circuits and high-voltage power circuits. It contains an infrared LED at the input side and a light-activated triac driver with built-in zero-cross detection at the output, allowing the load to switch ON when the AC waveform crosses the zero-voltage point.','The MOC3083 operates with low input trigger current and typically requires an external power triac to control high-power AC devices. It provides high isolation voltage, reliable switching characteristics, and simple interfacing, making it suitable for solid-state relay circuits, heater control systems, lamp switching units, motor control circuits, industrial automation equipment, and home appliance controllers',NULL,NULL,'products/1773483240439-370550141.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 10:14:00','2026-03-14 10:14:00'),
(3094,'HCPL2630',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'HCPL2630 is a high-speed dual opto-isolator integrated circuit used for fast digital signal isolation between low-voltage control circuits and high-voltage power circuits. It contains two independent optocoupler channels, each with an infrared LED input and a high-gain photodetector with integrated amplifier output. This design allows high data transfer rates, low propagation delay, and reliable switching performance in digital communication systems.','The HCPL2630 provides high isolation voltage, strong noise immunity, and stable operation, helping to protect sensitive electronic components from voltage spikes and electrical interference. It operates with low input drive current and typically features open-collector outputs that require external pull-up resistors.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773483342933-647601604.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 10:15:42','2026-03-14 10:15:42'),
(3095,'HCPL2731',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'HCPL2731 is a high-speed dual-channel opto-isolator integrated circuit designed for fast digital signal isolation between low-voltage logic circuits and high-voltage power systems. It contains two independent optocoupler channels, each consisting of an infrared LED input and a high-gain photodetector with an integrated output amplifier. This internal structure enables low propagation delay, high data transfer capability, and reliable switching performance in high-frequency digital applications.','The HCPL2731 provides high isolation voltage, strong noise immunity, and stable operation, helping protect sensitive electronic circuits from voltage transients and electrical interference. It operates with low input drive current and typically features open-collector outputs that require external pull-up resistors for proper logic interfacing.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773483443143-595217165.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 10:17:23','2026-03-14 10:17:23'),
(3096,'HCPL3700',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'HCPL3700 is an AC/DC input opto-isolator integrated circuit designed for voltage level detection and electrical isolation between high-voltage input signals and low-voltage control circuits. It contains an internal LED with threshold detection circuitry and an output photodetector with amplifier, allowing it to sense both AC and DC voltage levels without requiring complex external components. This feature makes it suitable for mains voltage sensing and logic signal isolation applications.','The HCPL3700 provides high isolation voltage, good noise immunity, and reliable switching performance, helping to protect sensitive electronics from voltage surges and electrical interference. It operates over a wide input voltage range and typically offers a TTL/CMOS compatible output, making it easy to interface with microcontrollers and digital logic circuits.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773483570016-228323087.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 10:19:30','2026-03-14 10:19:30'),
(3097,'MPC3023',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'MOC3023 is an opto-isolated triac driver integrated circuit used for controlling AC loads with electrical isolation between low-voltage control circuits and high-voltage power circuits. It consists of an infrared LED at the input and a light-activated triac driver at the output, allowing safe switching of AC devices without direct electrical connection. This isolation helps protect sensitive electronics from high-voltage surges, electrical noise, and ground loop problems.','The MOC3023 is designed for random-phase triggering, making it suitable for applications such as lamp dimmers, fan and motor speed control, heater control systems, and solid-state relay circuits. It operates with low input trigger current and normally requires an external power triac to handle high-power AC loads',NULL,NULL,'products/1773483683652-377385839.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 10:21:23','2026-03-14 10:21:23'),
(3098,'ADC0804',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'ADC0804 is an 8-bit analog-to-digital converter (ADC) integrated circuit used to convert analog voltage signals into digital data for processing by microcontrollers and digital systems. It operates using the successive approximation conversion method, which provides a good balance between speed and accuracy. The IC typically works with a single +5V power supply and can measure analog input voltages within a specified reference range.','ADC0804 includes built-in clock generation capability, control signals for start and end of conversion, and tri-state digital outputs, making it easy to interface with microprocessors and microcontrollers. It offers moderate conversion speed, reasonable resolution (8-bit), and reliable performance for general-purpose measurement applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773484841048-490767413.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 10:40:41','2026-03-14 10:40:41'),
(3099,'ADC0808',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'ADC0808 is an 8-bit analog-to-digital converter (ADC) integrated circuit that includes an 8-channel analog multiplexer, allowing multiple analog signals to be converted into digital form using a single IC. It uses the successive approximation conversion technique, which provides a good balance between conversion speed and accuracy. The IC typically operates with a +5V power supply and accepts analog input voltages within a defined reference range.','ADC0808 provides address select lines to choose one of the eight input channels, along with control signals such as Start Conversion (SC), End of Conversion (EOC), and Output Enable (OE) for easy interfacing with microcontrollers and microprocessors. It offers moderate conversion speed, reliable performance, and simple interfacing, making it suitable for general data acquisition applications',NULL,NULL,'products/1773485161488-595432731.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 10:46:01','2026-03-14 10:46:01'),
(3100,'ADC0809',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'ADC0809 is an 8-bit analog-to-digital converter (ADC) integrated circuit with a built-in 8-channel analog multiplexer, allowing multiple analog input signals to be converted into digital form using a single device. It works on the successive approximation conversion method, providing a good balance between conversion speed and accuracy. The IC typically operates from a single +5V power supply and accepts analog input voltages within a defined reference range.','ADC0809 includes channel address select lines, start conversion control, end-of-conversion indication, and tri-state digital outputs, making it easy to interface with microcontrollers and microprocessors. It offers reliable performance, moderate conversion speed, and simple circuit design, which are suitable for general-purpose measurement systems.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773485281604-312988100.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 10:48:01','2026-03-14 10:48:01'),
(3101,'ADC0838',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'ADC0838 is an 8-bit analog-to-digital converter (ADC) integrated circuit that features a multiplexed analog input structure, allowing multiple analog signals to be converted into digital data using a single device. It uses the successive approximation conversion technique, which provides reliable performance with moderate conversion speed. The IC typically operates from a single +5V supply and supports both single-ended and differential analog input modes, making it flexible for various measurement applications.','ADC0838 offers a serial data interface, which simplifies connection with microcontrollers by reducing the number of required input/output pins. It includes control signals for start of conversion, clock input, and data output, enabling efficient digital communication.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773485573586-897536688.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 10:52:53','2026-03-14 10:52:53'),
(3102,'DAC0800',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'DAC0800 is an 8-bit digital-to-analog converter (DAC) integrated circuit used to convert digital input data into corresponding analog output signals. It operates using current steering technology, providing fast conversion speed and good linearity for analog signal generation. The IC typically requires dual power supply (such as ±5V to ±15V) and produces a current output, which is usually converted into a voltage using an external operational amplifier.','DAC0800 offers high accuracy, low settling time, and reliable performance, making it suitable for waveform generation and control applications. It includes parallel digital input lines, allowing easy interfacing with microprocessors and digital logic circuits',NULL,NULL,'products/1773486139529-882003827.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 11:02:19','2026-03-14 11:02:19'),
(3103,'DAC0808',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'DAC0808 is an 8-bit digital-to-analog converter (DAC) integrated circuit used to convert digital binary data into a proportional analog current output. It operates using a current steering technique, which provides fast conversion speed and good linearity. The IC typically requires a dual power supply (such as ±5V to ±15V) and produces a current output that is usually converted into a voltage using an external operational amplifier.','DAC0808 offers high accuracy, low settling time, and stable performance, making it suitable for analog signal generation and control applications. It features parallel digital input lines, allowing easy interfacing with microprocessors, microcontrollers, and digital logic circuits',NULL,NULL,'products/1773486241392-518889177.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-14 11:04:01','2026-03-14 11:04:01'),
(3104,'IRF150',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'IRF150 is a power N-channel MOSFET transistor designed for high-current and high-voltage switching applications in electronic circuits. It operates in enhancement mode, meaning the device turns ON when a suitable positive voltage is applied to the gate terminal. The MOSFET typically supports high drain current capability and high power dissipation, making it suitable for demanding power control tasks.','IRF150 offers low ON-state resistance, fast switching speed, and good thermal stability, which help improve efficiency in switching circuits. It is commonly used in SMPS (switch-mode power supplies), motor control circuits, inverter systems, DC-DC converters, battery charging circuits, and industrial power control applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773634216459-172402561.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 04:10:16','2026-03-16 04:10:16'),
