(3123,'IRF840',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'IRF840 is a high-voltage power N-channel MOSFET transistor used for switching and power control applications in electronic circuits. It operates in enhancement mode, meaning the device turns ON when a suitable positive voltage is applied to the gate terminal. The MOSFET can withstand high drain-source voltage and moderate current levels, making it suitable for high-voltage switching operations.','IRF840 provides fast switching performance, relatively low ON-state resistance, and good thermal stability, which help improve efficiency in power conversion circuits. It is commonly used in switch-mode power supplies (SMPS), inverter circuits, lighting control systems, DC-DC converters, motor drive circuits, and industrial power control equipment. The device is usually available in a TO-220 package and typically requires a proper heat sink for reliable high-power operation. Due to its rugged construction and dependable performance, IRF840 is widely used in embedded electronics, hobby projects, and industrial switching applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773640324095-438594188.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 05:52:04','2026-03-16 05:52:04'),
