(3125,'Optical 4 Meter cable','Optical  cable',NULL,NULL,1.00,'A 4-meter optical cable is a short-to-medium length fiber optic patch cord used for connecting devices such as fiber modem (ONU), Wi-Fi router, network switch, patch panel, or fiber distribution box.','It is suitable for indoor broadband and networking setups where equipment is placed a few meters apart.','Keep connectors clean and covered with dust caps',NULL,'products/1773640758261-934175899.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 05:59:18','2026-03-16 05:59:18'),
(3126,'IRF3205',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'IRF3205 is a high-performance N-channel power MOSFET widely used for switching and power control applications in electronic circuits. It is designed to handle high current (up to about 110A) and moderate voltage levels (55V drain-source voltage) with very low ON-state resistance, which helps reduce power loss and improve efficiency','Due to its fast switching capability and rugged construction, the IRF3205 is commonly used in inverters, DC motor drivers, SMPS power supplies, battery chargers, DC-DC converters, and high-power LED drivers. The device is available in a TO-220 package, making it easy to mount on a heat sink for thermal management during high-load operation. Proper gate drive voltage, heat dissipation, and protection components such as gate resistors and flyback diodes are recommended to ensure reliable and long-term performance.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773640762426-280492277.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 05:59:22','2026-03-16 05:59:22'),
(3127,'IRF3710',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'IRF3710 is a powerful N-channel enhancement mode MOSFET designed for high-speed switching and high-current applications. It can handle drain-source voltage up to about 100V and continuous drain current around 57A, making it suitable for medium-to-high power electronic circuits. The device features low ON-state resistance, which helps to reduce heat generation and improve overall efficiency in switching operations.','Because of its fast switching characteristics and rugged design, the IRF3710 is widely used in inverters, motor control circuits, DC-DC converters, switching power supplies (SMPS), battery chargers, and power amplifier stages. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, allowing easy mounting with a heat sink for better thermal performance. For reliable operation, proper gate drive voltage, heat dissipation, and protection components such as gate resistors and flyback diodes should be used, especially when driving inductive loads.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773640958879-43482476.png',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 06:02:38','2026-03-16 06:02:38'),
(3128,'IRFP3710',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'IRFP3710 is a high-power N-channel MOSFET designed for efficient switching and power control in heavy-duty electronic applications. It is capable of handling high drain-source voltage (about 100V) and very high continuous drain current (around 57A or more depending on cooling conditions). The device features low ON-state resistance, which reduces conduction losses and improves overall circuit efficiency. Due to its fast switching performance and rugged construction, IRFP3710 is commonly used in inverters, high-power SMPS circuits, motor drivers, DC-DC converters, battery charging systems, and audio power amplifier stages.','It is typically available in a TO-247 package, which provides better heat dissipation compared to smaller packages and allows reliable operation in high-current environments when used with an appropriate heat sink. For stable performance, designers usually provide a suitable gate drive voltage (around 10–12V), gate resistor, and protection components such as flyback diodes when controlling inductive loads.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773641788159-311017388.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 06:16:28','2026-03-16 06:16:28'),
(3129,'IRF3415',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'IRF3415 is a reliable N-channel power MOSFET designed for efficient high-speed switching and power management applications. It supports a drain-source voltage of about 150V and can handle high current levels (around 40A depending on operating conditions and cooling). The device features low ON-state resistance, which helps reduce power dissipation and improves efficiency in switching circuits.','Because of its strong switching capability and rugged construction, the IRF3415 is widely used in SMPS power supplies, DC-DC converters, inverter circuits, motor control systems, battery charging units, and high-power electronic switching applications. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, allowing easy mounting on a heat sink for better thermal performance during continuous high-load operation. For reliable performance, designers typically use an adequate gate drive voltage, proper heat dissipation, and protection components such as gate resistors and flyback diodes, especially when driving inductive loads.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773642549681-95134486.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 06:29:09','2026-03-16 06:29:09'),
(3130,'IRF4905',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'IRF4905 is a high-power P-channel MOSFET mainly used for high-current switching and power control applications. It is designed to operate with a drain-source voltage of about −55V and can handle continuous drain current up to around −70A under proper cooling conditions. The device offers low ON-state resistance, which helps minimize conduction losses and improves overall efficiency in power circuits. Due to its fast switching characteristics and rugged construction, IRF4905 is widely used in battery protection circuits, DC motor control, inverter stages, power supply switching, load switching, and automotive electronics.','It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, making it easy to mount on a heat sink for better thermal management during high-load operation. For stable and reliable performance, designers typically provide an appropriate negative gate drive voltage, gate resistor, and protective components such as flyback diodes when switching inductive loads.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773642607263-463935343.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 06:30:07','2026-03-16 06:30:07'),
(3131,'IRF9520',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'IRF9520 is a widely used P-channel power MOSFET designed for medium-power switching and control applications. It can withstand a drain-source voltage of about −100V and supports continuous drain current around −6A to −10A depending on cooling and operating conditions. The device offers reasonably low ON-state resistance, which helps reduce power loss and improves efficiency in switching circuits.','Because of its reliable switching performance and simple gate drive requirements, the IRF9520 is commonly used in power supply circuits, load switching, motor control stages, battery-operated systems, audio amplifier sections, and DC-DC converter designs. It is generally available in a TO-220 package, allowing easy installation with a heat sink for better thermal dissipation during continuous operation. For safe and stable performance, designers typically use proper gate drive voltage, a gate resistor for switching stability, and protection components such as flyback diodes when driving inductive loads.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773642677003-183951196.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 06:31:17','2026-03-16 06:31:17'),
(3132,'IRF9530',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'IRF9530 is a P-channel enhancement mode power MOSFET commonly used for switching and power management in electronic circuits. It is designed to handle a drain-source voltage of about −100V and can carry continuous drain current up to around −12A under proper cooling conditions. The device provides moderate ON-state resistance, enabling efficient operation in medium-power switching applications.','Due to its dependable switching characteristics and rugged construction, the IRF9530 is widely used in power supply circuits, DC motor control, inverter sections, battery-powered equipment, load switching stages, and audio amplifier circuits. It is typically available in a TO-220 package, which allows convenient mounting on a heat sink for improved heat dissipation during prolonged high-load operation. For stable and reliable performance, designers usually ensure an appropriate negative gate drive voltage, use of a gate resistor, and protective components such as flyback diodes when switching inductive loads.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773642730171-693332063.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 06:32:10','2026-03-16 06:32:10'),
