(3138,'4N60',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'4N60 is a high-voltage N-channel power MOSFET widely used in switching power supply and power control applications. It is designed to withstand a drain-source voltage of about 600V and can handle continuous drain current around 4A depending on cooling and operating conditions. The device provides good switching performance and moderate ON-state resistance, making it suitable for high-voltage, low-to-medium current circuits.','Because of its reliable operation and rugged structure, the 4N60 MOSFET is commonly used in SMPS power supplies, LED driver circuits, inverter stages, battery chargers, AC-DC converters, and other high-voltage switching applications. It is generally available in a TO-220 package, allowing easy mounting on a heat sink for better thermal dissipation during continuous operation. For safe and stable performance, designers usually provide an appropriate gate drive voltage, a gate resistor for controlled switching, and protection components such as snubber circuits or flyback diodes when used with inductive loads.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773643197383-462042133.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 06:39:57','2026-03-16 06:39:57'),
(3139,'Optical  5 Meter Cables',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'A 5-meter optical cable is a fiber optic patch cord used to connect devices such as fiber modem (ONU), Wi-Fi router, network switch, patch panel, or fiber distribution box.\r\nIt is suitable for indoor broadband installations and networking setups where equipment is placed a few meters apart.','Constructed with thin glass or plastic fiber core that transmits data as light signals.','Keep connectors clean and protected with dust caps',NULL,'products/1773643766533-373986000.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 06:49:26','2026-03-16 06:49:26'),
(3140,'2SK962',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'2SK962 is an N-channel power MOSFET designed for high-voltage switching and power control applications. It is typically rated for a drain-source voltage of around 900V and supports continuous drain current of about 6A under suitable operating and cooling conditions. The device offers stable switching characteristics and is suitable for circuits where high voltage handling capability is required with moderate current load.','Due to its rugged construction and reliable performance, the 2SK962 is widely used in switching mode power supplies (SMPS), inverter circuits, CRT and monitor power sections, high-voltage regulators, and industrial power control systems. It is commonly available in a TO-220 style package, allowing convenient mounting on a heat sink to improve thermal management during continuous operation. For safe and efficient performance, designers usually ensure proper gate drive voltage, controlled switching with a gate resistor, and protection components such as snubber networks or flyback diodes when operating with inductive loads.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773644551743-76544654.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:02:31','2026-03-16 07:02:31'),
(3141,'IRFBG30',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'IRFBG30 is a high-voltage N-channel power MOSFET designed for efficient switching and power control in electronic circuits. It can withstand a drain-source voltage of about 1000V and is capable of handling continuous drain current around 3A–4A, depending on operating conditions and heat dissipation. The device features stable switching characteristics and moderate ON-state resistance, making it suitable for high-voltage, low-to-medium current applications.','Because of its rugged construction and reliable performance, IRFBG30 is commonly used in switch-mode power supplies (SMPS), inverter circuits, high-voltage regulators, industrial power control systems, CRT monitor power stages, and AC-DC converter applications. It is generally available in a TO-220 package, allowing easy mounting on a heat sink for improved thermal management during continuous operation. For safe and stable performance, designers typically use an appropriate gate drive voltage, gate resistor for controlled switching, and protection components such as snubber networks or flyback diodes when switching inductive loads.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773644606191-389836039.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:03:26','2026-03-16 07:03:26'),
(3142,'16TTS12',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'16TTS12 is a high-power SCR (Silicon Controlled Rectifier / Thyristor) designed for controlled rectification and switching in high-voltage power circuits. It is typically rated for a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 1200V and can handle average forward current around 16A, making it suitable for medium-to-high power industrial applications. The device operates by applying a trigger pulse at the gate terminal, which allows current to flow between the anode and cathode until the current drops below the holding level.','Because of its rugged construction and reliable switching characteristics, the 16TTS12 is widely used in controlled rectifiers, AC voltage regulators, motor speed control systems, battery chargers, inverter circuits, welding equipment, and industrial power control applications. It is commonly available in a stud-type power package, which enables efficient heat dissipation when mounted on an appropriate heat sink. For safe and stable operation, proper gate triggering circuitry, snubber networks, and adequate thermal management are recommended during high-load usage.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773644670545-521731461.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:04:30','2026-03-16 07:04:30'),
(3143,'25TTS12',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'25TTS12 is a high-power SCR (Silicon Controlled Rectifier / Thyristor) used for controlled switching and rectification in industrial and power electronic circuits. It is typically rated for a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 1200V and can handle average forward current around 25A, depending on cooling and operating conditions. The device is triggered by applying a gate pulse, which allows current to flow between the anode and cathode until the current falls below the holding level.','Because of its rugged construction and dependable performance, the 25TTS12 is widely used in controlled rectifier circuits, AC voltage regulators, motor speed controllers, battery charging systems, inverter stages, welding machines, and industrial power control equipment. It usually comes in a stud-type power package, allowing strong mechanical mounting and efficient heat dissipation when fixed to a suitable heat sink. For safe and reliable operation, designers typically use proper gate triggering circuits, snubber networks, and adequate thermal management during high-power applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773644728061-35217877.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:05:28','2026-03-16 07:05:28'),
(3144,'20ETS12',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'20ETS12 is a high-power SCR (Silicon Controlled Rectifier / Thyristor) designed for controlled rectification and switching in high-voltage power electronic circuits. It is typically rated for a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 1200 V and can handle an average forward current around 20 A, depending on operating conditions and heat dissipation. The device is turned ON by applying a trigger pulse to the gate terminal, allowing current to flow from anode to cathode until the current falls below the holding level.','Due to its rugged construction and reliable switching characteristics, the 20ETS12 is widely used in AC power control systems, controlled rectifiers, motor speed controllers, battery chargers, inverter circuits, welding equipment, and industrial power regulation applications. It is commonly available in a stud-type power package, which enables secure mounting on a heat sink for efficient thermal management during continuous high-load operation. For safe and stable performance, proper gate triggering circuitry, snubber networks, and adequate cooling arrangements are recommended.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773644797715-37489208.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:06:37','2026-03-16 07:06:37'),
(3145,'40TPS12',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'40TPS12 is a high-power SCR (Silicon Controlled Rectifier / Thyristor) used for controlled switching and rectification in heavy-duty power electronic applications. It is generally rated for a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 1200 V and can handle an average forward current around 40 A, depending on operating temperature and cooling conditions. The device is switched ON by applying a gate trigger pulse, allowing current to flow between the anode and cathode until the current drops below the holding level.','Because of its rugged design and high current capability, the 40TPS12 is widely used in industrial rectifier units, AC voltage regulators, motor speed control systems, battery charging equipment, inverter stages, welding machines, and other industrial power control circuits. It is commonly available in a stud-type power package, enabling strong mechanical mounting and efficient heat dissipation when installed on a suitable heat sink. For reliable operation, proper gate drive circuitry, snubber protection networks, and effective thermal management are recommended in high-power applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773644856162-208893052.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:07:36','2026-03-16 07:07:36'),
(3146,'40TTS12',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'40TTS12 is a high-power SCR (Silicon Controlled Rectifier / Thyristor) designed for controlled rectification and switching in industrial power electronic circuits. It is typically rated for a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 1200 V and can handle an average forward current of around 40 A, depending on operating conditions and cooling arrangements. The device is triggered into conduction by applying a gate pulse, allowing current to flow from the anode to the cathode until the current falls below the holding level.','Due to its rugged construction and reliable performance, the 40TTS12 is widely used in controlled rectifiers, AC voltage regulators, motor speed control systems, battery chargers, inverter circuits, welding machines, and industrial power control equipment. It generally comes in a stud-type power package, enabling strong mechanical mounting and effective heat dissipation when fitted with a suitable heat sink. For safe and stable operation, designers typically use proper gate triggering circuits, snubber networks, and adequate thermal management in high-power applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773644926777-579631849.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:08:46','2026-03-16 07:08:46'),
(3147,'CT60AM',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'CT60AM is a high-power SCR (Silicon Controlled Rectifier) / Thyristor module designed for heavy-duty power control and rectification applications. It is typically capable of handling high blocking voltage (around 600V to 1200V depending on variant) and high forward current capacity of about 60A, making it suitable for industrial and high-power electronic circuits. The device operates by applying a trigger signal at the gate terminal, which allows current conduction between the anode and cathode until the current drops below the holding level.','Because of its robust construction and high reliability, CT60AM is widely used in controlled rectifier units, motor speed control systems, AC voltage regulators, battery charging equipment, inverter stages, welding machines, and industrial automation power circuits. It is usually available in a power module or stud-type package, allowing secure mounting on a heat sink or metal chassis for efficient heat dissipation during continuous high-load operation. For safe and stable performance, proper gate triggering circuits, snubber protection networks, and adequate cooling arrangements are recommended in practical applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773644994267-835960888.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:09:54','2026-03-16 07:09:54'),
