(3153,'5LO380',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'5LO380 is a high-voltage power switching device (commonly used as a MOSFET or power transistor depending on manufacturer series) designed for use in switch-mode power supplies and high-voltage electronic circuits. It is typically capable of handling high collector/drain voltage in the range of about 700 V–900 V and supports moderate current levels, making it suitable for off-line power supply and inverter applications. The device is built for reliable switching performance, good thermal stability, and rugged operation in demanding power control environments.','Because of its high-voltage capability, the 5LO380 is commonly used in SMPS circuits, LED driver power stages, inverter sections, industrial power control systems, CRT/monitor power units, and AC-DC conversion circuits. It is generally available in a TO-220 or similar power package, allowing convenient mounting on a heat sink for efficient heat dissipation during continuous operation. For safe and stable use, designers typically include proper gate/base drive circuitry, snubber or protection networks, and adequate cooling arrangements in practical power designs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773645414433-553032774.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:16:54','2026-03-16 07:16:54'),
(3154,'FAN7392',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'FAN7392 is a high-speed high-side and low-side gate driver IC designed to drive MOSFETs or IGBTs in half-bridge and full-bridge power switching circuits. It is capable of operating with high floating supply voltage (up to around 600 V) and provides strong output drive capability for efficient switching performance. The IC includes features such as under-voltage lockout (UVLO), matched propagation delay, and high noise immunity, making it suitable for reliable operation in high-power electronic systems.','Because of its fast switching characteristics and robust design, the FAN7392 is widely used in inverter circuits, motor drive systems, induction heating equipment, switching mode power supplies (SMPS), UPS systems, and DC-AC converter applications. It is commonly available in a SOP / DIP power package, allowing compact PCB mounting in modern power electronics designs. For proper operation, designers typically use suitable bootstrap components, gate resistors, proper PCB layout, and adequate isolation techniques to ensure stable and efficient switching performance.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773646177194-922611147.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:29:37','2026-03-16 07:29:37'),
(3155,'FQA38N30',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'FQA38N30 is a high-power N-channel MOSFET designed for efficient switching and power control in medium-to-high voltage electronic circuits. It is typically rated for a drain-source voltage of about 300 V and can handle continuous drain current around 30 A to 38 A, depending on operating temperature and heat-sink conditions. The device features low ON-state resistance and fast switching capability, which helps reduce power loss and improve efficiency in high-power switching applications.','Because of its rugged construction and reliable performance, the FQA38N30 MOSFET is widely used in inverter systems, switching mode power supplies (SMPS), motor control circuits, DC-DC converters, induction heating equipment, UPS systems, and power amplifier stages. It is generally available in a TO-3P / TO-247 style power package, allowing secure mounting on a heat sink for effective thermal dissipation during continuous high-load operation. For stable performance, designers typically use a suitable gate drive voltage (around 10–15 V), gate resistor for controlled switching, and protective components such as snubber or flyback networks when driving inductive loads.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773646263802-929197365.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:31:03','2026-03-16 07:31:03'),
(3156,'IR2110',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'IR2110 is a widely used high-side and low-side gate driver IC designed to drive MOSFETs and IGBTs in half-bridge and full-bridge power switching circuits. It can operate with a high-side floating voltage up to about 500–600 V, making it suitable for high-voltage inverter and motor control applications. The IC provides high peak output current, fast switching speed, under-voltage lockout protection, and strong noise immunity, which helps ensure efficient and reliable switching performance.','Because of its versatility and rugged design, the IR2110 is commonly used in DC-AC inverters, UPS systems, SMPS power supplies, induction heating equipment, solar inverter circuits, and motor driver applications. It is available in DIP and SOIC packages, allowing easy integration into both prototype and compact PCB designs. For proper operation, designers typically use suitable bootstrap components, gate resistors, proper PCB grounding/layout, and isolation techniques to achieve stable and efficient switching in practical power electronics circuits.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773646343690-995315759.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:32:23','2026-03-16 07:32:23'),
(3157,'IR2121',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'IR2121 is a high-performance high-side gate driver IC designed to drive N-channel MOSFETs or IGBTs in high-voltage power switching applications. It can operate with a floating high-side voltage up to about 600 V, making it suitable for off-line and industrial power control circuits. The device provides fast switching capability, high peak gate drive current, under-voltage lockout protection, and built-in over-current detection, which helps improve system reliability and protection.','Because of its robust design and protective features, the IR2121 is widely used in inverter circuits, motor drive systems, switching mode power supplies (SMPS), UPS equipment, induction heating units, and DC-AC converter applications. It is commonly available in DIP or SOIC packages, allowing convenient PCB mounting in both prototype and compact power electronics designs. For stable operation, designers typically use proper bootstrap supply components, gate resistors, current-sense networks, and careful PCB layout to ensure efficient and reliable switching performance.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773646409908-643721585.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:33:29','2026-03-16 07:33:29'),
(3158,'IR2152',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'IR2152 is a self-oscillating half-bridge gate driver IC designed to drive MOSFETs or IGBTs in high-voltage power conversion circuits. It combines a high-side and low-side driver with an internal oscillator, allowing simple implementation of half-bridge inverter and SMPS designs without requiring an external PWM controller. The IC can typically operate with floating high-side voltage up to about 600 V, making it suitable for offline AC-DC and DC-AC power applications.','Because of its built-in oscillator, reliable switching performance, and simple circuit design, the IR2152 is widely used in electronic ballasts, SMPS power supplies, inverter circuits, LED drivers, induction heating units, and low-cost DC-AC converter applications. It is commonly available in DIP and SOIC packages, enabling easy PCB mounting for both prototype and compact power electronics systems. For stable and efficient operation, designers generally use suitable bootstrap components, timing resistor-capacitor network, gate resistors, and proper PCB grounding/layout techniques.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773646573038-974491053.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:36:13','2026-03-16 07:36:13'),
(3159,'AD421 BN',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'AD421BN is a precision 4–20 mA current loop transmitter IC developed for industrial process control and instrumentation applications. It is designed to convert digital or analog input signals into a standard 4–20 mA current output, which is widely used in industrial automation systems for reliable long-distance signal transmission with high noise immunity. The device integrates key functions such as voltage regulation, current control circuitry, reference source, and protection features, enabling simple and accurate implementation of transmitter modules.','Because of its high accuracy and stable performance, the AD421BN is commonly used in PLC systems, industrial sensors, pressure and temperature transmitters, data acquisition systems, and process control equipment. It is generally available in a DIP package, allowing easy PCB mounting and integration into industrial electronic designs. For proper operation, designers typically use suitable external sensing components, calibration networks, and filtering arrangements to achieve precise and reliable current loop transmission.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773647309818-373600016.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:48:29','2026-03-16 07:48:29'),
(3160,'AD536 AJH',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'AD536AJH is a precision true RMS-to-DC converter integrated circuit manufactured for accurate measurement of AC signals. It converts an AC input waveform into a proportional DC output voltage representing the true RMS value, independent of waveform shape. The device offers high accuracy, wide dynamic range, and good temperature stability, making it suitable for precision instrumentation and signal processing applications.','Because of its reliable performance and ability to measure complex waveforms, the AD536AJH is widely used in digital multimeters, power measurement equipment, audio level monitoring systems, industrial instrumentation, data acquisition systems, and laboratory test equipment. It is typically available in a metal can (TO-100 / TO-99 style) or DIP package, allowing secure mounting and shielding for sensitive measurement circuits. For proper operation, designers usually provide external averaging components, calibration adjustments, and proper shielding/grounding techniques to achieve stable and accurate RMS measurements.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773647411949-440556752.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:50:11','2026-03-16 07:50:11'),
(3161,'AD581 JH',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'AD581JH is a high-stability precision voltage reference IC designed to provide an accurate and temperature-compensated reference voltage for analog and digital measurement systems. It typically offers a stable reference output (commonly around 10 V) with low drift, low noise, and excellent long-term stability, making it suitable for precision instrumentation and calibration circuits. The device integrates internal temperature compensation and trimming, ensuring consistent performance over a wide operating temperature range.','Due to its reliable accuracy and robust construction, the AD581JH is widely used in digital multimeters, data acquisition systems, ADC/DAC reference circuits, laboratory test equipment, industrial process control instruments, and calibration standards. It is commonly available in a metal can (TO-99 / TO-100 style) package, which provides good shielding and thermal stability for sensitive analog applications. For best performance, designers typically use proper decoupling capacitors, stable power supply filtering, and careful PCB layout to maintain precision and reduce noise effects.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773647471043-107385278.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:51:11','2026-03-16 07:51:11'),
(3162,'AD590',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'AD590 is a precision two-terminal temperature sensor IC that outputs a current proportional to absolute temperature. It typically produces 1 µA per Kelvin (µA/K), which means the output current changes linearly with temperature, making it easy to measure temperature using simple resistor or amplifier circuits. The device offers high accuracy, good linearity, low self-heating, and excellent long-term stability, making it suitable for precision temperature sensing applications.','Because of its reliable performance and simple interface, the AD590 is widely used in industrial temperature monitoring, HVAC systems, data acquisition equipment, instrumentation, thermal protection circuits, and scientific measurement systems. It is commonly available in metal can (TO-52 / TO-99) and TO-92 packages, allowing flexible mounting for both laboratory and industrial environments. For best accuracy, designers typically use stable biasing, proper calibration, and shielding or filtering techniques to reduce noise and improve measurement stability.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773647545421-188371190.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:52:25','2026-03-16 07:52:25'),
(3163,'AD620',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'AD620 is a low-cost, high-accuracy instrumentation amplifier IC widely used for amplifying very small differential signals in noisy environments. It offers high input impedance, low offset voltage, low noise, and excellent common-mode rejection ratio (CMRR), making it ideal for precision signal conditioning applications. The amplifier gain can be easily set from 1 to 1000 using a single external resistor, which simplifies circuit design and calibration.','Because of its stable performance and easy gain control, the AD620 is commonly used in medical instrumentation (such as ECG/EEG amplifiers), load cell and strain gauge signal conditioning, temperature measurement systems, data acquisition equipment, industrial process control, and sensor interface circuits. It is typically available in DIP and SOIC packages, allowing convenient use in both prototype and compact PCB designs. For best performance, designers usually apply proper power supply decoupling, shielding, and careful PCB layout to reduce noise and ensure accurate signal amplification.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773647616582-871087495.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:53:36','2026-03-16 07:53:36'),
(3164,'AD633JH',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'AD633JH is a precision four-quadrant analog multiplier IC used for mathematical signal processing in analog circuits. It can perform operations such as multiplication, division, modulation, demodulation, squaring, and frequency mixing of analog signals. The device features laser-trimmed accuracy, wide bandwidth, low offset, and good temperature stability, making it suitable for reliable signal processing applications.','Because of its versatility and stable performance, the AD633JH is widely used in communication systems (AM modulation and demodulation), signal conditioning circuits, automatic gain control systems, instrumentation, function generators, and analog computation circuits. It is commonly available in a metal can (TO-99 / TO-100 style) or DIP package, allowing good shielding and easy integration into precision analog designs. For best results, designers typically use proper power supply decoupling, signal filtering, and careful PCB grounding/layout techniques to maintain accuracy and reduce noise effects.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773647682635-291253996.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 07:54:42','2026-03-16 07:54:42'),
(3165,'AD7538',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'AD7538 is an 8-bit digital-to-analog converter (DAC) IC designed to convert digital input data into a proportional analog output signal. It features a current output architecture, good linearity, fast settling time, and low power consumption, making it suitable for precision signal generation and control applications. The device is compatible with standard microprocessor and microcontroller systems, allowing easy interfacing for digital control of analog circuits.','Because of its reliable performance and simple interface, the AD7538 is widely used in data acquisition systems, waveform generation circuits, industrial control equipment, instrumentation, programmable gain control systems, and communication electronics. It is commonly available in a DIP package, enabling convenient PCB mounting in both prototype and production designs. For accurate operation, designers typically use a stable reference source, output amplifier stage, proper decoupling capacitors, and careful PCB layout to ensure clean and precise analog output signals.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773651500431-90519442.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 08:58:20','2026-03-16 08:58:20'),
(3166,'AD7541',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'AD7541 is a precision 12-bit digital-to-analog converter (DAC) IC designed to convert digital input data into a proportional analog output signal. It uses a current-output R-2R ladder architecture, providing good linearity, fast settling time, and low power consumption, which makes it suitable for high-accuracy signal generation and control applications. The device can be easily interfaced with microprocessors and microcontrollers, allowing digital systems to control analog circuits with high resolution.','Because of its stable performance and precision characteristics, the AD7541 is widely used in data acquisition systems, programmable power supplies, waveform generation circuits, instrumentation equipment, industrial process control, and communication electronics. It is typically available in a DIP package, enabling convenient PCB mounting for both laboratory and production designs. For reliable and accurate operation, designers usually provide a stable reference voltage source, output amplifier stage, proper power-supply decoupling, and careful PCB grounding/layout to minimize noise and maintain output accuracy.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773651577878-798365895.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 08:59:37','2026-03-16 08:59:37'),
(3167,'AD7703',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'AD7703 is a precision sigma-delta analog-to-digital converter (ADC) designed for measuring low-level analog signals with high resolution and accuracy. It typically provides 16-bit resolution, low noise performance, and built-in digital filtering, making it suitable for direct interface with sensors such as load cells, pressure sensors, and temperature transducers. The device includes an on-chip programmable gain amplifier (PGA) and reference circuitry, which simplifies signal conditioning and reduces the need for external components.','Because of its high accuracy and stable operation, the AD7703 is widely used in industrial process control, weighing scales, instrumentation systems, data acquisition equipment, and microcontroller-based measurement applications. It is commonly available in DIP and surface-mount packages, allowing flexible integration into both prototype and compact PCB designs. For reliable performance, designers typically use proper reference voltage sources, input filtering networks, decoupling capacitors, and careful PCB layout to minimize noise and achieve precise digital conversion results.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773651780773-241488310.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 09:03:00','2026-03-16 09:03:00'),
(3168,'AD7705',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'AD7705 is a precision 16-bit sigma-delta analog-to-digital converter (ADC) designed for accurate measurement of low-level analog signals. It features an on-chip programmable gain amplifier (PGA), digital filtering, and serial interface, allowing direct connection to sensors and microcontrollers with minimal external components. The device provides high resolution, low noise performance, and excellent accuracy, making it suitable for applications requiring precise data acquisition and signal conditioning.','Because of its reliable performance and simple interfacing capability, the AD7705 is widely used in weighing scales and load cell systems, industrial process control, temperature and pressure measurement, instrumentation equipment, data acquisition systems, and microcontroller-based monitoring circuits. It is commonly available in DIP and surface-mount packages, enabling flexible PCB integration for both prototype and production designs. For best results, designers typically use stable reference voltage sources, proper input filtering, decoupling capacitors, and careful PCB layout to reduce noise and ensure accurate digital conversion.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773652212767-231657942.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 09:10:12','2026-03-16 09:10:12'),
(3169,'AD7751',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'AD7751 is a dedicated single-phase energy metering IC designed for accurate measurement of electrical power consumption in AC systems. It integrates precision analog-to-digital conversion, digital signal processing, and pulse output circuitry, enabling direct calculation of real power and energy usage. The device accepts voltage and current inputs from sensors such as current transformers or shunt resistors and provides a frequency or pulse output proportional to consumed energy, which can be easily interfaced with microcontrollers or counters.','Because of its high accuracy, low drift, and stable performance, the AD7751 is widely used in electronic energy meters, smart power monitoring systems, industrial power measurement equipment, billing meters, and load monitoring applications. It is commonly available in DIP and surface-mount packages, allowing convenient PCB mounting in both prototype and commercial metering designs. For reliable operation, designers typically use proper signal conditioning networks, stable reference components, input filtering, and careful PCB layout to achieve precise energy measurement and long-term stability.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773652306863-505493960.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 09:11:46','2026-03-16 09:11:46'),
(3170,'OP177',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'OP177 is a high-precision operational amplifier (op-amp) designed for applications requiring very low offset voltage, low drift, and excellent long-term stability. It offers low noise performance and high open-loop gain, making it ideal for accurate signal amplification and conditioning in precision analog circuits. The device operates over a wide supply voltage range and maintains stable performance across varying temperatures.','Because of its reliable accuracy and stability, the OP177 is widely used in instrumentation systems, data acquisition equipment, sensor signal conditioning circuits, precision voltage references, active filters, and industrial measurement applications. It is typically available in DIP and metal can packages, allowing flexible integration into both laboratory prototypes and compact PCB designs. For best performance, designers generally use proper power supply decoupling, shielding, and careful PCB grounding/layout techniques to minimize noise and maintain high measurement accuracy.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773653189026-346820422.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 09:26:29','2026-03-16 09:26:29'),
(3171,'TOP223Y',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'TOP223Y is an integrated offline switch-mode power supply (SMPS) controller IC from Power Integrations, designed for efficient AC-DC power conversion in low-power electronic equipment. It combines a high-voltage power MOSFET, PWM controller, oscillator, protection circuitry, and thermal shutdown within a single device, which simplifies SMPS design and reduces the need for external components. The IC typically operates directly from mains input after rectification, making it suitable for compact and cost-effective power supply solutions.','Because of its high efficiency, built-in protection features, and simple circuit implementation, the TOP223Y is widely used in mobile chargers, standby power supplies, TV and set-top box power units, adapters, LED driver circuits, and various consumer electronic SMPS applications. It is commonly available in a TO-220 style package, allowing easy mounting with proper heat dissipation arrangements. For reliable operation, designers usually include snubber networks, feedback circuitry, input filtering, and careful PCB layout to ensure stable and safe power conversion.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773653335003-488477826.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 09:28:55','2026-03-16 09:28:55'),
(3172,'TOP224Y',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'TOP224Y is an integrated offline switch-mode power supply (SMPS) controller IC developed by Power Integrations for compact and efficient AC-DC power conversion. It combines a high-voltage power MOSFET, PWM control circuitry, oscillator, current limiting, thermal shutdown, and protection features in a single device, which significantly reduces external component count and simplifies SMPS design. The IC is designed to operate directly from rectified mains input, making it suitable for low-power power supplies used in consumer and industrial electronics.','Due to its high efficiency, built-in safety protections, and simple implementation, the TOP224Y is widely used in mobile phone chargers, standby power supplies, television and set-top box SMPS units, adapters, LED drivers, battery chargers, and other compact offline power supply applications. It is typically available in a TO-220 style package, allowing easy heat dissipation when mounted on a suitable heat sink or PCB copper area. For reliable operation, designers generally include proper input filtering, snubber networks, feedback control circuits, and careful PCB layout to ensure stable and safe power conversion.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773653429249-608695311.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-16 09:30:29','2026-03-16 09:30:29'),
