(3224,'DPA425PN',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'DPA425PN is an integrated offline switch-mode power supply (SMPS) controller IC from the DPA / TOPSwitch-FX series by Power Integrations. It combines a high-voltage power MOSFET, PWM controller, oscillator, current-limit protection, thermal shutdown, and auto-restart fault protection in a single compact device. This high level of integration helps reduce external component count, simplifies circuit design, and improves overall reliability in AC-DC converter applications. The IC is designed to operate directly from rectified AC mains input, making it suitable for compact offline flyback and forward converter power supplies.','Because of its high efficiency, low standby power consumption, and built-in safety features, the DPA425PN is widely used in TV and monitor SMPS units, battery chargers, power adapters, standby power supplies, LED driver circuits, industrial auxiliary supplies, and various consumer electronic AC-DC power systems. It is typically available in a DIP-8 package, allowing easy PCB mounting and dependable operation in practical designs. For stable and safe performance, designers generally include proper input EMI filtering, snubber or surge protection networks, feedback regulation circuitry, and careful PCB layout techniques to ensure efficient and long-term power conversion.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773735324532-285646947.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 08:15:24','2026-03-17 08:15:24'),
(3225,'93LC66',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'93LC66 is a serial EEPROM (Electrically Erasable Programmable Read-Only Memory) IC used for reliable non-volatile data storage in electronic circuits. It typically provides 4 Kbit (512 × 8 or 256 × 16) memory capacity and uses a Microwire serial interface, allowing easy communication with microcontrollers and digital systems using only a few control pins. The device supports low power consumption, high data retention, and multiple write/erase cycles, making it suitable for long-term storage of configuration or calibration data.','Because of its compact design and dependable performance, the 93LC66 is widely used in embedded systems, industrial control equipment, instrumentation, communication devices, automotive electronics, and consumer products. It is commonly available in DIP and surface-mount packages, enabling flexible PCB integration. For proper operation, designers typically use pull-up resistors, proper clock timing, and stable power supply decoupling to ensure accurate data communication and reliable memory performance.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773736446445-656205603.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 08:34:06','2026-03-17 08:34:06'),
(3226,'24LC256',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'24LC256 is a widely used serial EEPROM (Electrically Erasable Programmable Read-Only Memory) IC designed for non-volatile data storage in embedded electronic systems. It provides 256 Kbit (32K × 8) memory capacity and communicates through a standard I²C (two-wire) interface, which allows easy connection to microcontrollers using only SDA (data) and SCL (clock) lines. The device supports low power operation, high write endurance, and long data retention, making it suitable for storing configuration settings, calibration values, logs, and other important data.','Because of its compact size and reliable performance, the 24LC256 is commonly used in microcontroller-based projects, industrial automation systems, instrumentation, communication devices, automotive electronics, and consumer products. It is available in DIP and surface-mount packages, enabling flexible PCB design. For stable operation, designers typically include pull-up resistors on the I²C lines, proper supply decoupling, and correct device addressing to ensure accurate data transfer and dependable memory performance.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773736621788-55071950.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 08:37:01','2026-03-17 08:37:01'),
(3227,'24LC512',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'24LC512 is a 512-Kbit (64 KB) serial EEPROM memory integrated circuit widely used for non-volatile data storage in electronic and embedded systems. It communicates through the I²C two-wire interface, allowing easy connection with microcontrollers such as Arduino, PIC, AVR, and ARM controllers. The device operates over a wide supply voltage range of 2.5 V to 5.5 V, making it suitable for both low-power and standard logic applications.','The IC includes three hardware address pins (A0–A2) that enable multiple devices to be connected on the same I²C bus, and a write-protect (WP) pin to prevent accidental data modification. The 24LC512 is commonly used in data logging, configuration storage, calibration data saving, consumer electronics, industrial control systems, smart meters, and IoT devices, where secure and permanent storage of small to medium amounts of data is required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773736820425-578589897.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 08:40:20','2026-03-17 08:40:20'),
(3228,'12F675',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC12F675 is a compact 8-bit microcontroller from Microchip, designed for low-cost and space-constrained embedded applications. It belongs to the PIC12 family and comes in a small 8-pin package, making it suitable for simple control circuits and compact electronic projects. The controller features 1K words of Flash program memory, 64 bytes of EEPROM data memory, and 64 bytes of RAM, allowing it to store program instructions as well as non-volatile user data.','It operates with a supply voltage typically between 2.0 V and 5.5 V and includes an internal 4 MHz oscillator, which eliminates the need for an external crystal in many designs. The PIC12F675 provides six general-purpose I/O pins, an integrated 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels, timers, comparator modules, and power-saving features such as sleep mode and watchdog timer. Due to its simplicity, low power consumption, and built-in peripherals, it is commonly used in sensor interfacing, small automation systems, battery-powered devices, LED control circuits, security products, and basic embedded control applications where reliable and efficient microcontroller operation is required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773736914876-635780415.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 08:41:54','2026-03-17 08:41:54'),
(3229,'12F508',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'IC12F508 is a small and cost-effective 8-bit microcontroller from Microchip, designed for simple embedded control applications where minimal size and low power consumption are important. It is available in an 8-pin package and provides 512 words of program memory, 25 bytes of RAM, and a limited number of general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with external components. The device operates over a wide supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator (typically 4 MHz), which removes the need for an external clock in most designs.','The PIC12F508 features basic peripherals such as Timer0, watchdog timer, internal reset circuitry, and power-saving sleep mode, enabling reliable operation in low-power electronic systems. Unlike some higher models, it does not include built-in ADC or EEPROM data memory, making it suitable mainly for simple switching, timing, LED control, small automation circuits, alarms, toys, and basic consumer electronic products where straightforward programmable control is required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773737023893-841721425.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 08:43:43','2026-03-17 08:43:43'),
(3230,'12F509',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC12F509 is a compact and low-cost 8-bit microcontroller from Microchip, designed for simple embedded control applications where small size and low power consumption are essential. It comes in an 8-pin package and provides 1K words of program memory and about 41 bytes of RAM, allowing it to handle basic control logic and timing tasks. The device operates within a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes a built-in internal RC oscillator (typically 4 MHz), which eliminates the need for an external crystal in many circuits.','The PIC12F509 offers general-purpose I/O pins, Timer0, a watchdog timer, power-on reset, and sleep mode for energy-efficient operation in battery-powered systems. It does not include advanced peripherals such as ADC or hardware serial communication, making it suitable for simple switching circuits, LED flashers, alarms, toys, remote controls, small automation devices, and basic consumer electronic products where reliable and economical programmable control is required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773737095089-750720604.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 08:44:55','2026-03-17 08:44:55'),
(3231,'12F510',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC12F510 is a small and economical 8-bit microcontroller from Microchip, designed for simple embedded control applications that require low power consumption and minimal external components. It is available in an 8-pin package and features about 1K words of program memory and 64 bytes of RAM, providing sufficient space for basic control programs and temporary data storage. The microcontroller operates over a wide supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes a built-in internal oscillator (typically around 4 MHz), eliminating the need for an external clock source in most designs','It provides several general-purpose input/output pins, along with essential peripherals such as Timer0, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for efficient and reliable operation. The PIC12F510 does not include advanced modules like ADC or hardware serial communication, so it is mainly used in simple automation circuits, LED control units, small household electronics, security alarms, timers, toys, and battery-operated devices, where low cost, compact size, and dependable programmable control are important.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773737172300-212895346.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 08:46:12','2026-03-17 08:46:12'),
(3232,'12F615',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC12F615 is a compact 8-bit microcontroller from Microchip, designed for low-cost and space-limited embedded control applications. It is available in an 8-pin package and provides around 1K words of Flash program memory, 64 bytes of EEPROM data memory, and 64 bytes of RAM, enabling both program storage and non-volatile data retention. The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes a built-in internal oscillator (up to 8 MHz), which reduces the need for external timing components.','The PIC12F615 offers up to six general-purpose I/O pins, an integrated 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) for reading analog signals, PWM capability for motor or LED brightness control, Timer0, comparator functions, watchdog timer, brown-out reset, and low-power sleep mode for energy-efficient operation. Because of its small size, built-in peripherals, and reliable performance, it is commonly used in sensor interfacing circuits, LED dimmers, small motor control systems, battery-powered devices, home appliances, security systems, and basic industrial or consumer electronic applications where simple programmable control and analog signal handling are required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773737258072-81747398.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 08:47:38','2026-03-17 08:47:38'),
(3233,'12F629',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC12F629 is a compact and low-power 8-bit microcontroller from Microchip, widely used in small embedded control and automation applications. It is available in an 8-pin package and provides about 1K words of Flash program memory, 64 bytes of EEPROM data memory, and 64 bytes of RAM, allowing both program storage and non-volatile data retention. The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator (typically 4 MHz), which reduces the need for external clock components.','The PIC12F629 offers up to six general-purpose I/O pins, an internal comparator module, Timer0, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for efficient battery-operated designs. Although it does not include a built-in ADC module, it is suitable for digital control tasks such as LED control circuits, alarms, timers, small automation systems, remote control devices, security products, and simple consumer electronic equipment, where compact size, reliability, and economical programmable control are important.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773737369098-930364893.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 08:49:29','2026-03-17 08:49:29'),
(3234,'12F683',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC12F683 is a small and efficient 8-bit microcontroller from Microchip, designed for compact embedded control applications that require low power consumption and built-in analog features. It is available in an 8-pin package and provides about 2K words of Flash program memory, 128 bytes of EEPROM data memory, and 128 bytes of RAM, offering adequate space for program execution and non-volatile data storage. The device operates over a wide supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator that can run up to 8 MHz, reducing the need for external timing components.','The PIC12F683 features up to six general-purpose I/O pins, a 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple channels for reading analog signals, PWM (CCP module) for motor speed or LED brightness control, Timer0 and Timer1, comparator module, watchdog timer, brown-out reset, and sleep mode for power-saving operation. Because of its compact size and integrated peripherals, it is commonly used in sensor interfacing, LED dimmers, battery-powered devices, small motor control systems, security circuits, home appliances, and general consumer or industrial electronic control applications where reliable and economical programmable control is required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773737468087-304490815.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 08:51:08','2026-03-17 08:51:08'),
(3235,'16C54',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16C54 is an early-generation 8-bit microcontroller from Microchip, designed for simple embedded control applications requiring low cost and reliable operation. It belongs to the PIC16C5X family and is typically available in 18-pin and 28-pin packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output ports for interfacing with external devices. The controller uses OTP (One-Time Programmable) ROM program memory of about 512 words, along with a small amount of internal RAM for temporary data storage.','It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 3.0 V to 5.5 V and can work with either an external crystal/RC oscillator or clock source, depending on the configuration. The PIC16C54 includes basic built-in features such as Timer0, watchdog timer, power-on reset, and sleep mode for low-power operation. Although it does not provide advanced peripherals like ADC, EEPROM, or hardware serial communication, it is suitable for simple control tasks such as LED sequencing, alarm circuits, small automation systems, toys, timers, and basic consumer electronic products, where straightforward programmable logic and dependable performance are required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773737542780-470702383.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 08:52:22','2026-03-17 08:52:22'),
(3236,'16C716',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16C716 is an 8-bit microcontroller from Microchip belonging to the PIC16C7X family, designed for embedded control applications that require both digital and analog interfacing. It is typically available in an 18-pin DIP or SOIC package and provides about 2K words of OTP (One-Time Programmable) program memory, along with RAM for data processing. The device operates with a supply voltage of approximately 4.0 V to 5.5 V and supports different clock sources such as external crystal, RC oscillator, or clock input, depending on system requirements.','One of the key features of the PIC16C716 is its built-in 8-channel 8-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC), which allows the microcontroller to directly read analog sensor signals. It also includes Timer0, watchdog timer, power-on reset, sleep mode for low-power operation, and multiple general-purpose I/O pins for controlling external circuits. Although it does not provide advanced communication peripherals like hardware UART or I²C modules, it is suitable for sensor monitoring systems, industrial control units, measurement instruments, small automation devices, motor control circuits, and consumer electronic products, where basic analog signal processing and dependable programmable control are required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773737644374-614552659.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 08:54:04','2026-03-17 08:54:04'),
(3237,'16F72',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F72 is an 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for reliable embedded control and automation applications that require both digital and analog interfacing. It belongs to the PIC16F7X family and is commonly available in a 28-pin DIP or SOIC package, providing multiple input/output ports for connecting external components. The controller features about 2K words of Flash program memory, 128 bytes of RAM, and non-volatile data storage capability, allowing easy reprogramming during development and field updates.','The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and supports various clock options such as external crystal, RC oscillator, or clock input. A key feature of the PIC16F72 is its built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels, enabling direct interfacing with analog sensors and measurement circuits. It also includes Timer0, Timer1 and Timer2, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, PWM capability (CCP module), and low-power sleep mode for efficient system operation.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773737720736-7858366.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 08:55:20','2026-03-17 08:55:20'),
(3238,'16F73',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F73 is a versatile 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require multiple peripherals and analog signal processing capability. It belongs to the PIC16F7X family and is typically available in a 28-pin DIP or SOIC package, offering several general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with external circuits. The microcontroller provides about 4K words of Flash program memory, 192 bytes of RAM, and 128 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing both program storage and non-volatile data retention.','It operates within a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and supports different clock options such as external crystal, RC oscillator, or external clock input. The PIC16F73 includes a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels, making it suitable for reading analog sensor signals. It also features Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, PWM capability through the CCP module, SPI/I²C (MSSP) serial communication interface, watchdog timer, brown-out reset, power-on reset, and low-power sleep mode for energy-efficient operation.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773737802129-568798089.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 08:56:42','2026-03-17 08:56:42'),
(3239,'16F74',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F74 is a powerful and widely used 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require multiple input/output lines and integrated analog features. It belongs to the PIC16F7X family and is commonly available in a 40-pin DIP or 44-pin SMD package, providing several digital I/O ports for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, and other external devices. The microcontroller offers about 4K words of Flash program memory, 192 bytes of RAM, and 128 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing easy program updates and reliable storage of user data or configuration parameters.','The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and supports different clock sources such as external crystal, RC oscillator, or external clock input. A major feature of the PIC16F74 is its built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple channels for accurate reading of analog signals. It also includes Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, PWM output through the CCP module for motor speed or LED brightness control, and a hardware SPI/I²C serial communication interface (MSSP) for connecting memory devices, sensors, or other controllers. Additional features such as watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode improve system reliability and energy efficiency.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773737873355-110653546.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 08:57:53','2026-03-17 08:57:53'),
(3240,'16F76',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F76 is an advanced 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require multiple input/output ports and analog signal processing capability. It belongs to the PIC16F7X family and is typically available in a 28-pin DIP or SOIC package, providing several general-purpose I/O pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, and other external circuits. The microcontroller features about 8K words of Flash program memory, 368 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing efficient program execution and reliable non-volatile storage of configuration or user data.','The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and supports different clock options such as external crystal, RC oscillator, or external clock input. It includes a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for measuring analog signals, along with Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and PWM output through the CCP module for motor speed or LED brightness control. The PIC16F76 also provides a hardware SPI/I²C serial communication interface (MSSP) for easy connection to external memory devices, sensors, or other controllers. Additional features such as watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode enhance system reliability and energy efficiency.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773737950695-123460355.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 08:59:10','2026-03-17 08:59:10'),
(3241,'16F88',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F88 is a compact and versatile 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, widely used in embedded control applications that require both digital and analog interfacing. It is commonly available in an 18-pin DIP or SOIC package and provides about 4K words of Flash program memory, 368 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable storage of program code as well as non-volatile user data. The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator that can run up to 8 MHz, reducing the need for external clock components in many designs.','The PIC16F88 features up to 16 general-purpose I/O pins, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for sensor interfacing, PWM output through the CCP module for motor speed or LED brightness control, and essential timing resources such as Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2. It also provides USART serial communication, comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for energy-efficient operation in battery-powered systems.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773738090962-765193872.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 09:01:30','2026-03-17 09:01:30'),
(3242,'16F505',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F505 is a small and low-cost 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for simple embedded control and automation applications where compact size and low power consumption are important. It is typically available in 14-pin and 20-pin packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with switches, LEDs, relays, and other external components. The microcontroller features about 1K words of Flash program memory and 72 bytes of RAM, allowing basic program execution and temporary data storage.','The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator (typically around 4 MHz), which helps reduce the need for external clock circuitry. It provides essential built-in functions such as Timer0, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for reliable and energy-efficient operation. The PIC16F505 does not include advanced peripherals like ADC or hardware serial communication modules, making it most suitable for simple control systems such as LED flashing circuits, small automation devices, alarm systems, toys, timers, and basic consumer electronic products, where economical programmable control and dependable performance are required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773738167803-82856298.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 09:02:47','2026-03-17 09:02:47'),
(3243,'16F506',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F506 is a compact and economical 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, intended for simple embedded control applications where low power consumption and small size are important. It is commonly available in 14-pin and 20-pin packages, providing several general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with switches, LEDs, relays, and other external components. The device offers about 1K words of Flash program memory and around 67 bytes of RAM, allowing basic program execution and temporary data storage for control tasks.','The microcontroller operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal RC oscillator (typically around 4 MHz), which reduces the need for external timing components in many designs. It incorporates essential built-in features such as Timer0, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode to improve reliability and energy efficiency, especially in battery-operated devices. Although it does not include advanced peripherals such as ADC modules or hardware communication interfaces, the PIC16F506 is widely used in simple automation systems, LED control circuits, timers, alarm units, small household electronics, toys, and other cost-sensitive consumer electronic applications where straightforward programmable control is required',NULL,NULL,'products/1773738247794-248539764.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 09:04:07','2026-03-17 09:04:07'),
(3244,'16F616',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F616 is a compact and low-power 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require reliable digital operation along with some integrated analog and timing features. It is commonly available in 14-pin and 20-pin packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with switches, LEDs, relays, sensors, and other external circuits. The microcontroller includes about 2K words of Flash program memory, 128 bytes of RAM, and 128 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing easy program updates and non-volatile storage of configuration or user data.','The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and features an internal oscillator that can run up to around 8 MHz, reducing the need for external clock components in many designs. It offers built-in peripherals such as Timer0, Timer1, Timer2, PWM capability (ECCP module) for motor speed or LED brightness control, comparator module, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for energy-efficient operation. Because of its small size, integrated features, and dependable performance, the PIC16F616 is widely used in LED lighting control, battery-powered devices, small motor control circuits, security systems, sensor-based automation, home appliances, and general consumer electronic products, where compact programmable control is required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773738322429-913101964.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 09:05:22','2026-03-17 09:05:22'),
(3245,'16F628',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F628 is a popular and versatile 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, widely used in embedded systems and automation projects due to its low cost, compact size, and built-in communication features. It is typically available in an 18-pin DIP or SOIC package and provides about 2K words of Flash program memory, 224 bytes of RAM, and 128 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable program storage and non-volatile data retention. The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator (up to around 4 MHz), which reduces the need for external clock components in many designs.','The PIC16F628 offers up to 16 general-purpose I/O pins, built-in USART serial communication for interfacing with computers or other controllers, Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, PWM capability through the CCP module, and comparator modules for simple analog signal detection. It also includes essential reliability features such as watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for energy-efficient operation. Because of its flexible peripherals and dependable performance, the PIC16F628 is commonly used in serial communication projects, display control systems, alarm and security circuits, motor control units, automation devices, measurement instruments, and various consumer or industrial electronic applications, where compact programmable control and communication capability are required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773738399401-576992742.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 09:06:39','2026-03-17 09:06:39'),
(3246,'PIC 16F676',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F676 is a compact and low-power 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require both digital processing and analog signal measurement. It is commonly available in a 14-pin DIP or SOIC package, making it suitable for space-constrained circuit designs. The microcontroller provides about 1K words of Flash program memory, 64 bytes of RAM, and 128 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable storage of program code as well as non-volatile user data. It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator (typically up to 4 MHz), which helps reduce the need for external clock components.','The PIC16F676 features up to 12 general-purpose I/O pins, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for sensor interfacing, Timer0 and Timer1, comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for efficient operation in battery-powered systems. Because of its small size, integrated analog capability, and dependable performance, it is widely used in sensor monitoring circuits, temperature or voltage measurement systems, LED control units, small automation devices, security products, home appliances, and other consumer or industrial electronic applications where simple programmable control and analog signal handling are required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773738468284-36351514.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 09:07:48','2026-04-06 15:33:58'),
(3247,'16F677',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F677 is a compact and low-power 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require multiple input/output lines and analog signal processing capability. It is commonly available in a 20-pin DIP or SOIC package, making it suitable for small electronic circuit designs. The microcontroller provides about 2K words of Flash program memory, 128 bytes of RAM, and 128 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable storage of program instructions and non-volatile user data. It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator (typically up to 4 MHz), which helps reduce the need for external timing components.','The PIC16F677 features multiple general-purpose I/O pins, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with several input channels for direct sensor interfacing, Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, PWM capability through the CCP module for motor speed or LED brightness control, comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for energy-efficient operation. Because of its integrated analog functions and compact size, it is widely used in sensor monitoring systems, LED lighting control circuits, small motor control units, automation devices, battery-powered equipment, home appliances, and general consumer or industrial electronic applications, where simple programmable control and analog measurement are required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773739551439-772678669.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 09:25:51','2026-03-17 09:25:51'),
(3248,'16F684',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F684 is a compact and feature-rich 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require reliable digital processing along with analog and PWM capabilities. It is typically available in 14-pin DIP and SOIC packages, making it suitable for space-limited electronic designs. The microcontroller provides about 2K words of Flash program memory, 128 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing easy reprogramming and secure non-volatile storage of user or configuration data.','The device operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator that can run up to around 8 MHz, reducing the need for external timing components in many circuits. The PIC16F684 features multiple general-purpose I/O pins, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with several channels for sensor interfacing, Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and PWM output through the CCP module for applications such as motor speed control or LED dimming. It also includes comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for efficient operation in battery-powered systems.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773739637799-602045758.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 09:27:17','2026-03-17 09:27:17'),
(3249,'16F688',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F688 is a compact and versatile 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require both digital processing and analog interfacing features. It is commonly available in 14-pin DIP and SOIC packages, making it suitable for space-constrained electronic designs. The microcontroller provides about 4K words of Flash program memory, 256 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable storage of program code as well as non-volatile user or configuration data. It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator that can run up to around 8 MHz, reducing the need for external clock components.','The PIC16F688 features several general-purpose I/O pins, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for sensor interfacing, Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and PWM capability through the CCP module for motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment. It also includes comparator modules, USART serial communication, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for efficient operation in battery-powered devices. Because of its small size, integrated peripherals, and dependable performance, it is widely used in sensor monitoring systems, LED lighting control, small motor drives, automation equipment, home appliances, security devices, and general consumer or industrial electronic applications, where flexible programmable control and mixed-signal capability are required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773739715751-430329825.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 09:28:35','2026-03-17 09:28:35'),
(3250,'16F689',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F689 is a compact and low-power 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require multiple input/output pins and integrated analog features. It is commonly available in a 20-pin DIP or SOIC package, making it suitable for space-constrained electronic circuit designs. The microcontroller provides about 4K words of Flash program memory, 256 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable program execution and secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data. It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator that can run up to around 8 MHz, reducing the need for external clock components in many applications.','The PIC16F689 features several general-purpose I/O pins, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for sensor interfacing, Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and PWM capability through the CCP module for applications such as motor speed control or LED dimming. It also includes comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode, ensuring reliable and energy-efficient system operation. Because of its compact size, flexible peripherals, and dependable performance, the PIC16F689 is widely used in sensor monitoring systems, LED lighting controllers, small automation equipment, home appliances, battery-powered devices, security products, and various consumer or industrial electronic applications, where economical programmable control and mixed-signal capability are required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773739804149-286662930.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 09:30:04','2026-03-17 09:30:04'),
(3251,'16F690',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F690 is a versatile and low-power 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, widely used in embedded control and automation applications that require multiple input/output lines and analog signal processing capability. It is typically available in a 20-pin DIP or SOIC package, making it suitable for compact electronic designs. The microcontroller provides about 4K words of Flash program memory, 256 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable program storage along with non-volatile user data retention. It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator that can run up to around 8 MHz, reducing the need for external timing components in many circuits.','The PIC16F690 features multiple general-purpose I/O pins, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with several input channels for sensor interfacing, Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and PWM output through the CCP module for applications such as motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment. It also provides comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode to improve system reliability and energy efficiency. Because of its compact size, flexible peripheral set, and dependable performance, the PIC16F690 is widely used in sensor monitoring systems, LED lighting control circuits, small motor drives, automation devices, home appliances, battery-powered equipment, security products, and general consumer or industrial electronic applications, where economical programmable control and mixed-signal capability are required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773739989741-252175310.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 09:33:09','2026-03-17 09:33:09'),
(3252,'16F870',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F870 is a reliable and widely used 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control and automation applications that require multiple digital I/O lines and analog signal processing capability. It belongs to the PIC16F87X family and is commonly available in a 28-pin DIP or SOIC package, providing several input/output ports for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, and other external devices. The microcontroller offers about 2K words of Flash program memory, 128 bytes of RAM, and 64 bytes of EEPROM data memory, enabling easy program updates and secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data. It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and supports various clock options such as external crystal, RC oscillator, or external clock input.','The PIC16F870 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for accurate measurement of analog signals, along with Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and PWM capability through the CCP module for motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment. It also includes SPI/I²C serial communication (MSSP module) for connecting external memory devices or sensors, as well as watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for efficient operation in battery-powered systems.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773740106233-886459533.png',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 09:35:06','2026-03-17 09:35:06'),
(3253,'16F873',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F870 is a reliable and widely used 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control and automation applications that require multiple digital I/O lines and analog signal processing capability. It belongs to the PIC16F87X family and is commonly available in a 28-pin DIP or SOIC package, providing several input/output ports for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, and other external devices. The microcontroller offers about 2K words of Flash program memory, 128 bytes of RAM, and 64 bytes of EEPROM data memory, enabling easy program updates and secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data.','The PIC16F870 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for accurate measurement of analog signals, along with Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and PWM capability through the CCP module for motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment. It also includes SPI/I²C serial communication (MSSP module) for connecting external memory devices or sensors, as well as watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for efficient operation in battery-powered systems.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773740558456-824659619.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-17 09:42:38','2026-03-17 09:42:38'),
(3254,'16F876',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'PIC16F876 is a powerful and widely used 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control and automation applications that require multiple digital input/output lines and advanced analog processing capability. It belongs to the PIC16F87X family and is commonly available in a 28-pin DIP or SOIC package, making it suitable for compact yet feature-rich circuit designs. The microcontroller provides about 8K words of Flash program memory, 368 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable program execution and secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data','The PIC16F876 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for accurate measurement of analog signals from sensors and control circuits. It also includes Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, PWM output through the CCP module for applications such as motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment, and a hardware SPI/I²C serial communication interface (MSSP) for easy connection to memory devices, displays, and other controllers',NULL,NULL,'products/1773804641123-282799322.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 03:30:41','2026-03-18 03:30:41'),
(3255,'16F877A',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F877A is a highly popular and versatile 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, widely used in embedded systems, automation projects, and educational applications due to its rich peripheral set and reliable performance. It belongs to the PIC16F87X family and is commonly available in a 40-pin DIP or 44-pin SMD package, providing a large number of general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, motors, and communication devices. The microcontroller offers about 8K words of Flash program memory, 368 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing easy program development along with secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data. It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 4.0 V to 5.5 V and supports different clock options such as external crystal, RC oscillator, or external clock input.','The PIC16F877A includes a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple channels for accurate analog signal measurement, along with Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and two CCP modules that support PWM generation for motor control and LED dimming applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773804769811-157274055.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 03:32:49','2026-03-18 03:32:49'),
(3256,'16F882',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F882 is a feature-rich 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require reliable digital processing together with analog measurement and communication capability. It is commonly available in 28-pin DIP and SMD packages, offering multiple general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, and other external circuits. The microcontroller provides about 4K words of Flash program memory, 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, and 368 bytes of RAM, allowing easy reprogramming and secure storage of user or configuration data','The PIC16F882 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for direct sensor interfacing, along with Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and PWM capability through the CCP module for applications such as motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment. It also includes hardware serial communication interfaces such as USART and SPI/I²C (MSSP module) for easy connectivity with computers, memory devices, and other controllers. Additional functions like comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode improve system reliability and energy efficiency.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773804891145-832618452.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 03:34:51','2026-03-18 03:34:51'),
(3257,'16F883',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F883 is a versatile and low-power 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require digital processing along with analog signal measurement and communication capability. It is commonly available in 28-pin DIP or SMD packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, and other external devices. The microcontroller offers about 4K words of Flash program memory, 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, and 368 bytes of RAM, allowing reliable program execution and secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data.','The PIC16F883 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with several input channels for accurate sensor interfacing, along with Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, and PWM capability through the CCP module for motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment. It also includes hardware serial communication interfaces such as USART and SPI/I²C (MSSP module) for easy connection to computers, memory devices, and other controllers. Additional functions such as comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode enhance system reliability and energy efficiency',NULL,NULL,'products/1773805246744-731440437.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 03:40:46','2026-03-18 03:40:46'),
(3258,'16F886',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F886 is a versatile and low-power 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require multiple input/output pins, analog signal processing, and communication capability. It is commonly available in 28-pin DIP and SMD packages, making it suitable for compact yet feature-rich electronic circuit designs. The microcontroller provides about 8K words of Flash program memory, 368 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable program execution along with secure non-volatile storage of user or configuration data.','The PIC16F886 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for direct interfacing with sensors and measurement circuits. It also includes Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, PWM output through the CCP module for motor speed control or LED dimming, and hardware serial communication interfaces such as USART and SPI/I²C (MSSP module) for easy connectivity with computers, memory devices, and other controllers. Additional integrated functions such as comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode enhance system reliability and energy efficiency',NULL,NULL,'products/1773805357493-52762410.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 03:42:37','2026-03-18 03:42:37'),
(3259,'16F887',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F887 is a widely used and versatile 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require a large number of input/output pins along with analog and communication features. It belongs to the PIC16F88X family and is commonly available in 40-pin DIP and 44-pin SMD packages, making it suitable for both development boards and industrial circuit designs. The microcontroller provides about 8K words of Flash program memory, 368 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable program execution and non-volatile storage of user settings or configuration data. It operates over a wide supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator that can run up to around 8 MHz, reducing the need for external clock components in many applications.','The PIC16F887 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple channels for accurate measurement of analog signals from sensors. It also includes Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, PWM output through CCP modules for motor control or LED brightness adjustment, and hardware serial communication interfaces such as USART and SPI/I²C (MSSP module) for easy connectivity with computers, displays, memory devices, and other controllers. Additional integrated features like comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode enhance reliability and energy efficiency.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773805694548-234938579.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 03:48:14','2026-03-18 03:48:14'),
(3260,'16F913',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F913 is a compact and feature-rich 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require analog signal processing and direct LCD display interfacing. It is commonly available in 28-pin DIP and SMD packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output pins for connecting sensors, switches, relays, and display modules. The microcontroller offers about 4K words of Flash program memory, 128 bytes of EEPROM data memory, and 256 bytes of RAM, allowing reliable program storage along with non-volatile data retention. It operates over a wide supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal oscillator (typically up to 8 MHz), reducing the need for external clock components in many designs.','A key feature of the PIC16F913 is its integrated LCD driver module, which allows direct control of segmented LCD displays without additional external driver ICs. It also includes a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for sensor interfacing, along with Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for energy-efficient operation. Because of its LCD driving capability, compact size, and dependable performance, the PIC16F913 is widely used in digital meters, home appliance control panels, battery-powered instruments, small automation devices, medical equipment, and other consumer or industrial electronic applications where direct display control and mixed-signal processing are required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773805783795-767137274.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 03:49:43','2026-03-18 03:49:43'),
(3261,'16F917',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F917 is a feature-rich 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require analog signal processing and direct control of LCD displays. It belongs to the PIC16F91X family and is commonly available in 40-pin DIP and SMD packages, providing a large number of general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, switches, relays, and communication circuits. The microcontroller includes about 8K words of Flash program memory, 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, and 368 bytes of RAM, enabling reliable program execution along with secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data.','A major feature of the PIC16F917 is its built-in LCD driver module, which allows direct interfacing with segmented LCD panels without additional external driver ICs, making it ideal for display-oriented control systems. The device also includes a 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for sensor measurement, along with Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, PWM capability through the CCP module, comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for energy-efficient operation',NULL,NULL,'products/1773805876888-73467984.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 03:51:16','2026-03-18 03:51:16'),
(3262,'16F1501',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F1501 is a modern and low-power 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for compact embedded control applications that require flexible peripherals and efficient operation. It is typically available in 8-pin and 14-pin packages, making it suitable for space-constrained electronic designs. The microcontroller provides about 3.5 KB of Flash program memory, 256 bytes of RAM, and 128 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable program storage along with non-volatile data retention. It operates over a wide supply voltage range of approximately 1.8 V to 5.5 V, which makes it suitable for both battery-powered and standard logic systems.','The PIC16F1501 includes an internal oscillator (up to 16 MHz) that reduces the need for external clock components. It features several general-purpose I/O pins, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) for sensor interfacing, PWM capability through CCP/PWM modules for applications such as motor speed control or LED dimming, and Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2 for timing and counting functions. Additional integrated features such as comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out reset, configurable logic cells (CLC), and low-power sleep mode enhance system flexibility, reliability, and energy efficiency',NULL,NULL,'products/1773806027237-853868604.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 03:53:47','2026-03-18 03:53:47'),
(3263,'16F1508',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC16F1508 is a modern and feature-rich 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require flexible peripherals, analog capability, and low-power operation. It is commonly available in 20-pin DIP and SMD packages, making it suitable for compact electronic circuit designs. The microcontroller provides about 7 KB of Flash program memory, 512 bytes of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing reliable program execution along with secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data. It operates over a wide supply voltage range of approximately 1.8 V to 5.5 V and includes an internal high-speed oscillator (up to 16 MHz), reducing the need for external clock components in many applications.','The PIC16F1508 features multiple general-purpose I/O pins, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with several input channels for sensor interfacing, and enhanced PWM modules suitable for LED brightness control or small motor driving applications. It also includes Timer0, Timer1, and Timer2, comparator modules, watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode for efficient operation in battery-powered systems. In addition, modern internal features such as Configurable Logic Cells (CLC) and peripheral pin select improve design flexibility',NULL,NULL,'products/1773806140755-366137104.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 03:55:40','2026-03-18 03:55:40'),
(3264,'18F252',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC18F252 is a high-performance 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require faster processing speed, advanced communication features, and reliable analog interfacing. It belongs to the PIC18F family and is commonly available in 28-pin DIP and SMD packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output pins for connecting sensors, displays, relays, and communication devices. The microcontroller offers about 32 KB of Flash program memory, 1.5 KB of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing efficient program execution and secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data. It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and supports various clock options such as external crystal, RC oscillator, or internal clock source.','The PIC18F252 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for accurate analog signal measurement, along with several timers and PWM capability through CCP modules for motor control or LED dimming applications. It also provides hardware communication interfaces including USART, SPI, and I²C, enabling easy connectivity with computers, memory devices, displays, and other controllers. Additional integrated functions such as watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, and low-power sleep mode enhance system reliability and energy efficiency.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773806260270-387056230.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 03:57:40','2026-03-18 03:57:40'),
(3265,'18F452',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC18F452 is a powerful and widely used 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for advanced embedded control and automation applications that require higher program memory, multiple I/O lines, and reliable communication features. It belongs to the PIC18F family and is commonly available in 40-pin DIP and 44-pin SMD packages, providing a large number of general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, motors, and communication devices. The microcontroller includes about 32 KB of Flash program memory, 1.5 KB of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing efficient program execution along with secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data.','The PIC18F452 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for accurate measurement of analog signals. It also includes several timers, PWM capability through CCP modules for motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment, and hardware communication interfaces such as USART, SPI, and I²C, enabling easy connectivity with computers, sensors, memory devices, and other controllers',NULL,NULL,'products/1773806375863-84916640.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 03:59:35','2026-03-18 03:59:35'),
(3266,'18F458',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC18F458 is a high-performance 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require fast processing, advanced communication features, and reliable analog interfacing. It belongs to the PIC18F family and is commonly available in 40-pin DIP and 44-pin SMD packages, providing a large number of general-purpose input/output pins for connecting sensors, displays, relays, motors, and communication devices. The microcontroller offers about 32 KB of Flash program memory, 1.5 KB of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing efficient program execution along with secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data.','A key feature of the PIC18F458 is its integrated CAN (Controller Area Network) communication module, which makes it especially suitable for automotive and industrial networking applications. It also includes a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for accurate measurement of analog signals, along with multiple timers and PWM capability through CCP modules for motor speed control or power regulation tasks. Standard communication interfaces such as USART, SPI, and I²C are also provided for easy connectivity with computers, memory devices, sensors, and display modules',NULL,NULL,'products/1773806525565-577760743.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 04:02:05','2026-03-18 04:02:05'),
(3267,'18F2520',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC18F2520 is a high-performance and feature-rich 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require fast processing speed, advanced peripherals, and reliable communication capability. It belongs to the PIC18F family and is commonly available in 28-pin DIP and SMD packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, motors, and other external devices. The microcontroller offers about 32 KB of Flash program memory, 1.5 KB of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing efficient program execution along with secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data','The PIC18F2520 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for accurate analog signal measurement. It also includes multiple timers, PWM capability through CCP/ECCP modules for applications such as motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment, and hardware communication interfaces including USART, SPI, and I²C, enabling easy connectivity with computers, sensors, memory devices, and display modules. Additional integrated features such as watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, fail-safe clock monitor, and low-power sleep mode improve system reliability and energy efficiency.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773806615441-393635943.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 04:03:35','2026-03-18 04:03:35'),
(3268,'18F2550',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC18F2550 is a powerful and widely used 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control and communication applications that require USB connectivity and reliable analog interfacing. It belongs to the PIC18F family and is commonly available in 28-pin DIP and SMD packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, motors, and communication devices','The microcontroller includes about 32 KB of Flash program memory, 2 KB of RAM, and 256 bytes of EEPROM data memory, allowing efficient program execution along with secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data. It operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 2.0 V to 5.5 V and supports various clock options such as external crystal, PLL-based high-speed clock, or internal oscillator, enabling flexible system design.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773806740663-725726642.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 04:05:40','2026-03-18 04:05:40'),
(3269,'18F4520',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC18F4520 is a high-performance and feature-rich 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, widely used in advanced embedded control and automation applications that require fast processing, large program memory, and multiple communication interfaces. It belongs to the PIC18F family and is commonly available in 40-pin DIP and 44-pin SMD packages, providing a large number of general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, motors, and communication devices.','The PIC18F4520 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for accurate measurement of analog signals. It also includes multiple timer modules, enhanced PWM capability through CCP/ECCP modules for motor speed control or LED brightness adjustment, and hardware communication interfaces such as USART, SPI, and I²C, enabling easy connectivity with computers, sensors, displays, and external memory devices. Additional integrated features such as watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, fail-safe clock monitor, and low-power sleep mode enhance system reliability and energy efficiency.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773807393812-613577739.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 04:16:33','2026-03-18 04:16:33'),
(3270,'18F4550',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC18F4550 is a powerful and widely used 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require high processing speed, USB communication capability, and flexible peripheral integration. It belongs to the PIC18F family and is commonly available in 40-pin DIP and 44-pin SMD packages, providing a large number of general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, motors, and communication devices','A major feature of the PIC18F4550 is its integrated Full-Speed USB 2.0 interface, enabling direct connection to computers for data communication, firmware updates, and USB device control without requiring additional USB controller ICs. The device also includes a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for sensor measurement, along with several timers and enhanced PWM capability through CCP/ECCP modules for motor control or LED dimming applications. It provides hardware communication interfaces such as USART, SPI, and I²C for easy connectivity with memory devices, displays, sensors, and other controllers',NULL,NULL,'products/1773807509773-830239971.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 04:18:29','2026-03-18 04:18:29'),
(3271,'18F4620',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PIC18F4620 is a high-performance 8-bit Flash microcontroller from Microchip, designed for advanced embedded control and automation applications that require large program memory, multiple communication interfaces, and reliable analog processing capability. It belongs to the PIC18F family and is commonly available in 40-pin DIP and 44-pin SMD packages, providing a large number of general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, motors, and communication modules. The microcontroller offers about 64 KB of Flash program memory, 3.9 KB of RAM, and 1 KB of EEPROM data memory, allowing efficient execution of complex programs along with secure non-volatile storage of configuration or user data','The PIC18F4620 features a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels for accurate sensor signal measurement. It also includes multiple timer modules, enhanced PWM capability through CCP/ECCP modules for motor control or LED brightness adjustment, and hardware serial communication interfaces such as USART and SPI/I²C (MSSP module) for easy connectivity with computers, memory devices, displays, and other controllers. Additional integrated functions such as watchdog timer, power-on reset, brown-out protection, fail-safe clock monitoring, and low-power sleep mode improve system reliability and energy efficiency.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773807614533-710830488.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 04:20:14','2026-03-18 04:20:14'),
(3272,'30F2010',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'dsPIC30F2010 is a high-performance 16-bit Digital Signal Controller (DSC) from Microchip, designed for embedded applications that require fast processing speed, precise motor control capability, and advanced signal processing features. It combines the functionality of a microcontroller with digital signal processing performance, making it suitable for real-time control systems. The device is commonly available in 28-pin DIP and SMD packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, power circuits, and communication modules. It offers about 12 KB of Flash program memory and 1 KB of RAM, enabling efficient execution of control algorithms and signal-processing tasks.','The dsPIC30F2010 operates over a supply voltage range of approximately 4.5 V to 5.5 V and supports various clock sources such as external crystal or oscillator modules, allowing high-speed operation up to several tens of MIPS. It features advanced peripherals including high-resolution PWM modules specifically designed for motor control and power conversion applications, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple input channels, Timer modules, quadrature encoder interface (QEI) for position sensing, and hardware serial communication interfaces such as UART, SPI, and I²C for system connectivity.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773807828005-674038469.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 04:23:48','2026-03-18 04:23:48'),
(3273,'30F3010',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'dsPIC30F3010 is a high-performance 16-bit Digital Signal Controller (DSC) from Microchip, designed for embedded control applications that require fast computation, precise motor control, and real-time signal processing capability. It combines the features of a traditional microcontroller with digital signal processing performance, making it suitable for advanced automation and power electronics systems. The device is commonly available in 28-pin DIP and SMD packages, providing multiple general-purpose input/output pins for interfacing with sensors, drivers, and communication modules. It offers about 24 KB of Flash program memory and 2 KB of RAM, allowing efficient execution of control algorithms and signal-processing routines.','The dsPIC30F3010 typically operates with a supply voltage around 4.5 V to 5.5 V and supports external crystal or oscillator clock sources, enabling high-speed operation up to several tens of MIPS. It features advanced peripherals such as motor-control PWM modules, a built-in 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) with multiple channels, Timer modules, and interfaces for UART, SPI, and I²C communication, allowing easy connectivity with other controllers, sensors, and display units.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773808031167-154266200.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 04:27:11','2026-03-18 04:27:11'),
(3274,'30F3010',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'dsPIC30F3010 is a 16-bit Digital Signal Controller (DSC) developed by Microchip Technology, designed to combine the processing capability of a digital signal processor with the flexibility of a microcontroller. It operates at speeds up to 30 MIPS and features around 24 KB of Flash program memory and 2 KB of RAM, making it suitable for real-time embedded control applications.','The device includes integrated peripherals such as a 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC), multiple 16-bit timers, motor-control PWM modules, and communication interfaces like UART, SPI, and I²C. It typically operates within a voltage range of 4.5 V to 5.5 V and supports in-circuit serial programming (ICSP) for easy firmware updates. Due to its DSP engine and high-speed performance, the dsPIC30F3010 is widely used in motor control systems, power converters and inverters, robotics, automation equipment, and industrial control applications where precise timing and signal processing are required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773808709784-133388426.jpg',0,1,'active','2026-03-18 04:38:29','2026-03-18 04:38:50'),
(3275,'30F3011',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'dsPIC30F3011 is a 16-bit Digital Signal Controller (DSC) from Microchip Technology that combines the features of a high-performance microcontroller with digital signal processing capability. It can operate at speeds up to about 30 MIPS and is designed for real-time control applications that require fast mathematical processing and precise timing. The device typically includes around 24 KB of Flash program memory and about 2 KB of RAM for data storage','It integrates several useful peripherals such as a 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC), multiple 16-bit timers, motor-control PWM modules, and serial communication interfaces like UART, SPI, and I²C. The controller generally operates in the 4.5 V to 5.5 V supply voltage range and supports in-circuit serial programming (ICSP) for convenient firmware development and updates. Because of its DSP engine and built-in control peripherals, the dsPIC30F3011 is commonly used in motor drive systems, switched-mode power supplies, inverters, robotics, industrial automation equipment, and other embedded systems that require efficient signal processing and control performance.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773808838203-204670711.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 04:40:38','2026-03-18 04:40:38'),
(3276,'30F3012',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'dsPIC30F3012 is a 16-bit Digital Signal Controller (DSC) developed by Microchip Technology, designed to provide the combined advantages of a microcontroller and a digital signal processor for high-speed embedded control applications. It operates at performance levels of up to about 30 MIPS and typically features around 24 KB of Flash program memory along with approximately 2 KB of data RAM. The device includes several integrated peripherals such as a 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC), multiple 16-bit timers, enhanced motor-control PWM modules, and standard communication interfaces like UART, SPI, and I²C, enabling flexible system connectivity','It generally works with a supply voltage range of about 4.5 V to 5.5 V and supports In-Circuit Serial Programming (ICSP) for easy firmware loading and updates. Owing to its DSP processing capability and precise real-time control features, the dsPIC30F3012 is widely used in applications such as AC/DC motor drives, switched-mode power supplies, inverters, robotics systems, industrial automation controllers, and embedded signal-processing equipment.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773808920303-432196790.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 04:42:00','2026-03-18 04:42:00'),
(3277,'30F4011',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'dsPIC30F4011 is a high-performance 16-bit Digital Signal Controller (DSC) from Microchip Technology, designed to combine microcontroller functionality with digital signal processing capability for advanced real-time control applications. It can operate at speeds of up to about 30 MIPS and typically provides around 48 KB of Flash program memory and approximately 2 KB of data RAM, allowing it to handle complex control algorithms and signal-processing tasks. The controller includes a range of integrated peripherals such as a multi-channel 10-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC), multiple 16-bit timers, enhanced motor-control PWM modules, input capture and output compare features, and communication interfaces including UART, SPI, and I²C for system connectivity','It generally operates within a supply voltage range of about 4.5 V to 5.5 V and supports In-Circuit Serial Programming (ICSP) for convenient firmware development and updates. Because of its powerful DSP engine and dedicated control peripherals, the dsPIC30F4011 is widely used in applications such as AC and DC motor drives, power inverters, switched-mode power supplies, robotics, industrial automation systems, and other embedded control solutions that require accurate timing and fast signal processing.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773809009266-990785679.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 04:43:29','2026-03-18 04:43:29'),
(3278,'MCP602',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'MCP602 is a low-power, dual operational amplifier (op-amp) integrated circuit manufactured by Microchip Technology, designed for general-purpose analog signal conditioning and amplification applications. It operates with a single supply voltage ranging approximately from 2.7 V to 6.0 V, making it suitable for battery-powered and low-voltage electronic circuits. The device offers rail-to-rail input and output capability, allowing it to handle signals close to the supply voltage limits and improving dynamic range in low-voltage systems','MCP602 features low input bias current, low offset voltage, and good bandwidth performance, which help provide accurate amplification and stable operation in sensor interfaces, active filters, signal buffering, data acquisition systems, and audio processing circuits. It is commonly available in small packages such as DIP, SOIC, and MSOP, enabling easy integration into compact embedded designs and analog control applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773809087514-250544185.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 04:44:47','2026-03-18 04:44:47'),
(3279,'MCP604',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'MCP604 is a low-power, quad operational amplifier (op-amp) integrated circuit from Microchip Technology, designed for general-purpose analog signal amplification and conditioning in low-voltage electronic systems. It operates with a single supply voltage typically ranging from about 2.5 V to 6.0 V and provides rail-to-rail input and output capability, allowing it to process signals close to the supply limits and making it suitable for battery-operated devices','The device features low input bias current, low quiescent current consumption, and stable performance, which helps improve accuracy and efficiency in applications such as sensor signal conditioning, active filters, voltage followers, integrators, data acquisition circuits, and portable instrumentation. MCP604 is commonly available in compact packages like DIP, SOIC, and TSSOP, enabling easy use in space-constrained embedded systems and analog control designs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773809172816-774032557.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 04:46:12','2026-03-18 04:46:12'),
(3280,'MCP3201',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'MCP3201 is a 12-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) integrated circuit developed by Microchip Technology, designed for accurate and low-power data acquisition in embedded systems. It uses a successive approximation (SAR) conversion technique and communicates with microcontrollers through a high-speed SPI serial interface, allowing easy integration into digital control and measurement applications','The device typically operates with a single supply voltage in the range of about 2.7 V to 5.5 V and can achieve sampling rates up to around 100 ksps, depending on the clock frequency. MCP3201 provides good resolution and conversion accuracy, making it suitable for sensor interfacing, industrial monitoring, battery-powered instruments, medical devices, and data logging systems. Its compact package options and low power consumption help designers implement reliable analog signal measurement solutions in portable and space-constrained electronic designs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773809297877-798058543.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 04:48:17','2026-03-18 04:48:17'),
(3281,'MCP3202',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'MCP3202 is a 12-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) IC from Microchip Technology designed for precise analog signal measurement in embedded and data-acquisition systems. It uses a successive approximation (SAR) conversion method and communicates with microcontrollers through a high-speed SPI serial interface, enabling simple and efficient digital integration. The device provides two analog input channels that can be configured for single-ended or pseudo-differential operation, offering flexibility in sensor interfacing and signal monitoring applications','It typically operates with a single supply voltage in the range of about 2.7 V to 5.5 V and can achieve sampling speeds of up to approximately 100 ksps depending on the clock input. With low power consumption, good conversion accuracy, and compact package options such as DIP and SOIC, the MCP3202 is widely used in instrumentation, industrial control, portable measurement equipment, battery-powered devices, and general embedded analog data acquisition systems.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773809923574-912378044.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 04:58:43','2026-03-18 04:58:43'),
(3282,'MCP3204',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'MCP3204 is a 12-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) integrated circuit from Microchip Technology, designed for accurate multi-channel analog signal measurement in embedded and data-acquisition applications. It uses a successive approximation (SAR) conversion technique and communicates with microcontrollers through a high-speed SPI serial interface, allowing simple integration into digital systems. The device provides four analog input channels that can be configured as single-ended or pseudo-differential inputs, offering flexibility for sensor interfacing and signal monitoring','It typically operates with a single supply voltage in the range of about 2.7 V to 5.5 V and supports sampling rates up to around 100 ksps, depending on the clock frequency. With low power consumption, good linearity, and compact package options such as DIP and SOIC, the MCP3204 is commonly used in industrial control, instrumentation, portable measurement equipment, data logging systems, and general embedded analog signal processing applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773810170600-641635661.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 05:02:50','2026-03-18 05:02:50'),
(3283,'MCP3208',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'MCP3208 is a 12-bit Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC) integrated circuit manufactured by Microchip Technology, designed for high-accuracy multi-channel analog data acquisition in embedded electronic systems. It uses a successive approximation (SAR) conversion method and communicates with microcontrollers through a high-speed SPI serial interface, enabling simple and reliable digital communication. The device provides eight analog input channels, which can be configured for single-ended or pseudo-differential operation, allowing flexible connection of multiple sensors and analog signals.','MCP3208 typically operates from a single supply voltage in the range of approximately 2.7 V to 5.5 V and supports sampling rates up to about 100 ksps, depending on the system clock. It features low power consumption, good conversion accuracy, and stable performance, making it suitable for applications such as industrial monitoring, instrumentation systems, robotics, portable measurement devices, medical equipment, and general embedded data-logging and control solutions.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773810835623-2838960.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 05:13:55','2026-03-18 05:13:55'),
(3284,'MCP4728',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'MCP4728 is a quad 12-bit Digital-to-Analog Converter (DAC) integrated circuit from Microchip Technology, designed for precise generation of analog voltage signals in embedded and control systems. It communicates with microcontrollers through an I²C serial interface, allowing multiple DAC outputs to be controlled using only a few communication lines. The device provides four independent DAC output channels, each capable of producing rail-to-rail analog output voltages referenced to the supply or an internal reference, enabling flexible signal generation and calibration functions.','MCP4728 typically operates from a single supply voltage in the range of about 2.7 V to 5.5 V and includes non-volatile EEPROM memory to store DAC settings, allowing the outputs to retain their programmed values even after power cycling. With low power consumption, good linearity, and compact package options, it is widely used in applications such as waveform generation, programmable voltage sources, motor control feedback systems, instrumentation, industrial automation, and embedded signal-processing circuits.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773811184250-435544767.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 05:19:44','2026-03-18 05:19:44'),
(3285,'MCP2551',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'MCP2551 is a high-speed CAN (Controller Area Network) transceiver integrated circuit developed by Microchip Technology, used to interface a CAN protocol controller with the physical two-wire CAN bus. It is designed to support communication speeds of up to 1 Mb/s, making it suitable for real-time networking applications in automotive and industrial systems. The device operates typically with a 5 V supply voltage and provides differential transmit and receive capability through the CANH and CANL bus lines, helping to improve noise immunity and reliable data transmission over long distances.','MCP2551 includes features such as short-circuit protection, thermal shutdown, and slope control for reducing electromagnetic interference (EMI). It also supports standby mode for lower power consumption in energy-efficient designs. Due to its robust performance and compliance with CAN standards, the MCP2551 is widely used in automotive electronics, industrial automation networks, robotics, building control systems, and distributed embedded communication applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773811489257-973912892.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 05:24:49','2026-03-18 05:24:49'),
(3286,'MCP4921',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'MCP4921 is a 12-bit Digital-to-Analog Converter (DAC) integrated circuit from Microchip Technology, designed to provide accurate and stable analog voltage output in embedded electronic systems. It uses a high-speed SPI serial interface, allowing microcontrollers and digital processors to control the analog output easily with minimal wiring. The device features a single DAC channel with buffered voltage output and typically operates with a supply voltage range of about 2.7 V to 5.5 V, making it suitable for both low-power and standard logic applications.','MCP4921 offers good linearity, fast settling time, and selectable gain configuration, enabling flexible output voltage scaling for signal generation and control functions. With its low power consumption and compact package options such as DIP and SOIC, it is commonly used in applications like waveform generation, programmable voltage sources, motor control reference circuits, instrumentation systems, audio signal adjustment, and general embedded analog output applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773811605436-146946538.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 05:26:45','2026-03-18 05:26:45'),
(3287,'MCP4922',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'MCP4922 is a dual 12-bit Digital-to-Analog Converter (DAC) integrated circuit manufactured by Microchip Technology, designed for generating precise analog voltage outputs in embedded control and signal-processing applications. It communicates with microcontrollers and digital systems through a high-speed SPI serial interface, enabling fast and simple control of its two independent DAC output channels. The device typically operates with a single supply voltage in the range of about 2.7 V to 5.5 V and provides buffered, rail-to-rail voltage outputs with selectable gain settings for flexible output scaling','MCP4922 offers good linearity, low power consumption, and fast settling time, making it suitable for waveform generation, programmable reference voltage creation, audio level control, motor drive feedback systems, instrumentation equipment, and general embedded analog output applications. It is commonly available in compact packages such as DIP and SOIC, allowing easy integration into both prototype and production electronic designs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773811894516-773690987.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 05:31:34','2026-03-18 05:31:34'),
(3288,'MCP9701',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'MCP9701 is a low-power analog temperature sensor integrated circuit from Microchip Technology, designed to provide a voltage output that is directly proportional to ambient temperature. It operates with a wide supply voltage range, typically from about 2.3 V to 5.5 V, making it suitable for battery-powered and low-voltage embedded systems. The device produces a linear analog output with a temperature coefficient of approximately 19.5 mV/°C, allowing simple interfacing with microcontroller ADC inputs for temperature monitoring and control.','MCP9701 features low quiescent current consumption, fast thermal response, and good accuracy without requiring complex calibration circuitry. It is commonly available in small packages such as TO-92, SOT-23, and SC-70, enabling use in compact electronic designs. Due to its simplicity and efficiency, the MCP9701 is widely used in applications such as environmental monitoring, power supply temperature protection, consumer electronics, industrial control equipment, and portable measurement systems.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773812891643-92965961.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 05:48:11','2026-03-18 05:48:11'),
(3289,'YY Universal A/C Remote Control','YY-1311',NULL,NULL,1.00,'The YY-1311 remote is a replacement / universal air-conditioner remote control mainly used to operate split or window AC units.','Works using infrared (IR) signal to control the air conditioner.Usually comes with a small LCD display to show temperature and operating mode.Designed with plastic body and rubber keypad buttons for easy handling.','Keep the remote away from water and wet hands.',NULL,'products/1773818259592-752528225.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 07:17:39','2026-03-18 07:17:39'),
(3290,'87C52X2BN',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'87C52X2BN is an 8-bit microcontroller based on the popular 8051 architecture, originally manufactured by Philips (now NXP Semiconductors). It belongs to the high-speed 80C51 family and is designed for embedded control applications requiring reliable digital processing and peripheral interfacing. The device typically features 8 KB of EPROM program memory, 256 bytes of internal RAM, and operates at higher clock speeds compared to standard 8051 controllers due to its X2 mode, which allows faster instruction execution','It includes built-in peripherals such as three 16-bit timers/counters, a full-duplex UART serial port, multiple interrupt sources, and 32 programmable I/O lines for connecting external devices like displays, relays, sensors, and communication modules. The microcontroller generally operates with a 5 V supply and supports external crystal oscillators for system clock generation. Because of its stable performance and familiar instruction set, the 87C52X2BN is widely used in industrial control systems, instrumentation equipment, consumer electronics, automation projects, and educational embedded system designs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773819053089-906014684.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 07:30:53','2026-03-18 07:30:53'),
(3291,'89C61EQ (W78E365)',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'89C61EQ (W78E365) is a high-performance 8-bit microcontroller based on the standard 8051 architecture, manufactured by Winbond (and also referenced with compatible versions from other vendors). It is designed for embedded control applications that require faster processing and flexible memory options. The controller typically provides Flash program memory (around 64 KB) and internal RAM, allowing storage of application code and data within the chip.','It supports higher operating speeds compared to traditional 8051 devices and includes built-in peripherals such as multiple 16-bit timers/counters, a full-duplex UART serial communication interface, watchdog timer, and up to 32 programmable I/O pins for interfacing with external components. The device usually operates with a 5 V power supply and requires an external crystal oscillator for clock generation. Due to its reliable performance and compatibility with the widely used 8051 instruction set, the 89C61EQ (W78E365) is commonly used in industrial automation, instrumentation systems, communication equipment, consumer electronics, and general embedded system designs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773819656718-921767574.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 07:40:56','2026-03-18 07:40:56'),
(3292,'89V51RD2BN',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'89V51RD2BN (P89V51RD2BN) is a high-performance 8-bit microcontroller based on the standard 8051 architecture, manufactured by NXP (formerly Philips). It is designed for embedded control applications that require fast execution speed, large on-chip program memory, and flexible peripheral interfacing. The device typically features 64 KB of Flash program memory and 1 KB of internal RAM, allowing application code storage and efficient data handling within the chip. It supports In-System Programming (ISP) and In-Application Programming (IAP), enabling firmware updates without removing the microcontroller from the circuit.','The controller includes built-in peripherals such as three 16-bit timers/counters, a full-duplex UART serial communication interface, watchdog timer, power-saving modes, and up to 32 programmable I/O pins for connecting sensors, displays, relays, and communication modules. It usually operates with a 5 V supply voltage and uses an external crystal oscillator for clock generation. Due to its high speed and compatibility with the widely used 8051 instruction set, the 89V51RD2BN is commonly used in industrial automation systems, instrumentation equipment, consumer electronics, motor control circuits, communication devices, and general embedded system applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773819761542-80466464.png',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 07:42:41','2026-03-18 07:42:41'),
(3293,'PCF8563',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PCF8563 is a low-power Real-Time Clock (RTC) and calendar IC developed by NXP Semiconductors, designed to keep accurate time and date information in embedded electronic systems. It communicates with microcontrollers through a two-wire I²C serial interface, allowing simple connection using minimal pins. The device maintains data such as seconds, minutes, hours, day, date, month, and year, and includes features like programmable alarms, timer functions, and interrupt output for event-based control.','PCF8563 operates with a wide supply voltage range of approximately 1.0 V to 5.5 V, making it suitable for battery-backed and low-power portable devices. It requires an external 32.768 kHz crystal oscillator for accurate timekeeping and consumes very low current, enabling long battery life in standby operation. The IC is commonly available in compact packages such as SOIC and TSSOP, allowing easy integration into space-constrained designs. Due to its reliable timekeeping performance and simple interfacing, PCF8563 is widely used in digital clocks, energy meters, data loggers, industrial controllers, communication equipment, and consumer electronic products.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773820356258-887410686.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 07:52:36','2026-03-18 07:52:36'),
(3294,'PCF8574P',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PCF8574P is an 8-bit remote input/output (I/O) expander integrated circuit developed by NXP Semiconductors, designed to increase the number of digital input and output pins available to a microcontroller. It communicates through a two-wire I²C serial interface, allowing multiple devices to be connected on the same bus using configurable hardware addresses. The IC provides eight quasi-bidirectional I/O ports, which can be used as either inputs or outputs without needing separate direction control registers, simplifying circuit design.','The device typically operates with a supply voltage range of about 2.5 V to 6 V and features low power consumption, making it suitable for battery-powered and embedded applications. It also includes an interrupt output pin, which can notify the microcontroller when an input state changes, improving system efficiency. The PCF8574P is commonly available in DIP-16 and SOIC packages and is widely used for applications such as LCD interfacing, keypad scanning, LED control, relay driving, industrial automation systems, and general embedded I/O expansion tasks where additional digital ports are required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773820625510-702828368.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 07:57:05','2026-03-18 07:57:05'),
(3295,'PCF8583',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PCF8583 is a low-power real-time clock and calendar IC developed by NXP Semiconductors, designed to provide accurate timekeeping and event timing functions in embedded electronic systems. It communicates with microcontrollers through a two-wire I²C serial interface, allowing simple data transfer using minimal connection lines. The device can store and track time and date information such as seconds, minutes, hours, day, month, and year (with limited year counting) and also includes alarm, timer, and event counter functions for scheduling and monitoring operations.','PCF8583 typically operates with a supply voltage range of about 2.5 V to 6 V and requires an external 32.768 kHz crystal oscillator to maintain accurate clock timing. It features low power consumption, making it suitable for battery-backup applications where continuous timekeeping is required even when the main system power is off. The IC is commonly available in DIP and SOIC packages, enabling easy integration into both prototype and production designs. Because of its reliable operation and simple interfacing, the PCF8583 is widely used in digital clocks, energy meters, data logging systems, industrial automation equipment, communication devices, and various consumer electronic products that require real-time scheduling and time tracking.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773820722004-279927667.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 07:58:42','2026-03-18 07:58:42'),
(3296,'PCF8591',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'PCF8591 is an 8-bit analog-to-digital and digital-to-analog converter IC developed by NXP Semiconductors, designed for simple analog data acquisition and signal generation in embedded systems. It communicates with microcontrollers through a two-wire I²C serial interface, allowing multiple devices to share the same communication bus. The device provides four analog input channels that can be configured as single-ended or differential inputs, along with one analog voltage output (DAC) for generating reference or control signals.','PCF8591 typically operates with a supply voltage range of about 2.5 V to 6 V and features low power consumption, making it suitable for portable and battery-powered applications. It includes an internal sample-and-hold circuit and on-chip oscillator, simplifying external component requirements. The IC is commonly available in DIP and SOIC packages, enabling easy use in both development and production circuits. Due to its simple interfacing and versatile analog functions, PCF8591 is widely used in sensor interfacing, data logging, industrial control systems, robotics projects, educational experiments, and general embedded analog signal processing applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773820878788-24044194.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 08:01:18','2026-03-18 08:01:18'),
(3297,'87C52X2FN',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'87C52X2FN is a high-speed 8-bit microcontroller based on the widely used 8051 architecture, originally manufactured by Philips (now NXP Semiconductors). It belongs to the enhanced 80C51 family and is designed for embedded control applications requiring reliable operation and faster instruction execution. The controller typically provides about 8 KB of EPROM program memory and 256 bytes of internal RAM, allowing storage of application programs and data within the chip.','The device supports X2 mode operation, which enables higher processing speed by reducing the number of clock cycles required per instruction compared to standard 8051 controllers. It includes built-in peripherals such as three 16-bit timers/counters, a full-duplex UART serial communication interface, multiple interrupt sources, and up to 32 programmable I/O pins for interfacing with external components like sensors, displays, relays, and communication modules. The microcontroller generally operates with a 5 V supply voltage and requires an external crystal oscillator for clock generation.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773821176011-913845610.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 08:06:16','2026-03-18 08:06:16'),
(3298,'80C85',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'80C85 is a CMOS version of the classic 8-bit 8085 microprocessor, designed for general-purpose computing and embedded control applications. It is capable of addressing up to 64 KB of memory and features a multiplexed address and data bus, allowing efficient communication with external memory and peripheral devices. The processor operates with a single +5 V power supply and includes an on-chip clock generator, reducing the need for additional external timing circuitry.','The 80C85 supports multiple interrupt inputs, serial input/output lines, and status/control signals, enabling flexible interfacing with external hardware such as RAM, ROM, input/output ports, and communication modules. Due to its stable architecture, simple instruction set, and ease of system design, the 80C85 has been widely used in educational training kits, industrial controllers, instrumentation systems, early computer systems, and embedded development projects where basic processing and control functions are required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773821675755-570043824.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 08:14:35','2026-03-18 08:14:35'),
(3299,'80C88',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'80C88 is a CMOS version of the classic Intel 8088 8-bit microprocessor, designed for general-purpose computing and embedded control applications. Internally it uses a 16-bit architecture, but it communicates with external memory and peripherals through an 8-bit data bus, which helps reduce system cost and simplifies hardware design. The processor can address up to 1 MB of memory using its segmented memory architecture and typically operates with a single +5 V power supply.','The 80C88 includes a six-byte instruction prefetch queue, arithmetic logic unit (ALU), general-purpose registers, and various control and status signals for interfacing with external RAM, ROM, and input/output devices. It supports hardware interrupts, serial data communication lines, and clock synchronization features, enabling flexible system implementation. Due to its compatibility with the widely used x86 instruction set and reliable performance, the 80C88 has been used in early personal computers, industrial controllers, instrumentation equipment, communication systems, and educational microprocessor training kits where structured data processing and control operations are required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773822125767-84157606.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 08:22:05','2026-03-18 08:22:05'),
(3300,'82C51',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'82C51 is a CMOS version of the classic 8251 Universal Synchronous/Asynchronous Receiver Transmitter (USART) integrated circuit, designed to provide serial communication capability to microprocessor-based systems. It allows data transmission and reception in both synchronous and asynchronous modes, making it suitable for a wide range of communication applications. The device interfaces easily with microprocessors such as the 8085, 8086, and other bus-based systems, enabling conversion between parallel data from the CPU and serial data for communication lines.','The IC typically operates with a single +5 V supply and supports programmable features such as baud rate selection, character length, parity control, and stop bits, allowing flexible configuration of serial communication protocols. It includes transmit and receive buffers, status signals, and interrupt capability to improve communication efficiency and reduce processor workload. Due to its reliable operation and standard interface design, the 82C51 is widely used in industrial communication systems, data terminals, instrumentation equipment, embedded controllers, and educational microprocessor development kits where serial data transfer is required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773822738756-863480605.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 08:32:18','2026-03-18 08:32:18'),
(3301,'82C54',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'82C54 is a CMOS version of the 8254 Programmable Interval Timer (PIT) integrated circuit, used to generate accurate timing delays, frequency signals, and event counting functions in microprocessor-based systems. The device contains three independent 16-bit counters, each of which can be programmed to operate in various timing modes such as rate generator, square-wave generator, software-triggered strobe, and hardware-triggered strobe.','It typically operates from a single +5 V supply and interfaces easily with common microprocessors like the 8085, 8086, and similar bus-oriented systems. Each counter has separate clock, gate, and output pins, allowing flexible use for tasks such as time delay generation, frequency division, pulse counting, waveform generation, and real-time system control. Because of its reliable performance and programmable operation, the 82C54 is widely used in industrial automation equipment, communication systems, embedded controllers, instrumentation, and educational microprocessor training kits where precise timing control is required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773822850470-730719935.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 08:34:10','2026-03-18 08:34:10'),
(3302,'82C55',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'82C55 is a CMOS version of the classic 8255 Programmable Peripheral Interface (PPI) integrated circuit, designed to provide flexible digital input/output expansion for microprocessor-based systems. It offers 24 programmable I/O lines, organized into three 8-bit ports (Port A, Port B, and Port C), which can be configured for input or output operation in different modes. The device interfaces easily with common microprocessors such as the 8085, 8086, and similar bus-based controllers, enabling efficient connection of external devices like keyboards, displays, relays, printers, and sensors.','The IC typically operates with a single +5 V power supply and supports multiple operating modes including simple I/O mode, strobed I/O mode, and bidirectional bus mode, allowing reliable data transfer between the CPU and peripheral devices. It also provides handshaking and interrupt capability to improve system performance in real-time applications. Due to its simple programmability, stable operation, and wide compatibility, the 82C55 is widely used in industrial automation systems, instrumentation equipment, embedded controllers, communication devices, and educational microprocessor development kits where additional digital interfacing is required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773822976346-621869658.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 08:36:16','2026-03-18 08:36:16'),
(3303,'82C59',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'82C59 is a CMOS version of the 8259 Programmable Interrupt Controller (PIC) integrated circuit, designed to manage multiple interrupt requests in microprocessor-based systems. It helps prioritize and control hardware interrupts, allowing the CPU to respond efficiently to external events. The device can handle up to 8 interrupt input lines, and multiple 82C59 ICs can be cascaded to support up to 64 interrupt sources, making it suitable for complex control applications.','The IC typically operates with a single +5 V supply and interfaces easily with common microprocessors such as the 8085, 8086, and similar bus-oriented systems. It provides features like interrupt masking, priority resolution, interrupt vector generation, and programmable operating modes, which improve system performance and simplify interrupt management. Because of its reliable operation and flexible configuration, the 82C59 is widely used in industrial control systems, communication equipment, instrumentation, embedded controllers, and educational microprocessor training kits where efficient handling of multiple hardware interrupts is required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773823115826-548569639.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 08:38:35','2026-03-18 08:38:35'),
(3304,'YY Universal A/C Remote Control','YY-264',NULL,NULL,1.00,'Works using infrared (IR) signal technology to send commands to the AC indoor unit.Usually has an LCD display to show temperature, fan mode, timer, and other settings.','Operates using AAA batteries.Often requires manual code setting or auto-search setup for brand matching.','Supports essential cooling and comfort settings',NULL,'products/1773823701571-885444588.jfif',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 08:48:21','2026-03-18 08:48:21'),
(3305,'C106M',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'C106M is a Silicon Controlled Rectifier (SCR), a type of thyristor used for switching and controlling AC or DC power in electronic circuits. It is designed to handle moderate current and voltage levels, making it suitable for various power control applications. The device has three terminals — anode, cathode, and gate — and once triggered by a small gate current, it allows current to flow between anode and cathode until the current drops below its holding level.','C106M typically supports blocking voltages in the range of about 400 V (depending on variant) and can conduct several amperes of load current, making it useful in practical power control designs. It is commonly available in TO-225 / TO-126 type packages, allowing easy mounting and heat dissipation. Because of its reliable switching characteristics and simple gate triggering, the C106M SCR is widely used in light dimmers, heater control circuits, motor speed control systems, battery chargers, power regulators, and industrial switching applications where controlled rectification and load management are required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773823755611-82268383.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 08:49:15','2026-03-18 08:49:15'),
(3306,'BT139-800',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'BT139-800 is a bidirectional TRIAC (Triode for Alternating Current) used for switching and phase-control of AC loads in power electronics circuits. It is designed to control relatively high voltage and current loads, making it suitable for domestic and industrial AC power control applications. The device has three terminals — MT1 (Main Terminal 1), MT2 (Main Terminal 2), and Gate, and it can conduct current in both directions once triggered by a gate pulse.','This TRIAC typically supports a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 800 V and can handle load currents up to 16 A (depending on cooling and circuit conditions). It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, allowing easy mounting on heat sinks for better thermal performance. Because of its reliable switching characteristics and high voltage capability, the BT139-800 is widely used in light dimmers, fan speed regulators, heater control circuits, AC motor control systems, solid-state relays, and general AC power switching applications where efficient control of alternating current loads is required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773823868574-292742070.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 08:51:08','2026-03-18 08:51:08'),
(3307,'BTA12-600',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'BTA12-600 is a bidirectional TRIAC used for controlling AC power in switching and phase-control applications. It is designed to handle medium to high current loads, making it suitable for domestic appliances and industrial power control circuits. The device has three terminals — MT1 (Main Terminal 1), MT2 (Main Terminal 2), and Gate, and once triggered by a gate signal, it can conduct current in both directions through the AC cycle.','This TRIAC typically supports a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 600 V and a current rating around 12 A, depending on heat-sink conditions and operating environment. It is commonly available in an insulated TO-220 package, which simplifies mounting on heat sinks and improves electrical isolation. Because of its reliable performance and easy gate triggering, the BTA12-600 is widely used in light dimmers, fan regulators, heater control systems, AC motor speed controllers, solid-state relays, and general AC load switching applications where efficient control of mains power is required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773824171808-787588457.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 08:56:11','2026-03-18 08:56:11'),
(3308,'BTA16-600',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'BTA16-600 is a bidirectional TRIAC (AC power switching device) used for controlling alternating-current loads in domestic and industrial electronic circuits. It is designed to handle relatively high load currents and can conduct current in both directions once a triggering signal is applied to its gate terminal. The device has three terminals — MT1 (Main Terminal 1), MT2 (Main Terminal 2), and Gate, and is commonly used in phase-control circuits for regulating AC power.','This TRIAC typically supports a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 600 V and a current rating up to around 16 A, depending on proper heat-sink usage and operating conditions. It is generally available in an insulated TO-220 package, which helps simplify mounting and provides electrical isolation from the heat sink. Due to its robust switching capability and reliable performance, the BTA16-600 is widely used in light dimmers, fan speed regulators, heater controllers, AC motor speed control circuits, solid-state relays, and general mains power switching applications where efficient control of AC loads is required.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773824270426-731530663.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 08:57:50','2026-03-18 08:57:50'),
(3309,'Huayu Universal AC Remote ','K-6600',NULL,NULL,1.00,'Works using infrared (IR) signal to control the AC indoor unit.Usually plug-and-play or simple code setup depending on AC model.','Comes with a digital LCD display showing temperature and mode settings.Designed with lightweight plastic body and rubber keypad buttons.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773824931796-819992904.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 09:08:51','2026-03-18 09:08:51'),
(3310,'BTA40-600',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'BTA40-600 is a high-power bidirectional TRIAC used for switching and phase control of large AC loads in industrial and domestic power electronics circuits. It allows current to flow in both directions between the main terminals when a triggering pulse is applied to the gate, making it suitable for efficient control of alternating-current power. The device has three terminals — MT1, MT2, and Gate, and is designed to operate reliably in high-current applications.','This TRIAC typically features a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 600 V and can handle load currents up to approximately 40 A, depending on proper heat-sink usage and operating conditions. It is generally supplied in a TO-3P or high-power insulated package, which provides improved thermal dissipation and electrical isolation from the heat sink.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773825078329-301728067.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 09:11:18','2026-03-18 09:11:18'),
(3311,'BTA41-600',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'BTA41-600 is a high-current bidirectional TRIAC used for switching and phase-angle control of AC loads in power electronics applications. It allows current to flow in both directions between the main terminals once a gate trigger pulse is applied, making it suitable for controlling mains-operated equipment. The device has three terminals — MT1 (Main Terminal 1), MT2 (Main Terminal 2), and Gate, and is designed for reliable operation in heavy-duty circuits.','This TRIAC typically supports a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 600 V and can handle load currents up to around 40 A or more, depending on proper heat-sink design and operating conditions. It is usually available in a TO-3P / high-power insulated package, which improves thermal performance and simplifies mounting with electrical isolation.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773825196438-795324149.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 09:13:16','2026-03-18 09:13:16'),
(3312,'TYN612',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'TYN612 is a silicon controlled rectifier (SCR) designed for switching and controlled rectification of AC or DC power in electronic circuits. It has three terminals — anode, cathode, and gate — and once triggered by a small gate current, it conducts current from anode to cathode until the current falls below the holding level. This makes it suitable for controlled power delivery applications.','The device typically supports a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 600 V and can handle load currents around 12 A (depending on proper heat-sink conditions and circuit design). It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, which allows easy mounting and effective heat dissipation in power control circuits.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773825310541-567090754.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 09:15:10','2026-03-18 09:15:10'),
(3313,'TYN616',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'TYN616 is a high-voltage silicon controlled rectifier (SCR) designed for switching and controlled rectification of AC or DC power in industrial and domestic electronic circuits. It has three terminals — anode, cathode, and gate, and once a small triggering current is applied to the gate, the device allows current to flow between anode and cathode until the load current drops below the holding value.','This SCR typically supports a repetitive peak off-state voltage of about 800 V and can handle load currents up to around 16 A, depending on proper heat-sink usage and operating conditions. It is usually available in a TO-220 power package, which helps in efficient heat dissipation and easy mounting on heat sinks.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773825396069-449505582.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 09:16:36','2026-03-18 09:16:36'),
(3314,'YY Universal A/C Remote Control','YY-200',NULL,NULL,1.00,'Works using infrared (IR) signal technology to communicate with the AC indoor unit.Comes with a digital LCD display showing temperature, fan speed, and operating mode.','Supports multiple AC brand codes and may require manual code setup or auto search.','Keep away from water, moisture, and high heat',NULL,NULL,1,1,'active','2026-03-18 09:17:51','2026-03-18 09:17:51'),
(3315,'BC337-40',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'BC337-40 is a general-purpose NPN bipolar junction transistor (BJT) widely used for switching and amplification in low-power electronic circuits. It is designed to handle moderate current levels and provides high current gain, making it suitable for interfacing digital logic with loads such as relays, LEDs, buzzers, and small motors. The device is typically available in a compact TO-92 package and has three terminals — collector, base, and emitter.','This transistor generally supports a collector-emitter voltage of up to about 45 V and can handle collector currents up to around 800 mA, depending on operating conditions and heat dissipation. The “-40” suffix indicates a higher DC current gain group (hFE) compared to other BC337 variants, which helps improve switching sensitivity and amplification performance.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773825524766-143016694.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 09:18:44','2026-03-18 09:18:44'),
(3316,'BC558',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'BC558 is a general-purpose PNP bipolar junction transistor (BJT) widely used for low-power switching and signal amplification in electronic circuits. It is typically available in a compact TO-92 package and has three terminals — emitter, base, and collector. This transistor is designed for small-signal applications and works as a complementary device to popular NPN transistors such as BC547 or BC337.','The BC558 generally supports a collector-emitter voltage of up to about 30 V and can handle collector currents up to around 100 mA, depending on operating conditions. It provides good current gain and low noise characteristics, making it suitable for audio and signal processing circuits.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773825628205-730544759.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 09:20:28','2026-03-18 09:20:28'),
(3317,'BC550',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'BC550 is a low-noise NPN bipolar junction transistor (BJT) designed for signal amplification and low-current switching applications in electronic circuits. It is commonly available in a compact TO-92 package and has three terminals — collector, base, and emitter. This transistor is specially optimized for low-noise performance, making it suitable for sensitive audio and signal-processing stages.','The BC550 typically supports a collector-emitter voltage of up to about 45 V and can handle collector currents up to around 100 mA, depending on operating conditions. It offers good current gain and stable electrical characteristics, which help improve signal quality in amplification circuits.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773825716700-622021682.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 09:21:56','2026-03-18 09:21:56'),
(3318,'BC618',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'BC618 is a general-purpose NPN bipolar junction transistor (BJT) used for low-power switching and signal amplification in electronic circuits. It is typically available in a compact TO-92 package and has three terminals — collector, base, and emitter — enabling it to function as an electronic switch or amplifier.','The transistor is designed to operate with moderate collector-emitter voltage levels (around 30–45 V depending on variant) and can handle collector currents up to roughly 100 mA, making it suitable for small-signal and driver applications. It provides good current gain and stable performance, allowing efficient interfacing between low-power control circuits and external loads.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773825999429-596927296.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 09:26:39','2026-03-18 09:26:39'),
(3319,'BC635',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'BC635 is a general-purpose NPN bipolar junction transistor (BJT) designed for switching and amplification in medium-power electronic circuits. It is usually supplied in a compact TO-92 package and has three terminals — collector, base, and emitter — allowing it to function as an electronic switch or signal amplifier.','The device typically supports a collector-emitter voltage up to about 45 V and can handle collector currents up to around 1 A, depending on operating conditions and proper heat dissipation. It provides good current gain and fast switching characteristics, which make it suitable for driving loads that require more current than standard small-signal transistors.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773826395452-237476546.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 09:33:15','2026-03-18 09:33:15'),
(3320,'BC807',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'BC807 is a general-purpose PNP bipolar junction transistor (BJT) designed mainly for surface-mount electronic circuits. It is commonly available in a compact SOT-23 package, making it suitable for high-density PCB designs and portable devices. The transistor has three terminals — emitter, base, and collector — and is used for signal amplification as well as low-to-medium current switching applications.','The device typically supports a collector-emitter voltage of up to about 45 V and can handle collector currents up to around 500 mA, depending on operating conditions and heat dissipation. It offers good current gain and fast switching characteristics, enabling efficient interfacing between logic circuits and loads such as LEDs, relays (with driver stages), and small motors.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773826784433-658728718.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 09:39:44','2026-03-18 09:39:44'),
(3321,'BD241',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'BD241 is a medium-power NPN bipolar junction transistor (BJT) designed for switching and amplification in power electronic circuits. It is typically available in a TO-220 package, which allows efficient heat dissipation and easy mounting on a heat sink for higher current operation. The device has three terminals — collector, base, and emitter, enabling it to function as a power switch or amplifier stage.','The transistor generally supports a collector-emitter voltage of around 45 V to 80 V (depending on variant) and can handle collector currents up to about 3 A, making it suitable for driving moderate power loads. It provides good current gain and reliable thermal performance, which helps ensure stable operation in demanding applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773826937424-26327004.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 09:42:17','2026-03-18 09:42:17'),
(3322,'YY Universal A/C Remote Control','K-LG1358 ',NULL,NULL,1.00,'Works using infrared (IR) signal technology to communicate with the AC indoor unit.Usually comes with a digital LCD screen showing temperature, fan speed, and mode settings.','Enables convenient control of cooling functions from a distance.','Avoid dropping or strong impact',NULL,'products/1773827555938-925522753.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 09:52:35','2026-03-18 09:52:35'),
(3323,'BD679',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'BD679 is a medium-power NPN Darlington transistor designed for high-gain switching and amplification applications in electronic circuits. A Darlington configuration internally connects two transistors to provide very high current gain, allowing small base currents to control relatively large load currents. The device is commonly available in a TO-126 / TO-225 style package and has three terminals — collector, base, and emitter.','The transistor typically supports a collector-emitter voltage of about 80 V and can handle collector currents up to around 4 A, depending on proper heat dissipation and operating conditions. It also includes an internal base-emitter resistor and protection diode, which helps improve switching reliability and simplifies circuit design.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773827981719-283153196.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 09:59:41','2026-03-18 09:59:41'),
(3324,'BD682',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'BD682 is a medium-power PNP Darlington transistor designed for high-gain switching and amplification in power electronic circuits. Internally it consists of two transistors connected in Darlington configuration, providing very high current gain, which allows a small base current to control relatively large collector currents. The device is commonly available in a TO-126 / TO-225 package and has three terminals — emitter, base, and collector.','It typically supports a collector-emitter voltage of about 80 V and can handle collector currents up to around 4 A, depending on heat-sink conditions and operating environment. The transistor usually includes an internal base-emitter resistor and protection diode, which helps improve switching reliability and simplifies circuit design.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773828531067-137820093.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-18 10:08:51','2026-03-18 10:08:51'),
(3325,'Azone Universal Remote ',NULL,NULL,NULL,1.00,'Works using infrared (IR) signal technology to control the device.Many models support multiple brand codes and can be set using manual code entry or auto-search function.','Usually features a lightweight plastic body, rubber keypad, and LCD display (for AC remotes).Powered by AAA batteries and suitable for home and office use.','Easy plug-and-play operation in many models',NULL,NULL,1,1,'active','2026-03-18 11:33:13','2026-03-18 11:33:13'),
(3326,'AC Remote ','JE-JJ2',NULL,NULL,1.00,'Works using infrared (IR) signal technology to communicate with the AC indoor unit.Usually features a digital LCD display to show temperature, mode, timer, and fan speed.','Many versions support direct use or simple code-setting (manual / auto search).Powered by AAA batteries for convenient daily use.','Do not expose the remote to water, moisture, or high heat',NULL,NULL,1,1,'active','2026-03-18 11:50:32','2026-03-18 11:50:32'),
(3327,'BS170',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'BS170 is an N-channel enhancement mode MOSFET widely used in low-power electronic switching and amplification applications. It is designed in a compact TO-92 through-hole package, which makes it convenient for PCB mounting and breadboard prototyping. This MOSFET can handle a maximum drain-to-source voltage of around 60 volts and a continuous drain current of approximately 500 mA under suitable operating conditions.','In amplifier circuits, the BS170 can be used for signal processing and low-noise applications. Its simple three-pin configuration — gate, drain, and source — makes circuit design easy for beginners and professionals. Proper gate protection is important because the MOSFET gate is sensitive to static electricity. Heat dissipation should be considered when operating near maximum current ratings. The BS170 is also valued for its low cost, easy availability, and reliable performance in hobby, educational, and commercial electronics projects. Overall, it is a versatile and efficient component for small signal and switching applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773891334762-517048232.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 03:35:34','2026-03-19 03:35:34'),
(3328,'BUZ71',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'UZ71 is an N-channel enhancement mode power MOSFET designed for high-current and high-voltage switching applications. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, which allows efficient heat dissipation and easy mounting on heat sinks. This MOSFET can withstand a drain-to-source voltage of around 50V and can handle high drain current, making it suitable for power control circuits. The BUZ71 offers relatively low ON resistance, which helps reduce power loss during switching operations','The device supports fast switching speed, which improves efficiency in high-frequency applications. Its rugged construction ensures reliable performance in industrial and consumer electronic systems. Proper heat sink usage is recommended when operating at high load conditions to prevent thermal damage. Gate protection using resistors or zener diodes helps improve device life and stability. The simple three-terminal configuration — Gate, Drain, and Source — makes circuit design straightforward. Overall, BUZ71 is a dependable and cost-effective MOSFET for medium-power switching and control applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773891419327-847238372.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 03:36:59','2026-03-19 03:36:59'),
(3329,'BYQ28-200',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'BYQ28-200 is a high-efficiency ultrafast recovery rectifier diode designed for high-frequency power rectification and switching applications. It is typically available in a TO-220 package, which allows good heat dissipation and easy mounting on heat sinks in power circuits. The diode has a maximum repetitive peak reverse voltage of about 200 volts, making it suitable for medium-voltage power supply designs.','The device is commonly used in output rectification stages of switched-mode power supplies and high-frequency rectifier circuits. Its rugged construction ensures reliable operation under high-temperature and high-current conditions. Proper heat sinking is recommended during high load operation to avoid thermal stress and extend component life. Correct polarity must always be maintained during installation since it is a rectifier device. The BYQ28-200 also helps reduce switching losses and electromagnetic interference in power electronics systems. Due to its stable performance, easy availability, and efficient operation, it is widely used in industrial, commercial, and hobby power supply projects.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773891670452-343716347.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 03:41:10','2026-03-19 03:41:10'),
(3330,'BYV32-200',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'BYV32-200 is a high-performance ultrafast recovery rectifier diode designed for use in high-frequency power supply and switching circuits. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, which allows efficient heat dissipation and easy installation on heat sinks for improved thermal performance. The diode typically supports a maximum repetitive reverse voltage of about 200 volts and can handle relatively high forward current, making it suitable for medium-power rectification applications.','The device is known for stable operation under high-temperature conditions and reliable performance in industrial as well as consumer electronic equipment. Proper heat sink usage is recommended when operating at higher current levels to prevent overheating. Care must be taken to maintain correct polarity during installation since it is a rectifier diode. Due to its rugged construction, fast switching capability, and good efficiency, the BYV32-200 is a popular choice in modern power electronics designs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773891784981-542455652.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 03:43:04','2026-03-19 03:43:04'),
(3331,'BYV96E',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'BYV96E is a fast recovery rectifier diode mainly used in high-frequency rectification and switching power applications. It is generally available in an axial lead DO-15 package, making it suitable for through-hole mounting in power supply and converter circuits. The diode is designed to handle a high repetitive reverse voltage (around 1000V) and moderate forward current, which makes it useful in medium-power electronic designs. Its fast reverse recovery time helps to reduce switching losses and improve efficiency in circuits operating at high frequencies.','The BYV96E is commonly used in SMPS, inverter circuits, freewheeling protection, snubber networks, and DC-DC converters. It also provides low forward voltage drop, which contributes to lower heat generation and better overall performance. Due to its rugged construction, the device can operate reliably in demanding electrical environments. Proper lead spacing and adequate ventilation or heat dissipation should be ensured when used near maximum ratings. Correct polarity must always be maintained during installation since it functions as a rectifier. The diode is valued for its stable performance, durability, and wide availability, making it suitable for industrial equipment, consumer electronics, and hobby power projects.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773891863319-217354965.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 03:44:23','2026-03-19 03:44:23'),
(3332,'MJE3055',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'MJE3055 is a widely used NPN silicon power transistor designed for medium-power amplification and switching applications. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, which allows effective heat dissipation and convenient mounting on heat sinks in power circuits. This transistor can handle relatively high collector current and voltage, making it suitable for power control stages in electronic equipment. The MJE3055 provides good gain characteristics and reliable switching performance, which helps improve efficiency in amplifier and regulator circuits.','The transistor features a simple three-terminal configuration — Base, Collector, and Emitter, which makes circuit design straightforward for both beginners and professionals. Proper biasing and base current limiting resistors are recommended to ensure stable operation and long device life. When used near maximum ratings, adequate cooling arrangements should be provided to avoid thermal damage. The MJE3055 is valued for its low cost, easy availability, and dependable performance in industrial, educational, and hobby electronics projects.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773891938820-509777127.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 03:45:38','2026-03-19 03:45:38'),
(3333,'MJE13005',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'MJE13005 is a high-voltage NPN power switching transistor commonly used in switched-mode power supplies and high-frequency switching circuits. It is typically available in a TO-220 package, which allows efficient heat dissipation and easy mounting on heat sinks for improved thermal management. This transistor is designed to withstand high collector-emitter voltage (around 400V) and moderate collector current, making it suitable for offline power supply designs. The MJE13005 offers fast switching characteristics and good current gain, which helps improve efficiency and performance in switching regulator circuits','It is widely used in SMPS, inverter circuits, CFL and LED drivers, battery chargers, and power converters. Due to its rugged internal structure, the device provides reliable operation under high-voltage stress when proper biasing and cooling are maintained. The transistor has a simple three-pin configuration — Base, Collector, and Emitter, which simplifies circuit design and servicing. Proper base resistor selection and snubber or protection networks are recommended to enhance switching stability and device life. Adequate heat sinking is essential when operating near maximum load conditions to prevent overheating. Because of its low cost, durability, and wide availability, the MJE13005 is a popular choice in consumer and industrial power electronics applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773892007336-810784189.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 03:46:47','2026-03-19 03:46:47'),
(3334,'MBR2045',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'MBR2045 is a high-current Schottky barrier rectifier diode designed for low-voltage, high-efficiency power supply applications. It is generally available in a TO-220 package, which provides good heat dissipation and allows easy mounting on a heat sink for improved thermal performance. The diode typically supports a maximum reverse voltage of about 45 volts and can handle high forward current up to around 20 amperes, making it suitable for output rectification in switched-mode power supplies.','The MBR2045 also features fast switching characteristics, enabling reliable performance in high-frequency applications such as DC-DC converters, inverters, battery chargers, and power regulators. It is often used as a dual rectifier diode, commonly configured in center-tap rectification circuits. The device provides stable operation under high current conditions when proper heat sinking and PCB layout are maintained. Correct polarity and proper mounting insulation should be ensured during installation. Because of its high efficiency, rugged design, and wide availability, the MBR2045 is widely used in industrial equipment, computer power supplies, and various consumer electronic power systems.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773892268496-867031233.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 03:51:08','2026-03-19 03:51:08'),
(3335,'MBR3045',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'MBR3045 is a high-current Schottky barrier rectifier diode mainly used in low-voltage, high-efficiency power supply circuits. It is usually available in a TO-220 package, which allows effective heat dissipation and easy mounting on heat sinks for reliable operation under heavy load conditions. This diode typically supports a maximum reverse voltage of about 45 volts and can handle high forward current up to around 30 amperes, making it suitable for medium to high-power rectification stages.','The MBR3045 provides a very low forward voltage drop, which helps reduce power loss and heat generation, thereby improving overall system efficiency. Due to its fast switching characteristics, it is widely used in SMPS output rectification, DC-DC converters, inverters, battery chargers, and power regulation circuits. The device is commonly designed as a dual common-cathode rectifier, allowing flexible configuration in center-tap transformer applications. Its rugged construction ensures stable performance in industrial and consumer electronic equipment. Proper heat sink usage and correct polarity connection are important to prevent thermal damage and ensure long service life. Because of its high efficiency, durability, and wide availability, the MBR3045 is a popular choice in computer power supplies, solar power systems, and other high-current DC power applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773892368236-846413605.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 03:52:48','2026-03-19 03:52:48'),
(3336,'MBR3060',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'MBR3060 is a high-current Schottky barrier rectifier diode designed for efficient rectification in low-voltage and high-frequency power supply circuits. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, which enables effective heat dissipation and easy mounting on heat sinks for improved thermal performance. This diode typically supports a maximum reverse voltage of about 60 volts and can handle forward current up to around 30 amperes, making it suitable for medium to high-power applications.','It also features fast switching characteristics, allowing reliable operation in high-frequency circuits such as switched-mode power supplies, DC-DC converters, battery chargers, solar inverters, and power regulators. The device is usually configured as a dual rectifier (common cathode), enabling flexible design in center-tap rectification stages. Its rugged construction ensures stable performance under heavy load and varying temperature conditions. Proper heat sink installation and correct polarity connection are important to prevent overheating and extend the component’s service life. Due to its high efficiency, durability, and wide availability, the MBR3060 is widely used in computer SMPS units, industrial power modules, and other high-current DC power systems.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773892458847-51742062.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 03:54:18','2026-03-19 03:54:18'),
(3337,'MBR20100',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'MBR20100 is a high-performance Schottky barrier rectifier diode designed for efficient power rectification in low-to-medium voltage power supply applications. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, which allows easy mounting on a heat sink and provides good thermal dissipation during high current operation. This diode typically supports a maximum reverse voltage of around 100 volts and a forward current rating of about 20 amperes, making it suitable for SMPS output stages and DC power distribution circuits.','The MBR20100 offers a very low forward voltage drop, which helps minimize power loss and improves overall system efficiency. Due to its fast switching capability, it performs well in high-frequency applications such as DC-DC converters, battery chargers, solar power systems, and inverters. The device is generally configured as a dual common-cathode rectifier, allowing flexible use in center-tap rectification circuits. Its rugged design ensures reliable performance under varying load and temperature conditions. Proper heat sink usage and correct polarity connection are essential for safe and long-term operation. Because of its high efficiency, stable characteristics, and wide availability, the MBR20100 is widely used in industrial equipment, computer power supplies, and various consumer electronic power systems.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773892539663-550486891.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 03:55:39','2026-03-19 03:55:39'),
(3338,'MBR20200',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'MBR20200 is a high-voltage Schottky barrier rectifier diode designed for efficient power rectification in switched-mode power supplies and high-frequency converter circuits. It is commonly available in a TO-220 package, which allows effective heat dissipation and easy mounting on heat sinks for reliable operation at high current levels. This diode typically supports a maximum reverse voltage of about 200 volts and can handle forward current up to around 20 amperes, making it suitable for medium-power rectification stages. One of its key advantages is the low forward voltage drop, which helps reduce power loss and improves overall system efficiency.','The MBR20200 also features fast switching characteristics, enabling stable performance in high-frequency applications such as DC-DC converters, inverters, battery chargers, solar power systems, and SMPS output rectification. It is usually configured as a dual common-cathode rectifier, allowing flexible use in center-tap transformer designs. The device provides reliable operation under varying load and temperature conditions when proper heat sinking is used. Correct polarity connection and adequate PCB layout spacing are important for safe installation. Because of its rugged construction, efficiency, and wide availability, the MBR20200 is widely used in industrial power modules, computer SMPS units, and other high-current DC power circuits.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773892644468-655024265.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 03:57:24','2026-03-19 03:57:24'),
(3339,'2N2646',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'2N2646 is a well-known Unijunction Transistor (UJT) used mainly for timing, triggering, and pulse generation applications in electronic circuits. It is typically available in a compact TO-92 package, which makes it convenient for PCB mounting and breadboard prototyping. The device operates on the principle of negative resistance characteristics, allowing it to generate stable pulses and oscillations in relaxation oscillator circuits. The 2N2646 is widely used in SCR and TRIAC triggering circuits, phase control systems, and timing control units','It features three terminals known as Emitter (E), Base-1 (B1), and Base-2 (B2), which are used for controlling conduction and pulse generation. Due to its simple construction and reliable operation, it is suitable for educational, industrial, and hobby electronics projects. The transistor requires only a few external components to build oscillator or triggering circuits, making circuit design easy and economical. It provides stable switching performance over a wide range of supply voltages and temperatures. Proper resistor and capacitor selection is important for accurate timing operation. Care should be taken to avoid exceeding maximum emitter voltage and power dissipation limits. Because of its low cost, durability, and ease of use, the 2N2646 remains popular in waveform generation and controlled switching applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773892720952-37836445.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 03:58:40','2026-03-19 03:58:40'),
(3340,'2N2907',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'2N2907 is a widely used PNP bipolar junction transistor (BJT) designed for general-purpose switching and amplification applications. It is commonly available in a compact TO-92 package, which makes it suitable for PCB mounting as well as breadboard prototyping. This transistor can handle moderate collector current and voltage, making it useful in low-power control and signal processing circuits. The 2N2907 provides good current gain and reliable switching characteristics, allowing efficient operation in digital and analog electronic designs','It is frequently used in audio amplifier stages, relay and LED driver circuits, small motor control, and signal amplification applications. The device has three terminals — Emitter, Base, and Collector — which makes circuit connections simple and easy to understand. Because it is a PNP transistor, it conducts when the base is driven to a lower potential than the emitter. Proper base resistor selection is important to control base current and ensure stable performance. When used near maximum ratings, suitable heat dissipation and correct biasing should be provided. The 2N2907 is valued for its low cost, easy availability, and dependable performance, making it a popular choice in educational projects, consumer electronics, and industrial control circuits.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773892796787-728199860.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 03:59:56','2026-03-19 03:59:56'),
(3341,'A1015',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'A1015, also known as 2SA1015, is a low-noise PNP bipolar junction transistor widely used in small signal amplification and switching circuits. It is commonly available in a compact TO-92 package, which makes it suitable for PCB mounting and breadboard prototyping. This transistor is designed to handle moderate collector-emitter voltage (around 50V) and low to medium collector current, making it ideal for signal processing applications. The A1015 provides good current gain and low noise characteristics, which help improve audio quality in pre-amplifier and tone control circuits','It is frequently used in audio amplifier stages, oscillator circuits, signal amplification, and general-purpose switching applications. The device has three terminals — Emitter, Base, and Collector — allowing simple circuit design and easy replacement. Because it is a PNP transistor, conduction occurs when the base voltage is lower than the emitter voltage. Proper base biasing and current limiting resistors should be used to ensure stable operation and long device life. Adequate heat dissipation may be required when operating near maximum ratings. Due to its reliable performance, low cost, and wide availability, the A1015 is commonly used in consumer electronics, educational kits, and hobby electronic projects.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773892964228-92438565.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 04:02:44','2026-03-19 04:02:44'),
(3342,'2SC945',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'C945, also known as 2SC945, is a general-purpose NPN bipolar junction transistor widely used in small signal amplification and switching applications. It is commonly available in a compact TO-92 package, making it suitable for PCB mounting as well as breadboard prototyping. This transistor is designed to handle moderate collector-emitter voltage (around 50V) and low to medium collector current, which makes it ideal for signal processing and control circuits. The C945 offers good current gain and low noise performance, allowing it to be effectively used in audio pre-amplifier stages, tone control circuits, and oscillator designs.','It is also frequently used in relay drivers, LED switching circuits, small motor control, and digital logic interfacing. The device has three terminals — Collector, Base, and Emitter — which makes circuit design simple and easy for beginners and professionals. Proper base resistor selection is important to control base current and maintain stable operation. When used near maximum ratings, suitable heat dissipation and correct biasing should be ensured. Due to its low cost, easy availability, and dependable performance, the C945 transistor is commonly found in consumer electronics, DIY electronics kits, and educational projects.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773893088588-927491929.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 04:04:48','2026-03-19 04:04:48'),
(3343,'2N6107',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'2N6107 is a PNP silicon power transistor designed for medium-to-high power amplification and switching applications in electronic circuits. It is typically available in a TO-220 package, which allows efficient heat dissipation and convenient mounting on heat sinks for reliable operation at higher load conditions. This transistor can withstand relatively high collector-emitter voltage (around 70–80V) and supports higher collector current, making it suitable for power control stages','The 2N6107 provides good current gain and stable switching performance, which helps improve efficiency in regulator and driver circuits. It is widely used in audio power amplifiers, voltage regulator circuits, motor control systems, inverter stages, and general power switching applications. The device features a simple three-terminal configuration — Base, Collector, and Emitter, enabling straightforward circuit design and servicing. Proper base biasing and current-limiting resistors should be used to ensure safe and stable operation. Adequate heat sinking is recommended when the transistor is operated near its maximum ratings to prevent thermal damage. Due to its rugged construction, dependable performance, and wide availability, the 2N6107 is commonly used in industrial equipment, consumer electronics, and hobby power projects.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773893410936-776926019.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 04:10:10','2026-03-19 04:10:10'),
(3344,'28C64',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'28C64 is a non-volatile parallel EEPROM memory IC that provides 64 kilobits (8K × 8 bytes) of data storage capacity. It is widely used in microprocessor and microcontroller-based systems to store program data, configuration settings, lookup tables, and calibration values. The device retains stored information even when the power supply is turned off, making it suitable for permanent or semi-permanent data storage applications. The 28C64 usually operates with a standard 5-volt power supply and supports fast read and write operations through its parallel interface. It features multiple address lines for memory location selection and bidirectional data lines for reading and writing data','Control signals such as Chip Enable (CE), Output Enable (OE), and Write Enable (WE) are used to manage memory access. Unlike older EPROM devices, this EEPROM allows electrical byte-level erase and programming, eliminating the need for ultraviolet light erasing. The IC offers high endurance and long data retention, ensuring reliable performance over thousands of write cycles. Proper timing control and stable voltage supply are important for correct operation. The 28C64 is commonly available in DIP packages, making it easy to use in educational kits, industrial control systems, embedded projects, and digital storage circuits.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773893860871-601437631.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 04:17:40','2026-03-19 04:17:40'),
(3345,'AT89C55',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'89C55 (commonly AT89C55) is an 8-bit 8051-based microcontroller widely used in embedded control and digital electronics applications. It features Flash programmable memory, allowing users to easily write, erase, and reprogram application code. The device typically provides 20KB of Flash program memory, along with RAM, timers, serial communication interface, and multiple I/O ports. It operates with a standard 5V power supply and supports clock frequencies suitable for general-purpose control tasks.','The 89C55 includes four 8-bit parallel I/O ports, enabling easy interfacing with sensors, displays, relays, motors, and other digital components. Built-in peripherals such as timers/counters, UART serial port, and interrupt system help simplify embedded system design. It is commonly used in industrial automation systems, home appliance control, robotics, instrumentation, and educational development kits. The IC is generally available in DIP and SMD packages, making it suitable for both prototyping and mass production. Proper crystal oscillator connection and reset circuitry are required for reliable operation. Due to its stable performance, easy programming features, and wide availability, the 89C55 remains popular among students, hobbyists, and engineers working with classic 8051 architecture projects.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773894052215-466544936.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 04:20:52','2026-03-19 04:20:52'),
(3346,'AT89C2051',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'89C2051 (commonly AT89C2051) is a compact 8-bit 8051-based microcontroller designed for small embedded control applications. It contains 2KB of Flash programmable program memory, allowing easy development, modification, and reprogramming of embedded software. The device operates with a 5-volt power supply and supports standard crystal oscillator clock circuits for stable timing performance. It provides 15 programmable I/O lines, enabling direct interfacing with switches, LEDs, sensors, displays, relays, and other digital components.','The microcontroller includes important built-in peripherals such as timers/counters, interrupt system, and full-duplex serial communication (UART), which simplify embedded system design. Due to its small 20-pin package, the 89C2051 is ideal for compact circuit layouts and low-cost control systems. It is widely used in home appliance controllers, automation circuits, security systems, instrumentation, robotics projects, and educational development kits. Proper reset circuitry and oscillator connections are required for reliable operation. The IC offers low power consumption and stable performance, making it suitable for battery-operated and portable electronic devices. Because of its easy programming features, dependable operation, and wide availability, the 89C2051 remains popular in both hobby and industrial embedded applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773894191847-182372660.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 04:23:11','2026-03-19 04:23:11'),
(3347,'AT89C4051',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'89C4051 (commonly AT89C4051) is a compact 8-bit microcontroller based on the 8051 architecture, designed for small and medium embedded control applications. It features 4KB of Flash programmable program memory, allowing easy development, modification, and reprogramming of application code. The device typically operates with a 5-volt power supply and uses an external crystal oscillator to generate the system clock for reliable timing operation. It provides around 15 programmable input/output pins, enabling direct interfacing with switches, LEDs, relays, sensors, displays, and other digital components.','The microcontroller includes useful built-in peripherals such as timers/counters, interrupt system, and full-duplex serial communication (UART), which help simplify embedded system design. Because of its small 20-pin package, the 89C4051 is suitable for compact PCB layouts and low-cost control systems. It is widely used in home appliance controllers, industrial automation circuits, security devices, robotics projects, instrumentation, and educational development kits. Proper reset circuitry and stable clock connections are necessary to ensure dependable performance. The IC offers low power consumption, stable operation, and easy programming capability, making it a popular choice for students, hobbyists, and engineers working with classic 8051-based designs.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773894274235-81316693.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 04:24:34','2026-03-19 04:24:34'),
(3348,'AT89S8253',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'89S8253 (commonly AT89S8253) is an advanced 8-bit microcontroller based on the 8051 architecture, designed for embedded control and automation applications. It features 12KB of in-system programmable Flash memory, allowing program code to be written, erased, and updated without removing the IC from the circuit. The device also includes internal EEPROM data memory, which is useful for storing configuration data and system parameters even when power is removed. It operates with a 5-volt supply and supports standard crystal oscillator clock circuits for stable timing performance','The microcontroller provides 32 programmable I/O lines through four parallel ports, enabling easy interfacing with displays, sensors, relays, motors, and communication modules. Built-in peripherals such as timers/counters, interrupt controller, watchdog timer, and full-duplex serial UART help simplify system design. It also supports SPI programming interface, making firmware updates convenient in development and production environments. The 89S8253 is widely used in industrial automation systems, instrumentation, robotics, consumer electronic products, and educational development kits. Proper reset circuitry, clock connections, and power supply decoupling are important for reliable operation. Because of its stable performance, flexible memory features, and easy programming capability, the 89S8253 remains a practical choice for many classic 8051-based embedded applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1773894356587-649892750.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 04:25:56','2026-03-19 04:25:56'),
(3349,'Coaxial Cable with BNC Connector',NULL,NULL,NULL,399.00,'Coaxial cables with BNC connectors are available in different types such as RG59 and RG6, with RG59 being most common for CCTV installations due to its flexibility and adequate performance over shorter distances, while RG6 is used for longer runs with better shielding. These cables are known for their durability, resistance to electromagnetic interference (EMI), and ease of installation.','BNC connectors are typically made of metal with nickel or gold plating to enhance conductivity and corrosion resistance. They are compatible with a wide range of devices including cameras, video recorders, oscilloscopes, and test equipment.','Always ensure proper cable length and quality to avoid signal degradation, especially in long-distance installations. Secure connections are essential—loose BNC connectors can cause signal loss or distortion. It is recommended to use high-quality shielded cables in environments with high electrical noise. Regular inspection of connectors and cable insulation helps maintain performance and longevity.',NULL,'products/1773919748530-102380074.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 11:29:08','2026-03-19 11:29:08'),
(3350,'Female VGA Connector',NULL,NULL,NULL,399.00,'Female VGA Connector is a 15-pin analog interface port used to receive video signals from devices such as computers, laptops, and media players. It is commonly known as a HD-15 (High Density D-subminiature) connector and features three rows of five holes (pins) arranged in a trapezoidal shape. The female VGA connector is typically found on monitors, projectors, and extension cables, allowing a male VGA plug to connect securely.','Female VGA connectors are widely used in legacy systems and are usually color-coded blue for easy identification. They support various resolutions depending on the cable quality and hardware, commonly up to 1080p, though signal quality may degrade over longer distances. The connector includes screw holes on both sides to secure the connection firmly, preventing accidental disconnection.','VGA does not carry audio signals, so separate audio cables are required when sound transmission is needed. Despite being largely replaced by HDMI and DisplayPort, VGA is still used in many industrial, educational, and older office setups.',NULL,'products/1773921889857-735842220.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 12:04:49','2026-03-19 12:04:49'),
(3351,'Male VGA Connector',NULL,NULL,NULL,399.00,'Male VGA Connector is a 15-pin analog plug used to transmit video signals from a source device such as a computer, CPU, or laptop to a display device like a monitor or projector. It is also known as an HD-15 (High Density D-sub) connector and features three rows of exposed pins arranged in a trapezoidal shape. The male VGA connector is typically attached to the end of a VGA cable and is designed to fit securely into a female VGA port, ensuring proper alignment and stable signal transmission.','Male VGA connectors are commonly found on VGA cables and older graphics cards. They are usually blue in color for easy identification and include two side screws that allow the connector to be tightened into the female port, preventing accidental disconnection. These connectors carry analog video signals only and support various display resolutions, though performance depends on cable quality and length. VGA connections are widely used in older desktop systems, projectors, and industrial display setups.','Always handle the connector carefully to avoid bending or breaking the pins, as damaged pins can cause display issues such as missing colors or no signal. Ensure the connector is properly aligned before inserting it into the port. Avoid excessive force while connecting or disconnecting.',NULL,'products/1773922434812-139771412.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 12:13:54','2026-03-19 12:13:54'),
(3352,'RS232 Male Connector',NULL,NULL,NULL,399.00,'RS232 Male Connector is a standard serial communication interface plug used to transmit data between devices such as computers, modems, industrial machines, and networking equipment. It is commonly available in a DB9 (9-pin) or sometimes DB25 (25-pin) configuration, with the DB9 being the most widely used. The male connector features exposed metal pins arranged in a D-shaped (D-subminiature) housing, which ensures correct orientation and secure connection when plugged into a corresponding female port.','RS232 male connectors operate using voltage signals (typically between +3V to +15V and -3V to -15V) to represent binary data. They are widely used in legacy systems, industrial automation, POS machines, CNC equipment, and embedded systems.','The connector includes screw locks on either side to secure the connection and prevent accidental disconnection. RS232 communication is relatively slow compared to modern interfaces, typically supporting data rates up to 115.2 kbps, but it is highly reliable for short-distance communication (usually up to 15 meters).',NULL,'products/1773922688074-559425907.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 12:18:08','2026-03-19 12:18:08'),
(3353,'RS232 Female Connector',NULL,NULL,NULL,399.00,'RS232 Female Connector is a standard serial communication port designed to receive data connections from an RS232 male connector. It is most commonly found in a DB9 (9-pin) configuration, though older systems may use a DB25 (25-pin) version. The female connector features 9 holes (sockets) arranged in a D-shaped (D-subminiature) layout, ensuring proper alignment and secure mating with the corresponding male plug.','RS232 female connectors are typically mounted on devices such as PCs, PLCs, modems, POS systems, and embedded hardware. They use voltage-based signaling (positive and negative voltage levels) to transmit binary data asynchronously. The connector includes threaded screw locks on both sides, allowing the attached male connector to be tightened securely for stable communication.','Always match the correct pin configuration (straight-through or null modem) depending on the communication requirement. Ensure the connector is clean and free from dust or corrosion to maintain proper contact. Tighten the screws firmly to avoid loose connections that can cause data errors. Avoid applying excessive force while connecting or disconnecting.',NULL,'products/1773922836417-236353770.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-19 12:20:36','2026-03-19 12:20:36'),
(3354,'Black Single Strand Wire',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'Black Single Strand Wire is a type of electrical wire made from a single solid conductor, usually composed of copper or aluminum, and covered with a black insulating layer such as PVC. It is widely used in low-voltage electrical installations, circuit wiring, control panels, and basic electronic applications where a stable and secure connection is required. The solid core provides better mechanical strength and ensures minimal signal loss, making it suitable for fixed wiring rather than flexible movements.','The black color is often used for phase or live connections in certain wiring standards, though color codes may vary by region. This wire is easy to strip, solder, and terminate, making it convenient for electricians and technicians.','However, due to its rigidity, it is not ideal for applications requiring frequent bending or movement. Overall, Black Single Strand Wire is reliable, durable, and commonly used in residential, commercial, and industrial electrical systems.',NULL,'products/1774339409030-708881307.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-24 08:03:29','2026-03-24 08:03:29'),
(3355,'Red Single Strand Wire',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'Red Single Strand Wire is a solid-core electrical wire made from a single conductor, typically copper or aluminum, and insulated with a red-colored PVC or similar protective coating. It is commonly used in electrical wiring, electronic circuits, control panels, and power distribution systems where a consistent and stable connection is required. The red color is generally used to indicate live or positive connections, especially in DC circuits and battery systems, though color coding may vary depending on standards.','Due to its single solid core, the wire offers good conductivity, low resistance, and strong mechanical stability, making it suitable for fixed installations. It is easy to strip and connect, which simplifies installation work for technicians and electricians.','However, it is less flexible compared to multi-strand wires and is not ideal for applications involving frequent bending or movement. Overall, Red Single Strand Wire is a durable and efficient choice for reliable electrical connections in various applications.',NULL,'products/1774339588175-722858404.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-24 08:06:28','2026-03-24 08:06:28'),
(3356,'Yellow Multi Strand Wire',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'Yellow Multi Strand Wire is an electrical wire composed of multiple thin strands of copper or aluminum bundled together and covered with a yellow insulating layer, typically made of PVC or similar material. This type of wire is widely used in electrical systems, control panels, automotive wiring, and electronic circuits where flexibility and durability are essential.','The multi-strand construction provides excellent flexibility, making it suitable for applications that involve frequent bending, vibration, or movement without breaking. The yellow color is often used for specific identification purposes, such as signaling, grounding, or phase indication, depending on wiring standards and regional practices.','It offers good conductivity, reduced risk of breakage, and improved performance in dynamic conditions compared to single strand wires. Additionally, it is easy to route through tight spaces and is convenient for installation in complex wiring setups. Overall, Yellow Multi Strand Wire is a reliable, flexible, and efficient solution for both industrial and domestic electrical applications.',NULL,'products/1774339728155-889165083.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-24 08:08:48','2026-03-24 08:08:48'),
(3357,'Black Multi Strand Wire',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'Black Multi Strand Wire is an electrical wire made up of multiple fine strands of copper or aluminum conductors twisted together and coated with a black insulating material, typically PVC. This construction provides high flexibility and durability, making it ideal for applications where the wire needs to bend, move, or withstand vibrations, such as in control panels, automotive wiring, appliances, and electronic circuits.','The multi-strand design reduces the chances of breakage and ensures consistent electrical performance even under dynamic conditions. The black color is commonly used for phase, live, or neutral connections depending on regional wiring standards and application requirements.','It offers excellent conductivity, easy handling, and smooth installation, especially in tight or complex wiring spaces. Overall, Black Multi Strand Wire is a versatile and dependable choice for both residential and industrial electrical systems where flexibility and strength are important.',NULL,'products/1774339839353-676211400.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-24 08:10:39','2026-03-24 08:10:39'),
(3358,'Red Multi strand Wire',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'Red Multi Strand Wire is an electrical conductor made up of multiple fine strands of copper or aluminum twisted together and insulated with a red-colored PVC or similar protective coating. This type of wire is widely used in electrical systems, battery connections, automotive wiring, control panels, and electronic circuits where flexibility and durability are important.','he multi-strand construction allows the wire to bend easily and withstand continuous movement or vibration without breaking, making it more reliable than single strand wires in dynamic applications. The red color is typically used to indicate live or positive connections, especially in DC circuits and power supply systems, though color standards may vary by region.','It offers good conductivity, low resistance, and ease of installation, even in tight or complex wiring setups. Overall, Red Multi Strand Wire is a flexible, durable, and efficient solution for a wide range of residential, commercial, and industrial electrical applications.',NULL,'products/1774339947587-473045309.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-24 08:12:27','2026-03-24 08:12:27'),
(3359,'Green Multi Strand Wire',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'Green Multi Strand Wire is an electrical wire made of multiple fine strands of copper or aluminum twisted together and covered with a green insulating layer, usually PVC or similar material. It is commonly used in electrical installations, control panels, and electronic systems where flexibility and durability are required. The multi-strand construction provides excellent flexibility, allowing the wire to bend easily and withstand vibrations or repeated movement without breaking.','The green color is typically used to represent grounding or earthing connections in most wiring standards, ensuring safety in electrical systems by directing fault currents safely to the ground.','It offers good conductivity, reduced risk of damage, and easy handling during installation, especially in tight or complex spaces. Overall, Green Multi Strand Wire is a reliable, flexible, and essential component for safe and efficient electrical grounding and wiring applications.',NULL,'products/1774340048016-181503781.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-24 08:14:08','2026-03-24 08:14:08'),
(3360,'Rainbow Wire',NULL,NULL,NULL,149.00,'Rainbow wire refers to a bundle of multicolored electrical jumper wires commonly used in electronics and DIY projects. These wires are typically arranged in a ribbon format or separated strands, making circuit connections easy and organized. They are widely used with breadboards, Arduino, Raspberry Pi, and other development boards for prototyping without soldering.','The different colors help users quickly identify connections such as power, ground, and signal lines, reducing wiring mistakes. Rainbow wires are available in various types like Male-to-Male, Male-to-Female, and Female-to-Female, depending on connector requirements.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774340791239-553005119.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-24 08:26:31','2026-03-24 08:26:31'),
(3361,'Blue Multi Strand Wire',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'Blue multi-strand wire is a flexible electrical wire made of many thin copper strands twisted together and covered with blue insulation. It is widely used in electronics projects, internal wiring, power distribution, and domestic electrical installations due to its durability and ease of handling.The blue color is typically used for neutral wiring identification or organized circuit layout, helping electricians and hobbyists avoid wiring mistakes.','Multi-strand wires provide better flexibility and conductivity compared to single-core wires, making them suitable for connections that may bend or move frequently. They are usually insulated with PVC or silicone, which offers electrical safety and protection from heat or mechanical damage.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774341223550-883492348.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-24 08:33:43','2026-03-24 08:33:43'),
(3362,'DC Toy Motor(Red)',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'A DC Toy Motor (Red) is a small, low-voltage electric motor commonly used in toys, hobby electronics, and educational projects. It is designed with a compact plastic body (usually red in color for easy identification) and a metal shaft that rotates when electrical power is applied. These motors typically operate on 3V to 6V DC supply, making them safe and convenient for battery-powered applications such as toy cars, mini fans, and beginner robotics.','This motor works on the principle of electromagnetism, where current flowing through the internal coil generates a magnetic field that interacts with permanent magnets inside the motor, causing the shaft to rotate. Due to its simple construction, it is widely used by students and hobbyists for learning basic motor operation and building DIY projects.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774431226127-7052205.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-25 09:33:46','2026-03-25 09:33:46'),
(3363,'Double shaft DC Toy Motor(Red)',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'A Double Shaft DC Motor (Red) is a compact electric motor similar to a standard DC toy motor but with shafts extending from both ends of the motor. It operates on low voltage (typically 3V to 6V DC) and is widely used in robotics, mechanical models, and DIY projects where motion is required on both sides of the motor.','This motor works on the same electromagnetic principle as a regular DC motor. When a DC voltage is applied to its terminals, the internal rotor spins, causing both shafts to rotate simultaneously. The dual-shaft design makes it highly useful for applications that require balanced movement, dual output, or sensor integration.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774431369515-589411825.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-25 09:36:09','2026-03-25 09:36:09'),
(3364,'Dynamo Motor',NULL,NULL,NULL,399.00,'A Dynamo Motor is an electrical device that converts mechanical energy into electrical energy. Unlike a typical DC motor (which uses electricity to produce motion), a dynamo works in reverse—it generates electricity when its shaft is rotated. Dynamos are commonly used in bicycles, hand-crank generators, and small power generation systems.','The working principle of a dynamo is based on electromagnetic induction, where a rotating coil inside a magnetic field produces electric current. When the shaft of the dynamo is turned manually or by mechanical force (like a wheel or turbine), it generates a DC voltage output, which can be used to power small devices such as LEDs, batteries, or sensors.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774432302445-96163298.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-25 09:51:42','2026-03-25 09:51:42'),
(3365,'Water Solenoid Valve',NULL,NULL,NULL,499.00,'A Water Solenoid Valve is an electrically controlled valve used to regulate the flow of water automatically. It operates using an electromagnetic coil (solenoid) that opens or closes the valve when electrical power is applied. These valves are widely used in automation systems, irrigation, water dispensers, washing machines, and industrial fluid control applications.','A Water Solenoid Valve is an electrically controlled valve used to regulate the flow of water automatically. It operates using an electromagnetic coil (solenoid) that opens or closes the valve when electrical power is applied. These valves are widely used in automation systems, irrigation, water dispensers, washing machines, and industrial fluid control applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774437022651-879167099.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-25 11:10:22','2026-03-25 11:10:22'),
(3366,'L-Type Bo Motor',NULL,NULL,NULL,399.00,'An L-Type BO Motor (Battery Operated Motor) is a right-angle geared DC motor commonly used in robotics and DIY vehicle projects. Unlike standard BO motors, this motor has an L-shaped (90°) gearbox design, where the motor shaft and output shaft are positioned at a right angle. This unique structure allows better space management and flexible mounting in compact robotic designs.','The motor operates on low voltage (typically 3V to 12V DC) and includes an internal gear mechanism that reduces speed while increasing torque. This makes it ideal for driving wheels and carrying loads in small robots and automated systems.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,'active','2026-03-25 11:57:21','2026-03-25 11:57:21'),
(3367,'8Ch 5V Relay Module',NULL,NULL,NULL,799.00,'An 8 Channel 5V Relay Module is an electronic switching board that allows a microcontroller such as Arduino, Raspberry Pi, or other logic systems to control up to 8 high-power electrical devices simultaneously. Each channel consists of a relay that acts as an electrically operated switch, enabling safe control of AC or DC loads using low-voltage signals (5V).','This module is widely used in home automation, industrial control systems, IoT projects, and robotics, where multiple devices like lights, fans, motors, or appliances need to be controlled programmatically.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,'active','2026-03-25 13:04:17','2026-03-25 13:04:17'),
(3368,'12V Sugar Cube Relay',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'A 12V Sugar Cube Relay is a compact electromechanical switching device widely used in electronic circuits to control high-power loads using a low-voltage control signal. It gets the name “sugar cube” due to its small cube-shaped plastic casing, making it ideal for PCB mounting in compact designs. These relays are commonly found in automation systems, power control circuits, and embedded electronics.','The relay operates using a 12V DC coil. When voltage is applied to the coil, it creates a magnetic field that pulls an internal switch, changing the connection between its terminals. This allows a low-power circuit (like a microcontroller) to safely control high-voltage or high-current devices.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774444731136-933817029.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-25 13:18:22','2026-03-25 13:18:51'),
(3369,'12v Power Relay',NULL,NULL,NULL,199.00,'A 12V Power Relay is an electromechanical switching device designed to control high-current or high-voltage loads using a 12V DC control signal. It is commonly used in automotive systems, industrial control panels, home automation, and power switching applications. Compared to small relays (like sugar cube relays), power relays are built to handle higher current loads (10A to 40A or more).','When 12V is applied to the relay coil, it creates a magnetic field that moves an internal armature, switching the contacts from one position to another. This allows a low-power circuit (like a switch, microcontroller, or sensor) to safely control heavy electrical devices.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774444959697-918704280.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-25 13:22:39','2026-03-25 13:22:39'),
(3370,'Buzzer Module',NULL,NULL,NULL,399.00,'A Buzzer Module is a small electronic sound-producing device commonly used in embedded systems, alarms, and notification circuits. It typically consists of a piezoelectric buzzer mounted on a compact PCB along with supporting components, making it easy to interface with microcontrollers like Arduino, Raspberry Pi, or other digital systems.','The module operates on low voltage (usually 3.3V to 5V DC) and produces a beeping or buzzing sound when an electrical signal is applied. There are two main types—active buzzers, which generate sound automatically when powered, and passive buzzers, which require a frequency signal (PWM) to produce different tones.','Buzzer modules are widely used in applications such as alarm systems, timers, security devices, user alerts, and IoT projects due to their simplicity, low power consumption, compact size, and reliable performance.',NULL,'products/1774523574041-402987224.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-26 11:12:18','2026-03-26 11:12:54'),
(3371,'Arduino UNO Board',NULL,NULL,NULL,799.00,'The Arduino UNO Board is one of the most popular and widely used microcontroller boards in electronics and embedded systems. It is based on the ATmega328P microcontroller and is designed to make programming and hardware interfacing simple for beginners as well as professionals.','The board can read inputs such as sensors, buttons, or signals, and control outputs like LEDs, motors, displays, and relays. It is programmed using the Arduino IDE via a USB connection, making it easy to upload code and power the board simultaneously. Operating at 5V, the Arduino UNO provides multiple digital and analog input/output pins, allowing it to interact with a wide range of electronic components.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774524053189-363395888.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-26 11:20:53','2026-03-26 11:20:53'),
(3372,'A3144 Hall Effect Sensor',NULL,NULL,NULL,399.00,'The A3144 Hall Effect Sensor is a widely used magnetic field detection device that operates based on the Hall Effect principle. It is a digital Hall effect switch designed to detect the presence of a magnetic field and provide a simple HIGH or LOW output signal, making it easy to interface with microcontrollers like Arduino. The sensor consists of three pins—VCC, GND, and OUT—and typically operates within a voltage range of 4.5V to 24V.','When no magnetic field is present, the output remains HIGH, but when a magnet is brought near the sensor, the output switches to LOW. This sensor is known for its fast response time, reliability, and built-in protection features such as reverse polarity protection.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774531161184-193966102.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-26 13:19:21','2026-03-26 13:19:21'),
(3373,'A3144 Sensor',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'The A3144 Hall Effect Sensor is a digital magnetic field sensor widely used in electronic and embedded systems to detect the presence of a magnet. It operates based on the Hall Effect, where a voltage is generated when a magnetic field is applied perpendicular to the flow of current. The A3144 sensor has three pins—VCC (power supply), GND (ground), and OUT (output)—and typically works with a voltage range of 4.5V to 24V.','The A3144 is known for its compact size, fast switching speed, durability, and reliable performance. It is commonly used in applications such as speed detection, position sensing, proximity sensing, door sensors, and automation systems, making it a popular choice for student projects and IoT-based applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774531302812-87031474.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-26 13:21:42','2026-03-26 13:21:42'),
(3374,'Limit Switch Module',NULL,NULL,NULL,399.00,'The Limit Switch Module is an electromechanical device used to detect the physical position or movement of an object. It works by making or breaking an electrical connection when an object presses or releases the switch lever. This module typically includes a mechanical switch mounted on a small circuit board with three pins: VCC, GND, and OUT, making it easy to interface with microcontrollers like Arduino. When the switch is pressed, the output signal changes (HIGH to LOW or LOW to HIGH depending on the wiring), allowing the system to detect whether a limit or boundary has been reached.','Limit switch modules are simple, reliable, and widely used in automation systems, robotics, and safety mechanisms. They are commonly used to detect end positions in machines, such as in 3D printers, CNC machines, elevators, and conveyor systems. Because of their durability and accurate physical feedback, they are ideal for applications where precise position detection is required. Overall, the limit switch module is an essential component for controlling motion and ensuring safety in mechanical and electronic systems.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,'active','2026-03-26 13:38:14','2026-03-26 13:38:14'),
(3375,'GEONIX 128GB SSD SATA',NULL,NULL,NULL,3499.00,'The GEONIX 128GB SSD SATA is a compact and high-performance storage device designed to replace traditional hard drives in laptops and desktop computers. It uses a SATA III (6Gb/s) interface, which allows fast data transfer speeds, significantly improving system performance compared to HDDs. This SSD typically offers sequential read speeds up to around 560–570 MB/s and write speeds up to 500 MB/s, enabling quicker boot times, faster file transfers, and smooth application loading','The GEONIX 128GB SSD is suitable for everyday computing, office work, basic gaming, and upgrading older systems, offering a noticeable boost in speed and responsiveness. It also supports multiple operating systems such as Windows, Linux, and macOS, and often comes with a 3 to 5-year warranty, making it a cost-effective and dependable storage upgrade solution.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774583922619-786645643.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-27 03:58:42','2026-03-27 03:58:42'),
(3376,'Ram 8GB DDR4',NULL,NULL,NULL,6999.00,'An 8GB DDR4 RAM is a widely used computer memory module designed to improve system performance, speed, and multitasking capability in desktops and laptops. It belongs to the DDR4 (Double Data Rate 4) generation, which offers higher bandwidth and lower power consumption compared to older DDR3 memory. Typically operating at speeds ranging from 2133 MHz to 3200 MHz or higher, 8GB DDR4 RAM allows smooth handling of everyday tasks such as web browsing, office work, programming, and moderate gaming.','It works by temporarily storing data that the CPU needs quickly, resulting in faster application loading and better overall responsiveness. DDR4 RAM modules are available in different types such as DIMM for desktops and SO-DIMM for laptops, and they usually operate at a low voltage of around 1.2V, improving energy efficiency. Popular brands like Corsair, Kingston, Crucial, and ADATA offer reliable options, and this capacity is considered ideal for students, professionals, and casual users who need balanced performance without high cost',NULL,NULL,'products/1774584304069-754674302.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-27 04:05:04','2026-03-27 04:05:04'),
(3377,'DP to HDMI 4K',NULL,NULL,NULL,1499.00,'A DP to HDMI 4K adapter converts digital video and audio signals from a DisplayPort source into HDMI format, allowing compatibility between modern computers and HDMI displays. These adapters support Ultra HD resolutions like 3840×2160 (4K), depending on the version—many basic adapters support 4K at 30Hz, while advanced or active adapters support 4K at 60Hz for smoother visuals.','They are typically plug-and-play devices, requiring no additional drivers, and are widely used in desktop PCs, laptops, gaming setups, projectors, and office displays. Most DP to HDMI adapters are unidirectional, meaning they only convert from DisplayPort to HDMI',NULL,NULL,'products/1774584999250-294028149.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-27 04:16:39','2026-03-27 04:16:39'),
(3378,'DVI to VGA',NULL,NULL,NULL,499.00,'A DVI to VGA adapter is a video converter used to connect a device with a DVI (Digital Visual Interface) output to a monitor or projector that uses a VGA (Video Graphics Array) input. It is commonly used to connect modern computers or graphics cards to older display devices that only support VGA. This adapter typically has a DVI male connector on one side and a VGA female port on the other, allowing a standard VGA cable to be connected.','A DVI to VGA adapter works by converting the video signal so that devices with different display interfaces can communicate. VGA is an analog signal, while DVI can carry both analog (DVI-I) and digital (DVI-D) signals',NULL,NULL,'products/1774585511837-964982312.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-27 04:25:11','2026-03-27 04:25:11'),
(3379,'Hp 65w Blue C type Laptop Adaptor',NULL,NULL,NULL,999.00,'The HP 65W Blue Tip / USB-C Laptop Adapter is a reliable power supply designed to charge HP laptops efficiently using either USB Type-C or traditional blue-pin (4.5mm) connectors, depending on the model. This adapter delivers a maximum output of 65 watts, which is suitable for most HP laptops such as Pavilion, ProBook, EliteBook, Envy, and Spectre series. It supports fast charging technology, allowing the battery to charge quickly while also powering the laptop during use.','The adapter operates on a wide input voltage range (100–240V AC), making it ideal for both home and travel use. It provides multiple output levels such as 5V, 9V, 12V, 15V, and 20V, automatically adjusting power based on the device requirement for safe and efficient charging. Built with over-voltage, short-circuit, and thermal protection, it ensures safe operation and long-term durability.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774586182632-534116432.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-27 04:36:22','2026-03-27 04:36:22'),
(3380,'19V 3.42A C Type Laptop Adaptor',NULL,NULL,NULL,999.00,'A 19V 3.42A C-Type laptop adapter is a power supply designed to deliver approximately 65W (watts) of power (19V × 3.42A) for charging laptops and compatible devices. It converts AC mains power (100–240V) into stable DC output required by laptops. While traditional adapters with 19V 3.42A usually come with round pin connectors, modern versions use USB Type-C (PD – Power Delivery) technology, which automatically adjusts voltage levels such as 5V, 9V, 12V, 15V, and 20V depending on the device.','A 19V 3.42A (65W) USB-C laptop adapter is widely used for modern laptops, ultrabooks, and tablets that support USB-C charging. Unlike fixed 19V adapters, USB-C chargers use Power Delivery (PD) to dynamically supply the correct voltage, ensuring safe and efficient charging. Most adapters include over-voltage, over-current, and short-circuit protection, improving safety and device lifespan.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774588087737-112707796.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-27 05:08:07','2026-03-27 05:08:07'),
(3381,'90W C-Type Laptop Adaptor',NULL,NULL,NULL,1999.00,'A 90W C-Type laptop adapter is a high-power charger designed for modern laptops that support USB Type-C Power Delivery (PD). It provides up to 90 watts of power, making it suitable for high-performance laptops, ultrabooks, and some workstations that require more power than standard 45W or 65W chargers.','A 90W USB-C laptop adapter converts AC power (100–240V) into regulated DC output and uses USB-C Power Delivery technology to automatically adjust voltage levels such as 5V, 9V, 12V, 15V, and 20V, depending on the device requirement',NULL,NULL,'products/1774588265475-530831974.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-27 05:11:05','2026-03-27 05:11:05'),
(3382,'65W C-Type Laptop Adaptor',NULL,NULL,NULL,1499.00,'A 65W C-Type laptop adapter is a modern power supply designed to charge laptops and compatible devices using USB Type-C Power Delivery (PD) technology. It delivers up to 65 watts of power, making it ideal for most ultrabooks, business laptops, and mid-range devices.','A 65W USB-C laptop adapter converts AC power (100–240V) into regulated DC output and uses USB-C Power Delivery to automatically adjust voltage levels such as 5V, 9V, 12V, 15V, and 20V depending on the device requirement.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774588532331-915788931.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-03-27 05:15:32','2026-03-27 05:15:32'),
(3383,'re','re','re',NULL,11.00,'s','sa','as',NULL,NULL,0,1,'active','2026-03-27 09:25:56','2026-05-02 03:20:13'),
(3384,'Medium Bread Board',NULL,NULL,NULL,399.00,'Medium Bread Board','Medium Bread Board',NULL,NULL,'products/1774950685302-834242539.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-31 09:51:25','2026-03-31 09:51:25'),
(3385,'Dual Battery Charger',NULL,NULL,NULL,499.00,'A dual battery charger is an electronic device designed to charge two batteries simultaneously, offering convenience and efficiency for users who rely on multiple rechargeable batteries. It is commonly used for lithium-ion, NiMH, or lead-acid batteries depending on the model, and is widely applied in devices such as cameras, power tools, drones, and backup systems.','These chargers typically feature independent charging channels, allowing each battery to be monitored and charged separately for optimal performance and safety. Built-in protection mechanisms such as overcharge protection, short-circuit protection, temperature control, and reverse polarity protection ensure safe operation and extend battery life.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774951996153-725987318.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-31 10:13:16','2026-03-31 10:13:16'),
(3386,'Single Battery charger',NULL,NULL,NULL,399.00,'A single battery charger is a compact and efficient device designed to charge one rechargeable battery at a time. It is commonly used for various battery types such as lithium-ion, nickel-metal hydride (NiMH), and lead-acid batteries, depending on the charger model. These chargers are widely used in applications like mobile devices, cameras, power tools, and small electronic gadgets.','A single battery charger typically provides stable current and voltage to ensure safe and effective charging, helping to maintain battery health and extend its lifespan. Most models include safety features such as overcharge protection, short-circuit protection, and temperature control to prevent damage. Additionally, LED indicators or simple display systems are often included to show charging status, making the device easy to use for everyday applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774952189210-324440037.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-31 10:16:29','2026-03-31 10:16:29'),
(3387,'Single Side Battery Charger',NULL,NULL,NULL,499.00,'A single battery charger is a compact and efficient device designed to charge one rechargeable battery at a time. It is commonly used for various battery types such as lithium-ion, nickel-metal hydride (NiMH), and lead-acid batteries, depending on the charger model. These chargers are widely used in applications like mobile devices, cameras, power tools, and small electronic gadgets.','A single battery charger typically provides stable current and voltage to ensure safe and effective charging, helping to maintain battery health and extend its lifespan. Most models include safety features such as overcharge protection, short-circuit protection, and temperature control to prevent damage.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774952304748-677791328.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-31 10:18:24','2026-03-31 10:18:24'),
(3388,'12V DC Cooling Fan',NULL,NULL,NULL,499.00,'A 12V DC cooling fan is an electrical device designed to provide efficient airflow for cooling electronic components and enclosed systems. It operates on a 12-volt direct current (DC) power supply, making it ideal for use in computers, power supplies, inverters, automotive applications, and various electronic projects. These fans are typically available in different sizes such as 40mm, 60mm, 80mm, and 120mm, allowing them to fit a wide range of cooling requirements.','Most 12V DC fans use brushless motor technology, which ensures low noise operation, longer lifespan, and reduced maintenance compared to traditional fans. They are easy to install and usually come with two or three wires for power and speed control. Built for continuous operation, these fans help maintain optimal temperatures, prevent overheating, and improve the overall performance and durability of electronic devices.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,'active','2026-03-31 11:28:51','2026-03-31 11:28:51'),
(3389,'24V DC Cooling fan',NULL,NULL,NULL,499.00,'24V DC cooling fan is a high-performance airflow device designed to cool electrical and electronic systems that operate on a 24-volt direct current power supply. It is widely used in industrial equipment, control panels, telecom systems, automation setups, and heavy-duty electronics where stable and continuous cooling is required. These fans are commonly built with brushless motor technology, ensuring efficient operation, low power consumption, reduced noise, and a longer service life.','Available in various sizes and airflow capacities, 24V DC fans can effectively dissipate heat from components, preventing overheating and improving system reliability. They typically come with two or three wires for power connection and optional speed monitoring. With features like durable construction, high airflow output, and built-in protection against overheating and voltage fluctuations, 24V DC cooling fans are ideal for demanding environments and continuous operation.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774956770500-245267545.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-31 11:32:50','2026-03-31 11:32:50'),
(3390,'5V DC Cooling Fan',NULL,NULL,NULL,499.00,'A 5V DC cooling fan is a compact and energy-efficient device used to provide cooling for small electronic systems and portable devices. It operates on a 5-volt direct current power supply, making it ideal for applications such as USB-powered gadgets, microcontroller boards, Raspberry Pi projects, routers, and small enclosures. These fans are typically designed with brushless motor technology, ensuring low noise operation, longer lifespan, and minimal power consumption.','Due to their small size and lightweight construction, 5V DC fans are easy to install and suitable for tight spaces where effective heat dissipation is required. They usually come with simple two-wire or USB connections for easy power supply. By maintaining proper airflow, 5V DC cooling fans help prevent overheating, enhance device performance, and extend the life of sensitive electronic components.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774956854429-322345068.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-31 11:34:14','2026-03-31 11:34:14'),
(3391,'2 AA Battery Holder With Cover',NULL,NULL,NULL,199.00,'A 2 AA battery holder with cover is a compact and protective enclosure designed to securely hold two AA batteries while providing a stable power supply for electronic devices and DIY projects. It is typically made from durable plastic and features metal spring contacts to ensure reliable electrical connectivity. The built-in cover helps protect the batteries from dust, moisture, and accidental contact, enhancing safety and durability during use.','These holders are commonly used in applications such as remote controls, toys, LED projects, Arduino circuits, and portable devices. Most models come with pre-attached wires or terminals for easy connection, and some variants include an ON/OFF switch for convenient power control. By keeping the batteries securely in place and protected, this holder ensures efficient power delivery and long-lasting performance in various low-voltage applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774961897651-878700321.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-31 12:58:17','2026-03-31 12:58:17'),
(3392,'3 AA Battery Holder With Cover',NULL,NULL,NULL,199.00,'A 3 AA battery holder with cover is a sturdy and reliable enclosure designed to hold three AA batteries securely while providing a consistent power source for electronic devices and DIY applications. Made from high-quality plastic, it includes metal spring contacts that ensure strong electrical conductivity and stable battery placement. The protective cover helps shield the batteries from dust, moisture, and accidental short circuits, improving safety and durability.','This type of holder typically provides a 4.5V output when using standard 1.5V AA batteries, making it suitable for use in toys, LED lighting, Arduino projects, portable gadgets, and small electronic circuits. Many models come with pre-attached wires or terminals for easy connectivity, and some include an integrated ON/OFF switch for added convenience.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774962059442-325581540.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-31 13:00:59','2026-03-31 13:00:59'),
(3393,'2 Slot AA Battery Holder',NULL,NULL,NULL,199.00,'A 2 slot AA battery holder is a simple and practical component designed to hold two AA batteries securely and provide a stable power supply for electronic circuits and devices. Typically made from durable plastic, it features metal spring contacts that ensure proper electrical connection and firm battery placement. This type of holder usually provides an output of 3V when using standard 1.5V AA batteries connected in series.','It is widely used in DIY electronics, Arduino projects, toys, LED circuits, and portable devices. Most 2 slot holders come with pre-attached wires or metal terminals for easy integration into circuits, while some variants are designed for PCB mounting. Its compact design, ease of use, and reliable performance make it an essential component for low-voltage power applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774963789322-25823843.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-31 13:29:49','2026-03-31 13:29:49'),
(3394,'3.6V 2500mAh long Li-ion Battery',NULL,NULL,NULL,499.00,'A 2500mAh Li-ion battery is a rechargeable energy storage device widely used in portable electronic applications due to its high energy density and reliable performance. Typically rated at 3.7V, this battery can deliver a capacity of 2500 milliampere-hours, meaning it can supply a steady current over an extended period depending on the load. It is commonly available in cylindrical forms such as the popular 18650 cell, as well as in flat pouch designs for compact devices.','These batteries are widely used in applications such as laptops, power banks, LED lights, medical devices, handheld gadgets, and DIY electronics projects. Lithium-ion batteries are known for their lightweight construction, low self-discharge rate, and absence of memory effect, making them more efficient compared to traditional battery types. They also support multiple charge and discharge cycles, providing long-term usability.',NULL,NULL,'products/1774969166876-1733813.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-03-31 14:56:08','2026-03-31 15:00:02'),
(3395,'LR1130 Alkaline Coin Cell',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'The LR1130 Alkaline Coin Cell is a small, round, button-type battery commonly used in compact electronic devices. It operates at a nominal voltage of 1.5V and is designed to provide reliable, low-drain power for devices such as calculators, watches, toys, laser pointers, and small medical instruments.','Known for its compact size and lightweight design, the LR1130 battery is easy to install and replace. It is also referred to by equivalent names like AG10, 389, or LR54, depending on the manufacturer. This alkaline coin cell offers stable performance and a reasonable shelf life, making it a popular choice for everyday portable electronics.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775016763905-53939514.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-01 04:12:43','2026-04-01 04:12:43'),
(3396,'SR521 Maxell Battery',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'The SR521 Maxell Battery is a high-quality silver oxide coin cell battery designed for precision and long-lasting performance in small electronic devices. Manufactured by Maxell, this battery delivers a stable output voltage of 1.55V, making it ideal for sensitive devices like watches, calculators, medical instruments, and small electronic gadgets.','Compared to alkaline coin cells, silver oxide batteries like the SR521 provide more consistent voltage over their lifespan and better reliability. It is commonly known by other equivalent names such as SR521SW, 379, or LR521 (alkaline equivalent).',NULL,NULL,'products/1775016945656-407467070.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-01 04:15:45','2026-04-01 04:15:45'),
(3397,'CR1616 Lithum Battery',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'he CR1616 Lithium Battery is a compact coin cell battery commonly used in small electronic devices that require reliable and long-lasting power. It operates at a nominal voltage of 3V and uses lithium chemistry, which provides a higher energy density and longer shelf life compared to alkaline batteries.','Due to its slim profile and lightweight design, the CR1616 is widely used in car key fobs, watches, calculators, fitness devices, and computer motherboards. It delivers stable voltage output over time, making it suitable for precision electronics.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775017348783-955086321.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-01 04:22:28','2026-04-01 04:22:28'),
(3398,'LR626 Giga-tek battery',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'The LR626 Giga-Zek battery is a compact alkaline button cell designed to provide reliable 1.5V power for small electronic devices. Commonly known by equivalent names such as AG4, LR66, or 377A, this battery is widely used in wristwatches, calculators, toys, laser pointers, and other low-drain gadgets. Manufactured under the Giga-Zek brand, it offers stable performance and easy compatibility with a variety of devices requiring this size','The LR626 features a lightweight and space-saving design, making it ideal for portable electronics. While it provides cost-effective power, its alkaline chemistry typically has a shorter lifespan compared to silver oxide alternatives, but it remains a popular choice for everyday applications due to its affordability and availability.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775017636708-184970521.jpg',0,1,'active','2026-04-01 04:27:16','2026-04-03 08:26:06'),
(3399,'SR920SW vinnic Battery',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'The SR920SW Vinnic battery is a high-performance silver oxide coin cell designed for precision electronic devices that require stable and long-lasting power. Produced by Vinnic, this battery delivers a consistent 1.55V output, making it ideal for wristwatches, calculators, medical instruments, and other compact electronics. It is commonly known by equivalent codes such as 371 or SR69, ensuring broad compatibility across different devices and brands','Thanks to its silver oxide chemistry, the SR920SW provides a more stable voltage and longer lifespan compared to alkaline alternatives, making it especially suitable for sensitive equipment. Its compact size, leak-resistant design, and reliable performance make it a popular choice for everyday and professional use.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775018256343-127766284.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-01 04:37:36','2026-04-01 04:37:36'),
(3400,'LR41 Maxell Battery',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'The LR41 Maxell Battery is a compact alkaline button cell designed to provide reliable power for small electronic devices. Manufactured by Maxell, it delivers a nominal voltage of 1.5V and is commonly used in watches, calculators, toys, laser pointers, and medical devices like thermometers. This battery is also known by equivalent names such as AG3, 192, or LR736, making it widely compatible across various devices','This battery is also known by equivalent names such as AG3, 192, or LR736, making it widely compatible across various devices. Its lightweight and compact design make it ideal for space-constrained electronics, while its alkaline chemistry offers an economical solution for low-drain applications.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775018388160-857970397.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-01 04:39:48','2026-04-01 04:39:48'),
(3401,'LR1130 Maxell Battery',NULL,NULL,NULL,49.00,'The LR1130 Maxell Battery is a compact alkaline button cell designed for powering small electronic devices with reliable 1.5V output. Manufactured by Maxell, this battery is widely used in watches, calculators, toys, laser pointers, and medical devices. It is also known by equivalent names such as AG10, LR54, or 389, making it compatible with a wide range of devices.','With its lightweight and space-saving design, the LR1130 is ideal for compact electronics, offering stable performance and easy replacement. While it is a cost-effective solution, it is best suited for low-drain applications compared to silver oxide alternatives.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775018617701-241170907.png',1,1,'active','2026-04-01 04:43:37','2026-04-01 04:43:37'),
(3402,'14D141 MOV Thermister',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'The 14D141 MOV (Metal Oxide Varistor) is a voltage-dependent resistor used primarily for protecting electronic circuits from voltage spikes and surges. Although sometimes mistakenly called a thermistor, it is actually a varistor, meaning its resistance changes with applied voltage rather than temperature. The “14D141” designation indicates a 14 mm disc diameter and a varistor voltage of approximately 140V.','Under normal voltage conditions, the MOV has very high resistance and allows minimal current flow. However, when a voltage surge occurs (such as lightning or switching spikes), its resistance drops rapidly, diverting excess current away from sensitive components and preventing damage.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775019963631-803783399.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-01 05:06:03','2026-04-01 05:06:03'),
(3403,'14D681 MOV Thermistor',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'The 14D681 MOV is a Metal Oxide Varistor used for protecting electronic circuits against high-voltage surges and transient spikes. Although sometimes incorrectly referred to as a thermistor, it is actually a voltage-dependent resistor.The code “14D681” indicates a 14 mm disc size and a varistor voltage of approximately 680V. Under normal operating conditions, the MOV exhibits very high resistance and allows negligible current flow.','The code “14D681” indicates a 14 mm disc size and a varistor voltage of approximately 680V. Under normal operating conditions, the MOV exhibits very high resistance and allows negligible current flow. When a voltage surge occurs, its resistance drops rapidly, allowing it to absorb and divert excess voltage, thereby safeguarding sensitive components.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775020451972-145113317.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-01 05:14:11','2026-04-01 05:14:11'),
(3404,'14D911 MOV Thermistor',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'The 14D911 MOV is a Metal Oxide Varistor used for protecting electronic circuits from high-voltage surges and transient spikes. It is often mistakenly called a thermistor, but it is actually a voltage-dependent resistor. The code “14D911” indicates a 14 mm disc diameter and a varistor voltage of approximately 910V. Under normal voltage conditions, the MOV remains in a high-resistance state.','The code “14D911” indicates a 14 mm disc diameter and a varistor voltage of approximately 910V. Under normal voltage conditions, the MOV remains in a high-resistance state. When a sudden voltage surge occurs, its resistance drops instantly, allowing it to absorb and divert excess energy, thereby protecting sensitive electronic components from damage.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775021184625-815756774.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-01 05:26:24','2026-04-01 05:26:24'),
(3405,'14D751 MOV Thermistor',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'The 14D751 MOV (Metal Oxide Varistor) is a voltage-dependent protection component used to safeguard electronic circuits from sudden voltage surges and spikes. Although sometimes incorrectly referred to as a thermistor, it actually responds to voltage changes rather than temperature. The “14D751” designation indicates a 14 mm disc size and a varistor voltage of approximately 750V. Under normal operating conditions, the MOV maintains a very high resistance and allows minimal current flow.','However, when a high-voltage transient occurs, its resistance drops rapidly, enabling it to absorb and divert excess energy away from sensitive components. This makes it an essential component in power supplies, home appliances, and industrial equipment, ensuring reliable protection against electrical surges.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775021387281-187027438.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-01 05:29:47','2026-04-01 05:29:47'),
(3406,'14D271 MOV Thermistor',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'The 14D271 MOV is a Metal Oxide Varistor used for protecting electronic circuits from voltage surges and transient spikes. It is often mistakenly called a thermistor, but it actually works based on voltage changes rather than temperature. The code “14D271” indicates a 14 mm disc diameter and a varistor voltage of approximately 270V. Under normal voltage conditions, the MOV has very high resistance and allows very little current to pass.','The code “14D271” indicates a 14 mm disc diameter and a varistor voltage of approximately 270V. Under normal voltage conditions, the MOV has very high resistance and allows very little current to pass. When a voltage spike occurs, its resistance drops instantly, enabling it to absorb and clamp the excess voltage, thereby protecting sensitive components from damage.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775021502660-921916991.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-01 05:31:42','2026-04-01 05:31:42'),
