(3410,'7D471 MOV Thermistor',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'The 7D471 MOV (Metal Oxide Varistor) is a compact voltage-dependent resistor designed to protect electronic circuits from sudden voltage surges and transient spikes. Despite sometimes being incorrectly referred to as a thermistor, it actually responds to changes in voltage rather than temperature. The designation “7D471” indicates a disc diameter of 7 mm and a varistor voltage of approximately 470V. Under normal operating conditions, the MOV maintains a very high resistance, allowing only minimal current to pass through the circuit.','When a high-voltage surge occurs, its resistance drops rapidly, enabling it to absorb and clamp the excess voltage to a safe level. This fast response helps prevent damage to sensitive electronic components. Due to its small size, the 7D471 is ideal for compact circuit designs and low to medium power applications. It is commonly used in power adapters, LED drivers, consumer electronics, and small power supply units. The device is easy to mount on printed circuit boards and offers reliable, long-term protection under normal conditions.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775022372296-856593511.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-01 05:46:12','2026-04-01 05:46:12'),
