(3495,'High quality solder flux 500gms',NULL,NULL,NULL,1499.00,'High-quality solder flux paste is a semi-solid chemical used to improve soldering by cleaning metal surfaces, removing oxidation, and enhancing the flow of molten solder. It ensures strong, reliable electrical connections and reduces defects such as cold joints or bridging.','Available in no-clean and rosin types, premium flux paste is widely used in PCB assembly, mobile repair, and professional electronics work for smooth and efficient soldering.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775115568540-994886288.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 07:39:28','2026-04-02 07:39:28'),
(3496,'Frontech MS-0070 Wired Optical Mouse',NULL,NULL,NULL,840.00,'The Frontech MS‑0070 is a budget‑friendly wired optical mouse designed for everyday computer use on desktops and laptops. It offers a simple plug‑and‑play setup with an ergonomic design, making it suitable for basic tasks like browsing, office work, and casual use without needing any software or drivers.','Wired USB connection: Reliable connection with no batteries required — just plug it into a USB port and get started instantly.\r\nOptical tracking: Equipped with a 1200 DPI optical sensor for smooth and accurate cursor movement across most surfaces.\r\n3‑button design: Standard left and right buttons plus a scroll wheel for easy navigation and control.\r\nErgonomic & compact: Comfortable grip for everyday use, even during extended sessions.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775115613217-331802988.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 07:40:13','2026-04-02 07:40:13'),
(3497,'DL Soldering paste 10g',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'The DL Soldering Paste 10g is a compact and budget-friendly flux paste designed for general soldering applications such as PCB work, wire connections, and basic electronics repair. It contains high-quality additives and activators that help improve solder flow and create strong, clean joints.','This paste is known for producing low smoke, no bad smell, and minimal residue, making it suitable for indoor use and beginners. It is typically white in color and can be used for both soldering and desoldering tasks, depending on application',NULL,NULL,'products/1775115984493-230059044.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 07:46:24','2026-04-02 07:46:24'),
(3498,'Enter Eternal Wired Optical Mouse',NULL,NULL,NULL,899.00,'The Enter Eternal Wired Optical Mouse is a simple and affordable wired USB mouse designed for everyday computer use. It’s a basic plug‑and‑play accessory that provides reliable pointing and navigation for tasks like browsing, office work, and casual use on laptops or desktops.','Wired USB connection: Connects easily to a computer or laptop’s USB port with no drivers or software required — just plug it in and start using.\r\nOptical sensor: Provides smooth and responsive cursor movement for everyday navigation and productivity tasks.\r\n1000 DPI resolution: Offers balanced sensitivity for precise tracking — suitable for general computing needs.\r\n3‑button design: Standard layout with left, right, and scroll wheel buttons for easy control.\r\nErgonomic shape: Comfortable for regular use and fits most hand sizes.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775116065491-341697932.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 07:47:45','2026-04-02 07:47:45'),
(3499,'MV Solder Soldering paste 10g',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'The MV Soldering Paste 10g is a compact flux paste used for electronics soldering, wire joining, and PCB repair work. It works by cleaning metal surfaces and removing oxidation, allowing solder to flow smoothly and create strong electrical connections. Like other 10g solder pastes, it is designed for low smoke, minimal residue, and easy application, making it suitable for both beginners and technicians.','Most 10g flux pastes (including MV type) contain active soldering additives and flux agents that improve bonding and reduce soldering defects. They are commonly used for copper, brass, and electronic components, ensuring reliable joints in small repair jobs',NULL,NULL,'products/1775116263440-139511504.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 07:51:03','2026-04-02 07:51:03'),
(3500,'Cobson soldering paste 10g',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'The Cobson soldering paste 10g is a small, general-purpose flux paste used for electronics soldering, PCB repair, and wire connections. Like similar 10g flux pastes, it is formulated to remove oxidation, improve solder flow, and ensure strong electrical joints.','This type of solder paste typically has a smooth, semi-solid (cream-like) consistency, making it easy to apply on components and wires. It produces low smoke, minimal residue, and no strong odor, making it suitable for indoor use and beginners. High-quality flux pastes also contain active additives that improve bonding and prevent dry solder joints',NULL,NULL,'products/1775116516128-319563135.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 07:55:16','2026-04-02 07:55:16'),
(3501,'Cobson white soldering flux paste',NULL,NULL,NULL,99.00,'The Cobson white soldering flux paste (10g) is a general-purpose flux paste used for PCB soldering, wire connections, and electronic repairs. It is typically a white-colored rosin-based paste, designed to remove oxidation, improve solder flow, and create strong electrical joints.','The Cobson white soldering flux paste (10g) is a general-purpose flux paste used for PCB soldering, wire connections, and electronic repairs. It is typically a white-colored rosin-based paste, designed to remove oxidation, improve solder flow, and create strong electrical joints.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775116725440-79031040.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 07:58:45','2026-04-02 07:58:45'),
(3502,'Noel Micro soldering station 12V',NULL,NULL,NULL,2999.00,'The Noel Micro Soldering Station 12V is a compact and precision soldering tool designed for delicate electronic work such as mobile repair, SMD components, and PCB soldering. It operates on 12V output with a transformer-based station and offers variable wattage (around 6–12W), allowing better control over heat for sensitive components.','This station includes a micro soldering pen with a fine tip, making it ideal for precision jobs where accuracy is important. It supports a temperature range of approximately 180°C to 350°C, suitable for most electronics applications',NULL,NULL,'products/1775117128711-184293804.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 08:05:28','2026-04-02 08:05:28'),
(3503,'Desoldering Wick',NULL,NULL,NULL,299.00,'A desoldering wick is a braided copper wire coated with flux that is used to remove molten solder from electronic components and circuit boards. When heated, it absorbs solder quickly, leaving clean pads for repair or replacement. It is widely used in PCB work, mobile repair, and DIY electronics due to its efficiency, ease of use, and affordability.','A desoldering wick (solder wick) is a must-have tool for removing unwanted solder from PCBs, wires, and electronic components. When choosing one, focus on width (1.5–3.5mm), flux type (rosin / no-clean), and quality of copper braid for better absorption.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775117329179-208866992.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 08:08:49','2026-04-02 08:18:07'),
(3504,'Soldron soldering iron bit',NULL,NULL,NULL,499.00,'A Soldron soldering iron bit is a high-quality replaceable metal tip designed for use with Soldron soldering irons, playing a crucial role in transferring heat from the iron to the solder and components. These bits are typically made from copper with nickel or iron plating, which improves durability, heat conductivity, and resistance to oxidation. Soldron offers a wide range of bits such as needle (pointed), spade (chisel), and ceramic-coated types, each suited for different applications like PCB soldering, wire joining, and heavy-duty electrical work.','Available in multiple wattage ratings like 25W, 35W, 50W, and 100W, these bits ensure compatibility with various soldering irons and provide efficient heat transfer for smooth and reliable solder joints. Their easy replaceable design, long life, and precision performance make Soldron soldering bits a popular choice among technicians, students, and electronics professionals.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775117599393-340023012.png',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 08:13:19','2026-04-02 08:13:19'),
(3505,'Record classic soldering iron bit',NULL,NULL,NULL,499.00,'A record / classic soldering iron bit (commonly used in traditional Soldron soldering irons) is a standard replacement tip designed for everyday soldering applications. These classic bits are usually made from high-quality copper with nickel or iron plating, which provides good heat conductivity and protects the tip from corrosion and wear. They typically come in simple shapes like pointed (needle) or flat (spade), making them suitable for basic tasks such as wire connections, circuit board repairs, and general electrical work.','Classic Soldron bits are available in common wattage ratings like 15W, 25W, 35W, and higher, ensuring compatibility with different soldering irons. They are easy to install, heat up quickly, and offer stable performance for consistent solder flow. Due to their durability, affordability, and versatility, classic soldering bits are widely used by technicians, students, and hobbyists for routine soldering jobs',NULL,NULL,'products/1775117745344-123312464.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 08:15:45','2026-04-02 08:15:45'),
(3506,'AAA soldering iron 25W',NULL,NULL,NULL,1498.00,'A AAA soldering iron 25W is a basic, lightweight electric soldering tool designed for small electronic repairs and general-purpose soldering work. It typically operates on 220–240V AC power and uses a 25-watt heating element, which provides moderate heat suitable for PCB soldering, wire connections, and component fixing without damaging sensitive parts. These soldering irons usually come with a copper tip coated with iron or nickel for better heat transfer and durability','These soldering irons usually come with a copper tip coated with iron or nickel for better heat transfer and durability. Many 25W models feature simple designs with conical or flat tips, ergonomic handles for comfortable use, and quick heating (around 1–2 minutes). They are widely used by students, technicians, and hobbyists because they are affordable, easy to handle, and ideal for light-duty tasks rather than heavy industrial soldering',NULL,NULL,'products/1775118470671-870378975.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 08:27:50','2026-04-02 08:27:50'),
(3507,'5 in 1 Soldering Iron set',NULL,NULL,NULL,1499.00,'A 5 in 1 soldering iron set is a complete beginner-to-intermediate toolkit that includes a soldering iron along with essential accessories required for electronics repair and assembly work. These kits are designed to provide everything needed for soldering in one package, making them ideal for students, technicians, and hobbyists.','Typically, a 5-in-1 kit includes a soldering iron (25W or 30W), solder wire, desoldering wick (for removing solder), a stand for safely holding the hot iron, and a cutter or wire stripper. Some kits may also include flux paste or a tester. The soldering iron in these kits usually heats up quickly and is suitable for PCB work, small electronic components, and wire joints. These kits are widely used for DIY projects, mobile repair, and basic electrical work because they are affordable, portable, and easy to use',NULL,NULL,'products/1775118908479-609621980.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 08:35:08','2026-04-02 08:35:08'),
(3508,'Soldering iron with bit',NULL,NULL,NULL,2999.00,'A soldering iron with bit is a complete soldering tool that comes with a heating iron and a fitted tip (bit) used to melt solder for joining electronic components. The bit is the most important part of the iron, as it transfers heat to the solder and determines precision and performance. These irons are commonly available in 25W, 35W, and higher wattages, and are widely used for PCB work, wire connections, and general electrical repairs.','The bit is the most important part of the iron, as it transfers heat to the solder and determines precision and performance. These irons are commonly available in 25W, 35W, and higher wattages, and are widely used for PCB work, wire connections, and general electrical repairs. Most soldering irons come with copper bits coated with nickel or iron, which improves heat transfer and prevents oxidation, ensuring longer life and smooth soldering',NULL,NULL,'products/1775119060591-681978276.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 08:37:40','2026-04-02 08:37:40'),
(3509,'Enter Cursor Wired Optical Mouse',NULL,NULL,NULL,750.00,'The Enter Cursor Wired Optical Mouse is a simple and affordable wired USB mouse designed for everyday use with desktops and laptops. It’s a budget‑friendly accessory that offers reliable performance for basic computing tasks like web browsing, office work, and general navigation.','Wired USB connection: Plug‑and‑play USB connectivity — no drivers or software needed.\r\nOptical tracking: Uses an optical sensor for smooth and responsive cursor movement on most surfaces.\r\n1000 DPI: Standard sensitivity suitable for everyday tasks (navigation, editing, browsing).\r\nThree‑button design: Left/right buttons and a scroll wheel for easy control.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775119208401-269045715.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 08:40:08','2026-04-02 08:40:08'),
(3510,'3 in 1 Soldering iron set',NULL,NULL,NULL,999.00,'A 3 in 1 soldering iron set is a compact and budget-friendly soldering kit that includes three essential tools required for basic electronics work. It is mainly designed for beginners, students, and small repair tasks where only the core items are needed. Typically, a 3-in-1 set contains a soldering iron (usually 25W or 30W), solder wire, and flux (or solder paste), which together are enough for making simple solder joints on PCBs, wires, and small components.','Typically, a 3-in-1 set contains a soldering iron (usually 25W or 30W), solder wire, and flux (or solder paste), which together are enough for making simple solder joints on PCBs, wires, and small components. These kits are lightweight, easy to use, and heat up quickly, making them ideal for home use, DIY projects, and mobile repair. Compared to larger kits (like 5-in-1), they are more affordable but come with fewer accessories.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775119232135-946445957.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 08:40:32','2026-04-02 08:40:32'),
(3511,'Ariham soldering iron 25w',NULL,NULL,NULL,1499.00,'An Ariham 25W soldering iron is a simple and affordable electric soldering tool designed for light-duty electronics work such as PCB soldering, wire connections, and small repair jobs. It operates on standard 220–240V AC power and uses a 25-watt heating element, which provides controlled heat suitable for delicate components without causing damage. These soldering irons typically come with a copper tip (bit) coated with nickel or iron to ensure good heat transfer and resistance to oxidation.','The Ariham 25W iron heats up within a minute and maintains a steady temperature, making it ideal for students, technicians, and DIY users. It is lightweight, easy to handle, and commonly used for mobile repair, circuit board work, and small electrical tasks. Like most entry-level soldering irons, it does not have advanced temperature control but offers reliable performance for everyday use',NULL,NULL,'products/1775119338309-434122966.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 08:42:18','2026-04-02 08:42:18'),
(3512,'Zebronics Rise Wired Optical Mouse',NULL,NULL,NULL,510.00,'The Zebronics Rise Wired Optical Mouse is a simple, ergonomic, and budget‑friendly wired USB mouse designed for everyday computing tasks such as web browsing, office work, and general navigation. It’s a plug‑and‑play accessory that doesn’t require any software or drivers, making it easy to use with desktops and laptops.','Wired USB connectivity: Reliable plug‑and‑play performance — just connect the mouse and start using it.\r\nOptical tracking: Uses a 1200 DPI optical sensor for smooth and accurate cursor control across most surfaces.\r\n3‑button layout: Standard left and right buttons with a scroll wheel for easy navigation.\r\nCompact & stylish design: Lightweight and comfortable for regular use.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775119488076-193270170.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 08:44:48','2026-04-02 08:44:48'),
(3513,'D-Con Soldering iron',NULL,NULL,NULL,1499.00,'A D-Con soldering iron (often written as Dcon or D-Con type) is a simple, low-cost electric soldering tool designed for everyday electronics work. It typically comes in a 25W power rating, making it ideal for light-duty applications such as PCB soldering, small wire joints, and component repair. These irons operate on 220–240V AC power and use a fixed heating element that provides steady heat without temperature control.','The tool heats up quickly and is easy to handle due to its lightweight design, making it suitable for students, technicians, and hobbyists. However, since it is a basic model, it does not include advanced features like temperature adjustment or digital control. According to product listings, D-Con 25W irons generally use flat copper tips and reach around 200°C, which is sufficient for general-purpose soldering tasks.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775119550980-209576234.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 08:45:50','2026-04-02 08:45:50'),
(3514,'Devaji soldering iron',NULL,NULL,NULL,1499.00,'A Devaji soldering iron is a reliable and budget-friendly electric tool commonly used for electronics repair, DIY projects, and small electrical work. The popular 25W model operates on standard 220–240V AC power and provides moderate heat suitable for delicate soldering tasks like PCB components and wire joints. It is typically equipped with a high-quality copper bit, which ensures efficient heat transfer and smooth solder flow for strong connections.','Many Devaji soldering irons feature fast heating technology, allowing the tool to be ready within seconds, along with a heat-resistant ABS handle for safe and comfortable use during long working hours. Some models also include overheat protection, which helps maintain stable temperature and extends the lifespan of the heating element',NULL,NULL,'products/1775119643149-776189737.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 08:47:23','2026-04-02 08:47:23'),
(3515,'Royalstar soldering iron 25w',NULL,NULL,NULL,1499.00,'A Royalstar 25W soldering iron is a simple and economical electric soldering tool designed for light electronics work such as PCB soldering, wire connections, and small component repairs. It typically operates on 220–240V AC power and uses a 25-watt heating element, which provides moderate heat suitable for delicate electronic components without causing damage. Most Royalstar-type soldering irons come with a copper tip (bit)—either pointed or flat—offering good heat transfer and smooth solder flow for reliable joints.','These soldering irons are lightweight and easy to handle, making them ideal for students, technicians, and hobbyists. They usually heat up within a minute and maintain a steady working temperature, which is sufficient for general-purpose soldering. Like other basic models, they do not include temperature control but are valued for their affordability and ease of use. Similar 25W soldering irons commonly use nichrome heating elements and ergonomic handles for comfortable operation',NULL,NULL,'products/1775119736035-678999766.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 08:48:56','2026-04-02 08:48:56'),
(3516,'Lapcare L-70 Plus Wired Mouse',NULL,NULL,NULL,810.00,'The Lapcare L‑70 Plus Wired Optical Mouse is an affordable, plug‑and‑play wired USB mouse designed for everyday desktop and laptop use. It’s a reliable and simple peripheral that delivers smooth cursor control and comfortable handling, making it suitable for general computer tasks like browsing, office work, and basic navigation.','Wired USB connection: Easy plug‑and‑play setup — just insert into a USB port and start using with no drivers required.\r\n1200 DPI optical sensor: Provides accurate and responsive cursor tracking on most surfaces, helping with smooth movement and control.\r\n3‑button design: Standard left, right, and scroll wheel buttons for navigation and scrolling.\r\nErgonomic shape: Comfortable grip for extended use whether for office work or daily computing.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775120140670-976832061.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 08:55:40','2026-04-02 08:55:40'),
(3517,'Black Panther soldering iron 25w',NULL,NULL,NULL,1499.00,'The Black Panther 25W soldering iron is a compact and budget-friendly tool designed for precision electronics work such as PCB soldering, wire connections, and small repairs. It operates on 230V AC power and uses a 25-watt heating element, which provides moderate and stable heat suitable for delicate components. This makes it ideal for students, hobbyists, and technicians working on everyday electronic projects','The soldering iron is equipped with a copper-coated iron tip, ensuring efficient heat transfer and smooth solder flow for reliable joints. It features a lightweight body and ergonomic insulated handle, which makes it comfortable and safe to use even for longer durations. Additionally, the tool heats up quickly and maintains a steady temperature, helping achieve consistent soldering results',NULL,NULL,'products/1775120212512-35298155.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 08:56:52','2026-04-02 08:56:52'),
(3518,'Oswal soldering iron 25W',NULL,NULL,NULL,1499.00,'The Oswal 25W soldering iron is a reliable and widely used tool for basic electronics soldering and repair work. It operates on 230V AC power and delivers a 25-watt output, making it suitable for delicate tasks such as PCB soldering, wire joints, and small component repairs. The iron is designed with a replaceable copper bit (chisel type) that ensures efficient heat transfer and smooth solder flow, helping create strong and clean joints.','This soldering iron is known for its fast heating and stable temperature performance, reaching working temperature quickly and maintaining consistent heat during use. It also features a cool-grip insulated handle, which improves safety and comfort while working for longer periods. Additionally, the iron has low leakage current, making it safe for sensitive electronic components.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775120478562-152567480.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 09:01:18','2026-04-02 09:01:18'),
(3519,'Ironic soldering iron 25w',NULL,NULL,NULL,1499.00,'An Ironic 25W soldering iron is a basic, entry-level soldering tool designed for light electronic applications such as PCB soldering, wire joining, and small repair tasks. It operates on 220–240V AC power and uses a 25-watt heating element, which provides controlled heat suitable for delicate components. Like most standard soldering irons in this category, it features a nichrome heating element that ensures reliable heating and consistent performance','The soldering iron typically comes with a copper bit (tip)—either pointed or flat—which helps in efficient heat transfer and smooth solder flow. It heats up quickly (usually within 1–2 minutes) and maintains a stable working temperature, making it ideal for beginners, students, and technicians. These types of irons are widely used for general-purpose electronics because they are simple, lightweight, and easy to handle.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775120603640-758403521.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 09:03:23','2026-04-02 09:03:23'),
(3520,'Zebronics  Juggle Wired optical Mouse',NULL,NULL,NULL,1079.00,'The Zebronics Juggle Wired Optical Mouse is a simple and affordable USB wired mouse designed for everyday computing tasks such as browsing, typing, and general workstation use. It’s a basic but reliable peripheral that offers smooth cursor control and easy plug‑and‑play convenience without requiring any software installation.','Wired USB connection: Just plug into a USB port — no drivers or software needed (plug‑and‑play).\r\nOptical sensor: Provides accurate and responsive cursor tracking.\r\n1200 DPI resolution: Good sensitivity and smooth movement for everyday tasks like browsing, documents, and light productivity.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775120645603-664786513.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 09:04:05','2026-04-02 09:04:05'),
(3521,'Oswal soldering iron 8w',NULL,NULL,NULL,1499.00,'The Oswal 8W soldering iron is a low-power, precision soldering tool specially designed for delicate electronic work such as small PCB components, micro circuits, and fine wire soldering. It operates on 220V AC power and uses a very low 8-watt heating element, which produces controlled heat suitable for sensitive components without the risk of damage. This type of soldering iron usually comes with a fine pointed copper tip, allowing accurate and detailed soldering in tight spaces.','Due to its low wattage, the Oswal 8W iron heats up quickly but maintains a lower temperature compared to 25W irons, making it ideal for precision tasks rather than heavy soldering. It is lightweight, easy to handle, and commonly used by students, hobbyists, and technicians working on SMD components, small circuits, and repair work. The iron is also compatible with standard soldering bits and offers stable heating performance for consistent results.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775120723459-447048568.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 09:05:23','2026-04-02 09:05:23'),
(3522,'Maxx Micro soldering iron 12w',NULL,NULL,NULL,1499.00,'The Maxx Micro soldering iron 12W (commonly known as Maxx Pamma micro iron pen) is a low-power, precision soldering tool specially designed for delicate electronics and mobile repair work. Unlike standard 25W irons, this model operates on 12V DC power and uses a 12-watt heating element, making it ideal for fine soldering tasks such as SMD components, IC work, and small PCB repairs. It heats up quickly and provides controlled temperature, which helps avoid damage to sensitive electronic parts','This micro soldering iron features a thin, pointed tip (micro bit) that allows accurate work in tight spaces. It is lightweight and pen-shaped, offering better control for precision soldering. The tool is commonly used in mobile servicing, chip-level repair, watch repair, and small DIY electronics projects. It also includes a heat-resistant handle and durable construction for safe and long-term use.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775120849255-112889223.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 09:07:29','2026-04-02 09:07:29'),
(3523,'Ego soldering iron 12w',NULL,NULL,NULL,999.00,'The Ego 12W soldering iron is a micro-type, low-power soldering tool specially designed for precision electronics work such as mobile repair, SMD components, and small PCB soldering. It operates on 12V power and uses a 12-watt heating element, providing controlled heat that is safe for delicate components. This model (commonly SI-37) is known for its pen-like design, making it easy to handle and ideal for working in tight spaces.','This soldering iron features a fine pointed tip (micro bit) that allows accurate soldering on very small joints. It is lightweight (around 155 mm length) and equipped with a firm grip for comfortable long-term use. The iron heats up quickly and reaches a stable working temperature within seconds, improving efficiency during repair work',NULL,NULL,'products/1775121037986-642475385.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 09:10:37','2026-04-02 09:10:37'),
(3524,'Foxin Smart Blue Wired Optical Mouse',NULL,NULL,NULL,540.00,'The Foxin Smart Blue Wired Optical Mouse is a budget‑friendly wired USB mouse designed for everyday computing tasks. It offers a simple plug‑and‑play experience with responsive tracking and a comfortable grip, making it suitable for laptops, desktops, and basic office or home use.','Wired USB connection: Easy plug‑and‑play — just connect to a USB port and start using immediately, with no drivers needed.\r\nOptical tracking sensor: Provides smooth and accurate cursor movement for everyday tasks like browsing, document editing, and basic navigation.\r\n800 DPI sensitivity: Standard resolution suitable for general use (some listings reference up to 6400 DPI software resolution).',NULL,NULL,'products/1775121045337-11013259.jpeg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 09:10:45','2026-04-02 09:10:45'),
(3525,'JYD-JD020 soldering iron 30w',NULL,NULL,NULL,1499.00,'The JYD-JD020 soldering iron (30W) is a mid-power electric soldering tool designed for general electronics work, PCB soldering, and medium-duty applications. It operates on 220–240V AC power and provides a 30-watt heating output, which is slightly higher than 25W irons, offering better heat capacity for stronger and faster solder joints.','This model typically features a nichrome heating element and a replaceable copper tip (bit), ensuring efficient heat transfer and smooth solder flow. It heats up quickly (usually within 1–2 minutes) and maintains a stable working temperature, making it suitable for both beginners and technicians. Similar JYD JD020 series irons are also available in higher wattages with temperature control (200°C–450°C range), showing the series is designed for versatility and reliable performance.',NULL,NULL,'products/1775121159312-861324426.jpg',1,1,'active','2026-04-02 09:12:39','2026-04-02 09:12:39'),
