(33,'Agriculture','Agriculture is the practice of cultivating soil, growing crops, and rearing livestock to produce food, fiber, fuel, and other essential products for human use.','Modern agriculture combines traditional farming knowledge with science and technology to increase productivity, improve quality, and use natural resources efficiently. It includes activities such as crop production, horticulture, dairy farming, poultry, f','Agriculture is important for the economy of many countries.\r\nIt depends on soil, water, and climate.\r\nModern farming uses machines and fertilizers.','Subsistence farming – for family use.\r\nCommercial farming – for selling in markets.\r\nMixed farming – crops and animals together.\r\nOrganic farming – uses natural methods.','sector-titles/1771478510833-349857660.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,'','https://circuitpoint.in/agriculture',1,1,'active','2026-02-19 05:21:50','2026-02-19 05:21:50'),
